// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — 學測6000字 Level 5
window.L5_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"abnormal – advocate","cards":[{"w":"abnormal","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is usual or expected, often in a bad way","c":"不正常的；異常的","s":"The doctor noticed an abnormal heartbeat during the check-up, so she asked my father to come back for more tests.","t":"醫生在健康檢查時注意到不正常的心跳，所以她要我爸爸回來做更多檢查。","h":1},{"w":"normal","p":"adj.","d":"usual, ordinary, and expected","c":"正常的；一般的","s":"It is normal to feel nervous before a big exam, so take a deep breath and remember how much you have prepared.","t":"大考前感到緊張是正常的，所以深呼吸，記住你已經準備了多少。"},{"w":"abnormally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is not usual or expected","c":"異常地","s":"The weather has been abnormally warm this winter, and some cherry trees in the park have already started to bloom.","t":"今年冬天的天氣異常溫暖，公園裡有些櫻花樹已經開始開花了。"},{"w":"abnormality","p":"n.","d":"something that is not normal, especially in the body","c":"異常；畸形","s":"The scan showed a small abnormality in his lung, but the doctor said it was nothing serious and could be treated easily.","t":"掃描顯示他的肺部有一個小小的異常，但醫生說那沒什麼嚴重，可以輕易治療。"},{"w":"normally","p":"adv.","d":"usually; in the usual way","c":"通常；正常地","s":"I normally take the bus to school, but this morning my father drove me because it was raining so heavily.","t":"我通常搭公車上學，但今天早上因為雨下得太大，我爸爸開車送我。"},{"w":"abolish","p":"v.","d":"to officially end a law, system, or practice","c":"廢除；廢止","s":"Many countries decided to abolish the death penalty in the last century, and others are still discussing whether to do the same.","t":"許多國家在上個世紀決定廢除死刑，其他國家仍在討論是否要跟進。","h":1},{"w":"abolition","p":"n.","d":"the official ending of a law, system, or practice","c":"廢除；廢止","s":"The abolition of slavery in the United States came after a long war that divided families and the whole country.","t":"美國廢除奴隸制度是在一場讓家庭和整個國家分裂的漫長戰爭之後。"},{"w":"abolish slavery","p":"v.phr.","d":"to end the system of owning people as property","c":"廢除奴隸制","s":"Britain passed a law to abolish slavery in 1833, but it took many more years before all the slaves were actually free.","t":"英國在一八三三年通過法律廢除奴隸制，但又過了許多年所有的奴隸才真正獲得自由。"},{"w":"abortion","p":"n.","d":"a medical operation to end a pregnancy","c":"墮胎；人工流產","s":"The laws on abortion are different in every country, and the topic is still debated by doctors, lawmakers, and religious groups.","t":"各國關於墮胎的法律都不同，這個議題至今仍受到醫生、立法者和宗教團體的爭論。","h":1},{"w":"abort","p":"v.","d":"to stop a plan, mission, or activity before it is finished","c":"中止；放棄（計畫）","s":"The pilot decided to abort the landing when a strong wind suddenly pushed the plane to one side of the runway.","t":"當強風突然把飛機推向跑道一側時，機長決定中止降落。"},{"w":"abort a mission","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop a planned task because of danger or problems","c":"中止任務","s":"The space agency had to abort a mission only ten minutes before launch because a small leak was found in the fuel tank.","t":"太空總署在發射前僅十分鐘就不得不中止任務，因為燃料箱發現了一個小裂縫。"},{"w":"abrupt","p":"adj.","d":"sudden and unexpected","c":"突然的；意外的","s":"The movie came to an abrupt end without explaining what happened to the main character, and the audience was confused.","t":"電影突然結束，沒有解釋主角發生了什麼事，觀眾一頭霧水。","h":1},{"w":"abrupt","p":"adj.","d":"speaking in a short, unfriendly way","c":"唐突的；粗魯的","s":"The clerk's abrupt answer made the old lady feel unwelcome, so she decided to shop at a different store next time.","t":"店員唐突的回答讓老太太覺得不受歡迎，所以她決定下次去別家店買東西。"},{"w":"abruptly","p":"adv.","d":"suddenly and unexpectedly","c":"突然地；唐突地","s":"The bus stopped so abruptly that several passengers fell forward, and one man dropped his coffee on the floor.","t":"公車停得如此突然，好幾位乘客向前跌倒，一名男子把咖啡灑在地板上。"},{"w":"come to an abrupt end","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finish suddenly and unexpectedly","c":"突然結束","s":"The outdoor concert came to an abrupt end when lightning struck a tree nearby and the rain began to pour down.","t":"當閃電擊中附近的一棵樹、大雨開始傾盆而下時，露天演唱會突然結束了。","a":"came to an abrupt end"},{"w":"absurd","p":"adj.","d":"so silly or unreasonable that it makes you laugh","c":"荒謬的；可笑的","s":"It is absurd to expect a ten-year-old child to finish three hours of homework every night and still get enough sleep.","t":"期望一個十歲的孩子每晚做三小時功課還能睡飽，實在荒謬。","h":1},{"w":"absurdly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very silly or unreasonable way","c":"荒謬地；可笑地","s":"The prices at the airport café are absurdly high; a small bottle of water there costs as much as a full lunch in town.","t":"機場咖啡廳的價格高得離譜；那裡一小瓶水的價錢和市區一頓午餐一樣貴。"},{"w":"absurdity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being silly or unreasonable; a silly idea","c":"荒謬；荒唐的事","s":"Everyone laughed at the absurdity of the plan to build a swimming pool on the roof of the hundred-year-old wooden house.","t":"大家都笑那個計畫的荒謬：要在一百年歷史的木造老屋屋頂上蓋游泳池。"},{"w":"abundant","p":"adj.","d":"existing in large amounts; more than enough","c":"豐富的；充足的","s":"The island has abundant rainfall all year round, which is why its forests are so green and full of life.","t":"這座島全年雨量豐富，這就是為什麼它的森林如此翠綠且充滿生機。","h":1},{"w":"abundance","p":"n.","d":"a very large amount of something","c":"豐富；充裕","s":"In autumn the market tables are covered with an abundance of fresh fruit, and farmers sell persimmons at very low prices.","t":"秋天市場的攤位上擺滿了豐富的新鮮水果，農民以很低的價格賣柿子。"},{"w":"abundantly","p":"adv.","d":"in large amounts; very","c":"充足地；非常","s":"The teacher made it abundantly clear that any student caught using a phone during the test would receive a zero.","t":"老師非常清楚地表示，考試中任何被抓到用手機的學生都會得零分。"},{"w":"an abundance of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large amount of something","c":"大量的；豐富的","s":"Taiwan has an abundance of hot springs because the island sits on the edge of two plates that push against each other.","t":"台灣有豐富的溫泉，因為這座島位於兩個互相推擠的板塊邊緣。"},{"w":"abuse","p":"n.","d":"cruel or violent treatment of a person or animal","c":"虐待","s":"The shelter takes care of dogs that have suffered abuse, and many of them are afraid of people when they first arrive.","t":"收容所照顧曾遭受虐待的狗，牠們當中許多剛到時都很怕人。","h":1},{"w":"abuse","p":"n.","d":"the use of something in a wrong or harmful way","c":"濫用","s":"The abuse of antibiotics has created new kinds of bacteria that no medicine can kill, which worries doctors around the world.","t":"抗生素的濫用造成了沒有任何藥物能殺死的新型細菌，令全世界的醫生擔憂。"},{"w":"abuse","p":"v.","d":"to treat a person or animal cruelly; to use something in a harmful way","c":"虐待；濫用","s":"Anyone who is found to abuse an animal in this city can be fined up to one hundred thousand dollars.","t":"在這座城市，任何被發現虐待動物的人最高可被罰款十萬元。"},{"w":"abusive","p":"adj.","d":"using cruel words or violence toward someone","c":"辱罵的；虐待的","s":"The referee stopped the game and sent off a player who had shouted abusive words at a member of the other team.","t":"裁判停止比賽，將一名對對方隊員大喊辱罵字眼的球員罰下場。"},{"w":"drug abuse","p":"n.phr.","d":"the use of illegal drugs or the harmful use of medicine","c":"藥物濫用","s":"The school invited a former police officer to talk about drug abuse and the serious damage it can do to a young person's life.","t":"學校邀請一位退休警官來談藥物濫用以及它對年輕人生命可能造成的嚴重傷害。"},{"w":"accelerate","p":"v.","d":"to go faster; to make something happen sooner","c":"加速；促進","s":"The driver began to accelerate as soon as the traffic light turned green, and the car was soon far ahead of the others.","t":"交通號誌一變綠，駕駛就開始加速，汽車很快就遠遠領先其他車。","h":1},{"w":"accelerate","p":"v.","d":"to make a process happen faster","c":"加速（進行）","s":"Warm weather and heavy rain can accelerate the growth of weeds, so farmers have to clear their fields more often in summer.","t":"溫暖的天氣和大雨會加速雜草的生長，所以農民夏天必須更常清理田地。"},{"w":"acceleration","p":"n.","d":"an increase in speed; the rate at which something gets faster","c":"加速；加速度","s":"This electric car is famous for its acceleration; it can go from zero to one hundred kilometers an hour in just four seconds.","t":"這款電動車以其加速性能聞名；它能在短短四秒內從零加速到時速一百公里。"},{"w":"accelerator","p":"n.","d":"the pedal in a car that makes it go faster","c":"油門","s":"My driving teacher told me to press the accelerator gently, because the car jumps forward if you push it too hard.","t":"我的駕訓教練叫我輕踩油門，因為踩太用力車子會往前衝。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"easy to reach, enter, or use","c":"容易到達的；無障礙的；易取得的","s":"The new library is fully accessible to people in wheelchairs, with wide doors, low shelves, and an elevator to every floor.","t":"新圖書館對坐輪椅的人完全無障礙，有寬門、低書架，以及通往每一層樓的電梯。","h":1},{"w":"access","p":"n.","d":"the right or chance to use, enter, or see something","c":"使用權；進入","s":"Students who live in the dormitory have free access to the swimming pool and the gym on campus all year round.","t":"住在宿舍的學生全年都可以免費使用校園內的游泳池和健身房。"},{"w":"access","p":"v.","d":"to open or use information, especially on a computer","c":"存取；使用","s":"You can access your grades online by entering your student number and the password the school gave you.","t":"你可以輸入學號和學校給你的密碼，在線上查看你的成績。"},{"w":"inaccessible","p":"adj.","d":"very hard or impossible to reach or use","c":"難以到達的；無法取得的","s":"The village became inaccessible after the landslide blocked the only road, so helicopters had to bring in food and medicine.","t":"山崩堵住唯一的道路後，村莊變得難以到達，所以必須用直升機運送食物和藥品。"},{"w":"accessibility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being easy to reach or use","c":"可及性；無障礙程度","s":"The city has improved the accessibility of its MRT stations by adding elevators and special paths for blind passengers.","t":"這座城市透過增設電梯和視障者專用引導步道，改善了捷運站的無障礙程度。"},{"w":"have access to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be able to use or get something","c":"能夠使用／取得","s":"Children in remote mountain areas often do not have access to fast internet, which makes online learning very difficult for them.","t":"偏遠山區的孩子常常無法取得快速的網路，這讓線上學習對他們來說非常困難。"},{"w":"accommodate","p":"v.","d":"to provide enough space or rooms for people","c":"容納；為…提供住宿","s":"The new hotel near the station can accommodate up to five hundred guests, so it is popular with large tour groups from Japan.","t":"車站附近的新飯店最多可容納五百位客人，所以很受日本大型旅行團的歡迎。","h":1},{"w":"accommodate","p":"v.","d":"to change your plans or actions to fit someone's needs","c":"配合；遷就","s":"The restaurant is happy to accommodate customers with special diets, so you can ask for a dish without meat or nuts.","t":"這家餐廳很樂意配合有特殊飲食需求的顧客，所以你可以要求不含肉或堅果的餐點。","h":1},{"w":"accommodation","p":"n.","d":"a place to live or stay, such as a hotel room","c":"住宿；住處","s":"The school trip includes accommodation in a small hotel by the lake, and the students will share rooms in groups of four.","t":"校外教學包含湖邊小旅館的住宿，學生將四人一組共用房間。"},{"w":"accommodating","p":"adj.","d":"willing to help and to do what others ask","c":"樂於助人的；通融的","s":"Our host family in Canada was very accommodating; they even drove me to the airport at five in the morning on my last day.","t":"我們在加拿大的寄宿家庭非常通融；他們甚至在我最後一天早上五點開車送我去機場。"},{"w":"accord","p":"n.","d":"an official agreement between countries or groups","c":"協議；協定","s":"The two countries signed a peace accord last year, and the soldiers on both sides of the border finally went home.","t":"兩國去年簽署了和平協議，邊界兩側的士兵終於回家了。","h":1},{"w":"accord with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the same as or to agree with something","c":"與…一致；符合","s":"The witness's story did not accord with the video from the security camera, so the police asked her more questions.","t":"證人的說法與監視器的影片不一致，所以警方問了她更多問題。"},{"w":"in accordance with","p":"phr.","d":"following a rule, law, or wish","c":"依照；根據","s":"All the fire exits in the building were checked in accordance with the new safety law before the shopping mall opened.","t":"購物中心開幕前，大樓內所有的逃生出口都依照新的安全法規進行了檢查。"},{"w":"of one's own accord","p":"phr.","d":"without being asked or forced","c":"自願地；主動地","s":"Nobody told the boy to clean the classroom; he did it of his own accord because he wanted to surprise the teacher.","t":"沒有人叫那個男孩打掃教室；他自動自發地做了，因為他想給老師一個驚喜。","a":"of his own accord"},{"w":"according to","p":"phr.","d":"as stated by someone or something","c":"根據；按照","s":"According to the weather report, a typhoon will reach the east coast tomorrow afternoon, so all schools will be closed.","t":"根據氣象報告，颱風明天下午將抵達東海岸，所以所有學校都會停課。","a":"According to"},{"w":"accordingly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is suitable for the situation; therefore","c":"相應地；因此","s":"The teacher knew that half the class had the flu, so she changed the test date accordingly and gave everyone one more week.","t":"老師知道班上有一半的人得了流感，所以她相應地更改了考試日期，多給大家一週。"},{"w":"accounting","p":"n.","d":"the job or study of keeping and checking money records","c":"會計；會計學","s":"My sister chose to study accounting at university because she is good with numbers and wants a stable career after graduation.","t":"我姐姐選擇在大學讀會計，因為她擅長數字，而且希望畢業後有穩定的職業。","h":1},{"w":"account","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement with a bank to keep your money; a record of money","c":"帳戶；帳目","s":"I opened a savings account with the money I earned from my summer job, and I plan to add to it every month.","t":"我用暑期打工賺的錢開了一個儲蓄帳戶，並打算每個月存錢進去。"},{"w":"accountant","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to keep and check money records","c":"會計師","s":"The company hired a new accountant to check its books after the manager noticed that some money was missing.","t":"經理發現有些錢不見後，公司聘請了一位新的會計師來查帳。"},{"w":"account for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to explain the reason for something; to make up a part of","c":"說明…的原因；佔…比例","s":"Tourists from Japan and Korea account for nearly half of all the visitors to this night market during the winter holidays.","t":"寒假期間，來自日本和韓國的遊客佔這個夜市所有遊客的將近一半。"},{"w":"take into account","p":"v.phr.","d":"to consider something when making a decision","c":"考慮到；把…納入考量","s":"When planning the picnic, we need to take into account the fact that two of our friends are allergic to peanuts.","t":"規劃野餐時，我們需要考慮到我們有兩位朋友對花生過敏這件事。"},{"w":"on account of","p":"phr.","d":"because of","c":"因為；由於","s":"The outdoor graduation ceremony was moved into the gym on account of the heavy rain that started early in the morning.","t":"由於一大早就開始下的大雨，戶外畢業典禮移到了體育館舉行。"},{"w":"acknowledge","p":"v.","d":"to accept or admit that something is true","c":"承認","s":"The company finally had to acknowledge that its new phone had a serious battery problem, and it offered every buyer a free repair.","t":"該公司最後不得不承認它的新手機有嚴重的電池問題，並為每位買家提供免費維修。","h":1},{"w":"acknowledge","p":"v.","d":"to show that you have noticed or received something","c":"致意；確認收到","s":"The famous singer smiled and waved to acknowledge the fans who had waited outside the hotel for hours in the rain.","t":"那位知名歌手微笑揮手，向在飯店外冒雨等了好幾個小時的粉絲致意。"},{"w":"acknowledgement","p":"n.","d":"the act of admitting something is true; a statement of thanks","c":"承認；致謝","s":"At the front of the book, the author wrote an acknowledgement to thank her parents and the teacher who first encouraged her to write.","t":"在書的前面，作者寫了一段致謝，感謝她的父母和第一位鼓勵她寫作的老師。"},{"w":"acknowledged","p":"adj.","d":"accepted by most people as being true or excellent","c":"公認的","s":"Professor Lin is an acknowledged expert on earthquakes, and the government often asks for her advice after a big one hits.","t":"林教授是公認的地震專家，大地震發生後政府常常徵詢她的意見。"},{"w":"acquaint","p":"v.","d":"to make someone know about or get used to something","c":"使認識；使熟悉","s":"The first day of training is designed to acquaint new workers with the safety rules and the layout of the factory.","t":"訓練的第一天旨在讓新員工熟悉安全規則和工廠的配置。","h":1},{"w":"acquaintance","p":"n.","d":"a person you know a little but who is not a close friend","c":"熟人；認識的人","s":"He is only an acquaintance from my father's office, so I was surprised when he remembered my name at the party.","t":"他只是我爸爸辦公室的一個熟人，所以當他在派對上記得我的名字時，我很驚訝。"},{"w":"acquaint oneself with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to learn about something so you understand it","c":"熟悉；了解","s":"Before you start the game, please acquaint yourself with the rules, because players who break them will lose points.","t":"開始遊戲之前，請先熟悉規則，因為違規的玩家會被扣分。","a":"acquaint yourself with"},{"w":"be acquainted with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to know a person or a subject a little","c":"認識；熟悉","s":"Are you acquainted with our new neighbor, the tall man who moved into the apartment upstairs last week?","t":"你認識我們的新鄰居嗎？就是上週搬進樓上公寓的那位高個子男士。","a":"acquainted with"},{"w":"acquisition","p":"n.","d":"the act of buying a company or getting something","c":"收購；獲得","s":"The acquisition of the small game company by the tech giant was announced this morning, and its workers are worried about their jobs.","t":"科技巨頭收購那家小型遊戲公司的消息今天早上宣布了，它的員工擔心自己的工作。","h":1},{"w":"acquisition","p":"n.","d":"the process of learning a skill or language","c":"習得；學習","s":"Scientists say that language acquisition is easiest in early childhood, when the brain picks up new sounds without effort.","t":"科學家說語言習得在幼兒時期最容易，那時大腦不費力就能學會新的聲音。"},{"w":"acquire","p":"v.","d":"to get or buy something; to learn a skill","c":"獲得；取得；學會","s":"Over the years, my grandfather managed to acquire a large collection of old coins from markets all over Asia.","t":"多年來，我爺爺從亞洲各地的市場收集到大量的古錢幣。"},{"w":"language acquisition","p":"n.phr.","d":"the process of learning a language","c":"語言習得","s":"Our English teacher studied language acquisition in graduate school, so she knows why listening to stories helps children learn faster.","t":"我們的英文老師在研究所研究語言習得，所以她知道為什麼聽故事能幫助孩子學得更快。"},{"w":"activist","p":"n.","d":"a person who works hard to bring about social or political change","c":"社會運動者；積極分子","s":"The young activist organized a march to ask the government to protect the river from factory pollution.","t":"那位年輕的社運人士組織了一場遊行，要求政府保護河流免受工廠污染。","h":1},{"w":"active","p":"adj.","d":"busy doing things; taking part in something","c":"活躍的；積極的","s":"My grandmother stays active by swimming three times a week and helping at the community garden on weekends.","t":"我奶奶每週游泳三次，週末還在社區菜園幫忙，保持活躍。"},{"w":"activity","p":"n.","d":"something that you do for interest or pleasure; action","c":"活動","s":"Hiking is my favorite weekend activity because it keeps me healthy and lets me enjoy the fresh mountain air.","t":"健行是我最喜歡的週末活動，因為它讓我保持健康，也讓我享受山上的新鮮空氣。"},{"w":"activism","p":"n.","d":"the use of direct action to bring about social or political change","c":"行動主義；社會運動","s":"Online activism has become powerful; a single video can bring thousands of people to a protest within a day.","t":"網路社會運動已經變得很有力量；一支影片就能在一天內讓數千人參加抗議。"},{"w":"actively","p":"adv.","d":"in a busy way; by taking part in something","c":"積極地；活躍地","s":"The school actively encourages students to join clubs, because working with others teaches skills that textbooks cannot.","t":"學校積極鼓勵學生參加社團，因為與他人合作能學到課本教不了的技能。"},{"w":"acute","p":"adj.","d":"very serious or severe; happening suddenly","c":"嚴重的；急性的","s":"The patient was rushed to the hospital with acute stomach pain, and the doctors operated on him that same night.","t":"病人因急性腹痛被緊急送往醫院，醫生當晚就為他動了手術。","h":1},{"w":"acute","p":"adj.","d":"very sharp and quick to notice things","c":"敏銳的","s":"Dogs have an acute sense of smell, which is why the police use them to find missing people in the mountains.","t":"狗有敏銳的嗅覺，這就是為什麼警方用牠們在山區尋找失蹤的人。"},{"w":"acutely","p":"adv.","d":"very strongly; in a way that is clearly felt","c":"強烈地；敏銳地","s":"After moving to a foreign country, she became acutely aware of how much she missed her mother's cooking.","t":"搬到國外後，她強烈地意識到自己有多想念媽媽做的菜。"},{"w":"administration","p":"n.","d":"the management of a company, school, or government","c":"行政；管理；政府","s":"The school administration decided to start classes thirty minutes later so that students could get more sleep in the morning.","t":"學校行政單位決定將上課時間延後三十分鐘，讓學生早上能多睡一點。","h":1},{"w":"administrative","p":"adj.","d":"connected with managing a company, school, or government","c":"行政的；管理的","s":"Teachers complain that they spend too much time on administrative work, such as filling in forms, instead of preparing lessons.","t":"老師們抱怨他們花太多時間在填表格等行政工作上，而不是備課。","h":1},{"w":"administrator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to manage an organization","c":"行政人員；管理者","s":"The hospital administrator announced that a new wing with two hundred beds would be built next to the old building.","t":"醫院管理者宣布將在舊大樓旁興建一座有兩百張病床的新側翼。","h":1},{"w":"administer","p":"v.","d":"to manage or organize something; to give medicine to someone","c":"管理；施行；給藥","s":"The nurse was trained to administer the vaccine safely, and she explained each step to the nervous children.","t":"那位護士受過安全施打疫苗的訓練，她向緊張的孩子們解釋每一個步驟。"},{"w":"school administration","p":"n.phr.","d":"the people who manage a school","c":"學校行政單位","s":"Students who want to start a new club must first write a plan and send it to the school administration for approval.","t":"想成立新社團的學生必須先寫一份計畫，送交學校行政單位核准。"},{"w":"adolescent","p":"n.","d":"a young person who is developing into an adult","c":"青少年","s":"Many an adolescent feels that nobody understands him, so parents should listen patiently instead of giving orders.","t":"許多青少年覺得沒有人了解他，所以父母應該耐心傾聽，而不是下命令。","h":1},{"w":"adolescent","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the time between being a child and an adult","c":"青春期的；青少年的","s":"Doctors say that adolescent boys need more sleep than adults because their bodies and brains are still growing quickly.","t":"醫生說青春期的男孩比成人需要更多睡眠，因為他們的身體和大腦仍在快速成長。"},{"w":"adolescence","p":"n.","d":"the period of life between being a child and an adult","c":"青春期","s":"During adolescence, many teenagers worry a lot about how they look and what their classmates think of them.","t":"在青春期，許多青少年非常在意自己的外表以及同學對他們的看法。"},{"w":"adore","p":"v.","d":"to love someone or something very much","c":"熱愛；崇拜","s":"The children adore their grandfather because he tells funny stories and always keeps candy in his pocket.","t":"孩子們非常愛他們的爺爺，因為他會講好笑的故事，口袋裡總是有糖果。","h":1},{"w":"adorable","p":"adj.","d":"very attractive and easy to love","c":"可愛的；討人喜歡的","s":"The adorable puppy followed me around the pet shop, and I could not leave without taking him home.","t":"那隻可愛的小狗在寵物店裡一直跟著我，我沒辦法不帶牠回家就離開。"},{"w":"adoration","p":"n.","d":"great love and respect","c":"崇拜；愛慕","s":"The young fans screamed with adoration when the singer walked onto the stage and waved at the crowd.","t":"當歌手走上舞台向群眾揮手時，年輕的粉絲們崇拜地尖叫起來。"},{"w":"adoring","p":"adj.","d":"showing great love","c":"充滿愛意的；崇拜的","s":"The new mother looked at her baby with adoring eyes and softly sang the song her own mother used to sing.","t":"新手媽媽用充滿愛意的眼神看著她的寶寶，輕聲唱著她母親以前唱的歌。"},{"w":"adverse","p":"adj.","d":"bad or harmful; going against what you want","c":"不利的；有害的","s":"The new medicine may have adverse effects on some patients, so the doctor asked my mother to report any headache or dizziness.","t":"這種新藥可能對某些病人產生不良影響，所以醫生要我媽媽回報任何頭痛或頭暈。","h":1},{"w":"adverse weather conditions","p":"n.phr.","d":"bad weather that makes an activity difficult or dangerous","c":"惡劣的天氣狀況","s":"All flights to Hong Kong were canceled this morning because of adverse weather conditions, and hundreds of passengers slept at the airport.","t":"由於惡劣的天氣狀況，今天早上所有飛往香港的航班都取消了，數百名乘客在機場過夜。"},{"w":"adversely","p":"adv.","d":"in a harmful or negative way","c":"不利地；有害地","s":"Staying up late every night can adversely affect your memory, which is why students should not study until two in the morning.","t":"每晚熬夜會不利地影響你的記憶力，這就是為什麼學生不應該讀書讀到凌晨兩點。"},{"w":"adversity","p":"n.","d":"a difficult or unlucky situation","c":"逆境；困境","s":"The story of the young farmer who kept going in the face of adversity inspired the whole village to rebuild after the flood.","t":"那位年輕農夫在逆境中堅持不懈的故事，激勵了全村在水災後重建家園。"},{"w":"advocate","p":"v.","d":"to publicly support an idea or plan","c":"提倡；主張","s":"Many doctors advocate a diet with more vegetables and less sugar, because it helps prevent heart disease and diabetes.","t":"許多醫生提倡多蔬菜、少糖的飲食，因為它有助於預防心臟病和糖尿病。","h":1},{"w":"advocate","p":"n.","d":"a person who publicly supports an idea or group","c":"提倡者；擁護者","s":"She is a strong advocate for animal rights and spends every weekend at the shelter looking after abandoned cats.","t":"她是動物權利的堅定擁護者，每個週末都在收容所照顧被遺棄的貓。"},{"w":"advocacy","p":"n.","d":"public support for an idea or a group of people","c":"提倡；倡議","s":"The group's advocacy for safer bicycle lanes finally paid off when the city built a new path along the river.","t":"該團體對更安全自行車道的倡議終於有了成果，市政府沿河修建了一條新車道。"},{"w":"an advocate of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who supports a particular idea","c":"…的提倡者","s":"My uncle is an advocate of early rising; he says a person who gets up at five can finish more before noon than others do all day.","t":"我叔叔是早起的提倡者；他說五點起床的人在中午前完成的事，比別人一整天做的還多。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"affection – apt","cards":[{"w":"affection","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of liking or loving someone","c":"喜愛；感情","s":"My grandmother shows her affection for us by cooking our favorite dishes whenever we visit her on weekends.","t":"我奶奶每當我們週末去看她時，就煮我們最愛吃的菜，以此表達她對我們的喜愛。","h":1},{"w":"affectionate","p":"adj.","d":"showing love and caring","c":"充滿感情的；深情的","s":"The old man was so affectionate toward his dog that he talked to it as if it were a child.","t":"那位老先生對他的狗充滿感情，他跟牠說話的樣子就像在跟小孩說話一樣。"},{"w":"affectionately","p":"adv.","d":"in a loving way","c":"深情地；親暱地","s":"She affectionately patted her son's head and told him not to worry about the test results.","t":"她親暱地拍拍兒子的頭，告訴他不要擔心考試成績。"},{"w":"affect","p":"v.","d":"to have an influence on someone or something","c":"影響","s":"The heavy rain will affect the outdoor concert tonight, so the organizers may move it into the gym.","t":"大雨會影響今晚的戶外演唱會，所以主辦單位可能會把它移到體育館舉行。"},{"w":"have affection for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to like or love someone","c":"對…有感情；喜愛","s":"Many people in the village have affection for the old teacher, who taught three generations of children to read.","t":"村裡許多人都很喜愛那位老老師，他教了三代的孩子識字。"},{"w":"agenda","p":"n.","d":"a list of things to discuss at a meeting","c":"議程","s":"The first item on the agenda for today's class meeting is how to raise money for our graduation trip.","t":"今天班會議程的第一項是如何為我們的畢業旅行籌錢。","h":1},{"w":"on the agenda","p":"phr.","d":"planned to be discussed or done","c":"在議程上；列入計畫","s":"A new sports hall is on the agenda this year, but the school still needs to find the money to build it.","t":"新的體育館今年已列入計畫，但學校仍需要找到蓋它的經費。"},{"w":"hidden agenda","p":"n.phr.","d":"a secret reason for doing something","c":"不可告人的目的","s":"Some students suspected that the principal had a hidden agenda when he suddenly offered free pizza before the vote.","t":"有些學生懷疑校長在投票前突然請大家吃免費披薩是有不可告人的目的。"},{"w":"set the agenda","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide what will be discussed or done","c":"主導議題；設定議程","s":"The club president likes to set the agenda herself, so the members rarely get a chance to raise their own ideas.","t":"社長喜歡自己設定議程，所以社員很少有機會提出自己的想法。"},{"w":"aggression","p":"n.","d":"angry or violent behavior toward others","c":"侵略；攻擊性","s":"The zookeeper warned us that the monkeys may show aggression if visitors stare at them or try to touch them.","t":"動物園管理員警告我們，如果遊客盯著猴子看或想摸牠們，猴子可能會表現出攻擊性。","h":1},{"w":"aggressive","p":"adj.","d":"angry and ready to attack","c":"好鬥的；攻擊性的","s":"The dog became aggressive when the stranger walked into the yard, so the owner had to hold it back.","t":"當陌生人走進院子時，那隻狗變得有攻擊性，所以主人必須把牠拉住。"},{"w":"aggressive","p":"adj.","d":"determined and forceful in order to succeed","c":"積極進取的","s":"Our new sales manager is very aggressive and expects the team to double its sales before the end of the year.","t":"我們的新業務經理非常積極進取，期望團隊在年底前讓業績翻倍。"},{"w":"aggressively","p":"adv.","d":"in an angry or forceful way","c":"攻擊性地；積極地","s":"The driver honked aggressively at the cyclist, who had stopped in the middle of the road to answer his phone.","t":"那名駕駛兇狠地對騎單車的人按喇叭，因為他停在馬路中間接電話。"},{"w":"aggressor","p":"n.","d":"a person or country that starts a fight or war","c":"侵略者；攻擊者","s":"In the history class we discussed which country was the aggressor in the war and how it changed the map of Europe.","t":"在歷史課上，我們討論了哪個國家是那場戰爭的侵略者，以及它如何改變了歐洲的版圖。"},{"w":"agony","p":"n.","d":"very great pain or suffering","c":"極大的痛苦","s":"The runner was in agony after he twisted his ankle, and the medical team carried him off the track.","t":"那名跑者扭傷腳踝後痛苦不堪，醫療團隊把他抬離跑道。","h":1},{"w":"agonize","p":"v.","d":"to spend a long time worrying about a decision","c":"苦惱；極度焦慮","s":"Don't agonize over which university to choose; both of them have good programs for someone with your interests.","t":"別為了選哪所大學而苦惱；對有你這種興趣的人來說，這兩所都有很好的課程。"},{"w":"agonizing","p":"adj.","d":"causing great pain or worry","c":"令人痛苦的；折磨人的","s":"Waiting for the exam results was an agonizing week for my brother, who checked the website every hour.","t":"等待考試成績的那一週對我哥哥來說極為煎熬，他每小時都去看網站。"},{"w":"in agony","p":"phr.","d":"in great pain","c":"痛苦不堪","s":"The patient lay in agony on the floor until the ambulance arrived, so the nurse gave him a shot right away.","t":"病人痛苦地躺在地板上直到救護車抵達，所以護士立刻幫他打了一針。"},{"w":"agricultural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with farming","c":"農業的","s":"Most of the people in this agricultural area grow rice or vegetables, and their children help in the fields after school.","t":"這個農業地區的大多數人種稻米或蔬菜，他們的孩子放學後會到田裡幫忙。","h":1},{"w":"agriculture","p":"n.","d":"the science or practice of farming","c":"農業","s":"Taiwan's agriculture has changed a lot over the last fifty years, as farmers now use machines and sell their fruit abroad.","t":"台灣的農業在過去五十年改變很大，農民現在使用機器，並把水果賣到國外。"},{"w":"agricultural products","p":"n.phr.","d":"things that are grown on farms","c":"農產品","s":"The night market sells fresh agricultural products from nearby farms, such as sweet corn, bananas, and homemade honey.","t":"夜市販售來自附近農場的新鮮農產品，例如甜玉米、香蕉和自製蜂蜜。"},{"w":"aisle","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow passage between rows of seats or shelves","c":"走道","s":"Please keep your bags out of the aisle on the bus so that other passengers can walk to the back safely.","t":"請不要把包包放在公車走道上，這樣其他乘客才能安全地走到後面。","h":1},{"w":"aisle seat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a seat next to the passage on a plane or bus","c":"靠走道的座位","s":"I always ask for an aisle seat on long flights because I like to stand up and stretch without disturbing anyone.","t":"長途飛行時我總是要求靠走道的座位，因為我喜歡站起來伸展而不打擾別人。"},{"w":"walk down the aisle","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get married","c":"步入禮堂；結婚","s":"My cousin will walk down the aisle next month, and the whole family is flying to Kaohsiung for the wedding.","t":"我表姊下個月就要步入禮堂，全家人都要飛去高雄參加婚禮。"},{"w":"alcoholic","p":"adj.","d":"containing alcohol","c":"含酒精的","s":"The restaurant does not serve alcoholic drinks to anyone under eighteen, so the waiter asked to see my brother's ID.","t":"這家餐廳不提供含酒精的飲料給十八歲以下的人，所以服務生要求看我哥哥的身分證。","h":1},{"w":"alcoholic","p":"n.","d":"a person who cannot stop drinking alcohol","c":"酗酒者","s":"After years of heavy drinking, he finally admitted that he was an alcoholic and joined a support group for help.","t":"多年酗酒之後，他終於承認自己是個酗酒者，並加入了互助團體尋求幫助。"},{"w":"alcohol","p":"n.","d":"drinks such as beer and wine that can make people drunk","c":"酒；酒精","s":"Drinking alcohol and then driving is illegal in Taiwan, and the police set up checkpoints on weekend nights.","t":"在台灣喝酒後開車是違法的，警察會在週末晚上設置臨檢點。"},{"w":"alcoholism","p":"n.","d":"the medical condition of being unable to stop drinking alcohol","c":"酗酒（病）；酒精中毒","s":"Alcoholism can destroy a family, which is why the hospital runs a free program to help people stop drinking.","t":"酗酒可能毀掉一個家庭，這就是為什麼醫院開辦免費課程幫助人們戒酒。","a":"Alcoholism"},{"w":"non-alcoholic","p":"adj.","d":"not containing alcohol","c":"無酒精的","s":"The café offers several non-alcoholic cocktails made with fresh fruit, so teenagers can enjoy something special at the party.","t":"這家咖啡館提供數款用新鮮水果調製的無酒精雞尾酒，所以青少年在派對上也能享受特別的飲品。"},{"w":"alien","p":"n.","d":"a creature from another planet","c":"外星人","s":"In the movie, a friendly alien lands in a small town and learns to speak English by watching television.","t":"電影裡，一個友善的外星人降落在小鎮上，靠看電視學會說英語。","h":1},{"w":"alien","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a country but is not a citizen of it","c":"外國人；外僑","s":"Every alien who works in the country must carry a resident card and show it to the police when asked.","t":"每位在該國工作的外僑都必須攜帶居留證，並在警察要求時出示。"},{"w":"alien","p":"adj.","d":"strange and unfamiliar","c":"陌生的；外來的","s":"Eating with chopsticks was completely alien to our American guests, so we gave them forks after a few minutes.","t":"用筷子吃飯對我們的美國客人來說完全陌生，所以幾分鐘後我們就給了他們叉子。"},{"w":"alienate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel they do not belong or are not liked","c":"使疏遠","s":"The coach's harsh words began to alienate the younger players, and two of them quit the team.","t":"教練嚴厲的話開始疏遠年輕球員，其中兩人退出了球隊。"},{"w":"alien species","p":"n.phr.","d":"a plant or animal that does not naturally belong in a place","c":"外來物種","s":"The pond was filled with an alien species of fish that eats the eggs of the local frogs, so volunteers removed them.","t":"池塘裡滿是一種會吃本地青蛙卵的外來物種魚類，所以志工把牠們移走了。"},{"w":"allergic","p":"adj.","d":"having a bad physical reaction to a food, animal, or substance","c":"過敏的","s":"My sister is allergic to cats, so her eyes become red and itchy whenever she visits our neighbor's house.","t":"我姊姊對貓過敏，所以每次去鄰居家，她的眼睛就會又紅又癢。","h":1},{"w":"allergy","p":"n.","d":"a medical condition in which the body reacts badly to something","c":"過敏","s":"Because of his peanut allergy, the boy always reads the label carefully before he eats any cookies or candy.","t":"因為對花生過敏，那個男孩在吃任何餅乾或糖果前總是仔細閱讀標籤。","h":1},{"w":"be allergic to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have an allergy to something","c":"對…過敏","s":"Please tell the waiter if you are allergic to seafood, because many dishes here are cooked with shrimp paste.","t":"如果你對海鮮過敏，請告訴服務生，因為這裡許多菜都是用蝦醬烹調的。","a":"are allergic to"},{"w":"allergic reaction","p":"n.phr.","d":"the body's bad response to something it is allergic to","c":"過敏反應","s":"The nurse gave the student a shot right away because he was having a serious allergic reaction to a bee sting.","t":"護士立刻幫那名學生打針，因為他被蜜蜂螫到後出現嚴重的過敏反應。"},{"w":"alliance","p":"n.","d":"an agreement between countries or groups to work together","c":"聯盟；同盟","s":"The two small companies formed an alliance so that they could compete with the giant chain stores in the city.","t":"這兩家小公司組成聯盟，以便能與市內的大型連鎖商店競爭。","h":1},{"w":"ally","p":"n.","d":"a country or person that helps and supports another","c":"盟友；盟國","s":"During the war, Britain was a close ally of the United States, and the two countries shared their secrets.","t":"戰爭期間，英國是美國親密的盟友，兩國共享彼此的機密。","h":1},{"w":"ally with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to join with someone in order to get something done","c":"與…結盟","s":"The small parties decided to ally with each other before the election so that their voices would be heard.","t":"幾個小黨決定在選舉前彼此結盟，這樣他們的聲音才會被聽見。"},{"w":"allied","p":"adj.","d":"joined together for a shared purpose","c":"同盟的；聯合的","s":"The allied forces landed on the beaches of France in 1944 and began to push the enemy army back.","t":"盟軍部隊於一九四四年在法國海灘登陸，開始把敵軍逼退。"},{"w":"in alliance with","p":"phr.","d":"working together with","c":"與…結盟；與…合作","s":"The university is working in alliance with several hospitals to train more nurses for the aging population.","t":"這所大學正與幾家醫院合作，為高齡化社會培訓更多護理師。"},{"w":"allocate","p":"v.","d":"to give money, time, or space to someone or something for a purpose","c":"分配；撥出","s":"The city will allocate more money to public libraries next year so that they can stay open on Sundays.","t":"市政府明年將撥更多經費給公立圖書館，讓它們週日也能開放。","h":1},{"w":"allocation","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something given for a purpose","c":"分配；配額","s":"Each class received an allocation of five hundred dollars for the school fair, and we spent most of it on paint.","t":"每個班級都獲得五百元的園遊會經費配額，我們大部分都花在顏料上。"},{"w":"be allocated to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be given to someone or something as a share","c":"被分配給","s":"Half of the budget was allocated to new computers, and the rest will pay for the teachers' summer training.","t":"一半的預算被分配給新電腦，其餘的將用來支付老師的暑期培訓。","a":"was allocated to"},{"w":"alongside","p":"prep.","d":"next to the side of something","c":"在…旁邊","s":"The little boat tied up alongside the ferry, and the fishermen passed their baskets of fish up to the deck.","t":"小船停靠在渡輪旁邊，漁夫們把一籃籃的魚遞上甲板。","h":1},{"w":"alongside","p":"prep.","d":"together with someone","c":"與…一起","s":"Our teacher worked alongside the students all afternoon to clean the beach before the typhoon arrived.","t":"颱風來臨前，我們的老師整個下午和學生一起清理海灘。"},{"w":"alongside","p":"adv.","d":"beside something, at its side","c":"在旁邊","s":"The police car drove alongside for a few minutes and then signaled the truck driver to pull over.","t":"警車在旁邊行駛了幾分鐘，然後示意卡車司機靠邊停車。"},{"w":"work alongside","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work together with someone","c":"與…並肩工作","s":"During the summer, the interns work alongside real engineers and learn how a bridge is designed from start to finish.","t":"暑假期間，實習生與真正的工程師並肩工作，學習一座橋從頭到尾是如何設計的。"},{"w":"alter","p":"v.","d":"to change something","c":"改變；更改","s":"The airline had to alter its schedule because of the storm, and our flight now leaves two hours later.","t":"航空公司因暴風雨不得不更改班表，我們的航班現在延後兩小時起飛。","h":1},{"w":"alter","p":"v.","d":"to make a piece of clothing fit better","c":"修改（衣服）","s":"The tailor can alter the dress so that it fits you better, but it will take about a week.","t":"裁縫可以修改這件洋裝讓它更合身，但大約需要一個星期。"},{"w":"alteration","p":"n.","d":"a change made to something","c":"改變；修改","s":"The teacher made a small alteration to the exam schedule, moving the English test from Monday to Wednesday.","t":"老師對考試時間表做了一個小更動，把英文考試從星期一改到星期三。"},{"w":"unaltered","p":"adj.","d":"not changed","c":"未改變的","s":"The old temple has remained unaltered for three hundred years, even though the town around it has changed completely.","t":"這座老廟三百年來一直保持原貌，即使周圍的城鎮已完全改變。"},{"w":"alternate","p":"adj.","d":"happening in turns; every other","c":"交替的；間隔的","s":"The two sisters take turns cooking on alternate days, so each of them gets a free evening every second night.","t":"兩姊妹隔天輪流煮飯，所以每人每隔一晚就有一個自由的夜晚。","h":1},{"w":"alternate","p":"v.","d":"to happen or do something in turns","c":"輪流；交替","s":"The weather this week will alternate between sunshine and heavy showers, so keep an umbrella in your bag.","t":"這星期的天氣將在晴天和大雨之間交替，所以包包裡要放把傘。"},{"w":"alternate","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes the place of another when needed","c":"候補者；替代者","s":"Each team may bring one alternate to the contest in case a member gets sick on the day of the final.","t":"每隊可以帶一名候補參加比賽，以防有隊員在決賽當天生病。"},{"w":"alternative","p":"n.","d":"another choice or possibility","c":"替代方案；選擇","s":"If the train is full, the only alternative is to take the night bus, which stops at every small town.","t":"如果火車客滿，唯一的替代方案就是搭夜間巴士，但它每個小鎮都停。"},{"w":"alternatively","p":"adv.","d":"used to give another choice","c":"或者；要不然","s":"You can pay for the tickets online, or alternatively you can buy them at the counter an hour before the show.","t":"你可以在線上付款買票，或者你也可以在開演前一小時到櫃檯購買。"},{"w":"amend","p":"v.","d":"to change a law or document in order to improve it","c":"修正；修訂","s":"The government plans to amend the traffic law so that drivers who use phones will pay a much higher fine.","t":"政府計畫修訂交通法規，讓開車用手機的駕駛付出高得多的罰款。","h":1},{"w":"amendment","p":"n.","d":"a change made to a law or document","c":"修正案；修改","s":"The students proposed an amendment to the dress code that would allow them to wear sneakers on hot days.","t":"學生們對服裝規定提出一項修正案，允許他們在炎熱的日子穿運動鞋。"},{"w":"make amends","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something to show you are sorry for hurting someone","c":"彌補；賠罪","s":"After breaking his friend's camera, Tom tried to make amends by paying for the repair and buying him lunch.","t":"弄壞朋友的相機之後，湯姆試著付修理費並請他吃午餐來彌補。"},{"w":"ample","p":"adj.","d":"enough or more than enough","c":"充足的；充裕的","s":"There is ample parking space behind the restaurant, so you do not need to worry about finding a spot.","t":"餐廳後面有充足的停車位，所以你不必擔心找不到車位。","h":1},{"w":"amply","p":"adv.","d":"more than enough; fully","c":"充分地；足夠地","s":"Her hard work was amply rewarded when she won first prize and a scholarship to study in Japan.","t":"她的努力得到了充分的回報，她贏得了第一名和赴日留學的獎學金。"},{"w":"ample time","p":"n.phr.","d":"more than enough time","c":"充足的時間","s":"We left home at six, which gave us ample time to find the test center and relax before the exam began.","t":"我們六點就出門，這讓我們有充足的時間找到考場，並在考試開始前放鬆一下。"},{"w":"analyst","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to study information carefully and explain it","c":"分析師","s":"A financial analyst on TV said that housing prices in Taipei will keep rising unless the government takes action.","t":"電視上一位金融分析師說，除非政府採取行動，否則台北的房價會持續上漲。","h":1},{"w":"analyze","p":"v.","d":"to study something carefully in order to understand it","c":"分析","s":"In science class we learned how to analyze the data from our experiment and draw a graph of the results.","t":"在自然課上，我們學會如何分析實驗的數據，並畫出結果的圖表。"},{"w":"analysis","p":"n.","d":"a careful study of something to understand it","c":"分析","s":"The doctor sent a blood sample to the lab for analysis, and the results will be ready in two days.","t":"醫生把血液樣本送到實驗室分析，結果兩天後就會出來。"},{"w":"analytical","p":"adj.","d":"good at examining things carefully and logically","c":"分析的；善於分析的","s":"Ben has a very analytical mind; he likes to break every problem into small parts before trying to solve it.","t":"班有非常善於分析的頭腦；他喜歡先把每個問題拆成小部分，再試著解決。"},{"w":"data analyst","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who studies numbers and information for a company","c":"資料分析師","s":"My cousin works as a data analyst for an online shop and studies what customers buy at different times of the year.","t":"我表哥在一家網路商店擔任資料分析師，研究顧客在一年中不同時期購買的東西。"},{"w":"anonymous","p":"adj.","d":"with the name not known or not given","c":"匿名的","s":"An anonymous donor gave the school one million dollars for a new library, and nobody knows who it was.","t":"一位匿名捐款人捐給學校一百萬元蓋新圖書館，沒有人知道那是誰。","h":1},{"w":"anonymously","p":"adv.","d":"without giving your name","c":"匿名地","s":"Students can report bullying anonymously by dropping a note into the box outside the counselor's office.","t":"學生可以把紙條投入輔導室外的箱子，匿名通報霸凌事件。"},{"w":"anonymity","p":"n.","d":"the state of not having your name known","c":"匿名（性）","s":"The witness asked for anonymity because she was afraid the gang would find her if her name appeared in the news.","t":"證人要求匿名，因為她害怕如果名字出現在新聞上，幫派會找到她。"},{"w":"remain anonymous","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep your name unknown","c":"保持匿名","s":"The man who found the lost wallet wished to remain anonymous, so the police simply thanked him in the newspaper.","t":"撿到遺失錢包的那位男士希望保持匿名，所以警方只在報上向他致謝。"},{"w":"anticipate","p":"v.","d":"to expect that something will happen","c":"預期；預料","s":"The store did not anticipate such a big crowd on opening day, so it ran out of free gifts within an hour.","t":"這家店沒有預料到開幕當天會有這麼多人，所以不到一小時免費贈品就發完了。","h":1},{"w":"anticipation","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of excitement about something that is going to happen","c":"期待；預期","s":"The children waited in anticipation for the magician to open the box, and they screamed when a rabbit jumped out.","t":"孩子們滿心期待地等著魔術師打開箱子，當一隻兔子跳出來時，他們尖叫起來。"},{"w":"anticipated","p":"adj.","d":"expected and waited for","c":"預期的；備受期待的","s":"Tickets for the eagerly anticipated concert sold out in ten minutes, and some fans are now paying double on the internet.","t":"這場備受期待的演唱會門票十分鐘內就賣光了，有些粉絲現在在網路上付雙倍的價錢買票。"},{"w":"unanticipated","p":"adj.","d":"not expected","c":"未預料到的；意外的","s":"An unanticipated problem with the sound system delayed the graduation ceremony by nearly half an hour.","t":"音響系統一個意料之外的問題讓畢業典禮延遲了將近半小時。"},{"w":"antique","p":"n.","d":"an old and valuable object","c":"古董","s":"My grandfather's clock is a real antique; it was made in Germany more than one hundred and fifty years ago.","t":"我爺爺的時鐘是真正的古董；它是一百五十多年前在德國製造的。","h":1},{"w":"antique","p":"adj.","d":"old and valuable","c":"古老的；古董的","s":"She bought an antique wooden table at the weekend market and spent two days cleaning and polishing it.","t":"她在週末市集買了一張古董木桌，花了兩天清理和打磨它。"},{"w":"antique shop","p":"n.phr.","d":"a store that sells old and valuable things","c":"古董店","s":"There is a small antique shop near the temple where you can find old coins, teapots, and black-and-white photographs.","t":"廟附近有一家小古董店，你可以在那裡找到舊硬幣、茶壺和黑白照片。"},{"w":"antiquity","p":"n.","d":"ancient times, especially long ago in history","c":"古代","s":"The museum has a special room for objects from antiquity, including tools that are more than five thousand years old.","t":"博物館有一個專門展示古代文物的展廳，包括五千多年前的工具。"},{"w":"applause","p":"n.","d":"the sound of people clapping their hands to show they like something","c":"掌聲","s":"When the little girl finished her violin solo, the applause was so loud that she had to play one more song.","t":"當小女孩拉完小提琴獨奏時，掌聲如雷，她只好再演奏一曲。","h":1},{"w":"applaud","p":"v.","d":"to clap your hands to show you like something","c":"鼓掌","s":"The audience stood up to applaud the actors at the end of the play, and some people even threw flowers.","t":"戲劇結束時，觀眾起立為演員鼓掌，有些人甚至丟出鮮花。"},{"w":"applaud","p":"v.","d":"to say that you approve of something","c":"讚許；稱讚","s":"Teachers applaud the city's decision to open the libraries later at night during the exam season.","t":"老師們讚許市政府在考季期間延長圖書館夜間開放時間的決定。"},{"w":"a round of applause","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short period of clapping","c":"一陣掌聲","s":"Let's give a round of applause to the volunteers who cleaned the park all weekend while the rest of us were resting.","t":"讓我們給整個週末都在清理公園、而我們其他人在休息的志工們一陣掌聲。"},{"w":"appliance","p":"n.","d":"a machine used in the home, such as a washing machine","c":"家用電器","s":"The washing machine is the one appliance in our apartment that we cannot live without, especially in the rainy season.","t":"洗衣機是我們公寓裡最不能缺少的家電，尤其是在雨季。","h":1},{"w":"apply","p":"v.","d":"to ask officially for something, such as a job or a card","c":"申請","s":"You can apply for a library card online by filling in a short form and uploading a photo of your ID.","t":"你可以在網路上填寫簡短的表格並上傳身分證照片來申請借書證。"},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"an official request for something; a computer program","c":"申請；應用程式","s":"I sent my application for the summer camp two weeks ago, but I have not received any reply from them yet.","t":"我兩個星期前就寄出了夏令營的申請，但到現在還沒收到任何回覆。"},{"w":"home appliance","p":"n.phr.","d":"an electrical machine used in the house","c":"家電","s":"The store is having a big sale on every home appliance, so my parents are going to buy a new refrigerator.","t":"這家店所有家電都在大特價，所以我爸媽打算買一台新冰箱。"},{"w":"applicable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used in a particular situation","c":"適用的","s":"The discount is only applicable to students, so remember to bring your student card when you buy the tickets.","t":"這個折扣只適用於學生，所以買票時記得帶學生證。"},{"w":"apt","p":"adj.","d":"likely to do something","c":"易於…的；有…傾向的","s":"Young children are apt to forget their lunch boxes, so the teacher checks their bags before they leave the classroom.","t":"小孩子容易忘記帶便當盒，所以老師在他們離開教室前會檢查書包。","h":1},{"w":"apt","p":"adj.","d":"suitable or exactly right for the situation","c":"恰當的；貼切的","s":"The title of the movie is very apt, because the story really is about a long journey home.","t":"這部電影的片名非常貼切，因為故事真的是關於一段漫長的回家之路。"},{"w":"aptly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is suitable or exactly right","c":"恰當地；貼切地","s":"The restaurant is aptly named 'Grandma's Kitchen', since every dish tastes like something your grandmother would cook.","t":"這家餐廳被貼切地取名為「奶奶的廚房」，因為每道菜嘗起來都像你奶奶會做的菜。"},{"w":"aptitude","p":"n.","d":"natural ability to do something well","c":"天資；才能","s":"Lily showed an early aptitude for music, and she could play simple songs on the piano at the age of four.","t":"莉莉很早就展現出音樂天分，她四歲時就能在鋼琴上彈簡單的曲子。"},{"w":"be apt to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be likely to do something","c":"容易；往往會","s":"My father is apt to fall asleep in front of the TV after dinner, so we always turn it off for him.","t":"我爸爸晚餐後往往會在電視機前睡著，所以我們總是幫他把電視關掉。","a":"is apt to"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"architect – ballot","cards":[{"w":"architect","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to design buildings","c":"建築師","s":"The architect showed us a model of the new library, which will have a garden on its roof and large glass walls.","t":"建築師給我們看新圖書館的模型，它的屋頂將有一座花園，還有大片的玻璃牆。","h":1},{"w":"architecture","p":"n.","d":"the art of designing buildings; the style of a building","c":"建築；建築學","s":"My sister is studying architecture at university because she dreams of designing houses that use less energy.","t":"我姊姊在大學讀建築，因為她夢想設計更省能源的房子。","h":1},{"w":"architectural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the design of buildings","c":"建築的","s":"Taipei 101 is an architectural wonder; its design was inspired by bamboo, which bends in the wind but does not break.","t":"台北101是一個建築奇蹟；它的設計靈感來自竹子，竹子在風中會彎但不會斷。"},{"w":"landscape architect","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who designs parks and gardens","c":"景觀設計師","s":"The city hired a landscape architect to turn the old parking lot into a park with trees, a pond, and walking paths.","t":"市政府聘請一位景觀設計師，把舊停車場變成有樹木、池塘和步道的公園。"},{"w":"arena","p":"n.","d":"a large building where sports or concerts are held","c":"競技場；體育館","s":"The new arena can hold twenty thousand people, and the first event there will be a basketball game next month.","t":"新體育館可容納兩萬人，那裡的第一場活動將是下個月的籃球賽。","h":1},{"w":"arena","p":"n.","d":"an area of activity, such as politics or business","c":"領域；舞台","s":"She entered the political arena at the age of thirty and became the youngest mayor in the city's history.","t":"她三十歲進入政治舞台，成為這座城市史上最年輕的市長。"},{"w":"sports arena","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large building for sports events","c":"體育館；運動場館","s":"The old sports arena near the station will be torn down, and a shopping mall will be built on the land.","t":"車站附近的舊體育館將被拆除，那塊地上將蓋一座購物中心。"},{"w":"arouse","p":"v.","d":"to cause a feeling or interest in someone","c":"引起；激起","s":"The strange noise in the attic began to arouse my curiosity, so I took a flashlight and went upstairs to look.","t":"閣樓裡奇怪的聲音開始引起我的好奇心，所以我拿了手電筒上樓去看。","h":1},{"w":"arouse suspicion","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people think something is wrong","c":"引起懷疑","s":"The man's nervous behavior at the airport started to arouse suspicion, so the officers asked to look inside his bag.","t":"那名男子在機場緊張的舉動開始引起懷疑，所以官員要求檢查他的包包。"},{"w":"arouse interest","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people interested","c":"引起興趣","s":"The short video aroused interest in the school's new robot club, and forty students signed up in the first week.","t":"那支短片引起大家對學校新機器人社團的興趣，第一週就有四十名學生報名。","a":"aroused interest"},{"w":"array","p":"n.","d":"a large group or collection of things","c":"大批；一系列","s":"The night market offers an array of snacks, from fried chicken and stinky tofu to bubble tea and shaved ice.","t":"夜市提供一系列的小吃，從炸雞、臭豆腐到珍珠奶茶和剉冰都有。","h":1},{"w":"an array of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large number or variety of","c":"一系列的；大量的","s":"The store sells an array of phone cases in every color, so it took me twenty minutes to choose one.","t":"這家店賣各式各樣的手機殼，顏色齊全，所以我花了二十分鐘才選好一個。"},{"w":"array","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things in an orderly way","c":"排列；陳列","s":"The soldiers were arrayed in neat rows in front of the palace, waiting for the king to appear.","t":"士兵們整齊地排列在宮殿前，等待國王現身。","a":"arrayed"},{"w":"arrogant","p":"adj.","d":"believing you are better or more important than others","c":"傲慢的；自大的","s":"The new student seemed arrogant at first because he never listened to anyone, but he was just shy.","t":"新同學一開始看起來很傲慢，因為他從不聽別人說話，但其實他只是害羞。","h":1},{"w":"arrogance","p":"n.","d":"the quality of believing you are better than others","c":"傲慢；自大","s":"His arrogance cost him the election; voters did not like a man who thought he was never wrong.","t":"他的傲慢讓他輸掉了選舉；選民不喜歡一個自以為永遠不會錯的人。"},{"w":"arrogantly","p":"adv.","d":"in a proud and rude way","c":"傲慢地","s":"The champion arrogantly told reporters that nobody in the world could beat him, and he lost the very next day.","t":"那位冠軍傲慢地告訴記者世界上沒有人能打敗他，結果第二天就輸了。"},{"w":"articulate","p":"v.","d":"to express your thoughts or feelings clearly in words","c":"清楚表達","s":"It is hard for small children to articulate their feelings, so they often cry instead of saying what is wrong.","t":"小孩子很難清楚表達自己的感受，所以他們常常哭，而不是說出哪裡不對勁。","h":1},{"w":"articulate","p":"adj.","d":"able to express ideas clearly","c":"口齒清晰的；善於表達的","s":"Our class leader is very articulate, which is why we always ask her to speak for us in front of the teachers.","t":"我們的班長非常善於表達，這就是為什麼我們總是請她在老師面前替我們發言。"},{"w":"articulation","p":"n.","d":"the act of speaking or expressing something clearly","c":"發音；清楚的表達","s":"Clear articulation is important when you read the news on the radio, because listeners cannot see your face.","t":"在廣播中播報新聞時，清晰的發音很重要，因為聽眾看不到你的臉。"},{"w":"inarticulate","p":"adj.","d":"unable to express ideas clearly","c":"不善言辭的；說不清楚的","s":"The shy boy became completely inarticulate when the girl he liked suddenly asked him a question in front of everyone.","t":"當他喜歡的女孩突然在大家面前問他問題時，那個害羞的男孩變得完全說不出話來。"},{"w":"ass","p":"n.","d":"a donkey","c":"驢","s":"In the old story, the farmer loaded his ass with bags of salt and walked beside it to the market in town.","t":"在那個古老的故事裡，農夫把一袋袋的鹽放到驢背上，走在牠旁邊前往鎮上的市場。","h":1},{"w":"ass","p":"n.","d":"a silly or stupid person","c":"傻瓜；蠢人","s":"I felt like an ass when I realized I had been talking to the wrong person for ten minutes.","t":"當我發現自己跟錯的人講了十分鐘的話時，我覺得自己像個傻瓜。"},{"w":"make an ass of oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something silly that makes you look stupid","c":"出醜；做蠢事","s":"Jack made an ass of himself at the party by singing loudly even though he did not know the words of the song.","t":"傑克在派對上出了醜，他明明不知道歌詞，卻大聲地唱歌。","a":"made an ass of himself"},{"w":"assault","p":"n.","d":"a violent attack on a person","c":"攻擊；襲擊","s":"The man was arrested for assault after he hit a bus driver who had asked him to stop smoking.","t":"那名男子因為毆打一位要求他別抽菸的公車司機，而以傷害罪被捕。","h":1},{"w":"assault","p":"v.","d":"to attack someone violently","c":"攻擊；襲擊","s":"Two men tried to assault the shop owner late at night, but a neighbor heard the noise and called the police.","t":"兩名男子深夜企圖襲擊店主，但一位鄰居聽到聲音報了警。"},{"w":"assault on","p":"n.phr.","d":"an attack against a place or person","c":"對…的攻擊","s":"The army began its assault on the city at dawn, and the sound of guns could be heard for miles.","t":"軍隊在黎明時展開對這座城市的攻擊，幾英里外都能聽到槍砲聲。"},{"w":"assert","p":"v.","d":"to state firmly that something is true","c":"斷言；主張","s":"The lawyer continued to assert that his client was at home that night, even though nobody could prove it.","t":"律師繼續堅稱他的當事人那天晚上在家，即使沒有人能證明。","h":1},{"w":"assertion","p":"n.","d":"a statement that something is true","c":"斷言；主張","s":"The scientist's assertion that the medicine is safe needs more evidence before doctors will give it to children.","t":"那位科學家聲稱這種藥是安全的，但在醫生開給兒童之前還需要更多證據。"},{"w":"assertive","p":"adj.","d":"expressing your opinions in a strong, confident way","c":"果斷的；堅定自信的","s":"You need to be more assertive in meetings; if you never speak up, nobody will know how good your ideas are.","t":"你在開會時需要更堅定自信；如果你從不發言，沒有人會知道你的想法有多好。"},{"w":"assert oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to behave confidently so that people notice you","c":"堅持自己的主張；展現自我","s":"The youngest player finally began to assert herself on the court and asked for the ball when she was open.","t":"最年輕的球員終於開始在球場上展現自我，在沒人防守時要求隊友傳球給她。","a":"assert herself"},{"w":"assess","p":"v.","d":"to judge the value, quality, or amount of something","c":"評估","s":"After the earthquake, engineers were sent to assess the damage to every bridge before cars were allowed to cross.","t":"地震過後，工程師被派去評估每座橋的損壞情況，之後才允許汽車通行。","h":1},{"w":"assessment","p":"n.","d":"a judgment about the quality or amount of something; a test","c":"評估；評量","s":"The teacher gives a short assessment every Friday to check how much we have learned during the week.","t":"老師每週五都會進行一次簡短的評量，檢查我們這一週學了多少。"},{"w":"reassess","p":"v.","d":"to think again about something and decide if it is still right","c":"重新評估","s":"The company had to reassess its plans when the price of oil suddenly doubled within a few months.","t":"當油價在幾個月內突然翻倍時，公司不得不重新評估它的計畫。"},{"w":"risk assessment","p":"n.phr.","d":"a careful study of how dangerous an activity might be","c":"風險評估","s":"Before the hike, the teachers did a risk assessment and decided that the river path was too dangerous after the rain.","t":"健行前，老師們做了風險評估，認定雨後的河邊小路太危險。"},{"w":"asset","p":"n.","d":"a valuable thing, skill, or quality","c":"資產；優點；有用的人或物","s":"Her ability to speak three languages is a great asset when she applies for jobs at international companies.","t":"她會說三種語言的能力，在應徵國際公司的工作時是一大優勢。","h":1},{"w":"asset","p":"n.","d":"property or money that a person or company owns","c":"資產；財產","s":"The company sold several assets, including two office buildings, in order to pay back the money it owed.","t":"公司賣掉了幾項資產，包括兩棟辦公大樓，以便償還欠款。","a":"assets"},{"w":"be an asset to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very useful or valuable to a group","c":"對…是寶貴的人才","s":"Lisa is an asset to the team because she stays calm under pressure and never misses a deadline.","t":"麗莎是團隊的寶貴人才，因為她在壓力下能保持冷靜，而且從不錯過截止日期。","a":"is an asset to"},{"w":"assumption","p":"n.","d":"something you believe is true without proof","c":"假設；假定","s":"The plan was based on the assumption that it would not rain, so nobody brought umbrellas or tents to the picnic.","t":"這個計畫是建立在不會下雨的假設上，所以沒有人帶雨傘或帳篷去野餐。","h":1},{"w":"assume","p":"v.","d":"to believe something is true without proof","c":"假定；認為","s":"Don't assume that the store is open on holidays; call first, or you may waste a trip across town.","t":"別以為這家店假日有開；先打電話，否則你可能白跑一趟穿越全城。"},{"w":"make an assumption","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide something is true without proof","c":"做出假設","s":"It is unfair to make an assumption about a person's character just because of the clothes he or she wears.","t":"僅憑一個人穿的衣服就對他的品格做出假設是不公平的。"},{"w":"assuming","p":"conj.","d":"if we accept that something is true","c":"假設；假如","s":"Assuming the weather is fine, we will climb to the top of the mountain and have lunch by the lake.","t":"假設天氣好，我們就會爬到山頂，在湖邊吃午餐。","a":"Assuming"},{"w":"astonish","p":"v.","d":"to surprise someone very much","c":"使驚訝；使大為吃驚","s":"The magician continued to astonish the crowd by pulling a live bird out of an empty paper bag.","t":"魔術師從空紙袋裡拉出一隻活鳥，繼續讓觀眾大為驚奇。","h":1},{"w":"astonishment","p":"n.","d":"very great surprise","c":"驚訝；驚愕","s":"To the astonishment of her parents, the five-year-old girl read the whole newspaper article aloud without a single mistake.","t":"令父母驚訝的是，那個五歲的女孩把整篇報紙文章大聲唸完，一個錯都沒有。"},{"w":"astonishing","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising","c":"驚人的；令人驚訝的","s":"It is astonishing how quickly the city rebuilt the bridge; the work took only three months instead of a year.","t":"這座城市重建橋梁的速度驚人；工程只花了三個月，而不是一年。"},{"w":"astonished","p":"adj.","d":"very surprised","c":"感到驚訝的","s":"We were astonished to learn that our quiet math teacher used to be a famous rock singer in the 1990s.","t":"得知我們安靜的數學老師在一九九○年代曾是知名搖滾歌手時，我們驚訝極了。"},{"w":"athletics","p":"n.","d":"sports such as running, jumping, and throwing","c":"田徑運動；體育運動","s":"Our school is famous for athletics, and three of our runners won medals at the national games last year.","t":"我們學校以田徑聞名，去年我們有三位跑者在全國運動會上贏得獎牌。","h":1},{"w":"athlete","p":"n.","d":"a person who is good at sports or competes in them","c":"運動員","s":"A professional athlete must eat carefully, sleep well, and train for several hours almost every day.","t":"職業運動員必須注意飲食、睡眠充足，而且幾乎每天都要訓練好幾個小時。"},{"w":"athletic","p":"adj.","d":"physically strong and good at sports","c":"運動的；體格健壯的","s":"My brother is very athletic; he plays basketball on Mondays, swims on Wednesdays, and runs ten kilometers on weekends.","t":"我哥哥非常健壯愛運動；他星期一打籃球，星期三游泳，週末跑十公里。"},{"w":"attendance","p":"n.","d":"the act of being present at a place; the number of people present","c":"出席；出席率；出席人數","s":"The teacher takes attendance at the start of every class, and students who are late three times lose points.","t":"老師每堂課一開始都會點名記錄出席，遲到三次的學生會被扣分。","h":1},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event or a place such as a school","c":"出席；參加","s":"All parents are invited to attend the school concert on Friday evening, and the tickets are free.","t":"所有家長都受邀參加星期五晚上的學校音樂會，而且門票免費。"},{"w":"attendant","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to serve or help people in a public place","c":"服務員","s":"The flight attendant showed us how to use the life jacket and asked everyone to fasten their seat belts.","t":"空服員示範如何使用救生衣，並請大家繫好安全帶。"},{"w":"in attendance","p":"phr.","d":"present at an event","c":"出席；在場","s":"More than five hundred guests were in attendance at the wedding, including the mayor and several famous singers.","t":"超過五百位賓客出席婚禮，包括市長和幾位知名歌手。"},{"w":"attic","p":"n.","d":"a room or space under the roof of a house","c":"閣樓","s":"We found a box of my grandmother's old letters in the attic while we were cleaning the house last weekend.","t":"上週末打掃房子時，我們在閣樓發現一箱奶奶的舊信。","h":1},{"w":"in the attic","p":"phr.","d":"in the space under the roof","c":"在閣樓裡","s":"Grandpa keeps his old guitar in the attic, and he brings it down only when the whole family gathers at New Year.","t":"爺爺把他的舊吉他放在閣樓裡，只有過年全家團聚時才會拿下來。"},{"w":"attic window","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small window in the roof of a house","c":"閣樓的窗戶","s":"From the attic window you can see the whole village and the mountains behind it on a clear day.","t":"天氣晴朗時，從閣樓的窗戶可以看到整個村莊和後面的山。"},{"w":"attorney","p":"n.","d":"a lawyer","c":"律師","s":"If the police question you, you have the right to call an attorney before you answer any of their questions.","t":"如果警察訊問你，你有權在回答任何問題之前先打電話給律師。","h":1},{"w":"attorney general","p":"n.phr.","d":"the chief lawyer of a government","c":"檢察總長；司法部長","s":"The attorney general announced that the government would take the big company to court for cheating its customers.","t":"檢察總長宣布，政府將把那家大公司告上法庭，因為它欺騙顧客。"},{"w":"power of attorney","p":"n.phr.","d":"the legal right to act for another person","c":"授權書；委託書","s":"Before leaving for a year abroad, my aunt gave her brother power of attorney so that he could sell her car for her.","t":"出國一年之前，我阿姨給了她弟弟授權書，讓他可以替她賣車。"},{"w":"attribute","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is caused by a particular thing","c":"把…歸因於","s":"Doctors attribute the rise in heart disease to fast food, long working hours, and too little exercise.","t":"醫生把心臟病的增加歸因於速食、長工時和運動太少。","h":1},{"w":"attribute","p":"n.","d":"a quality or feature of a person or thing","c":"特質；屬性","s":"Patience is an important attribute for a teacher, because students do not always understand things the first time.","t":"耐心是老師重要的特質，因為學生不一定第一次就能聽懂。"},{"w":"be attributed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be thought to be caused by something","c":"被歸因於","s":"The success of the restaurant is attributed to its friendly staff and the fresh fish it buys from the harbor every morning.","t":"這家餐廳的成功被歸因於友善的員工，以及每天早上從漁港買來的新鮮魚貨。","a":"is attributed to"},{"w":"attributable","p":"adj.","d":"caused by a particular thing","c":"可歸因於…的","s":"Most of the traffic accidents last year were attributable to drivers who were looking at their phones.","t":"去年大部分的交通事故都可歸因於駕駛在看手機。"},{"w":"auction","p":"n.","d":"a public sale where things go to the person who offers the most money","c":"拍賣","s":"The painting was sold at an auction for two million dollars to a buyer who made the offer over the phone.","t":"那幅畫在拍賣會上以兩百萬元賣給一位透過電話出價的買家。","h":1},{"w":"auction","p":"v.","d":"to sell something at a public sale to the highest bidder","c":"拍賣","s":"The school will auction the students' artwork on Saturday and give the money to the children's hospital.","t":"學校星期六將拍賣學生的美術作品，並把所得捐給兒童醫院。"},{"w":"auctioneer","p":"n.","d":"a person who runs an auction","c":"拍賣員","s":"The auctioneer spoke so fast that I could hardly understand him, and the old vase was sold within thirty seconds.","t":"拍賣員講話太快，我幾乎聽不懂，那個舊花瓶三十秒內就賣掉了。"},{"w":"auction off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to sell something at an auction","c":"拍賣掉","s":"The city decided to auction off the bicycles that nobody had claimed from the lost-and-found office for over a year.","t":"市政府決定把失物招領處超過一年沒人認領的腳踏車拍賣掉。"},{"w":"authorize","p":"v.","d":"to give official permission for something","c":"授權；批准","s":"Only the manager can authorize a refund of more than one thousand dollars, so please wait while I call her.","t":"只有經理能批准超過一千元的退款，所以請稍等，我打電話給她。","h":1},{"w":"authorization","p":"n.","d":"official permission","c":"授權；許可","s":"You need written authorization from your parents before you can join the overnight camping trip in the mountains.","t":"你需要父母的書面許可，才能參加山上的過夜露營活動。"},{"w":"authority","p":"n.","d":"the power to make decisions or give orders","c":"權力；權威","s":"The principal has the authority to cancel classes when a typhoon is coming, and he did so this morning.","t":"颱風來臨時校長有權力停課，他今天早上就這麼做了。"},{"w":"unauthorized","p":"adj.","d":"without official permission","c":"未經授權的","s":"The sign on the door says that unauthorized persons are not allowed in the lab because of the dangerous chemicals inside.","t":"門上的標示寫著，由於裡面有危險化學品，未經授權的人員不得進入實驗室。"},{"w":"authorized","p":"adj.","d":"having official permission","c":"經授權的；特約的","s":"Take your phone to an authorized repair shop; otherwise, the company will not fix it for free if it breaks again.","t":"把你的手機拿到授權的維修店；否則，如果它再壞掉，公司不會免費修理。"},{"w":"autonomy","p":"n.","d":"the freedom to make your own decisions","c":"自治；自主","s":"The new principal gives teachers more autonomy to design their own lessons instead of following the textbook page by page.","t":"新校長給老師更多自主權來設計自己的課程，而不是逐頁照著課本教。","h":1},{"w":"autonomous","p":"adj.","d":"able to act or work without being controlled by others","c":"自主的；自動駕駛的","s":"Several companies are testing autonomous cars that can drive through the city without anyone touching the steering wheel.","t":"好幾家公司正在測試自動駕駛汽車，它們可以在沒有人碰方向盤的情況下穿越城市。"},{"w":"autonomously","p":"adv.","d":"without being controlled by others","c":"自主地；自動地","s":"The robot vacuum works autonomously, cleaning the whole floor and returning to its charger when it is finished.","t":"掃地機器人會自主地工作，清掃整個地板，完成後回到充電座。"},{"w":"awe","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great respect mixed with fear or wonder","c":"敬畏","s":"The children stood in awe as the giant whale rose out of the water right next to their boat.","t":"當巨大的鯨魚就在他們的船旁邊浮出水面時，孩子們敬畏地站著。","h":1},{"w":"awe","p":"v.","d":"to fill someone with respect and wonder","c":"使敬畏","s":"The size of the ancient temple continues to awe visitors, who often fall silent when they walk through its gate.","t":"這座古老神廟的規模持續令遊客敬畏，他們走進大門時常常安靜下來。"},{"w":"awesome","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; causing great respect or wonder","c":"很棒的；令人敬畏的","s":"The view from the top of the mountain was awesome; we could see the sea on one side and the city on the other.","t":"山頂上的景色太棒了；我們一邊可以看到海，另一邊可以看到城市。"},{"w":"in awe of","p":"phr.","d":"feeling great respect for someone or something","c":"對…敬畏；對…肅然起敬","s":"The young players were in awe of the famous coach and hardly dared to speak when he entered the gym.","t":"年輕球員們敬畏那位知名教練，當他走進體育館時，他們幾乎不敢說話。"},{"w":"awful","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or unpleasant","c":"糟糕的；可怕的","s":"The weather was awful on the day of our trip, so we stayed in the hotel and played cards all afternoon.","t":"我們旅行那天天氣糟透了，所以我們整個下午待在飯店裡打牌。"},{"w":"backyard","p":"n.","d":"an area of land behind a house","c":"後院","s":"We planted tomatoes and cucumbers in the backyard this spring, and now we have more vegetables than we can eat.","t":"今年春天我們在後院種了番茄和小黃瓜，現在蔬菜多到吃不完。","h":1},{"w":"backyard barbecue","p":"n.phr.","d":"a party where food is cooked outdoors behind a house","c":"後院烤肉","s":"Every summer my uncle holds a backyard barbecue for the whole street, and the neighbors bring their own chairs and drinks.","t":"每年夏天我叔叔都會為整條街的人辦一場後院烤肉，鄰居們自備椅子和飲料。"},{"w":"yard","p":"n.","d":"an area of land next to a house","c":"院子","s":"The dog spends most of the day sleeping in the yard under the big tree, where it is cool and shady.","t":"狗一天大部分時間都在院子裡的大樹下睡覺，那裡涼爽又有樹蔭。"},{"w":"front yard","p":"n.phr.","d":"the area of land in front of a house","c":"前院","s":"Mom planted roses along the fence in the front yard, and now people stop to take pictures when they walk by.","t":"媽媽在前院沿著圍籬種了玫瑰，現在路過的人都會停下來拍照。"},{"w":"ballot","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper used for voting; the act of voting","c":"選票；投票","s":"Each student received a ballot with the names of the three candidates and put it into the box after marking a choice.","t":"每位學生都拿到一張印有三位候選人名字的選票，圈選後投入票箱。","h":1},{"w":"ballot box","p":"n.phr.","d":"the box that voters put their votes into","c":"投票箱","s":"After the voting ended, the teachers opened the ballot box in front of everyone and counted the papers one by one.","t":"投票結束後，老師們當著大家的面打開投票箱，一張一張地計票。"},{"w":"secret ballot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a vote in which nobody knows how each person voted","c":"不記名投票","s":"The class president was chosen by secret ballot, so nobody knew who had voted for whom.","t":"班長是以不記名投票選出的，所以沒有人知道誰投給了誰。"},{"w":"cast a ballot","p":"v.phr.","d":"to vote","c":"投票","s":"More than eighty percent of the villagers cast a ballot in the election, which was the highest number in twenty years.","t":"超過百分之八十的村民在這次選舉中投了票，這是二十年來最高的數字。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"ban – bound","cards":[{"w":"ban","p":"v.","d":"to officially say that something is not allowed","c":"禁止","s":"The school decided to ban energy drinks after several students felt sick during the afternoon classes.","t":"在好幾名學生下午上課時感到不舒服之後，學校決定禁止能量飲料。","h":1},{"w":"ban","p":"n.","d":"an official rule that says something is not allowed","c":"禁令","s":"The city has placed a ban on fireworks this year because of the dry weather and the danger of fire.","t":"由於天氣乾燥和火災的危險，市政府今年對煙火下了禁令。"},{"w":"be banned from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be officially stopped from doing something","c":"被禁止（做某事）","s":"The player was banned from the next three games for pushing the referee during the final minutes of the match.","t":"那名球員因為在比賽最後幾分鐘推裁判，被禁止參加接下來的三場比賽。","a":"was banned from"},{"w":"smoking ban","p":"n.phr.","d":"a rule that stops people from smoking in a place","c":"禁菸令","s":"Since the smoking ban began, people can no longer smoke in restaurants, and the air inside is much cleaner.","t":"自從禁菸令實施以來，人們不能再在餐廳裡抽菸，裡面的空氣乾淨多了。"},{"w":"banner","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of cloth or paper with words on it","c":"橫幅；布條","s":"The students hung a huge banner across the school gate to welcome the visitors from our sister school in Japan.","t":"學生們在校門口掛起一條巨大的布條，歡迎來自日本姊妹校的訪客。","h":1},{"w":"banner","p":"n.","d":"an advertisement across the top of a web page","c":"橫幅廣告","s":"A moving banner at the top of the website kept showing shoes I had looked at last week.","t":"網站頂端一個會動的橫幅廣告一直顯示我上週看過的鞋子。"},{"w":"banner year","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very successful year","c":"豐收年；特別成功的一年","s":"It was a banner year for the farm; the weather was perfect, and the mangoes sold for twice the usual price.","t":"對農場來說那是豐收的一年；天氣完美，芒果賣到平常兩倍的價錢。"},{"w":"under the banner of","p":"phr.","d":"using a particular name or idea to bring people together","c":"在…的旗幟下；以…名義","s":"The volunteers worked under the banner of 'Clean Beach Day' and filled fifty bags with plastic in one morning.","t":"志工們以「淨灘日」的名義一起工作，一個早上就裝滿了五十袋塑膠垃圾。"},{"w":"barren","p":"adj.","d":"(of land) not able to produce plants","c":"貧瘠的；荒蕪的","s":"The land on the hill is so barren that even weeds have trouble growing there, so nobody tries to farm it.","t":"山丘上的土地如此貧瘠，連雜草都很難生長，所以沒有人試著在那裡耕種。","h":1},{"w":"barren","p":"adj.","d":"producing no useful result","c":"無成果的；沒有收穫的","s":"After a barren year without a single goal, the striker finally scored twice in last night's game.","t":"經過一整年一球未進的低潮之後，那位前鋒終於在昨晚的比賽中進了兩球。"},{"w":"barren land","p":"n.phr.","d":"land where nothing can grow","c":"荒地；不毛之地","s":"The government plans to turn the barren land near the old mine into a solar farm that will power ten thousand homes.","t":"政府計畫把舊礦場附近的荒地變成太陽能發電場，為一萬戶家庭供電。"},{"w":"batch","p":"n.","d":"a group of things made or dealt with at the same time","c":"一批；一組","s":"Grandma baked a fresh batch of cookies for the party, and the whole house smelled of butter and sugar.","t":"奶奶為派對烤了新鮮的一批餅乾，整間屋子都是奶油和糖的香味。","h":1},{"w":"a batch of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group or amount of things dealt with together","c":"一批","s":"The teacher is marking a batch of essays tonight, so she asked us not to send her any messages.","t":"老師今晚要批改一批作文，所以她要我們不要傳訊息給她。"},{"w":"in batches","p":"phr.","d":"in groups, one group at a time","c":"分批地","s":"The cookies are baked in batches of twelve because the small oven cannot hold more than one tray.","t":"餅乾每十二個分批烘烤，因為小烤箱一次放不下超過一盤。"},{"w":"behalf","p":"n.","d":"used in 'on behalf of': as the representative of someone","c":"代表（用於 on behalf of）","s":"The captain accepted the trophy on behalf of the whole team and thanked the coach for his hard work.","t":"隊長代表全隊接受獎盃，並感謝教練的辛勞。","h":1},{"w":"on behalf of","p":"phr.","d":"as the representative of a person or group","c":"代表…","s":"On behalf of everyone in the class, I would like to thank you for being such a patient and caring teacher.","t":"我想代表全班同學謝謝您，您是一位如此有耐心又關心學生的老師。","a":"On behalf of"},{"w":"on one's behalf","p":"phr.","d":"for someone or as their representative","c":"為了某人；代表某人","s":"Since my father could not attend the meeting, my uncle signed the papers on his behalf.","t":"因為我爸爸無法出席會議，我叔叔代替他簽了文件。","a":"on his behalf"},{"w":"belongings","p":"n.","d":"the things that a person owns","c":"財物；隨身物品","s":"Please take all your belongings with you when you leave the train, and check under the seat for anything you dropped.","t":"下車時請帶走所有隨身物品，並檢查座位底下有沒有掉落的東西。","h":1},{"w":"belong","p":"v.","d":"to be owned by someone; to be in the right place","c":"屬於","s":"This umbrella does not belong to me; I think someone left it in the classroom after the rain yesterday.","t":"這把傘不屬於我；我想是昨天下雨後有人把它忘在教室裡了。"},{"w":"belong to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be owned by; to be a member of","c":"屬於；是…的成員","s":"The blue bicycle outside belongs to my neighbor, who rides it to the market every morning before seven.","t":"外面那輛藍色腳踏車是我鄰居的，他每天早上七點前騎它去市場。","a":"belongs to"},{"w":"personal belongings","p":"n.phr.","d":"the things a person carries or owns","c":"個人物品","s":"The hotel is not responsible for personal belongings left in the room, so put your passport and money in the safe.","t":"飯店對留在房間裡的個人物品不負責任，所以請把護照和錢放進保險箱。"},{"w":"beloved","p":"adj.","d":"loved very much","c":"心愛的；深受喜愛的","s":"The whole town came to say goodbye to the beloved doctor who had cared for three generations of families.","t":"全鎮的人都來向那位深受愛戴的醫生道別，他照顧了三代家庭。","h":1},{"w":"beloved","p":"n.","d":"the person that you love","c":"心愛的人；愛人","s":"In the poem, the young soldier writes to his beloved and promises to return home before the cherry trees bloom.","t":"在這首詩裡，年輕的士兵寫信給他的愛人，承諾在櫻花開之前回家。"},{"w":"beloved by","p":"phr.","d":"loved very much by","c":"深受…喜愛","s":"The old teacher was beloved by his students, who still visit him every Teachers' Day with cakes and flowers.","t":"那位老老師深受學生愛戴，學生們至今每年教師節仍帶著蛋糕和鮮花去看他。"},{"w":"beneficial","p":"adj.","d":"having a good or helpful effect","c":"有益的；有利的","s":"Regular exercise is beneficial not only to the body but also to the mind, because it helps people sleep better.","t":"規律運動不僅對身體有益，對心智也有益，因為它能幫助人們睡得更好。","h":1},{"w":"benefit","p":"n.","d":"an advantage or good effect","c":"利益；好處","s":"One great benefit of living near the MRT station is that you never have to worry about traffic jams.","t":"住在捷運站附近的一大好處是，你永遠不必擔心塞車。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"v.","d":"to get help or an advantage from something","c":"受益","s":"Students who read every day will benefit greatly when they take the English test at the end of the year.","t":"每天閱讀的學生在年底考英文時會大大受益。"},{"w":"benefit from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get something good from","c":"從…受益","s":"Farmers in the valley benefit from the new dam, which gives them water even in the dry season.","t":"山谷裡的農民受益於新水壩，即使在乾季也有水可用。"},{"w":"be beneficial to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be good for","c":"對…有益","s":"Doctors say that eating fish twice a week is beneficial to the heart, so my mother cooks salmon every Tuesday.","t":"醫生說一週吃兩次魚對心臟有益，所以我媽媽每週二都煮鮭魚。","a":"is beneficial to"},{"w":"betray","p":"v.","d":"to hurt someone who trusts you by not being loyal","c":"背叛；出賣","s":"He promised to keep my secret, but he decided to betray me and told the whole class the next morning.","t":"他答應替我保守秘密，但他決定背叛我，第二天早上就告訴了全班。","h":1},{"w":"betray","p":"v.","d":"to show a feeling you are trying to hide","c":"洩露（情感）；流露","s":"Her voice was calm, but her shaking hands began to betray how nervous she really was before the interview.","t":"她的聲音很平靜，但顫抖的雙手開始洩露她面試前其實有多緊張。"},{"w":"betrayal","p":"n.","d":"the act of hurting someone who trusts you","c":"背叛","s":"Selling the team's plans to their rivals was an act of betrayal that none of his old teammates could forgive.","t":"把球隊的計畫賣給對手是一種背叛行為，他以前的隊友沒有一個能原諒他。"},{"w":"betray one's trust","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something that breaks the trust someone has in you","c":"辜負某人的信任","s":"Lending money to a friend is risky, because if he betrays your trust, you may lose both the money and the friend.","t":"借錢給朋友有風險，因為如果他辜負你的信任，你可能錢和朋友都失去。","a":"betrays your trust"},{"w":"beware","p":"v.","d":"to be careful because something is dangerous","c":"當心；提防","s":"Beware of the dog in the yard; it looks friendly, but it bites strangers who come too close to the gate.","t":"當心院子裡的狗；牠看起來友善，但會咬太靠近大門的陌生人。","a":"Beware","h":1},{"w":"beware of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be careful about something dangerous","c":"小心；提防","s":"Tourists should beware of pickpockets in the crowded night market, especially around the food stalls near the entrance.","t":"遊客在擁擠的夜市應該提防扒手，尤其是在入口附近的小吃攤周圍。"},{"w":"aware","p":"adj.","d":"knowing that something exists or is happening","c":"知道的；意識到的","s":"Many drivers are not aware that the speed limit on this road was lowered to forty kilometers an hour last month.","t":"許多駕駛不知道這條路的速限上個月已降為時速四十公里。"},{"w":"awareness","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or understanding of something","c":"意識；認識","s":"The campaign is meant to raise awareness of the dangers of texting while walking across busy streets.","t":"這項活動旨在提高大家對穿越繁忙街道時傳訊息之危險的意識。"},{"w":"bias","p":"n.","d":"an unfair preference for or against someone or something","c":"偏見；偏心","s":"The referee was accused of bias after he gave three penalties to the visiting team and none to the home side.","t":"裁判判給客隊三次罰球而主隊一次也沒有，之後被指控有偏見。","h":1},{"w":"biased","p":"adj.","d":"showing an unfair preference","c":"有偏見的；偏頗的","s":"The report seems biased in favor of the company, because it never mentions the pollution from the factory.","t":"這份報告似乎偏袒該公司，因為它從未提到工廠造成的污染。"},{"w":"be biased against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have an unfair opinion against someone","c":"對…有偏見","s":"Some employers are biased against older workers, even though experience is often more valuable than youth.","t":"有些雇主對年長的員工有偏見，即使經驗往往比年輕更有價值。","a":"are biased against"},{"w":"unbiased","p":"adj.","d":"fair; not influenced by personal feelings","c":"公正的；無偏見的","s":"A good judge must stay unbiased and decide every case only on the evidence, not on personal feelings.","t":"好法官必須保持公正，只根據證據而不是個人感受來判決每個案子。"},{"w":"bid","p":"n.","d":"an offer of money for something, especially at an auction","c":"出價；投標","s":"The highest bid for the old guitar was three thousand dollars, and it came from a young music student.","t":"那把舊吉他的最高出價是三千元，出價的是一位年輕的音樂系學生。","h":1},{"w":"bid, bid, bid","p":"v.","d":"to offer money for something; to try to win a contract","c":"出價；投標","s":"Several companies will bid for the right to build the new bridge across the river next year.","t":"明年有好幾家公司將投標爭取興建跨河新橋的權利。","a":"bid"},{"w":"make a bid","p":"v.phr.","d":"to offer money; to make an attempt to get something","c":"出價；嘗試爭取","s":"The city will make a bid to host the next Asian Games, but it needs to build a bigger stadium first.","t":"該市將爭取主辦下一屆亞運，但它需要先蓋一座更大的體育場。"},{"w":"bidder","p":"n.","d":"a person who offers money for something at an auction","c":"出價者；投標者","s":"The painting went to the highest bidder, a quiet man in a gray suit who had flown in from Hong Kong that morning.","t":"那幅畫落入最高出價者手中，他是一位穿灰西裝的安靜男士，當天早上才從香港飛來。"},{"w":"bid farewell","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say goodbye","c":"道別","s":"The whole village gathered at the station to bid farewell to the young doctor who was leaving for Africa.","t":"全村的人聚集在車站，向即將前往非洲的年輕醫生道別。"},{"w":"biological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with living things and how they work","c":"生物的；生物學的","s":"Scientists are studying the biological clock that tells birds when it is time to fly south for the winter.","t":"科學家正在研究告訴鳥類何時該往南飛過冬的生物時鐘。","h":1},{"w":"biology","p":"n.","d":"the scientific study of living things","c":"生物學","s":"In biology class we looked at onion cells under a microscope and drew what we saw in our notebooks.","t":"在生物課上，我們用顯微鏡觀察洋蔥細胞，並把看到的畫在筆記本上。"},{"w":"biologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies living things","c":"生物學家","s":"A marine biologist came to our school to talk about the sea turtles that lay their eggs on the island's beaches.","t":"一位海洋生物學家來我們學校演講，談在島上海灘產卵的海龜。"},{"w":"biological parents","p":"n.phr.","d":"the parents whose child you are by birth","c":"親生父母","s":"The adopted girl decided to search for her biological parents after she turned eighteen, and she found them in Tainan.","t":"那位被收養的女孩滿十八歲後決定尋找她的親生父母，她在台南找到了他們。"},{"w":"bizarre","p":"adj.","d":"very strange and unusual","c":"怪異的；離奇的","s":"The artist wore a bizarre hat made of plastic forks to the opening of his show, and everyone took photos.","t":"那位藝術家戴著一頂用塑膠叉子做的怪異帽子出席畫展開幕，大家都拍了照。","h":1},{"w":"bizarrely","p":"adv.","d":"in a very strange way","c":"怪異地；離奇地","s":"Bizarrely, the thief stole only the left shoe from every pair in the store and left the right ones behind.","t":"離奇的是，小偷只偷走店裡每雙鞋的左腳，把右腳的留了下來。","a":"Bizarrely"},{"w":"a bizarre coincidence","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very strange event that happens by chance","c":"離奇的巧合","s":"It was a bizarre coincidence that we met our old English teacher at a tiny café in Paris, thousands of kilometers from home.","t":"我們在離家幾千公里的巴黎一家小咖啡館遇到以前的英文老師，真是離奇的巧合。"},{"w":"blast","p":"n.","d":"an explosion","c":"爆炸；衝擊波","s":"The blast from the gas explosion broke windows in buildings two streets away and could be heard across the city.","t":"瓦斯爆炸的衝擊波震碎了兩條街外建築物的窗戶，整座城市都聽得到。","h":1},{"w":"blast","p":"n.","d":"a sudden strong rush of air or loud sound","c":"一陣（強風、巨響）","s":"A blast of cold air hit us when we opened the door, so we quickly ran back inside for our jackets.","t":"我們開門時一陣冷風撲面而來，所以我們趕緊跑回屋裡拿外套。"},{"w":"blast","p":"v.","d":"to break something apart with explosives","c":"炸毀；爆破","s":"Workers had to blast through the mountain with explosives to build the tunnel for the new high-speed railway.","t":"工人必須用炸藥炸穿山脈，才能為新高鐵建造隧道。"},{"w":"have a blast","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a very enjoyable time","c":"玩得很開心","s":"We had a blast at the water park yesterday, and my little brother went down the big slide ten times.","t":"我們昨天在水上樂園玩得很開心，我弟弟從大滑水道滑下來十次。","a":"had a blast"},{"w":"blast off","p":"v.phr.","d":"(of a rocket) to leave the ground","c":"發射升空","s":"The rocket will blast off at six tomorrow morning, and thousands of people are already waiting on the beach to watch.","t":"火箭將在明天早上六點發射升空，已有數千人在海灘上等著觀看。"},{"w":"blur","p":"n.","d":"something that you cannot see clearly","c":"模糊不清的東西","s":"Without my glasses, the words on the board are just a blur, so I always sit in the front row.","t":"沒戴眼鏡時，黑板上的字只是一片模糊，所以我總是坐第一排。","h":1},{"w":"blur","p":"v.","d":"to make something difficult to see clearly","c":"使模糊","s":"The rain on the windshield began to blur the road ahead, so my father slowed down and turned on the wipers.","t":"擋風玻璃上的雨水開始模糊前方的道路，所以我爸爸減速並打開雨刷。"},{"w":"blurred","p":"adj.","d":"not clear; without sharp edges","c":"模糊的","s":"The photo was so blurred that we could not tell whether the animal in it was a dog or a wolf.","t":"那張照片太模糊了，我們分不清裡面的動物是狗還是狼。"},{"w":"blurry","p":"adj.","d":"not clear or sharp","c":"模糊的","s":"My vision became blurry after I stared at the computer screen for six hours without a break.","t":"我盯著電腦螢幕六小時沒休息之後，視線變得模糊。"},{"w":"blush","p":"v.","d":"to become red in the face because you are embarrassed or shy","c":"臉紅","s":"Amy began to blush when the teacher read her love poem aloud to the class without saying whose it was.","t":"當老師沒說是誰寫的、就把艾咪的情詩唸給全班聽時，她開始臉紅。","h":1},{"w":"blush","p":"n.","d":"the red color on your face when you are embarrassed","c":"臉紅","s":"A deep blush spread across his face when the whole restaurant started singing 'Happy Birthday' to him.","t":"當整間餐廳的人開始為他唱生日快樂歌時，他的臉上泛起深深的紅暈。"},{"w":"blush","p":"n.","d":"pink powder put on the cheeks","c":"腮紅","s":"She put on a little blush before the party so that her cheeks would look pink and healthy in the photos.","t":"她在派對前擦了一點腮紅，讓臉頰在照片裡看起來粉嫩又健康。"},{"w":"blushing","p":"adj.","d":"having a red face because of embarrassment","c":"臉紅的","s":"The blushing boy handed the flowers to the girl and ran away before she could say a single word.","t":"那個臉紅的男孩把花交給女孩，在她還來不及說一個字之前就跑掉了。"},{"w":"bodyguard","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to protect someone important","c":"保鑣","s":"The famous singer walked through the airport with a bodyguard on each side to keep the crowd of fans away.","t":"那位知名歌手走過機場時，兩側各有一名保鑣，把大批粉絲隔開。","h":1},{"w":"guard","p":"n.","d":"a person who protects a place or watches prisoners","c":"警衛；守衛","s":"A guard stands at the gate of the factory all night and checks the ID of everyone who enters.","t":"一名警衛整晚站在工廠大門口，檢查每個進入者的證件。"},{"w":"guard","p":"v.","d":"to protect a person or place from danger","c":"守衛；保護","s":"Two large dogs guard the farmhouse at night, and they bark loudly whenever a car comes up the road.","t":"兩隻大狗晚上守衛農舍，只要有車開上這條路，牠們就會大聲吠叫。"},{"w":"lifeguard","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to save swimmers in danger","c":"救生員","s":"The lifeguard blew his whistle and ordered the children to get out of the pool when the storm clouds appeared.","t":"當暴風雨的雲出現時，救生員吹哨命令孩子們離開游泳池。"},{"w":"bolt","p":"n.","d":"a metal bar that slides across to lock a door; a metal screw","c":"門閂；螺栓","s":"The old gate is held shut by a heavy iron bolt, which my grandfather slides across every night before bed.","t":"老舊的大門靠一根沉重的鐵門閂閂住，我爺爺每晚睡前都會把它拉上。","h":1},{"w":"bolt","p":"v.","d":"to run away suddenly","c":"突然逃跑；狂奔","s":"The horse was frightened by the thunder and tried to bolt across the field, but the farmer held on to the rope.","t":"那匹馬被雷聲嚇到，想狂奔穿過田野，但農夫緊緊抓住了繩子。"},{"w":"bolt","p":"v.","d":"to lock a door with a sliding bar","c":"閂上","s":"Remember to bolt the back door before you go to sleep, because the lock on it is old and weak.","t":"睡覺前記得把後門閂上，因為它的鎖又舊又不牢。"},{"w":"a bolt of lightning","p":"n.phr.","d":"a single flash of lightning","c":"一道閃電","s":"A bolt of lightning struck the tall tree in the park, and the top half crashed down onto the empty playground.","t":"一道閃電擊中公園裡的大樹，上半截倒塌在空無一人的遊樂場上。","a":"A bolt of lightning"},{"w":"bolt upright","p":"phr.","d":"sitting or standing very straight, often because of surprise","c":"筆直地（坐起或站著）","s":"She sat bolt upright in bed when she heard the strange noise, and she stayed still until the house was quiet again.","t":"聽到奇怪的聲音時，她在床上筆直地坐起，一動也不動直到屋裡再度安靜。"},{"w":"bonus","p":"n.","d":"extra money given in addition to normal pay","c":"獎金；紅利","s":"Every worker received a year-end bonus of two months' pay because the company had its best year ever.","t":"因為公司有史以來業績最好，每位員工都收到了兩個月薪水的年終獎金。","h":1},{"w":"bonus","p":"n.","d":"something good that you did not expect","c":"額外的好處","s":"The hotel was cheap and clean, and the free breakfast was a nice bonus that we had not expected.","t":"這家飯店便宜又乾淨，免費早餐更是我們沒預料到的額外好處。"},{"w":"bonus point","p":"n.phr.","d":"an extra point added to a score","c":"加分","s":"The teacher gives a bonus point to anyone who can answer the hardest question at the end of the quiz.","t":"老師會給任何能答出小考最後一道最難題目的人一分加分。"},{"w":"added bonus","p":"n.phr.","d":"an extra advantage","c":"額外的好處","s":"The new apartment is close to school, and as an added bonus it has a small balcony where we can grow herbs.","t":"新公寓離學校很近，而且額外的好處是它有一個可以種香草的小陽台。"},{"w":"boom","p":"n.","d":"a period of fast growth in business or population","c":"繁榮；激增","s":"During the housing boom, prices doubled in three years, and many families could no longer afford to buy a home.","t":"在房市繁榮期，房價三年內翻倍，許多家庭再也買不起房子。","h":1},{"w":"boom","p":"n.","d":"a loud deep sound","c":"隆隆聲；轟鳴","s":"We heard a loud boom in the distance and later learned that a factory had caught fire across the river.","t":"我們聽到遠處一聲巨大的轟鳴，後來才知道河對岸有一家工廠起火了。"},{"w":"boom","p":"v.","d":"to grow or become successful very quickly","c":"迅速發展；興旺","s":"Business began to boom after the night market opened next door, and the owner had to hire three more workers.","t":"隔壁的夜市開張後生意開始興旺，老闆不得不多雇三名員工。"},{"w":"baby boom","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when many more babies than usual are born","c":"嬰兒潮","s":"Many schools were built during the baby boom after the war, when the number of children grew very quickly.","t":"許多學校是在戰後嬰兒潮期間興建的，當時兒童人數成長非常快。"},{"w":"booming","p":"adj.","d":"growing or doing very well","c":"蓬勃發展的","s":"The tourist industry in the town is booming now that the new high-speed rail station has opened nearby.","t":"自從新的高鐵站在附近啟用後，這個小鎮的觀光業正蓬勃發展。"},{"w":"boost","p":"v.","d":"to increase or improve something","c":"提高；促進","s":"Winning the first game helped to boost the team's confidence, and they played much better for the rest of the season.","t":"贏得第一場比賽有助於提升球隊的信心，他們在球季剩下的比賽中表現好多了。","h":1},{"w":"boost","p":"n.","d":"something that helps or encourages","c":"提升；鼓舞","s":"The teacher's kind words gave my sister a real boost before the speech contest, and she won second place.","t":"老師的鼓勵話語在演講比賽前給了我妹妹很大的鼓舞，她得到了第二名。"},{"w":"give someone a boost","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone feel more confident or energetic","c":"給某人鼓舞；讓某人精神一振","s":"A good breakfast can give you a boost before a long day of exams, so do not skip it tomorrow morning.","t":"一頓好早餐能在漫長的考試日之前讓你精神一振，所以明天早上別跳過它。","a":"give you a boost"},{"w":"booster","p":"n.","d":"something that increases power or protection","c":"助推器；加強劑","s":"The doctor said I need a booster shot next year because the protection from the first vaccine slowly becomes weaker.","t":"醫生說我明年需要打一劑加強針，因為第一劑疫苗的保護力會慢慢減弱。"},{"w":"booth","p":"n.","d":"a small enclosed space or a stall at a fair","c":"攤位；小隔間","s":"Our club set up a booth at the school fair and sold homemade lemonade to raise money for the trip.","t":"我們社團在校慶園遊會設了一個攤位，賣自製檸檬水為旅行籌錢。","h":1},{"w":"phone booth","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small enclosed space on the street with a public telephone","c":"電話亭","s":"There used to be a phone booth on every corner, but almost all of them disappeared after people started carrying mobile phones.","t":"以前每個街角都有一座電話亭，但人們開始隨身帶手機後，它們幾乎全都消失了。"},{"w":"ticket booth","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small place where tickets are sold","c":"售票亭","s":"Buy your tickets at the ticket booth by the entrance, and then line up at gate three for the first show.","t":"請到入口旁的售票亭買票，然後到三號門排隊看第一場演出。"},{"w":"voting booth","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small private space where people vote","c":"投票亭","s":"Each voter stepped into the voting booth alone, pulled the curtain, and marked the paper where nobody could see.","t":"每位選民獨自走進投票亭，拉上簾子，在沒人看得到的地方圈選選票。"},{"w":"boredom","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being bored","c":"無聊；厭倦","s":"To fight boredom on the long train ride, we played cards, listened to music, and counted the tunnels we passed through.","t":"為了對抗長途火車上的無聊，我們打牌、聽音樂，還數經過的隧道。","h":1},{"w":"bore","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel tired and uninterested","c":"使厭煩；使無聊","s":"The two-hour speech began to bore the audience, and some people in the back rows fell asleep.","t":"兩小時的演講開始讓聽眾感到無聊，後排有些人睡著了。"},{"w":"bored","p":"adj.","d":"feeling tired and unhappy because nothing is interesting","c":"感到無聊的","s":"The children got bored after an hour in the museum, so we took them to the park across the street.","t":"孩子們在博物館待了一小時後覺得無聊，所以我們帶他們去對街的公園。"},{"w":"boring","p":"adj.","d":"not interesting","c":"無聊的；乏味的","s":"The movie was so boring that half the audience left before the end, and my friend fell asleep.","t":"這部電影太無聊了，一半的觀眾在結束前就離開，我朋友也睡著了。"},{"w":"out of boredom","p":"phr.","d":"because there is nothing interesting to do","c":"出於無聊","s":"He started drawing pictures on his desk out of boredom, and the teacher made him clean it after class.","t":"他因為無聊開始在桌上畫畫，老師要他下課後把桌子清乾淨。"},{"w":"be bound to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be certain to happen or do something","c":"一定會；必然","s":"If you practice the piano every day, you are bound to improve, even if you cannot hear the difference yet.","t":"如果你每天練鋼琴，你一定會進步，即使你還聽不出差別。","a":"are bound to","h":1},{"w":"bound","p":"adj.","d":"traveling toward a particular place","c":"前往…的；開往…的","s":"The train bound for Kaohsiung leaves from platform two in five minutes, so we had better hurry.","t":"開往高雄的火車五分鐘後從第二月台出發，我們最好快一點。"},{"w":"bound","p":"v.","d":"to run with long jumping steps","c":"跳躍；跳著跑","s":"The dog will bound across the park the moment you throw the ball, and it never gets tired of the game.","t":"你一丟球，狗就會跳著跑過公園，而且牠永遠玩不膩這個遊戲。"},{"w":"bound","p":"n.","d":"(usually 'bounds') a limit","c":"界限；範圍","s":"The noise from the party was beyond all bounds, so the neighbors finally called the police at two in the morning.","t":"派對的噪音超出了所有界限，所以鄰居最後在凌晨兩點報了警。","a":"bounds"},{"w":"out of bounds","p":"phr.","d":"outside the allowed area; not allowed","c":"界外；禁止進入","s":"The teachers' lounge is out of bounds to students, so wait outside the door if you need to talk to Mr. Lin.","t":"教師休息室禁止學生進入，所以如果你需要找林老師，請在門外等。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"boundary – cemetery","cards":[{"w":"boundary","p":"n.","d":"the line that marks the edge of an area or country","c":"邊界；界線","s":"The river forms the natural boundary between the two countries, so farmers on both sides can see each other across the water.","t":"這條河形成兩國之間的天然邊界，所以兩岸的農夫隔著河水可以看見彼此。","h":1},{"w":"set boundaries","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make clear rules about what is allowed","c":"設定界限","s":"Good teachers set boundaries on the first day of class so that students know exactly which behaviors are not allowed.","t":"好老師會在開學第一天就設定界限，讓學生清楚知道哪些行為是不被允許的。"},{"w":"boundless","p":"adj.","d":"without any limit; very great","c":"無限的；無窮的","s":"My grandmother has boundless energy; at seventy-five she still swims every morning and takes care of a large garden.","t":"我奶奶有無窮的精力；七十五歲的她仍然每天早上游泳，還照顧一座大花園。"},{"w":"out of bounds","p":"phr.","d":"outside the area where a game is played","c":"出界","s":"The ball went out of bounds, so the referee stopped the game and gave the other team a free kick.","t":"球出界了，所以裁判停止比賽，讓對方球隊得到一個自由球。"},{"w":"boxer","p":"n.","d":"a person who fights with the fists as a sport","c":"拳擊手","s":"The young boxer trained for six hours every day because he wanted to win a gold medal at the Olympic Games.","t":"這位年輕的拳擊手每天訓練六小時，因為他想在奧運贏得金牌。","h":1},{"w":"box","p":"v.","d":"to fight someone with your fists as a sport","c":"打拳擊","s":"My cousin learned to box at a gym near his school, and now he teaches the sport to younger kids on weekends.","t":"我表哥在他學校附近的健身房學打拳擊，現在他週末教年紀較小的孩子這項運動。"},{"w":"boxing","p":"n.","d":"the sport of fighting with the fists","c":"拳擊","s":"Boxing is a dangerous sport, so the players always wear thick gloves and a doctor stays near the ring.","t":"拳擊是危險的運動，所以選手總是戴著厚手套，而且有醫生待在擂台附近。","a":"Boxing"},{"w":"boxing match","p":"n.phr.","d":"a boxing fight between two people","c":"拳擊賽","s":"Thousands of fans watched the boxing match on TV last night, and it ended after only three rounds.","t":"昨晚成千上萬的球迷在電視上觀看這場拳擊賽，它只打了三回合就結束了。"},{"w":"breakthrough","p":"n.","d":"an important discovery or success after a long time of trying","c":"突破","s":"Scientists have made a major breakthrough in cancer research, and the new treatment may help thousands of patients next year.","t":"科學家在癌症研究上有了重大突破，新的治療方法明年可能幫助成千上萬的病人。","h":1},{"w":"break through","p":"v.phr.","d":"to force a way through something","c":"突破；衝破","s":"The firefighters had to break through the wall with heavy tools before they could reach the family trapped inside.","t":"消防員必須用重型工具衝破牆壁，才能到達被困在裡面的那家人。"},{"w":"break, broke, broken","p":"v.","d":"to separate into pieces; to stop working","c":"打破；弄壞","s":"Be careful with that glass vase, because if you break it, we will have to pay the shop a lot of money.","t":"小心那個玻璃花瓶，因為如果你打破它，我們就得付商店很多錢。","a":"break"},{"w":"breakdown","p":"n.","d":"a situation when a machine stops working or a system fails","c":"故障；崩潰","s":"Our old car had a breakdown on the highway, so we waited two hours for a truck to come and tow it.","t":"我們的舊車在高速公路上故障了，所以我們等了兩個小時才有拖車來拖它。"},{"w":"break down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop working (a machine); to lose control of your feelings","c":"故障；崩潰","s":"The air conditioner broke down on the hottest day of summer, and the whole office felt like an oven.","t":"冷氣在夏天最熱的那天故障了，整個辦公室感覺像個烤箱。","a":"broke down"},{"w":"briefcase","p":"n.","d":"a flat case for carrying papers and documents","c":"公事包","s":"My father puts his laptop and important papers in his briefcase every morning before he leaves for the office.","t":"我爸爸每天早上出門去辦公室前，都會把筆電和重要文件放進他的公事包。","h":1},{"w":"brief","p":"adj.","d":"short in time or in words","c":"簡短的","s":"The manager gave a brief speech of only two minutes, and then everyone went back to work.","t":"經理發表了一段只有兩分鐘的簡短演說，然後大家就回去工作了。"},{"w":"in brief","p":"phr.","d":"in a few words","c":"簡而言之","s":"In brief, the plan is to leave at six, drive to the beach, and come home before dinner.","t":"簡而言之，計畫是六點出發，開車到海邊，然後在晚餐前回家。","a":"In brief"},{"w":"briefly","p":"adv.","d":"for a short time; in a few words","c":"簡短地","s":"The doctor briefly explained the results, and then she asked me to come back next week for another test.","t":"醫生簡短地解釋了結果，然後她要我下週回來做另一項檢查。"},{"w":"bronze","p":"n.","d":"a brown metal made of copper and tin","c":"青銅","s":"The old temple bell is made of bronze, and it has turned dark green after hundreds of years outside.","t":"這座古廟的鐘是用青銅做的，在外面幾百年後已經變成深綠色。","h":1},{"w":"bronze","p":"adj.","d":"made of bronze; brownish in color","c":"青銅製的；古銅色的","s":"A bronze statue of the famous writer stands in the middle of the park where he used to walk every evening.","t":"一座這位著名作家的青銅雕像矗立在公園中央，他以前每天傍晚都在那裡散步。"},{"w":"bronze medal","p":"n.phr.","d":"the prize for third place in a competition","c":"銅牌","s":"She finished third in the race and won a bronze medal, which was her first prize in an international competition.","t":"她在比賽中跑第三名，贏得一面銅牌，那是她在國際比賽中的第一個獎項。"},{"w":"the Bronze Age","p":"n.phr.","d":"the period in history when people made tools from bronze","c":"青銅時代","s":"People in the Bronze Age made knives and cooking pots from metal instead of stone, which changed their daily life greatly.","t":"青銅時代的人們用金屬而不是石頭製作刀子和鍋子，這大大改變了他們的日常生活。"},{"w":"browse","p":"v.","d":"to look at things in a shop or on the internet without a clear plan","c":"瀏覽；隨意看","s":"I like to browse in the bookstore on Saturday afternoons, even when I do not plan to buy anything.","t":"我喜歡星期六下午在書店隨意瀏覽，即使我沒有打算買任何東西。","h":1},{"w":"browse the internet","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look at different websites","c":"上網瀏覽","s":"Many students browse the internet for hours every night, and their teachers worry that they do not get enough sleep.","t":"許多學生每晚上網瀏覽好幾個小時，老師擔心他們睡眠不足。"},{"w":"browser","p":"n.","d":"a computer program used for looking at websites","c":"瀏覽器","s":"If the website does not open, try closing your browser and opening it again, or use a different one.","t":"如果網站打不開，試著關掉你的瀏覽器再重新打開，或者換一個用。"},{"w":"browse","p":"n.","d":"a quick look through something","c":"瀏覽","s":"Have a browse through the menu while I park the car, and then we can order as soon as I come in.","t":"我停車時你先瀏覽一下菜單，等我進來我們就可以馬上點餐。"},{"w":"bruise","p":"n.","d":"a dark mark on the skin caused by a hit or a fall","c":"瘀傷","s":"After falling off his bike, Tom had a large purple bruise on his leg that took two weeks to disappear.","t":"湯姆從腳踏車上摔下來後，腿上有一大塊紫色的瘀傷，花了兩個星期才消失。","h":1},{"w":"bruise","p":"v.","d":"to cause a dark mark on the skin or on fruit","c":"使瘀傷；碰傷","s":"Please handle the peaches gently, because they bruise easily and nobody wants to buy fruit with brown spots.","t":"請輕輕拿這些桃子，因為它們很容易碰傷，沒有人想買有褐色斑點的水果。"},{"w":"bruised","p":"adj.","d":"having bruises","c":"瘀傷的；碰傷的","s":"The football player left the field with a bruised knee, but the doctor said he could play again next week.","t":"那位足球員帶著瘀傷的膝蓋離開球場，但醫生說他下週可以再上場。"},{"w":"bulk","p":"n.","d":"the main or largest part of something","c":"大部分；主體","s":"The bulk of the work was finished by Friday, so we only needed one more hour on Monday to check the details.","t":"大部分的工作在星期五前就完成了，所以我們星期一只需要再花一小時檢查細節。","h":1},{"w":"in bulk","p":"phr.","d":"in large amounts","c":"大量地","s":"Our restaurant buys rice and cooking oil in bulk because it is much cheaper than buying small bags every week.","t":"我們餐廳大量購買米和食用油，因為這比每週買小包裝便宜多了。"},{"w":"bulk","p":"n.","d":"the large size or weight of something","c":"龐大的體積；身軀","s":"The elephant moved its huge bulk slowly through the forest, pushing small trees aside as it walked.","t":"大象緩慢地移動牠龐大的身軀穿過森林，邊走邊把小樹推到一旁。"},{"w":"bulky","p":"adj.","d":"large and difficult to carry or move","c":"笨重的","s":"The new sofa is too bulky to fit through our front door, so the delivery men had to bring it in through the window.","t":"新沙發太笨重了，無法從我們的前門進來，所以送貨員必須從窗戶把它搬進來。"},{"w":"bully","p":"n.","d":"a person who hurts or frightens weaker people","c":"霸凌者；惡霸","s":"The school bully took the younger boy's lunch money every day until a teacher finally saw what was happening.","t":"那個校園惡霸每天拿走那個小男孩的午餐錢，直到老師終於看見發生了什麼事。","h":1},{"w":"bully","p":"v.","d":"to hurt or frighten someone weaker, often again and again","c":"霸凌；欺負","s":"Nobody has the right to bully others, so if someone keeps hurting you at school, tell a teacher right away.","t":"沒有人有權利霸凌他人，所以如果有人在學校一直傷害你，要馬上告訴老師。"},{"w":"bullying","p":"n.","d":"the act of hurting or frightening weaker people","c":"霸凌行為","s":"Online bullying is a growing problem among teenagers, and many of them do not tell their parents about it.","t":"網路霸凌是青少年之間日益嚴重的問題，而且許多人不會告訴父母。"},{"w":"be bullied","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be hurt or frightened by a bully","c":"被霸凌","s":"The girl was bullied for months because of her accent, but her classmates finally stood up for her.","t":"這個女孩因為口音被霸凌了好幾個月，但她的同學最後站出來保護她。","a":"was bullied"},{"w":"bureau","p":"n.","d":"a government office or department","c":"（政府）局；處","s":"The weather bureau warned that a strong typhoon would hit the island on Saturday, so all schools were closed.","t":"氣象局警告強烈颱風將在星期六襲擊本島，所以所有學校都停課了。","h":1},{"w":"bureaucracy","p":"n.","d":"a system of government with many rules and offices, often slow","c":"官僚體系","s":"Because of the city's slow bureaucracy, it took my uncle three months just to get permission to open a small coffee shop.","t":"由於市政府緩慢的官僚體系，我叔叔光是取得開小咖啡店的許可就花了三個月。","h":1},{"w":"bureaucrat","p":"n.","d":"an official who works in a government office","c":"官僚；公務員","s":"The bureaucrat refused to sign the form because one small box was empty, so we had to come back the next day.","t":"那位官僚因為有一個小格子空著就拒絕簽署表格，所以我們第二天必須再回來。"},{"w":"bureaucratic","p":"adj.","d":"involving many complicated official rules","c":"官僚的","s":"Applying for the scholarship was a long bureaucratic process that required six different forms and four signatures.","t":"申請這項獎學金是一個漫長的官僚程序，需要六份不同的表格和四個簽名。"},{"w":"travel bureau","p":"n.phr.","d":"a company that helps people plan trips","c":"旅行社","s":"We booked our trip to Japan through a travel bureau because they offered a cheap package with the hotel and flights included.","t":"我們透過旅行社預訂去日本的旅行，因為他們提供包含飯店和機票的便宜套裝行程。"},{"w":"burial","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting a dead body into the ground","c":"埋葬；葬禮","s":"The family held a quiet burial for their grandfather on the hill behind the village where he was born.","t":"這家人在祖父出生的村子後面的山丘上，為他舉行了安靜的葬禮。","h":1},{"w":"bury, buried, buried","p":"v.","d":"to put something in the ground and cover it","c":"埋葬；埋藏","s":"My dog likes to bury his bones in the backyard, and then he forgets where he put them.","t":"我的狗喜歡把骨頭埋在後院，然後牠就忘了放在哪裡。","a":"bury"},{"w":"be buried in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be deeply busy with something; to be covered by","c":"埋首於；被…覆蓋","s":"My sister was buried in her homework all weekend, so she could not come to the movies with us.","t":"我姐姐整個週末都埋首於功課，所以她不能和我們一起去看電影。","a":"was buried in"},{"w":"buried treasure","p":"n.phr.","d":"valuable things hidden under the ground","c":"埋藏的寶藏","s":"The children spent the whole afternoon digging in the sand because they believed there was buried treasure on the beach.","t":"孩子們整個下午都在沙灘上挖沙，因為他們相信海灘上有埋藏的寶藏。"},{"w":"butcher","p":"n.","d":"a person who sells meat","c":"肉販；屠夫","s":"My mother always buys pork from the same butcher at the market because his meat is fresh and he gives her a good price.","t":"我媽媽總是向市場上同一個肉販買豬肉，因為他的肉新鮮，而且給她好價錢。","h":1},{"w":"butcher","p":"v.","d":"to kill an animal and cut it into meat","c":"屠宰","s":"On the farm, the men butcher a pig before the New Year, and every family in the village gets a share of the meat.","t":"在農場上，男人們在新年前宰一頭豬，村裡每個家庭都能分到一份肉。"},{"w":"butcher shop","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop that sells meat","c":"肉舖","s":"Could you stop by the butcher shop on your way home and pick up two kilograms of beef for tonight's dinner?","t":"你回家的路上可以順道去肉舖，買兩公斤牛肉當今晚的晚餐嗎？"},{"w":"calcium","p":"n.","d":"a mineral in milk and bones that keeps bones strong","c":"鈣","s":"Doctors say that children need plenty of calcium from milk and cheese so that their bones grow strong and healthy.","t":"醫生說孩子需要從牛奶和起司攝取大量的鈣，骨頭才能長得強壯又健康。","h":1},{"w":"rich in calcium","p":"adj.phr.","d":"containing a lot of calcium","c":"富含鈣的","s":"Small fish eaten with their soft bones are rich in calcium, so my grandmother has them every day to protect her bones.","t":"連軟骨一起吃的小魚富含鈣，所以我奶奶每天吃來保護她的骨頭。"},{"w":"calcium supplement","p":"n.phr.","d":"a pill that gives you extra calcium","c":"鈣片","s":"The doctor told my grandmother to take a calcium supplement every morning because her bones were getting weaker as she grew older.","t":"醫生要我奶奶每天早上吃一顆鈣片，因為她年紀越大，骨頭越來越弱。"},{"w":"mineral","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance such as calcium or iron that the body needs","c":"礦物質","s":"Vegetables, nuts, and fish give us the vitamins and minerals that our bodies need to stay healthy and full of energy.","t":"蔬菜、堅果和魚給我們身體維持健康和活力所需的維生素和礦物質。","a":"minerals"},{"w":"canal","p":"n.","d":"a man-made river for boats or for carrying water","c":"運河","s":"The farmers built a long canal to bring water from the river to their fields during the dry season.","t":"農夫們建了一條長長的運河，在乾季把河水引到他們的田裡。","h":1},{"w":"the Panama Canal","p":"n.phr.","d":"the man-made waterway that joins the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans","c":"巴拿馬運河","s":"Ships that pass through the Panama Canal save thousands of kilometers because they do not have to sail around South America.","t":"通過巴拿馬運河的船隻省下數千公里，因為它們不必繞行南美洲。"},{"w":"waterway","p":"n.","d":"a river or canal that boats can travel on","c":"水道","s":"Hundreds of years ago, this waterway was the main road for trade, and boats full of rice and tea traveled on it every day.","t":"幾百年前，這條水道是貿易的主要道路，載滿稻米和茶葉的船每天在上面航行。"},{"w":"canvas","p":"n.","d":"strong, heavy cloth used for tents, bags, and shoes","c":"帆布","s":"The tent is made of thick canvas, so it keeps out the rain even during a heavy storm in the mountains.","t":"這頂帳篷是用厚帆布做的，所以即使山上下大暴雨也能擋雨。","h":1},{"w":"canvas","p":"n.","d":"a piece of cloth that an artist paints on; an oil painting","c":"畫布；油畫","s":"The artist stood in front of the empty canvas for an hour before she finally picked up her brush and started to paint.","t":"藝術家在空白的畫布前站了一小時，才終於拿起畫筆開始畫。"},{"w":"canvas shoes","p":"n.phr.","d":"light shoes made of canvas","c":"帆布鞋","s":"I wear canvas shoes in summer because they are light and cool, but they get wet very easily in the rain.","t":"我夏天穿帆布鞋，因為它們又輕又涼，但在雨中很容易濕。"},{"w":"capability","p":"n.","d":"the ability or power to do something","c":"能力；性能","s":"The new phone has the capability to take clear photos at night, which is why so many young people want to buy it.","t":"這支新手機有在夜間拍出清晰照片的能力，這就是為什麼這麼多年輕人想買它。","h":1},{"w":"capable","p":"adj.","d":"able to do something well","c":"有能力的","s":"She is a very capable manager who stays calm under pressure and always finds a way to solve problems.","t":"她是一位非常有能力的經理，在壓力下保持冷靜，而且總是能找到解決問題的方法。"},{"w":"be capable of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have the ability to do something","c":"能夠…","s":"This small car is capable of going over 180 kilometers an hour, but of course you should never drive that fast.","t":"這輛小車能夠開到時速超過一百八十公里，但當然你絕對不應該開那麼快。","a":"is capable of"},{"w":"incapable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to do something","c":"無能力的；不能…的","s":"After the accident, he was incapable of walking for three months and had to use a wheelchair to move around the house.","t":"意外之後，他有三個月無法走路，必須用輪椅在家裡移動。"},{"w":"carbon","p":"n.","d":"a chemical element found in coal, diamonds, and all living things","c":"碳","s":"Diamonds and the black part of a pencil are both made of carbon, although one is hard and shiny and the other is soft.","t":"鑽石和鉛筆的黑色部分都是由碳組成的，雖然一個又硬又亮，另一個很軟。","h":1},{"w":"carbon dioxide","p":"n.phr.","d":"the gas produced when we breathe out or burn fuel","c":"二氧化碳","s":"Trees take in carbon dioxide from the air and give out oxygen, so planting more trees helps fight global warming.","t":"樹木從空氣中吸收二氧化碳並釋放氧氣，所以多種樹有助於對抗全球暖化。"},{"w":"carbon footprint","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of carbon dioxide a person or company produces","c":"碳足跡","s":"You can reduce your carbon footprint by taking the bus instead of driving and by eating less meat each week.","t":"你可以搭公車而不開車、每週少吃肉，來減少你的碳足跡。"},{"w":"carbon emissions","p":"n.phr.","d":"carbon dioxide released into the air by cars, factories, etc.","c":"碳排放","s":"The government wants to cut carbon emissions by half before 2040, so it is giving money to people who buy electric cars.","t":"政府想在2040年前把碳排放減半，所以提供補助給購買電動車的人。"},{"w":"carnival","p":"n.","d":"a public celebration with music, dancing, and parades","c":"嘉年華會","s":"Every February, the city holds a huge carnival with colorful costumes, loud music, and dancers in the streets all night long.","t":"每年二月，這座城市舉辦盛大的嘉年華會，整晚街上都有五彩的服裝、響亮的音樂和舞者。","h":1},{"w":"carnival","p":"n.","d":"a traveling fair with rides and games","c":"遊樂園；園遊會","s":"A small carnival came to our town last weekend, and my little brother rode the Ferris wheel five times.","t":"上週末一個小型遊樂園來到我們鎮上，我弟弟坐了五次摩天輪。"},{"w":"parade","p":"n.","d":"a public walk or march to celebrate something","c":"遊行","s":"Thousands of people lined the streets to watch the New Year parade, which had dragons, drums, and dancers from every school.","t":"成千上萬的人排在街道兩旁觀看新年遊行，裡面有舞龍、鼓和來自每所學校的舞者。"},{"w":"festival","p":"n.","d":"a special day or period of celebration","c":"節慶","s":"The Lantern Festival is my favorite time of the year because the whole town is lit up with thousands of colorful lights.","t":"元宵節是我一年中最喜歡的時候，因為全鎮點亮了成千上萬盞彩燈。","a":"Festival"},{"w":"casino","p":"n.","d":"a place where people play games to win money","c":"賭場","s":"My uncle lost all his holiday money at a casino in Macau, so he had to borrow from my father to buy a plane ticket home.","t":"我叔叔在澳門的賭場輸光了所有度假的錢，所以他必須向我爸爸借錢買機票回家。","h":1},{"w":"gamble","p":"v.","d":"to play games for money; to take a risk","c":"賭博；冒險","s":"People who gamble often believe they will win big next time, but most of them lose far more than they win.","t":"賭博的人常常相信下次會大贏，但他們大多數輸的遠比贏的多。"},{"w":"gambling","p":"n.","d":"the activity of playing games for money","c":"賭博","s":"Gambling is illegal in many countries because it can destroy families when people lose more money than they have.","t":"賭博在許多國家是違法的，因為當人們輸掉超過自己擁有的錢時，它會毀掉家庭。","a":"Gambling"},{"w":"gambler","p":"n.","d":"a person who gambles","c":"賭徒","s":"The old man was a heavy gambler in his youth, and he often warns young people never to make the same mistake.","t":"那位老人年輕時是個嗜賭的賭徒，他常常警告年輕人絕不要犯同樣的錯誤。"},{"w":"cathedral","p":"n.","d":"the main and largest church in an area","c":"大教堂","s":"The old cathedral in the center of the city took more than two hundred years to build, and tourists still visit it every day.","t":"市中心的古老大教堂花了兩百多年才建成，遊客至今每天仍來參觀。","h":1},{"w":"church","p":"n.","d":"a building where Christians go to pray","c":"教堂","s":"My grandmother goes to church every Sunday morning, and afterwards she has lunch with her friends from the choir.","t":"我奶奶每個星期日早上都去教堂，之後她和唱詩班的朋友一起吃午餐。"},{"w":"chapel","p":"n.","d":"a small church or a room for prayer","c":"小教堂","s":"The hospital has a quiet chapel on the first floor where family members can pray while they wait for news.","t":"醫院一樓有一間安靜的小教堂，家屬等候消息時可以在那裡祈禱。"},{"w":"temple","p":"n.","d":"a building where people of some religions pray","c":"寺廟","s":"During Chinese New Year, my family visits the temple near our home to pray for good luck in the coming year.","t":"農曆新年期間，我們家會去家附近的寺廟祈求來年好運。"},{"w":"caution","p":"n.","d":"great care to avoid danger or mistakes","c":"謹慎；小心","s":"The sign at the entrance tells drivers to use caution because the road becomes very narrow and icy in winter.","t":"入口處的標誌告訴駕駛要小心，因為這條路在冬天會變得非常狹窄又結冰。","h":1},{"w":"cautious","p":"adj.","d":"careful to avoid danger or mistakes","c":"謹慎的；小心的","s":"My grandfather is a very cautious driver who never goes over the speed limit, even when the road is completely empty.","t":"我爺爺是個非常謹慎的駕駛，即使路上完全沒車，他也從不超速。","h":1},{"w":"caution","p":"v.","d":"to warn someone about a danger","c":"警告；告誡","s":"The lifeguard cautioned the children not to swim too far from the beach because the waves were getting stronger.","t":"救生員告誡孩子們不要游離海灘太遠，因為海浪越來越強了。","a":"cautioned"},{"w":"with caution","p":"phr.","d":"carefully","c":"小心地","s":"You should handle this old document with caution, since the paper is so thin that it could tear at the slightest touch.","t":"你應該小心地處理這份古老的文件，因為紙張薄到輕輕一碰就可能撕裂。"},{"w":"cautiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful way","c":"小心地；謹慎地","s":"The hikers walked cautiously across the narrow bridge, holding the rope tightly and looking straight ahead.","t":"登山客小心翼翼地走過狹窄的橋，緊握繩索，眼睛直視前方。"},{"w":"precaution","p":"n.","d":"something done in advance to prevent harm","c":"預防措施","s":"As a precaution against fire, every classroom in our school has a smoke alarm and a small fire extinguisher by the door.","t":"作為防火的預防措施，我們學校每間教室都有煙霧警報器，門邊還有一個小滅火器。"},{"w":"celebrity","p":"n.","d":"a famous person, especially in entertainment","c":"名人","s":"The restaurant became very popular after a TV celebrity posted a photo of its noodles on social media last month.","t":"上個月一位電視名人在社群媒體上貼了這家餐廳麵的照片後，餐廳變得非常受歡迎。","h":1},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something special for a happy event","c":"慶祝","s":"We are going to celebrate my grandmother's eightieth birthday with a big dinner for the whole family at her favorite restaurant.","t":"我們要在奶奶最喜歡的餐廳辦一場全家的大餐，慶祝她的八十歲生日。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a party or special event for a happy occasion","c":"慶祝活動","s":"The celebration after the team won the championship lasted until midnight, with fireworks and music in the main square.","t":"球隊贏得冠軍後的慶祝活動持續到午夜，主廣場上有煙火和音樂。"},{"w":"celebrated","p":"adj.","d":"famous and praised by many people","c":"著名的","s":"The celebrated pianist will give only one concert in Taipei this year, so the tickets sold out in less than an hour.","t":"這位著名的鋼琴家今年只在台北舉辦一場音樂會，所以門票不到一小時就賣光了。"},{"w":"cemetery","p":"n.","d":"a place where dead people are buried","c":"墓園；公墓","s":"Every April, my family visits the cemetery on the hill to clean our grandparents' graves and leave fresh flowers.","t":"每年四月，我們家都會去山上的墓園清掃祖父母的墳墓，並獻上鮮花。","h":1},{"w":"grave","p":"n.","d":"a place in the ground where a dead person is buried","c":"墳墓","s":"She placed a bunch of white flowers on her mother's grave and stood there quietly for a few minutes.","t":"她在母親的墳墓上放了一束白花，靜靜地站了幾分鐘。"},{"w":"tomb","p":"n.","d":"a large stone structure where a dead person is buried","c":"陵墓；墓","s":"Thousands of tourists visit the ancient tomb of the emperor every year to see the clay soldiers buried with him.","t":"每年有成千上萬的遊客參觀這位皇帝的古陵墓，去看與他一起埋葬的陶土士兵。"},{"w":"funeral","p":"n.","d":"a ceremony for a dead person","c":"葬禮","s":"Hundreds of people came to the funeral of the kind old doctor who had treated the villagers for free for forty years.","t":"數百人來參加這位善良老醫生的葬禮，他免費為村民看病四十年。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"ceremony – cognitive","cards":[{"w":"ceremony","p":"n.","d":"a formal event with special actions, such as a wedding or graduation","c":"儀式；典禮","s":"The graduation ceremony will be held in the school gym on Saturday morning, and every student must wear a white shirt.","t":"畢業典禮將於星期六早上在學校體育館舉行，每位學生都必須穿白襯衫。","h":1},{"w":"opening ceremony","p":"n.phr.","d":"the event that marks the start of something big, like the Olympics","c":"開幕典禮","s":"Millions of people around the world watched the opening ceremony of the Olympic Games, which lasted more than three hours.","t":"全世界數百萬人觀看奧運的開幕典禮，它持續了三個多小時。"},{"w":"wedding ceremony","p":"n.phr.","d":"the formal event at which two people get married","c":"婚禮儀式","s":"The wedding ceremony took place in a small garden by the sea, and only close family and friends were invited.","t":"婚禮儀式在海邊的一座小花園舉行，只邀請了親近的家人和朋友。"},{"w":"ceremonial","p":"adj.","d":"used in or connected with a ceremony","c":"儀式的；禮儀用的","s":"The soldiers wore their ceremonial uniforms with gold buttons for the national day parade in front of the president.","t":"士兵們穿著有金色鈕扣的禮儀制服，在總統面前參加國慶遊行。"},{"w":"certainty","p":"n.","d":"the state of being sure; something that is sure to happen","c":"確定；必然的事","s":"Nobody can say with certainty whether it will rain tomorrow, so you had better bring an umbrella just in case.","t":"沒有人能確定地說明天會不會下雨，所以你最好帶把傘以防萬一。","h":1},{"w":"certain","p":"adj.","d":"sure; having no doubt","c":"確定的；肯定的","s":"I am certain that I locked the front door this morning, because I checked it twice before leaving for school.","t":"我確定今天早上鎖了前門，因為出門上學前我檢查了兩次。"},{"w":"certainly","p":"adv.","d":"without doubt; of course","c":"當然；無疑地","s":"You will certainly pass the exam if you review your notes every evening and get enough sleep the night before.","t":"如果你每天晚上複習筆記，並在考試前一晚睡飽，你一定會通過考試。"},{"w":"uncertainty","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being sure","c":"不確定；不確定性","s":"After the factory closed, there was a lot of uncertainty in the town because nobody knew where the new jobs would come from.","t":"工廠關閉後，鎮上充滿了不確定性，因為沒有人知道新的工作會從哪裡來。"},{"w":"for certain","p":"phr.","d":"for sure; without any doubt","c":"確切地；肯定地","s":"We do not know for certain when the package will arrive, but the shop said it should be here before Friday.","t":"我們不確切知道包裹什麼時候會到，但商店說應該在星期五前送達。"},{"w":"certificate","p":"n.","d":"an official paper that proves something, such as a birth or a course finished","c":"證書；證明書","s":"After finishing the six-week course, every student received a certificate that they could show to future employers.","t":"完成六週課程後，每位學生都拿到一張可以給未來雇主看的證書。","h":1},{"w":"birth certificate","p":"n.phr.","d":"an official paper that shows when and where you were born","c":"出生證明","s":"To apply for a passport, you need to bring your birth certificate, two photos, and your parents' ID cards to the office.","t":"申請護照時，你需要帶出生證明、兩張照片和父母的身分證到辦公室。"},{"w":"certify","p":"v.","d":"to state officially that something is true or correct","c":"證明；核證","s":"A doctor must certify that you are healthy enough before the school allows you to join the swimming team.","t":"醫生必須證明你身體夠健康，學校才會允許你加入游泳隊。"},{"w":"certified","p":"adj.","d":"officially recognized as having the right skills","c":"有證照的；合格的","s":"Only a certified teacher is allowed to give the driving test, so make sure your instructor has the right license.","t":"只有有證照的教練才能進行駕駛考試，所以要確定你的教練有正確的執照。"},{"w":"chaos","p":"n.","d":"a state of complete confusion and no order","c":"混亂","s":"The sudden power cut caused chaos in the shopping mall, with people pushing in the dark and alarms ringing everywhere.","t":"突然停電在購物中心造成混亂，人們在黑暗中推擠，警報聲四處響起。","h":1},{"w":"in chaos","p":"phr.","d":"in a state of total confusion","c":"處於混亂中","s":"The kitchen was in chaos after the party, with dirty dishes on every table and empty bottles all over the floor.","t":"派對後廚房一片混亂，每張桌上都是髒盤子，地上到處是空瓶子。"},{"w":"chaotic","p":"adj.","d":"completely confused and without order","c":"混亂的","s":"Traffic in the city becomes chaotic every time it rains heavily, because the roads flood and the traffic lights stop working.","t":"每次下大雨，市區的交通就變得混亂，因為道路淹水，紅綠燈也停止運作。"},{"w":"chapel","p":"n.","d":"a small church or a room in a building used for prayer","c":"小教堂；禮拜堂","s":"The old school has a beautiful stone chapel where students gather every Monday morning to sing and pray together.","t":"這所老學校有一座美麗的石造小教堂，學生每週一早上聚在那裡一起唱歌和祈禱。","h":1},{"w":"wedding chapel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small church where people can get married","c":"婚禮小教堂","s":"Many couples choose a wedding chapel by the lake for their big day because the view of the mountains is so beautiful.","t":"許多情侶選擇湖邊的婚禮小教堂舉行他們的大日子，因為山景非常美麗。"},{"w":"church","p":"n.","d":"a building where Christians go to pray","c":"教堂","s":"The bells of the village church ring every Sunday morning to call people to the service at nine o'clock.","t":"村裡教堂的鐘每個星期日早上都會響，叫大家來參加九點的禮拜。"},{"w":"cathedral","p":"n.","d":"the main and largest church in an area","c":"大教堂","s":"The famous cathedral has two tall towers, and visitors can climb three hundred steps to see the whole city from the top.","t":"這座著名的大教堂有兩座高塔，遊客可以爬三百階樓梯，從頂端眺望整座城市。"},{"w":"characterize","p":"v.","d":"to describe the typical qualities of something; to be typical of","c":"描繪…的特性；是…的特徵","s":"Reporters often characterize the new mayor as a quiet man who listens carefully before he makes any decision.","t":"記者常把新市長描繪成一個安靜的人，做任何決定前都會仔細傾聽。","h":1},{"w":"be characterized by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have something as a typical feature","c":"以…為特徵","s":"The food of this region is characterized by fresh seafood and a lot of chili, so bring a bottle of water with you.","t":"這個地區的食物以新鮮海鮮和大量辣椒為特色，所以要帶一瓶水。","a":"is characterized by"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"the qualities that make a person or thing different; a person in a story","c":"性格；角色","s":"My favorite character in the novel is the old fisherman, because he never gives up even when the sea is cruel to him.","t":"小說裡我最喜歡的角色是那位老漁夫，因為即使大海對他殘酷，他也從不放棄。"},{"w":"characteristic","p":"n.","d":"a typical quality or feature of something","c":"特徵；特色","s":"Patience is an important characteristic of a good teacher, because students do not all learn at the same speed.","t":"耐心是好老師的重要特質，因為學生學習的速度不會都一樣。"},{"w":"characteristic","p":"adj.","d":"typical of a person or thing","c":"典型的；特有的","s":"With her characteristic warm smile, the nurse calmed the frightened child before giving him the injection.","t":"護士帶著她特有的溫暖笑容，在打針前安撫了那個受驚的孩子。"},{"w":"chef","p":"n.","d":"a skilled cook, especially the main cook in a restaurant","c":"主廚；廚師","s":"The chef at this restaurant trained in Paris for five years, and his special fish dish is famous all over the city.","t":"這家餐廳的主廚在巴黎受訓五年，他的招牌魚料理在全市都很有名。","h":1},{"w":"head chef","p":"n.phr.","d":"the cook in charge of a restaurant kitchen","c":"行政主廚","s":"After ten years of hard work in the kitchen, she finally became the head chef of a five-star hotel in Taipei.","t":"在廚房辛苦工作十年後，她終於成為台北一家五星級飯店的行政主廚。"},{"w":"cook","p":"n.","d":"a person who prepares food","c":"廚師；做飯的人","s":"My grandfather was a cook in the army for twenty years, and he can still make dinner for fifty people without any trouble.","t":"我爺爺在軍隊當了二十年廚師，他現在仍然能毫不費力地為五十個人做晚餐。"},{"w":"cook","p":"v.","d":"to prepare food by heating it","c":"煮；烹調","s":"I am learning to cook simple dishes like fried rice and soup so that I can take care of myself at university.","t":"我正在學煮炒飯和湯這類簡單的菜，這樣上大學時我才能照顧自己。"},{"w":"choir","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who sing together","c":"合唱團；唱詩班","s":"My sister sings in the school choir, and they will perform three songs at the Christmas concert next week.","t":"我姐姐在學校合唱團唱歌，他們下週會在聖誕音樂會表演三首歌。","h":1},{"w":"sing in a choir","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be a member of a singing group","c":"在合唱團唱歌","s":"My grandmother has sung in a choir at her church for forty years, and she still practices every Thursday evening.","t":"我奶奶在她的教堂合唱團唱歌已經四十年了，她現在仍然每週四晚上練習。","a":"sung in a choir"},{"w":"chorus","p":"n.","d":"the part of a song that is repeated; a large group of singers","c":"副歌；合唱隊","s":"Everyone in the crowd knew the words to the chorus, so they sang along loudly each time the band played it.","t":"人群中每個人都知道副歌的歌詞，所以每次樂團演奏到那裡，他們都大聲跟著唱。"},{"w":"choir practice","p":"n.phr.","d":"a meeting where a choir rehearses","c":"合唱團練習","s":"I cannot play basketball after school today because I have choir practice at four, and the concert is only two days away.","t":"我今天放學後不能打籃球，因為四點有合唱團練習，而且音樂會只剩兩天了。"},{"w":"chord","p":"n.","d":"three or more musical notes played together","c":"和弦","s":"My guitar teacher taught me a new chord today, and now I can play the whole song without stopping.","t":"我的吉他老師今天教我一個新和弦，現在我可以不間斷地彈完整首歌。","h":1},{"w":"strike a chord","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause people to feel sympathy or agreement","c":"引起共鳴","s":"The singer's song about leaving home struck a chord with many young people who had moved to the city for work.","t":"這位歌手關於離家的歌引起許多為了工作搬到城市的年輕人的共鳴。","a":"struck a chord"},{"w":"guitar chord","p":"n.phr.","d":"a chord played on a guitar","c":"吉他和弦","s":"Beginners usually learn three or four easy guitar chords first, and with those they can already play hundreds of popular songs.","t":"初學者通常先學三、四個簡單的吉他和弦，光靠這些就已經能彈數百首流行歌。","a":"guitar chords"},{"w":"chore","p":"n.","d":"a boring but necessary job, especially at home","c":"家庭雜務；例行工作","s":"Taking out the trash is my least favorite chore, but my mother says everyone in the family has to help.","t":"倒垃圾是我最不喜歡的家事，但媽媽說家裡每個人都得幫忙。","h":1},{"w":"household chores","p":"n.phr.","d":"the regular jobs needed to keep a home clean and in order","c":"家務","s":"On Saturday mornings, we all do the household chores together, so the whole house is clean before lunch.","t":"星期六早上我們全家一起做家務，所以整個房子在午餐前就打掃乾淨了。"},{"w":"do the chores","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do the regular jobs at home","c":"做家事","s":"My parents give me extra pocket money if I do the chores without being asked, such as washing the dishes and feeding the dog.","t":"如果我不用人叫就主動做家事，像是洗碗和餵狗，爸媽會給我額外的零用錢。"},{"w":"chronic","p":"adj.","d":"(of an illness or problem) lasting a long time","c":"慢性的；長期的","s":"My grandfather has chronic back pain, so he cannot sit in the same chair for more than half an hour.","t":"我爺爺有慢性背痛，所以他不能在同一張椅子上坐超過半小時。","h":1},{"w":"chronic disease","p":"n.phr.","d":"an illness that lasts for a long time and cannot be cured quickly","c":"慢性病","s":"Diabetes is a chronic disease, so patients must watch what they eat and check their blood sugar every day for the rest of their lives.","t":"糖尿病是一種慢性病，所以病人終身都必須注意飲食，每天檢查血糖。"},{"w":"chronically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that lasts a long time","c":"長期地；慢性地","s":"The hospital is chronically short of nurses, and the ones who work there often have to stay for twelve hours a day.","t":"這家醫院長期缺乏護士，在那裡工作的人常常得一天待十二小時。"},{"w":"chubby","p":"adj.","d":"slightly fat in a pleasant way, especially a child","c":"圓胖的","s":"The chubby baby laughed and kicked his fat little legs every time his father made a funny face at him.","t":"每當爸爸對他做鬼臉，這個圓胖的嬰兒就大笑，踢著他胖胖的小腿。","h":1},{"w":"chubby cheeks","p":"n.phr.","d":"round, full cheeks","c":"圓鼓鼓的臉頰","s":"Everyone in the family loves to pinch the little girl's chubby cheeks, which makes her cry and run to her mother.","t":"家裡每個人都喜歡捏這個小女孩圓鼓鼓的臉頰，這讓她哭著跑去找媽媽。"},{"w":"plump","p":"adj.","d":"pleasantly fat and round","c":"豐滿的；飽滿的","s":"The farmer picked a basket of plump red tomatoes from his garden and gave them to the neighbors next door.","t":"農夫從菜園裡摘了一籃飽滿的紅番茄，送給隔壁的鄰居。"},{"w":"overweight","p":"adj.","d":"weighing more than is healthy","c":"過重的","s":"The doctor told my uncle that he was overweight and should walk for thirty minutes every day and eat less fried food.","t":"醫生告訴我叔叔他過重，應該每天走路三十分鐘，少吃油炸食物。"},{"w":"chunk","p":"n.","d":"a thick, solid piece of something","c":"大塊；厚片","s":"She cut a big chunk of cheese from the block and put it on the table with some bread and grapes.","t":"她從那塊起司切下一大塊，和一些麵包和葡萄一起放在桌上。","h":1},{"w":"a chunk of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large part or amount of something","c":"一大部分的","s":"Rent takes up a chunk of my salary every month, so I have very little left for travel or fun.","t":"房租每個月佔了我薪水一大部分，所以我剩下很少的錢可以旅行或玩樂。"},{"w":"chunky","p":"adj.","d":"thick and heavy; in large pieces","c":"厚實的；大塊的","s":"My grandmother makes a chunky vegetable soup with big pieces of potato and carrot that fill you up on a cold night.","t":"我奶奶煮的蔬菜湯料很大塊，有大塊的馬鈴薯和紅蘿蔔，在寒冷的夜晚能讓你吃得很飽。"},{"w":"circuit","p":"n.","d":"the complete path that electricity flows around","c":"電路","s":"If the circuit is broken anywhere, the electricity cannot flow, and the light bulb will not turn on.","t":"如果電路有任何地方斷掉，電流就無法流動，燈泡也不會亮。","h":1},{"w":"circuit board","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin board inside electronic devices that holds the circuits","c":"電路板","s":"When my laptop stopped working, the repairman opened it and found that water had damaged the circuit board inside.","t":"我的筆電壞掉時，維修人員打開它，發現水損壞了裡面的電路板。"},{"w":"circuit","p":"n.","d":"a track for car or motorcycle races","c":"賽車場；環形跑道","s":"The racing circuit is five kilometers long, and the drivers have to go around it sixty times to finish the race.","t":"這條賽道長五公里，車手必須繞六十圈才能完成比賽。"},{"w":"circular","p":"adj.","d":"shaped like a circle","c":"圓形的","s":"The new library has a circular reading room with windows all around, so sunlight comes in from every direction.","t":"新圖書館有一間圓形的閱覽室，四周都是窗戶，所以陽光從每個方向照進來。"},{"w":"circulate","p":"v.","d":"to move around freely; to pass from person to person","c":"循環；流通","s":"Open the windows so that fresh air can circulate through the classroom; it has been closed all weekend.","t":"把窗戶打開，讓新鮮空氣可以在教室裡流通；教室整個週末都關著。"},{"w":"cite","p":"v.","d":"to mention something as an example or proof; to quote","c":"引用；舉出","s":"In your essay, you should cite at least three studies to support your opinion, and remember to list them at the end.","t":"在你的文章中，你應該引用至少三項研究來支持你的看法，記得在最後列出它們。","h":1},{"w":"citation","p":"n.","d":"a line that shows where a quoted idea comes from","c":"引文；引用出處","s":"Every citation in your report must include the author's name and the year, or the teacher will take off points.","t":"你報告裡的每一條引用出處都必須包含作者姓名和年份，否則老師會扣分。"},{"w":"cite an example","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give an example to support what you say","c":"舉例","s":"When the teacher asked why exercise matters, Amy cited the example of her grandfather, who still runs every day at eighty.","t":"當老師問為什麼運動重要時，艾咪舉了她爺爺的例子，他八十歲仍然每天跑步。","a":"cited the example"},{"w":"citizenship","p":"n.","d":"the legal right of belonging to a country","c":"公民身分；國籍","s":"After living in Canada for five years, my aunt applied for citizenship so that she could vote and get a Canadian passport.","t":"在加拿大住了五年後，我阿姨申請了公民身分，這樣她就能投票並取得加拿大護照。","h":1},{"w":"citizen","p":"n.","d":"a person who legally belongs to a country","c":"公民；國民","s":"Every citizen over the age of eighteen has the right to vote in the election, so please remember to bring your ID.","t":"每位十八歲以上的公民都有權在選舉中投票，所以請記得帶身分證。"},{"w":"senior citizen","p":"n.phr.","d":"an old person, usually over 65","c":"老年人；年長者","s":"Bus rides are free for every senior citizen in our city, so my grandparents take the bus to the park every morning.","t":"在我們城市，每位年長者搭公車都免費，所以我祖父母每天早上搭公車去公園。"},{"w":"apply for citizenship","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask officially to become a citizen","c":"申請公民身分","s":"You must pass a language test and know the country's history before you can apply for citizenship in most European countries.","t":"在大多數歐洲國家，你必須通過語言測驗並了解該國歷史，才能申請公民身分。"},{"w":"civic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a city or town and the people who live there","c":"城市的；市民的","s":"Voting and keeping the streets clean are important civic duties that every person in the town should take seriously.","t":"投票和保持街道乾淨是重要的市民責任，鎮上每個人都應該認真看待。","h":1},{"w":"civic center","p":"n.phr.","d":"a public building where a town's offices or events are","c":"市民中心；市政中心","s":"The concert will be held at the civic center downtown, and tickets are free for students who show their school ID.","t":"音樂會將在市中心的市民中心舉行，出示學生證的學生可免費入場。"},{"w":"civil","p":"adj.","d":"relating to ordinary citizens, not the army or the church; polite","c":"公民的；民事的；有禮的","s":"Everyone has civil rights, such as the freedom to speak and the right to a fair trial in court.","t":"每個人都有公民權利，例如言論自由和在法庭接受公平審判的權利。"},{"w":"civilization","p":"n.","d":"a society with a high level of culture and organization","c":"文明","s":"Ancient Egypt was one of the first great civilizations, and its pyramids still stand after more than four thousand years.","t":"古埃及是最早的偉大文明之一，它的金字塔在四千多年後仍然屹立不搖。","a":"civilizations"},{"w":"clarity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being clear and easy to understand or see","c":"清晰；清楚","s":"The teacher explained the difficult math problem with such clarity that even the weakest students understood it right away.","t":"老師把這道困難的數學題解釋得如此清楚，連程度最弱的學生也馬上聽懂了。","h":1},{"w":"clear","p":"adj.","d":"easy to understand, see, or hear","c":"清楚的；清晰的","s":"The instructions on the box were very clear, so we put the bookshelf together in less than twenty minutes.","t":"盒子上的說明非常清楚，所以我們不到二十分鐘就把書架組裝好了。"},{"w":"clarify","p":"v.","d":"to make something clearer or easier to understand","c":"澄清；闡明","s":"Could you clarify what you mean by \"soon\"? Do we need to finish the report today or by the end of the week?","t":"你能說清楚你說的「很快」是什麼意思嗎？我們需要今天完成報告，還是這週末前？"},{"w":"clarification","p":"n.","d":"an explanation that makes something clearer","c":"澄清；說明","s":"The students asked for clarification because the exam notice did not say which chapters would be tested.","t":"學生們要求說明，因為考試通知沒有說會考哪幾章。"},{"w":"clause","p":"n.","d":"a group of words with a subject and a verb, part of a sentence","c":"子句","s":"In the sentence \"I stayed home because it rained,\" the second clause tells us the reason for the first.","t":"在「我因為下雨待在家」這個句子裡，第二個子句告訴我們第一個子句的原因。","h":1},{"w":"relative clause","p":"n.phr.","d":"a clause that begins with who, which, or that and describes a noun","c":"關係子句","s":"A relative clause such as \"who lives next door\" gives more information about the person we are talking about.","t":"像「住在隔壁的」這樣的關係子句，提供更多關於我們談論的那個人的資訊。"},{"w":"clause","p":"n.","d":"a part of a legal document or contract","c":"條款","s":"Read every clause in the contract carefully before you sign it, especially the part about what happens if you leave early.","t":"簽約前仔細閱讀合約裡的每一項條款，特別是關於提早離開會怎樣的那部分。"},{"w":"cling, clung, clung","p":"v.","d":"to hold on tightly to someone or something; to stick to","c":"緊抓；黏住","s":"Wet clothes cling to your skin on a hot, humid day, which is why many people in Taiwan wear loose cotton shirts in summer.","t":"在又熱又濕的日子裡，濕衣服會黏在皮膚上，這就是為什麼台灣很多人夏天穿寬鬆的棉襯衫。","a":"cling","h":1},{"w":"cling to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to refuse to give up a belief or hope","c":"堅持；抱著不放","s":"Even after the doctors gave up, the family continued to cling to the hope that their son would wake up one day.","t":"即使醫生放棄了，這家人仍繼續抱著兒子有一天會醒來的希望不放。"},{"w":"clingy","p":"adj.","d":"(of a person) needing to stay close to someone all the time","c":"黏人的","s":"My little brother is very clingy and cries whenever my mother leaves the room, even for just a minute.","t":"我弟弟非常黏人，每次媽媽離開房間，哪怕只是一分鐘，他都會哭。"},{"w":"clinical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the treatment of patients in hospitals","c":"臨床的","s":"Medical students spend their last two years doing clinical work in hospitals, where they see real patients every day.","t":"醫學生最後兩年在醫院做臨床工作，每天接觸真正的病人。","h":1},{"w":"clinic","p":"n.","d":"a small place where people go to see a doctor","c":"診所","s":"There is a small clinic around the corner, so you can see a doctor there without waiting for hours at the big hospital.","t":"轉角有一家小診所，所以你可以在那裡看醫生，不用在大醫院等好幾個小時。"},{"w":"clinical trial","p":"n.phr.","d":"a scientific test of a new medicine on patients","c":"臨床試驗","s":"The new medicine is still in a clinical trial, so it will take at least two more years before people can buy it.","t":"這種新藥還在臨床試驗階段，所以至少還要兩年人們才能買到。"},{"w":"cluster","p":"n.","d":"a group of similar things that are close together","c":"群；簇；串","s":"We saw a cluster of small white houses on the hillside, and a church tower stood in the middle of them.","t":"我們看到山坡上有一群小白房子，一座教堂的塔矗立在它們中間。","h":1},{"w":"cluster","p":"v.","d":"to gather in a small group","c":"群聚；聚集","s":"The children clustered around the ice cream truck as soon as they heard its music coming down the street.","t":"孩子們一聽到冰淇淋車的音樂從街上傳來，就聚集在車子周圍。","a":"clustered"},{"w":"a cluster of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small group of similar things close together","c":"一群／一簇…","s":"The scientists found a cluster of new stars far away in the sky, using the largest telescope in the world.","t":"科學家用世界上最大的望遠鏡，在遙遠的天空中發現了一群新恆星。"},{"w":"cocaine","p":"n.","d":"a powerful illegal drug","c":"古柯鹼","s":"The police found a large amount of cocaine hidden inside the truck's tires and arrested the driver at the border.","t":"警方在卡車輪胎裡發現大量藏匿的古柯鹼，並在邊界逮捕了司機。","h":1},{"w":"drug","p":"n.","d":"an illegal substance that changes how you feel; a medicine","c":"毒品；藥物","s":"Taking any kind of illegal drug can destroy your health and your future, so never let anyone talk you into trying one.","t":"吸食任何非法毒品都可能毀掉你的健康和未來，所以絕不要讓任何人說服你去嘗試。"},{"w":"drug addict","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who cannot stop taking drugs","c":"吸毒成癮者","s":"The hospital opened a special center to help every drug addict who wants to stop and start a new life.","t":"醫院開設了一個特別中心，幫助每位想戒毒並展開新生活的吸毒成癮者。"},{"w":"drug dealer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who sells illegal drugs","c":"毒販","s":"The drug dealer was caught selling pills near the school gate, and the judge sent him to prison for eight years.","t":"這名毒販在校門口附近賣藥丸時被抓，法官判他入獄八年。"},{"w":"coffin","p":"n.","d":"a long box in which a dead person is buried","c":"棺材","s":"Six men slowly carried the wooden coffin out of the church while the family followed behind in silence.","t":"六個男人緩緩將木製棺材抬出教堂，家屬默默跟在後面。","h":1},{"w":"funeral","p":"n.","d":"a ceremony for a dead person","c":"葬禮","s":"Hundreds of former students came to the funeral of the teacher who had taught at the school for forty years.","t":"數百名昔日的學生來參加這位在學校任教四十年的老師的葬禮。"},{"w":"corpse","p":"n.","d":"a dead body","c":"屍體","s":"The detective examined the corpse carefully and found a small key in the pocket of the dead man's coat.","t":"偵探仔細檢查屍體，在死者外套口袋裡找到一把小鑰匙。"},{"w":"grave","p":"n.","d":"a place in the ground where a dead person is buried","c":"墳墓","s":"Every spring, the whole family cleans the grave of our great-grandfather and leaves fruit and flowers in front of it.","t":"每年春天，全家人會清掃曾祖父的墳墓，並在前面放上水果和花。"},{"w":"cognitive","p":"adj.","d":"connected with thinking, learning, and understanding","c":"認知的","s":"Doing puzzles and learning a new language can improve the cognitive abilities of older people and keep their minds sharp.","t":"做拼圖和學新語言可以增進老年人的認知能力，讓他們的頭腦保持敏銳。","h":1},{"w":"cognition","p":"n.","d":"the process of thinking, knowing, and understanding","c":"認知","s":"Scientists who study cognition want to understand how the human brain turns what we see and hear into memories.","t":"研究認知的科學家想了解人腦如何把我們看到和聽到的東西變成記憶。"},{"w":"recognize","p":"v.","d":"to know who or what something is because you have seen it before","c":"認出；承認","s":"I did not recognize my old classmate at first because he had grown a beard and lost a lot of weight.","t":"我一開始沒有認出我的老同學，因為他留了鬍子，而且瘦了很多。"},{"w":"recognition","p":"n.","d":"the act of knowing someone or something; public praise","c":"認出；表彰","s":"The young scientist finally received international recognition for her work when she won the prize in Sweden last year.","t":"這位年輕科學家去年在瑞典獲獎時，她的研究終於獲得國際認可。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"coherent – compensation","cards":[{"w":"coherent","p":"adj.","d":"clear, logical, and easy to understand","c":"連貫的；條理清楚的","s":"Her essay was coherent from beginning to end, so the teacher gave it the highest score in the class.","t":"她的文章從頭到尾條理清楚，所以老師給了全班最高分。","h":1},{"w":"coherence","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being clear and logically connected","c":"連貫性；一致性","s":"A good speech needs coherence, so each idea should lead naturally to the next instead of jumping around.","t":"一場好的演講需要連貫性，所以每個想法應該自然地引出下一個，而不是跳來跳去。"},{"w":"incoherent","p":"adj.","d":"not clear and hard to understand","c":"語無倫次的；不連貫的","s":"The man was so tired and upset that his story became incoherent, and the police officer could not follow what he was saying.","t":"那個男人又累又難過，說的話變得語無倫次，警察聽不懂他在說什麼。"},{"w":"coherently","p":"adv.","d":"in a clear and logical way","c":"連貫地；有條理地","s":"Even though she was nervous, Lisa answered every question coherently and won first place in the speech contest.","t":"儘管很緊張，麗莎仍有條理地回答每個問題，贏得演講比賽第一名。"},{"w":"coincidence","p":"n.","d":"two things happening at the same time by chance","c":"巧合","s":"What a coincidence! I was just thinking about you when your message appeared on my phone a minute ago.","t":"真巧！一分鐘前我正想著你，你的訊息就出現在我手機上。","h":1},{"w":"by coincidence","p":"phr.","d":"by chance, without planning","c":"碰巧；湊巧","s":"We met our English teacher by coincidence at the airport, and it turned out she was taking the same flight to Tokyo.","t":"我們碰巧在機場遇到英文老師，結果她搭的是同一班去東京的飛機。"},{"w":"coincide","p":"v.","d":"to happen at the same time","c":"同時發生；一致","s":"My birthday will coincide with the school trip this year, so my friends plan to celebrate with me on the bus.","t":"我的生日今年會和學校旅行同一天，所以朋友們打算在車上幫我慶祝。"},{"w":"coincidental","p":"adj.","d":"happening by chance, not planned","c":"巧合的","s":"It was purely coincidental that both sisters chose the same dress for the party without telling each other.","t":"兩姊妹沒有告訴對方卻為派對選了同一件洋裝，這純屬巧合。"},{"w":"collaboration","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together to make or do something","c":"合作；協作","s":"The new science museum is a collaboration between the city government and three universities, and it will open next spring.","t":"新科學博物館是市政府和三所大學合作的成果，將於明年春天開幕。","h":1},{"w":"collaborate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with someone on a project","c":"合作","s":"Students from the two schools will collaborate on a short film about their town for the national competition.","t":"兩所學校的學生將合作拍一部關於他們小鎮的短片，參加全國比賽。"},{"w":"collaborate with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work together with a particular person or group","c":"與…合作","s":"The famous singer decided to collaborate with a young rapper on her new album, and the song became a big hit.","t":"這位知名歌手決定在新專輯裡與一位年輕饒舌歌手合作，這首歌大受歡迎。"},{"w":"collaborative","p":"adj.","d":"involving people working together","c":"合作的；協作的","s":"Group projects teach collaborative skills, because students must listen to one another and share the work fairly.","t":"小組專題能培養協作技能，因為學生必須傾聽彼此並公平分擔工作。"},{"w":"collective","p":"adj.","d":"shared by or done by a group of people together","c":"集體的；共同的","s":"Cleaning the beach every month is a collective effort by the whole village, and even young children help pick up trash.","t":"每個月清理海灘是全村的集體努力，連小孩子也幫忙撿垃圾。","h":1},{"w":"collectively","p":"adv.","d":"as a group; together","c":"集體地；共同地","s":"The students collectively decided to donate their prize money to the animal shelter instead of buying pizza.","t":"學生們共同決定把獎金捐給動物收容所，而不是拿去買披薩。"},{"w":"collective","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together and share the results","c":"集體；合作組織","s":"The farmers formed a collective so that they could share machines and sell their rice at a better price.","t":"農民們組成一個合作社，這樣他們就能共用機器，並以更好的價格賣米。"},{"w":"collector","p":"n.","d":"a person who collects things as a hobby or as a job","c":"收藏家；收集者","s":"My uncle is a serious collector of old coins, and some of the ones in his boxes are more than two hundred years old.","t":"我叔叔是認真的古錢幣收藏家，他盒子裡有些錢幣已經有兩百多年歷史。","h":1},{"w":"collect","p":"v.","d":"to bring things together; to gather as a hobby","c":"收集；蒐集","s":"My little sister likes to collect shells at the beach, and she keeps her favorite ones in a glass jar by the window.","t":"我妹妹喜歡在海邊收集貝殼，她把最喜歡的放在窗邊的玻璃罐裡。"},{"w":"stamp collector","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who collects stamps","c":"集郵者","s":"As a stamp collector, my grandfather has stamps from more than sixty countries, and he can tell a story about each one.","t":"身為集郵者，我爺爺有來自六十多個國家的郵票，而且每一張他都能說出一個故事。"},{"w":"collection","p":"n.","d":"a group of things kept together; the act of collecting","c":"收藏品；收集","s":"The museum's collection of ancient Chinese paintings is one of the best in the world, and it attracts visitors from everywhere.","t":"這座博物館的中國古畫收藏是世界上最好的之一，吸引來自各地的訪客。"},{"w":"colonial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a country controlling another country","c":"殖民的；殖民時期的","s":"The old train station was built during the colonial period, and its red bricks still look beautiful after a hundred years.","t":"這座舊火車站建於殖民時期，一百年後它的紅磚仍然很美。","h":1},{"w":"colony","p":"n.","d":"a country or area controlled by another country","c":"殖民地","s":"Taiwan was a Japanese colony for fifty years, which is why some older people still speak Japanese very well.","t":"台灣曾是日本的殖民地五十年，這就是為什麼有些老人家的日語仍然說得很好。"},{"w":"colonize","p":"v.","d":"to take control of another country and send people to live there","c":"殖民；開拓殖民地","s":"European countries began to colonize parts of Africa and Asia in the sixteenth century in search of gold and spices.","t":"歐洲國家在十六世紀開始殖民非洲和亞洲的部分地區，尋找黃金和香料。"},{"w":"colonist","p":"n.","d":"a person who goes to live in a new colony","c":"殖民者；移民者","s":"The first colonists arrived on the island by ship in 1620 and built small wooden houses near the harbor.","t":"第一批殖民者在一六二零年乘船抵達這座島，在港口附近建了小木屋。","a":"colonists"},{"w":"columnist","p":"n.","d":"a writer who writes a regular article for a newspaper or magazine","c":"專欄作家","s":"My aunt is a food columnist for a Sunday newspaper, and she visits three or four new restaurants every single week.","t":"我阿姨是一家週日報紙的美食專欄作家，她每週都會去三、四家新餐廳。","h":1},{"w":"column","p":"n.","d":"a regular article in a newspaper or magazine on a particular subject","c":"專欄","s":"I always read the advice column in the morning paper because the writer answers readers' questions in a funny and kind way.","t":"我總是讀早報上的建議專欄，因為作者用風趣又親切的方式回答讀者的問題。"},{"w":"column","p":"n.","d":"a tall post that holds up a building; a vertical line of numbers","c":"圓柱；欄","s":"The ancient temple has twelve stone columns in front, and each one is taller than a three-story building.","t":"這座古廟前面有十二根石柱，每一根都比三層樓的建築還高。","a":"columns"},{"w":"write a column","p":"v.phr.","d":"to write a regular newspaper or magazine article","c":"寫專欄","s":"After she retired from teaching, Mrs. Chen began to write a column about gardening for a local magazine every month.","t":"陳老師退休後，開始每個月為當地雜誌寫園藝專欄。"},{"w":"combat","p":"n.","d":"fighting, especially in a war","c":"戰鬥；格鬥","s":"The old soldier never liked to talk about his years in combat, but he always stood very straight during the national anthem.","t":"這位老兵從不喜歡談他在戰場上的歲月，但在國歌響起時他總是站得筆直。","h":1},{"w":"combat","p":"v.","d":"to try hard to stop something bad","c":"對抗；打擊","s":"The city is planting thousands of trees along the river to combat air pollution and give people a cool place to walk.","t":"這座城市正沿著河種植數千棵樹來對抗空氣污染，並給人們一個涼爽的散步地點。"},{"w":"in combat","p":"phr.","d":"during a battle or fight","c":"在戰鬥中","s":"Thousands of young men died in combat during the war, and their names are written on the wall of the memorial park.","t":"數千名年輕人在戰爭中戰死，他們的名字刻在紀念公園的牆上。"},{"w":"comedian","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to make people laugh","c":"喜劇演員","s":"The comedian told jokes about his family for an hour, and the whole audience laughed until their stomachs hurt.","t":"這位喜劇演員講了一小時關於他家人的笑話，全場觀眾笑到肚子痛。","h":1},{"w":"comedy","p":"n.","d":"a funny film, play, or TV show","c":"喜劇","s":"We watched a comedy about two brothers who open a noodle shop, and my father laughed so hard that he cried.","t":"我們看了一部關於兩兄弟開麵店的喜劇，我爸爸笑到都哭了。"},{"w":"comic","p":"adj.","d":"funny; making people laugh","c":"滑稽的；喜劇的","s":"The actor is famous for his comic roles, but in his newest film he plays a serious doctor who saves a village.","t":"這位演員以喜劇角色聞名，但在他最新的電影裡，他扮演一位拯救村莊的嚴肅醫生。"},{"w":"stand-up comedian","p":"n.phr.","d":"a comedian who performs alone on stage, telling jokes","c":"單口喜劇演員","s":"My cousin wants to be a stand-up comedian, so he practices telling jokes to our family at every dinner.","t":"我表哥想當單口喜劇演員，所以他每次晚餐都對我們全家練習講笑話。"},{"w":"commentary","p":"n.","d":"a spoken description of an event while it happens; a discussion of a topic","c":"實況報導；評論","s":"I like to listen to the radio commentary during baseball games because the speaker explains every play so clearly.","t":"我喜歡在棒球比賽時聽廣播的實況報導，因為播報員把每一球都解釋得很清楚。","h":1},{"w":"commentator","p":"n.","d":"a person who describes a sports event or discusses news on TV or radio","c":"播報員；評論員","s":"The TV commentator got so excited when the home team scored that he jumped out of his chair and shouted.","t":"主隊得分時，電視播報員興奮到從椅子上跳起來大叫。","h":1},{"w":"comment","p":"n.","d":"something you say or write that gives an opinion","c":"評論；意見","s":"The teacher wrote a kind comment at the bottom of my essay, telling me that my ideas were strong but my spelling needed work.","t":"老師在我文章的最後寫了一句親切的評語，說我的想法很好但拼字需要加強。"},{"w":"comment on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give an opinion about something","c":"評論；對…發表意見","s":"The coach refused to comment on the referee's decision after the game, saying only that his team had played well.","t":"賽後教練拒絕評論裁判的判決，只說他的球隊表現得很好。"},{"w":"commission","p":"n.","d":"an official group of people asked to study or control something","c":"委員會","s":"The government set up a special commission to find out why the bridge fell down and how to prevent such accidents.","t":"政府成立了一個特別委員會，調查橋為什麼倒塌，以及如何預防這類意外。","h":1},{"w":"commission","p":"n.","d":"money paid to a salesperson for each thing they sell","c":"佣金","s":"The car salesman earns a small basic salary plus a commission of two percent on every car that he sells.","t":"這位汽車銷售員領微薄的底薪，加上每賣一輛車百分之二的佣金。"},{"w":"commission","p":"v.","d":"to formally ask someone to make or do something","c":"委託；委任","s":"The city decided to commission a local artist to paint a huge picture of the harbor on the wall of the train station.","t":"市政府決定委託一位當地藝術家在火車站的牆上畫一幅巨大的港口圖。"},{"w":"commissioner","p":"n.","d":"an important official in charge of a government department","c":"專員；局長","s":"The police commissioner promised on TV that more officers would patrol the night market after the recent thefts.","t":"警察局長在電視上承諾，在最近的竊案之後會有更多警員在夜市巡邏。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"a promise to do something; strong dedication","c":"承諾；投入","s":"Joining the school team is a serious commitment, because you must come to practice four afternoons every week.","t":"加入校隊是一項認真的承諾，因為你每週必須來練習四個下午。","h":1},{"w":"commit","p":"v.","d":"to do something wrong or illegal","c":"犯（罪）","s":"The young man did not commit the crime; he was at work when the shop was robbed, and ten people saw him there.","t":"這個年輕人沒有犯罪；商店被搶時他在上班，有十個人看到他在那裡。"},{"w":"commit to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to promise to do something seriously","c":"承諾；致力於","s":"Before you commit to learning the piano, remember that you will need to practice at least thirty minutes every day.","t":"在你承諾學鋼琴之前，記住你每天至少需要練習三十分鐘。"},{"w":"committed","p":"adj.","d":"willing to work very hard for something","c":"盡心盡力的；堅定的","s":"Ms. Lee is a committed teacher who stays after school every day to help students who are struggling with math.","t":"李老師是一位盡心盡力的老師，她每天放學後都留下來幫助數學有困難的學生。"},{"w":"make a commitment","p":"v.phr.","d":"to promise to do something","c":"做出承諾","s":"My brother made a commitment to run every morning before work, and he has not missed a single day in three months.","t":"我哥哥承諾每天上班前跑步，三個月來他一天都沒有錯過。","a":"made a commitment"},{"w":"commodity","p":"n.","d":"a product that can be bought and sold, such as oil or rice","c":"商品；物資","s":"Oil is the most important commodity in the world market, and its price affects the cost of almost everything we buy.","t":"石油是世界市場上最重要的商品，它的價格影響我們購買的幾乎所有東西的成本。","h":1},{"w":"goods","p":"n.","d":"things that are made to be sold","c":"商品；貨物","s":"The truck was carrying goods from the factory to the port, where they would be loaded onto a ship for Europe.","t":"卡車把貨物從工廠運到港口，在那裡它們將被裝上開往歐洲的船。"},{"w":"merchandise","p":"n.","d":"products that are bought and sold in shops","c":"商品","s":"The store put all its summer merchandise on sale at half price to make room for the new winter clothes.","t":"這家店把所有夏季商品半價出清，好為新的冬裝騰出空間。"},{"w":"product","p":"n.","d":"something that is made or grown to be sold","c":"產品","s":"The company's newest product is a small speaker that can play music for twenty hours on one charge.","t":"這家公司最新的產品是一個充一次電就能播放二十小時音樂的小喇叭。"},{"w":"communism","p":"n.","d":"a political system in which the state owns everything and shares it","c":"共產主義","s":"Under communism, the government owned all the farms and factories, and people were not allowed to run their own businesses.","t":"在共產主義下，政府擁有所有的農場和工廠，人民不被允許經營自己的事業。","h":1},{"w":"communist","p":"n.","d":"a person who believes in communism","c":"共產主義者","s":"My grandfather told me that in the 1950s, anyone who was thought to be a communist could lose his job or even go to prison.","t":"我爺爺告訴我，在一九五零年代，任何被認為是共產主義者的人都可能丟掉工作，甚至入獄。","h":1},{"w":"communist","p":"adj.","d":"connected with or believing in communism","c":"共產主義的","s":"After the war, the country became a communist state, and for forty years its people could not travel freely to the West.","t":"戰後這個國家成為共產國家，四十年來人民無法自由前往西方。"},{"w":"the Communist Party","p":"n.phr.","d":"the political party that supports communism","c":"共產黨","s":"For most of the twentieth century, the Communist Party was the only political party allowed in the Soviet Union.","t":"在二十世紀的大部分時間裡，共產黨是蘇聯唯一被允許的政黨。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v.","d":"to travel regularly between home and work or school","c":"通勤","s":"My father has to commute for over an hour each way, so he leaves home at six and gets back after eight.","t":"我爸爸單程就得通勤一個多小時，所以他六點出門，八點多才回到家。","h":1},{"w":"commuter","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels regularly to and from work","c":"通勤者","s":"Every morning the MRT is packed with commuters, and many of them read the news on their phones while they stand.","t":"每天早上捷運擠滿了通勤的人，許多人站著用手機看新聞。","a":"commuters","h":1},{"w":"commute","p":"n.","d":"the regular journey between home and work","c":"通勤路程","s":"Her commute takes only fifteen minutes by bike, which is one reason she chose the apartment near the office.","t":"她的通勤路程騎腳踏車只要十五分鐘，這是她選擇辦公室附近那間公寓的原因之一。"},{"w":"commuter train","p":"n.phr.","d":"a train that carries people to and from work","c":"通勤列車","s":"The seven o'clock commuter train is always full, so I usually take the earlier one and read a book while I wait.","t":"七點的通勤列車總是客滿，所以我通常搭早一班的，等車時看書。"},{"w":"compact","p":"adj.","d":"small and taking up little space","c":"小巧的；緊湊的","s":"This compact camera fits easily into my pocket, but it still takes pictures as good as my father's big one.","t":"這台小巧的相機可以輕鬆放進我的口袋，但拍出來的照片和我爸那台大相機一樣好。","h":1},{"w":"compact car","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small car","c":"小型車","s":"We rented a compact car for our trip because it is cheaper to run and much easier to park in a crowded city.","t":"我們旅行租了一輛小型車，因為它比較省油，而且在擁擠的城市裡更容易停車。"},{"w":"compact","p":"v.","d":"to press something together so that it becomes smaller and firmer","c":"壓緊；壓實","s":"The workers used a heavy machine to compact the soil before they laid the stones for the new path.","t":"工人在鋪新步道的石頭之前，用一台重機器把土壤壓實。"},{"w":"compact disc","p":"n.phr.","d":"a CD; a small round disc that stores music or data","c":"光碟（CD）","s":"My parents still have hundreds of compact discs from the 1990s, although they now listen to most music on their phones.","t":"我父母仍然有數百張一九九零年代的光碟，雖然他們現在大多用手機聽音樂。","a":"compact discs"},{"w":"comparable","p":"adj.","d":"similar in size, quality, or amount, so it can be compared","c":"可比較的；相當的","s":"The two phones are comparable in price and quality, so just choose the one whose color you like more.","t":"這兩支手機在價格和品質上相當，所以就選你比較喜歡的顏色那支吧。","h":1},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at two or more things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"Before you buy a laptop, compare at least three models online so that you know which one gives you the best value.","t":"買筆電之前，先在網路上比較至少三款，這樣你才知道哪一款最划算。"},{"w":"comparison","p":"n.","d":"the act of comparing two or more things","c":"比較","s":"In comparison with last year, the weather this summer has been much hotter and drier, and the rice fields are suffering.","t":"和去年相比，今年夏天的天氣更熱更乾，稻田正受影響。"},{"w":"compared with","p":"phr.","d":"when looked at next to something else","c":"與…相比","s":"Compared with my old bike, the new one is lighter and faster, and it has gears for going up hills.","t":"與我的舊腳踏車相比，新的更輕更快，而且有爬坡用的變速齒輪。","a":"Compared with"},{"w":"comparative","p":"adj.","d":"measured by comparing with something else","c":"比較的；相對的","s":"After the noisy city, the little village felt like a place of comparative peace, where the only sound was birds.","t":"在吵雜的城市之後，這個小村莊感覺像是一個相對寧靜的地方，唯一的聲音是鳥叫。"},{"w":"compassion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of sympathy for people who are suffering","c":"同情心；憐憫","s":"The nurse treated every patient with great compassion, holding their hands and listening to their worries.","t":"這位護士以極大的同情心對待每位病人，握著他們的手，傾聽他們的擔憂。","h":1},{"w":"compassionate","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or showing sympathy for others","c":"有同情心的；慈悲的","s":"A compassionate doctor does not only treat the illness; he also takes time to comfort the frightened patient.","t":"一位有同情心的醫生不只治療疾病；他也會花時間安慰害怕的病人。","h":1},{"w":"show compassion","p":"v.phr.","d":"to act kindly toward someone who is suffering","c":"表現出同情心","s":"The teacher asked us to show compassion to the new student, who had just lost her father in an accident.","t":"老師要我們對剛在意外中失去父親的新同學表現出同情心。"},{"w":"compassionately","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind and caring way","c":"富有同情心地","s":"The vet spoke compassionately to the little girl whose dog was very sick, and she slowly stopped crying.","t":"獸醫溫柔有同情心地對狗狗病重的小女孩說話，她慢慢停止哭泣。"},{"w":"compatible","p":"adj.","d":"able to work or exist together without problems","c":"相容的；合得來的","s":"This printer is not compatible with my new laptop, so I have to borrow my sister's computer every time I print.","t":"這台印表機和我的新筆電不相容，所以每次列印我都得借我姐姐的電腦。","h":1},{"w":"be compatible with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work well together with something or someone","c":"與…相容；與…合得來","s":"The new software is compatible with both Windows and Mac computers, so everyone in the office can use it.","t":"這款新軟體與Windows 和 Mac 電腦都相容，所以辦公室每個人都能用。","a":"is compatible with"},{"w":"incompatible","p":"adj.","d":"not able to work or live together","c":"不相容的；合不來的","s":"The two roommates were completely incompatible: one liked to study in silence, and the other played loud music all night.","t":"這兩位室友完全合不來：一個喜歡安靜地讀書，另一個整晚播放吵鬧的音樂。"},{"w":"compatibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to work or live together well","c":"相容性；合得來","s":"Before buying a phone case online, check its compatibility with your phone model, or it may not fit at all.","t":"在網路上買手機殼前，先確認它和你手機型號的相容性，否則可能完全不合。"},{"w":"compel","p":"v.","d":"to force someone to do something","c":"強迫；迫使","s":"The heavy snow may compel the school to close for two days, since the buses cannot drive safely on icy roads.","t":"大雪可能迫使學校停課兩天，因為公車在結冰的路上無法安全行駛。","h":1},{"w":"be compelled to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be forced to do something","c":"被迫…","s":"After the factory closed, many families were compelled to leave the town and look for work in the big cities.","t":"工廠關閉後，許多家庭被迫離開小鎮，到大城市找工作。","a":"were compelled to"},{"w":"compelling","p":"adj.","d":"very interesting; strong enough to make you believe","c":"引人入勝的；令人信服的","s":"The documentary tells such a compelling story about the ocean that I watched the whole two hours without checking my phone.","t":"這部紀錄片講述關於海洋的故事如此引人入勝，我看了整整兩小時都沒看手機。"},{"w":"compulsory","p":"adj.","d":"required by a rule or law","c":"義務的；強制的","s":"In Taiwan, education is compulsory for all children from the age of six until they finish junior high school.","t":"在台灣，從六歲到國中畢業，所有兒童都必須接受義務教育。"},{"w":"compensate","p":"v.","d":"to pay someone for loss or damage; to make up for something","c":"補償；賠償；彌補","s":"The airline agreed to compensate the passengers for the ten-hour delay by giving each of them a free meal and a hotel room.","t":"航空公司同意為十小時的延誤補償乘客，給每人一份免費餐點和一間飯店房間。","h":1},{"w":"compensation","p":"n.","d":"money or something given to make up for loss or damage","c":"補償；賠償金","s":"The workers who were hurt in the accident received compensation from the company to cover their hospital bills.","t":"在意外中受傷的工人從公司獲得賠償金，用來支付醫療費用。","h":1},{"w":"compensate for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make up for something bad or missing","c":"彌補；補償","s":"Nothing can truly compensate for the loss of a loved one, but the kind words from friends helped the family a little.","t":"沒有什麼能真正彌補失去摯愛的痛，但朋友的暖心話語讓這家人好過一些。"},{"w":"receive compensation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be given money for loss, damage, or injury","c":"獲得賠償","s":"Farmers whose fields were flooded will receive compensation from the government, but the money may not arrive until next spring.","t":"田地被淹的農民將從政府獲得賠償，但錢可能要到明年春天才會到。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"competence – confront","cards":[{"w":"competence","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something well","c":"能力；勝任","s":"The new nurse showed great competence during the emergency, so the doctor trusted her to handle the next patient alone.","t":"這位新護士在緊急情況中展現了極佳的能力，所以醫生信任她獨自處理下一位病人。","h":1},{"w":"competent","p":"adj.","d":"having enough skill or knowledge to do something well","c":"能幹的；勝任的","s":"Although he is only twenty-three, he is a competent driver who has never had an accident on the busy city roads.","t":"雖然他只有二十三歲，但他是個能幹的駕駛，在繁忙的市區道路上從未發生過事故。","h":1},{"w":"incompetent","p":"adj.","d":"not having the skill to do a job properly","c":"無能的；不稱職的","s":"The customers complained that the incompetent waiter brought the wrong dishes to three different tables in one evening.","t":"顧客抱怨那位不稱職的服務生在一個晚上把錯的菜送到三張不同的桌子。"},{"w":"compete","p":"v.","d":"to try to win or be better than others","c":"競爭；比賽","s":"More than two hundred students will compete in the speech contest next month, and only ten of them can win a prize.","t":"下個月將有超過兩百名學生參加演講比賽，其中只有十人能獲獎。"},{"w":"competition","p":"n.","d":"an event in which people try to win","c":"比賽；競爭","s":"My sister entered a piano competition last spring, and she practiced for three hours every day to prepare for it.","t":"我姐姐去年春天參加了一場鋼琴比賽，為了準備她每天練習三小時。"},{"w":"complexity","p":"n.","d":"the state of having many parts that are hard to understand","c":"複雜（性）","s":"Because of the complexity of the tax rules, many people pay an accountant to fill in the forms for them every year.","t":"由於稅務規定的複雜，許多人每年付錢請會計師替他們填寫表格。","h":1},{"w":"complex","p":"adj.","d":"having many parts and difficult to understand","c":"複雜的","s":"The human brain is a very complex organ, and scientists still do not fully understand how memory works.","t":"人類的大腦是一個非常複雜的器官，科學家至今仍未完全了解記憶如何運作。"},{"w":"complex","p":"n.","d":"a group of buildings used for one purpose","c":"綜合建築群","s":"The new sports complex near the river has a swimming pool, two gyms, and a running track that is open all day.","t":"河邊新的運動中心有一座游泳池、兩間健身房和一條全天開放的跑道。"},{"w":"complicated","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to understand because of many parts","c":"複雜的","s":"The instructions for building the bookshelf were so complicated that it took my father the whole afternoon to finish it.","t":"組裝書架的說明書太複雜了，我爸爸花了一整個下午才完成。"},{"w":"compliance","p":"n.","d":"the act of obeying a rule or request","c":"遵守；服從","s":"The factory was closed for a week because the inspector found that it was not in compliance with the fire safety rules.","t":"這家工廠被關閉一週，因為檢查員發現它沒有遵守消防安全規定。","h":1},{"w":"comply","p":"v.","d":"to do what a rule or a person tells you to do","c":"遵守；順從","s":"All passengers must comply with the airline's rules about luggage, or they will have to pay an extra fee at the gate.","t":"所有乘客都必須遵守航空公司的行李規定，否則他們必須在登機門付額外費用。","h":1},{"w":"comply with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to obey a rule or request","c":"遵守…","s":"Companies that fail to comply with the new environmental laws may have to pay a fine of up to one million dollars.","t":"未能遵守新環保法規的公司可能必須支付高達一百萬元的罰款。"},{"w":"in compliance with","p":"phr.","d":"following a rule or law","c":"遵照…；符合…","s":"The restaurant keeps its kitchen in compliance with the health rules, so it has passed every inspection for the last five years.","t":"這家餐廳讓廚房保持符合衛生規定，所以過去五年通過了每一次檢查。"},{"w":"compliant","p":"adj.","d":"willing to obey rules; following the rules","c":"順從的；符合規定的","s":"The hotel became fully compliant with the new safety standards after it installed smoke alarms in every room last month.","t":"這家飯店上個月在每個房間安裝煙霧警報器後，已完全符合新的安全標準。"},{"w":"complication","p":"n.","d":"a problem that makes a situation more difficult; a new illness after treatment","c":"併發症；複雜的問題","s":"The surgery went well, but the doctor warned that any complication such as a fever should be reported to the hospital at once.","t":"手術很順利，但醫生警告說，任何像發燒這樣的併發症都應立即向醫院報告。","h":1},{"w":"complicate","p":"v.","d":"to make something more difficult to deal with","c":"使複雜化","s":"Please do not complicate the plan with too many extra ideas; we only have one week to finish the whole project.","t":"請不要用太多額外的想法把計畫弄複雜；我們只有一週的時間完成整個專案。"},{"w":"complicate matters","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a situation harder to deal with","c":"使事情更複雜","s":"The heavy rain only served to complicate matters, because the roads to the mountain village were already blocked by fallen trees.","t":"大雨只是讓事情更複雜，因為通往山村的道路早已被倒下的樹木擋住了。"},{"w":"compliment","p":"n.","d":"something nice you say to praise someone","c":"讚美；恭維","s":"She received many compliments on her new dress at the party, and she smiled every time someone said how lovely it looked.","t":"她在派對上因為新洋裝收到許多讚美，每次有人說它多好看時她都會微笑。","a":"compliments","h":1},{"w":"compliment","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone that you admire something about them","c":"讚美；稱讚","s":"My teacher complimented me on my clear handwriting, which made me feel proud because I had practiced for months.","t":"老師稱讚我字跡清楚，這讓我感到驕傲，因為我已經練習了好幾個月。","a":"complimented"},{"w":"pay sb a compliment","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say something nice to someone","c":"稱讚某人","s":"The manager paid her a compliment on her presentation, saying it was the best he had seen all year.","t":"經理稱讚她的簡報，說那是他今年看過最好的一場。","a":"paid her a compliment"},{"w":"complimentary","p":"adj.","d":"given free of charge; full of praise","c":"免費贈送的；讚美的","s":"The hotel offers a complimentary breakfast to all guests, so you do not need to pay extra for coffee and toast in the morning.","t":"飯店為所有房客提供免費的早餐，所以你早上不需要另外付錢買咖啡和吐司。"},{"w":"component","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts that something is made of","c":"零件；組成部分","s":"If one small component of the engine breaks, the whole car may stop working, so mechanics check every part carefully.","t":"如果引擎的一個小零件壞了，整輛車可能就無法運作，所以技師會仔細檢查每個部分。","h":1},{"w":"component","p":"adj.","d":"forming a part of something","c":"組成的","s":"The teacher explained the three component parts of a good essay: a clear beginning, a strong middle, and a short ending.","t":"老師解釋了一篇好文章的三個組成部分：清楚的開頭、有力的中段和簡短的結尾。"},{"w":"a key component","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very important part of something","c":"關鍵的組成部分","s":"Regular exercise is a key component of a healthy life, and doctors say thirty minutes a day is enough to make a difference.","t":"規律運動是健康生活的關鍵部分，醫生說每天三十分鐘就足以帶來改變。"},{"w":"compose","p":"v.","d":"to form or make up something; to write music","c":"組成；作曲","s":"Our class is composed of thirty students, and about half of them come from towns outside the city.","t":"我們班由三十名學生組成，其中大約一半來自市外的城鎮。","a":"composed"},{"w":"compound","p":"n.","d":"a substance made of two or more elements","c":"化合物","s":"Water is a compound made of hydrogen and oxygen, which is why its chemical name is written as H2O.","t":"水是由氫和氧組成的化合物，這就是為什麼它的化學名稱寫成 H2O。","h":1},{"w":"compound","p":"adj.","d":"made of two or more parts","c":"複合的","s":"A compound sentence joins two complete ideas with a word like 'and' or 'but', so it is longer than a simple sentence.","t":"複合句用 and 或 but 這類字把兩個完整的想法連起來，所以它比簡單句長。"},{"w":"compound","p":"v.","d":"to make a problem worse","c":"使惡化；加重","s":"The company's money problems were compounded by the sudden rise in oil prices, and it had to close two factories.","t":"油價突然上漲加重了這家公司的財務問題，它不得不關閉兩座工廠。","a":"compounded"},{"w":"compound word","p":"n.phr.","d":"a word made by joining two words","c":"複合詞","s":"'Toothbrush' is a compound word because it joins 'tooth' and 'brush' into one new word that everybody understands.","t":"toothbrush 是一個複合詞，因為它把 tooth 和 brush 結合成一個大家都懂的新字。"},{"w":"comprehend","p":"v.","d":"to understand something fully","c":"理解；領會","s":"The lecture was given in very fast English, so the exchange students could not comprehend everything the professor said.","t":"這場演講用非常快的英語進行，所以交換學生無法理解教授說的每一句話。","h":1},{"w":"comprehension","p":"n.","d":"the ability to understand something","c":"理解（力）","s":"Reading comprehension is tested in the second part of the exam, where students answer questions about a short article.","t":"閱讀理解在考試的第二部分測驗，學生要回答關於一篇短文的問題。","h":1},{"w":"comprehensive","p":"adj.","d":"including everything or almost everything","c":"全面的；綜合的","s":"The travel guide gives a comprehensive list of hotels, restaurants, and bus routes, so you will not need any other book.","t":"這本旅遊指南提供全面的飯店、餐廳和公車路線清單，所以你不需要其他任何書。"},{"w":"comprehensible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be understood","c":"可理解的；易懂的","s":"The doctor explained the illness in simple words that were comprehensible even to the patient's eight-year-old son.","t":"醫生用簡單的話解釋這種病，連病人八歲的兒子都聽得懂。"},{"w":"incomprehensible","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to understand","c":"無法理解的","s":"The old legal paper was written in language so incomprehensible that even the lawyer had to read it three times.","t":"那份舊的法律文件用語晦澀難懂，連律師都得讀三遍。"},{"w":"comprise","p":"v.","d":"to consist of; to be made up of","c":"包含；由…組成","s":"The exam will comprise three parts: a listening test, a reading test, and a short piece of writing about your hobbies.","t":"這場考試將包含三個部分：聽力測驗、閱讀測驗，以及一篇關於你嗜好的短文。","h":1},{"w":"comprise","p":"v.","d":"to form or make up a part of a whole","c":"構成；佔","s":"Women now comprise nearly half of the workers in the company, which was not true twenty years ago.","t":"女性現在佔這家公司員工近一半，而二十年前並非如此。"},{"w":"be comprised of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be made up of","c":"由…組成","s":"The committee is comprised of two teachers, three parents, and one student who was chosen by the whole school.","t":"這個委員會由兩位老師、三位家長和一位全校選出的學生組成。","a":"is comprised of"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement in which each side gives up something","c":"妥協；折衷","s":"After arguing for an hour about where to go on holiday, my parents finally reached a compromise: three days at the beach and two in the mountains.","t":"為了去哪裡度假爭論了一小時後，我爸媽終於達成妥協：三天在海邊，兩天在山上。","h":1},{"w":"compromise","p":"v.","d":"to agree by each side giving up something","c":"妥協；讓步","s":"If neither side is willing to compromise, the strike could last for weeks and hurt both the workers and the company.","t":"如果雙方都不願意妥協，罷工可能持續數週，傷害工人也傷害公司。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"v.","d":"to harm or weaken something","c":"危及；損害","s":"Staying up late every night will compromise your health, and you may find it hard to concentrate in class.","t":"每晚熬夜會損害你的健康，你可能會發現上課很難專心。"},{"w":"reach a compromise","p":"v.phr.","d":"to agree on a middle way","c":"達成妥協","s":"The two brothers reached a compromise about the bedroom: one gets the window side and the other gets the bigger closet.","t":"兩兄弟對臥室的安排達成了妥協：一個拿靠窗的那邊，另一個拿比較大的衣櫃。","a":"reached a compromise"},{"w":"compulsory","p":"adj.","d":"required by law or rules; that you must do","c":"義務的；強制的","s":"Wearing a helmet is compulsory for everyone who rides a scooter in Taiwan, and the police give fines to riders without one.","t":"在台灣，所有騎機車的人都必須戴安全帽，警察會對沒戴的騎士開罰單。","h":1},{"w":"compulsory education","p":"n.phr.","d":"schooling that all children must receive by law","c":"義務教育","s":"In Taiwan, compulsory education lasts for nine years, so every child must go to school from age six to fifteen.","t":"在台灣，義務教育有九年，所以每個孩子從六歲到十五歲都必須上學。"},{"w":"compel","p":"v.","d":"to force someone to do something","c":"強迫；迫使","s":"The heavy snow compelled the airline to cancel all of its flights, and hundreds of passengers slept in the airport.","t":"大雪迫使航空公司取消所有航班，數百名乘客在機場過夜。","a":"compelled"},{"w":"compulsion","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to do something that is hard to control","c":"強迫；難以抑制的衝動","s":"He felt a strange compulsion to check his phone every few minutes, even when he knew there were no new messages.","t":"他有一種奇怪的衝動，每隔幾分鐘就要查看手機，即使他知道沒有新訊息。"},{"w":"conceal","p":"v.","d":"to hide something carefully","c":"隱藏；隱瞞","s":"The thief tried to conceal the stolen watch inside his shoe, but the security guard found it at the exit.","t":"小偷試圖把偷來的手錶藏在鞋子裡，但警衛在出口處發現了它。","h":1},{"w":"conceal the truth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep the real facts secret","c":"隱瞞真相","s":"The company tried to conceal the truth about the broken machine, but a worker told a newspaper what had really happened.","t":"公司試圖隱瞞機器故障的真相，但一名工人把真正發生的事告訴了報社。"},{"w":"concealed","p":"adj.","d":"hidden from view","c":"隱蔽的；隱藏的","s":"The old house has a concealed door behind the bookshelf that leads to a small room nobody knew about.","t":"這棟老房子書架後面有一扇隱藏的門，通往一個沒人知道的小房間。"},{"w":"concealment","p":"n.","d":"the act of hiding something","c":"隱藏；隱瞞","s":"The concealment of the company's real profits from the government led to a long court case and a large fine.","t":"這家公司向政府隱瞞真實獲利，導致了漫長的官司和鉅額罰款。"},{"w":"concede","p":"v.","d":"to admit that something is true, often unwillingly","c":"（不情願地）承認","s":"After seeing the video, the coach had to concede that the referee's decision was correct, even though his team lost.","t":"看過影片後，教練不得不承認裁判的判決是正確的，即使他的球隊輸了。","h":1},{"w":"concede defeat","p":"v.phr.","d":"to accept that you have lost","c":"承認失敗；認輸","s":"The candidate conceded defeat shortly after midnight when it became clear that she could not win enough votes.","t":"午夜過後不久，當情況明朗她無法贏得足夠選票時，這位候選人承認敗選。","a":"conceded defeat"},{"w":"concession","p":"n.","d":"something you give up in order to end an argument","c":"讓步","s":"The workers agreed to return to work after the company made a small concession and raised their pay by three percent.","t":"公司做出小小讓步、把薪水提高百分之三之後，工人們同意回去工作。"},{"w":"conceive","p":"v.","d":"to think of a new idea or plan","c":"構想；想出","s":"The young engineer conceived the idea for the folding bicycle while she was stuck in traffic on her way to work.","t":"這位年輕工程師在上班途中塞車時想出了摺疊腳踏車的點子。","a":"conceived","h":1},{"w":"conceive of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to imagine something","c":"想像","s":"A hundred years ago, people could not conceive of a world in which everyone carried a small phone in their pocket.","t":"一百年前，人們無法想像一個每個人口袋裡都帶著小手機的世界。","h":1},{"w":"conception","p":"n.","d":"an idea of what something is like","c":"概念；構想","s":"Many people have a wrong conception of what a scientist's daily work is like, thinking it is all exciting discoveries.","t":"許多人對科學家的日常工作有錯誤的概念，以為全都是令人興奮的發現。"},{"w":"concept","p":"n.","d":"an idea or principle","c":"概念","s":"The concept of sharing a car with strangers was strange to my grandfather, but now he uses the app every week.","t":"和陌生人共乘一輛車的概念對我爺爺來說很奇怪，但現在他每週都用那個 App。"},{"w":"conceivable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to imagine","c":"可想像的；可能的","s":"The store sells every conceivable kind of tea, from cheap tea bags to rare leaves that cost thousands of dollars.","t":"這家店販售每一種想得到的茶，從便宜的茶包到要價數千元的稀有茶葉都有。"},{"w":"condemn","p":"v.","d":"to say strongly that something is wrong","c":"譴責","s":"World leaders were quick to condemn the attack on the hospital, calling it a terrible crime against innocent people.","t":"世界各國領袖迅速譴責對醫院的攻擊，稱之為對無辜民眾的可怕罪行。","h":1},{"w":"be condemned to death","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be given the punishment of death","c":"被判死刑","s":"In the old story, the prisoner was condemned to death for a crime he did not commit, but the king's daughter saved him at the last minute.","t":"在那個古老的故事裡，囚犯因為一樁他沒犯的罪被判死刑，但國王的女兒在最後一刻救了他。","a":"was condemned to death"},{"w":"condemnation","p":"n.","d":"strong public criticism","c":"譴責","s":"The company's decision to dump waste into the river brought condemnation from environmental groups all over the country.","t":"這家公司把廢棄物倒進河裡的決定，招來全國環保團體的譴責。"},{"w":"condemned","p":"adj.","d":"officially declared unsafe to use","c":"被宣告危險而不能使用的","s":"The condemned building has been empty since the earthquake, and the city plans to pull it down next month.","t":"這棟被宣告危險的建築自地震後就一直空著，市政府計畫下個月拆除它。"},{"w":"conduct","p":"v.","d":"to organize and carry out something such as a study","c":"進行；實施","s":"The scientists will conduct a survey of three thousand teenagers to find out how many hours they sleep each night.","t":"科學家將進行一項三千名青少年的調查，以了解他們每晚睡幾個小時。","h":1},{"w":"conduct","p":"n.","d":"the way a person behaves","c":"行為；品行","s":"The school gives a prize each year for good conduct, and this year it went to a boy who helped a classmate in a wheelchair.","t":"學校每年頒發品行優良獎，今年得主是一個幫助坐輪椅同學的男孩。"},{"w":"conduct","p":"v.","d":"to carry electricity or heat; to lead an orchestra","c":"傳導；指揮","s":"Metals such as copper conduct electricity very well, which is why they are used to make wires.","t":"像銅這樣的金屬非常能傳導電，這就是為什麼它們被用來製造電線。"},{"w":"conductor","p":"n.","d":"a person who leads an orchestra; a material that carries electricity","c":"指揮；導體","s":"The conductor raised her hands, the hall became silent, and the orchestra began to play the first notes of the symphony.","t":"指揮舉起雙手，大廳安靜下來，樂團開始演奏交響曲的第一個音符。"},{"w":"code of conduct","p":"n.phr.","d":"a set of rules about how to behave","c":"行為準則","s":"Every new employee must read and sign the company's code of conduct before starting work on the first day.","t":"每位新員工在第一天開始工作前，都必須閱讀並簽署公司的行為準則。"},{"w":"confession","p":"n.","d":"a statement admitting that you did something wrong","c":"坦白；自白","s":"After three hours of questions, the police finally got a full confession from the man who had robbed the bank.","t":"經過三小時的訊問，警方終於從搶銀行的男子那裡得到完整的自白。","h":1},{"w":"confess","p":"v.","d":"to admit that you have done something wrong","c":"承認；坦白","s":"I have to confess that I ate the last piece of cake, even though I told Mom it was my brother.","t":"我必須承認最後一塊蛋糕是我吃的，雖然我跟媽媽說是我弟弟。"},{"w":"confess to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to admit doing something wrong","c":"承認（做了某事）","s":"The boy finally confessed to breaking the window after his mother promised that she would not be angry.","t":"在媽媽保證不會生氣之後，男孩終於承認打破了窗戶。","a":"confessed to"},{"w":"make a confession","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell the truth about something you did","c":"坦白；認罪","s":"Before the wedding, he made a confession to his best friend: he had never actually learned how to dance.","t":"婚禮前，他向最好的朋友坦白了一件事：他其實從來沒學過跳舞。","a":"made a confession"},{"w":"confidential","p":"adj.","d":"meant to be kept secret","c":"機密的","s":"The doctor keeps all patient records confidential, so nobody outside the hospital can see your medical history without permission.","t":"醫生將所有病人紀錄保持機密，所以醫院以外的人未經許可無法查看你的病史。","h":1},{"w":"confidentially","p":"adv.","d":"in secret; privately","c":"秘密地；私下地","s":"The manager told me confidentially that the company plans to open a new office in Japan next year, so please keep it quiet.","t":"經理私下告訴我公司計畫明年在日本開設新辦公室，所以請保密。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n.","d":"belief in yourself; trust in someone","c":"信心；信任","s":"Practicing in front of a mirror every evening gave her the confidence to give the speech without reading from her notes.","t":"每天晚上對著鏡子練習，讓她有信心不看稿子就能發表演說。"},{"w":"in confidence","p":"phr.","d":"as a secret that should not be shared","c":"私下地；秘密地","s":"She told me in confidence that she was looking for a new job, so I cannot share the news with anyone else.","t":"她私下告訴我她正在找新工作，所以我不能把這個消息告訴其他任何人。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"sure of yourself and your abilities","c":"有自信的","s":"After months of practice, Tom felt confident that he could pass the driving test on his very first try.","t":"經過幾個月的練習，湯姆有信心第一次就能通過駕照考試。"},{"w":"confine","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone or something within limits","c":"限制；關住","s":"Please confine your speech to five minutes, because there are twelve other speakers waiting to present after you.","t":"請把你的演講限制在五分鐘內，因為還有十二位講者在你之後等著上台。","h":1},{"w":"be confined to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be kept within a place and unable to leave it","c":"被限制在…；臥病在…","s":"Grandpa was confined to his bed for two weeks after the operation, so we took turns reading the newspaper to him.","t":"手術後爺爺臥病在床兩週，所以我們輪流讀報紙給他聽。","a":"was confined to"},{"w":"confined","p":"adj.","d":"small and enclosed","c":"狹小的；受限的","s":"Working in a confined space like a submarine can be hard for people who get nervous in small rooms.","t":"在潛水艇這樣狹小的空間工作，對在小房間裡會緊張的人來說可能很辛苦。"},{"w":"confinement","p":"n.","d":"the state of being kept in a place","c":"監禁；限制","s":"After six months of confinement in the small cage, the rescued bear was finally released into a large forest park.","t":"在小籠子裡被關了六個月後，這隻獲救的熊終於被放到一座大型森林公園裡。"},{"w":"conform","p":"v.","d":"to follow rules or behave the same way as others","c":"遵守；順從","s":"Teenagers often feel pressure to conform and wear the same clothes as their friends, even when they do not like the style.","t":"青少年常常感到壓力要隨從眾人、穿和朋友一樣的衣服，即使他們不喜歡那種風格。","h":1},{"w":"conform to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to follow a rule or standard","c":"符合；遵照","s":"All toys sold in the shop must conform to the national safety standards, and each one is tested before it goes on the shelf.","t":"店裡販售的所有玩具都必須符合國家安全標準，每一件上架前都經過測試。"},{"w":"conformity","p":"n.","d":"behavior that follows rules or what other people do","c":"遵守；一致","s":"The school uniform is meant to create a sense of conformity, but many students still find ways to show their own style.","t":"校服的用意是營造一致感，但許多學生仍想辦法展現自己的風格。"},{"w":"conformist","p":"n.","d":"a person who follows rules and customs without question","c":"墨守成規的人","s":"He is not a conformist; he always questions the rules and likes to try new ways of doing things.","t":"他不是個墨守成規的人；他總是質疑規則，喜歡嘗試新的做事方法。"},{"w":"confront","p":"v.","d":"to face a problem or a person directly","c":"面對；對抗","s":"Instead of hiding from the problem, you should confront it directly and talk to your teacher about the missing homework.","t":"與其逃避問題，你應該直接面對它，和老師談談缺交的作業。","h":1},{"w":"be confronted with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be faced with something difficult","c":"面臨；遭遇","s":"When the hikers were confronted with a river too deep to cross, they had to turn back and find another path.","t":"當登山客面臨一條深得無法渡過的河時，他們只好折返另尋路徑。","a":"were confronted with"},{"w":"confrontation","p":"n.","d":"an angry argument or fight between people","c":"衝突；對抗","s":"The teacher stepped in quickly to stop a confrontation between two boys who were shouting at each other in the hallway.","t":"老師迅速介入，制止了兩個在走廊上互相大吼的男孩之間的衝突。"},{"w":"confrontational","p":"adj.","d":"likely to argue or fight with people","c":"好鬥的；挑釁的","s":"His confrontational way of speaking at meetings makes other people feel attacked, so few of them want to work with him.","t":"他在會議上挑釁的說話方式讓其他人覺得受到攻擊，所以很少人想和他共事。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"confrontation – conviction","cards":[{"w":"confrontation","p":"n.","d":"an angry argument or fight between people or groups","c":"衝突；對抗","s":"The teacher stepped in quickly to stop a confrontation between two boys who were shouting at each other in the hallway.","t":"老師迅速介入，制止了兩個在走廊上互相大吼的男孩之間的衝突。","h":1},{"w":"confront","p":"v.","d":"to face a problem or a person directly","c":"面對；對抗","s":"Instead of hiding from the problem, you should confront it directly and talk to your teacher about the missing homework.","t":"與其逃避問題，你應該直接面對它，和老師談談缺交的作業。"},{"w":"be confronted with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be faced with something difficult","c":"面臨；遭遇","s":"When the hikers were confronted with a river too deep to cross, they had to turn back and find another path.","t":"當登山客面臨一條深得無法渡過的河時，他們只好折返另尋路徑。","a":"were confronted with"},{"w":"confrontational","p":"adj.","d":"likely to argue or fight with people","c":"好鬥的；挑釁的","s":"His confrontational way of speaking at meetings makes other people feel attacked, so few of them want to work with him.","t":"他在會議上挑釁的說話方式讓其他人覺得受到攻擊，所以很少人想和他共事。"},{"w":"consecutive","p":"adj.","d":"following one after another without a break","c":"連續的","s":"Our basketball team has won five consecutive games this season, and the players believe they can win the championship.","t":"我們的籃球隊本季已連續贏了五場比賽，球員們相信他們能拿下冠軍。","h":1},{"w":"consecutively","p":"adv.","d":"one after another without a break","c":"連續地","s":"It rained for ten days consecutively last month, so the farmers could not harvest their rice on time.","t":"上個月連續下了十天雨，所以農民無法準時收割稻米。"},{"w":"for the third consecutive year","p":"phr.","d":"for three years in a row","c":"連續第三年","s":"The small bakery won the best-bread award for the third consecutive year, and customers now line up outside before it opens.","t":"這家小麵包店連續第三年贏得最佳麵包獎，現在顧客在開店前就在外面排隊。"},{"w":"consensus","p":"n.","d":"an opinion that all members of a group agree on","c":"共識","s":"After a long discussion, the class finally reached a consensus and decided to hold the party at the beach instead of the park.","t":"經過長時間討論，全班終於達成共識，決定在海邊而不是公園辦派對。","h":1},{"w":"reach a consensus","p":"v.phr.","d":"to come to an agreement that everyone accepts","c":"達成共識","s":"The two families could not reach a consensus on where to hold the wedding, so the young couple chose the place themselves.","t":"兩家人無法就婚禮地點達成共識，所以這對年輕夫妻自己選了地方。"},{"w":"general consensus","p":"n.phr.","d":"what most people agree on","c":"普遍的共識","s":"The general consensus among doctors is that children should sleep at least nine hours a night to stay healthy.","t":"醫生們的普遍共識是，孩子每晚至少要睡九小時才能保持健康。"},{"w":"consent","p":"n.","d":"permission to do something","c":"同意；許可","s":"Students under eighteen need their parents' written consent before they can join the three-day camping trip.","t":"十八歲以下的學生在參加三天露營活動前，需要父母的書面同意。","h":1},{"w":"consent","p":"v.","d":"to agree to something or give permission","c":"同意；答應","s":"Her father finally consented to let her study abroad after she promised to call home every single week.","t":"在她保證每週都會打電話回家之後，她的父親終於同意讓她出國讀書。","a":"consented"},{"w":"consent to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to agree to allow something","c":"同意…","s":"The patient must consent to the operation in writing, and the doctor has to explain every possible risk first.","t":"病人必須以書面同意接受手術，醫生必須先解釋每一個可能的風險。"},{"w":"without sb's consent","p":"phr.","d":"without someone's permission","c":"未經某人同意","s":"The company used the singer's photo in its advertisement without her consent, so she decided to take it to court.","t":"這家公司未經她同意就在廣告中使用了這位歌手的照片，所以她決定提告。","a":"without her consent"},{"w":"conservation","p":"n.","d":"the protection of nature, animals, and natural resources","c":"保護；保育","s":"The students joined a conservation project in the mountains, where they planted trees and cleaned up a small river.","t":"學生們參加了山區的一項保育計畫，在那裡種樹並清理一條小河。","h":1},{"w":"conserve","p":"v.","d":"to use something carefully so it is not wasted; to protect","c":"節約；保護","s":"During the dry season, every family is asked to conserve water by taking shorter showers and fixing leaking taps.","t":"在乾季期間，每個家庭都被要求縮短淋浴時間、修理漏水的水龍頭來節約用水。"},{"w":"conservative","p":"adj.","d":"not liking change; traditional","c":"保守的","s":"My grandparents are quite conservative about clothes, so they were shocked when my cousin dyed her hair bright pink.","t":"我的祖父母對穿著相當保守，所以當我表妹把頭髮染成亮粉紅色時，他們很震驚。"},{"w":"conservative","p":"n.","d":"a person who does not like change","c":"保守派人士","s":"In the debate, the conservatives argued that the old school rules should stay exactly the same for another ten years.","t":"在辯論中，保守派主張舊的校規應該再維持十年完全不變。","a":"conservatives"},{"w":"wildlife conservation","p":"n.phr.","d":"the protection of wild animals and plants","c":"野生動物保育","s":"Many tourists visit the island for its beaches, but wildlife conservation groups worry about the sea turtles that nest there.","t":"許多遊客為了海灘來到這座島，但野生動物保育團體擔心在那裡築巢的海龜。"},{"w":"considerate","p":"adj.","d":"kind and careful about other people's feelings","c":"體貼的；周到的","s":"It was very considerate of you to bring an umbrella for me, because I would have gotten wet walking to the station.","t":"你為我帶傘真是太體貼了，不然我走去車站會被淋濕。","h":1},{"w":"inconsiderate","p":"adj.","d":"not caring about other people's feelings","c":"不體貼的；不顧他人的","s":"It is inconsiderate to play loud music late at night when your neighbors have to get up early for work.","t":"鄰居一早要起床上班，你卻在深夜放大聲的音樂，這很不體貼。"},{"w":"consideration","p":"n.","d":"careful thought; care about other people","c":"考慮；體貼","s":"After much consideration, my parents decided to move to Taichung so that my grandmother would not live alone.","t":"經過深思熟慮的考慮，我爸媽決定搬到台中，這樣奶奶就不會一個人住。"},{"w":"consider","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something","c":"考慮","s":"You should consider all the costs, including rent and food, before you decide to study in a big city.","t":"在決定去大城市讀書之前，你應該考慮所有費用，包括房租和伙食。"},{"w":"take ... into consideration","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think about something when making a decision","c":"把…納入考量","s":"The judges will take into consideration the age of each singer, so younger children are not competing directly with teenagers.","t":"評審會考量每位歌手的年齡，所以年幼的孩子不會直接和青少年競爭。","a":"take into consideration"},{"w":"constitutional","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by or connected with the constitution","c":"憲法的；合憲的","s":"The court decided that the new law was not constitutional, so the government had to rewrite it within six months.","t":"法院裁定新法律不合憲，所以政府必須在六個月內重新修訂。","h":1},{"w":"constitution","p":"n.","d":"the set of basic laws of a country","c":"憲法","s":"The constitution of our country protects the right of every citizen to speak freely and to choose their leaders.","t":"我國的憲法保障每位公民自由發言和選擇領導人的權利。"},{"w":"constitute","p":"v.","d":"to form or make up something","c":"構成；組成","s":"Twelve players constitute a full team, so the coach needs to find two more students before the season begins.","t":"十二名球員組成一支完整的球隊，所以教練需要在球季開始前再找兩名學生。"},{"w":"unconstitutional","p":"adj.","d":"against the constitution","c":"違憲的","s":"Lawyers argued that stopping people from protesting in the park was unconstitutional and asked the court to cancel the rule.","t":"律師主張禁止民眾在公園抗議是違憲的，並請求法院取消這項規定。"},{"w":"constraint","p":"n.","d":"something that limits what you can do","c":"限制；約束","s":"The biggest constraint on our school trip is money, because many families cannot pay for a hotel for three nights.","t":"我們校外教學最大的限制是經費，因為許多家庭無法負擔三晚的飯店費用。","h":1},{"w":"time constraints","p":"n.phr.","d":"limits on how much time you have","c":"時間限制","s":"Because of time constraints, the speaker had to skip the last part of her talk and go straight to the questions.","t":"由於時間限制，講者不得不跳過演講的最後部分，直接進入問答。"},{"w":"constrain","p":"v.","d":"to limit or force someone to do something","c":"限制；約束","s":"The small budget constrained the director, so he filmed the whole movie in one house with only three actors.","t":"少得可憐的預算限制了導演，所以他只用三名演員在一棟房子裡拍完整部電影。","a":"constrained"},{"w":"consultation","p":"n.","d":"a meeting to get advice or discuss something","c":"諮詢；會診","s":"Before the operation, my mother had a long consultation with the surgeon about the risks and how long recovery would take.","t":"手術前，我媽媽和外科醫生進行了一次長時間的諮詢，討論風險以及恢復需要多久。","h":1},{"w":"consult","p":"v.","d":"to ask an expert for advice; to look for information in a book","c":"請教；查閱","s":"If the pain in your knee continues for another week, you should consult a doctor instead of just resting at home.","t":"如果你膝蓋的疼痛再持續一週，你應該去看醫生，而不是只在家休息。"},{"w":"consult with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to discuss something with someone before deciding","c":"與…商量","s":"The principal promised to consult with the students before changing the rules about phones in the classroom.","t":"校長承諾在改變教室手機規定之前會先與學生商量。"},{"w":"consultant","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives expert advice to companies or people","c":"顧問","s":"The restaurant hired a food consultant to help design a healthier menu that still tastes good to customers.","t":"這家餐廳聘請了一位飲食顧問，協助設計更健康卻仍受顧客喜愛的菜單。"},{"w":"consumption","p":"n.","d":"the act of using, eating, or drinking something","c":"消耗；消費；攝取","s":"Doctors say that the consumption of sugary drinks among teenagers has doubled in the past ten years.","t":"醫生說，青少年含糖飲料的攝取量在過去十年增加了一倍。","h":1},{"w":"consume","p":"v.","d":"to use, eat, or drink something","c":"消耗；吃；喝","s":"A big truck can consume more fuel in one day than a small car uses in a whole month.","t":"一輛大卡車一天消耗的燃料，可能比一輛小車一整個月用的還多。"},{"w":"consumer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys goods or uses services","c":"消費者","s":"Many consumers now read online reviews before they buy a phone, so companies pay close attention to customer comments.","t":"現在許多消費者在買手機前會先看網路評論，所以公司非常重視顧客的留言。","a":"consumers"},{"w":"energy consumption","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of energy that is used","c":"能源消耗","s":"The school cut its energy consumption by thirty percent after it replaced all the old lights with LED bulbs.","t":"學校把所有舊燈換成 LED 燈泡後，能源消耗減少了百分之三十。"},{"w":"contagious","p":"adj.","d":"(of a disease) able to spread from one person to another","c":"傳染性的","s":"The flu is highly contagious, so the school asked sick students to stay home until they had no fever for a full day.","t":"流感的傳染性很強，所以學校要求生病的學生待在家裡，直到整整一天沒發燒為止。","h":1},{"w":"contagious","p":"adj.","d":"(of a feeling) spreading quickly to other people","c":"有感染力的","s":"Her laughter was so contagious that soon the whole classroom was laughing, even though nobody knew what the joke was.","t":"她的笑聲太有感染力了，很快整間教室都在笑，雖然沒人知道笑話是什麼。"},{"w":"contagious disease","p":"n.phr.","d":"an illness that passes easily from person to person","c":"傳染病","s":"Washing your hands often is the simplest way to protect yourself from a contagious disease during the winter months.","t":"勤洗手是冬季保護自己免受傳染病侵害最簡單的方法。"},{"w":"contaminate","p":"v.","d":"to make something dirty or poisonous","c":"污染","s":"Chemicals from the old factory began to contaminate the river, and soon the fish in it were no longer safe to eat.","t":"舊工廠的化學物質開始污染河流，很快河裡的魚就不能安全食用了。","h":1},{"w":"contamination","p":"n.","d":"the process of making something dirty or poisonous","c":"污染","s":"After the flood, the city warned people to boil their water because of possible contamination from broken pipes.","t":"洪水過後，市政府警告民眾要把水煮沸，因為管線破裂可能造成污染。"},{"w":"contaminated","p":"adj.","d":"made dirty or poisonous","c":"受污染的","s":"Hundreds of people became sick after eating contaminated food at the festival, and the restaurant was closed for a month.","t":"數百人在園遊會吃了受污染的食物後生病，那家餐廳被關閉了一個月。"},{"w":"contaminant","p":"n.","d":"a substance that makes something dirty or poisonous","c":"污染物","s":"The new filter removes almost every contaminant from the water, so the villagers can finally drink straight from the tap.","t":"新的濾水器能去除水中幾乎所有的污染物，村民們終於可以直接喝自來水了。"},{"w":"contemplate","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something for a long time","c":"沉思；考慮","s":"Sitting by the lake, the old man liked to contemplate his long life and the many changes he had seen in the village.","t":"坐在湖邊，老人喜歡沉思自己漫長的一生以及他在村裡見證過的許多變化。","h":1},{"w":"contemplate doing sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to consider doing something","c":"考慮做某事","s":"After ten years at the same company, she is contemplating leaving her job and opening a small coffee shop near the beach.","t":"在同一家公司待了十年後，她正考慮離開工作，到海邊開一家小咖啡店。","a":"contemplating leaving"},{"w":"contemplation","p":"n.","d":"deep, quiet thought","c":"沉思；冥想","s":"The temple garden is a quiet place for contemplation, and visitors are asked to turn off their phones at the gate.","t":"寺廟的庭園是個適合沉思的安靜場所，訪客在門口就被要求關掉手機。"},{"w":"contemporary","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the present time; modern","c":"當代的；現代的","s":"The museum's new wing shows contemporary art, including a huge painting made entirely of old bus tickets.","t":"博物館的新側廳展出當代藝術，包括一幅完全用舊公車票做成的巨大畫作。","h":1},{"w":"contemporary","p":"adj.","d":"living or happening at the same time","c":"同時代的","s":"The letters give us a contemporary account of the earthquake, written by people who actually lived through it.","t":"這些信件提供了地震同時代的記述，由真正經歷過它的人所寫。"},{"w":"contemporary","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives at the same time as another","c":"同時代的人","s":"Unlike many of his contemporaries, the painter was famous during his own lifetime and sold every picture he finished.","t":"和許多同時代的人不同，這位畫家在世時就很有名，完成的每幅畫都賣出去了。","a":"contemporaries"},{"w":"contemporary music","p":"n.phr.","d":"music written in the present time","c":"當代音樂","s":"Although my grandfather prefers old folk songs, he came to the concert of contemporary music to support my sister.","t":"雖然我爺爺比較喜歡老民謠，他還是來聽當代音樂演奏會以支持我姐姐。"},{"w":"contempt","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that someone or something deserves no respect","c":"輕蔑；鄙視","s":"The old coach felt nothing but contempt for players who gave up before the game was over.","t":"老教練對那些比賽還沒結束就放棄的球員只有輕蔑。","h":1},{"w":"contemptuous","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you think someone deserves no respect","c":"輕蔑的；鄙視的","s":"She gave a contemptuous laugh when her brother said he could cook a better dinner than their mother.","t":"當她弟弟說他能做出比媽媽更好吃的晚餐時，她發出輕蔑的一笑。"},{"w":"with contempt","p":"phr.","d":"in a way that shows no respect","c":"輕蔑地","s":"The manager treated the new workers with contempt, so most of them left the company within their first year.","t":"經理輕蔑地對待新員工，所以大多數人在第一年內就離開了公司。"},{"w":"contend","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is true; to compete","c":"主張；爭奪","s":"The lawyer will contend that his client was at home all evening and could not have been near the bank.","t":"律師將主張他的當事人整個晚上都在家，不可能出現在銀行附近。","h":1},{"w":"contend with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have to deal with a difficult problem","c":"應付；對付","s":"Farmers in the valley have to contend with floods every summer and dry winds every winter.","t":"山谷裡的農民每年夏天必須應付洪水，每年冬天則要對付乾燥的風。"},{"w":"contender","p":"n.","d":"a person who competes for a prize or title","c":"競爭者；角逐者","s":"At only sixteen, she is already a serious contender for a place on the national swimming team.","t":"才十六歲，她就已經是國家游泳隊席位的有力角逐者。"},{"w":"contention","p":"n.","d":"an opinion that someone argues for; disagreement","c":"論點；爭論","s":"It is my contention that students learn more from projects than from tests, and the results of our class support this.","t":"我的論點是學生從專題中學到的比從考試中學到的多，而我們班的成績支持這一點。"},{"w":"continental","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a continent, especially mainland Europe","c":"大陸的；歐洲大陸的","s":"The island has a continental climate in the north, with hot summers and cold winters, unlike the mild coast.","t":"這座島北部屬於大陸性氣候，夏熱冬冷，和溫和的海岸地區不同。","h":1},{"w":"continent","p":"n.","d":"one of the seven large areas of land in the world","c":"洲；大陸","s":"Africa is the second largest continent in the world, and it is home to more than fifty different countries.","t":"非洲是世界第二大洲，有五十多個不同的國家。"},{"w":"continental breakfast","p":"n.phr.","d":"a light breakfast of bread, jam, and coffee","c":"歐陸式早餐","s":"The hotel offers a simple continental breakfast of bread, butter, and coffee, so we bought fruit at the market before leaving.","t":"飯店提供簡單的歐陸式早餐，只有麵包、奶油和咖啡，所以我們出發前在市場買了水果。"},{"w":"contractor","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that does building work for others","c":"承包商","s":"My parents hired a contractor to rebuild the kitchen, and the whole job took almost two months to finish.","t":"我爸媽聘請一位承包商重建廚房，整個工程花了將近兩個月才完成。","h":1},{"w":"contract","p":"n.","d":"a written legal agreement between people or companies","c":"合約","s":"Read every page of the contract carefully before you sign it, because it says you cannot leave the job for two years.","t":"簽名前請仔細閱讀合約的每一頁，因為上面寫著你兩年內不能離職。"},{"w":"contract","p":"v.","d":"to get a serious disease; to become smaller","c":"感染；收縮","s":"Travelers who contract the disease in the jungle usually get a high fever within a week of returning home.","t":"在叢林裡感染這種疾病的旅客，通常在回家一週內就會發高燒。"},{"w":"sign a contract","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put your name on a legal agreement","c":"簽約","s":"The young singer signed a contract with a famous music company last week, and her first album will come out in May.","t":"這位年輕歌手上週和一家知名唱片公司簽約，她的第一張專輯將在五月發行。","a":"signed a contract"},{"w":"contradiction","p":"n.","d":"a difference between two statements that cannot both be true","c":"矛盾","s":"There is a clear contradiction between what the witness said yesterday and what he told the police two weeks ago.","t":"證人昨天說的話和他兩週前告訴警方的內容有明顯的矛盾。","h":1},{"w":"contradict","p":"v.","d":"to say that the opposite of something is true","c":"反駁；與…矛盾","s":"The new study seems to contradict the old belief that eating eggs every day is bad for your heart.","t":"這項新研究似乎推翻了每天吃蛋對心臟不好的舊觀念。"},{"w":"contradictory","p":"adj.","d":"containing ideas that cannot both be true","c":"矛盾的","s":"The two weather reports were completely contradictory: one promised sunshine, while the other warned of heavy rain.","t":"兩份天氣預報完全矛盾：一份保證晴天，另一份卻警告有大雨。"},{"w":"controversial","p":"adj.","d":"causing a lot of disagreement","c":"有爭議的","s":"The plan to build a shopping mall on the old farmland is highly controversial, and hundreds of people protested outside city hall.","t":"在舊農地上蓋購物中心的計畫非常有爭議，數百人在市政府外抗議。","h":1},{"w":"controversy","p":"n.","d":"a lot of public disagreement about something","c":"爭議","s":"The decision to close the small school caused great controversy in the village, and parents wrote angry letters to the newspaper.","t":"關閉小學的決定在村裡引起極大爭議，家長們寫了憤怒的信給報社。","h":1},{"w":"cause controversy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make many people argue about something","c":"引起爭議","s":"The singer's new video caused controversy as soon as it came out, because some people found the dancing inappropriate.","t":"這位歌手的新影片一推出就引起爭議，因為有些人認為舞蹈不恰當。","a":"caused controversy"},{"w":"controversial issue","p":"n.phr.","d":"a topic that people strongly disagree about","c":"有爭議的議題","s":"Whether students should wear uniforms is still a controversial issue in many schools, and every year the debate starts again.","t":"學生是否該穿制服在許多學校仍是個有爭議的議題，每年這場辯論都會重新開始。"},{"w":"conversion","p":"n.","d":"the act of changing something into a different form","c":"轉換；改變","s":"The conversion of the old train station into a public library took three years and cost the city millions of dollars.","t":"把舊火車站改建成公共圖書館花了三年，讓市政府耗費數百萬元。","h":1},{"w":"convert","p":"v.","d":"to change something into a different form or use","c":"轉換；改變","s":"My uncle decided to convert his garage into a small studio where he can paint on weekends.","t":"我叔叔決定把車庫改造成一間小畫室，讓他週末可以畫畫。","h":1},{"w":"convert into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change something into something else","c":"把…轉變成…","s":"Solar panels on the roof convert sunlight electricity, which cuts the family's power bill almost in half.","t":"屋頂上的太陽能板把陽光轉換成電力，讓這家人的電費幾乎減半。","a":"convert"},{"w":"convert","p":"n.","d":"a person who has changed to a new religion or belief","c":"皈依者；改變信念的人","s":"After years of eating meat every day, my brother is now a true convert to vegetarian food and even cooks for us.","t":"多年來每天吃肉的哥哥現在是素食的忠實信徒，甚至還為我們下廚。"},{"w":"convertible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed into something else","c":"可轉換的；可改變的","s":"The sofa is convertible into a bed, so guests can sleep comfortably in the living room when they visit.","t":"這張沙發可以變成床，所以客人來訪時可以舒服地睡在客廳。"},{"w":"convict","p":"v.","d":"to decide in a court that someone is guilty of a crime","c":"定罪","s":"The court did not have enough evidence to convict the man, so he walked out of the building a free person.","t":"法院沒有足夠證據將這名男子定罪，所以他以自由之身走出法院。","h":1},{"w":"conviction","p":"n.","d":"the act of finding someone guilty in a court","c":"定罪；判罪","s":"Because of his earlier conviction for stealing, the shop owner refused to give him a job behind the counter.","t":"由於他先前偷竊的前科，店主拒絕讓他在櫃檯工作。","h":1},{"w":"conviction","p":"n.","d":"a strong belief or opinion","c":"堅定的信念","s":"She spoke with such conviction about saving the forest that even the businessmen in the room began to listen.","t":"她談到拯救森林時充滿堅定的信念，連房間裡的商人也開始聽她說。"},{"w":"convict","p":"n.","d":"a person who has been found guilty and sent to prison","c":"囚犯；罪犯","s":"The escaped convict was caught two days later when he tried to buy a train ticket with a stolen credit card.","t":"逃跑的囚犯兩天後試圖用偷來的信用卡買火車票時被抓到了。"},{"w":"be convicted of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be found guilty of a crime","c":"被判…罪","s":"The driver was convicted of dangerous driving and lost his license for two years after the accident on the highway.","t":"高速公路上的事故發生後，這名駕駛被判危險駕駛罪，吊銷駕照兩年。","a":"was convicted of"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"coordinate – curriculum","cards":[{"w":"coordinate","p":"v.","d":"to organize different people or things so they work well together","c":"協調；統籌","s":"The school asked Ms. Chen to coordinate the sports day, so she has to plan every game and find enough helpers.","t":"學校請陳老師統籌運動會，所以她必須規劃每一項比賽並找到足夠的幫手。","h":1},{"w":"coordinate","p":"n.","d":"one of the numbers that show the exact position of a point on a map","c":"座標","s":"The rescue team found the lost hikers quickly because the hikers had sent the coordinates of their location by phone.","t":"救難隊很快找到迷路的登山客，因為登山客用手機傳送了他們位置的座標。","a":"coordinates"},{"w":"coordination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make different parts of your body work together; organizing things together","c":"協調（能力）","s":"Dancing and playing basketball both require good coordination between your eyes, hands, and feet, so practice every day.","t":"跳舞和打籃球都需要眼、手、腳之間良好的協調能力，所以要每天練習。"},{"w":"coordinator","p":"n.","d":"a person who organizes the different parts of an activity","c":"協調者；統籌人","s":"As the coordinator of the school festival, Jenny had to call every class leader and make sure each stall was ready.","t":"身為校慶的統籌人，珍妮必須打電話給每位班長，確認每個攤位都準備好了。"},{"w":"copyright","p":"n.","d":"the legal right to control the copying of a book, song, or picture","c":"版權；著作權","s":"The singer owns the copyright to all her songs, so nobody can use them in a film without paying her first.","t":"這位歌手擁有她所有歌曲的版權，所以沒有人能不先付錢就把它們用在電影裡。","h":1},{"w":"copyright","p":"v.","d":"to get the legal right to control copies of your work","c":"為…取得版權","s":"The young writer decided to copyright her story before posting it online, so that nobody could sell it as their own.","t":"這位年輕作家決定在上傳故事之前先登記版權，這樣就沒有人能把它當成自己的作品出售。"},{"w":"copyright law","p":"n.phr.","d":"the law that protects the work of writers, artists, and musicians","c":"著作權法","s":"Under copyright law, copying a whole textbook for your classmates is illegal, even if you do not sell the copies.","t":"根據著作權法，為同學影印整本課本是違法的，即使你沒有販售那些影本。"},{"w":"copyrighted","p":"adj.","d":"protected by copyright","c":"受版權保護的","s":"The video was removed from the website because it used copyrighted music without permission from the band.","t":"這部影片被網站移除，因為它未經樂團許可就使用了受版權保護的音樂。"},{"w":"core","p":"n.","d":"the central or most important part of something","c":"核心；中心","s":"Honesty is at the core of a good friendship, and friends who lie to each other rarely stay close for long.","t":"誠實是良好友誼的核心，彼此說謊的朋友很少能長久親近。","h":1},{"w":"core","p":"n.","d":"the hard middle part of a fruit such as an apple","c":"果核","s":"After eating the apple, my little brother threw the core into the garden, hoping a new tree would grow there.","t":"吃完蘋果後，我弟弟把果核丟進花園，希望那裡會長出一棵新樹。"},{"w":"core","p":"adj.","d":"most important or basic","c":"核心的；主要的","s":"Math, Chinese, and English are core subjects at our school, so every student has to study them for three years.","t":"數學、國文和英文是我們學校的核心科目，所以每個學生都必須修讀三年。"},{"w":"core values","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most important beliefs of a person or organization","c":"核心價值","s":"The company's core values are honesty, respect, and teamwork, and new workers learn about them on their first day.","t":"這家公司的核心價值是誠實、尊重和團隊合作，新員工在第一天就會學到這些。"},{"w":"to the core","p":"phr.","d":"completely; in every way","c":"徹底地；骨子裡","s":"My grandfather is a farmer to the core; even at eighty, he still gets up at five every morning to check his fields.","t":"我爺爺骨子裡就是個農夫；即使八十歲了，他仍然每天早上五點起床去看田。"},{"w":"corporate","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a large company","c":"公司的；企業的","s":"After ten years in a small shop, she found the corporate world very different, with long meetings and strict dress rules.","t":"在小店工作十年後，她發現企業界非常不同，有冗長的會議和嚴格的服裝規定。","h":1},{"w":"corporation","p":"n.","d":"a large company or group of companies","c":"大公司；企業","s":"The small coffee shop was bought by a large corporation last year, and now the menu is the same in every city.","t":"這家小咖啡店去年被一家大企業買下，現在每個城市的菜單都一樣。","h":1},{"w":"corporate culture","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way people think and behave in a company","c":"企業文化","s":"The corporate culture at the new company is relaxed, so workers can wear jeans and bring their dogs to the office.","t":"這家新公司的企業文化很輕鬆，員工可以穿牛仔褲，還可以帶狗來辦公室。"},{"w":"incorporate","p":"v.","d":"to include something as part of a whole","c":"納入；包含","s":"The teacher decided to incorporate short videos into her lessons, because students remember stories better than lists of facts.","t":"老師決定把短片納入課程，因為學生對故事的記憶比對一串事實的記憶更好。"},{"w":"correlation","p":"n.","d":"a connection between two things in which one changes when the other does","c":"相關性；關聯","s":"Researchers found a strong correlation between the hours students sleep and the grades they get on their tests.","t":"研究人員發現學生的睡眠時數和考試成績之間有很強的相關性。","h":1},{"w":"correlate","p":"v.","d":"to be connected so that one thing changes when the other changes","c":"相關；有關聯","s":"The study shows that time spent on social media does not always correlate with how lonely a person feels.","t":"研究顯示，花在社群媒體上的時間並不總是和一個人的孤獨感相關。"},{"w":"correlated","p":"adj.","d":"connected with each other","c":"相關的","s":"Height and shoe size are closely correlated, so taller people usually need bigger shoes, though there are exceptions.","t":"身高和鞋子尺寸密切相關，所以高的人通常需要更大的鞋子，不過也有例外。"},{"w":"correspondent","p":"n.","d":"a reporter who sends news from a particular place or about a subject","c":"特派記者；通訊記者","s":"The TV station's correspondent in Tokyo reported live from the street while the earthquake was still shaking the city.","t":"電視台駐東京的特派記者在地震仍在搖晃城市時，從街上現場報導。","h":1},{"w":"correspond","p":"v.","d":"to match or be the same as something; to write letters to someone","c":"相符；通信","s":"The numbers on your ticket should correspond to the seat numbers on the wall, so please check before you sit down.","t":"你票上的號碼應該和牆上的座位號碼相符，所以坐下前請先確認。"},{"w":"correspondence","p":"n.","d":"letters or emails between people","c":"通信；信件","s":"The museum keeps the correspondence between the two famous writers, and visitors can read their letters behind glass.","t":"博物館保存著這兩位名作家之間的信件，參觀者可以隔著玻璃閱讀他們的信。"},{"w":"corresponding","p":"adj.","d":"matching or connected with something you have just mentioned","c":"相對應的","s":"Sales went up by ten percent, but there was no corresponding rise in profit because the cost of materials also increased.","t":"銷售量上升了百分之十，但利潤並沒有相對應的增加，因為原料成本也上漲了。"},{"w":"corridor","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow passage inside a building with doors on each side","c":"走廊","s":"Please do not run in the corridor between classes, because the floor was just washed and someone could easily slip.","t":"下課時請不要在走廊奔跑，因為地板剛洗過，很容易有人滑倒。","h":1},{"w":"corridor","p":"n.","d":"a narrow strip of land or route that connects two places","c":"走廊地帶；通道","s":"The new railway corridor will link the port with the capital, cutting the travel time for goods from two days to five hours.","t":"新的鐵路通道將連接港口與首都，把貨物運送時間從兩天縮短到五小時。"},{"w":"at the end of the corridor","p":"phr.","d":"at the far end of a passage in a building","c":"在走廊盡頭","s":"The nurse told us that the doctor's office was at the end of the corridor, just past the elevators and on the left.","t":"護士告訴我們醫生的辦公室在走廊盡頭，剛過電梯的左手邊。"},{"w":"corrupt","p":"adj.","d":"using power dishonestly for money or personal gain","c":"貪污的；腐敗的","s":"The corrupt official took money from builders and then allowed them to put up unsafe apartments near the river.","t":"那位貪污的官員收了建商的錢，然後允許他們在河邊蓋不安全的公寓。","h":1},{"w":"corrupt","p":"v.","d":"to make someone dishonest or immoral","c":"使腐化；使墮落","s":"Some parents worry that too much money at a young age can corrupt a child and make him lazy and selfish.","t":"有些父母擔心年紀輕輕就有太多錢會使孩子墮落，讓他變得懶惰又自私。","h":1},{"w":"corruption","p":"n.","d":"dishonest behavior by people in power, especially taking money","c":"貪污；腐敗","s":"The mayor promised to fight corruption in the city government, and three officials were arrested within a month.","t":"市長承諾打擊市政府內的貪污，一個月內就有三名官員被逮捕。"},{"w":"corrupted","p":"adj.","d":"(of a computer file) damaged so that it cannot be used","c":"（檔案）損毀的","s":"I could not open my homework this morning because the file had become corrupted when the computer suddenly shut down.","t":"我今天早上打不開作業，因為電腦突然關機時檔案已經損毀了。"},{"w":"counsel","p":"n.","d":"advice, especially from someone older or wiser","c":"忠告；建議","s":"Before choosing a university, Peter sought the counsel of his uncle, who had studied abroad for six years.","t":"在選擇大學之前，彼得向在國外讀了六年書的叔叔尋求建議。","h":1},{"w":"counsel","p":"n.","d":"a lawyer who speaks for someone in court","c":"律師；法律顧問","s":"The counsel for the company argued that the workers had been told about the danger before the accident happened.","t":"公司的律師主張，在事故發生之前，工人們已經被告知了危險。","h":1},{"w":"counsel","p":"v.","d":"to give advice to someone with a problem","c":"勸告；輔導","s":"The school nurse was trained to counsel students who feel too stressed before the big exams in January.","t":"校護受過訓練，能輔導在一月大考前感到壓力太大的學生。"},{"w":"counselor","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to help people with problems or plans","c":"輔導員；顧問","s":"The school counselor helped me choose which subjects to take so that I can apply to study medicine later.","t":"學校的輔導員幫我選擇要修哪些科目，讓我之後可以申請讀醫學。"},{"w":"counseling","p":"n.","d":"professional advice given to people with problems","c":"諮商；輔導","s":"After the accident, the hospital offered free counseling to the families, and many said that talking helped them a lot.","t":"事故發生後，醫院為家屬提供免費諮商，許多人說談話對他們幫助很大。"},{"w":"courteous","p":"adj.","d":"polite and respectful","c":"有禮貌的；客氣的","s":"The hotel staff were so courteous that they carried our bags to the room and even brought hot tea for my grandmother.","t":"飯店員工非常有禮貌，他們幫我們把行李提到房間，還為我奶奶送來熱茶。","h":1},{"w":"courtesy","p":"n.","d":"polite behavior; a polite action","c":"禮貌；禮節","s":"It is common courtesy to let older people get on the bus first, especially when the vehicle is very crowded.","t":"讓年長者先上公車是基本的禮貌，尤其是在車上很擠的時候。"},{"w":"courteously","p":"adv.","d":"in a polite way","c":"有禮貌地","s":"Even though the customer was shouting, the young clerk answered courteously and offered to exchange the broken toy.","t":"雖然顧客在大吼，年輕的店員仍然有禮貌地回答，並主動提出要更換壞掉的玩具。"},{"w":"discourteous","p":"adj.","d":"not polite; rude","c":"無禮的","s":"It is discourteous to look at your phone the whole time while someone is talking to you about something important.","t":"當別人在跟你說重要的事時，你卻一直看手機，這是很無禮的。"},{"w":"coverage","p":"n.","d":"the reporting of news on TV, radio, or in newspapers","c":"（新聞）報導","s":"The typhoon received so much coverage that every channel showed the same pictures of flooded streets all evening.","t":"這場颱風受到大量報導，整個晚上每個頻道都在播放相同的街道淹水畫面。","h":1},{"w":"coverage","p":"n.","d":"the area or amount that something such as insurance or a phone signal reaches","c":"涵蓋範圍；保障範圍","s":"Our travel insurance gives full coverage for lost luggage, so we were paid back the cost of the missing suitcase.","t":"我們的旅遊保險對行李遺失提供完整保障，所以遺失行李箱的費用都賠給我們了。"},{"w":"cover","p":"v.","d":"to report on an event for a newspaper or TV station","c":"報導","s":"Two reporters were sent to cover the election in the small town, and they stayed there for a whole week.","t":"兩名記者被派去報導這個小鎮的選舉，他們在那裡待了整整一週。"},{"w":"media coverage","p":"n.phr.","d":"the attention that newspapers and TV give to an event","c":"媒體報導","s":"The little bakery got a lot of media coverage after a famous actor said its bread was the best he had ever eaten.","t":"一位知名演員說這家小麵包店的麵包是他吃過最好的之後，店裡得到了大量媒體報導。"},{"w":"credibility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being believed and trusted","c":"可信度；信譽","s":"The newspaper lost much of its credibility after it printed a story about a flood that had never actually happened.","t":"這家報社在刊登了一則從未真正發生的洪水報導之後，失去了許多信譽。","h":1},{"w":"credible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be believed or trusted","c":"可信的；可靠的","s":"The boy's excuse for missing class was not very credible, because his teacher had seen him at the game center.","t":"這個男孩缺課的理由不太可信，因為老師在遊戲場看到過他。"},{"w":"incredible","p":"adj.","d":"impossible or very hard to believe; extremely good","c":"難以置信的；極好的","s":"It is incredible that a nine-year-old girl swam across the lake alone, but her father filmed the whole thing.","t":"一個九歲女孩獨自游過湖泊實在難以置信，但她爸爸把整個過程都拍下來了。"},{"w":"lose credibility","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop being believed or trusted","c":"失去信譽","s":"A politician who breaks every promise will quickly lose credibility with the people who voted for him.","t":"一個每個承諾都不遵守的政治人物，很快就會在投票給他的人心中失去信譽。"},{"w":"creek","p":"n.","d":"a small narrow river or stream","c":"小溪；溪流","s":"On hot summer afternoons, the children loved to catch tiny fish in the creek that runs behind their grandmother's house.","t":"在炎熱的夏日午後，孩子們喜歡在奶奶家後面的小溪裡抓小魚。","h":1},{"w":"creek","p":"n.","d":"(British English) a narrow area of water where the sea flows into the land","c":"小海灣；小港汊","s":"The fishing boats hide in a quiet creek during storms, where the high rocks protect them from the strong wind.","t":"暴風雨期間，漁船躲在一個安靜的小海灣裡，高高的岩石保護它們不受強風侵襲。"},{"w":"creek bed","p":"n.phr.","d":"the bottom of a creek, where the water flows","c":"溪床","s":"The creek bed was completely dry after three months without rain, and the smooth stones burned under the sun.","t":"三個月沒下雨後，溪床完全乾涸，光滑的石頭在太陽下發燙。"},{"w":"cripple","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it cannot work properly","c":"使癱瘓；嚴重削弱","s":"A single computer virus was able to cripple the bank's whole system, and customers could not get money for two days.","t":"一個電腦病毒就能癱瘓整個銀行系統，顧客兩天都領不到錢。","h":1},{"w":"cripple","p":"v.","d":"to injure someone so that they cannot walk or move normally","c":"使殘廢；使跛","s":"The accident on the mountain road crippled the young driver, and he had to learn to walk again over the next year.","t":"山路上的那場事故使這位年輕駕駛殘廢，接下來一年他必須重新學走路。","a":"crippled"},{"w":"crippled","p":"adj.","d":"unable to move normally; badly damaged","c":"殘廢的；嚴重受損的","s":"The crippled ship floated without power for six hours until a rescue boat arrived and pulled it back to the harbor.","t":"這艘嚴重受損的船在沒有動力的情況下漂流了六小時，直到救援船抵達把它拖回港口。"},{"w":"crippling","p":"adj.","d":"causing serious damage or problems","c":"嚴重損害的；極其沉重的","s":"Many young people in the city face crippling rents, with more than half of their pay going to the landlord each month.","t":"這座城市裡許多年輕人面臨極其沉重的房租，每個月超過一半的薪水都交給房東。"},{"w":"criterion","p":"n.","d":"a standard used to judge or decide something (singular)","c":"標準；準則","s":"The most important criterion for the scholarship is financial need, not grades, so even average students can apply.","t":"這項獎學金最重要的標準是經濟需求而不是成績，所以即使成績普通的學生也可以申請。","h":1},{"w":"criteria","p":"n.","d":"standards used to judge or decide something (plural of criterion)","c":"標準；準則（複數）","s":"The judges will use three criteria to pick the winning poster: a clear message, bright colors, and original ideas.","t":"評審將依據三項標準挑選得獎海報：訊息清楚、色彩鮮明和想法原創。","h":1},{"w":"meet the criteria","p":"v.phr.","d":"to satisfy the required standards","c":"符合標準","s":"Only five of the forty applicants met the criteria for the job, because the others did not speak both English and Japanese.","t":"四十名申請者中只有五人符合這份工作的標準，因為其他人不會同時說英語和日語。","a":"met the criteria"},{"w":"selection criteria","p":"n.phr.","d":"the standards used to choose people or things","c":"甄選標準","s":"The selection criteria for the school team are posted on the gym door, and every player must be able to run two kilometers.","t":"校隊的甄選標準貼在體育館門上，每位球員都必須能跑兩公里。"},{"w":"crucial","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important","c":"至關重要的；關鍵的","s":"The last ten minutes of the game were crucial, and the whole stadium stood up when our team scored the winning goal.","t":"比賽的最後十分鐘至關重要，當我們的球隊踢進致勝球時，整個球場的人都站了起來。","h":1},{"w":"crucially","p":"adv.","d":"in a very important way","c":"至關重要地","s":"The new medicine is cheap and, crucially, it can be stored without a fridge, so it can reach villages far from the city.","t":"這種新藥很便宜，而且至關重要的是，它不需要冰箱也能保存，所以能送到離城市很遠的村莊。"},{"w":"play a crucial role","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very important in making something happen","c":"扮演關鍵角色","s":"Our librarian played a crucial role in the reading program, choosing books that even the students who hate reading enjoyed.","t":"我們的圖書館員在閱讀計畫中扮演了關鍵角色，她挑選的書連討厭閱讀的學生都喜歡。","a":"played a crucial role"},{"w":"crucial to","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very important for something","c":"對…至關重要","s":"Getting enough sleep is crucial to doing well in school, yet many teenagers stay up past midnight playing games.","t":"充足的睡眠對學業表現至關重要，但許多青少年熬夜到午夜過後打電動。"},{"w":"crude","p":"adj.","d":"in its natural state; not yet treated or refined","c":"未加工的；原始的","s":"The ship carries crude oil from the Middle East to Taiwan, where factories turn it into gasoline and plastic.","t":"這艘船把未精煉的原油從中東運到台灣，工廠在那裡把它製成汽油和塑膠。","h":1},{"w":"crude","p":"adj.","d":"simple and rough, not carefully made or planned","c":"粗糙的；簡陋的","s":"The children built a crude boat out of old boards and rope, and to everyone's surprise it actually floated.","t":"孩子們用舊木板和繩子造了一艘簡陋的船，讓大家驚訝的是它真的浮起來了。"},{"w":"crude","p":"adj.","d":"rude and offensive, especially about sex","c":"粗俗的","s":"The comedian's crude jokes made some parents in the audience take their children out of the theater early.","t":"這位喜劇演員粗俗的笑話讓觀眾席中的一些家長提早帶孩子離開劇院。"},{"w":"crude oil","p":"n.phr.","d":"oil in its natural state, taken from under the ground","c":"原油","s":"When the price of crude oil goes up, the cost of gasoline at every station in the country rises within a few days.","t":"當原油價格上漲時，全國每個加油站的汽油價格都會在幾天內上漲。"},{"w":"cruise","p":"n.","d":"a holiday on a large ship that stops at several places","c":"郵輪旅行；巡航","s":"My grandparents are going on a two-week cruise around Japan, and they will visit a different port almost every day.","t":"我的祖父母要去日本進行兩週的郵輪旅行，他們幾乎每天都會造訪不同的港口。","h":1},{"w":"cruise","p":"v.","d":"to travel by ship for pleasure; to move at a steady, comfortable speed","c":"乘船遊覽；以穩定速度行駛","s":"On the highway at night, the bus cruised along at a steady speed while most of the passengers slept.","t":"夜晚在高速公路上，巴士以穩定的速度平穩行駛，大多數乘客都睡著了。","a":"cruised"},{"w":"cruise ship","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large ship that carries passengers on a holiday","c":"郵輪","s":"A huge cruise ship with three thousand tourists arrived at the port this morning, and the shops in town were suddenly full.","t":"一艘載有三千名遊客的巨大郵輪今天早上抵達港口，鎮上的商店突然擠滿了人。"},{"w":"cruise control","p":"n.phr.","d":"a system in a car that keeps it at a steady speed","c":"定速巡航","s":"On long trips, my father uses cruise control so that the car keeps the same speed without him pressing the pedal.","t":"長途旅行時，我爸爸會使用定速巡航，這樣車子不用踩油門也能保持相同速度。"},{"w":"crystal","p":"n.","d":"a hard, clear mineral; a small regular shape formed by a substance","c":"水晶；結晶","s":"The cave was full of white crystals that sparkled like ice when the guide shone her flashlight on the walls.","t":"洞穴裡滿是白色的水晶，當導遊用手電筒照向牆壁時，它們像冰一樣閃閃發光。","a":"crystals","h":1},{"w":"crystal","p":"n.","d":"very high-quality glass","c":"水晶玻璃","s":"Grandma only uses her crystal glasses on New Year's Eve, because they were a wedding gift and are easy to break.","t":"奶奶只在除夕夜使用她的水晶玻璃杯，因為那是結婚禮物，而且很容易破。"},{"w":"crystal clear","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very easy to understand; completely clear","c":"清澈透明的；一清二楚的","s":"The water in the mountain lake was crystal clear, and we could see fish swimming three meters below the boat.","t":"山中湖泊的水清澈透明，我們可以看到魚在船下三公尺處游動。"},{"w":"crystallize","p":"v.","d":"to form crystals; to become clear and fixed","c":"結晶；（想法）變得明確","s":"If you leave the honey in a cold cupboard for a few months, it will slowly crystallize and turn hard and white.","t":"如果你把蜂蜜放在冰冷的櫥櫃裡幾個月，它會慢慢結晶，變硬變白。"},{"w":"cuisine","p":"n.","d":"a style of cooking, especially of a country or region","c":"菜餚；烹飪風格","s":"Thai cuisine is famous for its mix of sweet, sour, and spicy flavors, and the night markets there are full of wonderful smells.","t":"泰國菜餚以酸甜辣交織的風味聞名，那裡的夜市充滿美妙的香味。","h":1},{"w":"local cuisine","p":"n.phr.","d":"the food that is typical of a particular place","c":"當地美食","s":"When we travel, my mother always tries the local cuisine first, because she says food tells you the most about a place.","t":"我們旅行時，媽媽總是先嘗試當地美食，因為她說食物最能讓你了解一個地方。"},{"w":"culinary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with cooking or food","c":"烹飪的；美食的","s":"After high school, my cousin went to a culinary school in Paris, where he learned to make bread and fancy desserts.","t":"高中畢業後，我表哥去了巴黎的一所烹飪學校，在那裡學做麵包和精緻的甜點。"},{"w":"currency","p":"n.","d":"the system of money used in a country","c":"貨幣","s":"Before flying to Korea, Dad changed some money into the local currency so we could buy snacks as soon as we landed.","t":"飛往韓國前，爸爸換了一些當地貨幣，這樣我們一落地就能買零食。","h":1},{"w":"foreign currency","p":"n.phr.","d":"the money of another country","c":"外幣","s":"The bank near the airport exchanges foreign currency twenty-four hours a day, which is useful for travelers on late flights.","t":"機場附近的銀行二十四小時兌換外幣，對搭深夜班機的旅客很方便。"},{"w":"current","p":"adj.","d":"happening or existing now","c":"現在的；目前的","s":"The current school rules do not allow phones in class, but the student council is asking for a change next year.","t":"目前的校規不允許在課堂上使用手機，但學生會正要求明年做出改變。"},{"w":"currently","p":"adv.","d":"at the present time","c":"目前；現在","s":"My older sister is currently studying in Canada, and she plans to come home for Chinese New Year in February.","t":"我姐姐目前在加拿大讀書，她計畫二月回家過農曆新年。"},{"w":"curriculum","p":"n.","d":"the subjects that are taught at a school or college","c":"課程","s":"The new curriculum includes a computer programming class for every student, starting from the first year of senior high school.","t":"新的課程包含每位學生都要上的電腦程式設計課，從高中一年級開始。","h":1},{"w":"extracurricular","p":"adj.","d":"(of activities) done at school but not part of the normal lessons","c":"課外的","s":"Joining an extracurricular club like drama or music can help you make friends and discover talents you never knew you had.","t":"加入戲劇或音樂這類課外社團可以幫你交朋友，並發現你從不知道自己擁有的才能。"},{"w":"extracurricular activities","p":"n.phr.","d":"clubs, sports, and other activities outside normal lessons","c":"課外活動","s":"Universities often look at a student's extracurricular activities, not just test scores, when they decide whom to accept.","t":"大學在決定錄取誰時，通常不只看考試成績，也會看學生的課外活動。"},{"w":"curriculum vitae (CV)","p":"n.phr.","d":"a written record of your education and work experience","c":"履歷","s":"Before applying for the summer job, she updated her curriculum vitae to include the volunteer work she did at the animal shelter.","t":"申請暑期工作前，她更新了履歷，加入她在動物收容所做的志工工作。","a":"curriculum vitae"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"custody – derive","cards":[{"w":"custody","p":"n.","d":"the legal right or duty to take care of a child, or to keep something safe","c":"監護權；保管","s":"After the divorce, the court gave the mother custody of the two children, but their father can visit them every weekend.","t":"離婚後，法院把兩個孩子的監護權判給母親，但他們的父親每個週末都可以探視。","h":1},{"w":"in custody","p":"phr.","d":"kept in prison by the police while waiting for a trial","c":"被拘留；在押","s":"The man who stole the car is now in custody, and the police will question him about two other robberies tomorrow.","t":"偷車的男子現在遭到拘留，警方明天將就另外兩起搶案訊問他。"},{"w":"take sb into custody","p":"v.phr.","d":"to arrest someone and keep them at the police station","c":"拘留某人","s":"The police took him into custody after they found three stolen phones in his backpack at the night market.","t":"警方在夜市發現他背包裡有三支被偷的手機後，將他拘留。","a":"took him into custody"},{"w":"custodian","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to take care of a building or a thing","c":"保管人；管理員","s":"The school custodian locks every door at ten o'clock, so students must leave the building before then.","t":"學校的管理員十點會鎖上每扇門，所以學生必須在那之前離開大樓。"},{"w":"customs","p":"n.","d":"the place at an airport or border where officers check what you bring into a country","c":"海關","s":"When we arrived at the airport in Tokyo, we had to go through customs and show the officer what was inside our bags.","t":"我們抵達東京機場時，必須通過海關，並讓官員看我們袋子裡的東西。","h":1},{"w":"customs officer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who checks bags and goods at an airport or border","c":"海關人員","s":"The customs officer asked my uncle to open his suitcase because the X-ray machine showed something strange inside it.","t":"海關人員要我叔叔打開行李箱，因為 X 光機顯示裡面有奇怪的東西。"},{"w":"custom","p":"n.","d":"a way of behaving that a group of people has had for a long time","c":"習俗","s":"It is a custom in Taiwan to give red envelopes with money to children during the Lunar New Year holiday.","t":"在台灣，農曆新年假期給小孩裝錢的紅包是一種習俗。"},{"w":"customer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys something from a shop or company","c":"顧客","s":"A polite customer thanked the waiter for his help, and he even left a small tip before leaving the restaurant.","t":"一位有禮貌的顧客感謝服務生的幫忙，離開餐廳前甚至留下一點小費。"},{"w":"customary","p":"adj.","d":"usual; done because it is a custom","c":"習慣的；慣例的","s":"It is customary to take off your shoes before you enter a Japanese home, so remember to wear clean socks.","t":"進入日本人家裡之前脫鞋是慣例，所以記得穿乾淨的襪子。"},{"w":"deadly","p":"adj.","d":"able to kill people or animals","c":"致命的","s":"The mushroom looks harmless, but it is actually deadly, and one small piece can kill an adult within a day.","t":"這種蘑菇看起來無害，但其實是致命的，一小片就能在一天內讓成人喪命。","h":1},{"w":"deadly","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; very (used before an adjective)","c":"極其；非常","s":"The lecture was deadly boring, so half of the students in the back row fell asleep before it ended.","t":"這場演講極其無聊，所以後排一半的學生在結束前就睡著了。"},{"w":"dead","p":"adj.","d":"no longer alive; (of a battery or phone) having no power","c":"死的；沒電的","s":"My phone battery is dead, so could you lend me your charger for about half an hour before we leave?","t":"我的手機電池沒電了，你能在我們離開前借我充電器大約半小時嗎？"},{"w":"death","p":"n.","d":"the end of life","c":"死亡","s":"The sudden death of the famous singer shocked her fans, and thousands of them gathered outside the hospital that night.","t":"這位知名歌手的驟然去世震驚了她的歌迷，當晚有數千人聚集在醫院外。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the time by which something must be finished","c":"截止日期","s":"The deadline for the science report is this Friday, so you had better finish your experiment before Wednesday.","t":"科學報告的截止日期是這個星期五，所以你最好在星期三之前完成實驗。"},{"w":"debris","p":"n.","d":"broken pieces left after something is destroyed","c":"碎片；殘骸","s":"After the earthquake, rescue workers searched through the debris of the fallen building for people who might still be alive.","t":"地震過後，救難人員在倒塌大樓的殘骸中搜尋可能還活著的人。","h":1},{"w":"clear away the debris","p":"v.phr.","d":"to remove the broken pieces after a storm or accident","c":"清除碎片殘骸","s":"Volunteers worked all weekend to clear away the debris that the typhoon had left on the beach, filling more than fifty garbage bags.","t":"志工們整個週末努力清除颱風留在海灘上的碎片殘骸，裝滿了五十多個垃圾袋。"},{"w":"space debris","p":"n.phr.","d":"broken pieces of old rockets and satellites that fly around the Earth","c":"太空垃圾","s":"Scientists worry that space debris from old satellites could hit the space station, so they track every piece larger than a tennis ball.","t":"科學家擔心舊衛星的太空垃圾可能撞上太空站，所以他們追蹤每一塊比網球大的碎片。"},{"w":"debut","p":"n.","d":"the first time a performer or player appears in public","c":"首次亮相；初次登台","s":"The young singer made her debut on a TV talent show last year, and now she has millions of fans around Asia.","t":"這位年輕歌手去年在電視選秀節目首次亮相，現在她在亞洲有數百萬粉絲。","h":1},{"w":"make one's debut","p":"v.phr.","d":"to appear or perform in public for the first time","c":"首次登場","s":"The 17-year-old pitcher will make his debut for the national team tonight, and his whole family is flying to Taichung to watch.","t":"這位十七歲的投手今晚將為國家隊首次登場，他全家人都要飛到台中去看。","a":"make his debut"},{"w":"debut album","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first album a singer or band makes","c":"首張專輯","s":"Her debut album sold more than one million copies in its first month, which surprised even the record company that produced it.","t":"她的首張專輯在第一個月就賣出超過一百萬張，連製作它的唱片公司都感到驚訝。"},{"w":"debut","p":"v.","d":"to appear or be shown in public for the first time","c":"首次登場；首次推出","s":"The new electric car will debut at the Taipei auto show in January, and the company hopes it will attract young buyers.","t":"這款新電動車將在一月的台北車展首次亮相，公司希望它能吸引年輕買家。"},{"w":"decay","p":"n.","d":"the slow process of being destroyed, like a tooth or old fruit","c":"腐爛；蛀牙；衰敗","s":"Brushing your teeth twice a day helps prevent tooth decay, which is why the dentist asks you about it at every visit.","t":"每天刷牙兩次有助於預防蛀牙，這就是為什麼牙醫每次看診都會問你這件事。","h":1},{"w":"decay","p":"v.","d":"to slowly go bad or be destroyed","c":"腐爛；衰退","s":"If you leave fruit in a warm kitchen for a week, it will quickly decay and attract many small flies.","t":"如果你把水果放在溫暖的廚房裡一個星期，它會很快腐爛並引來許多小蒼蠅。"},{"w":"decayed","p":"adj.","d":"gone bad; destroyed slowly over time","c":"腐爛的；蛀壞的","s":"The dentist had to remove two decayed teeth from the little boy because he ate candy every day and seldom brushed.","t":"牙醫必須拔掉小男孩兩顆蛀壞的牙齒，因為他每天吃糖果而且很少刷牙。"},{"w":"fall into decay","p":"v.phr.","d":"to slowly become old, broken, and poor","c":"衰敗；年久失修","s":"After the factory closed, the whole town slowly fell into decay, and today most of the shops on the main street are empty.","t":"工廠關閉後，整個小鎮慢慢走向衰敗，如今主街上大多數商店都空了。","a":"fell into decay"},{"w":"deceive","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe something that is not true","c":"欺騙","s":"The salesman tried to deceive the old lady by telling her that the cheap necklace was made of real gold.","t":"那位推銷員試圖欺騙老太太，告訴她那條便宜的項鍊是真金做的。","h":1},{"w":"be deceived into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be tricked into doing something","c":"被騙去做…","s":"Many people were deceived into sending money to a fake charity after they saw its sad photos on social media last month.","t":"許多人上個月在社群媒體上看到悲傷的照片後，被騙捐錢給一個假的慈善機構。","a":"were deceived into"},{"w":"deceit","p":"n.","d":"the act of making people believe something untrue","c":"欺騙；詭計","s":"His whole business was built on deceit, and when the truth came out, hundreds of customers lost their savings.","t":"他的整個事業建立在欺騙之上，真相大白時，數百名顧客失去了積蓄。"},{"w":"deceptive","p":"adj.","d":"making you believe something that is not true","c":"騙人的；誤導的","s":"Looks can be deceptive; the small restaurant does not look special from outside, but its noodles are the best in town.","t":"外表可能是騙人的；這家小餐館從外面看並不特別，但它的麵是鎮上最好吃的。"},{"w":"deception","p":"n.","d":"a trick that makes someone believe something false","c":"欺騙行為；騙局","s":"The magician's show is all about clever deception, and the audience loves trying to guess how each trick is done.","t":"魔術師的表演全是巧妙的欺騙手法，觀眾喜歡猜每個戲法是怎麼變的。"},{"w":"decent","p":"adj.","d":"good enough; of an acceptable standard","c":"像樣的；不錯的","s":"After months of job hunting, my brother finally found a decent job with a fair salary and weekends off.","t":"找了幾個月的工作後，我哥哥終於找到一份有合理薪水又週末休假的像樣的工作。","h":1},{"w":"decent","p":"adj.","d":"honest and kind; behaving in a way people respect","c":"正派的；規矩的","s":"He is a decent man who always returns extra change to the cashier and never tells lies to his friends.","t":"他是個正派的人，總是把多找的零錢還給收銀員，也從不對朋友說謊。"},{"w":"decently","p":"adv.","d":"in a proper or acceptable way","c":"得體地；像樣地","s":"Please dress decently for your grandmother's birthday dinner because the whole family will be there, including your great-uncle.","t":"請為奶奶的生日晚餐穿得得體一點，因為全家人都會到，包括你的舅公。"},{"w":"decency","p":"n.","d":"honest and polite behavior that people respect","c":"正派；禮貌；風度","s":"Even when he lost the game, the young player had the decency to shake hands with his opponent and thank the referee.","t":"即使輸了比賽，這位年輕選手仍有風度與對手握手並感謝裁判。"},{"w":"declaration","p":"n.","d":"an official or public statement","c":"宣言；聲明；申報","s":"The company made a public declaration that it would stop using plastic bags in all of its stores by next year.","t":"該公司公開聲明明年前將在所有門市停止使用塑膠袋。","h":1},{"w":"declare","p":"v.","d":"to say something officially or publicly; to tell customs what you are carrying","c":"宣布；申報","s":"At the airport, you must declare any food or plants you are carrying, or you may have to pay a heavy fine.","t":"在機場，你必須申報攜帶的任何食物或植物，否則可能要付高額罰款。"},{"w":"declare war on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to officially announce that your country will fight another","c":"向…宣戰","s":"In 1941, the United States declared war on Japan after the attack on Pearl Harbor, and the war lasted four more years.","t":"1941 年珍珠港事件後，美國向日本宣戰，戰爭又持續了四年。","a":"declared war on"},{"w":"customs declaration","p":"n.phr.","d":"a form on which you list the goods you are bringing into a country","c":"海關申報單","s":"Fill in the customs declaration form on the plane so that you can pass through the airport more quickly after you land.","t":"在飛機上填好海關申報表格，這樣降落後你就能更快通過機場。"},{"w":"decline","p":"v.","d":"to become smaller, fewer, or weaker","c":"下降；衰退","s":"Sales of printed newspapers have continued to decline because most young people now read the news on their phones.","t":"印刷報紙的銷量持續下滑，因為現在大多數年輕人用手機看新聞。","h":1},{"w":"decline","p":"v.","d":"to politely say no to an offer or invitation","c":"婉拒","s":"She had to decline the invitation to the party because her grandmother was in the hospital that weekend.","t":"她不得不婉拒派對的邀請，因為那個週末她奶奶住院。"},{"w":"decline","p":"n.","d":"a change to a smaller number or a worse state","c":"下降；衰退","s":"The town has seen a sharp decline in its population since the factory moved to another country ten years ago.","t":"自從工廠十年前搬到另一個國家後，這個小鎮的人口出現急劇下降。"},{"w":"on the decline","p":"phr.","d":"becoming less common or less popular","c":"在衰退中；日益減少","s":"Many traditional crafts are on the decline because young people prefer office jobs to learning a skill from an old master.","t":"許多傳統工藝正在衰退，因為年輕人寧願做辦公室工作，也不願向老師傅學習技藝。"},{"w":"declining","p":"adj.","d":"becoming smaller or weaker","c":"逐漸減少的；衰退中的","s":"Because of the declining birth rate, several elementary schools in the countryside will close next year.","t":"由於逐漸下降的出生率，鄉下幾所小學明年將關閉。"},{"w":"dedicate","p":"v.","d":"to give your time and energy to something important","c":"奉獻；致力於","s":"Dr. Lin decided to dedicate her life to helping poor children get a good education in the mountain villages.","t":"林醫師決定奉獻一生幫助山區村落的貧困兒童獲得良好教育。","h":1},{"w":"be dedicated to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be made for one purpose; to give all your effort to something","c":"致力於；專門用於","s":"The new website is dedicated to teaching English grammar, and it offers free exercises for students at every level.","t":"這個新網站致力於教英文文法，為各級學生提供免費練習。","a":"is dedicated to"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"working very hard because you care about something","c":"盡心盡力的；敬業的","s":"Our class is lucky to have such a dedicated teacher who stays after school every day to answer our questions.","t":"我們班很幸運有這麼一位盡心盡力的老師，每天放學後都留下來回答我們的問題。"},{"w":"dedication","p":"n.","d":"hard work and care given to something over a long time","c":"奉獻；敬業","s":"The nurse received an award for her dedication, since she had worked in the same hospital for forty years without missing a shift.","t":"這位護士因她的敬業奉獻獲獎，她在同一家醫院工作了四十年從未缺班。"},{"w":"defendant","p":"n.","d":"the person in a court who is said to have done something wrong","c":"被告","s":"The defendant stood up in court and told the judge that he had been at home with his family on the night of the robbery.","t":"被告在法庭上站起來告訴法官，搶案發生當晚他和家人在家。","h":1},{"w":"defend","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone; to speak for someone in court","c":"保衛；辯護","s":"A lawyer's job is to defend his client in court, even when most people believe the person is guilty.","t":"律師的工作是在法庭上為當事人辯護，即使大多數人認為那個人有罪。"},{"w":"defense","p":"n.","d":"the act of protecting; the players who stop the other team from scoring","c":"防禦；辯護；防守","s":"The team's defense was so strong in the second half that the other side could not score a single point.","t":"這支球隊下半場的防守非常強，對方連一分都得不到。"},{"w":"defensive","p":"adj.","d":"behaving as if you are being attacked; used for protecting","c":"防禦性的；防衛的","s":"Whenever his mother asks about his grades, Kevin becomes defensive and changes the subject as quickly as he can.","t":"每當媽媽問起成績，凱文就變得很防衛，並盡快轉移話題。"},{"w":"defender","p":"n.","d":"a player who stops the other team from scoring; a person who protects something","c":"後衛；捍衛者","s":"The defender kicked the ball away just before the striker could shoot, and the crowd cheered loudly for him.","t":"後衛在前鋒射門前一刻把球踢開，群眾為他大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"deficit","p":"n.","d":"the amount by which money spent is more than money received","c":"赤字；不足額","s":"The government has a large budget deficit this year because it spent much more money than it collected in taxes.","t":"政府今年有龐大的預算赤字，因為它花的錢遠多於收到的稅。","h":1},{"w":"trade deficit","p":"n.phr.","d":"when a country buys more from other countries than it sells to them","c":"貿易逆差","s":"The country has had a trade deficit for years because it buys far more goods from abroad than it sells to other nations.","t":"這個國家多年來一直有貿易逆差，因為它從國外買的商品遠多於賣給其他國家的。"},{"w":"deficient","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough of something important","c":"缺乏的；不足的","s":"People who eat no vegetables are often deficient in vitamin C, so doctors suggest at least three servings a day.","t":"不吃蔬菜的人常缺乏維生素 C，所以醫生建議每天至少吃三份。"},{"w":"deficiency","p":"n.","d":"a lack of something that the body or a system needs","c":"缺乏；缺陷","s":"A deficiency of iron can make you feel tired all the time, and a simple blood test can show whether you have one.","t":"缺乏鐵質會讓你一直覺得疲倦，簡單的血液檢查就能顯示你是否缺鐵。"},{"w":"defy","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to obey a person, rule, or law","c":"違抗；反抗","s":"The teenager decided to defy his parents and go to the concert, even though they had clearly told him to stay home.","t":"這名青少年決定違抗父母去看演唱會，儘管他們明確告訴他要待在家。","h":1},{"w":"defy description","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be so great or strange that words cannot describe it","c":"難以形容","s":"The beauty of the sunrise over the mountains defies description; you really have to see it with your own eyes.","t":"山上日出的美難以形容；你真的必須親眼看看。","a":"defies description"},{"w":"defiant","p":"adj.","d":"openly refusing to obey","c":"反抗的；挑釁的","s":"The little girl gave her mother a defiant look and refused to put on her coat before going outside.","t":"小女孩給了媽媽一個反抗的眼神，出門前拒絕穿上外套。"},{"w":"defiance","p":"n.","d":"open refusal to obey","c":"違抗；反抗","s":"In an act of defiance, the workers kept singing outside the factory gate even after the manager told them to leave.","t":"作為一種反抗行為，工人們在經理叫他們離開後仍繼續在工廠大門外唱歌。"},{"w":"delegate","p":"n.","d":"a person chosen to speak or vote for a group at a meeting","c":"代表","s":"Each country sent one delegate to the climate meeting in Paris, and together they discussed how to reduce air pollution.","t":"每個國家派一位代表參加巴黎氣候會議，他們一起討論如何減少空氣污染。","h":1},{"w":"delegation","p":"n.","d":"a group of people chosen to represent others","c":"代表團","s":"A delegation of twenty Japanese teachers visited our school last week to learn about our English program.","t":"二十位日本教師組成的代表團上週參訪我們學校，了解我們的英語課程。","h":1},{"w":"delegate","p":"v.","d":"to give part of your work or power to someone else","c":"委派；授權","s":"A good manager knows how to delegate tasks to team members instead of trying to do all the work alone.","t":"好的經理知道如何把任務委派給團隊成員，而不是試圖獨自做完所有的工作。"},{"w":"head of the delegation","p":"n.phr.","d":"the leader of a group that represents others","c":"代表團團長","s":"The head of the delegation gave a short speech in Chinese, which made all the students in the hall clap and cheer.","t":"代表團團長用中文發表簡短演說，讓禮堂裡所有學生鼓掌歡呼。"},{"w":"deliberate","p":"adj.","d":"done on purpose, not by accident","c":"故意的","s":"The referee said the push was deliberate, so the player received a red card and had to leave the field.","t":"裁判說那次推人是故意的，所以那名球員被出示紅牌，必須離場。","h":1},{"w":"deliberate","p":"adj.","d":"slow and careful","c":"從容的；慎重的","s":"The old craftsman worked with slow, deliberate movements, checking each piece of wood twice before he cut it.","t":"老工匠以緩慢而慎重的動作工作，每塊木頭切割前都檢查兩次。"},{"w":"deliberate","p":"v.","d":"to think about or discuss something carefully before deciding","c":"仔細考慮；商議","s":"The jury had to deliberate for three days before they finally agreed that the man was not guilty.","t":"陪審團商議了三天，才終於一致認為那名男子無罪。"},{"w":"deliberately","p":"adv.","d":"on purpose","c":"故意地","s":"I believe he deliberately left his homework at home because he had not finished it and did not want the teacher to know.","t":"我相信他是故意把作業留在家裡，因為他沒做完，不想讓老師知道。"},{"w":"deliberation","p":"n.","d":"long and careful thought or discussion","c":"深思熟慮；商議","s":"After much deliberation, the committee chose Kaohsiung as the city for next year's national music competition.","t":"經過多番審慎討論，委員會選擇高雄作為明年全國音樂比賽的城市。"},{"w":"democrat","p":"n.","d":"a person who believes that people should choose their leaders by voting","c":"民主主義者；民主黨人","s":"As a true democrat, my grandfather believes that every adult should have the right to vote, no matter how poor they are.","t":"身為一位真正的民主主義者，我爺爺相信每個成年人無論多窮都應該有投票權。","h":1},{"w":"democracy","p":"n.","d":"a system in which people choose their government by voting; a country with this system","c":"民主；民主國家","s":"In a democracy, people choose their leaders by voting, and the government must listen to what the people want.","t":"在民主國家，人民透過投票選擇領導人，政府必須傾聽人民的需求。"},{"w":"democratic","p":"adj.","d":"based on the idea that everyone has an equal right to vote and decide","c":"民主的","s":"The class made a democratic decision about the trip; everyone voted, and the beach won by just two votes.","t":"全班對旅行做出了民主的決定；每個人都投票，海邊以兩票之差勝出。"},{"w":"democratically","p":"adv.","d":"by a fair vote of all the people","c":"以民主方式","s":"The student council president is chosen democratically each September, and every student in the school can cast a vote.","t":"學生會會長每年九月以民主方式選出，學校每位學生都可以投票。"},{"w":"denial","p":"n.","d":"a statement that something is not true","c":"否認","s":"Despite his strong denial, the video clearly showed the boy taking the money from the teacher's desk.","t":"儘管他強烈否認，影片清楚顯示那男孩從老師桌上拿錢。","h":1},{"w":"deny","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is not true","c":"否認","s":"The player continued to deny that he had touched the ball with his hand, even after watching the replay.","t":"即使看了重播，那名球員仍繼續否認他用手碰過球。"},{"w":"be in denial","p":"phr.","d":"to refuse to accept that something bad is true","c":"拒絕面對現實","s":"My uncle is in denial about his health; he still smokes a pack a day even though his doctor warned him twice.","t":"我叔叔對自己的健康拒絕面對現實；儘管醫生警告過他兩次，他仍每天抽一包菸。","a":"is in denial"},{"w":"undeniable","p":"adj.","d":"so clearly true that nobody can say it is false","c":"不可否認的","s":"It is undeniable that smartphones have changed the way we study, shop, and talk to our friends every day.","t":"智慧型手機改變了我們每天讀書、購物和與朋友交談的方式，這是不可否認的。"},{"w":"density","p":"n.","d":"how many people or things there are in a space","c":"密度","s":"Taipei has a very high population density, so apartments are small and the MRT is crowded during rush hour.","t":"台北的人口密度非常高，所以公寓很小，尖峰時間捷運很擁擠。","h":1},{"w":"dense","p":"adj.","d":"thick; with many people or things close together","c":"稠密的；濃密的","s":"The fog was so dense this morning that drivers could barely see the car in front of them on the highway.","t":"今天早上的霧太濃了，高速公路上的駕駛幾乎看不到前面的車。"},{"w":"densely","p":"adv.","d":"with many people or things close together","c":"稠密地","s":"The island is densely populated, with more than two million people living in an area smaller than Taipei City.","t":"這座島人口稠密，超過兩百萬人住在比台北市還小的區域。"},{"w":"population density","p":"n.phr.","d":"the number of people living in each square kilometer","c":"人口密度","s":"The population density of Hong Kong is one of the highest in the world, which explains why its buildings are so tall.","t":"香港的人口密度是世界最高之一，這解釋了為什麼它的建築那麼高。"},{"w":"depict","p":"v.","d":"to show something in a picture or describe it in words","c":"描繪；描述","s":"The painting on the temple wall depicts a dragon flying over the sea, and visitors love taking photos of it.","t":"廟牆上的畫描繪一條龍飛過大海，遊客很喜歡拍它。","a":"depicts","h":1},{"w":"be depicted as","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be shown or described as a certain kind of person or thing","c":"被描繪成","s":"In many old stories, the fox is depicted as a clever animal that tricks the other creatures in the forest.","t":"在許多古老的故事裡，狐狸被描繪成會欺騙森林裡其他動物的聰明動物。","a":"is depicted as"},{"w":"depiction","p":"n.","d":"the way something is shown in a picture or story","c":"描繪；描述","s":"The movie's depiction of life in a Taiwanese fishing village in the 1960s felt so real that my grandmother cried.","t":"這部電影對 1960 年代台灣漁村生活的描繪真實到讓我奶奶哭了。"},{"w":"deploy","p":"v.","d":"to move soldiers or equipment to a place so they are ready to act","c":"部署；調度","s":"The government decided to deploy two thousand soldiers to the flooded area to help move people to safety.","t":"政府決定部署兩千名士兵到淹水地區，協助把居民移到安全的地方。","h":1},{"w":"deploy","p":"v.","d":"to use something in an effective way","c":"運用；利用","s":"Good teachers deploy different methods in class, such as games and group work, to keep every student interested.","t":"好老師在課堂上運用不同方法，例如遊戲和小組活動，讓每位學生保持興趣。"},{"w":"be deployed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be sent to a place to work, especially as a soldier","c":"被派駐到","s":"My cousin, who is a soldier, was deployed to a small island last month and will stay there for six months.","t":"我表哥是軍人，上個月被派駐到一座小島，將在那裡待六個月。","a":"was deployed to"},{"w":"deployment","p":"n.","d":"the act of moving soldiers or equipment into position","c":"部署","s":"The quick deployment of rescue teams after the earthquake saved many lives in the first few hours.","t":"地震後救難隊迅速的部署在最初幾小時內拯救了許多生命。"},{"w":"depress","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel very sad and without hope","c":"使沮喪；使消沉","s":"Rainy weather for two weeks in a row can really depress people, especially those who love outdoor sports.","t":"連續兩週的雨天真的會讓人沮喪，尤其是熱愛戶外運動的人。","h":1},{"w":"depressed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling very sad and without hope","c":"沮喪的；消沉的","s":"After failing the driving test for the third time, my sister felt so depressed that she did not want to talk to anyone.","t":"第三次駕照考試沒過後，我姐姐覺得非常沮喪，不想和任何人說話。"},{"w":"depressing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel sad and without hope","c":"令人沮喪的","s":"The news about the forest fires was so depressing that I turned off the TV and went for a walk instead.","t":"森林大火的新聞太令人沮喪了，我關掉電視改去散步。"},{"w":"depression","p":"n.","d":"a long period of feeling very sad; a time when business is very bad","c":"憂鬱症；蕭條","s":"The Great Depression of the 1930s left millions of Americans without jobs, and many families lost their homes.","t":"1930 年代的經濟大蕭條使數百萬美國人失業，許多家庭失去了房子。","a":"Depression"},{"w":"deputy","p":"n.","d":"a person who is second in charge and takes over when the leader is away","c":"副手；代理人","s":"When the principal is away on business, the deputy takes charge of the school and signs all the important papers.","t":"校長出差不在時，副手負責管理學校並簽署所有重要文件。","h":1},{"w":"deputy","p":"adj.","d":"second in rank; helping and standing in for the leader","c":"副的","s":"The deputy manager will run the meeting this afternoon because the manager has flown to Japan on business.","t":"副經理將主持今天下午的會議，因為經理已飛往日本出差。"},{"w":"deputy mayor","p":"n.phr.","d":"the person who is second in charge of a city","c":"副市長","s":"The deputy mayor cut the ribbon at the opening of the new library, since the mayor was attending another event that day.","t":"副市長為新圖書館開幕剪綵，因為市長當天出席另一場活動。"},{"w":"derive","p":"v.","d":"to get something, such as pleasure or benefit, from something","c":"獲得；取得","s":"She derives great pleasure from growing vegetables on her balcony, even though she lives in the middle of the city.","t":"她從在陽台種菜中獲得極大的樂趣，儘管她住在市中心。","a":"derives","h":1},{"w":"be derived from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to come from something; to have something as its origin","c":"源自於","s":"The word \"typhoon\" is derived from a Chinese word that means \"big wind,\" and it entered English hundreds of years ago.","t":"「typhoon」這個字源自意思是「大風」的中文詞，數百年前進入英文。","a":"is derived from"},{"w":"derivative","p":"n.","d":"a word or thing that is made from another","c":"衍生詞；衍生物","s":"\"Happiness\" is a derivative of \"happy,\" and learning such word families can help you remember new vocabulary much faster.","t":"「happiness」是「happy」的衍生詞，學習這類字族能幫助你更快記住新單字。"},{"w":"derivation","p":"n.","d":"the origin of a word or thing","c":"詞源；起源","s":"The derivation of the name \"Taiwan\" is still debated, and historians have offered several different explanations over the years.","t":"「Taiwan」這個名稱的起源仍有爭議，多年來歷史學家提出了幾種不同的解釋。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"descend – disrupt","cards":[{"w":"descend","p":"v.","d":"to go or come down","c":"下降；下來","s":"The plane began to descend slowly toward the airport, and the passengers could see the lights of the city below them.","t":"飛機開始慢慢朝機場下降，乘客可以看到下方城市的燈光。","h":1},{"w":"be descended from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be related to a person or family who lived long ago","c":"是…的後代","s":"My grandmother says our family is descended from a famous general who lived in China more than three hundred years ago.","t":"我奶奶說我們家族是一位三百多年前住在中國的名將的後代。","a":"is descended from"},{"w":"descent","p":"n.","d":"the act of going down; your family origin","c":"下降；下山；血統","s":"The descent from the top of the mountain took three hours because the path was wet and very slippery after the rain.","t":"從山頂下山花了三個小時，因為雨後小路又濕又滑。"},{"w":"descendant","p":"n.","d":"a person related to someone who lived long ago","c":"後代；子孫","s":"Many people in this village are descendants of the fishermen who first settled here nearly two hundred years ago.","t":"這個村子裡的許多人是近兩百年前最早在這裡定居的漁民的後代。","a":"descendants"},{"w":"descending","p":"adj.","d":"going from the biggest or highest to the smallest or lowest","c":"遞減的","s":"Please list the students' scores in descending order, starting with the highest and ending with the lowest.","t":"請把學生的分數按遞減順序列出，從最高分開始到最低分結束。"},{"w":"descriptive","p":"adj.","d":"giving a clear picture of something in words","c":"描述性的；描寫的","s":"The writer uses descriptive language so well that readers can almost smell the sea and feel the wind in her stories.","t":"這位作家把描述性的語言運用得非常好，讀者幾乎能在她的故事中聞到海的味道、感受到風。","h":1},{"w":"describe","p":"v.","d":"to say what someone or something is like","c":"描述","s":"Can you describe the man who took your bag, such as his height, his hair, and what he was wearing?","t":"你能描述拿走你包包的那個男人嗎？例如他的身高、頭髮和穿著？"},{"w":"description","p":"n.","d":"words that tell what someone or something is like","c":"描述","s":"The police gave a clear description of the missing boy on the news, and someone found him in a park an hour later.","t":"警方在新聞上對失蹤男孩做了清楚的描述，一小時後有人在公園找到他。"},{"w":"beyond description","p":"phr.","d":"too good, bad, or strange to put into words","c":"無法形容","s":"The view from the top of Taipei 101 at night is beyond description; you really have to go and see it for yourself.","t":"夜晚從台北 101 頂樓看到的景色無法形容；你真的得親自去看看。"},{"w":"despair","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of having no hope at all","c":"絕望","s":"After searching for her lost dog for a whole week, the girl was close to despair, but then a neighbor called with good news.","t":"找了走失的狗整整一週後，女孩幾乎陷入絕望，但接著鄰居打電話來報了好消息。","h":1},{"w":"despair","p":"v.","d":"to lose all hope","c":"絕望；喪失信心","s":"Do not despair if you fail the test the first time; many students pass it on their second or third try.","t":"如果第一次考試沒過，不要絕望；許多學生第二次或第三次就通過了。"},{"w":"in despair","p":"phr.","d":"feeling that there is no hope","c":"絕望地","s":"The farmer looked at his dry fields in despair, because it had not rained for more than two months.","t":"農夫絕望地看著乾涸的田地，因為已經超過兩個月沒下雨了。"},{"w":"desperate","p":"adj.","d":"needing or wanting something very much; feeling hopeless","c":"極度渴望的；絕望的","s":"The family was desperate for news after the earthquake because their son was working in the city when it happened.","t":"地震後這家人極度渴望得到消息，因為地震發生時他們的兒子正在城裡工作。"},{"w":"desperately","p":"adv.","d":"very much; in a way that shows great need","c":"急切地；拚命地","s":"The young mother desperately needed a job, so she applied to every restaurant and shop in the neighborhood.","t":"這位年輕母親急切地需要一份工作，所以她向附近每家餐廳和商店應徵。"},{"w":"destination","p":"n.","d":"the place you are going to","c":"目的地","s":"After a twelve-hour flight, we finally arrived at our destination, a small town by the sea in the south of France.","t":"經過十二小時的飛行，我們終於抵達目的地，一個位於法國南部海邊的小鎮。","h":1},{"w":"tourist destination","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place that many travelers like to visit","c":"觀光景點","s":"Jiufen has become a popular tourist destination because of its old tea houses, narrow streets, and beautiful views of the ocean.","t":"九份因為老茶館、狹窄的街道和美麗的海景，成了熱門的觀光景點。"},{"w":"final destination","p":"n.phr.","d":"the last stop of a journey","c":"最終目的地","s":"This train's final destination is Kaohsiung, but it will stop at Taichung, Chiayi, and Tainan along the way.","t":"這班火車的最終目的地是高雄，但沿途會停靠台中、嘉義和台南。"},{"w":"destiny","p":"n.","d":"the things that will happen to you in the future; fate","c":"命運","s":"Some people believe that everything in life is decided by destiny, while others think we make our own future through hard work.","t":"有些人相信人生中的一切都由命運決定，另一些人則認為我們靠努力創造自己的未來。","h":1},{"w":"destined","p":"adj.","d":"certain to be or do something in the future","c":"注定的","s":"From the day she first held a violin at age four, everyone could see that she was destined to become a musician.","t":"從她四歲第一次拿起小提琴的那天起，每個人都看得出她注定要成為音樂家。"},{"w":"be destined for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be traveling to a place; to be certain to reach something","c":"前往；注定要…","s":"The ship was destined for Japan when a strong storm forced it to turn back to the port in Keelung.","t":"這艘船原本前往日本，但一場強烈暴風雨迫使它折返基隆港。","a":"was destined for"},{"w":"destructive","p":"adj.","d":"causing a lot of damage","c":"破壞性的","s":"The typhoon was the most destructive storm in thirty years, and it took the town almost a year to rebuild.","t":"這場颱風是三十年來最具破壞性的風暴，小鎮花了將近一年才重建。","h":1},{"w":"destroy","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it cannot be used","c":"摧毀；破壞","s":"The fire destroyed the old wooden temple in less than an hour, but luckily nobody was hurt.","t":"大火在不到一小時內摧毀了這座古老的木造寺廟，但幸好沒有人受傷。","a":"destroyed"},{"w":"destruction","p":"n.","d":"the act of destroying something","c":"破壞；毀滅","s":"The destruction of the rain forest continues every day, and many animals are losing the only home they have.","t":"雨林的破壞每天持續進行，許多動物正失去它們唯一的家。"},{"w":"self-destructive","p":"adj.","d":"harmful to yourself","c":"自我毀滅的；自殘的","s":"Staying up all night before an important exam is self-destructive behavior, because a tired brain cannot remember what it learned.","t":"重要考試前整夜不睡是自我毀滅的行為，因為疲倦的大腦記不住學過的東西。"},{"w":"devotion","p":"n.","d":"great love or loyalty that makes you give a lot of time and care","c":"奉獻；忠誠；熱愛","s":"The old teacher's devotion to her students was so great that she kept teaching for free after she retired.","t":"這位老教師對學生的奉獻如此深厚，退休後她仍繼續免費教學。","h":1},{"w":"devote","p":"v.","d":"to give your time or effort to something","c":"奉獻；投入","s":"My father decided to devote his weekends to coaching the school basketball team, even though he was not paid for it.","t":"我父親決定把週末奉獻給指導學校籃球隊，即使他沒有因此得到報酬。"},{"w":"devote oneself to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spend most of your time and energy on something","c":"致力於","s":"After the accident, the doctor devoted herself to helping children who had lost the use of their legs.","t":"那場意外之後，這位醫師致力於幫助失去雙腿功能的孩子。","a":"devoted herself to"},{"w":"devoted","p":"adj.","d":"loving someone or something very much","c":"忠誠的；深愛的","s":"He is a devoted father who never misses his daughter's piano concerts, even when he has to leave work early.","t":"他是個深愛孩子的父親，從不錯過女兒的鋼琴演奏會，即使必須提早下班。"},{"w":"diagnose","p":"v.","d":"to find out what illness or problem someone has","c":"診斷","s":"After looking at the X-ray, the doctor was able to diagnose the problem: the boy had broken a small bone in his wrist.","t":"看過 X 光片後，醫生得以診斷出問題：男孩手腕的一根小骨頭斷了。","h":1},{"w":"diagnosis","p":"n.","d":"a doctor's statement about what illness someone has","c":"診斷","s":"The diagnosis was good news; the lump was not cancer, and the patient would not need an operation.","t":"這個診斷是好消息；腫塊不是癌症，病人不需要動手術。","h":1},{"w":"be diagnosed with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be told by a doctor that you have a certain illness","c":"被診斷出患有","s":"My aunt was diagnosed with diabetes last year, so she now checks her blood sugar every morning and eats much less sugar.","t":"我阿姨去年被診斷出患有糖尿病，所以她現在每天早上測血糖，而且吃的糖少很多。","a":"was diagnosed with"},{"w":"diagnostic","p":"adj.","d":"used for finding out what is wrong","c":"診斷的","s":"The hospital bought a new diagnostic machine that can find heart problems much earlier than the old equipment could.","t":"醫院買了一台新的診斷儀器，能比舊設備更早發現心臟問題。"},{"w":"dialect","p":"n.","d":"a form of a language spoken in one area","c":"方言","s":"My grandmother speaks a dialect from southern China that even my mother has trouble understanding.","t":"我奶奶說一種中國南方的方言，連我媽媽都聽不太懂。","h":1},{"w":"local dialect","p":"n.phr.","d":"the form of a language used by people in one place","c":"當地方言","s":"The taxi driver spoke in the local dialect, so our tour guide had to translate everything he said for us.","t":"計程車司機說的是當地方言，所以我們的導遊必須替我們翻譯他說的每句話。"},{"w":"dialogue","p":"n.","d":"a conversation, especially in a book, play, or movie","c":"對話","s":"The dialogue in the movie is so natural that you feel like you are listening to real friends talking.","t":"這部電影的對話非常自然，讓你覺得像在聽真正的朋友聊天。"},{"w":"diameter","p":"n.","d":"a straight line across the middle of a circle; its length","c":"直徑","s":"The pizza has a diameter of thirty centimeters, which is big enough for three hungry teenagers to share.","t":"這個披薩的直徑是三十公分，足夠三個餓壞的青少年分享。","h":1},{"w":"in diameter","p":"phr.","d":"measured across the middle of a circle","c":"直徑為…","s":"The old tree in the park is almost two meters in diameter, and it takes four children holding hands to circle it.","t":"公園裡的老樹直徑將近兩公尺，要四個孩子手牽手才能環抱它。"},{"w":"meter","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring length, equal to 100 centimeters","c":"公尺","s":"The swimming pool is fifty meters long, so swimmers must go up and back ten times to complete one kilometer.","t":"這座游泳池長五十公尺，所以泳者必須來回游十次才能完成一公里。","a":"meters"},{"w":"diaper","p":"n.","d":"a soft cloth or paper that a baby wears between its legs","c":"尿布","s":"The baby started crying in the middle of the night, so her father got up to change her wet diaper.","t":"寶寶半夜哭了起來，所以她爸爸起床幫她換濕掉的尿布。","h":1},{"w":"change a diaper","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take off a baby's dirty diaper and put on a clean one","c":"換尿布","s":"Many new fathers do not know how to change a diaper, so the hospital now offers a short class to teach them.","t":"許多新手爸爸不知道怎麼換尿布，所以醫院現在提供簡短課程教他們。"},{"w":"disposable diaper","p":"n.phr.","d":"a diaper that is thrown away after one use","c":"拋棄式尿布","s":"Disposable diapers are convenient, but they create a lot of garbage, so some parents prefer cloth ones that can be washed.","t":"拋棄式尿布很方便，但會製造很多垃圾，所以有些父母偏好可以洗的布尿布。","a":"Disposable diapers"},{"w":"digestion","p":"n.","d":"the process by which your body breaks down food","c":"消化","s":"Eating slowly and chewing your food well helps digestion, so try not to finish your lunch in five minutes.","t":"慢慢吃並把食物嚼碎有助於消化，所以盡量別在五分鐘內吃完午餐。","h":1},{"w":"digest","p":"v.","d":"to break down food in the stomach; to understand information","c":"消化；理解","s":"Rice is easy to digest, which is why doctors often suggest it for people who have an upset stomach.","t":"米飯容易消化，這就是為什麼醫生常建議腸胃不適的人吃它。"},{"w":"digestive","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the breaking down of food in the body","c":"消化的","s":"Drinking too much cold soda with meals can upset your digestive system and give you a stomachache.","t":"吃飯時喝太多冰汽水可能會擾亂你的消化系統，讓你肚子痛。"},{"w":"indigestion","p":"n.","d":"pain in the stomach because food is hard to break down","c":"消化不良","s":"Grandpa suffers from indigestion whenever he eats fried food late at night, so he now has a light dinner.","t":"爺爺只要深夜吃油炸食物就會消化不良，所以他現在晚餐吃得清淡。"},{"w":"dilemma","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which you must choose between two difficult things","c":"兩難；困境","s":"Lisa faced a dilemma: she could go to her best friend's wedding or take the entrance exam, but both were on the same day.","t":"麗莎面臨兩難：她可以去參加最好朋友的婚禮或參加入學考試，但兩者都在同一天。","h":1},{"w":"be in a dilemma","p":"phr.","d":"to find it very hard to choose between two things","c":"陷入兩難","s":"I am in a dilemma about which university to choose, because one has a better program and the other is much closer to home.","t":"我對選哪所大學陷入兩難，因為一所課程較好，另一所離家近得多。","a":"am in a dilemma"},{"w":"moral dilemma","p":"n.phr.","d":"a hard choice between two things that both seem right or wrong","c":"道德兩難","s":"The movie presents a moral dilemma: should the doctor tell the truth and hurt the family, or keep a secret to protect them?","t":"這部電影呈現了一個道德兩難：醫生應該說實話傷害這家人，還是保守秘密保護他們？"},{"w":"dimension","p":"n.","d":"a part or side of a situation or idea","c":"方面；層面","s":"Learning a foreign language adds a new dimension to your life, because you can make friends from other cultures.","t":"學習外語為你的人生增添了新的層面，因為你可以結交來自其他文化的朋友。","h":1},{"w":"dimensions","p":"n.","d":"the length, width, and height of something","c":"尺寸；大小","s":"Please measure the dimensions of the room before you buy a sofa, or it may not fit through the door.","t":"買沙發前請先量房間的尺寸，否則它可能進不了門。"},{"w":"three-dimensional","p":"adj.","d":"having length, width, and height; not flat","c":"立體的；三維的","s":"The new museum has a three-dimensional model of the whole city, and children love finding their own schools on it.","t":"新博物館有一個全市的立體模型，孩子們喜歡在上面找自己的學校。"},{"w":"diminish","p":"v.","d":"to become or make something smaller or weaker","c":"減少；減輕","s":"The pain in my knee began to diminish after I rested for a week and stopped running on hard roads.","t":"我休息一週並停止在硬路面跑步後，膝蓋的疼痛開始減輕。","h":1},{"w":"diminish","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem less important","c":"貶低；輕視","s":"Nothing can diminish what she achieved; finishing the marathon with an injured foot was truly brave.","t":"沒有什麼能貶低她的成就；帶著受傷的腳跑完馬拉松真的很勇敢。"},{"w":"diminishing","p":"adj.","d":"becoming smaller or less","c":"逐漸減少的","s":"With diminishing oil supplies, many countries are now investing heavily in solar and wind power.","t":"隨著石油供應日益減少，許多國家現在大量投資太陽能和風力發電。"},{"w":"diplomatic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with managing relations between countries","c":"外交的","s":"After thirty years of diplomatic work in five countries, my uncle finally came home to retire in Tainan.","t":"在五個國家從事三十年外交工作後，我叔叔終於回到台南退休。","h":1},{"w":"diplomatic","p":"adj.","d":"good at dealing with people without upsetting them","c":"圓滑的；有手腕的","s":"The manager gave a diplomatic answer that did not upset either side, and the meeting ended peacefully.","t":"經理給了一個圓滑的回答，沒有得罪任何一方，會議平和地結束了。"},{"w":"diplomat","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to represent their country in another country","c":"外交官","s":"As a diplomat, she represents Taiwan abroad and often has dinner with leaders from other countries.","t":"身為外交官，她在國外代表台灣，經常與其他國家的領袖共進晚餐。"},{"w":"diplomacy","p":"n.","d":"the work of managing relations between countries by talking","c":"外交","s":"The two countries solved the problem through diplomacy instead of war, and their leaders shook hands in front of the cameras.","t":"兩國透過外交而非戰爭解決了問題，兩國領袖在鏡頭前握手。"},{"w":"directory","p":"n.","d":"a list of names, phone numbers, or offices in order","c":"名錄；目錄；電話簿","s":"You can find the phone number of every office in the building in the directory next to the elevator on the first floor.","t":"你可以在一樓電梯旁的名錄中找到大樓裡每間辦公室的電話號碼。","h":1},{"w":"telephone directory","p":"n.phr.","d":"a book that lists people's phone numbers","c":"電話簿","s":"Before the Internet, people looked for a shop's number in the telephone directory, a thick book that every home kept near the phone.","t":"在網路出現之前，人們在電話簿裡找商店的電話，那是每個家庭放在電話旁的一本厚書。"},{"w":"direct","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone the way to a place","c":"指引；指路","s":"Could you direct me to the nearest MRT station? I am new here and my phone has run out of power.","t":"你能指引我去最近的捷運站嗎？我剛來這裡，手機又沒電了。"},{"w":"direction","p":"n.","d":"the way that someone or something goes or faces","c":"方向","s":"We walked in the wrong direction for twenty minutes before we realized the museum was behind us.","t":"我們朝錯誤的方向走了二十分鐘，才發現博物館在我們後面。"},{"w":"director","p":"n.","d":"the person who tells the actors what to do in a movie; a manager","c":"導演；主管","s":"The director of the movie thanked all the actors on stage after it won the award for best picture.","t":"這部電影獲得最佳影片獎後，導演在台上感謝所有演員。"},{"w":"disapprove","p":"v.","d":"to think that someone or something is bad or wrong","c":"不贊成；反對","s":"Although my grandparents disapproved, my sister dyed her hair bright pink before the school trip.","t":"雖然祖父母不贊成，我姐姐還是在校外教學前把頭髮染成亮粉紅色。","a":"disapproved","h":1},{"w":"disapprove of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not agree with or not like something","c":"不贊成…","s":"Many teachers disapprove of students using phones in class because it makes it hard for them to pay attention.","t":"許多老師不贊成學生在課堂上用手機，因為那會讓他們難以專心。"},{"w":"disapproval","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that something is bad or wrong","c":"不贊成；反對","s":"The coach shook his head in disapproval when the player threw his racket on the ground after losing the point.","t":"當球員輸掉那一分後把球拍扔在地上時，教練不以為然地搖了搖頭。"},{"w":"approve","p":"v.","d":"to agree to something officially; to think something is good","c":"批准；贊成","s":"The city government finally decided to approve the plan for a new park after months of discussion with local residents.","t":"經過與當地居民數月的討論，市政府終於決定批准新公園的計畫。"},{"w":"approval","p":"n.","d":"the act of agreeing to something; a good opinion","c":"同意；批准；贊同","s":"You need your parents' written approval before you can join the overnight camping trip next month.","t":"你必須先取得父母的書面同意，才能參加下個月的過夜露營。"},{"w":"disclose","p":"v.","d":"to tell people something that was secret","c":"透露；揭露","s":"The company refused to disclose how many customers had their passwords stolen in the attack last week.","t":"該公司拒絕透露上週攻擊事件中有多少顧客的密碼被竊。","h":1},{"w":"disclosure","p":"n.","d":"the act of making secret information known","c":"揭露；公開","s":"The disclosure of the politician's secret bank accounts shocked the whole country and forced him to resign.","t":"這位政治人物秘密銀行帳戶的曝光震驚全國，迫使他辭職。"},{"w":"enclose","p":"v.","d":"to put something inside a letter or package; to surround","c":"附上；圍住","s":"Please enclose a copy of your student ID with the application form so that we can confirm your age.","t":"請把學生證影本連同申請表一起附上，以便我們確認你的年齡。"},{"w":"undisclosed","p":"adj.","d":"not told to the public","c":"未公開的","s":"The singer sold her house to a buyer for an undisclosed price, but neighbors guess it was more than fifty million dollars.","t":"這位歌手以未公開的價格把房子賣給買家，但鄰居猜測超過五千萬元。"},{"w":"disconnect","p":"v.","d":"to separate something from a power supply or another thing","c":"切斷；斷開","s":"Please disconnect the printer from the computer before you move it, or you might damage the cable.","t":"移動印表機之前請先把它與電腦斷開，否則你可能會弄壞連接線。","h":1},{"w":"be disconnected","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a phone, power, or Internet line cut off","c":"被切斷；斷線","s":"Our phone line was disconnected because my father forgot to pay the bill for two months in a row.","t":"我們的電話線被切斷了，因為我爸爸連續兩個月忘記繳費。","a":"was disconnected"},{"w":"connect","p":"v.","d":"to join two things together","c":"連接","s":"You need a password to connect to the Wi-Fi in this café, so ask the waiter when you order your coffee.","t":"你需要密碼才能連接這家咖啡館的 Wi-Fi，所以點咖啡時問一下服務生。"},{"w":"connection","p":"n.","d":"a link between two things; a phone or Internet line","c":"連線；關聯","s":"The Internet connection in the mountains was so slow that it took ten minutes to send one photo.","t":"山上的網路連線慢到傳一張照片要十分鐘。"},{"w":"disconnected","p":"adj.","d":"not linked together; not making sense as a whole","c":"脫節的；無關聯的","s":"His speech was full of disconnected ideas, so the audience could not understand what his main point was.","t":"他的演講充滿彼此無關的想法，所以聽眾不明白他的重點是什麼。"},{"w":"discourse","p":"n.","d":"serious talk or writing about a subject","c":"論述；言論；談話","s":"Social media has changed public discourse; people now share their opinions online instead of in newspapers.","t":"社群媒體改變了公共論述；人們現在在網路上而不是在報紙上分享意見。","h":1},{"w":"political discourse","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way people talk and argue about politics","c":"政治言論","s":"Many people are worried that political discourse has become too angry and that leaders no longer listen to each other.","t":"許多人擔心政治言論變得太憤怒，領袖們不再傾聽彼此。"},{"w":"course","p":"n.","d":"a series of lessons on a subject","c":"課程","s":"I signed up for an online course in Japanese because I want to travel to Kyoto next summer.","t":"我報名了一門線上日語課程，因為我明年夏天想去京都旅行。"},{"w":"discriminate","p":"v.","d":"to see the difference between two things","c":"分辨；區別","s":"Some people cannot discriminate between real news and fake news, so they share false stories without checking.","t":"有些人無法分辨真新聞和假新聞，所以不經查證就分享假消息。","h":1},{"w":"discrimination","p":"n.","d":"treating a person or group unfairly because of their race, sex, age, etc.","c":"歧視","s":"The new law aims to end discrimination against people with disabilities, especially when they apply for jobs.","t":"新法律旨在終止對身心障礙者的歧視，尤其是在他們求職的時候。","h":1},{"w":"discriminate against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to treat a person or group unfairly","c":"歧視…","s":"The hotel was fined because it discriminated against guests from certain countries by giving them the worst rooms.","t":"這家飯店被罰款，因為它把最差的房間給某些國家的客人，歧視他們。","a":"discriminated against"},{"w":"racial discrimination","p":"n.phr.","d":"unfair treatment of people because of their race","c":"種族歧視","s":"Martin Luther King Jr. spent his life fighting racial discrimination in the United States, and he gave his most famous speech in 1963.","t":"馬丁·路德·金恩一生在美國對抗種族歧視，他在 1963 年發表了最著名的演說。"},{"w":"discriminatory","p":"adj.","d":"treating some people unfairly","c":"歧視性的","s":"The school removed the discriminatory rule that had kept girls out of the robot club for more than ten years.","t":"學校廢除了那條十多年來把女生排除在機器人社之外的歧視性規定。"},{"w":"disrupt","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from continuing normally","c":"擾亂；中斷","s":"A loud alarm disrupted the exam, and the students had to wait outside for twenty minutes before they could continue.","t":"一聲響亮的警報中斷了考試，學生必須在外面等二十分鐘才能繼續。","a":"disrupted","h":1},{"w":"disruption","p":"n.","d":"a problem that stops something from continuing normally","c":"擾亂；中斷","s":"The typhoon caused serious disruption to train services, and thousands of passengers were stuck at the station all night.","t":"颱風對火車服務造成嚴重中斷，數千名乘客整夜被困在車站。"},{"w":"disruptive","p":"adj.","d":"causing trouble and stopping things from going normally","c":"擾亂的；搗亂的","s":"The teacher moved the disruptive student to the front row so that he would stop talking and bothering his classmates.","t":"老師把那個搗亂的學生換到前排，好讓他停止說話和打擾同學。"},{"w":"interrupt","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone while they are speaking or doing something","c":"打斷","s":"Please do not interrupt me while I am on the phone; I will answer your question as soon as the call ends.","t":"我講電話時請不要打斷我；通話一結束我就會回答你的問題。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"dissolve – embrace","cards":[{"w":"dissolve","p":"v.","d":"to mix into a liquid and disappear","c":"溶解","s":"Stir the sugar until it dissolves completely in the hot tea; otherwise, the last sip will be far too sweet.","t":"攪拌糖直到它在熱茶中完全溶解；否則最後一口會太甜。","a":"dissolves","h":1},{"w":"dissolve","p":"v.","d":"to officially end a company, group, or marriage","c":"解散；解除","s":"The two business partners decided to dissolve their company after ten years because they could no longer agree on anything.","t":"兩位事業夥伴十年後決定解散公司，因為他們再也無法在任何事上達成共識。"},{"w":"dissolve into tears","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly start crying","c":"忍不住哭了起來","s":"When the little boy saw his lost puppy running toward him, he dissolved into tears and hugged it tightly.","t":"當小男孩看到走失的小狗朝他跑來時，他忍不住哭了起來，緊緊抱住牠。","a":"dissolved into tears"},{"w":"solution","p":"n.","d":"a liquid with something dissolved in it; an answer to a problem","c":"溶液；解決辦法","s":"Mix the salt into the water, and the solution can be used to clean the small cut on your finger.","t":"把鹽溶入水中，這溶液可以用來清潔你手指上的小傷口。"},{"w":"distinction","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference between two things","c":"區別；差別","s":"There is a clear distinction between being confident and being rude, and good leaders know where the line is.","t":"自信和無禮之間有明顯的區別，好的領導者知道界線在哪裡。","h":1},{"w":"distinctive","p":"adj.","d":"easy to recognize because it is different from others","c":"獨特的；有特色的","s":"The singer has such a distinctive voice that you can recognize her song after hearing only two or three notes.","t":"這位歌手的聲音非常獨特，你只要聽兩三個音就能認出她的歌。","h":1},{"w":"distinguish","p":"v.","d":"to see or show the difference between things","c":"分辨；區別","s":"It is hard to distinguish the twins from each other, so their mother dresses them in different colors.","t":"很難把這對雙胞胎分辨開來，所以他們的媽媽給他們穿不同顏色的衣服。"},{"w":"distinct","p":"adj.","d":"clearly different; easy to notice","c":"明顯的；不同的","s":"The soup had a distinct smell of ginger, which reminded me of the dishes my grandmother used to cook in winter.","t":"這湯有一股明顯的薑味，讓我想起奶奶以前冬天煮的菜。"},{"w":"draw a distinction between","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show that two things are different","c":"區分…","s":"Teachers should draw a distinction between a student who is lazy and one who is simply struggling with the subject.","t":"老師應該區分懶惰的學生和單純在這科目上學得辛苦的學生。"},{"w":"with distinction","p":"phr.","d":"with very high marks or great success","c":"以優異成績","s":"My cousin graduated from medical school with distinction, and three hospitals offered her a job in the same week.","t":"我表姐以優異成績從醫學院畢業，同一週就有三家醫院提供她工作。"},{"w":"distract","p":"v.","d":"to take someone's attention away from what they are doing","c":"使分心","s":"Please turn off the music while I study; it will distract me, and I have a big test tomorrow morning.","t":"我讀書時請把音樂關掉；它會讓我分心，而且我明天早上有大考。","h":1},{"w":"be distracted by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop paying attention because of something","c":"被…分散注意力","s":"The driver was distracted by a message on his phone and did not notice that the light had turned red.","t":"駕駛被手機上的訊息分散了注意力，沒注意到燈已經變紅了。","a":"was distracted by"},{"w":"distraction","p":"n.","d":"something that takes your attention away","c":"使人分心的事物","s":"My phone is my biggest distraction, so I leave it in another room when I need to finish my homework.","t":"手機是最讓我分心的東西，所以需要寫完作業時我會把它放在另一個房間。"},{"w":"distracted","p":"adj.","d":"not able to pay attention because you are thinking of other things","c":"心不在焉的","s":"Tom seemed distracted in class today; he kept looking out the window and did not hear the teacher call his name.","t":"湯姆今天上課似乎心不在焉；他一直看著窗外，沒聽到老師叫他的名字。"},{"w":"doctrine","p":"n.","d":"a set of beliefs taught by a religion or group","c":"教義；主義；信條","s":"The temple's doctrine teaches that people should be kind to all living things, including the smallest insects.","t":"這座寺廟的教義教導人們應該善待所有生物，包括最小的昆蟲。","h":1},{"w":"religious doctrine","p":"n.phr.","d":"the beliefs that a religion teaches","c":"宗教教義","s":"Students in the history class compared the religious doctrine of several faiths and found that most of them value honesty and kindness.","t":"歷史課的學生比較了幾個信仰的宗教教義，發現大多數都重視誠實和善良。"},{"w":"doctor","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to treat sick people","c":"醫生","s":"The doctor told my father to walk for thirty minutes every day and to eat less salt and sugar.","t":"醫生告訴我爸爸每天走路三十分鐘，而且要少吃鹽和糖。"},{"w":"document","p":"n.","d":"an official paper with information on it","c":"文件","s":"Keep this document in a safe place because you will need it when you apply for your passport next year.","t":"把這份文件放在安全的地方，因為明年申請護照時你會需要它。","h":1},{"w":"documentary","p":"n.","d":"a film or TV program about real people and events","c":"紀錄片","s":"We watched a documentary about penguins in science class, and I was surprised to learn how far they walk to find food.","t":"我們在自然課看了一部關於企鵝的紀錄片，我很驚訝牠們為了找食物走那麼遠。","h":1},{"w":"document","p":"v.","d":"to record something in writing, photos, or film","c":"記錄；記載","s":"The scientists spent five years in the forest to document the daily life of the wild monkeys that live there.","t":"科學家在森林裡花了五年時間記錄住在那裡的野生猴子的日常生活。"},{"w":"documentary","p":"adj.","d":"in the form of written papers; based on real facts","c":"書面的；紀實的","s":"The lawyer asked for documentary evidence, such as receipts and letters, to prove that the money had really been paid.","t":"律師要求書面證據，例如收據和信件，以證明那筆錢真的付過了。"},{"w":"official document","p":"n.phr.","d":"a paper given by the government or an organization","c":"正式文件","s":"A birth certificate is an official document that shows when and where you were born, so never throw it away.","t":"出生證明是一份顯示你出生時間和地點的正式文件，所以千萬別丟掉。"},{"w":"documentation","p":"n.","d":"papers that prove something or give information","c":"證明文件；文件資料","s":"Bring all the necessary documentation to the bank, including your ID card and a recent bill with your address on it.","t":"把所有必要的證明文件帶到銀行，包括身分證和一張有你地址的近期帳單。"},{"w":"domain","p":"n.","d":"an area of activity, interest, or knowledge","c":"領域；範圍","s":"Cooking used to be seen as a woman's domain, but today many of the world's most famous chefs are men.","t":"烹飪過去被視為女性的領域，但今天世界上許多最有名的主廚都是男性。","h":1},{"w":"domain name","p":"n.phr.","d":"the address of a website, such as example.com","c":"網域名稱","s":"Before you build a website for your shop, you need to buy a domain name that customers can remember easily.","t":"在為你的店建立網站之前，你需要買一個顧客容易記住的網域名稱。"},{"w":"public domain","p":"n.phr.","d":"works that anyone may use freely because no one owns the rights","c":"公有領域","s":"Old books whose authors died more than seventy years ago are in the public domain, so anyone can print or share them freely.","t":"作者去世超過七十年的舊書屬於公有領域，所以任何人都可以自由印製或分享。"},{"w":"domestic","p":"adj.","d":"inside one country; connected with the home","c":"國內的；家庭的","s":"Domestic flights from Taipei to Kaohsiung take less than an hour, but most people prefer the high-speed train.","t":"從台北到高雄的國內航班不到一小時，但大多數人偏好高鐵。","a":"Domestic"},{"w":"dome","p":"n.","d":"a round roof shaped like half a ball","c":"圓頂","s":"The dome of the old church is painted with gold stars, and visitors always look up as soon as they walk in.","t":"這座古老教堂的圓頂上畫著金色的星星，遊客一走進去就會抬頭看。","h":1},{"w":"domed","p":"adj.","d":"having a round roof","c":"有圓頂的","s":"The new domed stadium lets baseball games continue even on rainy days, so fans no longer worry about the weather.","t":"新的圓頂體育場讓棒球比賽即使在雨天也能繼續進行，所以球迷不再擔心天氣。"},{"w":"glass dome","p":"n.phr.","d":"a round roof made of glass","c":"玻璃圓頂","s":"The shopping mall has a huge glass dome that lets sunlight pour into the center of the building all day long.","t":"這座購物中心有一個巨大的玻璃圓頂，讓陽光整天灑進大樓中央。"},{"w":"donate","p":"v.","d":"to give money or things to help people","c":"捐贈；捐獻","s":"Every winter our school asks students to donate warm clothes they no longer wear to families in need.","t":"每年冬天我們學校都請學生把不再穿的保暖衣物捐給有需要的家庭。","h":1},{"w":"donation","p":"n.","d":"money or things given to help people","c":"捐款；捐贈物","s":"The animal shelter received a large donation from a local company, which will pay for food and medicine for a whole year.","t":"動物收容所收到當地一家公司的一大筆捐款，足以支付一整年的食物和醫藥費。","h":1},{"w":"donor","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives money, blood, or an organ to help others","c":"捐贈者","s":"A generous donor gave the library ten thousand books, but she asked the staff not to tell anyone her name.","t":"一位慷慨的捐贈者送給圖書館一萬本書，但她要求館員不要告訴任何人她的名字。","h":1},{"w":"blood donor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who gives blood for sick people to use","c":"捐血者","s":"Hospitals need more blood donors in summer because fewer people give blood during the hot vacation months.","t":"醫院在夏天需要更多捐血者，因為在炎熱的假期月份捐血的人比較少。","a":"blood donors"},{"w":"make a donation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give money to a charity or cause","c":"捐款","s":"If you would like to make a donation to the earthquake fund, you can scan the QR code on the poster by the door.","t":"如果你想為地震基金捐款，可以掃描門邊海報上的 QR code。"},{"w":"organ donation","p":"n.phr.","d":"giving a part of your body, such as a kidney, to save someone","c":"器官捐贈","s":"Thanks to organ donation, the young man received a new kidney and was able to return to school six months later.","t":"多虧器官捐贈，這位年輕人得到一顆新的腎臟，六個月後就能回到學校。"},{"w":"doorway","p":"n.","d":"the space where a door opens into a room or building","c":"門口","s":"The tall man stood in the doorway for a moment, looking around the crowded room for his friends.","t":"那個高個子男人在門口站了一會兒，在擁擠的房間裡四處尋找他的朋友。","h":1},{"w":"door","p":"n.","d":"the thing you open to go into a room or building","c":"門","s":"Please close the door quietly when you leave, because the baby has just fallen asleep in the next room.","t":"離開時請輕輕關門，因為寶寶剛在隔壁房間睡著。"},{"w":"doorbell","p":"n.","d":"a bell beside a door that visitors ring","c":"門鈴","s":"Someone rang the doorbell at seven this morning, but when I opened the door, there was only a package on the step.","t":"今天早上七點有人按門鈴，但當我開門時，台階上只有一個包裹。"},{"w":"doorstep","p":"n.","d":"the step just outside the door of a building","c":"門階；門口","s":"Every morning the newspaper is left on our doorstep, and my grandfather reads it with his first cup of tea.","t":"每天早上報紙都放在我們家門階上，我爺爺會邊喝第一杯茶邊看報。"},{"w":"next door","p":"phr.","d":"in the house or room beside yours","c":"隔壁","s":"The family who lives next door has a big dog that barks every time someone walks past their gate.","t":"住在隔壁的那家人有一隻大狗，每次有人經過他們的大門牠就會叫。"},{"w":"dough","p":"n.","d":"a soft mix of flour and water used to make bread","c":"麵團","s":"Grandma let the dough rest for an hour before she shaped it into small round buns and put them in the oven.","t":"奶奶讓麵團靜置一小時，然後把它捏成小圓麵包放進烤箱。","h":1},{"w":"knead the dough","p":"v.phr.","d":"to press and push the dough with your hands","c":"揉麵團","s":"You must knead the dough for at least ten minutes so that the bread will be soft and light when it is baked.","t":"你必須揉麵團至少十分鐘，這樣烤出來的麵包才會柔軟蓬鬆。"},{"w":"doughnut","p":"n.","d":"a small round sweet cake fried in oil, often with a hole in the middle","c":"甜甜圈","s":"My little brother loves chocolate doughnuts, so we always stop at the bakery on the way home from school.","t":"我弟弟愛吃巧克力甜甜圈，所以我們放學回家的路上總會在麵包店停一下。","a":"doughnuts"},{"w":"pizza dough","p":"n.phr.","d":"the dough used to make the base of a pizza","c":"披薩麵團","s":"The restaurant makes its own pizza dough every morning, which is why the crust tastes so fresh and crispy.","t":"這家餐廳每天早上自己做披薩麵團，這就是為什麼餅皮吃起來那麼新鮮酥脆。"},{"w":"dreadful","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or unpleasant","c":"可怕的；糟糕的","s":"The weather was dreadful during our trip; it rained every day, and the wind was so strong that we could not use umbrellas.","t":"我們旅行期間的天氣糟糕透了；每天都下雨，風大到我們無法撐傘。","h":1},{"w":"dread","p":"v.","d":"to feel very worried about something that will happen","c":"害怕；畏懼","s":"I dread going to the dentist, so I always wait until the pain becomes too strong to ignore.","t":"我害怕看牙醫，所以總是等到痛得無法忽視才去。"},{"w":"dread","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of fear about something that will happen","c":"恐懼；擔憂","s":"She felt a sense of dread as she slowly opened the envelope with her exam results inside.","t":"她慢慢打開裝著考試成績的信封時，感到一陣恐懼。"},{"w":"dreadfully","p":"adv.","d":"very; extremely (used for something bad)","c":"非常；糟糕地","s":"I am dreadfully sorry for breaking your vase; please let me pay for a new one this weekend.","t":"打破你的花瓶我非常抱歉；請讓我這個週末賠你一個新的。"},{"w":"driveway","p":"n.","d":"a short private road from the street to a house or garage","c":"私人車道","s":"Please do not park in front of our driveway, because my mother cannot get her car out of the garage.","t":"請不要停在我們家車道前面，因為我媽媽的車會開不出車庫。","h":1},{"w":"drive","p":"v.","d":"to control a car and make it move","c":"開車；駕駛","s":"My sister is learning to drive, so she practices in the empty parking lot every Sunday morning with Dad.","t":"我姐姐在學開車，所以她每個星期天早上和爸爸在空停車場練習。"},{"w":"driver","p":"n.","d":"a person who drives a car, bus, or truck","c":"駕駛；司機","s":"The bus driver waited patiently while the old woman slowly climbed the steps with her heavy bags.","t":"公車司機耐心等候，老太太提著沉重的袋子慢慢爬上階梯。"},{"w":"driver's license","p":"n.phr.","d":"an official card that allows you to drive","c":"駕照","s":"You have to be eighteen to get a driver's license in Taiwan, and you must pass both a written test and a road test.","t":"在台灣你必須年滿十八歲才能考駕照，而且必須通過筆試和路考。"},{"w":"drive sb crazy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone very annoyed","c":"使某人抓狂","s":"The noise from the construction site next door is driving me crazy, so I study at the library in the afternoon.","t":"隔壁工地的噪音快把我逼瘋了，所以我下午都在圖書館讀書。","a":"driving me crazy"},{"w":"drought","p":"n.","d":"a long period with little or no rain","c":"乾旱","s":"After six months of drought, the reservoir was almost empty, and the city had to limit water use to five days a week.","t":"經過六個月的乾旱，水庫幾乎見底，城市必須把用水限制為每週五天。","h":1},{"w":"severe drought","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very serious lack of rain","c":"嚴重乾旱","s":"The severe drought in the south destroyed most of the rice crop, and farmers asked the government for help.","t":"南部的嚴重乾旱毀掉了大部分稻作，農民向政府求助。"},{"w":"dry","p":"adj.","d":"without water or wet feeling","c":"乾的","s":"The towels on the balcony are already dry, so please bring them in before it starts raining again.","t":"陽台上的毛巾已經乾了，請在再次下雨前把它們收進來。"},{"w":"dry up","p":"v.phr.","d":"(of a river or lake) to lose all its water","c":"乾涸","s":"The small river near our village tends to dry up every summer, and the fish disappear until the rains return.","t":"我們村子附近的小河每年夏天都會乾涸，魚群消失直到雨季再來。"},{"w":"ecological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the relationship between living things and their environment","c":"生態的","s":"The oil spill caused an ecological disaster along the coast, killing thousands of birds and fish.","t":"漏油在沿岸造成一場生態災難，導致數千隻鳥和魚死亡。","h":1},{"w":"ecology","p":"n.","d":"the study of how living things depend on each other and their surroundings","c":"生態；生態學","s":"She studied ecology at university because she wanted to understand how animals, plants, and people depend on each other.","t":"她在大學讀生態學，因為她想了解動物、植物和人類如何互相依賴。","h":1},{"w":"ecosystem","p":"n.","d":"all the living things in an area and the way they affect each other","c":"生態系統","s":"A coral reef is a rich ecosystem where thousands of different fish, plants, and tiny animals live together.","t":"珊瑚礁是一個豐富的生態系統，數千種不同的魚類、植物和微小動物一起生活在那裡。","h":1},{"w":"ecologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies ecology","c":"生態學家","s":"An ecologist visited our school to explain why cutting down the forest on the hill would harm the birds and the river.","t":"一位生態學家來我們學校解釋為什麼砍掉山丘上的森林會傷害鳥類和河流。"},{"w":"eco-friendly","p":"adj.","d":"not harmful to the environment","c":"環保的","s":"More and more shops now sell eco-friendly products, such as bamboo toothbrushes and bags made from old plastic bottles.","t":"越來越多商店現在販賣環保產品，例如竹製牙刷和用舊寶特瓶做的袋子。"},{"w":"ecological footprint","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of natural resources a person or group uses","c":"生態足跡","s":"You can reduce your ecological footprint by taking the bus, eating less meat, and buying only what you really need.","t":"你可以透過搭公車、少吃肉、只買真正需要的東西來減少你的生態足跡。"},{"w":"ego","p":"n.","d":"your idea of how important or good you are","c":"自我；自尊心","s":"The famous actor has a huge ego; he talks about himself all the time and never listens to anyone else.","t":"這位名演員自我意識很強；他總是談論自己，從不聽別人說話。","h":1},{"w":"boost one's ego","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone feel more confident and important","c":"增強某人的自信心","s":"Winning the speech contest really boosted his ego, and now he is not afraid to speak in front of the whole school.","t":"贏得演講比賽真的增強了他的自信心，現在他不怕在全校面前說話了。","a":"boosted his ego"},{"w":"egocentric","p":"adj.","d":"thinking only about yourself","c":"自我中心的","s":"My roommate is so egocentric that he plays loud music at midnight without thinking about anyone else in the apartment.","t":"我室友非常自我中心，半夜放很大聲的音樂，完全不考慮公寓裡的其他人。"},{"w":"elaborate","p":"adj.","d":"having many parts and details; carefully made","c":"精心製作的；複雜的","s":"The bride wore an elaborate dress covered with tiny flowers that took three people two months to sew by hand.","t":"新娘穿著一件精心製作的禮服，上面佈滿小花，三個人花了兩個月手工縫製。","h":1},{"w":"elaborate","p":"v.","d":"to explain something in more detail","c":"詳細說明","s":"Your plan sounds interesting, but could you elaborate on how you are going to pay for all the equipment?","t":"你的計畫聽起來很有趣，但你能詳細說明打算怎麼支付所有設備的費用嗎？"},{"w":"elaborately","p":"adv.","d":"with a lot of care and detail","c":"精心地","s":"The cake was elaborately decorated with chocolate leaves and sugar roses, so nobody wanted to be the first to cut it.","t":"蛋糕被精心裝飾著巧克力葉子和糖玫瑰，所以沒有人想當第一個切它的人。"},{"w":"labor","p":"n.","d":"hard physical work","c":"勞動；勞力","s":"Building the stone wall by hand took a whole year of hard labor, but the farmer was proud of every stone.","t":"徒手砌這道石牆花了整整一年的辛苦勞動，但農夫對每一塊石頭都感到自豪。"},{"w":"eligible","p":"adj.","d":"allowed to do or have something because you meet the rules","c":"有資格的；合格的","s":"Only students who have finished all three levels are eligible for the advanced course, so please check your records first.","t":"只有完成全部三個等級的學生才有資格上進階課程，所以請先查看你的紀錄。","h":1},{"w":"be eligible for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have the right to get something","c":"有資格獲得…","s":"People over sixty-five are eligible for a free bus pass in this city, and they can apply for it at any MRT station.","t":"這座城市六十五歲以上的人有資格獲得免費公車卡，可以在任何捷運站申請。","a":"are eligible for"},{"w":"eligibility","p":"n.","d":"the state of being allowed to do or have something","c":"資格","s":"Please read the eligibility rules carefully before you enter the contest, because only students under eighteen can take part.","t":"參加比賽前請仔細閱讀資格規定，因為只有十八歲以下的學生可以參加。"},{"w":"ineligible","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed to do or have something","c":"無資格的","s":"He was ineligible to vote in the election because he had moved to the city only two weeks earlier.","t":"他沒有資格在這次選舉中投票，因為他兩週前才搬到這座城市。"},{"w":"elect","p":"v.","d":"to choose someone for a position by voting","c":"選舉；推選","s":"The class will elect a new leader next Monday, and three students have already said they want the job.","t":"班上下星期一將選出新班長，已經有三位學生表示想要這個職位。"},{"w":"eloquent","p":"adj.","d":"able to speak or write well and persuade people","c":"雄辯的；口才好的","s":"The young lawyer was so eloquent that even people who disagreed with her enjoyed listening to her speak.","t":"這位年輕律師非常雄辯，連不同意她的人都喜歡聽她說話。","h":1},{"w":"eloquently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is clear, strong, and persuasive","c":"雄辯地；有說服力地","s":"He spoke so eloquently about the need for clean rivers that the city council agreed to fund the project that very night.","t":"他對乾淨河流的必要性說得非常有說服力，市議會當晚就同意資助這項計畫。"},{"w":"eloquence","p":"n.","d":"the ability to speak or write well and persuade people","c":"口才；雄辯","s":"Martin Luther King Jr. is remembered for his eloquence, and his speeches are still studied in schools around the world.","t":"馬丁·路德·金恩以他的口才為人所銘記，他的演講至今仍在世界各地的學校被研究。"},{"w":"embrace","p":"v.","d":"to hold someone in your arms to show love","c":"擁抱","s":"At the airport, the mother ran to embrace her son, whom she had not seen for three long years.","t":"在機場，母親跑過去擁抱她三年沒見的兒子。","h":1},{"w":"embrace","p":"v.","d":"to accept a new idea or change gladly","c":"欣然接受","s":"Many older workers find it hard to embrace new technology, but my grandfather learned to use a tablet in a week.","t":"許多年長的員工覺得很難欣然接受新科技，但我爺爺一週就學會用平板電腦了。"},{"w":"embrace","p":"n.","d":"the act of holding someone in your arms","c":"擁抱","s":"The two old friends held each other in a warm embrace before they said goodbye at the train station.","t":"兩位老朋友在火車站道別前溫暖地擁抱了彼此。"},{"w":"brace yourself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get ready for something unpleasant","c":"做好心理準備","s":"Brace yourself for some bad news: the school trip to Japan has been canceled because of the typhoon.","t":"做好心理準備聽壞消息：去日本的校外教學因為颱風取消了。","a":"Brace yourself"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"emission – evolve","cards":[{"w":"emission","p":"n.","d":"gas, heat, or light that is sent out into the air","c":"排放；排放物","s":"The new law says that every factory must cut its emission of dirty smoke by half before the end of next year.","t":"新法律規定，每家工廠必須在明年年底前把髒煙的排放量減少一半。","h":1},{"w":"emit","p":"v.","d":"to send out gas, heat, light, or sound","c":"排放；發出","s":"Old buses emit a lot of black smoke, so the city is slowly replacing them with electric ones that are much cleaner.","t":"舊公車會排放很多黑煙，所以市政府正慢慢用更乾淨的電動公車取代它們。"},{"w":"carbon emissions","p":"n.phr.","d":"the carbon dioxide gas that cars, planes, and factories send into the air","c":"碳排放","s":"If more people ride bikes or take the MRT to work, the city's carbon emissions will drop and the air will become cleaner.","t":"如果更多人騎腳踏車或搭捷運上班，這座城市的碳排放就會下降，空氣也會變得更乾淨。"},{"w":"endorse","p":"v.","d":"to say publicly that you support a person, product, or idea","c":"公開支持；代言","s":"Several famous doctors decided to endorse the new health plan, so many voters began to trust it more than before.","t":"幾位知名醫生決定公開支持這項新的健康計畫，所以許多選民開始比以前更信任它。","h":1},{"w":"endorsement","p":"n.","d":"public support for a person, product, or idea, often by someone famous","c":"支持；代言","s":"The basketball star earns millions of dollars every year from his endorsement of a popular brand of sports shoes.","t":"這位籃球明星每年靠代言一個熱門運動鞋品牌賺進數百萬美元。"},{"w":"endorse a product","p":"v.phr.","d":"to appear in ads saying that you use and like a product","c":"為產品代言","s":"Companies pay movie stars a lot of money to endorse a product, because fans often buy whatever their favorite actors use.","t":"公司付給電影明星很多錢來為產品代言，因為粉絲常常會買他們最愛的演員所使用的東西。"},{"w":"enterprise","p":"n.","d":"a company or business; a big or difficult plan","c":"企業；事業","s":"My uncle started a small enterprise that sells handmade soap online, and now it has grown into a company with twenty workers.","t":"我叔叔創立了一家在網路上賣手工皂的小企業，現在它已經成長為一家有二十名員工的公司。","h":1},{"w":"enterprising","p":"adj.","d":"having the energy and new ideas to start things, especially in business","c":"有進取心的；有事業心的","s":"An enterprising student in our class turned her love of baking into a weekend business that sells cookies to the whole school.","t":"我們班上一位有進取心的學生把她對烘焙的熱愛變成了週末生意，賣餅乾給全校的人。"},{"w":"free enterprise","p":"n.phr.","d":"an economic system in which private businesses compete without much government control","c":"自由企業制度","s":"In a system of free enterprise, anyone with a good idea can open a shop and compete with the big companies on the same street.","t":"在自由企業制度下，任何有好點子的人都可以開店，和同一條街上的大公司競爭。"},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lot of excitement and interest about something","c":"熱情的；熱衷的","s":"The new English teacher is so enthusiastic about reading that even the quiet students now borrow books from the library every week.","t":"新來的英文老師對閱讀非常熱衷，連安靜的學生現在也每週去圖書館借書。","h":1},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of excitement and interest","c":"熱情；熱忱","s":"The players showed great enthusiasm during practice, and the coach believes they will play well in the final game next week.","t":"球員們在練習時展現出極大的熱情，教練相信他們在下週的決賽會表現得很好。"},{"w":"enthusiastically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows great excitement and interest","c":"熱情地；熱烈地","s":"When the singer walked onto the stage, the crowd clapped enthusiastically and some fans even started to cry with joy.","t":"當歌手走上舞台時，觀眾熱烈地鼓掌，有些粉絲甚至開心得哭了。"},{"w":"be enthusiastic about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very excited about and interested in something","c":"對…很熱衷","s":"My little sister is enthusiastic about learning the piano, so she practices for an hour every day without anyone telling her to.","t":"我妹妹對學鋼琴很熱衷，所以她每天練一個小時，不用任何人叫她。","a":"is enthusiastic about"},{"w":"enthusiast","p":"n.","d":"a person who is very interested in a particular activity","c":"愛好者；熱衷者","s":"As a camera enthusiast, my father spends every weekend taking photos of birds in the park near our house.","t":"身為一個相機愛好者，我爸爸每個週末都在我們家附近的公園拍鳥的照片。"},{"w":"entitle","p":"v.","d":"to give someone the right to have or do something","c":"使有權利；給予資格","s":"This student card will entitle you to a fifty percent discount at the museum and free entry to the city swimming pool.","t":"這張學生證使你有權在博物館享有五折優惠，並免費進入市立游泳池。","h":1},{"w":"entitle","p":"v.","d":"to give a title to a book, film, or piece of writing","c":"給（書、文章等）題名","s":"The author decided to entitle her new novel \"The Last Summer\" because most of the story happens in August.","t":"作者決定把她的新小說題名為《最後的夏天》，因為故事大部分發生在八月。"},{"w":"be entitled to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have the right to have or do something","c":"有權享有…","s":"Every worker in this company is entitled to fourteen days of paid vacation a year, even if they joined only a few months ago.","t":"這家公司的每位員工每年都有權享有十四天的有薪假，即使他們幾個月前才加入。","a":"is entitled to"},{"w":"entitlement","p":"n.","d":"the right to have or do something","c":"權利；應得的權益","s":"In many countries, free education until the age of eighteen is a basic entitlement that every child should receive.","t":"在許多國家，十八歲以前的免費教育是每個孩子都應該得到的基本權利。"},{"w":"entity","p":"n.","d":"something that exists as a single and complete thing","c":"實體；獨立存在的個體","s":"After the two small companies joined together last year, they became one large entity with offices in five different cities.","t":"去年這兩家小公司合併之後，它們成為一個在五個城市設有辦公室的大型實體。","h":1},{"w":"legal entity","p":"n.phr.","d":"a company or organization that has legal rights and duties like a person","c":"法律實體；法人","s":"Once a business is registered as a legal entity, it can sign contracts, open bank accounts, and pay taxes under its own name.","t":"一旦企業登記為法律實體，它就可以用自己的名義簽約、開銀行帳戶和繳稅。"},{"w":"separate entity","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that exists on its own, apart from other things","c":"獨立的個體","s":"Although the two schools share the same campus, each one is a separate entity with its own principal, teachers, and rules.","t":"雖然這兩所學校共用同一個校區，但每一所都是有自己校長、老師和校規的獨立個體。"},{"w":"entrepreneur","p":"n.","d":"a person who starts a business and takes risks to make money","c":"企業家；創業者","s":"The young entrepreneur opened her first bubble tea shop at twenty-two, and today she owns thirty stores across Taiwan.","t":"這位年輕的創業者二十二歲時開了第一家珍珠奶茶店，如今她在全台灣擁有三十家店。","h":1},{"w":"entrepreneurial","p":"adj.","d":"having the skills and energy to start new businesses","c":"創業的；有創業精神的","s":"Our school holds an entrepreneurial competition every spring, in which teams of students design products and sell them at a fair.","t":"我們學校每年春天舉辦一場創業競賽，學生團隊設計產品並在園遊會上販售。"},{"w":"entrepreneurship","p":"n.","d":"the activity of starting and running new businesses","c":"創業精神；創業活動","s":"Many universities now offer courses in entrepreneurship because more and more students dream of running their own companies.","t":"許多大學現在開設創業課程，因為越來越多學生夢想經營自己的公司。"},{"w":"envious","p":"adj.","d":"wishing you had what someone else has","c":"羨慕的；嫉妒的","s":"I felt a little envious when my best friend showed me the new phone her parents bought her for her birthday.","t":"當我最好的朋友給我看她父母買給她的生日禮物新手機時，我覺得有點羨慕。","h":1},{"w":"envy","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of wanting what someone else has","c":"羨慕；嫉妒","s":"His beautiful new sports car was the envy of all his neighbors, who kept asking how much he had paid for it.","t":"他漂亮的新跑車是所有鄰居羨慕的對象，他們一直問他花了多少錢買的。"},{"w":"envy","p":"v.","d":"to wish you had something that someone else has","c":"羨慕；嫉妒","s":"Many students envy Lisa because she can speak three languages and travels to a different country every summer.","t":"許多學生羨慕麗莎，因為她會說三種語言，而且每年夏天都到不同的國家旅行。"},{"w":"enviable","p":"adj.","d":"so good that other people wish they had it","c":"令人羨慕的","s":"She has the enviable ability to fall asleep anywhere, even on a noisy bus full of talking passengers.","t":"她有一種令人羨慕的能力，能在任何地方睡著，即使是在滿是聊天乘客的嘈雜公車上。"},{"w":"be envious of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel that you want what another person has","c":"羨慕…","s":"Don't be envious of your classmates' high scores; instead, ask them how they study and try their methods yourself.","t":"不要羨慕同學的高分；相反地，問問他們怎麼讀書，然後自己試試他們的方法。"},{"w":"envision","p":"v.","d":"to imagine what something will be like in the future","c":"想像；展望","s":"When the architect looked at the empty field, she could already envision a park with tall trees and a playground for children.","t":"當建築師看著那片空地時，她已經能想像一座有高大樹木和兒童遊樂場的公園。","h":1},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"the ability to see; a clear idea of what the future should be like","c":"視力；願景","s":"The new principal shared her vision for the school, which includes a bigger library and more time for sports and art.","t":"新校長分享了她對學校的願景，其中包括更大的圖書館以及更多運動和藝術的時間。"},{"w":"visionary","p":"adj.","d":"having clear and original ideas about the future","c":"有遠見的","s":"Steve Jobs was a visionary leader who imagined phones without buttons long before most people thought it was possible.","t":"賈伯斯是一位有遠見的領導者，早在大多數人認為可能之前，他就想像出沒有按鍵的手機。"},{"w":"epidemic","p":"n.","d":"a disease that spreads quickly to many people in an area","c":"流行病；傳染病流行","s":"During the flu epidemic last winter, so many students were sick that our school had to close for a whole week.","t":"去年冬天流感大流行期間，太多學生生病了，所以我們學校不得不停課整整一週。","h":1},{"w":"epidemic","p":"adj.","d":"spreading very quickly and affecting many people","c":"流行性的；盛行的","s":"Phone addiction has reached epidemic levels among teenagers, and many parents do not know how to deal with it.","t":"手機成癮在青少年之間已經達到流行性的程度，許多家長不知道該如何處理。"},{"w":"pandemic","p":"n.","d":"a disease that spreads across many countries or the whole world","c":"全球大流行病","s":"The COVID-19 pandemic changed the way we live, and many people still wear masks on crowded trains and buses today.","t":"新冠肺炎全球大流行改變了我們的生活方式，許多人今天在擠滿人的火車和公車上仍然戴口罩。"},{"w":"episode","p":"n.","d":"one part of a TV or radio series","c":"（影集的）一集","s":"I stayed up until two in the morning because I wanted to watch just one more episode of my favorite Korean drama.","t":"我熬夜到凌晨兩點，因為我想再多看一集我最愛的韓劇。","h":1},{"w":"episode","p":"n.","d":"an event or a short period of time in someone's life","c":"一段經歷；事件","s":"Losing the final game was a painful episode in his life, but it taught him to practice harder and never give up.","t":"輸掉決賽是他人生中一段痛苦的經歷，但這教會他更努力練習、永不放棄。"},{"w":"the final episode","p":"n.phr.","d":"the last part of a TV series","c":"最後一集；完結篇","s":"Millions of fans around the world watched the final episode of the show on the same night and shared their feelings online.","t":"全世界數百萬粉絲在同一個晚上觀看了這部影集的最後一集，並在網路上分享他們的感受。"},{"w":"equation","p":"n.","d":"a math statement showing that two things are equal, such as 2 + 3 = 5","c":"方程式；等式","s":"The math teacher wrote a long equation on the board and asked us to find the value of x before the bell rang.","t":"數學老師在黑板上寫了一道很長的方程式，要我們在鐘響前求出 x 的值。","h":1},{"w":"equate","p":"v.","d":"to consider one thing to be the same as another","c":"把…等同於","s":"Many people equate money with happiness, but studies show that good friends and health matter much more in the long run.","t":"許多人把金錢等同於快樂，但研究顯示，長期來看好朋友和健康重要得多。"},{"w":"equal","p":"adj.","d":"the same in size, number, or value","c":"相等的；平等的","s":"Cut the cake into eight equal pieces so that every child at the party gets exactly the same amount.","t":"把蛋糕切成八等份，這樣派對上的每個孩子都能拿到完全一樣的分量。"},{"w":"equality","p":"n.","d":"the state of being equal, especially in rights and chances","c":"平等","s":"The new law aims to bring more equality to the workplace by making sure men and women receive the same pay for the same job.","t":"這項新法律旨在確保男女同工同酬，為職場帶來更多平等。"},{"w":"equity","p":"n.","d":"fairness; treating everyone in a way that is fair and right","c":"公平；公正","s":"The teacher believes in equity, so she gives extra help to students who need it instead of treating everyone exactly the same.","t":"這位老師相信公平，所以她會給需要的學生額外的幫助，而不是對每個人一視同仁。","h":1},{"w":"equitable","p":"adj.","d":"fair and reasonable for everyone involved","c":"公平合理的","s":"The two brothers finally found an equitable way to share the housework, so neither of them feels that he is doing more.","t":"兩兄弟終於找到一個公平合理的方式分擔家務，所以兩人都不覺得自己做得比較多。"},{"w":"inequity","p":"n.","d":"a situation that is unfair to some people","c":"不公平；不公正","s":"There is still great inequity in education, because children in rich areas usually have better schools than those in poor villages.","t":"教育上仍然存在很大的不公平，因為富裕地區的孩子通常比貧窮村莊的孩子有更好的學校。"},{"w":"equivalent","p":"adj.","d":"equal in value, amount, meaning, or importance","c":"相等的；等值的","s":"One kilogram is equivalent to about 2.2 pounds, so a ten-kilogram bag of rice weighs around twenty-two pounds.","t":"一公斤相當於大約 2.2 磅，所以一袋十公斤的米大約重二十二磅。","h":1},{"w":"equivalent","p":"n.","d":"something that has the same value, size, or meaning as something else","c":"相等物；對等的東西","s":"There is no English equivalent for the Chinese word \"緣分,\" so translators often have to explain it in a whole sentence.","t":"中文「緣分」這個詞在英文裡沒有對等的字，所以譯者常常得用一整句話來解釋它。"},{"w":"be equivalent to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be equal to something in value or meaning","c":"相當於…","s":"In this game, three silver coins are equivalent to one gold coin, so you need thirty silver coins to buy the magic sword.","t":"在這個遊戲裡，三枚銀幣相當於一枚金幣，所以你需要三十枚銀幣才能買魔法劍。","a":"are equivalent to"},{"w":"equivalence","p":"n.","d":"the state of being equal in value or meaning","c":"等值；相等","s":"The two schools signed an agreement on the equivalence of their courses, so students can transfer credits without losing a year.","t":"兩所學校簽署了課程等值協議，所以學生可以轉換學分而不會損失一年。"},{"w":"erect","p":"v.","d":"to build something or put something in an upright position","c":"建立；豎起","s":"The city plans to erect a statue of the famous writer in the main square to celebrate the 100th anniversary of his birth.","t":"市政府計畫在主廣場豎立一座這位著名作家的雕像，以慶祝他的百歲誕辰。","h":1},{"w":"erect","p":"adj.","d":"standing or sitting straight up","c":"直立的；筆直的","s":"The soldiers stood erect and silent for ten minutes while the national flag was slowly raised in the morning wind.","t":"士兵們筆直地站著，安靜了十分鐘，而國旗在晨風中緩緩升起。"},{"w":"stand erect","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stand up very straight","c":"站得筆直","s":"The dance teacher told us to stand erect with our shoulders back, because good posture makes every movement look more beautiful.","t":"舞蹈老師告訴我們要站得筆直、肩膀往後，因為良好的姿態會讓每個動作看起來更美。"},{"w":"errand","p":"n.","d":"a short trip to do a small job, such as buying something or delivering a message","c":"差事；跑腿","s":"Before dinner, my mother sent me on an errand to buy some eggs and soy sauce from the corner store.","t":"晚餐前，我媽媽派我去跑一趟差事，到轉角的商店買些雞蛋和醬油。","h":1},{"w":"run errands","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go out and do several small jobs, like shopping or going to the bank","c":"跑腿；辦雜事","s":"Every Saturday morning, my grandfather likes to run errands on his bicycle, visiting the post office, the bank, and the market.","t":"每個星期六早上，我爺爺喜歡騎腳踏車去辦雜事，去郵局、銀行和市場。"},{"w":"on an errand","p":"phr.","d":"away doing a small job for someone","c":"出去辦事","s":"The secretary is on an errand right now, but she should be back in the office in about twenty minutes if you can wait.","t":"秘書現在出去辦事了，不過如果你可以等的話，她大約二十分鐘後應該會回到辦公室。"},{"w":"erupt","p":"v.","d":"(of a volcano) to explode and send out hot rock, ash, and smoke","c":"（火山）爆發","s":"Scientists warned that the volcano might erupt within days, so thousands of people living nearby were moved to safer places.","t":"科學家警告火山可能在幾天內爆發，所以附近數千名居民被遷移到較安全的地方。","h":1},{"w":"erupt","p":"v.","d":"to start suddenly and violently, such as a fight, anger, or laughter","c":"爆發；突然發生","s":"A fight suddenly began to erupt between fans of the two teams, and the police had to step in to stop it.","t":"兩隊球迷之間突然爆發了一場打鬥，警察不得不介入制止。"},{"w":"eruption","p":"n.","d":"the act of a volcano exploding; a sudden start of something violent","c":"爆發；噴發","s":"The eruption in 1991 covered nearby towns with thick gray ash, and farmers could not grow anything for several years.","t":"1991 年的那次噴發讓附近的城鎮覆上厚厚的灰色火山灰，農民好幾年都種不出任何東西。"},{"w":"volcanic eruption","p":"n.phr.","d":"an explosion of a volcano","c":"火山爆發","s":"After the volcanic eruption, the sky stayed dark for two days and planes could not fly because of the ash in the air.","t":"火山爆發之後，天空暗了兩天，飛機也因為空氣中的火山灰而無法飛行。"},{"w":"escalator","p":"n.","d":"a set of moving stairs that carries people up or down","c":"電扶梯","s":"Please hold the handrail and stand still on the escalator, because running on it is dangerous for you and other passengers.","t":"請握好扶手並在電扶梯上站好，因為在上面跑對你和其他乘客都很危險。","h":1},{"w":"escalate","p":"v.","d":"to become greater, more serious, or more violent","c":"升高；惡化；升級","s":"The small argument between the two drivers quickly began to escalate into a shouting match in the middle of the road.","t":"兩位駕駛之間的小爭執很快就升級成馬路中央的互相叫罵。"},{"w":"escalation","p":"n.","d":"an increase in the amount or seriousness of something","c":"升高；惡化","s":"Teachers are worried about the escalation of online bullying, which has doubled in the past three years according to a new report.","t":"老師們擔心網路霸凌的惡化，根據一份新報告，過去三年它已經增加了一倍。"},{"w":"take the escalator","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use the moving stairs","c":"搭電扶梯","s":"If the elevator is too crowded, you can take the escalator to the third floor, where the food court and the bookstore are.","t":"如果電梯太擠，你可以搭電扶梯到三樓，美食街和書店就在那裡。"},{"w":"essence","p":"n.","d":"the most important and basic quality of something","c":"本質；精髓","s":"Although the movie has many funny scenes, the essence of the story is a mother's love for her lost son.","t":"雖然這部電影有許多好笑的場面，但故事的本質是一位母親對失蹤兒子的愛。","h":1},{"w":"in essence","p":"phr.","d":"when you consider only the most basic and important part","c":"本質上；基本上","s":"The two plans look very different, but in essence they both ask students to spend more time reading and less time on their phones.","t":"這兩個計畫看起來很不一樣，但本質上它們都要求學生多花時間閱讀、少花時間在手機上。"},{"w":"essential","p":"adj.","d":"completely necessary; extremely important","c":"必要的；極重要的","s":"Clean water is essential for life, so the volunteers worked day and night to repair the pipes after the earthquake.","t":"乾淨的水對生命是不可或缺的，所以志工們在地震後日夜不停地搶修水管。"},{"w":"essentially","p":"adv.","d":"basically; in the most important ways","c":"基本上；本質上","s":"The new phone is essentially the same as last year's model, except that the camera is a little better and the price is higher.","t":"這款新手機基本上和去年的款式一樣，只是相機好一點、價格高一點。"},{"w":"essentials","p":"n.","d":"the most important and necessary things","c":"必需品；要點","s":"When you pack for a camping trip, bring only the essentials: water, food, a flashlight, and warm clothes for the night.","t":"露營打包時，只帶必需品：水、食物、手電筒，以及晚上穿的保暖衣物。"},{"w":"estate","p":"n.","d":"a large area of land with a big house; all the money and property a person owns","c":"莊園；地產；遺產","s":"The old man left his whole estate, including the farm and three houses, to the hospital that had cared for him.","t":"老人把他全部的遺產，包括農場和三間房子，留給了照顧過他的醫院。","h":1},{"w":"real estate","p":"n.phr.","d":"land and the buildings on it, especially when bought and sold","c":"房地產","s":"Prices of real estate in Taipei have risen so much that many young couples cannot afford to buy even a small apartment.","t":"台北的房地產價格漲得太高，許多年輕夫妻連一間小公寓都買不起。"},{"w":"estate agent","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose job is to sell or rent houses and land for others","c":"房地產仲介","s":"The estate agent showed us five apartments in one afternoon, but my parents liked the one closest to the MRT station best.","t":"那位房地產仲介一個下午帶我們看了五間公寓，但我父母最喜歡離捷運站最近的那一間。"},{"w":"housing estate","p":"n.phr.","d":"an area where many houses or apartment buildings were built at the same time","c":"住宅區；社區","s":"My grandparents live in a quiet housing estate with a small park in the middle where the neighbors exercise every morning.","t":"我的祖父母住在一個安靜的住宅區，中間有個小公園，鄰居們每天早上都在那裡運動。"},{"w":"eternal","p":"adj.","d":"lasting forever; never ending","c":"永恆的；永久的","s":"In the fairy tale, the prince and princess promise each other eternal love and live happily together for the rest of their lives.","t":"在童話裡，王子和公主互相許下永恆的愛，並幸福地共度餘生。","h":1},{"w":"eternally","p":"adv.","d":"forever; always","c":"永遠地；永恆地","s":"I will be eternally grateful to the doctor who saved my grandmother's life when she suddenly fell ill last winter.","t":"我將永遠感激那位在我奶奶去年冬天突然生病時救了她一命的醫生。"},{"w":"eternity","p":"n.","d":"time that never ends; a very long time","c":"永恆；漫長的時間","s":"Waiting for the test results felt like an eternity, although the teacher actually handed them back after only ten minutes.","t":"等待考試成績感覺像永恆那麼久，雖然老師其實只過了十分鐘就發回來了。"},{"w":"ethic","p":"n.","d":"a set of beliefs about what is right and how people should behave","c":"倫理；道德準則","s":"A strong work ethic is the reason she finishes every task on time, even when nobody is checking on her.","t":"強烈的工作倫理是她總能準時完成每項任務的原因，即使沒有人在檢查她。","h":1},{"w":"ethical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with right and wrong; morally right","c":"道德的；合乎倫理的","s":"Is it ethical to test new medicine on animals? The students discussed this difficult question for the whole class period.","t":"在動物身上測試新藥是道德的嗎？學生們整堂課都在討論這個困難的問題。","h":1},{"w":"ethics","p":"n.","d":"moral rules about what is right and wrong; the study of these rules","c":"倫理學；道德規範","s":"Doctors must follow strict medical ethics, which means they cannot share a patient's information with anyone else.","t":"醫生必須遵守嚴格的醫學倫理，這意味著他們不能把病人的資料分享給任何人。"},{"w":"unethical","p":"adj.","d":"morally wrong; not following the rules of right behavior","c":"不道德的","s":"Copying your friend's homework and handing it in as your own is unethical, and the school punishes students who do it.","t":"抄朋友的作業並當成自己的交出去是不道德的，學校會處罰這樣做的學生。"},{"w":"ethically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is morally right","c":"合乎道德地；倫理上","s":"The company promises that all of its clothes are made ethically, so no child workers are used and everyone is paid fairly.","t":"這家公司承諾所有衣服都是合乎道德地製造的，所以不使用童工，而且每個人都獲得公平的報酬。"},{"w":"work ethic","p":"n.phr.","d":"the belief that working hard is important and good","c":"工作倫理；敬業精神","s":"Thanks to his excellent work ethic, the new employee was promoted to team leader after only one year with the company.","t":"由於他出色的工作倫理，這位新員工在公司僅僅一年後就被升為組長。"},{"w":"evolution","p":"n.","d":"the slow change and development of living things over millions of years; gradual change","c":"演化；進化；逐漸發展","s":"In biology class, we learned that the evolution of birds from dinosaurs took millions of years and many small changes.","t":"在生物課上，我們學到鳥類從恐龍演化而來花了數百萬年和許多細小的改變。","h":1},{"w":"evolve","p":"v.","d":"to develop slowly over time; (of living things) to change over many generations","c":"演化；逐漸發展","s":"Smartphones continue to evolve every year, and the models we use today are far more powerful than the first ones from 2007.","t":"智慧型手機每年持續演進，我們今天使用的機型比 2007 年的第一批強大得多。","h":1},{"w":"evolve into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to develop slowly and become something different","c":"逐漸發展成…","s":"What started as a small school club has slowly evolved into a national organization with thousands of young volunteers.","t":"一開始只是一個小小的學校社團，如今已慢慢發展成一個擁有數千名年輕志工的全國性組織。","a":"evolved into"},{"w":"evolutionary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the slow development of living things or ideas","c":"演化的；進化的","s":"From an evolutionary point of view, humans like sweet food because sugar gave our ancestors quick energy when food was hard to find.","t":"從演化的觀點來看，人類喜歡甜食是因為在食物難找的時代，糖給了我們的祖先快速的能量。"},{"w":"theory of evolution","p":"n.phr.","d":"Darwin's idea that living things slowly change over time to fit their environment","c":"演化論","s":"Charles Darwin published his theory of evolution in 1859, and it changed the way scientists understand all life on Earth.","t":"達爾文在 1859 年發表了他的演化論，它改變了科學家理解地球上所有生命的方式。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"exaggeration – fabulous","cards":[{"w":"exaggeration","p":"n.","d":"a statement that makes something seem bigger, better, or worse than it really is","c":"誇張；誇大","s":"When my brother says he caught a fish as big as a car, everyone knows it is an exaggeration, because the lake only has small fish.","t":"當我哥哥說他釣到一條跟汽車一樣大的魚時，大家都知道那是誇張，因為那座湖裡只有小魚。","h":1},{"w":"exaggerate","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem bigger, better, or worse than it really is","c":"誇大；誇張","s":"Please do not exaggerate how long the trip took; it was two hours, not five, and we even stopped for lunch on the way.","t":"請不要誇大這趟旅程花了多久；是兩小時，不是五小時，而且我們途中還停下來吃午餐。"},{"w":"exaggerated","p":"adj.","d":"made to seem bigger or more important than it really is","c":"誇大的；誇張的","s":"The ad makes exaggerated claims about the cream, saying it can make you look ten years younger in only one week.","t":"這則廣告對這款乳霜做了誇大的宣稱，說它能讓你在短短一週內看起來年輕十歲。"},{"w":"exceed","p":"v.","d":"to be greater than a number or amount; to go beyond a limit","c":"超過；超出","s":"The number of visitors to the night market this weekend is expected to exceed fifty thousand because of the long holiday.","t":"由於連假的關係，這個週末夜市的遊客人數預計會超過五萬人。","h":1},{"w":"excessive","p":"adj.","d":"more than is necessary, normal, or reasonable","c":"過多的；過度的","s":"Doctors warn that excessive use of smartphones at night can hurt your eyes and make it hard to fall asleep.","t":"醫生警告，夜間過度使用智慧型手機會傷害眼睛，並讓人難以入睡。","h":1},{"w":"excess","p":"n.","d":"an amount that is more than what is needed or allowed","c":"過量；超過的部分","s":"The airline charges extra money for any excess baggage, so make sure your suitcase weighs less than twenty-three kilograms.","t":"航空公司對任何超重行李都會加收費用，所以請確認你的行李箱不到二十三公斤。"},{"w":"excessively","p":"adv.","d":"too much; more than is reasonable","c":"過度地；過分地","s":"My grandmother worries excessively about my health, so she calls me every evening to ask if I have eaten enough vegetables.","t":"我奶奶過度擔心我的健康，所以她每天晚上都打電話問我有沒有吃夠蔬菜。"},{"w":"exceed the speed limit","p":"v.phr.","d":"to drive faster than the law allows","c":"超速","s":"The police officer stopped my uncle because he had been caught on camera trying to exceed the speed limit on the highway near the airport.","t":"警察攔下我叔叔，因為他在機場附近的高速公路上被相機拍到超速。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"unusually good; much better than usual","c":"卓越的；傑出的；異常的","s":"Only students with exceptional grades in both math and science are invited to join the special program at the national university.","t":"只有數學和自然都拿到卓越成績的學生，才會受邀參加國立大學的特別課程。","h":1},{"w":"exceptionally","p":"adv.","d":"unusually; to a much greater degree than normal","c":"格外地；異常地","s":"It was an exceptionally cold winter last year, and snow even fell on some low mountains near Taipei for the first time in decades.","t":"去年冬天異常寒冷，台北附近一些低矮的山上甚至幾十年來第一次下雪。"},{"w":"exception","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that is not included in a rule or group","c":"例外","s":"Everyone must wear a uniform to school, and the only exception is on Fridays, when students can wear their club T-shirts.","t":"每個人上學都必須穿制服，唯一的例外是星期五，那天學生可以穿社團 T 恤。"},{"w":"except","p":"prep.","d":"not including; apart from","c":"除了…之外","s":"The small restaurant is open every day except Monday, so we will have to go there on Tuesday evening instead.","t":"這家小餐廳除了星期一以外每天都營業，所以我們得改在星期二晚上去。"},{"w":"exclaim","p":"v.","d":"to say something suddenly and loudly because you are surprised, excited, or angry","c":"驚呼；大聲說","s":"\"Look at the size of that cake!\" the little girl began to exclaim when her mother opened the box on her birthday.","t":"「看看那個蛋糕有多大！」小女孩在生日那天看到媽媽打開盒子時驚呼起來。","h":1},{"w":"exclamation","p":"n.","d":"a short sound or words said suddenly to show surprise, pain, or excitement","c":"驚呼；感嘆","s":"There was an exclamation of joy from the crowd when the home team scored the winning goal in the last minute.","t":"當主隊在最後一分鐘踢進致勝球時，人群中響起一陣喜悅的驚呼。"},{"w":"exclamation mark","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sign (!) used after a sentence to show strong feeling","c":"驚嘆號","s":"In formal writing, you should use an exclamation mark very rarely, because too many of them make your essay look childish.","t":"在正式寫作中，你應該很少使用驚嘆號，因為太多驚嘆號會讓你的文章看起來很幼稚。"},{"w":"exclude","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone or something out; to not include","c":"排除；不包括","s":"The coach decided to exclude two players from the final game because they had missed practice three times without any reason.","t":"教練決定將兩名球員排除在決賽之外，因為他們無故缺席了三次練習。","h":1},{"w":"exclusive","p":"adj.","d":"only for a particular group of people; not shared with others","c":"獨家的；專屬的","s":"The hotel has an exclusive beach that only its guests can use, so it is never crowded even in the middle of summer.","t":"這家飯店有一片只有房客能使用的專屬海灘，所以即使在盛夏也從不擁擠。","h":1},{"w":"exclude sb from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop someone from taking part in something","c":"把某人排除在…之外","s":"It is unfair to exclude her from the game just because she is new and does not know all the rules yet.","t":"只因為她是新來的、還不懂所有規則，就把她排除在遊戲之外是不公平的。","a":"exclude her from"},{"w":"exclusion","p":"n.","d":"the act of keeping someone or something out","c":"排除；排斥","s":"The exclusion of younger students from the school trip made many of them cry, so the principal promised a special trip just for them.","t":"校外教學排除了低年級學生，讓許多人哭了，所以校長承諾會為他們安排一趟專屬的旅行。"},{"w":"exclusively","p":"adv.","d":"only; and nothing or no one else","c":"僅僅；專門地","s":"This small shop sells exclusively handmade chocolate, so you will not find any candy or cookies on its shelves.","t":"這家小店只賣手工巧克力，所以你在它的架上找不到任何糖果或餅乾。"},{"w":"execute","p":"v.","d":"to do or carry out a plan, order, or piece of work","c":"執行；實行","s":"It is easy to make a plan, but it takes hard work and good teamwork to execute it successfully from beginning to end.","t":"制定計畫很容易，但要從頭到尾成功執行它，需要努力和良好的團隊合作。","h":1},{"w":"execute","p":"v.","d":"to kill someone as a legal punishment for a crime","c":"處決；處死","s":"In the past, kings had the power to execute anyone who disagreed with them, so most people were afraid to speak freely.","t":"過去，國王有權處決任何與他意見不合的人，所以大多數人都不敢自由發言。","h":1},{"w":"execution","p":"n.","d":"the carrying out of a plan; the killing of someone as a punishment","c":"執行；處決","s":"The idea for the school festival was wonderful, but its execution was poor because nobody checked the weather or booked the equipment.","t":"校慶的構想很棒，但執行得很差，因為沒有人查天氣，也沒有人預訂設備。","h":1},{"w":"executive","p":"n.","d":"a senior manager in a company or organization","c":"主管；高階經理","s":"My aunt is a top executive at a bank, so she travels to Hong Kong and Singapore almost every month for important meetings.","t":"我阿姨是一家銀行的高階主管，所以她幾乎每個月都要到香港和新加坡參加重要會議。"},{"w":"executive","p":"adj.","d":"connected with managing a company or making important decisions","c":"行政的；管理的","s":"The company's executive team meets every Monday morning to decide which new products should be sold next year.","t":"公司的管理團隊每週一早上開會，決定明年要販售哪些新產品。"},{"w":"chief executive officer","p":"n.phr.","d":"the person with the most power in a company (CEO)","c":"執行長","s":"At only thirty-five, she became the chief executive officer of the company and quickly doubled its sales by opening stores in Japan.","t":"她在三十五歲時就成為公司的執行長，並透過在日本開店迅速讓銷售額翻倍。"},{"w":"exile","p":"n.","d":"the state of being forced to live away from your own country; a person in this state","c":"流放；流亡；流亡者","s":"After the war, the king spent twenty years in exile in France and never saw his home country again before he died.","t":"戰後，國王在法國流亡了二十年，去世前再也沒有見過自己的祖國。","h":1},{"w":"exile","p":"v.","d":"to force someone to leave their country as a punishment","c":"流放；放逐","s":"The new government decided to exile the old leader to a small island, where he lived quietly for the rest of his life.","t":"新政府決定把前領導人流放到一座小島，他在那裡安靜地度過餘生。"},{"w":"in exile","p":"phr.","d":"living away from your own country because you are not allowed to return","c":"流亡中","s":"The writer lived in exile for many years, but his books were secretly passed from hand to hand in his home country.","t":"這位作家流亡多年，但他的書在祖國被人們偷偷地一手傳一手。"},{"w":"exotic","p":"adj.","d":"from a far-away country and therefore unusual and interesting","c":"異國的；外來的","s":"The zoo has many exotic animals from Africa and South America, including a bird that can copy human speech.","t":"這座動物園有許多來自非洲和南美洲的異國動物，包括一隻會模仿人說話的鳥。","h":1},{"w":"exotic","p":"adj.","d":"unusual and exciting in a way that seems different from everyday life","c":"奇異的；充滿異國情調的","s":"The restaurant is famous for its exotic flavors, like mango with chili and ice cream made from black sesame.","t":"這家餐廳以奇特的風味聞名，像是芒果配辣椒，以及用黑芝麻做的冰淇淋。"},{"w":"exotic food","p":"n.phr.","d":"unusual dishes from other countries","c":"異國料理","s":"My father loves trying exotic food when he travels, so last year he ate fried insects in Thailand and snails in France.","t":"我爸爸旅行時喜歡嘗試異國料理，所以去年他在泰國吃了炸昆蟲，在法國吃了蝸牛。"},{"w":"expedition","p":"n.","d":"a long journey made for a special purpose, such as science or exploring","c":"遠征；探險","s":"In 1911, a small team reached the South Pole after a dangerous expedition across hundreds of kilometers of ice and snow.","t":"1911 年，一支小隊在穿越數百公里冰雪的危險遠征後抵達了南極點。","h":1},{"w":"go on an expedition","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a long journey for exploring or research","c":"去探險；進行遠征","s":"Next summer, a group of scientists will go on an expedition to the deep sea near Taiwan to look for animals nobody has ever seen.","t":"明年夏天，一群科學家將前往台灣附近的深海探險，尋找從來沒有人見過的動物。"},{"w":"expedition team","p":"n.phr.","d":"the group of people who make a special journey together","c":"探險隊；遠征隊","s":"The expedition team carried enough food for forty days, because there would be no villages or shops on the way up the mountain.","t":"探險隊帶了足夠四十天的食物，因為上山的路上不會有任何村莊或商店。"},{"w":"expertise","p":"n.","d":"special skill or knowledge that you get from experience or training","c":"專門知識；專長","s":"We asked Mr. Wang to fix the old computer because of his expertise in repairing machines that nobody else can save.","t":"我們請王先生修那台舊電腦，因為他在修理別人都救不了的機器方面有專業知識。","h":1},{"w":"expert","p":"n.","d":"a person who knows a lot about a subject or is very skilled at something","c":"專家","s":"My grandfather is an expert on tea, and he can tell which mountain a tea comes from just by smelling it.","t":"我爺爺是茶葉專家，光靠聞一聞就能說出一款茶來自哪座山。"},{"w":"expert","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing special skill or knowledge","c":"專業的；熟練的","s":"Thanks to the expert advice of our coach, the team learned to pass the ball faster and won the city championship.","t":"多虧教練專業的建議，球隊學會了更快地傳球，贏得了市冠軍。"},{"w":"expertly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very skillful way","c":"熟練地；專業地","s":"The chef expertly cut the fish into thin slices in less than a minute while the customers watched in silence.","t":"廚師在不到一分鐘內熟練地把魚切成薄片，顧客們安靜地看著。"},{"w":"explicit","p":"adj.","d":"said or shown clearly and directly, so there is no doubt about the meaning","c":"明確的；清楚直接的","s":"The teacher gave explicit instructions about the homework, so nobody could say later that they did not understand what to do.","t":"老師對作業給了明確的指示，所以之後沒有人能說自己不知道要做什麼。","h":1},{"w":"explicitly","p":"adv.","d":"clearly and directly","c":"明確地；清楚地","s":"The sign explicitly says that no food or drinks are allowed in the library, but some students still bring snacks inside.","t":"告示牌明確地寫著圖書館內不准攜帶食物或飲料，但有些學生仍然把零食帶進去。"},{"w":"implicit","p":"adj.","d":"suggested but not said directly","c":"含蓄的；暗示的","s":"There was an implicit promise in the manager's words that anyone who worked hard this year would get a raise next spring.","t":"經理的話中有一個含蓄的承諾：今年努力工作的人明年春天都會加薪。"},{"w":"exploit","p":"v.","d":"to treat someone unfairly in order to get something from them","c":"剝削；利用","s":"Some factories exploit young workers by paying them very little and making them work twelve hours a day without a break.","t":"有些工廠剝削年輕工人，付他們很少的薪水，還讓他們每天工作十二小時不休息。","h":1},{"w":"exploit","p":"v.","d":"to use something fully and get as much benefit from it as possible","c":"開發；充分利用","s":"The island plans to exploit its strong winds by building fifty wind machines that will produce electricity for the whole town.","t":"這座島計畫充分利用強風，建造五十座風力機組，為整個城鎮發電。"},{"w":"exploit","p":"n.","d":"a brave, exciting, or interesting act","c":"英勇事蹟；壯舉","s":"The book tells the exploits of a young pilot who flew across the ocean alone at a time when planes were still very simple.","t":"這本書講述一位年輕飛行員的英勇事蹟，他在飛機還很簡陋的年代獨自飛越海洋。","a":"exploits"},{"w":"exploitation","p":"n.","d":"the act of treating people unfairly to benefit from their work","c":"剝削；利用","s":"The new law aims to stop the exploitation of foreign workers, who often receive less pay than local workers for the same job.","t":"新法律旨在阻止對外籍勞工的剝削，他們做同樣的工作卻常常拿到比本地勞工少的薪水。"},{"w":"exploration","p":"n.","d":"the act of traveling through a place to learn about it; careful study of a subject","c":"探索；探勘；探究","s":"The exploration of the deep ocean is still in its early days, and scientists believe thousands of sea animals are waiting to be found.","t":"深海探索仍在起步階段，科學家相信有數千種海洋動物等著被發現。","h":1},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around a place to learn about it; to examine something carefully","c":"探索；探究","s":"On the first day of our trip, we decided to explore the old town on foot and found a tiny bookstore hidden in a narrow lane.","t":"旅行的第一天，我們決定步行探索舊城區，結果發現一家藏在窄巷裡的小書店。"},{"w":"explorer","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels to unknown places to find out about them","c":"探險家","s":"The famous explorer spent three years in the jungle and drew the first map of the river for people back home.","t":"這位著名的探險家在叢林裡待了三年，為家鄉的人畫出了這條河的第一張地圖。"},{"w":"space exploration","p":"n.phr.","d":"the study of space by sending rockets, machines, and people there","c":"太空探索","s":"Many countries spend billions of dollars on space exploration, hoping to send people to Mars within the next twenty years.","t":"許多國家在太空探索上花費數十億美元，希望在未來二十年內把人送上火星。"},{"w":"extension","p":"n.","d":"extra time given to finish something; a part added to make something longer or bigger","c":"延期；延長；擴建部分","s":"Because I was sick for a week, the teacher gave me a three-day extension to finish my science report.","t":"因為我病了一個星期，老師給我三天的延期來完成科學報告。","h":1},{"w":"extensive","p":"adj.","d":"covering a large area or a lot of things; very great in amount","c":"廣泛的；大量的","s":"The typhoon caused extensive damage along the east coast, and some roads will take months to repair.","t":"颱風在東海岸造成大範圍的損害，有些道路需要幾個月才能修好。","h":1},{"w":"extend","p":"v.","d":"to make something longer or bigger; to continue for a distance or time","c":"延長；擴大；延伸","s":"The city plans to extend the MRT line to the airport, so travelers will no longer need to take a bus or a taxi.","t":"市政府計畫把捷運線延伸到機場，這樣旅客就不用再搭公車或計程車了。"},{"w":"extent","p":"n.","d":"the size, amount, or degree of something","c":"程度；範圍","s":"After the fire, the owner walked through the building to see the extent of the damage before calling the insurance company.","t":"火災過後，屋主走過整棟建築查看損害的程度，然後才打電話給保險公司。"},{"w":"extensively","p":"adv.","d":"widely; in a way that covers a lot","c":"廣泛地；大量地","s":"Before writing her book about Taiwan's temples, the author traveled extensively around the island for more than two years.","t":"在撰寫關於台灣寺廟的書之前，作者花了兩年多的時間在島上廣泛地旅行。"},{"w":"exterior","p":"n.","d":"the outside of something, especially a building","c":"外部；外觀","s":"The exterior of the old house looks plain and gray, but the rooms inside are full of color and beautiful furniture.","t":"這棟老房子的外觀看起來樸素又灰暗，但裡面的房間充滿色彩和漂亮的家具。","h":1},{"w":"exterior","p":"adj.","d":"on or from the outside","c":"外部的；外面的","s":"The exterior walls of the school were painted bright yellow last summer, so now you can see the building from far away.","t":"學校的外牆去年夏天漆成了亮黃色，所以現在你從很遠的地方就能看見這棟建築。"},{"w":"interior","p":"n.","d":"the inside of something, especially a building or car","c":"內部；室內","s":"The interior of the new library is bright and quiet, with soft chairs by the windows where students love to read.","t":"新圖書館的內部明亮又安靜，窗邊有舒適的椅子，學生們很喜歡在那裡閱讀。"},{"w":"external","p":"adj.","d":"coming from or connected with the outside","c":"外部的；外來的","s":"The doctor said the cut was only an external wound, so it would heal in a week without any need for an operation.","t":"醫生說這道傷口只是外部的傷，一週內就會癒合，不需要手術。","h":1},{"w":"externally","p":"adv.","d":"on or from the outside","c":"在外部；從外部","s":"This medicine should only be used externally on the skin, so never swallow it, even if the pain is very bad.","t":"這種藥只能外用在皮膚上，所以即使疼痛很嚴重也絕對不要吞下去。"},{"w":"internal","p":"adj.","d":"inside something; happening within a country, company, or body","c":"內部的；體內的","s":"The company is holding an internal meeting this afternoon, so no visitors or reporters are allowed into the building.","t":"公司今天下午要開內部會議，所以不允許任何訪客或記者進入大樓。"},{"w":"extinct","p":"adj.","d":"(of an animal or plant) no longer existing","c":"絕種的；滅絕的","s":"Dinosaurs have been extinct for about sixty-five million years, but we can still learn about them from their bones.","t":"恐龍已經絕種大約六千五百萬年了，但我們仍然可以從牠們的骨頭了解牠們。","h":1},{"w":"extinction","p":"n.","d":"the situation in which an animal or plant stops existing","c":"絕種；滅絕","s":"Many sea turtles are in danger of extinction because plastic bags in the ocean look like the jellyfish they eat.","t":"許多海龜面臨絕種的危險，因為海洋裡的塑膠袋看起來就像牠們吃的水母。"},{"w":"become extinct","p":"v.phr.","d":"to die out completely","c":"滅絕；絕種","s":"If we keep cutting down the forest, this rare bird will become extinct within twenty years, and our children will only see it in pictures.","t":"如果我們繼續砍伐森林，這種稀有的鳥將在二十年內絕種，我們的孩子就只能在圖片上看到牠了。"},{"w":"extraordinary","p":"adj.","d":"very unusual, surprising, or special","c":"非凡的；驚人的","s":"The young pianist has an extraordinary memory and can play a whole concert without looking at a single page of music.","t":"這位年輕的鋼琴家有驚人的記憶力，可以不看一頁樂譜就演奏整場音樂會。","h":1},{"w":"extraordinarily","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; in a very unusual way","c":"非常；格外地","s":"The test was extraordinarily difficult this time, and even the best student in our class could not finish all the questions.","t":"這次考試格外困難，連我們班最優秀的學生都無法做完所有題目。"},{"w":"ordinary","p":"adj.","d":"normal and not special or different in any way","c":"普通的；平凡的","s":"It started as an ordinary Monday morning, but by noon the whole school was talking about the surprise visit from a famous singer.","t":"那天一開始只是個普通的星期一早晨，但到了中午，全校都在談論一位知名歌手的驚喜造訪。"},{"w":"fabric","p":"n.","d":"cloth used for making clothes, curtains, and other things","c":"布料；織物","s":"My mother bought three meters of soft blue fabric at the market to make new curtains for my bedroom.","t":"我媽媽在市場買了三公尺柔軟的藍色布料，要為我的臥室做新窗簾。","h":1},{"w":"the fabric of society","p":"n.phr.","d":"the basic structure that holds a society together","c":"社會結構；社會基礎","s":"Many people believe that trust between neighbors is part of the fabric of society, and when it disappears, crime and fear increase.","t":"許多人相信鄰居之間的信任是社會結構的一部分，一旦它消失，犯罪和恐懼就會增加。"},{"w":"fabricate","p":"v.","d":"to invent false information in order to trick people","c":"捏造；編造","s":"The student tried to fabricate a story about a sick grandmother to explain why his homework was late, but the teacher did not believe him.","t":"這個學生試圖編造一個關於生病奶奶的故事來解釋作業為什麼遲交，但老師不相信他。"},{"w":"fabulous","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; wonderful","c":"極好的；美妙的","s":"We had a fabulous time at the beach yesterday; the weather was perfect, and the water was warm enough for swimming all afternoon.","t":"我們昨天在海邊玩得非常開心；天氣完美，海水也溫暖到可以游一整個下午。","h":1},{"w":"fabulously","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; in a wonderful way","c":"極其；非常地","s":"The singer is fabulously rich now, but she still visits the small town where she grew up and gives free concerts there every year.","t":"這位歌手現在極其富有，但她仍然每年回到她長大的小鎮，在那裡舉辦免費演唱會。"},{"w":"fable","p":"n.","d":"a short story, often with animals as characters, that teaches a lesson","c":"寓言","s":"\"The Tortoise and the Hare\" is a famous fable that teaches children that slow and steady effort can win the race.","t":"《龜兔賽跑》是一則著名的寓言，教導孩子緩慢而穩定的努力也能贏得比賽。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"facilitate – frontier","cards":[{"w":"facilitate","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier or more possible","c":"促進；使便利","s":"The new online system will facilitate communication between teachers and parents, so questions can be answered within a day.","t":"新的線上系統將促進老師和家長之間的溝通，所以問題可以在一天內得到回答。","h":1},{"w":"facility","p":"n.","d":"a building, room, or piece of equipment provided for a particular purpose","c":"設施；設備","s":"The new sports facility has an indoor pool and a gym, so students can exercise even when it rains outside.","t":"新的運動設施有室內游泳池和健身房，所以即使外面下雨學生也能運動。"},{"w":"facilitator","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps a group work together and discuss things well","c":"引導者；協調者","s":"In our class discussion, the teacher acted as a facilitator who asked questions but let the students find the answers themselves.","t":"在我們的課堂討論中，老師扮演引導者的角色，提出問題但讓學生自己找答案。"},{"w":"faculty","p":"n.","d":"all the teachers of a school, college, or university","c":"全體教師","s":"The faculty of our school voted to start classes thirty minutes later, because studies show teenagers need more morning sleep.","t":"我們學校的全體教師投票決定延後三十分鐘上課，因為研究顯示青少年早上需要更多睡眠。","h":1},{"w":"faculty","p":"n.","d":"a department of a university that teaches one subject area","c":"（大學的）學院","s":"My sister studies at the Faculty of Medicine, where students spend seven years learning before they can become doctors.","t":"我姐姐在醫學院讀書，學生在那裡要學習七年才能成為醫生。","a":"Faculty"},{"w":"faculty","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability of the mind or body","c":"官能；能力","s":"Even at the age of ninety, my grandmother still has the full faculty of memory and can name every student she ever taught.","t":"即使九十歲了，我奶奶仍然擁有完整的記憶能力，能說出她教過的每一個學生的名字。"},{"w":"fascinate","p":"v.","d":"to attract and hold someone's interest very strongly","c":"使著迷；深深吸引","s":"Stories about ancient Egypt always fascinate my little brother, so he wants to visit the pyramids when he grows up.","t":"關於古埃及的故事總是讓我弟弟著迷，所以他長大後想去參觀金字塔。","h":1},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"迷人的；極有趣的","s":"The museum guide told us a fascinating story about how the old painting was stolen twice and found both times in a train station.","t":"博物館導覽員告訴我們一個極有趣的故事，關於那幅古畫被偷了兩次，兩次都在火車站被找到。"},{"w":"fascinated","p":"adj.","d":"very interested in something","c":"著迷的；入迷的","s":"The children were so fascinated by the magic show that they forgot about the ice cream melting in their hands.","t":"孩子們被魔術表演迷住了，忘了手上的冰淇淋正在融化。"},{"w":"be fascinated by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to find something extremely interesting","c":"對…著迷","s":"Ever since she visited the night sky observatory, my cousin has been fascinated by the stars and reads about space every night.","t":"自從參觀了天文台之後，我表妹就一直對星星著迷，每天晚上都讀關於太空的書。","a":"has been fascinated by"},{"w":"fascination","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest in something","c":"迷戀；著迷","s":"My father's fascination with old cars started when he was ten, and now his garage is full of parts from the 1960s.","t":"我爸爸對老爺車的迷戀從十歲開始，現在他的車庫裡堆滿了 1960 年代的零件。"},{"w":"fatigue","p":"n.","d":"great tiredness of body or mind","c":"疲勞；疲倦","s":"After working twelve hours a day for a month, the nurse began to feel fatigue so deep that even a full night's sleep did not help.","t":"在一個月每天工作十二小時之後，這位護士開始感到深深的疲勞，連睡一整晚都沒有幫助。","h":1},{"w":"fatigued","p":"adj.","d":"extremely tired","c":"疲憊的；疲倦的","s":"The hikers were so fatigued after climbing for nine hours that they fell asleep as soon as they reached the mountain hut.","t":"登山客在爬了九個小時後疲憊不堪，一到山屋就睡著了。"},{"w":"suffer from fatigue","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel extremely tired, often because of illness or too much work","c":"感到疲勞；深受疲勞之苦","s":"Students who stay up late playing games often suffer from fatigue during the day and cannot pay attention to their teachers.","t":"熬夜玩遊戲的學生白天常常感到疲勞，無法專心聽老師講課。"},{"w":"federal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the central government of a country made up of several states","c":"聯邦的","s":"In the United States, federal law is the same in every state, but each state can also make its own rules about things like driving.","t":"在美國，聯邦法律在每一州都相同，但每一州也可以為開車等事務制定自己的規定。","h":1},{"w":"federal government","p":"n.phr.","d":"the central government of a country such as the US, Canada, or Australia","c":"聯邦政府","s":"After the big flood, the federal government sent money and soldiers to help the state rebuild its roads and bridges as quickly as possible.","t":"大洪水之後，聯邦政府派出資金和士兵，幫助該州盡快重建道路和橋梁。"},{"w":"federation","p":"n.","d":"a group of states or organizations that have joined together under one central group","c":"聯邦；聯合會","s":"The international football federation decided that the next World Cup would be held in three different countries at the same time.","t":"國際足球聯合會決定下一屆世界盃將同時在三個不同的國家舉行。"},{"w":"fiber","p":"n.","d":"the part of fruits, vegetables, and grains that your body cannot digest but that keeps you healthy","c":"纖維；膳食纖維","s":"Doctors say we should eat more vegetables and whole grains, because the fiber in them helps our stomachs work properly.","t":"醫生說我們應該多吃蔬菜和全穀物，因為它們含有的纖維有助於我們的腸胃正常運作。","h":1},{"w":"fiber","p":"n.","d":"a thin thread of natural or man-made material used to make cloth or rope","c":"纖維；纖維質材料","s":"Cotton is a natural fiber that is soft and cool, which is why most summer T-shirts in Taiwan are made from it.","t":"棉是一種柔軟又涼爽的天然纖維，這就是為什麼台灣大多數夏季 T 恤是用它做的。"},{"w":"dietary fiber","p":"n.phr.","d":"fiber in food that helps digestion","c":"膳食纖維","s":"A bowl of oatmeal with fruit is a great breakfast because it is full of dietary fiber and keeps you feeling full until lunch.","t":"一碗加水果的燕麥粥是很棒的早餐，因為它富含膳食纖維，能讓你飽到午餐時間。"},{"w":"filter","p":"n.","d":"a device that removes unwanted things from water, air, or light","c":"過濾器；濾網","s":"You should change the filter in the air cleaner every three months, or it will stop removing dust from the room.","t":"你應該每三個月更換一次空氣清淨機的濾網，否則它就無法再清除房間裡的灰塵。","h":1},{"w":"filter","p":"v.","d":"to pass a liquid or gas through a device to remove unwanted things","c":"過濾","s":"In the countryside, my grandparents filter rainwater through sand and charcoal before they use it for cooking or drinking.","t":"在鄉下，我的祖父母先用沙子和木炭過濾雨水，然後才用它來煮飯或飲用。"},{"w":"filter out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to remove something unwanted from a group of things","c":"濾除；篩掉","s":"The new email program can filter out most advertising messages, so only letters from real people reach your inbox.","t":"新的電子郵件程式可以濾除大部分的廣告訊息，所以只有真人寄的信會進入你的收件匣。"},{"w":"water filter","p":"n.phr.","d":"a device that makes water clean enough to drink","c":"濾水器","s":"We installed a water filter in the kitchen last year, so now the whole family drinks tap water instead of buying bottles.","t":"我們去年在廚房裝了一台濾水器，所以現在全家人都喝自來水，而不是買瓶裝水。"},{"w":"fiscal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with government money, taxes, and public spending","c":"財政的；會計的","s":"The government announced a new fiscal plan that will raise taxes on cigarettes and use the money to build more hospitals.","t":"政府宣布了一項新的財政計畫，將提高香菸稅，並用這筆錢蓋更多醫院。","h":1},{"w":"fiscal year","p":"n.phr.","d":"a twelve-month period that a company or government uses for its money records","c":"會計年度；財政年度","s":"The company's fiscal year ends in March, so all the managers are busy finishing their money reports before the deadline.","t":"這家公司的會計年度在三月結束，所以所有經理都忙著在期限前完成財務報告。"},{"w":"fiscal policy","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way a government uses taxes and spending to manage the economy","c":"財政政策","s":"Experts say a good fiscal policy should help poor families through hard times without putting the country deeply into debt.","t":"專家說好的財政政策應該幫助貧困家庭度過難關，又不讓國家陷入嚴重的債務。"},{"w":"fleet","p":"n.","d":"a group of ships that sail together or belong to one country or company","c":"艦隊；船隊","s":"A large fleet of fishing boats leaves the harbor every morning before sunrise and returns with fresh fish by noon.","t":"一支龐大的漁船隊每天早上日出前離開港口，中午前帶著新鮮的魚回來。","h":1},{"w":"fleet","p":"n.","d":"a group of buses, taxis, or planes owned by one company","c":"車隊；機隊","s":"The taxi company is replacing its whole fleet with electric cars, which are quieter and cheaper to run in the city.","t":"這家計程車公司正在把整個車隊換成電動車，它們在市區更安靜，也更省錢。"},{"w":"fishing fleet","p":"n.phr.","d":"all the fishing boats of a port or country","c":"漁船隊","s":"The small town depends on its fishing fleet for jobs, so everyone worried when the price of fish fell sharply last year.","t":"這個小鎮依靠它的漁船隊提供工作機會，所以去年魚價大跌時每個人都很擔心。"},{"w":"flexibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to bend easily; the ability to change plans or ideas when needed","c":"柔軟度；靈活性；彈性","s":"Doing yoga every morning has improved my flexibility so much that I can now touch my toes without bending my knees.","t":"每天早上做瑜伽讓我的柔軟度進步很多，現在我不用彎膝蓋就能摸到腳趾。","h":1},{"w":"flexible","p":"adj.","d":"able to bend easily; able to change to suit new situations","c":"柔軟的；有彈性的；靈活的","s":"My boss is very flexible about working hours, so I can start late on days when I need to take my daughter to school.","t":"我的老闆對工作時間很有彈性，所以在我需要送女兒上學的日子可以晚一點開始上班。"},{"w":"flexibly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that can change easily to suit different needs","c":"靈活地；有彈性地","s":"Good teachers plan their lessons flexibly, so they can spend more time on a topic if students find it hard.","t":"好老師靈活地規劃課程，所以如果學生覺得某個主題很難，他們可以多花一些時間。"},{"w":"inflexible","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to change; impossible to bend","c":"不靈活的；固執的；僵硬的","s":"The hotel's inflexible rules did not allow us to check in even ten minutes early, so we waited in the lobby with our heavy bags.","t":"飯店死板的規定不允許我們提早十分鐘入住，所以我們提著沉重的行李在大廳等候。"},{"w":"flip","p":"v.","d":"to turn something over quickly; to turn over in the air","c":"翻轉；快速翻動","s":"Wait until the pancake has bubbles on top, and then flip it quickly so that the other side turns golden brown too.","t":"等到鬆餅表面出現氣泡，然後快速把它翻面，讓另一面也變成金黃色。","h":1},{"w":"flip","p":"n.","d":"a quick turn or movement, often in the air","c":"翻轉；空翻","s":"The gymnast did a perfect flip in the air and landed on both feet, and the judges gave her the highest score of the night.","t":"體操選手在空中做了一個完美的空翻並雙腳落地，裁判給了她當晚的最高分。"},{"w":"flip a coin","p":"v.phr.","d":"to throw a coin in the air to decide something by chance","c":"擲硬幣決定","s":"We could not agree on which movie to watch, so we decided to flip a coin and let luck make the choice for us.","t":"我們無法決定要看哪部電影，所以決定擲硬幣，讓運氣替我們做選擇。"},{"w":"flip through","p":"v.phr.","d":"to turn the pages of a book or magazine quickly","c":"快速翻閱","s":"While waiting for the dentist, I began to flip through an old magazine and found a recipe that I wanted to try at home.","t":"等牙醫的時候，我開始快速翻閱一本舊雜誌，發現一道我想在家試做的食譜。"},{"w":"fluency","p":"n.","d":"the ability to speak or write a language easily and well","c":"流利；流暢","s":"After living in Canada for two years, her fluency in English improved so much that people thought she had grown up there.","t":"在加拿大住了兩年之後，她英語的流利程度大有進步，人們以為她是在那裡長大的。","h":1},{"w":"fluent","p":"adj.","d":"able to speak or write a language easily and well","c":"流利的","s":"My uncle is fluent in Japanese because he worked in Tokyo for ten years, and he still watches Japanese news every day.","t":"我叔叔的日語很流利，因為他在東京工作了十年，而且他現在每天還看日本新聞。"},{"w":"fluently","p":"adv.","d":"in an easy and smooth way","c":"流利地","s":"The tour guide spoke three languages fluently and switched between them without any trouble as she answered the visitors' questions.","t":"導遊能流利地說三種語言，在回答遊客問題時毫無困難地在它們之間切換。"},{"w":"fluid","p":"n.","d":"a liquid; a substance that can flow","c":"液體；流體","s":"When you have a fever, you should drink plenty of fluids such as water and soup, because your body loses water quickly.","t":"發燒時你應該喝大量的液體，像是水和湯，因為你的身體會快速流失水分。","a":"fluids","h":1},{"w":"fluid","p":"adj.","d":"able to flow like a liquid; smooth and graceful","c":"流動的；流暢的","s":"The dancer's movements were so fluid that she seemed to float across the stage like water running down a hill.","t":"舞者的動作如此流暢，她彷彿像從山坡流下的水一樣飄過舞台。"},{"w":"fluid","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change; not fixed","c":"不固定的；易變的","s":"Our travel plans are still fluid, so we might go to Japan in July or wait until the cooler weather in October.","t":"我們的旅行計畫還不確定，所以我們可能七月去日本，或者等到十月天氣涼一點再去。"},{"w":"forge","p":"v.","d":"to make an illegal copy of something, such as money or a signature","c":"偽造","s":"The student tried to forge his father's signature on the test paper, but the teacher noticed that the handwriting looked wrong.","t":"這個學生試圖在考卷上偽造父親的簽名，但老師注意到筆跡看起來不對。","h":1},{"w":"forge","p":"v.","d":"to build a strong relationship or agreement with effort","c":"建立；締結","s":"The two schools hope to forge a long-term partnership so that students can visit each other's country every summer.","t":"這兩所學校希望建立長期的夥伴關係，讓學生每年夏天可以互訪彼此的國家。"},{"w":"forgery","p":"n.","d":"an illegal copy of a document, painting, or signature; the crime of making one","c":"偽造品；偽造罪","s":"The painting sold for millions of dollars, but experts later proved it was a forgery made only thirty years ago.","t":"這幅畫以數百萬美元售出，但專家後來證明它是三十年前才製作的偽造品。"},{"w":"forge a friendship","p":"v.phr.","d":"to build a strong friendship over time","c":"建立友誼","s":"During the two-week camp, children from different countries managed to forge a friendship that lasted long after they went home.","t":"在兩週的營隊期間，來自不同國家的孩子建立了友誼，在他們回家後仍持續了很久。"},{"w":"format","p":"n.","d":"the way in which something is arranged or presented","c":"格式；形式；版式","s":"The teacher asked us to follow the same format for every report: a title, a short introduction, three main parts, and a conclusion.","t":"老師要求我們每份報告都遵循相同的格式：標題、簡短的引言、三個主要部分和結論。","h":1},{"w":"format","p":"v.","d":"to arrange text or data in a particular way on a computer","c":"排版；格式化","s":"Before you hand in your essay, please format it with double spacing and a twelve-point font so that it is easy to read.","t":"交作文之前，請把它排版成兩倍行距和十二級字型，這樣比較容易閱讀。"},{"w":"file format","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way information is stored in a computer file, such as PDF or JPG","c":"檔案格式","s":"The teacher could not open my homework because I saved it in the wrong file format, so I had to send it again as a PDF.","t":"老師打不開我的作業，因為我存成了錯誤的檔案格式，所以我必須再用 PDF 寄一次。"},{"w":"forum","p":"n.","d":"a meeting or place where people can discuss important matters","c":"論壇；討論會","s":"The city held a public forum last night so that residents could share their opinions about the plan for a new highway.","t":"市政府昨晚舉辦了一場公開論壇，讓居民分享他們對新公路計畫的意見。","h":1},{"w":"forum","p":"n.","d":"a website where people post messages and discuss topics","c":"網路論壇","s":"I found the answer to my computer problem on a technology forum, where a kind stranger had explained the fix step by step.","t":"我在一個科技論壇上找到了電腦問題的答案，一位善心的陌生人一步步解釋了解決方法。"},{"w":"online forum","p":"n.phr.","d":"an internet site for discussion","c":"線上論壇","s":"Many parents join an online forum to ask other families for advice about schools, after-school classes, and summer camps.","t":"許多家長加入線上論壇，向其他家庭詢問關於學校、課後班和夏令營的建議。"},{"w":"foster","p":"v.","d":"to encourage something to develop","c":"培養；促進","s":"Reading stories aloud to young children helps to foster a love of books that can last for the rest of their lives.","t":"大聲朗讀故事給幼兒聽有助於培養對書籍的熱愛，這種熱愛可以持續一輩子。","h":1},{"w":"foster","p":"adj.","d":"taking care of a child who is not your own without becoming the legal parent","c":"寄養的","s":"The kind couple have been foster parents to more than twenty children over the years, giving each one a safe and loving home.","t":"這對善良的夫妻多年來成為二十多個孩子的寄養父母，給每個孩子一個安全又充滿愛的家。"},{"w":"foster","p":"v.","d":"to take care of a child who is not your own for a period of time","c":"寄養；照顧","s":"My aunt decided to foster a six-year-old boy whose parents could not look after him, and now he calls her \"Mom.\"","t":"我阿姨決定寄養一個父母無法照顧他的六歲男孩，現在他叫她「媽媽」。"},{"w":"foster family","p":"n.phr.","d":"a family that takes care of a child who is not their own","c":"寄養家庭","s":"After the accident, the twins lived with a warm foster family in the countryside until their grandmother was able to take them in.","t":"意外之後，這對雙胞胎和鄉下一個溫暖的寄養家庭住在一起，直到他們的奶奶能夠接他們回去。"},{"w":"foul","p":"adj.","d":"very unpleasant to smell, taste, or experience","c":"惡臭的；骯髒的；惡劣的","s":"A foul smell came from the refrigerator because someone had forgotten a piece of fish inside for two whole weeks.","t":"冰箱裡傳來一股惡臭，因為有人把一塊魚忘在裡面整整兩個星期。","h":1},{"w":"foul","p":"n.","d":"an action in a sport that is against the rules","c":"犯規","s":"The referee called a foul on the tall player for pushing, so the other team got two free throws and won the game.","t":"裁判判那名高個子球員推人犯規，所以對方獲得兩次罰球並贏得了比賽。"},{"w":"foul","p":"v.","d":"to break the rules in a sport by touching or hitting another player","c":"對…犯規","s":"The defender tried to foul the striker just before he could shoot, and the whole stadium shouted in anger.","t":"後衛試圖在前鋒射門前對他犯規，整個體育場的人都憤怒地大喊。"},{"w":"foul language","p":"n.phr.","d":"rude and offensive words","c":"髒話；粗話","s":"Players who use foul language toward the referee will be sent off the field immediately, according to the new league rules.","t":"根據聯盟的新規定，對裁判說髒話的球員將立刻被罰下場。"},{"w":"foul play","p":"n.phr.","d":"a crime, especially one in which someone is killed; unfair action","c":"謀殺；不正當行為","s":"The police found no sign of foul play in the old man's death, and the doctor said he had simply died of a heart attack.","t":"警方在老人的死亡中沒有發現謀殺的跡象，醫生說他只是死於心臟病發作。"},{"w":"fraction","p":"n.","d":"a number such as 1/2 or 3/4 that is part of a whole number","c":"分數","s":"In today's math class, we learned how to add a fraction like one half to another like one third by finding a common bottom number.","t":"在今天的數學課上，我們學會了如何透過找公分母，把二分之一這樣的分數加上三分之一。","h":1},{"w":"fraction","p":"n.","d":"a very small part or amount of something","c":"一小部分；少量","s":"The second-hand bike cost only a fraction of the price of a new one, and it still works perfectly after two years.","t":"這台二手腳踏車的價格只有新車的一小部分，而且兩年後仍然運作良好。"},{"w":"a fraction of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very small part of something","c":"…的一小部分","s":"Online shops can sell goods for a fraction of the price in big stores because they do not have to pay rent for a building.","t":"網路商店能以大型商店價格的一小部分出售商品，因為它們不必為建築物支付租金。"},{"w":"fragment","p":"n.","d":"a small piece that has broken off something","c":"碎片；片段","s":"The scientists found a fragment of an old bowl in the cave, and they believe people cooked there over three thousand years ago.","t":"科學家在洞穴裡發現一個古老碗的碎片，他們認為三千多年前有人在那裡煮食。","h":1},{"w":"fragment","p":"v.","d":"to break into small pieces","c":"使碎裂；分裂","s":"Heavy traffic and new roads continue to fragment the forest, so wild animals find it harder and harder to move between areas.","t":"繁忙的交通和新道路持續把森林分割成碎塊，所以野生動物越來越難在各區域間移動。"},{"w":"fragmented","p":"adj.","d":"broken into many small and separate parts","c":"零碎的；分裂的","s":"After the long war, the country was so fragmented that each region had its own leader, its own army, and even its own money.","t":"經過漫長的戰爭後，這個國家四分五裂，每個地區都有自己的領袖、軍隊，甚至自己的貨幣。"},{"w":"framework","p":"n.","d":"a set of rules, ideas, or beliefs used to plan or decide something","c":"架構；框架","s":"The new framework for grading gives points for class participation, so students who speak up in class can earn higher scores.","t":"新的評分架構對課堂參與給分，所以在課堂上發言的學生可以得到更高的分數。","h":1},{"w":"framework","p":"n.","d":"the basic structure that supports a building or object","c":"骨架；構架","s":"Workers finished the steel framework of the new library in just three months, and now the walls and windows are being added.","t":"工人僅用三個月就完成了新圖書館的鋼鐵骨架，現在正在加上牆壁和窗戶。"},{"w":"frame","p":"n.","d":"a border of wood or metal around a picture, window, or door; the structure of something","c":"框架；邊框；骨架","s":"My grandfather put the old family photo in a wooden frame and hung it on the wall above the dining table.","t":"我爺爺把那張舊的全家福放進木框裡，掛在餐桌上方的牆上。"},{"w":"franchise","p":"n.","d":"the right given by a company to sell its products or use its name in a particular area","c":"特許經營權；加盟權","s":"My cousin bought a franchise from a famous coffee company, so his new shop uses the brand's name, menu, and uniforms.","t":"我表哥向一家知名咖啡公司購買了加盟權，所以他的新店使用該品牌的名稱、菜單和制服。","h":1},{"w":"fast-food franchise","p":"n.phr.","d":"a restaurant that is part of a large fast-food chain under a license","c":"速食連鎖加盟店","s":"Opening a fast-food franchise costs a lot of money at first, but the owner gets a well-known name and help with training the staff.","t":"開一家速食連鎖加盟店一開始要花很多錢，但店主能獲得知名品牌以及員工訓練的協助。"},{"w":"franchise","p":"n.","d":"the right to vote in elections","c":"選舉權；公民權","s":"Women in Taiwan have had the franchise since 1947, but in some countries they could not vote until many years later.","t":"台灣的女性自 1947 年起就擁有選舉權，但在某些國家，她們多年以後才能投票。"},{"w":"fraud","p":"n.","d":"the crime of tricking people to get money or something valuable","c":"詐欺；詐騙","s":"The police warned old people about phone fraud, in which callers pretend to be family members who urgently need money.","t":"警方提醒老年人注意電話詐騙，來電者假裝成急需用錢的家人。","h":1},{"w":"fraud","p":"n.","d":"a person who pretends to be someone or something they are not","c":"騙子；冒牌貨","s":"The man who said he was a doctor turned out to be a fraud who had never studied medicine for a single day.","t":"那個自稱是醫生的男人結果是個騙子，他連一天醫學都沒讀過。"},{"w":"fraudulent","p":"adj.","d":"done to trick people, especially to get money illegally","c":"詐欺的；欺騙的","s":"The bank closed the account after it found several fraudulent payments that the owner had never actually made.","t":"銀行在發現幾筆帳戶持有人從未真正支付的詐欺付款後，關閉了該帳戶。"},{"w":"commit fraud","p":"v.phr.","d":"to break the law by tricking people to get money","c":"犯詐欺罪","s":"The company manager was sent to prison for five years because he had tried to commit fraud by selling the same house to three different families.","t":"公司經理被判入獄五年，因為他把同一棟房子賣給三個不同的家庭，試圖犯詐欺罪。"},{"w":"freight","p":"n.","d":"goods that are carried by ship, train, truck, or plane","c":"貨物；貨運","s":"The port handles millions of tons of freight every year, including fruit from the south and machines from Japan.","t":"這座港口每年處理數百萬噸的貨物，包括南部的水果和來自日本的機器。","h":1},{"w":"freight","p":"v.","d":"to send goods by ship, train, truck, or plane","c":"運送（貨物）","s":"The factory will freight the new bicycles to Europe by sea, because shipping by plane would cost five times as much.","t":"工廠將透過海運把新腳踏車運送到歐洲，因為空運的費用是海運的五倍。"},{"w":"freight train","p":"n.phr.","d":"a train that carries goods, not passengers","c":"貨運列車","s":"We had to wait at the crossing for ten minutes while a long freight train with more than fifty cars slowly rolled past.","t":"我們不得不在平交道等了十分鐘，一列有五十多節車廂的長長貨運列車慢慢駛過。"},{"w":"air freight","p":"n.phr.","d":"goods sent by plane; the business of sending goods by plane","c":"空運貨物；空運","s":"Fresh flowers from Holland arrive in Taipei by air freight within two days, so they are still beautiful when they reach the shops.","t":"來自荷蘭的鮮花透過空運在兩天內抵達台北，所以送到花店時仍然很美。"},{"w":"frontier","p":"n.","d":"a border between two countries; the edge of land where people have settled","c":"邊境；邊疆","s":"In the old days, families who moved to the western frontier had to build their own houses and grow all their own food.","t":"在過去，搬到西部邊疆的家庭必須自己蓋房子，自己種植所有的食物。","h":1},{"w":"frontier","p":"n.","d":"the limit of what is known about a subject","c":"（知識的）前沿；尖端","s":"Scientists working at the frontier of medicine hope to find a way to grow new organs from a patient's own cells.","t":"在醫學前沿工作的科學家希望找到一種方法，用病人自己的細胞培養出新的器官。"},{"w":"the frontiers of science","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most advanced areas of scientific knowledge","c":"科學的前沿","s":"Young researchers who want to push the frontiers of science must be ready to fail many times before they finally succeed.","t":"想要推進科學前沿的年輕研究人員，必須準備好在最終成功之前失敗許多次。"}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"galaxy – hazard","cards":[{"w":"galaxy","p":"n.","d":"a very large group of stars and planets in space","c":"星系","s":"Scientists believe there are billions of stars in our galaxy, and most of them are too far away for us to see.","t":"科學家相信我們的星系裡有數十億顆星星，而其中大多數離我們太遠而看不見。","h":1},{"w":"galactic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a galaxy or galaxies","c":"星系的；銀河的","s":"The museum's new galactic show uses a huge round screen, so visitors feel as if they are flying through space.","t":"博物館新的銀河秀使用一個巨大的圓形螢幕，所以參觀者會覺得好像在太空中飛行。"},{"w":"the Milky Way","p":"n.phr.","d":"the galaxy that contains the Earth and the sun","c":"銀河（我們所在的星系）","s":"On a clear night in the mountains, you can see the Milky Way stretching across the sky like a river of light.","t":"在山上晴朗的夜晚，你可以看到銀河像一條光之河般橫跨天空。"},{"w":"gasp","p":"v.","d":"to breathe in quickly and loudly because you are surprised or need air","c":"喘氣；（因驚訝）屏息","s":"When the magician made the car disappear, the whole audience gasped in surprise and then started to clap loudly.","t":"當魔術師讓車子消失時，全場觀眾驚訝地屏息喘氣，然後開始大聲鼓掌。","a":"gasped","h":1},{"w":"gasp","p":"n.","d":"a quick, loud breath taken in surprise or pain","c":"喘氣聲；驚呼","s":"There was a gasp from the crowd when the player fell, but luckily he stood up a few seconds later.","t":"那位球員跌倒時人群中傳出一聲驚呼，但幸好幾秒後他就站了起來。"},{"w":"gasp for breath","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try hard to breathe because you have no air","c":"上氣不接下氣；喘不過氣","s":"After running up ten floors because the elevator was broken, I was gasping for breath and had to sit down.","t":"因為電梯壞了，我跑上十層樓後上氣不接下氣，不得不坐下來。","a":"gasping for breath"},{"w":"the last gasp","p":"n.phr.","d":"the final moment or effort before something ends","c":"最後一刻；最後掙扎","s":"The team scored the winning goal at the last gasp of the match, and their fans could hardly believe it.","t":"球隊在比賽最後一刻踢進致勝球，他們的球迷幾乎不敢相信。"},{"w":"gathering","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people for a special purpose","c":"聚會；集會","s":"Every Lunar New Year, our family has a big gathering at my grandparents' house, and more than thirty people come.","t":"每年農曆新年，我們家都在爺爺奶奶家舉辦一場大型聚會，有三十多人參加。","h":1},{"w":"gather","p":"v.","d":"to come together in a group; to collect things","c":"聚集；收集","s":"Hundreds of fans began to gather outside the stadium hours before the concert, even though it was raining.","t":"演唱會開始前幾小時，數百名粉絲就開始在體育場外聚集，儘管當時正在下雨。"},{"w":"gather information","p":"v.phr.","d":"to collect facts or details about something","c":"收集資訊","s":"Before you write the report, you should gather information from at least three different websites and compare what they say.","t":"在寫報告之前，你應該從至少三個不同的網站收集資訊，並比較它們的說法。"},{"w":"family gathering","p":"n.phr.","d":"an event where family members meet","c":"家庭聚會","s":"My cousin flew back from Japan just for the family gathering, because she did not want to miss Grandma's eightieth birthday.","t":"我表妹特地從日本飛回來參加家庭聚會，因為她不想錯過奶奶的八十歲生日。"},{"w":"generate","p":"v.","d":"to produce or create something, such as energy or ideas","c":"產生；製造","s":"The new wind farm on the coast can generate enough electricity for about fifty thousand homes every year.","t":"海岸上的新風力發電場每年可以產生足夠約五萬戶家庭使用的電力。","h":1},{"w":"generator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that produces electricity","c":"發電機","s":"When the typhoon cut off the power, the hospital turned on its generator so that the operating rooms could keep working.","t":"颱風造成停電時，醫院啟動了發電機，讓手術室能繼續運作。","h":1},{"w":"generation","p":"n.","d":"all the people born at about the same time; one stage in a family","c":"世代；一代","s":"My grandfather often says that the younger generation spends too much time on phones and too little time talking to people.","t":"我爺爺常說年輕世代花太多時間在手機上，和人說話的時間太少。"},{"w":"generate electricity","p":"v.phr.","d":"to produce electric power","c":"發電","s":"Taiwan uses solar panels and wind turbines to generate electricity, but it still depends heavily on imported natural gas.","t":"台灣利用太陽能板和風力渦輪機發電，但仍然嚴重依賴進口的天然氣。"},{"w":"regenerate","p":"v.","d":"to grow again or make something grow and become strong again","c":"再生；復興","s":"Some lizards can regenerate their tails after losing them, which is something scientists are still trying to understand.","t":"有些蜥蜴在失去尾巴後能再生尾巴，這是科學家仍在努力了解的現象。"},{"w":"genetic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with genes, which parents pass to their children","c":"遺傳的；基因的","s":"Doctors say the disease is partly genetic, so people whose parents had it should get checked more often.","t":"醫生說這種疾病有一部分是遺傳的，所以父母患有此病的人應該更常接受檢查。","h":1},{"w":"genetics","p":"n.","d":"the science of how living things pass features to their children","c":"遺傳學","s":"She is studying genetics at university because she wants to understand why some people get sick more easily than others.","t":"她在大學研讀遺傳學，因為她想了解為什麼有些人比其他人更容易生病。","h":1},{"w":"gene","p":"n.","d":"a part of a cell that controls what a living thing is like","c":"基因","s":"A single gene can decide whether a person has brown eyes or blue eyes, which is why eye color runs in families.","t":"單一個基因就能決定一個人是棕色還是藍色眼睛，這就是為什麼眼睛顏色會在家族中遺傳。"},{"w":"genetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with genes","c":"在基因上；遺傳上","s":"Many of the tomatoes sold in supermarkets have been genetically changed so that they stay fresh for a longer time.","t":"超市販售的許多番茄都經過基因改造，以便能保鮮更久。"},{"w":"genetic engineering","p":"n.phr.","d":"changing the genes of a living thing in a laboratory","c":"基因工程","s":"Some farmers support genetic engineering because it can create rice that grows well even in very dry weather.","t":"有些農民支持基因工程，因為它能創造出即使在非常乾燥的天氣也能長得好的稻米。"},{"w":"genre","p":"n.","d":"a type of art, music, film, or writing with its own style","c":"（文藝作品的）類型；體裁","s":"Science fiction is my favorite genre, so I have watched almost every space movie that came out this year.","t":"科幻是我最喜愛的類型，所以今年上映的太空電影我幾乎全都看過了。","h":1},{"w":"music genre","p":"n.phr.","d":"a style of music such as jazz, rock, or hip-hop","c":"音樂類型","s":"Jazz is a music genre that began in the United States, but today you can hear it in cafes all over Taipei.","t":"爵士是一種起源於美國的音樂類型，但今天你在台北各地的咖啡館都能聽到它。"},{"w":"literary genre","p":"n.phr.","d":"a type of writing such as poetry, novels, or drama","c":"文學體裁","s":"Poetry is the oldest literary genre in many cultures, and people were singing poems long before they could write them down.","t":"詩是許多文化中最古老的文學體裁，人們早在能把詩寫下來之前就在吟唱詩歌了。"},{"w":"glare","p":"v.","d":"to look at someone in an angry way","c":"怒視；瞪","s":"The librarian began to glare at the boys who were laughing loudly, so they quickly stopped and opened their books.","t":"圖書館員開始怒視那些大聲笑的男孩，所以他們很快停下來打開書。","h":1},{"w":"glare","p":"n.","d":"an angry look","c":"怒視；瞪眼","s":"My mother gave me a glare across the dinner table when I started to play with my phone in front of our guests.","t":"當我在客人面前開始玩手機時，媽媽隔著餐桌給了我一個怒視的眼神。"},{"w":"glare","p":"n.","d":"very strong, bright light that hurts your eyes","c":"強光；刺眼的光","s":"The glare of the sun on the wet road made it hard to see, so my father put on his sunglasses while driving.","t":"太陽照在濕路面上的強光讓人很難看清楚，所以我爸爸開車時戴上了太陽眼鏡。"},{"w":"glaring","p":"adj.","d":"very obvious and bad; too bright","c":"明顯的（錯誤）；刺眼的","s":"The report had several glaring mistakes on the first page, so the manager sent it back to be corrected.","t":"這份報告第一頁就有幾個明顯的錯誤，所以經理把它退回去修改。"},{"w":"glare at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stare angrily at someone","c":"怒視某人","s":"Instead of answering my question, my sister just glared at me and walked out of the room without a word.","t":"我姐姐沒有回答我的問題，只是怒視我，然後一句話也沒說就走出房間。","a":"glared at"},{"w":"gloomy","p":"adj.","d":"dark and sad; without hope","c":"陰暗的；憂鬱的；悲觀的","s":"The weather has been gloomy all week, and the gray skies make everyone in the office feel tired and quiet.","t":"這整個星期天氣都很陰沉，灰色的天空讓辦公室裡每個人都覺得疲倦又安靜。","h":1},{"w":"gloom","p":"n.","d":"darkness; a feeling of sadness and no hope","c":"黑暗；憂鬱","s":"After the team lost the final, a feeling of gloom filled the locker room, and nobody wanted to talk.","t":"球隊輸掉決賽後，一種憂鬱的氣氛籠罩著更衣室，沒有人想說話。"},{"w":"gloomily","p":"adv.","d":"in a sad way without hope","c":"憂鬱地；悲觀地","s":"\"We will never finish this project on time,\" he said gloomily, looking at the long list of tasks on the board.","t":"「我們永遠無法準時完成這個專案，」他看著白板上長長的工作清單憂鬱地說。"},{"w":"gorgeous","p":"adj.","d":"very beautiful or pleasant","c":"非常漂亮的；華麗的","s":"The view from the top of the mountain was gorgeous, and we could see the whole city and the ocean beyond it.","t":"山頂的景色美極了，我們可以看到整座城市和城市以外的海洋。","h":1},{"w":"gorgeously","p":"adv.","d":"in a very beautiful way","c":"華麗地；美麗地","s":"The old temple was gorgeously decorated with red lanterns and gold paper for the festival, and tourists stopped to take pictures.","t":"這座古廟為了節慶被紅燈籠和金紙華麗地裝飾著，遊客紛紛停下來拍照。"},{"w":"look gorgeous","p":"v.phr.","d":"to appear very beautiful","c":"看起來很美","s":"My sister looked gorgeous in her new blue dress at the wedding, and everyone kept asking her where she had bought it.","t":"我姐姐在婚禮上穿著新的藍色洋裝看起來美極了，大家一直問她是在哪裡買的。","a":"looked gorgeous"},{"w":"grant","p":"v.","d":"to give someone what they ask for, especially officially","c":"准予；授予","s":"The city government decided to grant the school permission to build a new swimming pool next to the playground.","t":"市政府決定准予學校在操場旁邊興建一座新游泳池。","h":1},{"w":"grant","p":"n.","d":"money given by the government or an organization for a special purpose","c":"補助金；獎學金","s":"The young scientist received a grant of two million dollars to continue her research on clean energy.","t":"這位年輕科學家獲得一筆兩百萬元的補助金，以繼續她在清潔能源方面的研究。"},{"w":"take ... for granted","p":"v.phr.","d":"to expect something to always be there without thinking about it","c":"視為理所當然","s":"Many of us take for granted clean water and electricity until a typhoon cuts them off for a few days.","t":"我們許多人把乾淨的水和電力視為理所當然，直到颱風讓它們中斷幾天為止。","a":"take for granted"},{"w":"granted","p":"adv.","d":"used to admit that something is true before saying something else","c":"的確；誠然","s":"Granted, the restaurant is a little expensive, but the food is excellent and the service is always friendly.","t":"的確，這家餐廳有點貴，但食物很棒，服務也總是很親切。","a":"Granted"},{"w":"grant permission","p":"v.phr.","d":"to officially allow someone to do something","c":"准許；給予許可","s":"The principal finally granted permission for the students to hold a music festival in the school hall next month.","t":"校長終於准許學生下個月在學校禮堂舉辦音樂節。","a":"granted permission"},{"w":"graphic","p":"adj.","d":"very clear and full of details, especially about something unpleasant","c":"生動的；寫實的；圖像的","s":"The news report gave a graphic description of the accident, so some viewers turned off their televisions.","t":"新聞報導對這場事故做了生動寫實的描述，所以有些觀眾關掉了電視。","h":1},{"w":"graphic","p":"n.","d":"a picture, drawing, or image, especially on a computer","c":"圖像；圖形","s":"The designer added a colorful graphic to the poster, which made the information much easier to understand.","t":"設計師在海報上加了一個色彩豐富的圖像，讓資訊變得更容易理解。"},{"w":"graph","p":"n.","d":"a drawing that uses lines or bars to show numbers","c":"圖表；曲線圖","s":"The graph on the screen clearly showed that the number of visitors doubled after the museum opened on weekends.","t":"螢幕上的圖表清楚顯示，博物館週末開放後，參觀人數翻了一倍。"},{"w":"graphically","p":"adv.","d":"in a very clear and detailed way; by using pictures","c":"生動地；用圖表地","s":"The teacher graphically explained how plastic waste travels from our rivers to the ocean by showing a series of photos.","t":"老師透過一系列照片生動地說明塑膠垃圾如何從我們的河流流入海洋。"},{"w":"graphic design","p":"n.phr.","d":"the art of combining pictures and words for posters, websites, and so on","c":"平面設計","s":"After high school, my brother wants to study graphic design because he loves making posters and logos on his computer.","t":"高中畢業後，我哥哥想念平面設計，因為他喜歡在電腦上製作海報和標誌。"},{"w":"gravity","p":"n.","d":"the force that pulls things toward the earth","c":"重力；引力","s":"Because of gravity, an apple always falls down from the tree instead of floating up into the sky.","t":"由於重力，蘋果總是從樹上掉下來，而不是往天上飄。","h":1},{"w":"gravity","p":"n.","d":"the serious or dangerous nature of a situation","c":"嚴重性","s":"The students did not understand the gravity of the situation until the teacher told them the school might close.","t":"直到老師告訴學生學校可能會關閉，他們才了解情況的嚴重性。"},{"w":"gravitational","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the force of gravity","c":"重力的；引力的","s":"The moon's gravitational pull causes the ocean tides, which is why the sea level rises and falls twice a day.","t":"月球的引力造成海洋潮汐，這就是為什麼海平面每天漲落兩次。"},{"w":"grave","p":"adj.","d":"very serious and worrying","c":"嚴重的；嚴肅的","s":"The doctor had a grave look on his face when he came out, so we knew the news would not be good.","t":"醫生出來時臉上帶著嚴肅的表情，所以我們知道消息不會是好的。"},{"w":"gravely","p":"adv.","d":"in a very serious way","c":"嚴重地；嚴肅地","s":"The firefighter was gravely injured while saving a child, and he spent nearly three months in the hospital.","t":"那位消防員在救一個孩子時嚴重受傷，在醫院待了將近三個月。"},{"w":"greed","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish for more money, food, or power than you need","c":"貪婪；貪心","s":"The company's greed for profit led it to sell unsafe products, and in the end it lost all of its customers.","t":"這家公司對利潤的貪婪導致它銷售不安全的產品，最後失去了所有客戶。","h":1},{"w":"greedy","p":"adj.","d":"wanting more than you need","c":"貪心的","s":"Don't be so greedy and take all the cookies; leave some for your little brother, who has not had any yet.","t":"別那麼貪心把餅乾全拿走；留一些給還沒吃到的弟弟。"},{"w":"greedily","p":"adv.","d":"in a greedy way","c":"貪心地","s":"The hungry puppy ate greedily from the bowl, and it finished all of the food in less than one minute.","t":"飢餓的小狗貪心地吃著碗裡的食物，不到一分鐘就全部吃完了。"},{"w":"grieve","p":"v.","d":"to feel very sad because someone has died or something is lost","c":"悲傷；哀悼","s":"It is natural to grieve for a long time after losing a pet, because animals become part of the family.","t":"失去寵物後長時間悲傷是很自然的，因為動物已成為家庭的一部分。","h":1},{"w":"grief","p":"n.","d":"great sadness, especially after someone dies","c":"悲痛；悲傷","s":"Her grief was so deep after her grandfather passed away that she could not go to school for a week.","t":"爺爺過世後，她的悲痛如此深沉，以致她一個星期都無法上學。"},{"w":"grieve for / over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel deep sadness about a person or a loss","c":"為…悲傷","s":"The whole town grieved for the young firefighter, and hundreds of people brought flowers to the station.","t":"全鎮的人都為那位年輕的消防員哀悼，數百人帶著鮮花到消防局。","a":"grieved for"},{"w":"grievance","p":"n.","d":"a complaint about being treated unfairly","c":"不滿；委屈；申訴","s":"The workers wrote down their main grievance, which was that they had not received a pay raise in five years.","t":"工人們寫下他們主要的不滿，也就是他們五年來沒有加過薪。"},{"w":"grief-stricken","p":"adj.","d":"extremely sad because of a loss","c":"悲痛欲絕的","s":"The grief-stricken mother could not speak to the reporters, so her brother answered the questions for her.","t":"那位悲痛欲絕的母親無法對記者說話，所以她的弟弟替她回答問題。"},{"w":"grill","p":"v.","d":"to cook food on metal bars over a fire or under strong heat","c":"燒烤；烤","s":"On Moon Festival night, we grill corn, chicken, and vegetables in the backyard while watching the full moon.","t":"中秋節晚上，我們在後院燒烤玉米、雞肉和蔬菜，一邊欣賞滿月。","h":1},{"w":"grill","p":"n.","d":"a metal frame or machine for cooking food over heat","c":"烤架；燒烤爐","s":"My father bought a new grill for the balcony, and now he cooks outside almost every weekend in summer.","t":"我爸爸為陽台買了一個新烤架，現在夏天幾乎每個週末他都在外面煮飯。"},{"w":"grilled","p":"adj.","d":"cooked on a grill","c":"烤的；燒烤的","s":"I ordered grilled fish with lemon instead of fried chicken, because I am trying to eat healthier this month.","t":"我點了烤檸檬魚而不是炸雞，因為這個月我努力吃得更健康。"},{"w":"grill","p":"v.","d":"to ask someone many difficult questions for a long time","c":"盤問；追問","s":"The police officers began to grill the suspect about where he had been on the night of the robbery.","t":"警察開始盤問嫌犯在搶案當晚去了哪裡。"},{"w":"grim","p":"adj.","d":"very serious, unpleasant, or without hope","c":"嚴峻的；陰森的；令人沮喪的","s":"The doctor's grim expression told us the test results were bad even before she said a single word.","t":"醫生嚴肅凝重的表情在她說出任何一個字之前，就告訴我們檢查結果不好。","h":1},{"w":"grimly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very serious way without any hope or humor","c":"嚴峻地；堅定而冷酷地","s":"The captain grimly announced that the ship would not reach the port before the storm hit that evening.","t":"船長嚴峻地宣布，船無法在當晚暴風雨來襲前抵達港口。"},{"w":"look grim","p":"v.phr.","d":"to seem very bad or serious","c":"情況看起來很糟","s":"Things looked grim for the small bookstore when a huge shopping mall opened across the street last year.","t":"去年對街開了一間大型購物中心後，這家小書店的情況看起來很糟。","a":"looked grim"},{"w":"grip","p":"v.","d":"to hold something very tightly","c":"緊握；抓緊","s":"She had to grip the handle tightly as the roller coaster rushed down the track at full speed.","t":"雲霄飛車全速衝下軌道時，她不得不緊握把手。","h":1},{"w":"grip","p":"n.","d":"a tight hold on something","c":"緊握；抓力","s":"The climber kept a firm grip on the rope and slowly pulled himself up toward the top of the cliff.","t":"攀登者緊緊抓住繩索，慢慢把自己拉向懸崖頂端。"},{"w":"lose one's grip","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop holding something tightly; to lose control","c":"鬆手；失去控制","s":"The boy lost his grip on the balloon string, and the red balloon floated high above the night market.","t":"男孩鬆開了抓著氣球線的手，紅色氣球飄到夜市上空。","a":"lost his grip"},{"w":"gripping","p":"adj.","d":"so exciting that it holds your attention completely","c":"扣人心弦的；引人入勝的","s":"The movie was so gripping that nobody in the theater checked their phone for the whole two hours.","t":"這部電影太扣人心弦了，整整兩小時電影院裡沒有人看手機。"},{"w":"get a grip","p":"phr.","d":"to control your feelings and act calmly","c":"冷靜下來；控制自己","s":"\"Get a grip on yourself and stop crying,\" the coach said gently; \"you still have two more races to run today.\"","t":"「冷靜下來，別哭了，」教練溫和地說，「你今天還有兩場比賽要跑。」","a":"Get a grip"},{"w":"gross","p":"adj.","d":"total, before anything such as tax is taken away","c":"總的；毛的（未扣除的）","s":"His gross salary is sixty thousand dollars a month, but after tax and insurance he takes home much less.","t":"他的總薪資是每月六萬元，但扣除稅和保險後，實際拿到的少得多。","h":1},{"w":"gross","p":"adj.","d":"very unpleasant; disgusting","c":"令人作噁的；噁心的","s":"The milk had been left out of the fridge for three days, and it smelled so gross that I almost threw up.","t":"牛奶在冰箱外放了三天，味道噁心到我差點吐出來。"},{"w":"gross","p":"v.","d":"to earn a total amount of money before costs are taken away","c":"總收入為；賺得（毛收入）","s":"The new superhero movie grossed over one billion dollars worldwide in just its first two weeks in theaters.","t":"這部新的超級英雄電影在上映短短兩週內，全球總票房達十億美元以上。","a":"grossed"},{"w":"gross income","p":"n.phr.","d":"the total amount of money earned before tax","c":"總收入；稅前收入","s":"To apply for the loan, you need to show the bank your gross income for the past two years.","t":"要申請貸款，你需要向銀行出示過去兩年的稅前總收入。"},{"w":"grossly","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; in a way that is very wrong or unfair","c":"極度地；嚴重地","s":"The old building was grossly overcrowded, with more than twenty people living in rooms meant for six.","t":"那棟舊建築嚴重超載，原本供六人居住的房間住了二十多人。"},{"w":"guideline","p":"n.","d":"an official rule or advice on how to do something","c":"指導方針；準則","s":"The school has a new guideline on phone use, which says students must keep their phones in their bags during class.","t":"學校有一條關於手機使用的新準則，規定學生上課時必須把手機放在書包裡。","h":1},{"w":"guide","p":"v.","d":"to show someone the way or help them do something","c":"引導；指導","s":"A local volunteer offered to guide us through the old town, and she told us stories about every temple we passed.","t":"一位當地志工主動帶領我們遊覽老城區，並為我們講述經過的每座廟宇的故事。"},{"w":"guidance","p":"n.","d":"help and advice about what to do","c":"指導；輔導","s":"With the careful guidance of her teacher, Lily improved her writing so much that she won the city essay contest.","t":"在老師細心的指導下，莉莉的寫作進步很多，贏得了市作文比賽。"},{"w":"follow the guidelines","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do what the official rules or advice say","c":"遵守準則","s":"If every restaurant followed the guidelines on food safety, there would be far fewer cases of food poisoning each summer.","t":"如果每家餐廳都遵守食品安全準則，每年夏天食物中毒的案例就會少得多。","a":"followed the guidelines"},{"w":"gut","p":"n.","d":"the tube inside the body that food passes through; the stomach area","c":"腸道；腸子","s":"Eating more vegetables and yogurt is good for your gut, and doctors say a healthy stomach helps you feel happier.","t":"多吃蔬菜和優格對你的腸道有益，醫生說健康的腸胃能讓你感覺更快樂。","h":1},{"w":"guts","p":"n.","d":"courage to do something difficult","c":"勇氣；膽量","s":"It took a lot of guts for the shy student to stand up and sing in front of the whole school.","t":"那位害羞的學生需要很大的勇氣才能站起來在全校面前唱歌。"},{"w":"gut","p":"v.","d":"to destroy the inside of a building; to remove the inside of a fish","c":"燒毀（內部）；去除內臟","s":"Experts warned that a fire could gut the old wooden factory within an hour, so the owner installed new alarms last week.","t":"專家警告火災可能在一小時內燒毀這座舊木造工廠的內部，所以老闆上週安裝了新的警報器。"},{"w":"gut feeling","p":"n.phr.","d":"a strong feeling about something that you cannot explain","c":"直覺","s":"I had a gut feeling that the man was lying, so I did not give him my phone number or address.","t":"我有一種直覺覺得那個男人在說謊，所以我沒有給他我的電話號碼或地址。"},{"w":"have the guts to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be brave enough to do something","c":"有勇氣做…","s":"Nobody in the class had the guts to tell the teacher that she had written the wrong date on the board.","t":"班上沒有人有勇氣告訴老師她在黑板上寫錯了日期。","a":"had the guts to"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural place where an animal or plant lives","c":"（動植物的）棲息地","s":"When people cut down the forest, many birds lost their habitat and had to fly far away to find new homes.","t":"人們砍伐森林時，許多鳥類失去了棲息地，必須飛到很遠的地方尋找新家。","h":1},{"w":"natural habitat","p":"n.phr.","d":"the wild place where an animal normally lives","c":"自然棲息地","s":"It is much better to watch elephants in their natural habitat than to see them standing sadly inside a small cage.","t":"在自然棲息地觀看大象，比看它們悲傷地站在小籠子裡好得多。"},{"w":"inhabit","p":"v.","d":"to live in a place","c":"居住於；棲息於","s":"Only a few hundred people inhabit the small island, and most of them make a living by fishing.","t":"只有幾百人居住在這座小島上，其中大多數靠捕魚為生。"},{"w":"inhabitant","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal that lives in a place","c":"居民；棲息動物","s":"The oldest inhabitant of the village is ninety-eight years old, and she still remembers when there was no electricity.","t":"這個村子最年長的居民九十八歲，她還記得沒有電的時代。"},{"w":"habitable","p":"adj.","d":"good enough for people to live in","c":"可居住的","s":"After the flood, the ground floor of the house was no longer habitable, so the family moved upstairs for two months.","t":"水災過後，房子的一樓不再適合居住，所以這家人搬到樓上住了兩個月。"},{"w":"haul","p":"v.","d":"to pull or carry something heavy with great effort","c":"拖；拉；運送","s":"The fishermen had to haul the heavy net onto the boat by hand because the machine had stopped working.","t":"因為機器停止運作，漁民們不得不用手把沉重的漁網拖上船。","h":1},{"w":"haul","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of something that has been collected or stolen","c":"（一次捕獲或偷得的）大量東西","s":"The police found a huge haul of stolen phones in the back of the truck, worth more than three million dollars.","t":"警方在卡車後面發現大量被偷的手機，價值超過三百萬元。"},{"w":"long-haul","p":"adj.","d":"traveling a long distance, especially by plane","c":"長途的（飛行）","s":"On long-haul flights to Europe, I always bring a neck pillow and a good book because I cannot sleep on planes.","t":"搭乘飛往歐洲的長途航班時，我總是帶著頸枕和一本好書，因為我在飛機上睡不著。"},{"w":"haul away","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take something away, usually with a vehicle","c":"運走；拖走","s":"After the typhoon, trucks came every morning to haul away the broken trees and signs that had fallen on the roads.","t":"颱風過後，卡車每天早上都來運走掉落在路上的斷樹和招牌。"},{"w":"hazard","p":"n.","d":"something that can be dangerous or cause harm","c":"危險；危害物","s":"The loose wires on the floor are a serious hazard, and someone could trip over them or get an electric shock.","t":"地板上鬆散的電線是嚴重的危險，有人可能會被絆倒或觸電。","h":1},{"w":"hazardous","p":"adj.","d":"dangerous, especially to health or safety","c":"有危險的；有害的","s":"Workers who handle hazardous chemicals must wear gloves and masks, and they are checked by a doctor every six months.","t":"處理有害化學物質的工人必須戴手套和口罩，而且每六個月要接受醫生檢查。"},{"w":"hazard a guess","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a guess even though you are not sure","c":"冒昧猜測；大膽猜猜","s":"I don't know how much the house costs, but if I had to hazard a guess, I would say about twenty million dollars.","t":"我不知道這房子多少錢，但如果要我大膽猜一下，我會說大約兩千萬元。"},{"w":"fire hazard","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that could easily start a fire","c":"火災隱患","s":"Piles of old newspapers next to the stove are a fire hazard, so please move them to the recycling bin outside.","t":"爐子旁邊成堆的舊報紙是一種火災隱患，所以請把它們搬到外面的回收桶。"},{"w":"health hazard","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that can damage people's health","c":"健康危害","s":"Air pollution in big cities has become a major health hazard, especially for children and elderly people with weak lungs.","t":"大城市的空氣污染已成為主要的健康危害，尤其對肺部較弱的兒童和老人而言。"}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"heir – incentive","cards":[{"w":"heir","p":"n.","d":"a person who will receive money, property, or a title when someone dies","c":"繼承人","s":"The old man had no children, so his nephew became the only heir to his house and his large farm.","t":"老先生沒有孩子，所以他的姪子成了他房子和大農場唯一的繼承人。","h":1},{"w":"heiress","p":"n.","d":"a woman who will receive a lot of money or property","c":"女繼承人","s":"The young heiress surprised everyone by giving most of her family's money to schools in poor villages.","t":"這位年輕的女繼承人把家族大部分的錢捐給貧窮村莊的學校，讓所有人都很驚訝。"},{"w":"inherit","p":"v.","d":"to receive money, property, or a feature from someone after they die","c":"繼承；遺傳到","s":"When my grandmother passed away, my mother inherited her small apartment and the gold ring she always wore.","t":"我奶奶過世時，我媽媽繼承了她的小公寓和她一直戴著的金戒指。","a":"inherited"},{"w":"inheritance","p":"n.","d":"money or property that you receive from someone who has died","c":"遺產；繼承物","s":"He used part of his inheritance to open a bakery, which had been his dream since he was a teenager.","t":"他用一部分遺產開了一家麵包店，那是他從青少年時期就有的夢想。"},{"w":"heir to the throne","p":"n.phr.","d":"the person who will become the next king or queen","c":"王位繼承人","s":"The prince became heir to the throne when he was born, and he was trained for the job from a very young age.","t":"王子一出生就成為王位繼承人，從很小就接受這項職責的訓練。"},{"w":"hence","p":"adv.","d":"for this reason; therefore","c":"因此；所以","s":"The road to the village was washed away by the flood; hence, the school had to close for three days.","t":"通往村莊的道路被洪水沖毀了；因此，學校不得不停課三天。","h":1},{"w":"henceforth","p":"adv.","d":"from this time on","c":"從今以後","s":"The principal announced that henceforth all students must turn off their phones before entering the classroom.","t":"校長宣布從今以後所有學生進教室前都必須關掉手機。"},{"w":"hence the name","p":"phr.","d":"and that is the reason for its name","c":"因此得名","s":"The small town is surrounded by hills covered with orange trees, hence the name \"Orange Valley\" on the map.","t":"這個小鎮四周環繞著種滿橘子樹的山丘，因此在地圖上得名「橘子谷」。"},{"w":"herb","p":"n.","d":"a plant whose leaves are used in cooking or as medicine","c":"香草；草藥","s":"My grandmother grows every herb she needs on her balcony, so her soup always smells fresh and green.","t":"我奶奶在陽台上種她需要的每一種香草，所以她的湯總是聞起來新鮮又清香。","h":1},{"w":"herbal","p":"adj.","d":"made from herbs","c":"草本的；草藥的","s":"When I have a cold, my mother makes me a cup of hot herbal tea with ginger and honey before bed.","t":"我感冒時，媽媽會在睡前幫我泡一杯加了薑和蜂蜜的熱草本茶。"},{"w":"herbal tea","p":"n.phr.","d":"a drink made by putting herbs in hot water","c":"花草茶；草本茶","s":"Many cafes in Taipei now serve herbal tea instead of coffee at night, because it helps customers sleep better.","t":"台北許多咖啡館現在晚上供應花草茶而不是咖啡，因為它能幫助顧客睡得更好。"},{"w":"fresh herbs","p":"n.phr.","d":"herbs that have just been picked and not dried","c":"新鮮香草","s":"The chef adds fresh herbs from the garden to every dish, which is why his pasta tastes so different from others.","t":"主廚在每道菜裡加入花園裡的新鮮香草，這就是他的義大利麵和別人的味道如此不同的原因。"},{"w":"heritage","p":"n.","d":"the traditions, buildings, and culture passed down from the past","c":"遺產；傳統；文化資產","s":"The old temple is an important part of our city's heritage, so the government spent millions to repair it.","t":"這座古廟是我們城市文化資產的重要部分，所以政府花了數百萬元修復它。","h":1},{"w":"cultural heritage","p":"n.phr.","d":"the art, customs, and traditions of a country or group","c":"文化遺產","s":"Learning traditional songs and dances helps young people understand the cultural heritage of their grandparents.","t":"學習傳統歌曲和舞蹈，能幫助年輕人了解祖父母那一代的文化遺產。"},{"w":"World Heritage site","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place protected by UNESCO because it is important to all people","c":"世界遺產","s":"Every year, millions of tourists visit the Great Wall, which became a World Heritage site in 1987 because of its history.","t":"每年有數百萬遊客參觀長城，它因其歷史於1987年成為世界遺產。"},{"w":"highlight","p":"v.","d":"to make people notice something important","c":"強調；突顯","s":"The news report tried to highlight the problem of plastic waste by showing photos of dead sea turtles.","t":"這則新聞報導透過展示死亡海龜的照片，試圖突顯塑膠垃圾的問題。","h":1},{"w":"highlight","p":"n.","d":"the best or most exciting part of something","c":"最精彩的部分","s":"The highlight of our trip to Japan was the night we watched fireworks over the river in Osaka.","t":"我們日本之旅最精彩的部分是在大阪看河上煙火的那個晚上。"},{"w":"highlighter","p":"n.","d":"a bright pen used to mark important words","c":"螢光筆","s":"Before the test, I used a yellow highlighter to mark the key words in my notes so I could review them quickly.","t":"考試前，我用黃色螢光筆標出筆記裡的關鍵字，以便快速複習。"},{"w":"the highlight of","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most enjoyable or important part of","c":"…的亮點；…最精彩的部分","s":"Meeting my favorite singer backstage was the highlight of the whole year, and I still cannot believe it happened.","t":"在後台見到我最喜歡的歌手是這一整年最精彩的部分，我到現在還是不敢相信這真的發生了。"},{"w":"hockey","p":"n.","d":"a game played on ice or grass in which players hit a small object with long sticks","c":"曲棍球","s":"My cousin in Canada plays hockey every winter, and his team practices on a frozen lake near his house.","t":"我在加拿大的表哥每年冬天都打曲棍球，他的球隊在他家附近一座結冰的湖上練習。","h":1},{"w":"ice hockey","p":"n.phr.","d":"hockey played on ice by players wearing skates","c":"冰上曲棍球","s":"Ice hockey is the most popular sport in Canada, and even small children learn to skate so they can play it.","t":"冰上曲棍球是加拿大最受歡迎的運動，連小孩子都學溜冰，好能參加比賽。","a":"Ice hockey"},{"w":"field hockey","p":"n.phr.","d":"hockey played on grass with a small hard ball","c":"草地曲棍球","s":"Our school started a field hockey team last year, and the girls already won second place in the city competition.","t":"我們學校去年成立了草地曲棍球隊，女生們已經在市賽中拿下第二名。"},{"w":"hockey stick","p":"n.phr.","d":"the long stick used to hit the ball or puck in hockey","c":"曲棍球桿","s":"He saved his pocket money for six months to buy a new hockey stick signed by his favorite player.","t":"他存了六個月的零用錢，買了一支有他最喜歡的球員簽名的新曲棍球桿。"},{"w":"honorable","p":"adj.","d":"deserving respect because of good and fair behavior","c":"光榮的；可敬的；正直的","s":"Returning the lost wallet with all the money inside was an honorable thing to do, and the owner thanked him warmly.","t":"把裝著所有錢的遺失錢包歸還是一件正直可敬的行為，失主熱情地向他道謝。","h":1},{"w":"honor","p":"n.","d":"great respect; something that makes you feel proud","c":"榮譽；光榮","s":"It was a great honor for our small school to be chosen to sing at the national ceremony in Taipei.","t":"我們這所小學校被選中在台北的全國典禮上演唱，這是一項極大的榮譽。"},{"w":"honor","p":"v.","d":"to show great respect for someone, often at a public event","c":"向…致敬；給予榮譽","s":"The city will honor the brave firefighters with a special parade on Saturday morning along the main street.","t":"市政府將在星期六早上於主街舉行一場特別遊行，向勇敢的消防員致敬。"},{"w":"honorary","p":"adj.","d":"given as an honor, without the usual duties or requirements","c":"名譽的；榮譽的","s":"The university gave the famous writer an honorary degree, even though she had never finished high school.","t":"這所大學授予這位著名作家名譽學位，儘管她從未讀完高中。"},{"w":"in honor of","p":"phr.","d":"in order to show respect for someone or something","c":"為了向…致敬；為了紀念","s":"The new library was named in honor of the teacher who had worked at the school for forty years.","t":"新圖書館以那位在學校服務四十年的老師命名，以表敬意。"},{"w":"horizontal","p":"adj.","d":"flat and level; going from side to side, not up and down","c":"水平的；橫的","s":"Draw a horizontal line across the middle of the page, and then write the dates above it and the events below it.","t":"在頁面中間畫一條水平線，然後在線上方寫日期，在線下方寫事件。","h":1},{"w":"horizontally","p":"adv.","d":"in a flat, level way from side to side","c":"水平地；橫向地","s":"If you hold the phone horizontally, the video will fill the whole screen and look much better.","t":"如果你橫向拿著手機，影片會填滿整個螢幕，看起來好很多。"},{"w":"horizon","p":"n.","d":"the line where the sky seems to meet the land or sea","c":"地平線；水平線","s":"We sat on the beach and watched the sun slowly sink below the horizon until the sky turned purple.","t":"我們坐在海灘上，看著太陽慢慢沉到地平線下，直到天空變成紫色。"},{"w":"on the horizon","p":"phr.","d":"likely to happen soon","c":"即將來臨；在望","s":"With the exams finally over and summer vacation on the horizon, the students could hardly sit still in class.","t":"考試終於結束，暑假即將來臨，學生們在課堂上幾乎坐不住。"},{"w":"hormone","p":"n.","d":"a chemical made in the body that controls how it grows and works","c":"荷爾蒙；激素","s":"Doctors explained that a hormone problem was the reason the boy was much shorter than his classmates.","t":"醫生解釋說，荷爾蒙問題是這個男孩比同學矮很多的原因。","h":1},{"w":"hormonal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with hormones","c":"荷爾蒙的；激素的","s":"Teenagers often feel moody because of hormonal changes, so parents should try to be patient with them.","t":"青少年常因荷爾蒙變化而情緒不穩，所以父母應該試著對他們有耐心。"},{"w":"growth hormone","p":"n.phr.","d":"a hormone that makes the body grow","c":"生長激素","s":"Children produce the most growth hormone while they sleep, which is why doctors say they need nine hours of rest.","t":"兒童在睡眠時分泌最多的生長激素，這就是為什麼醫生說他們需要九小時的休息。"},{"w":"hostage","p":"n.","d":"a person kept as a prisoner until certain demands are met","c":"人質","s":"The bank robbers held a hostage for six hours before the police finally talked them into giving up.","t":"銀行搶匪挾持一名人質六個小時，警方最後才說服他們投降。","h":1},{"w":"take sb hostage","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone a prisoner in order to get what you want","c":"挾持某人為人質","s":"The movie is about a pilot whose plane is taken hostage by two men who want to fly to another country.","t":"這部電影講的是一位飛行員，他的飛機被兩個想飛往別國的男子挾持。","a":"taken hostage"},{"w":"hold sb hostage","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep someone as a prisoner until your demands are met","c":"扣押某人為人質","s":"The gunman held three people hostage inside the shop, but luckily nobody was hurt when the police rushed in.","t":"持槍歹徒在店裡挾持三人為人質，但幸運的是，警方衝進去時沒有人受傷。","a":"held three people hostage"},{"w":"hostile","p":"adj.","d":"unfriendly and showing that you are against someone","c":"有敵意的；不友善的","s":"The new student felt that his classmates were hostile at first, but within a month they became good friends.","t":"新同學起初覺得班上同學不友善，但一個月內他們就成了好朋友。","h":1},{"w":"hostility","p":"n.","d":"unfriendly or angry feelings or behavior","c":"敵意；敵對","s":"There was clear hostility between the two teams, and the referee had to stop the game twice to calm the players down.","t":"兩隊之間有明顯的敵意，裁判不得不兩次暫停比賽讓球員冷靜下來。","h":1},{"w":"hostile to / toward","p":"adj.phr.","d":"strongly against something or someone","c":"對…懷有敵意；反對…","s":"Many shop owners were hostile to the plan to close the street to cars, because they worried about losing customers.","t":"許多店主反對禁止汽車進入這條街的計畫，因為他們擔心會失去顧客。","a":"hostile to"},{"w":"hostilities","p":"n.","d":"fighting in a war","c":"戰爭行為；敵對行動","s":"After three years of war, the two countries finally agreed to end hostilities and start peace talks in Geneva.","t":"經過三年的戰爭，兩國終於同意結束敵對行動，並在日內瓦展開和平談判。"},{"w":"housing","p":"n.","d":"houses and apartments for people to live in","c":"住房；住宅","s":"The city needs more cheap housing for young workers, because many of them cannot afford to rent an apartment downtown.","t":"這座城市需要更多便宜的住宅給年輕的上班族，因為他們很多人付不起市中心的公寓租金。","h":1},{"w":"house","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a place to live; to keep something in a place","c":"為…提供住處；收藏","s":"After the earthquake, the school gym was used to house more than two hundred families who had lost their homes.","t":"地震過後，學校體育館被用來安置兩百多個失去家園的家庭。"},{"w":"household","p":"n.","d":"all the people who live together in one house","c":"家庭；一戶","s":"Nearly every household in Taiwan now has at least one smartphone, and many families have more than three.","t":"台灣現在幾乎每個家庭至少有一支智慧型手機，許多家庭有超過三支。"},{"w":"public housing","p":"n.phr.","d":"housing built by the government for people with low incomes","c":"公共住宅；社會住宅","s":"The government plans to build twenty thousand units of public housing near MRT stations over the next five years.","t":"政府計畫在未來五年內於捷運站附近興建兩萬戶社會住宅。"},{"w":"housing prices","p":"n.phr.","d":"the cost of buying a house or apartment","c":"房價","s":"Housing prices in Taipei have risen so fast that many young couples have decided to buy homes in Taoyuan instead.","t":"台北的房價漲得太快，許多年輕夫妻決定改在桃園買房。","a":"Housing prices"},{"w":"howl","p":"v.","d":"to make a long, loud, sad sound, like a dog or wolf; to cry loudly","c":"嗥叫；哀號；大叫","s":"Our neighbor's dog began to howl at midnight, and it did not stop until its owner came home an hour later.","t":"鄰居的狗半夜開始嗥叫，直到一小時後主人回家才停止。","h":1},{"w":"howl","p":"n.","d":"a long, loud crying sound","c":"嗥叫聲；哀號聲","s":"We heard a strange howl from the forest during the camping trip, and nobody wanted to leave the tent.","t":"露營時我們聽到森林裡傳來奇怪的嗥叫聲，沒有人想離開帳篷。"},{"w":"howl with laughter","p":"v.phr.","d":"to laugh very loudly","c":"放聲大笑","s":"The comedian's jokes were so funny that the whole audience howled with laughter for the entire ninety-minute show.","t":"那位喜劇演員的笑話太好笑了，全場觀眾在整整九十分鐘的表演裡放聲大笑。","a":"howled with laughter"},{"w":"howling","p":"adj.","d":"(of wind) blowing hard with a loud noise","c":"呼嘯的（風）","s":"A howling wind shook the windows all night, and in the morning we found several trees lying across the road.","t":"呼嘯的風整夜搖動窗戶，早上我們發現好幾棵樹橫倒在路上。"},{"w":"hypothesis","p":"n.","d":"an idea that is suggested as an explanation but has not been proved","c":"假設；假說","s":"Our science teacher asked us to write a hypothesis about which plant would grow faster before we started the experiment.","t":"我們的自然老師要我們在開始實驗前，先寫下一個關於哪種植物會長得比較快的假設。","h":1},{"w":"hypothesize","p":"v.","d":"to suggest an idea as a possible explanation","c":"假設；假定","s":"Scientists hypothesize that the birds fly south because the days get shorter, not because the weather gets colder.","t":"科學家假設鳥類往南飛是因為白天變短，而不是因為天氣變冷。"},{"w":"hypothetical","p":"adj.","d":"based on an idea or situation that is imagined, not real","c":"假設的；假想的","s":"The teacher gave us a hypothetical question: what would you do if you found one million dollars on the street?","t":"老師問了我們一個假設性的問題：如果你在街上撿到一百萬元，你會怎麼做？"},{"w":"test a hypothesis","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do experiments to find out whether an idea is true","c":"驗證假設","s":"To test a hypothesis, you need to change only one thing at a time and keep everything else exactly the same.","t":"要驗證假設，你一次只能改變一個條件，其他的一切都要保持完全相同。"},{"w":"icon","p":"n.","d":"a very famous person or thing that represents something","c":"偶像；象徵；代表人物","s":"The singer became a fashion icon in the 1990s, and young people everywhere copied her hairstyle and clothes.","t":"這位歌手在1990年代成為時尚偶像，各地的年輕人都模仿她的髮型和服裝。","h":1},{"w":"icon","p":"n.","d":"a small picture on a computer or phone screen that you click to open something","c":"圖示","s":"Tap the blue icon on your phone screen to open the app, and then type your name in the first box.","t":"點一下手機螢幕上的藍色圖示打開應用程式，然後在第一個方格裡輸入你的名字。"},{"w":"iconic","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and representing something important","c":"標誌性的；具代表性的","s":"Taipei 101 is the most iconic building in Taiwan, and almost every tourist takes a photo in front of it.","t":"台北101是台灣最具代表性的建築，幾乎每個觀光客都會在它前面拍照。"},{"w":"fashion icon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose style many people copy","c":"時尚偶像","s":"My aunt calls herself a fashion icon, but she has worn the same black jacket to every party for ten years.","t":"我阿姨自稱是時尚偶像，但她十年來每次派對都穿同一件黑色外套。"},{"w":"ideology","p":"n.","d":"a set of political or social beliefs that a group shares","c":"意識形態；思想體系","s":"The two parties have a very different ideology, so they rarely agree on how to spend the city's money.","t":"這兩個政黨的意識形態非常不同，所以他們很少在如何花市政經費上達成一致。","h":1},{"w":"ideological","p":"adj.","d":"based on a set of political or social beliefs","c":"意識形態的；思想上的","s":"The argument between the two brothers was ideological, not personal, so they were friends again by dinner time.","t":"兩兄弟之間的爭論是思想上的，不是針對個人，所以到了晚餐時間他們又和好了。"},{"w":"ideologically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way connected with political or social beliefs","c":"在意識形態上","s":"Although the two newspapers are ideologically very different, they both reported the earthquake in exactly the same way.","t":"雖然這兩份報紙在意識形態上大不相同，但它們對地震的報導方式完全一樣。"},{"w":"political ideology","p":"n.phr.","d":"a set of beliefs about how a country should be run","c":"政治意識形態","s":"Students should learn to judge each idea on its own, rather than following one political ideology without thinking.","t":"學生應該學會獨立判斷每個想法，而不是不加思考地追隨某一種政治意識形態。"},{"w":"idiot","p":"n.","d":"a very stupid person (an insulting word)","c":"白癡；傻瓜","s":"I felt like a complete idiot when I realized I had been waiting at the wrong bus stop for forty minutes.","t":"當我發現自己在錯的公車站等了四十分鐘時，我覺得自己像個十足的傻瓜。","h":1},{"w":"idiotic","p":"adj.","d":"very stupid","c":"愚蠢的；白癡的","s":"Riding a scooter without a helmet in heavy rain is an idiotic thing to do, no matter how late you are.","t":"不管你多晚，在大雨中不戴安全帽騎機車都是一件愚蠢的事。"},{"w":"feel like an idiot","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel very embarrassed about something stupid you did","c":"覺得自己很蠢","s":"She felt like an idiot after calling her teacher \"Mom\" in front of the whole class, but everyone just laughed kindly.","t":"她在全班面前把老師叫成「媽媽」後覺得自己很蠢，但大家只是善意地笑了笑。","a":"felt like an idiot"},{"w":"illusion","p":"n.","d":"something that seems real or true but is not","c":"錯覺；幻覺；假象","s":"The mirror on the wall creates an illusion of space, so the tiny restaurant looks twice as big as it really is.","t":"牆上的鏡子製造出空間的錯覺，所以這家小餐廳看起來比實際大一倍。","h":1},{"w":"optical illusion","p":"n.phr.","d":"a picture that tricks your eyes into seeing something that is not there","c":"視錯覺；錯視圖","s":"In this famous optical illusion, the two lines look different in length, but if you measure them they are exactly the same.","t":"在這幅著名的錯視圖中，兩條線看起來長度不同，但如果你量一量，它們完全一樣長。"},{"w":"be under the illusion that","p":"v.phr.","d":"to wrongly believe that something is true","c":"誤以為…","s":"Many students are under the illusion that they can learn English just by watching videos, but they also need to practice speaking.","t":"許多學生誤以為只靠看影片就能學好英文，但他們也需要練習口說。","a":"are under the illusion that"},{"w":"have no illusions about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to understand clearly how difficult or bad something is","c":"對…不抱幻想；清楚了解","s":"The coach had no illusions about how strong the other team was, so he made his players train twice as hard that week.","t":"教練清楚了解對手有多強，所以那一週他讓球員加倍努力訓練。","a":"had no illusions about"},{"w":"immense","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large or great","c":"巨大的；極大的","s":"Building the new bridge across the river took an immense amount of money, but it saves drivers an hour every day.","t":"興建這座跨河新橋花了巨額的錢，但它每天為駕駛人省下一小時。","h":1},{"w":"immensely","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; very much","c":"極其；非常","s":"The students enjoyed the field trip immensely, and they asked the teacher if they could visit the science museum again.","t":"學生們非常享受這次校外教學，還問老師能不能再去一次科學博物館。"},{"w":"immensity","p":"n.","d":"the very large size of something","c":"巨大；廣大","s":"Standing alone in the desert at night, I finally understood the immensity of the sky and how small we really are.","t":"夜晚獨自站在沙漠中，我終於體會到天空的廣大，以及我們是多麼渺小。"},{"w":"immune","p":"adj.","d":"protected from a disease; not affected by something","c":"免疫的；不受影響的","s":"People who had the disease as children are usually immune to it for the rest of their lives.","t":"小時候得過這種病的人通常終身對它免疫。","h":1},{"w":"immunity","p":"n.","d":"the body's ability to fight a disease; protection from something","c":"免疫力；豁免","s":"Doctors say that getting enough sleep and eating fruit every day can help build your immunity against colds.","t":"醫生說每天睡眠充足和吃水果，有助於建立你對感冒的免疫力。"},{"w":"immune system","p":"n.phr.","d":"the parts of the body that fight disease","c":"免疫系統","s":"When your immune system is weak, even a small cold can last for weeks and make you feel very tired.","t":"當你的免疫系統虛弱時，即使是小感冒也可能持續好幾週，讓你覺得非常疲倦。"},{"w":"immune to","p":"adj.phr.","d":"not affected by something","c":"對…免疫；不受…影響","s":"My grandfather seems immune to criticism; no matter what people say about his cooking, he keeps smiling and cooking.","t":"我爺爺似乎不受批評影響；不管別人怎麼說他的廚藝，他總是微笑著繼續煮。"},{"w":"immunize","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone from a disease by giving them an injection","c":"使免疫；為…接種疫苗","s":"The health department will immunize all first-grade students against the flu at school next Tuesday morning.","t":"衛生局下星期二早上將在學校為所有一年級學生接種流感疫苗。"},{"w":"implement","p":"v.","d":"to make a plan, system, or law start to work","c":"實施；執行","s":"The school will implement the new lunch program in September, and students will get fresh fruit every day.","t":"學校將在九月實施新的午餐計畫，學生每天都能吃到新鮮水果。","h":1},{"w":"implement","p":"n.","d":"a tool, especially one used for farming or gardening","c":"工具；器具","s":"The museum displays every farming implement used by early settlers, from wooden plows to simple hand rakes.","t":"博物館展示早期移民使用的各種農耕工具，從木犁到簡單的手耙都有。"},{"w":"implementation","p":"n.","d":"the act of making a plan or system start to work","c":"實施；執行","s":"The implementation of the new traffic rules was delayed for a month because the road signs were not ready.","t":"新交通規則的實施延後了一個月，因為路標還沒準備好。"},{"w":"implement a plan / policy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put a plan or policy into action","c":"執行計畫／政策","s":"It is easy to make a plan, but much harder to implement a plan when the whole team must change their habits.","t":"制定計畫很容易，但當整個團隊都必須改變習慣時，執行計畫就困難多了。","a":"implement a plan"},{"w":"implication","p":"n.","d":"a possible result or effect; something suggested but not said directly","c":"含意；可能的影響；暗示","s":"The new law has a serious implication for small shops, because they will have to pay much higher taxes next year.","t":"新法律對小商店有嚴重的影響，因為他們明年必須繳交高得多的稅。","h":1},{"w":"imply","p":"v.","d":"to suggest something without saying it directly","c":"暗示；意味著","s":"When my mother said the kitchen was a mess, she was trying to imply that I should wash the dishes.","t":"我媽媽說廚房一團亂時，她是想暗示我應該去洗碗。"},{"w":"implicit","p":"adj.","d":"suggested but not said directly","c":"含蓄的；不言明的","s":"There was an implicit agreement among the roommates that whoever cooked dinner would not have to clean up.","t":"室友之間有一個不言明的默契：誰煮晚餐，誰就不用洗碗。"},{"w":"have implications for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to possibly affect something in the future","c":"對…有影響","s":"Rising sea levels have implications for every coastal city, and some towns may have to move inland within fifty years.","t":"海平面上升對每一個沿海城市都有影響，有些城鎮可能在五十年內必須遷往內陸。"},{"w":"implied","p":"adj.","d":"suggested without being stated directly","c":"暗指的；含蓄的","s":"Her implied message was clear: if we did not finish the project by Friday, she would give it to another team.","t":"她暗示的訊息很清楚：如果我們星期五前沒完成專案，她就會把它交給另一個團隊。"},{"w":"impulse","p":"n.","d":"a sudden strong wish to do something without thinking first","c":"衝動","s":"I had a sudden impulse to buy the red guitar in the shop window, even though I cannot play a single note.","t":"我突然有一股衝動想買櫥窗裡那把紅色吉他，儘管我一個音都不會彈。","h":1},{"w":"impulsive","p":"adj.","d":"doing things suddenly without thinking about the results","c":"衝動的","s":"My brother is so impulsive that he booked a trip to Thailand last night and is leaving tomorrow morning.","t":"我哥哥非常衝動，昨晚訂了去泰國的旅行，明天早上就要出發。"},{"w":"impulsively","p":"adv.","d":"suddenly and without thinking first","c":"衝動地","s":"She impulsively cut her long hair short after the argument, and the next morning she wished she had waited.","t":"吵架之後她衝動地把長髮剪短，第二天早上她就後悔沒有再等一等。"},{"w":"on impulse","p":"phr.","d":"suddenly, without planning","c":"一時衝動；突然","s":"We bought the puppy on impulse at the night market, and now we have to learn how to take care of it.","t":"我們在夜市一時衝動買了這隻小狗，現在得學習如何照顧牠。"},{"w":"impulse buying","p":"n.phr.","d":"buying things suddenly without planning to","c":"衝動購物","s":"To avoid impulse buying, make a shopping list before you go to the supermarket and never shop when you are hungry.","t":"為了避免衝動購物，去超市前先列購物清單，而且絕不要在餓的時候購物。"},{"w":"incentive","p":"n.","d":"something that encourages you to work harder or do something","c":"誘因；激勵；獎勵","s":"The company offers a cash incentive to workers who come up with ideas that help save energy in the factory.","t":"公司對提出有助於工廠節能點子的員工提供現金獎勵。","h":1},{"w":"financial incentive","p":"n.phr.","d":"money offered to encourage people to do something","c":"經濟誘因；金錢獎勵","s":"The government gives families a financial incentive to buy electric scooters, so the air in the city is slowly getting cleaner.","t":"政府提供家庭購買電動機車的經濟誘因，所以城市的空氣正慢慢變乾淨。"},{"w":"give sb an incentive to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to encourage someone to do something by offering a reward","c":"給某人誘因去做…","s":"Free bus rides on weekends give people an incentive to leave their cars at home and explore the city on foot.","t":"週末免費搭公車給了人們誘因把車留在家裡，徒步探索這座城市。","a":"give people an incentive to"},{"w":"incentivize","p":"v.","d":"to encourage people to do something by offering a reward","c":"以獎勵激勵；鼓勵","s":"The school hopes to incentivize reading by giving a free book to every student who finishes ten library books this term.","t":"學校希望透過送一本免費書給本學期讀完十本館藏書的學生，來鼓勵閱讀。"}]},{"unit":19,"theme":"incorporate – institution","cards":[{"w":"incorporate","p":"v.","d":"to include something as part of a bigger thing","c":"包含；納入；合併","s":"The new English textbook will incorporate short videos and songs, so students can practice listening at home as well.","t":"新的英文教科書將納入短片和歌曲，讓學生在家也能練習聽力。","h":1},{"w":"incorporate ... into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to add something so that it becomes part of something else","c":"把…納入…","s":"Our teacher tries to incorporate games into every lesson, which is why nobody falls asleep in her class.","t":"我們老師試著把遊戲納入每一堂課，這就是為什麼沒有人在她的課上睡著。","a":"incorporate"},{"w":"incorporation","p":"n.","d":"the act of including something as part of a whole","c":"納入；合併；公司成立","s":"The incorporation of local history into the school program helped students feel proud of their hometown.","t":"把在地歷史納入學校課程，幫助學生對家鄉感到驕傲。"},{"w":"incorporated","p":"adj.","d":"formed as a legal company (often written Inc.)","c":"股份有限公司的；合併的","s":"After five years of selling cakes from her kitchen, my aunt turned her small business into an incorporated company.","t":"在廚房賣了五年蛋糕之後，我阿姨把她的小生意變成了一家股份有限公司。"},{"w":"index","p":"n.","d":"an alphabetical list at the back of a book that shows where to find things","c":"索引","s":"If you cannot find the topic you need, check the index at the back of the book for the right page number.","t":"如果你找不到需要的主題，查一下書後面的索引，找到正確的頁碼。","h":1},{"w":"index","p":"n.","d":"a number that shows how prices or levels have changed","c":"指數","s":"The air quality index was so high this morning that the school canceled all outdoor sports for the day.","t":"今天早上空氣品質指數太高，學校取消了當天所有的戶外運動。"},{"w":"index finger","p":"n.phr.","d":"the finger next to your thumb","c":"食指","s":"The little boy pointed his index finger at the puppy in the window and begged his mother to buy it.","t":"小男孩用食指指著櫥窗裡的小狗，求媽媽買給他。"},{"w":"index","p":"v.","d":"to make a list of things in order so they can be found easily","c":"編索引；編入索引","s":"The librarian spent the whole summer trying to index every old newspaper so that students could search them by date.","t":"圖書館員花了整個暑假為每一份舊報紙編索引，讓學生可以依日期查找。"},{"w":"indifferent","p":"adj.","d":"not interested in or caring about something","c":"漠不關心的；冷淡的","s":"The shop assistant seemed completely indifferent to our questions, so we left without buying the camera.","t":"那位店員對我們的問題似乎完全漠不關心，所以我們沒買相機就離開了。","h":1},{"w":"indifference","p":"n.","d":"lack of interest or care","c":"漠不關心；冷漠","s":"The government's indifference to the problem made the villagers angry, and they decided to protest in the capital.","t":"政府對這個問題的漠不關心讓村民很生氣，他們決定到首都抗議。"},{"w":"indifferent to","p":"adj.phr.","d":"not caring about something","c":"對…漠不關心","s":"My brother is indifferent to fashion; he wears the same gray T-shirt and jeans almost every day of the year.","t":"我哥哥對時尚漠不關心；他一年中幾乎每天都穿同一件灰色T恤和牛仔褲。"},{"w":"indifferently","p":"adv.","d":"without interest or care","c":"冷淡地；漠不關心地","s":"\"Do whatever you want,\" she said indifferently, without even looking up from the game on her phone.","t":"「隨便你，」她冷淡地說，甚至沒有從手機遊戲上抬起頭來。"},{"w":"indigenous","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to a place naturally; native","c":"原住民的；本土的；原生的","s":"Many indigenous languages in Taiwan are in danger of disappearing, so schools now offer classes to keep them alive.","t":"台灣許多原住民語言面臨消失的危險，所以學校現在開設課程讓它們延續下去。","h":1},{"w":"indigenous people","p":"n.phr.","d":"the people who lived in a place before others arrived","c":"原住民","s":"The festival celebrates the music and dances of the indigenous people who have lived in these mountains for thousands of years.","t":"這個節慶歌頌在這些山區生活了數千年的原住民的音樂和舞蹈。"},{"w":"indigenous to","p":"adj.phr.","d":"naturally found in a particular place","c":"原產於…的","s":"The Formosan black bear is indigenous to Taiwan, and you cannot find this animal anywhere else in the world.","t":"台灣黑熊是原產於台灣的動物，在世界其他地方都找不到。"},{"w":"indispensable","p":"adj.","d":"so important that you cannot do without it","c":"不可或缺的；必不可少的","s":"A good dictionary is indispensable for anyone learning a new language, even in the age of smartphone apps.","t":"即使在智慧型手機應用程式的時代，一本好字典對任何學習新語言的人來說都是不可或缺的。","h":1},{"w":"indispensable to / for","p":"adj.phr.","d":"absolutely necessary for someone or something","c":"對…不可或缺","s":"Clean water is indispensable to human life, yet millions of people around the world still do not have it.","t":"乾淨的水對人類生命不可或缺，但世界上仍有數百萬人沒有乾淨的水。","a":"indispensable to"},{"w":"dispensable","p":"adj.","d":"not necessary; able to be removed","c":"非必要的；可有可無的","s":"When money got tight, the family cut every dispensable cost, starting with the three streaming services they rarely watched.","t":"錢變緊時，這家人砍掉了所有非必要的開支，先從他們很少看的三個串流服務開始。"},{"w":"dispense","p":"v.","d":"to give out something to people; to provide a service","c":"分發；配藥；提供","s":"The machine in the lobby will dispense hot coffee and tea for free to anyone who is waiting for an appointment.","t":"大廳裡的機器會免費提供熱咖啡和茶給任何等候預約的人。"},{"w":"indulge","p":"v.","d":"to allow yourself or someone else to have something enjoyable","c":"放縱；沉溺；縱容","s":"On my birthday, I decided to indulge myself with a huge chocolate cake and an afternoon of doing nothing.","t":"生日那天，我決定用一個巨大的巧克力蛋糕和一個無所事事的下午來放縱自己。","h":1},{"w":"indulge in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to let yourself enjoy something, especially something not good for you","c":"沉溺於；盡情享受","s":"After the exams were over, we indulged in ice cream and video games for a whole weekend without feeling guilty.","t":"考試結束後，我們整個週末盡情享受冰淇淋和電動遊戲，一點也不覺得內疚。","a":"indulged in"},{"w":"indulgence","p":"n.","d":"something you allow yourself to enjoy; the act of indulging","c":"放縱；嗜好；享受","s":"A warm bath with music is my only indulgence after a long week of work, and I never skip it on Friday nights.","t":"忙碌一週後，放著音樂泡個熱水澡是我唯一的享受，我星期五晚上從不錯過。"},{"w":"indulgent","p":"adj.","d":"allowing someone to have or do whatever they want","c":"縱容的；寬容的","s":"My indulgent grandparents let me stay up late and eat candy every time I visit, which drives my mother crazy.","t":"我縱容的爺爺奶奶每次我去都讓我熬夜、吃糖果，這讓我媽媽很抓狂。"},{"w":"inevitable","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen and impossible to avoid","c":"不可避免的；必然的","s":"With such heavy rain every afternoon this week, it was inevitable that the river would flood the low fields.","t":"這星期每天下午都下這麼大的雨，河水淹沒低窪農田是不可避免的。","h":1},{"w":"inevitably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that cannot be avoided","c":"不可避免地；必然地","s":"If you keep using your phone until midnight, you will inevitably feel tired and sleepy in your first class.","t":"如果你一直用手機到半夜，你第一堂課必然會覺得疲倦想睡。"},{"w":"inevitability","p":"n.","d":"the fact that something is certain to happen","c":"必然性；不可避免","s":"The old farmer accepted the inevitability of change, and he finally let his son use machines on the family farm.","t":"老農夫接受了改變的必然性，終於讓兒子在家裡的農場上使用機器。"},{"w":"infect","p":"v.","d":"to pass a disease to a person, animal, or plant","c":"傳染；感染","s":"Please stay home if you have a fever, because you could infect your classmates before you even know you are sick.","t":"如果你發燒請待在家裡，因為你可能在自己知道生病之前就傳染給同學。","h":1},{"w":"infection","p":"n.","d":"a disease caused by germs entering the body","c":"感染；傳染病","s":"The doctor cleaned the cut on my knee carefully to prevent an infection and told me to change the bandage daily.","t":"醫生仔細清潔我膝蓋上的傷口以防止感染，並要我每天換繃帶。"},{"w":"infectious","p":"adj.","d":"able to be passed from one person to another","c":"傳染性的；有感染力的","s":"Her laugh is so infectious that within a minute the whole classroom was laughing, even the strict teacher.","t":"她的笑聲極具感染力，不到一分鐘整間教室都笑了起來，連嚴格的老師也是。"},{"w":"infected","p":"adj.","d":"containing germs that cause disease","c":"受感染的","s":"The infected wound became red and painful, so my mother took me to the clinic the next morning.","t":"受感染的傷口變得又紅又痛，所以我媽媽第二天早上帶我去診所。"},{"w":"infinite","p":"adj.","d":"without any limit or end","c":"無限的；無窮的","s":"Teaching young children requires infinite patience, because they ask the same question again and again all day.","t":"教幼童需要無限的耐心，因為他們一整天都會一再問同樣的問題。","h":1},{"w":"infinitely","p":"adv.","d":"very much; without limit","c":"無限地；非常","s":"The new apartment is infinitely better than our old one, mainly because it is quiet and only five minutes from the MRT.","t":"新公寓比我們的舊公寓好得太多了，主要是因為它很安靜，而且離捷運只要五分鐘。"},{"w":"infinity","p":"n.","d":"a space, time, or number without any end","c":"無限；無窮","s":"Looking up at the stars, the little girl asked her father whether the universe really went on to infinity.","t":"抬頭看著星星，小女孩問爸爸宇宙是不是真的延伸到無限遠。"},{"w":"finite","p":"adj.","d":"having a limit or end","c":"有限的","s":"Oil and coal are finite resources, so countries are investing in wind and solar power before they run out.","t":"石油和煤是有限的資源，所以各國在它們用完之前投資風力和太陽能。"},{"w":"infrastructure","p":"n.","d":"the basic systems a country needs, such as roads, power, and water","c":"基礎建設；基礎設施","s":"The earthquake damaged the city's infrastructure so badly that some areas had no water or electricity for two weeks.","t":"地震嚴重破壞了這座城市的基礎設施，有些地區兩個星期沒有水電。","h":1},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"the way something is built or organized; a building","c":"結構；建築物","s":"The old wooden structure by the river has stood for over a hundred years, surviving dozens of typhoons.","t":"河邊那座古老的木造建築已經矗立了一百多年，撐過了數十次颱風。"},{"w":"structural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the way something is built","c":"結構上的；結構性的","s":"Engineers found structural problems in the bridge, so it was closed to trucks until the repairs were finished.","t":"工程師發現橋樑有結構上的問題，所以在修復完成前禁止卡車通行。"},{"w":"transport infrastructure","p":"n.phr.","d":"roads, railways, airports, and ports","c":"交通基礎建設","s":"Taiwan's excellent transport infrastructure means you can travel from Taipei to Kaohsiung in less than two hours by high-speed rail.","t":"台灣優良的交通基礎建設意味著你搭高鐵從台北到高雄不到兩小時。"},{"w":"inherent","p":"adj.","d":"existing as a natural and basic part of something","c":"固有的；內在的","s":"There is an inherent risk in every sport, which is why players wear helmets and coaches teach safety first.","t":"每項運動都有固有的風險，這就是為什麼球員要戴頭盔、教練要先教安全。","h":1},{"w":"inherently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is a natural and basic part of something","c":"本質上；固有地","s":"Social media is not inherently bad, but spending five hours a day on it can harm your sleep and your grades.","t":"社群媒體本質上並不壞，但每天花五小時在上面可能傷害你的睡眠和成績。"},{"w":"inherent in","p":"adj.phr.","d":"naturally part of something","c":"…所固有的","s":"Some stress is inherent in any job, so learning to relax after work is just as important as working hard.","t":"任何工作都固有一些壓力，所以學會下班後放鬆和努力工作同樣重要。"},{"w":"inherit","p":"v.","d":"to receive money, property, or a feature from someone after they die","c":"繼承；遺傳到","s":"If nobody writes a will, the law decides who will inherit the house, which can cause arguments in the family.","t":"如果沒有人立遺囑，法律會決定誰繼承房子，這可能在家族中引起爭執。","h":1},{"w":"inheritance","p":"n.","d":"money or property received from someone who has died","c":"遺產；繼承物","s":"She spent her whole inheritance on a trip around the world, saying that her grandfather would have wanted her to enjoy life.","t":"她把全部遺產花在環遊世界的旅行上，說她爺爺會希望她享受人生。"},{"w":"heir","p":"n.","d":"a person who will receive money or property when someone dies","c":"繼承人","s":"The rich businessman has three children, but he has not yet decided which one will be the main heir to his company.","t":"這位富商有三個孩子，但他還沒決定哪一個會成為公司的主要繼承人。"},{"w":"inherit ... from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get a quality or thing from a parent or relative","c":"從…遺傳到；從…繼承","s":"I inherited my curly hair from my father, but my love of music clearly comes from my mother's side.","t":"我的捲髮遺傳自我爸爸，但我對音樂的熱愛顯然來自媽媽那一邊。","a":"inherited"},{"w":"initiate","p":"v.","d":"to make something start, such as a plan or process","c":"開始；發起；創始","s":"The new principal decided to initiate a reading program in which every class spends twenty minutes a day with a book.","t":"新校長決定發起一項閱讀計畫，每個班級每天花二十分鐘看書。","h":1},{"w":"initiative","p":"n.","d":"a new plan or action to solve a problem or reach a goal","c":"倡議；新措施；計畫","s":"The city's latest green initiative gives every family a free tree to plant in front of their house.","t":"市政府最新的綠化計畫送每個家庭一棵免費的樹，種在自家門前。","h":1},{"w":"initiative","p":"n.","d":"the ability to decide and act on your own without being told","c":"主動性；進取心","s":"Employers love workers who show initiative, like the new assistant who fixed the printer before anyone asked.","t":"雇主喜歡展現主動性的員工，就像那位在沒人要求前就把印表機修好的新助理。"},{"w":"take the initiative","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the first to act in order to make something happen","c":"採取主動；帶頭","s":"Nobody wanted to clean the messy classroom, so Amy took the initiative and started picking up the papers on the floor.","t":"沒有人想打掃凌亂的教室，所以艾咪主動帶頭，開始撿起地上的紙。","a":"took the initiative"},{"w":"initial","p":"adj.","d":"happening at the beginning; first","c":"最初的；開始的","s":"My initial plan was to study medicine, but after one biology class I realized I preferred languages.","t":"我最初的計畫是讀醫學，但上了一堂生物課後，我發現自己更喜歡語言。"},{"w":"initially","p":"adv.","d":"at the beginning; at first","c":"起初；最初","s":"Initially, the students were afraid of the new teacher, but by October they were all laughing at her jokes.","t":"起初學生們很怕新老師，但到了十月，他們都在笑她講的笑話。","a":"Initially"},{"w":"inject","p":"v.","d":"to put a liquid, especially medicine, into the body with a needle","c":"注射；注入","s":"The nurse will inject the medicine into your arm, and you should feel better within a few hours.","t":"護士會把藥注射到你的手臂裡，幾小時內你應該會覺得好一些。","h":1},{"w":"injection","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting medicine into the body with a needle","c":"注射；打針","s":"The doctor gave the crying child an injection so quickly that it was over before he even noticed the needle.","t":"醫生很快地給哭鬧的孩子打了一針，在他注意到針頭之前就結束了。","h":1},{"w":"inject ... into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to add something new, such as money or energy, to something","c":"把…注入…","s":"The government hopes to inject new life into the old town by opening a night market and a youth center.","t":"政府希望透過開設夜市和青年中心，為老城區注入新生命。","a":"inject"},{"w":"give sb an injection","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put medicine into someone's body with a needle","c":"給某人打針","s":"Before the trip to Africa, the clinic gave me an injection to protect me from a dangerous fever carried by mosquitoes.","t":"去非洲旅行前，診所給我打了一針，以預防蚊子傳播的危險熱病。","a":"gave me an injection"},{"w":"inning","p":"n.","d":"one of the nine parts of a baseball game in which each team bats","c":"（棒球的）一局","s":"Our team was losing by three runs, but we scored four in the final inning and won the game.","t":"我們的球隊落後三分，但在最後一局得了四分，贏得了比賽。","h":1},{"w":"the ninth inning","p":"n.phr.","d":"the last regular part of a baseball game","c":"第九局","s":"The stadium went crazy when the young batter hit a home run in the ninth inning to tie the game.","t":"當那位年輕打者在第九局擊出全壘打追平比數時，整個球場都瘋狂了。"},{"w":"extra innings","p":"n.phr.","d":"additional parts of a baseball game played when the score is tied","c":"延長賽","s":"The game went into extra innings after both teams scored five runs, and it did not end until nearly midnight.","t":"兩隊各得五分後，比賽進入延長賽，一直到將近午夜才結束。"},{"w":"innovation","p":"n.","d":"a new idea, method, or invention","c":"創新；新發明","s":"The smartphone was the biggest innovation of the last twenty years, and it changed how we shop, study, and talk.","t":"智慧型手機是過去二十年最大的創新，它改變了我們購物、學習和交談的方式。","h":1},{"w":"innovative","p":"adj.","d":"using new ideas and methods","c":"創新的；革新的","s":"The innovative teacher lets her students make short films instead of writing reports about the books they read.","t":"這位創新的老師讓學生拍短片，而不是寫讀書報告。","h":1},{"w":"innovate","p":"v.","d":"to introduce new ideas or methods","c":"創新；革新","s":"Companies that fail to innovate are soon left behind, just as many film camera makers were when digital cameras arrived.","t":"無法創新的公司很快就會被淘汰，就像數位相機出現時許多底片相機製造商的下場一樣。"},{"w":"innovator","p":"n.","d":"a person who introduces new ideas or methods","c":"創新者；革新者","s":"Steve Jobs is remembered as a great innovator because he turned complicated computers into products everyone could use.","t":"史蒂夫·賈伯斯被人們記住是一位偉大的創新者，因為他把複雜的電腦變成人人都能使用的產品。"},{"w":"inquiry","p":"n.","d":"a question asking for information; an official investigation","c":"詢問；調查","s":"The hotel received an inquiry from a school that wanted to book forty rooms for a trip in July.","t":"飯店收到一所學校的詢問，他們想為七月的旅行預訂四十個房間。","h":1},{"w":"inquire","p":"v.","d":"to ask for information","c":"詢問；打聽","s":"I called the station to inquire whether the last train to Taichung had been canceled because of the typhoon.","t":"我打電話到車站詢問最後一班到台中的火車是否因颱風取消了。"},{"w":"inquire about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask for information about something","c":"詢問關於…","s":"Several parents came to the office to inquire about the summer camp, so the school added two more sessions.","t":"好幾位家長來辦公室詢問夏令營的事，所以學校增加了兩個梯次。"},{"w":"make inquiries","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to find out information by asking questions","c":"打聽；查詢","s":"The police made inquiries in the neighborhood, and a shop owner finally remembered seeing the missing boy.","t":"警方在附近打聽，一位店主終於想起曾看見那個失蹤的男孩。","a":"made inquiries"},{"w":"insane","p":"adj.","d":"seriously mentally ill; very foolish or crazy","c":"瘋狂的；精神失常的","s":"It would be insane to go hiking in the mountains today, because the weather report says a typhoon is coming tonight.","t":"今天去山上健行是瘋狂的，因為氣象報告說今晚颱風要來。","h":1},{"w":"insanity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being seriously mentally ill; extreme foolishness","c":"瘋狂；精神失常","s":"Spending your whole month's salary on one pair of shoes is pure insanity, no matter how beautiful they are.","t":"把整個月的薪水花在一雙鞋上簡直是瘋狂，不管它們有多漂亮。"},{"w":"insanely","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; in a crazy way","c":"極度地；瘋狂地","s":"The new roller coaster is insanely fast, and my friend screamed from the first second to the last.","t":"新的雲霄飛車極度快速，我朋友從第一秒尖叫到最後一秒。"},{"w":"sane","p":"adj.","d":"having a healthy mind; sensible","c":"神智正常的；理智的","s":"No sane person would leave a small child alone at home all night, so the neighbors called the police.","t":"沒有理智的人會整夜把小孩單獨留在家裡，所以鄰居報了警。"},{"w":"insight","p":"n.","d":"a clear and deep understanding of something","c":"洞察力；深刻的了解","s":"Talking with the old fisherman gave me real insight into how much the sea has changed in the last fifty years.","t":"和老漁夫聊天讓我深刻了解到過去五十年海洋改變了多少。","h":1},{"w":"insightful","p":"adj.","d":"showing a clear and deep understanding","c":"有洞察力的；見解深刻的","s":"Her insightful comments on the novel helped the whole class understand why the main character made such a strange choice.","t":"她對這部小說見解深刻的評論，幫助全班理解主角為何做出如此奇怪的選擇。"},{"w":"gain insight into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to come to understand something clearly","c":"深入了解…","s":"By living with a host family for a month, the students gained insight into daily life in Japan that no textbook could give.","t":"透過和寄宿家庭住一個月，學生們深入了解了課本無法提供的日本日常生活。","a":"gained insight into"},{"w":"installation","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting equipment or software in place so it can be used","c":"安裝；裝設","s":"The installation of the new air conditioners in every classroom took the workers three days during the summer break.","t":"暑假期間，工人花了三天在每間教室安裝新冷氣。","h":1},{"w":"install","p":"v.","d":"to put equipment or software in place so it can be used","c":"安裝","s":"My father asked me to install the new printer because he could not understand the instructions in the box.","t":"我爸爸要我安裝新印表機，因為他看不懂盒子裡的說明書。"},{"w":"art installation","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large work of art built in a space for people to walk around","c":"裝置藝術","s":"The art installation in the park is made of ten thousand plastic bottles, and it reminds visitors how much waste we produce.","t":"公園裡的裝置藝術由一萬個塑膠瓶製成，提醒參觀者我們製造了多少垃圾。"},{"w":"institute","p":"n.","d":"an organization for research, education, or a special purpose","c":"學院；研究所；機構","s":"After college, she joined a research institute in Hsinchu, where scientists are developing faster computer chips.","t":"大學畢業後，她進入新竹的一家研究機構，那裡的科學家正在開發更快的電腦晶片。","h":1},{"w":"institution","p":"n.","d":"a large important organization such as a university, bank, or hospital","c":"機構；制度","s":"The university is the oldest educational institution in the city, and it has trained doctors for over one hundred years.","t":"這所大學是本市最古老的教育機構，培養醫生已有一百多年。","h":1},{"w":"institute","p":"v.","d":"to introduce or start a system, rule, or policy","c":"制定；開始實施","s":"The school decided to institute a new rule that bans sugary drinks from the campus starting next semester.","t":"學校決定制定一項新規定，從下學期開始禁止含糖飲料進入校園。"},{"w":"institutional","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a large organization or system","c":"機構的；制度上的","s":"The report found institutional problems in the hospital, such as poor record keeping and too few night nurses.","t":"報告發現這家醫院有制度上的問題，例如紀錄保存不佳和夜班護士太少。"},{"w":"research institute","p":"n.phr.","d":"an organization where scientists study a subject","c":"研究機構；研究所","s":"The research institute on the coast studies how warmer oceans are affecting the fish that local families depend on.","t":"海岸邊的研究機構研究暖化的海洋如何影響當地家庭賴以為生的魚類。"},{"w":"financial institution","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bank or other organization that deals with money","c":"金融機構","s":"Before you choose a financial institution for your savings, compare the interest rates and fees of at least three banks.","t":"在為你的存款選擇金融機構之前，先比較至少三家銀行的利率和手續費。"}]},{"unit":20,"theme":"intact – lawsuit","cards":[{"w":"intact","p":"adj.","d":"complete and not damaged or broken","c":"完整無損的","s":"Although the box fell off the truck on the highway, the glass vase inside was still intact when we opened it.","t":"雖然箱子在高速公路上從卡車掉下來，但我們打開時裡面的玻璃花瓶仍然完整無損。","h":1},{"w":"remain intact","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay whole and undamaged","c":"保持完整","s":"The old city wall has remained intact for more than four hundred years, even though several big earthquakes have hit the area.","t":"這座古城牆已經保持完整超過四百年，即使這個地區發生過好幾次大地震。","a":"remained intact"},{"w":"leave sth intact","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not change or damage something","c":"使某物保持原樣","s":"The new owner decided to leave the ceiling intact because the hand-painted ceiling was the most beautiful part of the house.","t":"新屋主決定讓天花板保持原樣，因為手繪的天花板是這棟房子最美的部分。","a":"leave the ceiling intact"},{"w":"integrate","p":"v.","d":"to join or combine things so they work well together","c":"整合；融入","s":"The new app can integrate your calendar, your e-mail, and your to-do list, so you never miss an important meeting again.","t":"這個新 App 可以整合你的行事曆、電子郵件和待辦清單，讓你再也不會錯過重要會議。","h":1},{"w":"integration","p":"n.","d":"the process of joining or combining things or people into one group","c":"整合；融合","s":"The integration of students from different countries takes time, but sports and music clubs help them become friends quickly.","t":"來自不同國家學生的融合需要時間，但運動和音樂社團幫助他們很快成為朋友。","h":1},{"w":"integrate into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become part of a group or society","c":"融入…","s":"It took my cousin almost a year to integrate into Canadian society, but now she has many local friends and speaks English fluently.","t":"我表姐花了將近一年才融入加拿大社會，但現在她有很多當地朋友，英文也說得很流利。"},{"w":"integrated","p":"adj.","d":"with different parts combined so they work together","c":"整合的；融合的","s":"The city built an integrated transport system, so one card lets you ride the bus, the MRT, and even rent a bike.","t":"這座城市建立了一套整合的交通系統，所以一張卡就可以搭公車、捷運，甚至租腳踏車。"},{"w":"integral","p":"adj.","d":"necessary to make something complete","c":"不可或缺的；構成整體所必需的","s":"Teamwork is an integral part of this project, so every member must share his or her ideas at the weekly meeting.","t":"團隊合作是這個專案不可或缺的一部分，所以每個成員都必須在每週會議上分享想法。"},{"w":"integrity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles","c":"正直；誠信","s":"Our school trusts Ms. Huang to count the votes because she is known for her integrity and has never told a lie.","t":"我們學校信任黃老師來計票，因為她以正直聞名，從來沒有說過謊。","h":1},{"w":"integrity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being whole and not damaged","c":"完整性","s":"Engineers checked the integrity of the bridge after the earthquake, and they found a long crack on one of its columns.","t":"地震後工程師檢查了這座橋的完整性，結果在其中一根柱子上發現一道長裂縫。"},{"w":"a person of integrity","p":"n.phr.","d":"someone who is honest and does the right thing","c":"正直的人","s":"My grandfather returned the wallet with all the money inside, and the whole village knows he is a man of integrity.","t":"我爺爺把錢包連同裡面所有的錢都還了回去，全村的人都知道他是個正直的人。","a":"a man of integrity"},{"w":"intensify","p":"v.","d":"to become or make something stronger or greater","c":"加強；增強","s":"The wind began to intensify in the evening, so the fishermen quickly tied their boats to the dock and went home.","t":"傍晚風開始增強，所以漁民們趕緊把船綁在碼頭上回家。","h":1},{"w":"intense","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or extreme in degree","c":"強烈的；劇烈的","s":"The intense heat in the kitchen made the cook step outside every twenty minutes to drink some water and cool down.","t":"廚房裡強烈的高溫讓廚師每二十分鐘就得走到外面喝水降溫。"},{"w":"intensity","p":"n.","d":"the strength or power of something","c":"強度；強烈","s":"The intensity of the sunlight at noon is so high that doctors advise people to wear a hat and sunglasses outdoors.","t":"中午陽光的強度非常高，所以醫生建議大家在戶外要戴帽子和太陽眼鏡。"},{"w":"intensive","p":"adj.","d":"involving a lot of work or activity in a short time","c":"密集的；集中的","s":"Before the big exam, my brother took an intensive two-week course in which he studied math for eight hours every day.","t":"大考前，我哥哥上了一個為期兩週的密集課程，每天讀八小時的數學。"},{"w":"intensely","p":"adv.","d":"in a very strong or extreme way","c":"強烈地；極度地","s":"She felt intensely nervous before her first piano concert, but once she started playing, all her fear disappeared.","t":"第一次鋼琴演奏會前她極度緊張，但一開始彈奏，所有的恐懼就消失了。"},{"w":"intent","p":"n.","d":"what you plan or mean to do","c":"意圖；目的","s":"The boy broke the window by accident, and the police agreed that he had no intent to damage the shop.","t":"那個男孩不小心打破了窗戶，警方也同意他沒有破壞商店的意圖。","h":1},{"w":"intent","p":"adj.","d":"giving all your attention to something","c":"專注的；專心的","s":"With an intent look on her face, the little girl watched the baker turn a ball of dough into a swan.","t":"小女孩臉上帶著專注的表情，看著麵包師把一團麵團變成一隻天鵝。"},{"w":"be intent on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be determined to do something","c":"決心要…","s":"Even after failing twice, my sister is intent on passing her driving test, so she practices every weekend with Dad.","t":"即使已經失敗兩次，我姐姐仍然決心要通過駕照考試，所以她每個週末都和爸爸練習。","a":"is intent on"},{"w":"intention","p":"n.","d":"something you plan or want to do","c":"意圖；打算","s":"I had every intention of finishing my homework last night, but I fell asleep at my desk around nine o'clock.","t":"我昨晚完全打算把功課做完，但九點左右我就在書桌前睡著了。"},{"w":"intend","p":"v.","d":"to plan or mean to do something","c":"打算；意圖","s":"We intend to visit Grandma this Sunday, but if it rains heavily, we will go the following week instead.","t":"我們打算這個星期日去看奶奶，但如果下大雨，我們就改成下週去。"},{"w":"intentional","p":"adj.","d":"done on purpose, not by accident","c":"故意的","s":"The referee decided that the foul was intentional, so the player received a red card and had to leave the game.","t":"裁判判定那次犯規是故意的，所以那名球員拿到紅牌，必須離場。"},{"w":"interference","p":"n.","d":"the act of getting involved in something that is not your business","c":"干涉；干擾","s":"The students planned the whole school festival by themselves, and they were proud that it succeeded without any interference from teachers.","t":"學生們自己策劃了整個校慶，他們很自豪在沒有老師任何干涉的情況下成功了。","h":1},{"w":"interference","p":"n.","d":"unwanted noise or signals that stop a radio or TV from working well","c":"（訊號）干擾","s":"There was so much interference on the radio during the storm that we could hardly hear the weather report.","t":"暴風雨期間收音機有太多干擾，我們幾乎聽不到氣象報告。"},{"w":"interfere","p":"v.","d":"to get involved in a situation when you are not wanted","c":"干涉；妨礙","s":"My parents try not to interfere when my brother and I argue, because they want us to solve our own problems.","t":"我哥哥和我吵架時，爸媽盡量不干涉，因為他們希望我們自己解決問題。"},{"w":"interfere with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to prevent something from working or happening properly","c":"妨礙；干擾","s":"Playing video games late at night can interfere with your sleep, and you will feel tired and slow in class the next day.","t":"深夜打電動會妨礙你的睡眠，第二天上課你會覺得又累又遲鈍。"},{"w":"interior","p":"adj.","d":"inside a building, car, or other object","c":"內部的；室內的","s":"The interior walls of the café are painted dark green, which makes the room feel calm and cozy on rainy days.","t":"這家咖啡館的內部牆壁漆成深綠色，讓房間在雨天感覺平靜又舒適。","h":1},{"w":"interior","p":"n.","d":"the inside part of something","c":"內部","s":"The interior of the old church was dark and cool, and the only light came through the colored glass windows.","t":"這座老教堂的內部陰暗而涼爽，唯一的光線從彩色玻璃窗透進來。"},{"w":"interior design","p":"n.phr.","d":"the art of planning how the inside of a room or building looks","c":"室內設計","s":"My aunt studied interior design in Milan, and now she helps hotel owners choose furniture, colors, and lighting for their rooms.","t":"我阿姨在米蘭學室內設計，現在她幫飯店老闆挑選房間的家具、顏色和燈光。"},{"w":"exterior","p":"n.","d":"the outside part of something","c":"外部；外觀","s":"The exterior of the house needs a new coat of paint, because the old yellow color has turned gray after years of rain.","t":"這棟房子的外觀需要重新上漆，因為舊的黃色經過多年雨水沖刷已經變灰了。"},{"w":"interpretation","p":"n.","d":"an explanation of the meaning of something","c":"解釋；詮釋","s":"Every reader has a different interpretation of the poem's last line, and our teacher says that none of them is wrong.","t":"每位讀者對這首詩最後一行都有不同的詮釋，我們老師說沒有一種是錯的。","h":1},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to explain or decide what something means","c":"解釋；理解","s":"Scientists are still trying to interpret the strange signals from space, which repeat every sixteen days like a clock.","t":"科學家仍在試著解釋那些來自太空的奇怪訊號，它們像時鐘一樣每十六天重複一次。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to translate what someone says into another language as they speak","c":"口譯","s":"When the Japanese tourists asked for directions, my brother was able to interpret for them because he studies Japanese at school.","t":"日本觀光客問路時，我哥哥能幫他們口譯，因為他在學校學日文。"},{"w":"interpreter","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to translate spoken words into another language","c":"口譯員","s":"The president spoke only Spanish at the meeting, so an interpreter stood beside him and repeated every sentence in English.","t":"總統在會議上只說西班牙語，所以一位口譯員站在他旁邊，把每句話重複成英文。"},{"w":"open to interpretation","p":"adj.phr.","d":"able to be understood in different ways","c":"可以有不同解讀的","s":"The ending of the movie is open to interpretation, so my friends and I argued for an hour about whether the hero really died.","t":"這部電影的結局可以有不同解讀，所以我和朋友爭論了一小時主角到底有沒有死。"},{"w":"interval","p":"n.","d":"a period of time between two events","c":"間隔；間隔時間","s":"The doctor told my grandmother to take the pills at an interval of six hours, so she sets an alarm on her phone.","t":"醫生告訴我奶奶每間隔六小時吃一次藥，所以她在手機上設了鬧鐘。","h":1},{"w":"at regular intervals","p":"phr.","d":"happening again and again with the same amount of time or space between","c":"定期地；每隔一定距離","s":"Along the hiking trail, the park placed wooden signs at regular intervals so that visitors would not lose their way in the forest.","t":"沿著登山步道，公園每隔一定距離設置木牌，這樣遊客就不會在森林裡迷路。"},{"w":"interval","p":"n.","d":"a short break between the parts of a play, concert, or game","c":"（表演的）幕間休息","s":"During the interval, the audience left their seats to buy drinks, and the actors changed costumes behind the curtain.","t":"幕間休息時，觀眾離開座位去買飲料，演員們則在幕後換戲服。"},{"w":"intervention","p":"n.","d":"the act of becoming involved in a situation to change or stop it","c":"介入；干預","s":"Thanks to the quick intervention of a passing nurse, the old man who had fainted at the bus stop was soon breathing normally again.","t":"多虧一位路過護理師的迅速介入，在公車站昏倒的老先生很快就恢復正常呼吸了。","h":1},{"w":"intervene","p":"v.","d":"to become involved in a situation in order to help or stop it","c":"介入；調停","s":"When the two boys started pushing each other in the hallway, a teacher had to intervene before anyone got hurt.","t":"當兩個男孩開始在走廊上互推時，一位老師必須在有人受傷前介入。"},{"w":"intervene in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get involved in a problem or argument that is not your own","c":"介入…","s":"The United Nations decided to intervene in the conflict and sent food, doctors, and peacekeepers to the region.","t":"聯合國決定介入這場衝突，派遣食物、醫生和維和部隊到該地區。"},{"w":"government intervention","p":"n.phr.","d":"action taken by the government to control something, especially the economy","c":"政府干預","s":"When food prices rose too fast last year, many people called for government intervention to keep rice and vegetables affordable for poor families.","t":"去年食物價格漲得太快時，許多人呼籲政府干預，讓貧困家庭買得起米和蔬菜。"},{"w":"investigator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to find out the facts about something","c":"調查員","s":"After the fire, an investigator from the insurance company spent two days in the building looking for the cause.","t":"火災後，保險公司的一位調查員在那棟建築裡花了兩天尋找起火原因。","h":1},{"w":"investigate","p":"v.","d":"to try to find out the truth about something, especially a crime","c":"調查","s":"The police are going to investigate the robbery at the jewelry store, and they have already checked the security cameras nearby.","t":"警方將調查珠寶店的搶案，他們已經查看了附近的監視器。"},{"w":"investigation","p":"n.","d":"an official attempt to find out the facts about something","c":"調查","s":"The investigation into the plane crash took almost a year, but it finally showed that a small part of the engine had broken.","t":"對這起空難的調查花了將近一年，但最終顯示引擎的一個小零件壞了。"},{"w":"private investigator","p":"n.phr.","d":"a detective who is paid by a person, not by the police","c":"私家偵探","s":"In the movie, a private investigator is hired to follow a rich man's wife, but he soon discovers a much bigger secret.","t":"電影裡，一位私家偵探被雇來跟蹤一位富翁的妻子，但他很快就發現了一個更大的秘密。"},{"w":"under investigation","p":"phr.","d":"being examined officially to find out the truth","c":"正在接受調查","s":"The company is currently under investigation for selling food past its expiration date, so its shops have been closed for a week.","t":"這家公司目前因販賣過期食品正在接受調查，所以它的店面已經關閉一週了。"},{"w":"irony","p":"n.","d":"a situation that is strange or funny because it is the opposite of what you expect","c":"諷刺；反諷","s":"The irony is that the fire station itself burned down while all the firefighters were out fighting a fire somewhere else.","t":"諷刺的是，消防局本身燒掉了，而當時所有消防員都在別處救火。","h":1},{"w":"irony","p":"n.","d":"the use of words that say the opposite of what you really mean, often as a joke","c":"反話；諷刺","s":"When Dad said \"Great weather for a picnic\" as the rain poured down, my little brother did not understand his irony.","t":"當大雨傾盆而下時爸爸說「真是野餐的好天氣」，我弟弟聽不懂他的反話。"},{"w":"ironic","p":"adj.","d":"strange or funny because it is the opposite of what you would expect","c":"諷刺的；出乎意料的","s":"It is ironic that the doctor who tells everyone to exercise has not been to the gym himself in five years.","t":"諷刺的是，那位叫大家運動的醫生自己已經五年沒去健身房了。"},{"w":"ironically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is the opposite of what you would expect","c":"諷刺地；出乎意料地","s":"Ironically, the student who missed the most classes got the highest score on the final exam and surprised the whole school.","t":"諷刺的是，缺課最多的那位學生在期末考拿到最高分，讓全校都很驚訝。","a":"Ironically"},{"w":"journalism","p":"n.","d":"the job of writing news reports for newspapers, TV, or the Internet","c":"新聞業；新聞工作","s":"Amy chose to study journalism at university because she loves asking questions and telling true stories about real people.","t":"艾美選擇在大學讀新聞，因為她喜歡提問，也喜歡講述真實人物的真實故事。","h":1},{"w":"journalist","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes news reports for newspapers, TV, or the Internet","c":"記者；新聞工作者","s":"A journalist from a national newspaper came to our town to write about the farmers whose fields were destroyed by the flood.","t":"一位全國性報紙的記者來到我們鎮上，報導田地被洪水毀掉的農民。","h":1},{"w":"journal","p":"n.","d":"a magazine for people with a special interest or profession","c":"期刊","s":"The professor's research on sea turtles was published in a famous science journal, and reporters from many countries wrote about it.","t":"這位教授關於海龜的研究發表在一本著名的科學期刊上，許多國家的記者都報導了。"},{"w":"journal","p":"n.","d":"a written record of what you do or think each day","c":"日誌；日記","s":"During her trip to Europe, my sister kept a travel journal and wrote down what she saw and ate every single day.","t":"歐洲旅行期間，我姐姐寫了一本旅行日誌，每天記下她看到和吃到的東西。"},{"w":"judicial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with courts of law and judges","c":"司法的","s":"In a fair country, the judicial system works independently, so judges can make decisions without pressure from politicians.","t":"在一個公平的國家，司法體系獨立運作，所以法官可以在沒有政治人物壓力下做出判決。","h":1},{"w":"judge","p":"n.","d":"the person in a court who decides how a criminal should be punished","c":"法官","s":"The judge listened carefully to both lawyers for three hours before she announced that the man would go to prison.","t":"法官仔細聽了兩位律師三個小時的陳述，然後才宣布那名男子將入獄。"},{"w":"judge","p":"v.","d":"to form an opinion about someone or something","c":"判斷；評價","s":"You should not judge a book by its cover, because the plain-looking novel on that shelf is actually the most exciting one.","t":"你不應該以封面評斷一本書，因為那個架上看起來樸素的小說其實是最精彩的一本。"},{"w":"judgment","p":"n.","d":"an opinion or decision made after thinking carefully","c":"判斷；判斷力","s":"In my judgment, the blue dress looks better on you than the red one, but of course the final choice is yours.","t":"依我的判斷，藍色洋裝比紅色的更適合你，但當然最後的選擇還是你的。"},{"w":"the judicial system","p":"n.phr.","d":"all the courts and judges of a country","c":"司法體系","s":"Many people believe that the judicial system should treat the rich and the poor in exactly the same way under the law.","t":"許多人認為司法體系應該在法律之下以完全相同的方式對待富人和窮人。"},{"w":"jug","p":"n.","d":"a container with a handle and a lip for holding and pouring liquids","c":"水壺；壺","s":"Mom filled a large jug with cold lemon tea and put it on the table so everyone could pour a glass whenever they liked.","t":"媽媽把一個大水壺裝滿冰檸檬茶放在桌上，讓大家想喝的時候可以隨時倒一杯。","h":1},{"w":"a jug of","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of liquid that fills a jug","c":"一壺…","s":"The waiter brought us a jug of water with ice and lemon slices before we had even looked at the menu.","t":"我們還沒看菜單，服務生就為我們送來一壺加了冰塊和檸檬片的水。"},{"w":"milk jug","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small container for serving milk, used with tea or coffee","c":"牛奶壺","s":"Grandma's tea set includes six cups, a teapot, a sugar bowl, and a tiny milk jug painted with blue flowers.","t":"奶奶的茶具組包括六個杯子、一個茶壺、一個糖罐和一個畫著藍色小花的小牛奶壺。"},{"w":"jury","p":"n.","d":"a group of ordinary people in a court who decide whether someone is guilty","c":"陪審團","s":"After listening to the evidence for five days, the jury decided that the young man was not guilty of stealing the car.","t":"聽了五天的證據後，陪審團判定那名年輕男子沒有偷車的罪。","h":1},{"w":"juror","p":"n.","d":"one of the members of a jury","c":"陪審員","s":"Each juror must promise to listen to the facts carefully and not to talk about the case with family or friends.","t":"每位陪審員都必須承諾仔細聆聽事實，並且不和家人或朋友討論案件。"},{"w":"serve on a jury","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be a member of a jury in a court case","c":"擔任陪審員","s":"My uncle had to take a week off work to serve on a jury in a case about a car accident in the city center.","t":"我叔叔必須請一週的假去擔任陪審員，審理一件市中心的車禍案。"},{"w":"the jury is still out","p":"phr.","d":"people have not yet decided whether something is good or true","c":"尚無定論","s":"Some teachers love the new online textbooks, but the jury is still out on whether they really help students learn better than paper books.","t":"有些老師很喜歡新的線上教科書，但它們是否真的比紙本書更能幫助學生學習，尚無定論。"},{"w":"justify","p":"v.","d":"to give a good reason for something","c":"為…辯護；證明…有理","s":"Kevin tried to justify being late again by blaming the heavy traffic, but his boss had seen him at the coffee shop.","t":"凱文又遲到了，他試圖以交通繁忙來辯解，但他的老闆早就在咖啡店看到他了。","h":1},{"w":"justified","p":"adj.","d":"having a good reason; fair and reasonable","c":"有正當理由的；合理的","s":"The teacher's anger was justified, because three students had copied their whole report from the same website.","t":"老師的生氣是有道理的，因為有三個學生從同一個網站抄了整篇報告。"},{"w":"justification","p":"n.","d":"a good reason for doing something","c":"正當理由","s":"There is no justification for hitting a child, no matter how badly he or she has behaved at home or at school.","t":"無論孩子在家或在學校表現得多糟，打小孩都沒有任何正當理由。"},{"w":"justice","p":"n.","d":"fair treatment of people according to the law","c":"正義；公正","s":"The family of the victim waited ten years for justice, and they cried with relief when the criminal was finally sent to prison.","t":"受害者的家人等了十年才等到正義，當罪犯終於被送進監獄時，他們如釋重負地哭了。"},{"w":"unjustified","p":"adj.","d":"not fair or reasonable; without a good reason","c":"不合理的；無正當理由的","s":"The fine was completely unjustified because the parking sign was hidden behind a tree and nobody could see it.","t":"這張罰單完全不合理，因為停車標誌藏在樹後面，沒有人看得到。"},{"w":"juvenile","p":"adj.","d":"connected with young people who are not yet adults","c":"青少年的；少年的","s":"The number of juvenile crimes has dropped in our city since the government opened more free sports centers for teenagers.","t":"自從政府為青少年開設更多免費運動中心後，我們城市的少年犯罪數量已經下降。","h":1},{"w":"juvenile","p":"n.","d":"a young person who is not yet an adult","c":"青少年；未成年人","s":"Under the law, a juvenile who steals cannot be sent to an adult prison and must be given a chance to change.","t":"依照法律，偷竊的未成年人不能被送進成人監獄，而且必須給他改過的機會。"},{"w":"juvenile court","p":"n.phr.","d":"a special court that deals with crimes committed by young people","c":"少年法庭","s":"The fifteen-year-old boy who broke the shop window will appear in juvenile court, where the judge may order him to do community service.","t":"那個打破商店櫥窗的十五歲男孩將出席少年法庭，法官可能會判他做社區服務。"},{"w":"juvenile delinquency","p":"n.phr.","d":"crime or bad behavior by young people","c":"青少年犯罪","s":"Many experts believe that strong family support and good schools are the best ways to prevent juvenile delinquency in big cities.","t":"許多專家認為，強大的家庭支持和良好的學校是預防大城市青少年犯罪的最好方法。"},{"w":"kidnap, kidnapped, kidnapped","p":"v.","d":"to take someone away by force, usually to get money","c":"綁架","s":"In the movie, three men kidnapped the rich man's son and asked for a million dollars, but the boy cleverly escaped.","t":"電影裡，三個男人綁架了富翁的兒子並索求一百萬美元，但男孩機智地逃走了。","a":"kidnapped","h":1},{"w":"kidnapper","p":"n.","d":"a person who kidnaps someone","c":"綁匪","s":"The police caught the kidnapper within two days because a shop camera had recorded his car and its license plate.","t":"警方在兩天內抓到了綁匪，因為一家商店的攝影機拍到了他的車和車牌。"},{"w":"kidnapping","p":"n.","d":"the crime of taking someone away by force","c":"綁架（罪）","s":"The kidnapping of the famous singer's dog made the news in many countries, and fans offered a big reward for its return.","t":"那位知名歌手的狗被綁架的事件在許多國家成為新聞，粉絲們懸賞高額獎金尋狗。"},{"w":"landlord","p":"n.","d":"a man who owns a house or apartment and rents it to others","c":"房東（男）","s":"When the water heater stopped working, I called my landlord, and he sent someone to fix it the very next morning.","t":"熱水器壞掉時，我打電話給我的房東，他隔天早上就派人來修理了。","h":1},{"w":"landlady","p":"n.","d":"a woman who owns a house or apartment and rents it to others","c":"房東（女）","s":"Our landlady lives downstairs, and she often brings us homemade dumplings during the Chinese New Year holiday.","t":"我們的女房東住在樓下，農曆新年假期時她常常帶自己做的水餃給我們。"},{"w":"land","p":"n.","d":"an area of ground, especially one used for farming or building","c":"土地","s":"My grandparents own a small piece of land in the countryside, where they grow vegetables and keep a few chickens.","t":"我的祖父母在鄉下擁有一小塊土地，他們在那裡種菜並養幾隻雞。"},{"w":"landowner","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns land","c":"地主","s":"The landowner agreed to let the village children play soccer on his field as long as they did not damage the fence.","t":"那位地主同意讓村裡的孩子在他的田地上踢足球，只要他們不弄壞圍欄。"},{"w":"laser","p":"n.","d":"a machine that produces a very narrow, strong beam of light","c":"雷射","s":"The doctor used a laser to remove the small dark spot on my aunt's face, and the whole treatment took only ten minutes.","t":"醫生用雷射去除我阿姨臉上的小黑斑，整個治療只花了十分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"laser printer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a printer that uses a laser to produce clear text and pictures","c":"雷射印表機","s":"Our office bought a new laser printer last month, and now we can print fifty pages of the report in less than two minutes.","t":"我們辦公室上個月買了一台新的雷射印表機，現在不到兩分鐘就能印出五十頁報告。"},{"w":"laser surgery","p":"n.phr.","d":"a medical operation that uses a laser instead of a knife","c":"雷射手術","s":"My father had laser surgery on his eyes last year, so he no longer needs the thick glasses he had worn for twenty years.","t":"我爸爸去年做了眼睛的雷射手術，所以他不再需要戴那副戴了二十年的厚眼鏡。"},{"w":"laser beam","p":"n.phr.","d":"a narrow line of light produced by a laser","c":"雷射光束","s":"At the concert, green laser beams crossed the dark sky above the stage while the band played its most famous song.","t":"演唱會上，綠色的雷射光束在舞台上方的黑暗天空中交錯，樂團則演奏著他們最有名的歌。","a":"laser beams"},{"w":"lawmaker","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes laws, such as a member of a parliament","c":"立法者；立法委員","s":"Hundreds of parents wrote letters to every lawmaker in the country, asking for a law that would make school lunches healthier.","t":"數百位家長寫信給全國每一位立法委員，要求制定讓學校午餐更健康的法律。","h":1},{"w":"law","p":"n.","d":"a rule made by the government that everyone must follow","c":"法律","s":"According to the new law, drivers who use their phones at the wheel will have to pay a fine of three thousand dollars.","t":"根據新法律，開車時使用手機的駕駛人必須繳三千元罰款。"},{"w":"lawyer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to advise people about the law and speak for them in court","c":"律師","s":"Before signing the contract for the new apartment, my parents asked a lawyer to read every page and explain the difficult parts.","t":"簽新公寓合約前，我爸媽請一位律師閱讀每一頁並解釋困難的部分。"},{"w":"lawful","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by the law","c":"合法的","s":"It is lawful to park here after seven in the evening, but during the day the space is reserved for delivery trucks.","t":"晚上七點以後在這裡停車是合法的，但白天這個位置是保留給送貨卡車的。"},{"w":"break the law","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something that the law does not allow","c":"違法","s":"If you download movies from illegal websites, you break the law, even though you may think nobody will ever find out.","t":"如果你從非法網站下載電影，你就是在違法，即使你可能以為沒有人會發現。"},{"w":"lawsuit","p":"n.","d":"a problem or complaint that a person brings to a court of law","c":"訴訟；官司","s":"The company lost the lawsuit and had to pay millions of dollars to customers whose phones had caught fire while charging.","t":"這家公司輸了官司，必須賠償數百萬美元給手機充電時起火的顧客。","h":1},{"w":"file a lawsuit","p":"v.phr.","d":"to officially start a legal case against someone","c":"提出訴訟","s":"Several angry parents decided to file a lawsuit against the toy maker after their children were hurt by the sharp plastic pieces.","t":"幾位憤怒的家長在孩子被尖銳塑膠片弄傷後，決定對玩具製造商提出訴訟。"},{"w":"sue","p":"v.","d":"to take legal action against someone to get money from them","c":"控告；提告","s":"The famous actor said he would sue the magazine for printing a false story about his family and his private life.","t":"這位知名演員說他會控告那家雜誌刊登關於他家庭和私生活的虛假報導。"},{"w":"suit","p":"n.","d":"a case brought to a court of law","c":"訴訟（＝lawsuit）","s":"The singer brought a suit against her former manager, claiming that he had kept most of the money from her concerts.","t":"這位歌手對她的前經紀人提起訴訟，聲稱他拿走了她演唱會大部分的收入。"}]},{"unit":21,"theme":"layer – massive","cards":[{"w":"layer","p":"n.","d":"a thin sheet of something that lies on top of or under another","c":"層","s":"In winter it is smart to wear several thin layers of clothing, because you can take one off whenever you feel too warm.","t":"冬天穿好幾層薄衣服是明智的，因為只要覺得太熱，你就可以脫掉一件。","a":"layers","h":1},{"w":"layer","p":"v.","d":"to arrange something in layers","c":"把…分層放置","s":"To make the cake, you layer the cream and the strawberries between the pieces of sponge, and then you cover the top with chocolate.","t":"做這個蛋糕時，你把奶油和草莓一層層鋪在海綿蛋糕之間，然後在最上面蓋上巧克力。"},{"w":"ozone layer","p":"n.phr.","d":"the layer of gas high in the sky that protects the earth from the sun's harmful rays","c":"臭氧層","s":"Scientists warned that chemicals from old refrigerators were making a hole in the ozone layer, so many countries agreed to stop using them.","t":"科學家警告說舊冰箱的化學物質正在臭氧層上造成破洞，所以許多國家同意停止使用它們。"},{"w":"layered","p":"adj.","d":"made of several layers","c":"分層的；多層的","s":"My sister asked the hairdresser for a layered haircut, because she wanted her thick hair to look lighter and easier to dry.","t":"我姐姐請髮型師剪層次髮型，因為她希望自己的厚頭髮看起來更輕盈、更容易吹乾。"},{"w":"league","p":"n.","d":"a group of sports teams that play against each other","c":"聯盟；聯賽","s":"Our school basketball team joined the city league this year, so we play a match against another school every Saturday afternoon.","t":"我們學校的籃球隊今年加入了市聯賽，所以每週六下午都要和另一所學校比賽。","h":1},{"w":"major league","p":"n.phr.","d":"the highest level of professional baseball in the United States","c":"大聯盟","s":"Several Taiwanese pitchers have played in the major league, and their games are shown on TV early in the morning here.","t":"有幾位台灣投手曾在大聯盟打球，他們的比賽在這裡會在清晨的電視上播出。"},{"w":"in a league of one's own","p":"phr.","d":"much better than everyone else","c":"出類拔萃；無人能及","s":"When it comes to cooking beef noodles, my grandmother is in a league of her own, and even famous chefs have asked for her recipe.","t":"說到煮牛肉麵，我奶奶無人能及，連名廚都向她要過食譜。","a":"in a league of her own"},{"w":"out of one's league","p":"adj.phr.","d":"too good or too expensive for someone","c":"高攀不上；超出能力範圍","s":"That sports car is completely out of my league, so I will keep riding my old scooter until I find a much better job.","t":"那輛跑車完全超出我的能力範圍，所以在找到更好的工作之前，我會繼續騎我的舊機車。","a":"out of my league"},{"w":"legacy","p":"n.","d":"money or property that you leave to someone when you die","c":"遺產","s":"My great-aunt left a small legacy to the village library, which used the money to buy new books for children.","t":"我的姑婆留了一筆小遺產給村裡的圖書館，圖書館用這筆錢為孩子們買了新書。","h":1},{"w":"legacy","p":"n.","d":"something that continues to exist as a result of past events or people","c":"留給後世的影響；傳承","s":"The legacy of the old teacher lives on, because many of her students became teachers and now use her methods in their own classrooms.","t":"這位老教師留下的影響持續存在，因為她的許多學生成為老師，現在在自己的教室裡使用她的方法。"},{"w":"leave a legacy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave something behind that people will remember or benefit from","c":"留下遺澤；留下深遠影響","s":"The famous scientist hoped to leave a legacy of clean energy, so she gave all her research to the public for free.","t":"這位著名的科學家希望留下乾淨能源的遺澤，所以她把所有研究免費公開給大眾。"},{"w":"legendary","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and admired, especially over a long time","c":"傳奇的；極有名的","s":"The legendary singer gave her last concert at the age of eighty, and fans flew in from all over the world to hear her.","t":"這位傳奇的歌手在八十歲時舉辦了最後一場演唱會，粉絲從世界各地飛來聽她演唱。","h":1},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"an old story about people and events that may not be true","c":"傳說","s":"According to an old legend, a dragon sleeps under the lake, and the water turns warm whenever it breathes.","t":"根據一個古老的傳說，一條龍睡在湖底，每當牠呼吸時湖水就會變暖。"},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"a very famous person, especially in sports or entertainment","c":"傳奇人物","s":"The basketball legend visited our school and told us that he had failed to make the team in junior high.","t":"這位籃球傳奇人物來我們學校訪問，告訴我們他國中時曾經沒被選進校隊。"},{"w":"living legend","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is very famous while still alive","c":"活傳奇","s":"At ninety, the pianist is a living legend, and young musicians still travel hundreds of miles to take a single lesson with him.","t":"九十歲的這位鋼琴家是個活傳奇，年輕音樂家仍然長途跋涉數百英里只為上他一堂課。"},{"w":"legislation","p":"n.","d":"a law or set of laws made by a government","c":"法律；立法","s":"New legislation that bans smoking in all parks will take effect next month, and people who break it will be fined.","t":"禁止在所有公園吸菸的新法律將於下個月生效，違反者將被罰款。","h":1},{"w":"legislative","p":"adj.","d":"connected with making laws","c":"立法的","s":"The legislative body of Taiwan is called the Legislative Yuan, and its members are elected by the people every four years.","t":"台灣的立法機關叫做立法院，其成員每四年由人民選出。","h":1},{"w":"legislate","p":"v.","d":"to make a law or laws","c":"立法","s":"Many parents want the government to legislate against junk food in schools, so that students eat healthier lunches.","t":"許多家長希望政府立法禁止學校裡的垃圾食物，讓學生吃更健康的午餐。"},{"w":"legislator","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes laws","c":"立法者；立法委員","s":"A local legislator visited our class today and explained how an idea becomes a law in Taiwan step by step.","t":"一位本地的立法委員今天來我們班上，一步步解釋在台灣一個想法如何變成法律。"},{"w":"legislature","p":"n.","d":"the group of people who make laws for a country or state","c":"立法機關","s":"The state legislature voted to raise the minimum wage, and the new rule will help thousands of part-time workers.","t":"州立法機關投票通過提高最低工資，這項新規定將幫助數千名兼職工作者。"},{"w":"legitimate","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by law; fair and reasonable","c":"合法的；正當的","s":"The shop asked for my ID before selling me the phone, which is a legitimate request because many stolen cards are used online.","t":"商店在賣手機給我之前要求看我的身分證，這是個正當的要求，因為網路上有很多被盜的卡片被使用。","h":1},{"w":"legitimately","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is legal or reasonable","c":"合法地；正當地","s":"The company won the contract legitimately, because it offered the lowest price and the best design in an open competition.","t":"這家公司正當地贏得了合約，因為它在公開競爭中提供了最低的價格和最好的設計。"},{"w":"illegitimate","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed by law or by the rules","c":"不合法的；不正當的","s":"Using a fake doctor's note to skip the exam is an illegitimate excuse, and the school will punish anyone who tries it.","t":"用假的醫生證明來逃避考試是不正當的藉口，學校會處罰任何嘗試這麼做的人。"},{"w":"legitimacy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being legal, fair, or acceptable","c":"合法性；正當性","s":"After the election, some people questioned the legitimacy of the result, so the votes were counted again in front of reporters.","t":"選舉後，有些人質疑結果的正當性，所以選票在記者面前重新計算了一次。"},{"w":"lest","p":"conj.","d":"in order to prevent something bad from happening; for fear that","c":"以免；唯恐","s":"Grandma held the little boy's hand tightly on the stairs lest he should slip and hurt himself on the hard steps.","t":"奶奶在樓梯上緊緊握著小男孩的手，以免他滑倒，在堅硬的階梯上受傷。","h":1},{"w":"as though","p":"conj.","d":"in a way that suggests something is true, even if it is not","c":"好像；彷彿","s":"My cousin talks as though he knew everything about cars, but he has never even changed a flat tire by himself.","t":"我表哥說話好像他對汽車無所不知，但他甚至從來沒有自己換過一個爆胎。"},{"w":"even if","p":"conj.","d":"used to say that something will not change what happens","c":"即使；就算","s":"We will still have the picnic on Saturday even if it rains a little, because the park has a big covered area with tables.","t":"即使下點小雨，我們星期六還是會辦野餐，因為公園有一個很大的有頂棚區域，還有桌子。"},{"w":"so that","p":"conj.","d":"in order that; with the result that","c":"以便；為了","s":"My father gets up at five every morning so that he can exercise in the park before the summer heat begins.","t":"我爸爸每天早上五點起床，以便在夏天的酷熱開始前到公園運動。"},{"w":"liability","p":"n.","d":"legal responsibility for something, especially for paying money","c":"（法律）責任","s":"The sign says that the parking lot has no liability for stolen items, so never leave your laptop in the car.","t":"告示上寫著停車場對失竊物品不負任何責任，所以絕對不要把筆電留在車上。","h":1},{"w":"liability","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that causes problems for others","c":"累贅；負擔","s":"The old printer has become a liability to the office, because it breaks down almost every week and wastes everyone's time.","t":"這台舊印表機已經成為辦公室的累贅，因為它幾乎每週都壞掉，浪費大家的時間。"},{"w":"liable","p":"adj.","d":"legally responsible for something","c":"負有法律責任的","s":"Parents are liable for any damage their children cause in the store, so please keep an eye on your kids.","t":"父母對孩子在店裡造成的任何損壞負有法律責任，所以請看好你的小孩。"},{"w":"be liable to","p":"adj.phr.","d":"likely to do or experience something, usually something bad","c":"容易…；有…傾向","s":"People who skip breakfast are liable to feel tired and hungry by ten o'clock, and then they often buy unhealthy snacks.","t":"不吃早餐的人容易在十點前感到又累又餓，然後他們常常買不健康的零食。","a":"are liable to"},{"w":"likelihood","p":"n.","d":"the chance that something will happen","c":"可能性","s":"The weather report says there is a strong likelihood of snow tonight, so the school may be closed tomorrow morning.","t":"氣象報告說今晚下雪的可能性很高，所以學校明天早上可能會停課。","h":1},{"w":"likely","p":"adj.","d":"probable; expected to happen","c":"可能的；很有可能的","s":"It is likely that the concert will be moved indoors, since the typhoon is expected to arrive on Saturday evening.","t":"演唱會很有可能會移到室內舉行，因為颱風預計週六晚上到達。"},{"w":"likely","p":"adv.","d":"probably","c":"很可能地","s":"The bus will likely be late again this morning, so we had better leave the house ten minutes earlier than usual.","t":"公車今天早上很可能又會晚到，所以我們最好比平常提早十分鐘出門。"},{"w":"unlikely","p":"adj.","d":"not probable; not expected to happen","c":"不太可能的","s":"It is unlikely that we will finish the project today, because two members of our group are sick at home.","t":"我們今天不太可能完成這個專案，因為我們組裡有兩個成員在家生病。"},{"w":"in all likelihood","p":"phr.","d":"very probably","c":"十之八九；極有可能","s":"In all likelihood, the museum will be crowded on Sunday afternoon, so let us go early in the morning when it opens.","t":"十之八九博物館週日下午會很擁擠，所以我們早上一開門就去吧。","a":"In all likelihood"},{"w":"likewise","p":"adv.","d":"in the same way; also","c":"同樣地；也","s":"My sister decided to study abroad after high school, and her best friend, who shares all her dreams, did likewise.","t":"我姐姐決定高中畢業後出國留學，而和她有著相同夢想的好朋友也同樣地這麼做了。","h":1},{"w":"alike","p":"adj.","d":"very similar","c":"相似的；相像的","s":"The twins look so much alike that even their teachers mix them up, especially when they wear the same uniform.","t":"這對雙胞胎長得非常相像，連老師都會搞混，尤其是當他們穿同樣的制服時。"},{"w":"alike","p":"adv.","d":"in the same way; equally","c":"同樣地；一樣地","s":"The new park is loved by children and adults alike, because it has both a playground and quiet paths for walking.","t":"新公園受到小孩和大人同樣的喜愛，因為它既有遊樂場也有安靜的散步小徑。"},{"w":"likeness","p":"n.","d":"the fact of being similar in appearance","c":"相似；相像","s":"There is a strong likeness between my mother and her grandmother in the old photo, from the eyes to the shape of the smile.","t":"在那張舊照片裡，我媽媽和她的外婆有很強的相似之處，從眼睛到微笑的形狀都是。"},{"w":"loop","p":"n.","d":"a shape like a circle made by a line curving back on itself","c":"環；圈","s":"To tie your shoelaces, make a loop with one lace, wrap the other around it, and pull it through the hole.","t":"要綁鞋帶，先用一條鞋帶做一個圈，再把另一條繞過去，然後從洞裡拉出來。","h":1},{"w":"loop","p":"v.","d":"to form something into a circle, or to go around in a circle","c":"繞成圈；環繞","s":"The hiking trail will loop around the lake and bring you back to the parking lot in about two hours.","t":"這條登山步道會環繞湖泊一圈，大約兩小時後把你帶回停車場。"},{"w":"in the loop","p":"phr.","d":"informed about what is happening","c":"知道內情的；掌握最新消息的","s":"Please keep me in the loop about the school trip, because I will be on vacation when the final plan is announced.","t":"請讓我隨時掌握校外教學的消息，因為最終計畫公布時我正在度假。"},{"w":"out of the loop","p":"phr.","d":"not informed about what is happening","c":"不知情的；狀況外的","s":"After a month in the hospital, Jack felt completely out of the loop, and he did not even know that his class had a new teacher.","t":"住院一個月後，傑克覺得完全狀況外，他甚至不知道他們班換了新老師。"},{"w":"lounge","p":"n.","d":"a comfortable room for sitting and relaxing in a hotel, airport, or home","c":"休息室；交誼廳","s":"The hotel lounge has soft sofas and free coffee, so many guests sit there to read the newspaper after breakfast.","t":"飯店的交誼廳有柔軟的沙發和免費咖啡，所以許多客人早餐後坐在那裡看報紙。","h":1},{"w":"lounge","p":"v.","d":"to sit or lie in a relaxed, lazy way","c":"懶洋洋地躺著／坐著","s":"On Sunday mornings my cat and I like to lounge on the sofa and watch the rain fall outside the window.","t":"星期天早上我和我的貓喜歡懶洋洋地窩在沙發上，看窗外的雨落下。"},{"w":"departure lounge","p":"n.phr.","d":"the area in an airport where passengers wait before getting on a plane","c":"候機室","s":"Our flight was delayed for three hours, so we sat in the departure lounge and played cards to pass the time.","t":"我們的航班延誤了三個小時，所以我們坐在候機室裡玩牌打發時間。"},{"w":"lounge around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spend time relaxing and doing nothing","c":"閒晃；懶散地消磨時間","s":"Instead of helping with the housework, my brother likes to lounge around all weekend with his phone in his hand.","t":"我哥哥不幫忙做家事，反而喜歡整個週末手拿著手機閒晃。"},{"w":"lump","p":"n.","d":"a piece of something solid without a particular shape","c":"塊；腫塊","s":"There was a hard lump of sugar at the bottom of the jar, so Mom broke it up with a spoon before making tea.","t":"罐子底部有一塊硬掉的糖，所以媽媽泡茶前先用湯匙把它弄碎。","h":1},{"w":"lump","p":"v.","d":"to put different things together in one group","c":"把…歸為一類","s":"It is unfair to lump all teenagers together as lazy, because many of them study hard and work part-time as well.","t":"把所有青少年歸為懶惰的一類是不公平的，因為他們當中許多人既努力讀書也兼職工作。"},{"w":"a lump of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a piece of something, especially one with no clear shape","c":"一塊…","s":"The sculptor started with a lump of clay the size of a football and slowly turned it into a sleeping cat.","t":"雕塑家從一塊足球大小的黏土開始，慢慢把它變成一隻睡著的貓。"},{"w":"a lump in one's throat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tight feeling in your throat because you are about to cry","c":"哽咽","s":"When the whole class sang happy birthday to the old teacher, she had a lump in her throat and could not speak for a moment.","t":"當全班為老教師唱生日快樂歌時，她哽咽了，一時說不出話來。","a":"a lump in her throat"},{"w":"lump sum","p":"n.phr.","d":"a single large payment made at one time","c":"一次付清的款項","s":"Instead of monthly payments, the company paid the retired worker a lump sum of two million dollars.","t":"公司不是按月付款，而是一次付給那位退休員工兩百萬元的整筆款項。"},{"w":"mainstream","p":"n.","d":"the ideas and ways of living that are accepted by most people","c":"主流","s":"Electric cars were once seen as strange, but they have now entered the mainstream, and you see them on every street.","t":"電動車曾經被視為奇怪的東西，但現在它們已經進入主流，每條街上都看得到。","h":1},{"w":"mainstream","p":"adj.","d":"accepted or used by most people","c":"主流的","s":"Jazz is not very popular with teenagers today, but mainstream pop music still borrows many of its sounds and rhythms.","t":"爵士樂在今天的青少年中不太流行，但主流流行音樂仍然借用了它的許多聲音和節奏。"},{"w":"mainstream media","p":"n.phr.","d":"the main newspapers and TV stations that most people read or watch","c":"主流媒體","s":"The story first appeared on a small blog, and only two days later did the mainstream media start to report it.","t":"這個故事最早出現在一個小部落格上，兩天後主流媒體才開始報導。"},{"w":"mainstream","p":"v.","d":"to make something part of what most people accept or use","c":"使成為主流","s":"Over the last ten years, online shopping has been mainstreamed so completely that even my grandmother buys her tea on the Internet.","t":"過去十年來，網路購物已經完全成為主流，連我奶奶都在網路上買茶葉。","a":"mainstreamed"},{"w":"maintenance","p":"n.","d":"the work of keeping something in good condition","c":"維修；保養","s":"The elevator is closed for maintenance this morning, so please use the stairs if you need to go to the fifth floor.","t":"電梯今天早上因保養而關閉，所以如果你需要到五樓，請走樓梯。","h":1},{"w":"maintain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in good condition","c":"維護；保養","s":"If you maintain your bicycle well by oiling the chain and checking the tires, it will last for many years.","t":"如果你好好保養腳踏車，給鏈條上油並檢查輪胎，它可以用很多年。"},{"w":"maintain","p":"v.","d":"to make something continue at the same level","c":"維持；保持","s":"It is hard to maintain a healthy weight during the holidays, when every table is covered with cakes and fried food.","t":"假期期間很難維持健康的體重，因為每張桌子上都擺滿了蛋糕和油炸食物。"},{"w":"low-maintenance","p":"adj.","d":"needing very little care or work","c":"不需太多照顧的；低維護的","s":"Cactus plants are low-maintenance, so they are perfect for busy students who forget to water their plants for weeks.","t":"仙人掌是不需太多照顧的植物，所以非常適合會好幾週忘記澆水的忙碌學生。"},{"w":"mammal","p":"n.","d":"an animal that feeds its babies with milk from the mother's body","c":"哺乳動物","s":"A whale is not a fish but a mammal, because it breathes air and feeds its babies with milk just as humans do.","t":"鯨魚不是魚，而是哺乳動物，因為牠呼吸空氣，而且像人類一樣用乳汁餵養寶寶。","h":1},{"w":"marine mammal","p":"n.phr.","d":"a mammal that lives in the sea, such as a dolphin or seal","c":"海洋哺乳動物","s":"Dolphins are the most intelligent marine mammals in the ocean, and they can learn to understand more than sixty hand signals.","t":"海豚是海洋中最聰明的海洋哺乳動物，牠們能學會理解六十多種手勢。","a":"marine mammals"},{"w":"mammalian","p":"adj.","d":"connected with mammals","c":"哺乳動物的","s":"All mammalian babies drink their mother's milk, which is why a newborn kitten searches for its mother right after birth.","t":"所有哺乳動物的寶寶都喝母乳，這就是為什麼剛出生的小貓一生下來就會尋找媽媽。"},{"w":"mandate","p":"n.","d":"the authority to do something, given by the people through an election","c":"授權；委託","s":"After winning seventy percent of the votes, the new mayor said she had a clear mandate to build more bike lanes.","t":"贏得七成選票後，新市長表示她獲得了明確的授權來建造更多自行車道。","h":1},{"w":"mandate","p":"n.","d":"an official order to do something","c":"命令；指令","s":"The school received a mandate from the government to install air conditioners in every classroom before the summer.","t":"學校收到政府的指令，要在夏天前在每間教室安裝冷氣。"},{"w":"mandate","p":"v.","d":"to officially order something to be done","c":"強制規定","s":"The new law will mandate that every car has a camera, which will help the police find out who caused an accident.","t":"新法律將強制規定每輛車都要有行車紀錄器，這將幫助警方查出是誰造成事故。"},{"w":"mandatory","p":"adj.","d":"required by law or rules; compulsory","c":"強制的；義務的","s":"Wearing a helmet is mandatory for everyone who rides a scooter in Taiwan, and the fine for breaking the rule is 500 dollars.","t":"在台灣，所有騎機車的人都必須戴安全帽，違規的罰款是五百元。"},{"w":"manifest","p":"v.","d":"to show something clearly, especially a feeling or quality","c":"顯示；表明","s":"Her love for animals began to manifest itself when she was five, because she brought home every lost cat in the neighborhood.","t":"她對動物的愛在五歲時就開始顯現出來，因為她把附近每一隻走失的貓都帶回家。","h":1},{"w":"manifest","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see or understand; obvious","c":"明顯的；顯而易見的","s":"The boy's manifest joy at seeing the puppy made everyone in the room smile, and his mother finally agreed to keep it.","t":"男孩看到小狗時明顯的喜悅讓房間裡的每個人都微笑了，他媽媽終於同意留下牠。"},{"w":"manifestation","p":"n.","d":"a sign or event that shows something clearly","c":"表現；顯現","s":"The long lines outside the new bakery are a clear manifestation of how much people in this town love fresh bread.","t":"新麵包店外排的長隊清楚表現出這個鎮上的人有多喜愛新鮮麵包。"},{"w":"manifest itself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to appear or become easy to see","c":"顯現出來","s":"Stress can manifest itself in many ways, such as headaches, poor sleep, or getting angry over very small things.","t":"壓力可以用許多方式顯現出來，例如頭痛、睡不好，或是為非常小的事情生氣。"},{"w":"manipulate","p":"v.","d":"to control or influence someone in a clever and unfair way","c":"操縱；操控","s":"Some advertisements try to manipulate children into wanting toys by showing happy kids who seem to have everything.","t":"有些廣告試圖透過展示看似擁有一切的快樂孩子，來操控小孩想要玩具。","h":1},{"w":"manipulate","p":"v.","d":"to handle or control something skillfully with your hands or a machine","c":"熟練地操作","s":"The surgeon can manipulate the tiny robot arms with great care, so the cut on the patient is only one centimeter long.","t":"外科醫生能非常小心地操作那些微小的機械手臂，所以病人身上的切口只有一公分長。"},{"w":"manipulation","p":"n.","d":"the act of controlling someone or something in a clever or unfair way","c":"操縱；操控","s":"The judge said the old man had been a victim of manipulation, because the salesman had tricked him into signing the contract.","t":"法官說這位老先生是操縱的受害者，因為那個推銷員騙他簽了合約。"},{"w":"manipulative","p":"adj.","d":"trying to control people in a clever and unfair way","c":"善於操控他人的","s":"Her manipulative friend always cried whenever she did not get her way, so the other girls finally stopped spending time with her.","t":"她那位善於操控別人的朋友每次不如意就哭，所以其他女孩最後不再和她來往了。"},{"w":"mansion","p":"n.","d":"a very large and expensive house","c":"大宅；豪宅","s":"The movie star lives in a mansion with twenty rooms and a swimming pool, but she says it often feels too quiet and empty.","t":"這位電影明星住在一棟有二十個房間和一座游泳池的豪宅裡，但她說那裡常常感覺太安靜、太空蕩。","h":1},{"w":"luxury mansion","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very large house with expensive furniture and equipment","c":"豪華大宅","s":"The luxury mansion on the hill has its own cinema and tennis court, and it was sold last month for over 300 million dollars.","t":"山丘上那棟豪華大宅有自己的電影院和網球場，上個月以超過三億元的價格賣出。"},{"w":"live in a mansion","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a very large and expensive house as your home","c":"住在豪宅裡","s":"My little brother dreams of becoming a famous singer so that he can live in a mansion with a garden full of dogs.","t":"我弟弟夢想成為知名歌手，這樣他就可以住在豪宅裡，還有一座養滿狗的花園。"},{"w":"marine","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the sea and the creatures that live in it","c":"海洋的","s":"Plastic bags are a serious danger to marine animals, because sea turtles often mistake them for jellyfish and eat them.","t":"塑膠袋對海洋動物是嚴重的危險，因為海龜常常把它們誤認為水母而吃下去。","h":1},{"w":"marine","p":"n.","d":"a soldier who is trained to fight both on land and at sea","c":"海軍陸戰隊員","s":"My cousin served as a marine for four years, and he learned to swim long distances in cold water carrying a heavy pack.","t":"我表哥當了四年海軍陸戰隊員，他學會了背著沉重的背包在冷水中長距離游泳。"},{"w":"marine life","p":"n.phr.","d":"the plants and animals that live in the sea","c":"海洋生物","s":"The glass-bottom boat lets visitors watch the colorful marine life of the coral reef without getting wet at all.","t":"玻璃底船讓遊客可以觀賞珊瑚礁色彩繽紛的海洋生物，完全不用弄濕身體。"},{"w":"submarine","p":"n.","d":"a ship that can travel under the water","c":"潛水艇","s":"The submarine stayed under the sea for three months, and the sailors did not see the sun during the whole trip.","t":"這艘潛水艇在海底待了三個月，水手們在整個航程中都沒有看到太陽。"},{"w":"masculine","p":"adj.","d":"having qualities that are thought to be typical of men","c":"男性的；陽剛的","s":"In the past, a deep voice and a strong body were seen as masculine qualities, but ideas about men have changed a lot.","t":"過去，低沉的嗓音和強壯的身體被視為陽剛的特質，但人們對男性的看法已經改變很多。","h":1},{"w":"masculinity","p":"n.","d":"the qualities that are thought to be typical of men","c":"男子氣概","s":"Some boys think that crying is a sign of weak masculinity, but doctors say that showing feelings is healthy for everyone.","t":"有些男孩認為哭泣是男子氣概不足的表現，但醫生說表達感受對每個人都有益健康。"},{"w":"feminine","p":"adj.","d":"having qualities that are thought to be typical of women","c":"女性的；陰柔的","s":"The designer mixed soft, feminine colors like pink and cream with strong black lines to create a very modern dress.","t":"設計師把粉紅和奶油色等柔和、女性化的顏色和強烈的黑色線條混合，創造出一件非常現代的洋裝。"},{"w":"massage","p":"n.","d":"the action of pressing and rubbing someone's body to relax the muscles","c":"按摩","s":"After running the marathon, my uncle went for a one-hour massage to relax his tired legs and sore back.","t":"跑完馬拉松後，我叔叔去做了一小時的按摩，放鬆他疲憊的雙腿和酸痛的背部。","h":1},{"w":"massage","p":"v.","d":"to press and rub someone's body to relax the muscles","c":"按摩","s":"Every night my grandmother asks me to massage her shoulders for ten minutes, because they hurt after a day of gardening.","t":"每天晚上我奶奶都要我幫她按摩肩膀十分鐘，因為做了一整天園藝後肩膀很痛。"},{"w":"give sb a massage","p":"v.phr.","d":"to massage someone","c":"替某人按摩","s":"The trainer will give the player a massage before the game so that his muscles are warm and ready for the big match.","t":"教練會在比賽前替球員按摩，讓他的肌肉暖和起來，為大賽做好準備。","a":"give the player a massage"},{"w":"foot massage","p":"n.phr.","d":"a massage of the feet","c":"腳底按摩","s":"Many tourists in Taipei try a foot massage after a long day of walking, even though it can be quite painful at first.","t":"許多在台北的觀光客走了一整天後會去做腳底按摩，即使一開始可能相當痛。"},{"w":"massive","p":"adj.","d":"very large, heavy, or serious","c":"巨大的；大規模的","s":"A massive rock fell onto the mountain road during the typhoon, and it took the workers two days to clear the way.","t":"颱風期間一塊巨大的岩石落到山路上，工人花了兩天才把路清開。","h":1},{"w":"massively","p":"adv.","d":"very much; to a very great degree","c":"大規模地；極度地","s":"The price of eggs has risen massively this year, so many breakfast shops now charge more for a simple egg sandwich.","t":"今年雞蛋價格大幅上漲，所以許多早餐店現在一個簡單的蛋三明治都要收更多錢。"},{"w":"mass","p":"n.","d":"a large amount or number of something","c":"大量；團；塊","s":"After the parade, a mass of paper and plastic cups covered the street, and volunteers spent hours cleaning it up.","t":"遊行過後，街上覆蓋著大量的紙屑和塑膠杯，志工花了好幾個小時清理。"},{"w":"mass","p":"adj.","d":"involving a very large number of people or things","c":"大規模的；大眾的","s":"Thanks to mass production, a simple T-shirt now costs less than a cup of coffee in many shops.","t":"多虧了大規模生產，現在在許多商店裡一件簡單的 T 恤比一杯咖啡還便宜。"},{"w":"the masses","p":"n.","d":"ordinary people, especially in contrast to the rich and powerful","c":"大眾；平民百姓","s":"The new library was built for the masses, so anyone in the city can borrow books and use the computers for free.","t":"新圖書館是為大眾建造的，所以城裡任何人都可以免費借書和使用電腦。"}]},{"unit":22,"theme":"masterpiece – mortality","cards":[{"w":"masterpiece","p":"n.","d":"a work of art, music, or writing that is the best of its kind","c":"傑作；代表作","s":"The painting on the museum's top floor took the artist seven years to finish, and many experts call it his greatest masterpiece.","t":"博物館頂樓的那幅畫花了這位藝術家七年才完成，許多專家稱它為他最偉大的傑作。","h":1},{"w":"master","p":"n.","d":"a person who is very skilled at something","c":"大師；高手","s":"My grandfather is a master of Chinese chess, and even the champion of our city has never managed to beat him.","t":"我爺爺是象棋高手，連我們城市的冠軍都從來沒有贏過他。"},{"w":"master","p":"v.","d":"to learn something so well that you can do it very skillfully","c":"精通；熟練掌握","s":"It took my cousin three years to master the difficult piano piece, but now he can play it without looking at the music.","t":"我表哥花了三年才精通那首困難的鋼琴曲，但現在他不看譜就能彈奏。"},{"w":"masterful","p":"adj.","d":"showing great skill","c":"技藝高超的","s":"The goalkeeper gave a masterful performance in the final, stopping five shots in the last ten minutes of the game.","t":"守門員在決賽中有技藝高超的表現，在比賽最後十分鐘擋下了五次射門。"},{"w":"mattress","p":"n.","d":"the thick, soft part of a bed that you lie on","c":"床墊","s":"My back hurt every morning because the old mattress was too soft, so last month I finally bought a firmer one.","t":"我每天早上背都痛，因為舊床墊太軟了，所以上個月我終於買了一個比較硬的。","h":1},{"w":"air mattress","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bed that you fill with air, often used for camping","c":"充氣床墊","s":"We slept on an air mattress in the tent, but it slowly lost air during the night, and by morning we were lying on the ground.","t":"我們在帳篷裡睡在充氣床墊上，但它夜裡慢慢漏氣，到了早上我們就躺在地上了。"},{"w":"mat","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of thick material that covers part of a floor","c":"墊子；地墊","s":"Please wipe your shoes on the mat by the door before you come in, because I just washed the floor this morning.","t":"進來之前請在門邊的地墊上擦擦鞋子，因為我今天早上才剛洗過地板。"},{"w":"yoga mat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin mat that you use for doing yoga exercises","c":"瑜伽墊","s":"Every evening my mother rolls out her purple yoga mat in the living room and practices for half an hour before dinner.","t":"每天傍晚我媽媽都會在客廳鋪開她的紫色瑜伽墊，晚餐前練習半小時。"},{"w":"meantime","p":"n.","d":"the time between two events","c":"其間；同時","s":"The pizza will take thirty minutes to arrive; in the meantime, let's set the table and choose a movie that everyone wants to watch.","t":"披薩要三十分鐘才會送到；在這期間，我們來擺餐桌，選一部大家都想看的電影吧。","h":1},{"w":"in the meantime","p":"phr.","d":"while something else is happening; until something happens","c":"在此期間；同時","s":"The new library will not open until September, but in the meantime students can borrow books from the small room next to the gym.","t":"新圖書館要到九月才開放，但在此期間學生可以從體育館旁邊的小房間借書。"},{"w":"meanwhile","p":"adv.","d":"at the same time; while something else is happening","c":"同時；在此期間","s":"Dad was cooking dinner in the kitchen; meanwhile, my sister and I finished our homework at the dining table.","t":"爸爸在廚房做晚餐；同時，我和姐姐在餐桌上把功課做完了。"},{"w":"mechanism","p":"n.","d":"a part of a machine that does a particular job","c":"機械裝置；機件","s":"The repairman opened the back of the old clock and found that a tiny wheel in the mechanism had broken in two.","t":"修理工打開舊時鐘的背面，發現機械裝置裡的一個小齒輪斷成了兩半。","h":1},{"w":"mechanism","p":"n.","d":"a system or way of doing something","c":"機制；方法","s":"The school needs a better mechanism for reporting bullying, because many students are afraid to talk to their teachers directly.","t":"學校需要一個更好的通報霸凌的機制，因為許多學生害怕直接和老師說。"},{"w":"mechanic","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to repair machines, especially cars","c":"機械工；修車技師","s":"The mechanic told my father that the car needed new brakes, and the repair would cost about ten thousand dollars.","t":"修車技師告訴我爸爸，車子需要換新的煞車，修理大約要花一萬元。"},{"w":"mechanical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with machines; operated by a machine","c":"機械的；機械操作的","s":"The elevator stopped between floors because of a mechanical problem, and we had to wait twenty minutes to be rescued.","t":"電梯因為機械問題停在樓層之間，我們必須等二十分鐘才獲救。"},{"w":"defense mechanism","p":"n.phr.","d":"a way that the body or mind protects itself","c":"防衛機制","s":"Laughing at a scary situation can be a defense mechanism, a way for the mind to deal with fear it cannot control.","t":"對可怕的情況發笑可能是一種防衛機制，是心靈處理無法控制的恐懼的方式。"},{"w":"medication","p":"n.","d":"a drug or drugs that you take to treat an illness","c":"藥物；藥物治療","s":"Grandpa has to take his heart medication at the same time every morning, because missing even one day could be dangerous.","t":"爺爺每天早上必須在同一時間吃他的心臟藥物，因為就算漏掉一天也可能很危險。","h":1},{"w":"be on medication","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be taking medicine regularly for an illness","c":"正在服藥","s":"My aunt is on medication for high blood pressure, so she avoids salty food and checks her pressure every evening.","t":"我阿姨因為高血壓正在服藥，所以她避免吃鹹的食物，每天晚上都量血壓。","a":"is on medication"},{"w":"medicine","p":"n.","d":"a substance you take to treat an illness; the study of illness","c":"藥；醫學","s":"The doctor gave me some medicine for my cough and told me to drink plenty of warm water and rest for two days.","t":"醫生給我一些治咳嗽的藥，並叫我多喝溫水，休息兩天。"},{"w":"medical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with illness and the treatment of illness","c":"醫學的；醫療的","s":"Jane is studying hard because she wants to finish her medical training and work as a doctor in a mountain village.","t":"珍很用功讀書，因為她想完成醫學訓練，到山區的村莊當醫生。"},{"w":"mentor","p":"n.","d":"an experienced person who helps and advises a younger or less experienced person","c":"導師；良師","s":"When Amy started her first job, an older worker patiently taught her everything, and she still calls him her mentor.","t":"艾美開始第一份工作時，一位資深員工耐心地教她所有事情，她到現在仍稱他為她的良師。","h":1},{"w":"mentor","p":"v.","d":"to help and advise a less experienced person over a period of time","c":"指導；輔導","s":"The famous chef agreed to mentor three young cooks from the school, and he visits their kitchen every Friday afternoon.","t":"這位名廚同意指導學校裡的三位年輕廚師，每週五下午都會去他們的廚房。"},{"w":"mentorship","p":"n.","d":"the help and advice given by a mentor over a period of time","c":"師徒關係；輔導","s":"The company runs a mentorship program in which every new employee is paired with a senior worker for the first six months.","t":"這家公司推行一個師徒輔導計畫，每位新員工在前六個月都會和一位資深員工配對。"},{"w":"merge","p":"v.","d":"to join together to form one thing","c":"合併；融合","s":"Two small banks in our town were losing money, so last year they decided to merge into one larger and stronger bank.","t":"我們鎮上的兩家小銀行一直在虧錢，所以去年它們決定合併成一家更大、更強的銀行。","h":1},{"w":"merge with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to join together with something else","c":"與…合併","s":"The small road will merge with the highway after the bridge, so slow down and watch for fast cars coming from your left.","t":"這條小路過了橋後會與高速公路會合，所以請減速，注意從左邊來的快車。"},{"w":"merger","p":"n.","d":"the act of joining two companies or organizations into one","c":"（公司）合併","s":"After the merger of the two airlines, passengers can now use one ticket to fly to more than eighty cities.","t":"兩家航空公司合併之後，乘客現在可以用一張機票飛往八十多個城市。"},{"w":"emerge","p":"v.","d":"to come out from somewhere; to become known","c":"出現；浮現","s":"The sun began to emerge from behind the dark clouds after the storm, and soon the whole beach was bright again.","t":"暴風雨過後，太陽開始從烏雲後面露出來，很快整個海灘又明亮了。"},{"w":"metaphor","p":"n.","d":"a word or phrase that describes something by comparing it to something else","c":"隱喻；比喻","s":"When the poet calls life \"a long and winding road,\" she is using a metaphor to describe its many surprises and changes.","t":"當詩人把人生稱為「一條漫長而曲折的道路」時，她是在用隱喻來描述人生的許多驚喜和變化。","h":1},{"w":"a metaphor for","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thing that stands for or represents something else","c":"…的隱喻；象徵…","s":"In the story, the long winter is a metaphor for the sadness the family feels after the grandfather passes away.","t":"在這個故事裡，漫長的冬天是家人在祖父過世後感到悲傷的隱喻。"},{"w":"metaphorical","p":"adj.","d":"using a metaphor; not literal","c":"隱喻的；比喻的","s":"When my coach said I had \"a mountain to climb,\" he meant it in a metaphorical way; there was no real mountain near the school.","t":"當我的教練說我「有一座山要爬」時，他是用比喻的方式說的；學校附近並沒有真正的山。"},{"w":"metaphorically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that uses a metaphor; not literally","c":"隱喻地；比喻地","s":"Metaphorically speaking, the new coach lit a fire under the team, and the players began to train harder than ever.","t":"比喻地說，新教練在球隊底下點了一把火，球員們開始比以往更努力訓練。","a":"Metaphorically"},{"w":"metropolitan","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a large or capital city","c":"大都會的；大都市的","s":"Over seven million people live in the Taipei metropolitan area, and every morning trains bring workers in from the towns around it.","t":"超過七百萬人住在台北都會區，每天早上火車把工人從周圍的城鎮載進來。","h":1},{"w":"metropolis","p":"n.","d":"a very large and important city","c":"大都市；大都會","s":"Tokyo is a busy metropolis of more than thirty million people, but it also has quiet temples and gardens hidden between the tall buildings.","t":"東京是個有三千多萬人的繁忙大都會，但在高樓之間也藏著安靜的寺廟和花園。"},{"w":"metropolitan area","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large city together with the towns around it","c":"都會區","s":"House prices in the metropolitan area have risen so fast that many young couples now choose to live an hour away by train.","t":"都會區的房價漲得太快，許多年輕夫妻現在選擇住在搭火車一小時遠的地方。"},{"w":"midst","p":"n.","d":"the middle of a period of time, an event, or a group","c":"中間；當中","s":"The phone rang in the midst of our family dinner, and Dad was annoyed until he heard it was good news from my aunt.","t":"電話在我們家庭晚餐進行中響起，爸爸很惱火，直到他聽到那是阿姨帶來的好消息。","h":1},{"w":"in the midst of","p":"phr.","d":"while something is happening; in the middle of","c":"在…之中；正當…的時候","s":"The country is in the midst of a serious water shortage, so the government has asked everyone to take shorter showers.","t":"這個國家正處於嚴重的缺水之中，所以政府要求大家淋浴時間縮短。"},{"w":"in our midst","p":"phr.","d":"among us; in our group","c":"在我們之中","s":"We did not know there was a famous writer in our midst until she signed a copy of her book for the school library.","t":"我們不知道我們之中有一位知名作家，直到她為學校圖書館簽了一本她的書。"},{"w":"amid","p":"prep.","d":"in the middle of or surrounded by something","c":"在…之中；在…中間","s":"The little girl stood amid the crowd of shoppers, looking for her mother and holding a red balloon tightly.","t":"小女孩站在購物人群之中，緊握著一個紅氣球，尋找她的媽媽。"},{"w":"migration","p":"n.","d":"the movement of large numbers of people or animals from one place to another","c":"遷徙；移居","s":"Every autumn thousands of birds fly south from Siberia, and scientists follow this migration to learn how the birds find their way.","t":"每年秋天成千上萬的鳥從西伯利亞往南飛，科學家追蹤這場遷徙，以了解鳥類如何找到路。","h":1},{"w":"migrate","p":"v.","d":"to move from one place to another, especially at a particular time of year","c":"遷徙；移居","s":"Gray whales migrate more than ten thousand kilometers every year, swimming from cold Alaska to the warm waters of Mexico.","t":"灰鯨每年遷徙一萬多公里，從寒冷的阿拉斯加游到墨西哥的溫暖海域。"},{"w":"migrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who moves to another place or country, often to find work","c":"移民；移工","s":"Many migrant workers come to Taiwan from Southeast Asia, and they often send most of their pay home to support their families.","t":"許多移工從東南亞來到台灣，他們常常把大部分的薪水寄回家養家。"},{"w":"immigrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who comes to live permanently in a foreign country","c":"（外來）移民","s":"My neighbor is an immigrant from Vietnam who opened a small restaurant, and now the whole street loves her spring rolls.","t":"我的鄰居是來自越南的移民，她開了一家小餐廳，現在整條街的人都愛她的春捲。"},{"w":"milestone","p":"n.","d":"an important event or stage in the development of something","c":"里程碑","s":"Selling the one-millionth cup of bubble tea was a big milestone for the small shop, so the owner gave every worker a day off.","t":"賣出第一百萬杯珍珠奶茶是這家小店的一個重要里程碑，所以老闆給每位員工放一天假。","h":1},{"w":"reach a milestone","p":"v.phr.","d":"to arrive at an important stage in a process","c":"達到里程碑","s":"Our charity will reach a milestone next month when it gives out its ten-thousandth free lunch box to children in need.","t":"我們的慈善團體下個月將達到一個里程碑，屆時會送出第一萬個免費便當給需要的孩子。"},{"w":"mile","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring distance, equal to about 1.6 kilometers","c":"英里","s":"The farm is about a mile from the station, so we can easily walk there in twenty minutes if the weather is nice.","t":"農場離車站大約一英里，所以如果天氣好，我們二十分鐘就能輕鬆走到那裡。"},{"w":"mileage","p":"n.","d":"the distance that a vehicle has traveled","c":"里程數","s":"Before buying a used car, check its mileage carefully, because a car that has traveled too far may need expensive repairs soon.","t":"買二手車之前要仔細檢查里程數，因為跑太遠的車可能很快就需要昂貴的修理。"},{"w":"miniature","p":"adj.","d":"very small; much smaller than usual","c":"微型的；小型的","s":"The museum displays a miniature model of the old city, so small that its tallest tower is only as high as a pencil.","t":"博物館展示了一個舊城的微型模型，小到最高的塔只有一支鉛筆那麼高。","h":1},{"w":"miniature","p":"n.","d":"a very small copy of something","c":"縮小模型；微型複製品","s":"My uncle collects miniatures of famous buildings, and his bookshelf holds a tiny Eiffel Tower and a Taipei 101 the size of a bottle.","t":"我叔叔收集知名建築的縮小模型，他的書架上有一座小小的艾菲爾鐵塔和一座瓶子大小的台北 101。","a":"miniatures"},{"w":"in miniature","p":"phr.","d":"in a very small form","c":"以縮小的形式","s":"The garden shows the whole island in miniature, with tiny mountains, rivers, and even a train that runs around the edge.","t":"這座花園以縮小的形式呈現整座島，有小小的山脈、河流，甚至還有一列繞著邊緣跑的火車。"},{"w":"mini","p":"adj.","d":"very small; smaller than the usual size","c":"迷你的","s":"My sister bought a mini fridge for her dorm room, which is just big enough for a few drinks and some fruit.","t":"我姐姐為宿舍房間買了一台迷你冰箱，大小剛好夠放幾瓶飲料和一些水果。"},{"w":"minimal","p":"adj.","d":"very small in amount or degree; the least possible","c":"極少的；最低限度的","s":"The storm was strong, but the damage to our house was minimal; only two roof tiles fell off and nothing inside was broken.","t":"暴風雨很強，但我們房子的損壞極小；只掉了兩片屋瓦，裡面什麼都沒壞。","h":1},{"w":"minimize","p":"v.","d":"to reduce something to the smallest possible amount or degree","c":"使減到最少；最小化","s":"Wearing a seat belt cannot stop an accident, but it can greatly minimize the chance of serious injury if your car crashes.","t":"繫安全帶不能阻止意外發生，但如果你的車撞到了，它能大大減少重傷的機會。","h":1},{"w":"minimum","p":"n.","d":"the smallest amount or number that is possible or allowed","c":"最低限度；最小量","s":"You need a minimum of eight hours of sleep before the big test, so please turn off your phone by ten tonight.","t":"大考前你需要至少八小時的睡眠，所以今晚十點前請把手機關掉。"},{"w":"minimum","p":"adj.","d":"smallest in amount or degree that is possible or allowed","c":"最低的；最小的","s":"The minimum age for getting a scooter license in Taiwan is eighteen, so my brother has to wait two more years.","t":"在台灣考機車駕照的最低年齡是十八歲，所以我哥哥還得再等兩年。"},{"w":"minimum wage","p":"n.phr.","d":"the lowest amount of money that employers are allowed to pay workers","c":"最低工資","s":"The government raised the minimum wage this year, so students who work part-time at convenience stores now earn a little more.","t":"政府今年提高了最低工資，所以在便利商店打工的學生現在賺得多一點了。"},{"w":"minimally","p":"adv.","d":"to a very small degree","c":"極少地；最低限度地","s":"The new medicine helped the patient only minimally, so the doctor decided to try a different treatment next week.","t":"這種新藥對病人只有極小的幫助，所以醫生決定下週嘗試不同的治療。"},{"w":"mint","p":"n.","d":"a plant with sweet-smelling leaves used in cooking and tea","c":"薄荷","s":"My grandmother grows mint in a pot by the kitchen window and picks a few fresh leaves for her tea every afternoon.","t":"我奶奶在廚房窗邊的花盆裡種薄荷，每天下午摘幾片新鮮葉子泡茶。","h":1},{"w":"mint","p":"n.","d":"a sweet with a strong fresh taste","c":"薄荷糖","s":"After the garlic noodles, my father offered everyone a mint so that our breath would be fresh for the meeting.","t":"吃完蒜味麵後，我爸爸給每個人一顆薄荷糖，讓我們開會時口氣清新。"},{"w":"in mint condition","p":"adj.phr.","d":"in perfect condition, as if new","c":"完好如新的","s":"The old comic book is in mint condition even though it was printed fifty years ago, so collectors are willing to pay a lot for it.","t":"這本舊漫畫雖然是五十年前印的，卻完好如新，所以收藏家願意付很多錢買它。"},{"w":"peppermint","p":"n.","d":"a type of mint with a very strong taste, used in sweets and tea","c":"胡椒薄荷","s":"A cup of hot peppermint tea after dinner helps my stomach feel better, especially when I have eaten too much.","t":"晚餐後一杯熱胡椒薄荷茶能讓我的胃舒服一點，尤其是當我吃太多的時候。"},{"w":"missionary","p":"n.","d":"a person who is sent to another country to teach people about a religion","c":"傳教士","s":"Dr. Mackay came to Taiwan as a missionary more than a hundred years ago, and besides preaching, he opened schools and a hospital.","t":"馬偕博士一百多年前以傳教士的身分來到台灣，除了傳教之外，他還開辦了學校和醫院。","h":1},{"w":"missionary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the work of missionaries","c":"傳教的","s":"The church sent a small missionary team to the mountain village, where they taught children to read and helped build a clinic.","t":"教會派了一個小型傳教團隊到山區村莊，在那裡教孩子閱讀，並幫忙建了一間診所。"},{"w":"mission","p":"n.","d":"an important job that someone is sent to do","c":"任務；使命","s":"The astronauts spent six months on the space station, and their mission ended safely when their ship landed in the desert.","t":"太空人在太空站待了六個月，他們的任務在太空船安全降落沙漠時結束了。"},{"w":"on a mission","p":"phr.","d":"determined to do something; sent to do a job","c":"肩負任務；一心想完成某事","s":"My little sister is on a mission to find the lost cat, and she has put posters on every street corner in the neighborhood.","t":"我妹妹一心想找到走失的貓，她已經在附近每個街角都貼了海報。"},{"w":"moan","p":"n.","d":"a long, low sound that someone makes because of pain or sadness","c":"呻吟聲","s":"We heard a soft moan from under the fallen tree, and the firefighters quickly found the injured hiker lying there.","t":"我們聽到倒下的樹底下傳來微弱的呻吟聲，消防員很快就找到躺在那裡受傷的登山客。","h":1},{"w":"moan","p":"v.","d":"to make a long, low sound because of pain or sadness","c":"呻吟","s":"The old man fell off his bike and hurt his leg badly, and we could hear him moan in pain while we waited for the ambulance.","t":"老先生從腳踏車上摔下來，腿傷得很重，我們等救護車時聽得到他痛苦地呻吟。"},{"w":"moan","p":"v.","d":"to complain about something in an annoying way","c":"抱怨；發牢騷","s":"My brother likes to moan about the food in the school cafeteria, but he still eats every single thing on his plate.","t":"我哥哥喜歡抱怨學校餐廳的食物，但他還是把盤子裡的每樣東西都吃光。"},{"w":"moan about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to complain about something","c":"抱怨…","s":"Instead of continuing to moan about the heat, let's buy a cheap fan for the classroom and ask the teacher if we can open the windows.","t":"與其繼續抱怨炎熱，我們不如為教室買一台便宜的電扇，並問老師能不能開窗。"},{"w":"mock","p":"v.","d":"to laugh at someone in an unkind way","c":"嘲笑；嘲弄","s":"The other boys used to mock Tom for his thick glasses, but now they ask him for help with their math homework.","t":"其他男孩以前常因為湯姆的厚眼鏡嘲笑他，但現在他們都向他請教數學功課。","h":1},{"w":"mock","p":"adj.","d":"not real; made to look like the real thing, often for practice","c":"模擬的；假的","s":"Next week we will take a mock exam that looks exactly like the real test, so we can find out what we still need to study.","t":"下週我們會考一場和真正考試完全一樣的模擬考，這樣我們就能知道還需要讀什麼。"},{"w":"mock exam","p":"n.phr.","d":"a practice exam that is like the real one","c":"模擬考","s":"Our teacher said the mock exam would not count toward our grades, but she wanted us to treat it as seriously as the real one.","t":"我們老師說模擬考不算成績，但她希望我們像對待真正的考試一樣認真。"},{"w":"mockery","p":"n.","d":"unkind comments or laughter that make someone look silly","c":"嘲笑；嘲弄","s":"His first speech was met with mockery from the class, but a year later the same students cheered when he won the contest.","t":"他的第一次演講遭到全班的嘲笑，但一年後，當他贏得比賽時，同樣的學生為他歡呼。"},{"w":"mocking","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you think someone or something is silly","c":"嘲弄的","s":"She gave me a mocking smile when I said I would run the marathon, but I finished the race and proved her wrong.","t":"當我說要跑馬拉松時，她給了我一個嘲弄的微笑，但我跑完了比賽，證明她錯了。"},{"w":"mode","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of doing something","c":"方式；模式","s":"The bus is the cheapest mode of travel between the two cities, but the train is faster and much more comfortable.","t":"公車是這兩個城市之間最便宜的交通方式，但火車更快，也舒服得多。","h":1},{"w":"mode","p":"n.","d":"a particular setting on a machine or device","c":"（機器的）模式","s":"My phone was in silent mode during the movie, so I did not hear my mother calling, and she was really worried.","t":"看電影時我的手機是靜音模式，所以我沒聽到媽媽打來，她非常擔心。"},{"w":"airplane mode","p":"n.phr.","d":"a setting that turns off a phone's wireless connections","c":"飛航模式","s":"Please switch your phone to airplane mode before the plane takes off, and you may turn it back on after we land.","t":"飛機起飛前請把手機切換到飛航模式，降落後可以再打開。"},{"w":"mode of transport","p":"n.phr.","d":"a way of traveling, such as bus, train, or bike","c":"交通方式","s":"Cycling is a popular mode of transport in the Netherlands, where there are more bicycles than people in many cities.","t":"騎腳踏車在荷蘭是一種受歡迎的交通方式，那裡許多城市的腳踏車比人還多。"},{"w":"modify","p":"v.","d":"to change something slightly, especially to improve it","c":"修改；調整","s":"The chef's new dish was too spicy for most customers, so he decided to modify the recipe by using fewer chili peppers.","t":"主廚的新菜對大多數顧客來說太辣了，所以他決定減少辣椒的用量來修改食譜。","h":1},{"w":"modification","p":"n.","d":"a small change made to something","c":"修改；修正","s":"The teacher made a small modification to the class rules, and now we may drink water during lessons on hot days.","t":"老師對班規做了一個小修改，現在天氣熱的時候我們可以在上課時喝水。"},{"w":"modified","p":"adj.","d":"changed slightly from the original form","c":"經過修改的","s":"The team used a modified version of the robot in the final, with longer arms that could pick up the ball more easily.","t":"這個團隊在決賽中使用了經過修改的機器人版本，更長的手臂可以更容易撿起球。"},{"w":"genetically modified","p":"adj.phr.","d":"having genes that have been changed by scientists","c":"基因改造的","s":"Some people refuse to eat genetically modified food, while others say these crops can help feed the growing population of the world.","t":"有些人拒絕吃基因改造食物，而另一些人則說這些作物可以幫助餵飽世界上不斷增加的人口。"},{"w":"molecule","p":"n.","d":"the smallest unit of a substance, made of two or more atoms","c":"分子","s":"Water is made of tiny parts far too small to see, and each molecule has two hydrogen atoms joined to one oxygen atom.","t":"水是由小到看不見的微小部分組成的，每個分子有兩個氫原子和一個氧原子結合在一起。","h":1},{"w":"molecular","p":"adj.","d":"connected with molecules","c":"分子的","s":"My cousin studies molecular biology at university, where she looks at how tiny parts inside cells carry information.","t":"我表姐在大學讀分子生物學，研究細胞裡的微小部分如何傳遞訊息。"},{"w":"a molecule of","p":"n.phr.","d":"one unit of a substance made of atoms","c":"一個…分子","s":"Scientists explained that a molecule of sugar is much larger than one of water, which is why sugar dissolves slowly in cold drinks.","t":"科學家解釋說，一個糖分子比一個水分子大得多，這就是為什麼糖在冷飲中溶解得很慢。"},{"w":"monopoly","p":"n.","d":"complete control of a business or market by one company","c":"壟斷；獨占","s":"For years only one company was allowed to sell electricity, but its monopoly ended when the government opened the market to others.","t":"多年來只有一家公司被允許賣電，但當政府把市場開放給其他公司時，它的壟斷就結束了。","h":1},{"w":"have a monopoly on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the only one who has or controls something","c":"獨占…；壟斷…","s":"No single country can have a monopoly on good ideas, which is why scientists from around the world share their research online.","t":"沒有任何一個國家能獨占好點子，這就是為什麼世界各地的科學家在網路上分享他們的研究。"},{"w":"monopolize","p":"v.","d":"to control something completely so that others cannot share it","c":"壟斷；獨占","s":"My little brother tends to monopolize the conversation at dinner, so nobody else gets a chance to talk about their day.","t":"我弟弟晚餐時總是獨占談話，所以其他人都沒有機會談自己的一天。"},{"w":"morality","p":"n.","d":"ideas about what is right and wrong behavior","c":"道德；道德觀","s":"Some people think downloading movies for free is fine, but others say it is a question of morality, because the filmmakers get nothing.","t":"有些人認為免費下載電影沒關係，但另一些人說這是道德問題，因為電影製作者什麼都得不到。","h":1},{"w":"moral","p":"adj.","d":"connected with what is right and wrong","c":"道德的；道德上的","s":"Lying to your friends might keep you out of trouble today, but it is not the moral thing to do, and they will find out.","t":"對朋友說謊今天也許能讓你免於麻煩，但那不是道德的做法，而且他們會發現的。"},{"w":"moral","p":"n.","d":"a lesson about right and wrong that you learn from a story","c":"寓意；教訓","s":"The moral of the story is that slow and steady work wins the race, even against someone who is much faster than you.","t":"這個故事的寓意是，穩紮穩打的努力能贏得比賽，即使對手比你快得多。"},{"w":"morals","p":"n.","d":"standards of good behavior","c":"道德標準；品行","s":"My grandmother taught us strong morals: never lie, never steal, and always help someone who is in trouble.","t":"我奶奶教我們嚴格的道德標準：絕不說謊、絕不偷竊，並且永遠幫助有困難的人。"},{"w":"immoral","p":"adj.","d":"not following accepted standards of right and wrong","c":"不道德的","s":"Most people agree that it is immoral to sell medicine you know is fake, because sick people trust the seller with their lives.","t":"大多數人都同意，賣你明知是假的藥是不道德的，因為病人把生命託付給賣家。"},{"w":"mortality","p":"n.","d":"the number of deaths in a particular period or place","c":"死亡率；死亡人數","s":"Clean water and vaccines have saved millions of young lives, and child mortality has dropped sharply in most countries since 1970.","t":"乾淨的水和疫苗挽救了數百萬年輕生命，自 1970 年以來大多數國家的兒童死亡率已大幅下降。","h":1},{"w":"mortality","p":"n.","d":"the fact that everyone must die one day","c":"必死性；終有一死","s":"After his grandfather passed away, the boy began to think about his own mortality and decided to spend more time with his family.","t":"祖父過世後，男孩開始思考自己終有一死這件事，並決定多花時間陪伴家人。"},{"w":"mortal","p":"adj.","d":"that cannot live forever; causing death","c":"終將死亡的；致命的","s":"In the old story, the gods lived forever, but every mortal human being had to grow old and finally die.","t":"在古老的故事裡，神永遠活著，但每個終將一死的凡人都必須變老，最後死去。"},{"w":"immortal","p":"adj.","d":"living or lasting forever","c":"不朽的；永生的","s":"Shakespeare died more than four hundred years ago, but his plays are immortal and are still performed all over the world today.","t":"莎士比亞四百多年前就過世了，但他的劇作是不朽的，今天仍在全世界各地演出。"},{"w":"mortality rate","p":"n.phr.","d":"the number of deaths in a year for every thousand people","c":"死亡率","s":"The mortality rate from traffic accidents fell by half after the city lowered speed limits and built more crossings for pedestrians.","t":"在城市降低速限並為行人建造更多穿越道之後，交通事故的死亡率下降了一半。"}]},{"unit":23,"theme":"mortgage – obligation","cards":[{"w":"mortgage","p":"n.","d":"money you borrow from a bank to buy a house and pay back over many years","c":"房屋貸款；抵押貸款","s":"My parents still pay the mortgage on our apartment every month, and they will finally finish paying it off in three years.","t":"我父母每個月仍在付我們公寓的房屋貸款，三年後他們終於會把它還清。","h":1},{"w":"take out a mortgage","p":"v.phr.","d":"to borrow money from a bank in order to buy a home","c":"申請房貸","s":"After they got married, my cousin and her husband decided to take out a mortgage and buy a small house near her office.","t":"結婚後，我表姐和她丈夫決定申請房貸，在她公司附近買一間小房子。"},{"w":"mortgage","p":"v.","d":"to give a bank the right to take your house if you cannot pay back the money you borrowed","c":"抵押","s":"The old man had to mortgage his home to pay for his son's hospital bills, so now he worries about losing it.","t":"那位老先生不得不抵押自己的房子來付兒子的醫院帳單，所以現在他擔心會失去它。"},{"w":"pay off a mortgage","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finish paying back all the money you borrowed to buy a house","c":"還清房貸","s":"It took my grandparents twenty-five years to pay off their mortgage, and they held a big family dinner to celebrate the day.","t":"我的祖父母花了二十五年才還清房貸，他們辦了一場家庭聚餐來慶祝那一天。","a":"pay off their mortgage"},{"w":"motive","p":"n.","d":"the reason why a person does something, especially something bad","c":"動機","s":"The police believe that money was the motive for the robbery, because the thief only took cash and left everything else behind.","t":"警方認為錢是這起搶案的動機，因為小偷只拿走現金，其他東西都留下來了。","h":1},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something or work hard","c":"激勵；促使","s":"A good teacher knows how to motivate students who have lost interest, and she often uses games and real-life stories in class.","t":"好老師知道如何激勵失去興趣的學生，而且她常在課堂上使用遊戲和真實故事。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of wanting to do something; the reason for doing it","c":"動機；積極性","s":"When the weather is cold and dark, I have very little motivation to get out of bed and go jogging in the morning.","t":"天氣又冷又暗時，我很少有動力早上起床去慢跑。"},{"w":"motivated","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to do something and willing to work hard for it","c":"有動力的；積極的","s":"The new workers are highly motivated because the company promised them a bonus if they finish the project before December.","t":"新員工們都非常有動力，因為公司承諾若他們在十二月前完成專案就會發獎金。"},{"w":"mount","p":"v.","d":"to go up something; to get on a horse or a bicycle","c":"登上；騎上","s":"The queen slowly began to mount the stairs to the palace while hundreds of people cheered and waved flags below her.","t":"女王緩緩開始登上通往宮殿的階梯，數百人在她下方歡呼並揮舞旗子。","h":1},{"w":"mount","p":"v.","d":"to increase slowly in amount or level","c":"增加；上升","s":"As the days passed without any news from the lost ship, the fear and worry of the families continued to mount.","t":"隨著失蹤船隻多日沒有消息，家屬們的恐懼與擔憂持續增加。"},{"w":"mount","p":"n.","d":"a mountain; used before the name of a mountain","c":"山（用於山名）","s":"Mount Jade is the highest peak in Taiwan, and thousands of hikers apply for permits to climb it every single year.","t":"玉山是台灣最高峰，每年有數千名登山客申請入山證去攀登它。","a":"Mount"},{"w":"mountain","p":"n.","d":"a very high hill","c":"山","s":"We drove up the mountain early in the morning, and by noon we could see the whole valley covered in clouds.","t":"我們一大早開車上山，到了中午就能看到整個山谷被雲覆蓋。"},{"w":"mounting","p":"adj.","d":"growing larger or stronger over time","c":"日益增加的","s":"There is mounting pressure on the government to lower the price of electricity before the hot summer months arrive.","t":"政府面臨日益增加的壓力，要在炎熱的夏季月份來臨之前降低電價。"},{"w":"mumble","p":"v.","d":"to speak quietly and not clearly, so people cannot understand you","c":"咕噥；含糊地說","s":"Please do not mumble when you give your speech tomorrow, because the people at the back of the hall need to hear every word.","t":"明天演講時請不要含糊地說話，因為大廳後面的人需要聽清楚每個字。","h":1},{"w":"mumble","p":"n.","d":"a quiet and unclear way of speaking","c":"咕噥聲；含糊的話","s":"The shy boy answered the teacher's question in a low mumble, so she kindly asked him to say it again more loudly.","t":"那個害羞的男孩用低聲的咕噥回答老師的問題，所以她親切地請他再大聲說一次。"},{"w":"mumble to oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say something quietly to yourself that others cannot hear clearly","c":"自言自語地咕噥","s":"My grandfather often mumbles to himself while he reads the newspaper, and sometimes he even argues with the articles.","t":"我爺爺看報紙時常常自言自語地咕噥，有時甚至還會跟文章吵起來。","a":"mumbles to himself"},{"w":"murmur","p":"v.","d":"to say something very softly and gently","c":"低聲說；喃喃地說","s":"The mother began to murmur a sweet song to her baby, and within a few minutes the child was sleeping peacefully.","t":"媽媽開始對寶寶低聲唱一首甜美的歌，幾分鐘內孩子就安穩地睡著了。"},{"w":"municipal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the government of a city or town","c":"市的；市政的","s":"The municipal library stays open until ten every night, so students who live downtown often go there to study after dinner.","t":"市立圖書館每晚開放到十點，所以住在市中心的學生常在晚餐後去那裡讀書。","h":1},{"w":"municipal government","p":"n.phr.","d":"the group of people who run a city or town","c":"市政府","s":"The municipal government promised to build more bike lanes this year, because too many people have been hurt riding on busy roads.","t":"市政府承諾今年要建造更多自行車道，因為太多人在繁忙的道路上騎車受傷。"},{"w":"municipality","p":"n.","d":"a city or town that has its own local government","c":"市；自治市","s":"Each municipality in Taiwan decides its own rules about garbage collection, so the schedule changes when you move to another city.","t":"台灣的每個自治市自己決定垃圾收集的規定，所以當你搬到另一個城市時，時間表會改變。"},{"w":"muscular","p":"adj.","d":"having big, strong muscles","c":"肌肉發達的","s":"The muscular firefighter carried the heavy man down three floors by himself, and nobody was surprised that he could do it.","t":"那位肌肉發達的消防員獨自把那個重重的男人從三樓背下來，沒有人對他能做到感到驚訝。","h":1},{"w":"muscle","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts inside your body that you use to move","c":"肌肉","s":"If you lift weights three times a week and eat enough protein, you will build muscle and feel much stronger in a few months.","t":"如果你每週舉重三次並吃足夠的蛋白質，幾個月內你就會長出肌肉並覺得強壯許多。"},{"w":"pull a muscle","p":"v.phr.","d":"to hurt a muscle by stretching it too far or too quickly","c":"拉傷肌肉","s":"Tom forgot to warm up before the race and pulled a muscle in his leg, so he could not run for the next two weeks.","t":"湯姆比賽前忘了熱身，結果拉傷了腿部肌肉，所以接下來兩週他都不能跑步。","a":"pulled a muscle"},{"w":"muscular strength","p":"n.phr.","d":"how strong your muscles are","c":"肌力","s":"Doctors say that older people should keep up their muscular strength with simple exercises, because strong legs help prevent dangerous falls.","t":"醫生說年長者應該用簡單的運動維持肌力，因為強壯的雙腿有助於預防危險的跌倒。"},{"w":"mustard","p":"n.","d":"a yellow sauce with a hot taste that people eat with meat","c":"芥末；黃芥末醬","s":"I always put a little mustard on my hot dog at the baseball game, but my sister prefers ketchup and lots of onions.","t":"在棒球賽上我總是在熱狗上加一點芥末醬，但我姐姐比較喜歡番茄醬和很多洋蔥。","h":1},{"w":"mustard","p":"adj.","d":"having a dark yellow color","c":"芥末黃的","s":"She wore a mustard sweater with her blue jeans to the party, and everyone said the warm color looked perfect for autumn.","t":"她穿著一件芥末黃毛衣配藍色牛仔褲去派對，大家都說這溫暖的顏色非常適合秋天。"},{"w":"mustard seed","p":"n.phr.","d":"the tiny seed of the mustard plant, used as a spice","c":"芥菜籽","s":"The cook heated some oil in a pan and added a spoonful of mustard seed, which began to pop and fill the kitchen with a wonderful smell.","t":"廚師在鍋裡熱了一些油，加入一湯匙芥菜籽，籽開始爆開，廚房裡充滿了美妙的香味。"},{"w":"myth","p":"n.","d":"an old story about gods, heroes, or how the world began","c":"神話","s":"According to an ancient Chinese myth, a woman named Chang'e drank a magic potion and flew up to live on the moon forever.","t":"根據一則古老的中國神話，一位名叫嫦娥的女子喝了仙藥，飛上月亮永遠住在那裡。","h":1},{"w":"myth","p":"n.","d":"something that many people believe but that is not true","c":"迷思；錯誤的觀念","s":"It is a common myth that we only use ten percent of our brains, but scientists have shown that this is simply false.","t":"我們只用了大腦的百分之十是個常見的迷思，但科學家已經證明這完全是錯的。"},{"w":"mythology","p":"n.","d":"the myths of a particular people or culture, taken together","c":"神話（總稱）","s":"In Greek mythology, Zeus was the king of the gods, and he controlled the sky, the thunder, and the weather.","t":"在希臘神話中，宙斯是眾神之王，他掌管天空、雷電和天氣。"},{"w":"mythical","p":"adj.","d":"existing only in myths or stories, not in real life","c":"神話中的；虛構的","s":"The dragon is a mythical creature in many cultures, yet people in Taiwan still celebrate it with boat races every summer.","t":"龍在許多文化中是一種神話中的生物，然而台灣人每年夏天仍然用划龍舟來慶祝它。"},{"w":"naive","p":"adj.","d":"believing things too easily because you have little experience of life","c":"天真的；幼稚的","s":"I was naive enough to believe the email saying I had won a free car, and I almost sent them my bank details.","t":"我天真到相信那封說我贏了一台免費汽車的電子郵件，差點就把銀行資料寄給他們。","h":1},{"w":"naively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you believe things too easily","c":"天真地","s":"The young couple naively trusted the agent and paid for the apartment before they had seen it, which turned out to be a big mistake.","t":"這對年輕夫妻天真地相信了仲介，還沒看房就付了公寓的錢，結果證明是個大錯誤。"},{"w":"naivety","p":"n.","d":"the quality of believing things too easily or lacking experience","c":"天真；輕信","s":"Because of his naivety, the new student lent money to a classmate he barely knew and never got it back.","t":"由於他的天真，這位新生把錢借給一個幾乎不認識的同學，再也沒有拿回來。"},{"w":"narrative","p":"n.","d":"a story, or a description of a series of events","c":"敘述；故事","s":"The documentary presents a clear narrative of how the small town recovered after the terrible earthquake twenty years ago.","t":"這部紀錄片清楚地敘述了這個小鎮在二十年前那場可怕的地震後如何重建。","h":1},{"w":"narrative","p":"adj.","d":"telling a story","c":"敘事的","s":"In narrative writing, you describe events in the order they happened, which is why many students start with a strong opening scene.","t":"在敘事寫作中，你要按照事件發生的順序描述，這就是為什麼許多學生會以強而有力的開場畫面開始。"},{"w":"narrate","p":"v.","d":"to tell a story or describe events, often in a film or program","c":"敘述；講述","s":"A famous actor was invited to narrate the nature film, and his deep voice made the scenes of the ocean even more beautiful.","t":"一位知名演員受邀為這部自然影片旁白敘述，他低沉的聲音讓海洋的畫面更加美麗。"},{"w":"narrator","p":"n.","d":"the person who tells the story in a book, film, or play","c":"敘述者；旁白","s":"In the novel, the narrator is a ten-year-old boy, so readers see the war through the eyes of a child.","t":"在這本小說中，敘述者是個十歲男孩，所以讀者透過孩子的眼睛看見戰爭。"},{"w":"nasty","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or unpleasant","c":"令人不快的；惡劣的","s":"The medicine had such a nasty taste that the little girl refused to take it until her mother mixed it with honey.","t":"那藥的味道難聞得令人不快，小女孩拒絕吃，直到媽媽把它和蜂蜜混在一起。","h":1},{"w":"nasty","p":"adj.","d":"unkind and cruel in the way you treat people","c":"刻薄的；惡意的","s":"Some people leave nasty comments under videos just to hurt the creators, which is why many young people stop sharing their work.","t":"有些人在影片下留下惡意的評論只是為了傷害創作者，這就是為什麼許多年輕人不再分享他們的作品。"},{"w":"a nasty surprise","p":"n.phr.","d":"something unexpected and unpleasant","c":"不愉快的意外","s":"We got a nasty surprise when we opened the electricity bill this month, because it was almost double what we usually pay.","t":"這個月打開電費帳單時我們遇到一個不愉快的意外，因為金額幾乎是我們平常付的兩倍。"},{"w":"negotiation","p":"n.","d":"formal talks between people or groups who are trying to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"After weeks of difficult negotiation, the two companies finally agreed on a price, and the deal was signed last Friday.","t":"經過數週艱難的談判，兩家公司終於就價格達成協議，並在上週五簽約。","h":1},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"to talk with someone in order to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"Before you accept a new job, it is wise to negotiate your salary, because most companies expect you to ask for more.","t":"接受新工作前，明智的做法是協商薪水，因為大多數公司預期你會要求更多。"},{"w":"under negotiation","p":"phr.","d":"still being discussed; not yet agreed","c":"正在協商中","s":"The details of the new school uniform are still under negotiation, so students should keep wearing the old one until further notice.","t":"新校服的細節仍在協商中，所以學生應繼續穿舊校服，直到另行通知。"},{"w":"negotiator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to talk with others and reach an agreement","c":"談判者；協商者","s":"The police sent an experienced negotiator to talk to the man on the roof, and after an hour he agreed to come down safely.","t":"警方派了一位經驗豐富的談判專家和屋頂上的男子對話，一小時後他同意安全地下來。"},{"w":"neutral","p":"adj.","d":"not supporting either side in an argument, war, or competition","c":"中立的","s":"A good judge must stay neutral and listen to both sides carefully before deciding who is right and who is wrong.","t":"好的法官必須保持中立，在決定誰對誰錯之前仔細聽取雙方的意見。","h":1},{"w":"neutral","p":"adj.","d":"not strong or bright in color; not showing any feeling","c":"中性的；不帶感情的","s":"She painted the living room in neutral colors like beige and soft gray, so any furniture she buys later will match the walls.","t":"她把客廳漆成米色和柔灰等中性色，這樣以後買的任何家具都會和牆壁搭配。"},{"w":"remain neutral","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep refusing to support either side","c":"保持中立","s":"When my two best friends argued about the trip, I tried to remain neutral, but both of them became angry with me anyway.","t":"當我兩個最好的朋友為了旅行吵架時，我試著保持中立，但他們倆還是都對我生氣了。"},{"w":"neutrality","p":"n.","d":"the state of not supporting either side","c":"中立","s":"Switzerland is famous for its neutrality, since the country has not joined a war in Europe for more than two hundred years.","t":"瑞士以其中立聞名，因為這個國家已有兩百多年沒有加入歐洲的戰爭。"},{"w":"neutralize","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from having any effect","c":"使無效；中和","s":"Baking soda can neutralize the acid in your stomach, which is why some people drink a little with water when they feel unwell.","t":"小蘇打可以中和胃裡的酸，這就是為什麼有些人覺得不舒服時會用水沖一點喝。"},{"w":"nominate","p":"v.","d":"to officially suggest someone for a job, a prize, or a position","c":"提名","s":"The students decided to nominate Lisa for class president because she always listens to everyone and works very hard.","t":"學生們決定提名麗莎當班長，因為她總是傾聽每個人的意見，而且非常努力。","h":1},{"w":"nomination","p":"n.","d":"the act of officially suggesting someone for a job, prize, or position","c":"提名","s":"The young director received her first Oscar nomination this year, and she cried with joy when she heard the news on the radio.","t":"這位年輕導演今年獲得她的第一個奧斯卡提名，在收音機聽到消息時她喜極而泣。","h":1},{"w":"nominee","p":"n.","d":"a person who has been officially suggested for a job, prize, or position","c":"被提名人","s":"Each nominee for the science prize must give a ten-minute talk about his or her research before the final vote next week.","t":"科學獎的每位被提名人必須在下週最終投票前，就自己的研究發表十分鐘的演講。","h":1},{"w":"be nominated for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be officially suggested as a possible winner of a prize","c":"獲提名…","s":"The film was nominated for six awards, including Best Picture, but in the end it won only the prize for best music.","t":"這部電影獲提名六項獎，包括最佳影片，但最後只贏得最佳配樂獎。","a":"was nominated for"},{"w":"nominal","p":"adj.","d":"very small in amount; existing in name only","c":"名義上的；微不足道的","s":"The museum charges only a nominal fee of ten dollars, so almost every family in the neighborhood can afford to visit.","t":"這座博物館只收微不足道的十元費用，所以附近幾乎每個家庭都能負擔得起去參觀。"},{"w":"nonprofit","p":"adj.","d":"not run in order to make money, but to help people or society","c":"非營利的","s":"The nonprofit group gives free English lessons to children in the mountains, and all its teachers are unpaid volunteers.","t":"這個非營利團體為山區的孩子提供免費英文課，所有老師都是無薪志工。","h":1},{"w":"nonprofit organization","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group that works to help people and does not try to make money","c":"非營利組織","s":"My aunt works for a nonprofit organization that protects sea turtles, so she spends most of her summer on the beaches of eastern Taiwan.","t":"我阿姨在一個保護海龜的非營利組織工作，所以她夏天大部分時間都在台灣東部的海灘上。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"the money you make after paying all your costs","c":"利潤","s":"The bakery made a small profit in its first year, but the owner expects to earn much more once more people know about it.","t":"這家麵包店第一年賺了少許利潤，但老闆預期一旦更多人知道它，就會賺得更多。"},{"w":"profitable","p":"adj.","d":"making money; bringing a good result","c":"有利可圖的；有益的","s":"Selling bubble tea near the high school turned out to be very profitable, because students line up for drinks every afternoon.","t":"在高中附近賣珍珠奶茶結果非常有利可圖，因為學生每天下午都排隊買飲料。"},{"w":"norm","p":"n.","d":"a way of behaving that is usual and expected in a group or society","c":"規範；常態","s":"In many Asian countries, taking off your shoes before entering a home is a social norm that visitors are expected to follow.","t":"在許多亞洲國家，進屋前脫鞋是訪客應該遵守的社會規範。","h":1},{"w":"the norm","p":"n.phr.","d":"the usual situation or way of doing things","c":"常態","s":"Working from home two days a week has become the norm in many companies since the pandemic changed how people think about offices.","t":"自從疫情改變了人們對辦公室的看法後，每週在家工作兩天在許多公司已成為常態。"},{"w":"normal","p":"adj.","d":"usual, ordinary, and expected","c":"正常的","s":"It is perfectly normal to feel nervous before a big exam, so take a deep breath and remember how much you have prepared.","t":"大考前感到緊張是完全正常的，所以深呼吸，記住你準備了多少。"},{"w":"normally","p":"adv.","d":"usually; in the usual way","c":"通常；正常地","s":"I normally take the MRT to school, but this morning the trains were not running, so my father drove me instead.","t":"我通常搭捷運上學，但今天早上列車停駛，所以改由我爸爸開車送我。"},{"w":"abnormal","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is usual or expected, often in a worrying way","c":"不正常的；異常的","s":"The doctor noticed an abnormal heartbeat during the check-up and asked the patient to come back for more tests next week.","t":"醫生在健康檢查時注意到不正常的心跳，請病人下週回來做更多檢查。"},{"w":"noticeable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see or notice; clear","c":"明顯的","s":"There has been a noticeable improvement in Jack's English since he started chatting with his Canadian cousin online every night.","t":"自從傑克每晚開始和他的加拿大表哥線上聊天後，他的英文有了明顯的進步。","h":1},{"w":"noticeably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is easy to see or notice","c":"明顯地","s":"The air in the city became noticeably cleaner after the government banned old diesel trucks from the downtown area.","t":"政府禁止老舊柴油卡車進入市中心後，城市的空氣明顯地變乾淨了。"},{"w":"notice","p":"v.","d":"to see or become aware of something","c":"注意到","s":"Did you notice that the new student always eats lunch alone, and maybe we should invite him to sit with us tomorrow?","t":"你有注意到那位新同學總是一個人吃午餐嗎？也許我們明天應該邀他和我們一起坐。"},{"w":"notice","p":"n.","d":"a written sign or paper that gives information or a warning","c":"公告；通知","s":"The notice on the classroom door said that the English test had been moved to Thursday because the teacher was sick.","t":"教室門上的公告說英文考試因為老師生病改到星期四。"},{"w":"unnoticed","p":"adj.","d":"not seen or noticed by anyone","c":"未被注意到的","s":"The small mistake in the report went unnoticed for weeks, until a careful reader wrote to the newspaper to point it out.","t":"報告中的小錯誤幾週來都沒被注意到，直到一位細心的讀者寫信給報社指出來。"},{"w":"notify","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone officially about something","c":"通知","s":"The school will notify all parents by text message if classes are cancelled tomorrow because of the approaching typhoon.","t":"如果明天因颱風逼近而停課，學校會用簡訊通知所有家長。","h":1},{"w":"notify sb of sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to officially tell someone about something","c":"通知某人某事","s":"The airline notified passengers of the delay only twenty minutes before the flight, so many people were already waiting at the gate.","t":"航空公司在起飛前二十分鐘才通知乘客延誤的事，所以許多人早已在登機門等候。","a":"notified passengers of"},{"w":"notification","p":"n.","d":"a message or paper that officially tells you something","c":"通知","s":"I received a notification on my phone saying that my package had arrived at the convenience store down the street.","t":"我手機收到一則通知，說我的包裹已經送到街尾的便利商店了。"},{"w":"notion","p":"n.","d":"an idea or belief about something","c":"概念；想法","s":"My grandmother has the notion that cold drinks are bad for your health, so she always serves warm tea even in summer.","t":"我奶奶有個觀念，認為冷飲對健康不好，所以即使在夏天她也總是端出溫茶。","h":1},{"w":"have no notion of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have no idea or understanding of something","c":"對…毫無概念","s":"Before I visited the countryside, I had no notion of how hard farmers work, waking up before sunrise every single day.","t":"在我造訪鄉下之前，我完全不知道農民工作有多辛苦，每天日出前就得起床。","a":"had no notion of"},{"w":"notable","p":"adj.","d":"important or interesting enough to be noticed","c":"值得注意的；顯著的","s":"One notable change in the new library is the quiet reading room on the top floor, where phones are not allowed at all.","t":"新圖書館一個值得注意的改變是頂樓的安靜閱讀室，那裡完全不允許使用手機。"},{"w":"nowhere","p":"adv.","d":"not in or to any place","c":"任何地方都不；無處","s":"We drove around the busy night market area for forty minutes, but there was nowhere to park the car.","t":"我們在熱鬧的夜市附近繞了四十分鐘，但沒有任何地方可以停車。","h":1},{"w":"be nowhere to be found","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be impossible to find anywhere","c":"到處都找不到","s":"When the teacher wanted to collect the homework, my notebook was nowhere to be found, and I later discovered I had left it on the bus.","t":"老師要收作業時，我的筆記本到處都找不到，後來我才發現把它留在公車上了。","a":"was nowhere to be found"},{"w":"in the middle of nowhere","p":"phr.","d":"in a place far away from any town or city","c":"在荒郊野外","s":"Our car broke down in the middle of nowhere, and we had to walk for an hour before we found a small store with a phone.","t":"我們的車在荒郊野外拋錨了，我們走了一個小時才找到一家有電話的小店。"},{"w":"get nowhere","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make no progress or have no success","c":"毫無進展","s":"I tried to explain the problem to the customer service robot for an hour but got nowhere, so I finally asked for a real person.","t":"我試著向客服機器人解釋問題一個小時卻毫無進展，所以最後我要求找真人。","a":"got nowhere"},{"w":"out of nowhere","p":"phr.","d":"suddenly and unexpectedly","c":"突然冒出來；不知從何處","s":"A dog ran onto the road out of nowhere, and the driver had to stop so quickly that all the bags fell off the back seat.","t":"一隻狗突然冒出來跑到路上，司機不得不急停，後座的袋子全都掉了下來。"},{"w":"nutrient","p":"n.","d":"a substance in food that plants, animals, and people need to live and grow","c":"養分；營養素","s":"Spinach is rich in iron and other important nutrients, which is why my mother puts it in our soup at least twice a week.","t":"菠菜富含鐵質和其他重要的營養素，這就是為什麼我媽媽每週至少兩次把它放進我們的湯裡。","a":"nutrients","h":1},{"w":"nutrition","p":"n.","d":"the food you eat and the way it affects your health","c":"營養","s":"Good nutrition in the first years of life is extremely important, because children who eat well grow taller and learn more easily.","t":"生命最初幾年的良好營養極為重要，因為吃得好的孩子長得更高，學習也更容易。","h":1},{"w":"nutritious","p":"adj.","d":"containing substances that your body needs to stay healthy","c":"有營養的","s":"A bowl of oatmeal with fruit is a cheap and nutritious breakfast that keeps you full until lunchtime without any sugar.","t":"一碗加水果的燕麥粥是便宜又有營養的早餐，不含糖卻能讓你飽到午餐時間。"},{"w":"nutritional","p":"adj.","d":"connected with nutrition","c":"營養的；營養方面的","s":"Always read the nutritional information on the package before you buy snacks, because some look healthy but contain a lot of salt.","t":"買零食前一定要看包裝上的營養標示，因為有些看起來健康卻含有大量的鹽。"},{"w":"malnutrition","p":"n.","d":"bad health caused by not having enough food or the right kind of food","c":"營養不良","s":"The charity sends rice, beans, and milk powder to the village because many children there suffer from malnutrition during the dry season.","t":"這個慈善機構把米、豆子和奶粉送到那個村子，因為那裡有許多孩子在乾季時營養不良。"},{"w":"obligation","p":"n.","d":"something you must do because of a law, a rule, or a promise","c":"義務；責任","s":"Parents have a legal obligation to send their children to school, so the government checks on families whose kids stop attending.","t":"父母有送孩子上學的法律義務，所以政府會查訪那些孩子不再上學的家庭。","h":1},{"w":"have an obligation to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be required to do something because of a rule or a promise","c":"有義務…","s":"Since the company sold us a broken washing machine, it has an obligation to repair it for free or give us our money back.","t":"既然公司賣給我們一台壞掉的洗衣機，它就有義務免費修理或退錢給我們。","a":"has an obligation to"},{"w":"obligatory","p":"adj.","d":"something that you must do because of a rule or law","c":"必須的；強制性的","s":"Wearing a helmet is obligatory for everyone who rides a scooter in Taiwan, and the police will fine you if you forget.","t":"在台灣，所有騎機車的人都必須戴安全帽，如果忘了戴，警察會開罰。"},{"w":"oblige","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel that they must do something","c":"迫使；使負有義務","s":"The new rule will oblige every restaurant to show the price of each dish clearly before customers order their food.","t":"新規定將迫使每家餐廳在顧客點餐前清楚標示每道菜的價格。"},{"w":"be obliged to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have to do something because of a rule, law, or situation","c":"不得不；有義務","s":"Because of the heavy snow, the airline was obliged to cancel all its morning flights and give the passengers hotel rooms for the night.","t":"由於大雪，航空公司不得不取消所有早班航班，並為乘客安排當晚的旅館房間。","a":"was obliged to"}]},{"unit":24,"theme":"obscure – parallel","cards":[{"w":"obscure","p":"adj.","d":"not known by many people","c":"不知名的；默默無聞的","s":"The band was obscure for almost ten years, playing in small bars, until one of their songs was used in a popular TV drama.","t":"這個樂團有將近十年都默默無聞，只在小酒吧演出，直到他們的一首歌被一部熱門電視劇採用。","h":1},{"w":"obscure","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to understand or see clearly","c":"晦澀的；模糊的","s":"The poem is full of obscure words and old expressions, so our teacher spent the whole class explaining what it really means.","t":"這首詩充滿晦澀的字詞和古老的用語，所以我們老師花了一整節課解釋它真正的意思。"},{"w":"obscure","p":"v.","d":"to hide something so that it cannot be seen or understood clearly","c":"遮蔽；使模糊","s":"Thick fog began to obscure the road ahead, so the bus driver turned on his lights and slowed down to almost walking speed.","t":"濃霧開始遮蔽前方的道路，所以公車司機打開車燈，把速度放慢到幾乎像走路一樣。"},{"w":"obscurity","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being known or remembered","c":"默默無聞；無名","s":"After one hit song, the singer disappeared into obscurity, and today even her biggest fans cannot remember her full name.","t":"在一首暢銷歌曲之後，這位歌手就銷聲匿跡了，如今連她最忠實的粉絲都記不得她的全名。"},{"w":"observer","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches something carefully, often officially","c":"觀察者；觀察員","s":"An international observer sat at the back of the voting station all day to make sure that the election was fair.","t":"一位國際觀察員整天坐在投票所後面，確保選舉公平。","h":1},{"w":"observe","p":"v.","d":"to watch something carefully; to notice","c":"觀察；注意到","s":"The students were asked to observe the ants for twenty minutes and write down everything the insects did.","t":"學生們被要求觀察螞蟻二十分鐘，並寫下這些昆蟲做的每一件事。"},{"w":"observation","p":"n.","d":"the act of watching something carefully; a remark","c":"觀察；評論","s":"After three days of careful observation, the nurse decided that the baby was healthy enough to go home with his parents.","t":"經過三天仔細的觀察，護士決定寶寶已經夠健康，可以和父母一起回家了。"},{"w":"observant","p":"adj.","d":"good at noticing things","c":"觀察力敏銳的","s":"My little sister is very observant, and she was the first to notice that the neighbor's cat had been missing for two days.","t":"我妹妹觀察力很敏銳，她是第一個注意到鄰居的貓已經失蹤兩天的人。"},{"w":"odds","p":"n.","d":"how likely it is that something will or will not happen","c":"機率；可能性","s":"The odds of winning the lottery are extremely small, so my father says it is wiser to save the money in the bank.","t":"中樂透的機率極小，所以我爸爸說把錢存在銀行比較明智。","h":1},{"w":"against all odds","p":"phr.","d":"in spite of great difficulties; when success seemed impossible","c":"排除萬難；儘管困難重重","s":"Against all odds, the small village team beat the city champions in the final, and the whole town celebrated until midnight.","t":"儘管困難重重，這個小村莊的球隊在決賽中打敗了城市冠軍，整個鎮慶祝到半夜。","a":"Against all odds"},{"w":"be at odds with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to disagree with someone; to be different from something","c":"與…意見不合；與…不一致","s":"My brother is at odds with my parents about his future, because he wants to be a chef while they hope he will study law.","t":"我哥哥在未來的問題上與父母意見不合，因為他想當廚師，而他們希望他讀法律。","a":"is at odds with"},{"w":"odd","p":"adj.","d":"strange or unusual","c":"奇怪的；古怪的","s":"It was odd that the lights in the empty house were on at midnight, so we called the police to check it.","t":"那間空屋半夜燈還亮著很奇怪，所以我們報警去查看。"},{"w":"offering","p":"n.","d":"something that is given to a god as part of worship","c":"供品；祭品","s":"On the first day of Lunar New Year, my grandmother places an offering of oranges and rice cakes on the family altar.","t":"農曆新年的第一天，我奶奶會在家裡的神桌上擺上橘子和年糕作為供品。","h":1},{"w":"offering","p":"n.","d":"something that a company or person makes available for people to buy or enjoy","c":"提供的產品；作品","s":"The restaurant's newest offering is a mango ice dessert, and on hot afternoons the line for it goes out the door.","t":"這家餐廳最新推出的產品是芒果冰甜點，炎熱的下午排隊的人龍一直排到門外。"},{"w":"offer","p":"v.","d":"to say that you are willing to give or do something","c":"提供；主動提出","s":"When the old lady dropped her bags, a teenager stopped to offer help and carried everything to her door.","t":"當老太太的袋子掉了，一位青少年停下來主動提供幫助，把所有東西搬到她家門口。"},{"w":"offer","p":"n.","d":"something that someone says they will give you or do for you","c":"提議；報價","s":"She received a job offer from a company in Kaohsiung, but she is still thinking about whether she wants to move so far.","t":"她收到高雄一家公司的工作邀約，但她還在考慮是否願意搬到那麼遠的地方。"},{"w":"olive","p":"n.","d":"a small green or black fruit with a strong taste, often used to make oil","c":"橄欖","s":"My aunt always puts a few black olives on her pizza, although the rest of the family picks them off right away.","t":"我阿姨總是在披薩上放幾顆黑橄欖，雖然家裡其他人馬上就把它們挑掉。","a":"olives","h":1},{"w":"olive oil","p":"n.phr.","d":"oil made from olives, used in cooking","c":"橄欖油","s":"Many doctors recommend cooking with olive oil instead of butter, because it is better for your heart and still tastes great.","t":"許多醫生建議用橄欖油代替奶油做菜，因為它對心臟比較好，而且味道依然很棒。"},{"w":"olive","p":"adj.","d":"having a yellowish-green color","c":"橄欖綠的","s":"The soldiers wore olive uniforms that matched the color of the forest, so they were very hard to see among the trees.","t":"士兵們穿著和森林顏色相配的橄欖綠制服，所以在樹林間非常難被看見。"},{"w":"operational","p":"adj.","d":"working and ready to be used","c":"可運作的；運轉中的","s":"The new airport will not be fully operational until next spring, because the second runway still needs more safety checks.","t":"新機場要到明年春天才會完全投入運作，因為第二條跑道仍需要更多安全檢查。","h":1},{"w":"operate","p":"v.","d":"to work or run a machine, business, or system","c":"操作；經營；運作","s":"Only trained workers are allowed to operate this machine, because one small mistake could cause a serious accident.","t":"只有受過訓練的員工才可以操作這台機器，因為一個小錯誤就可能造成嚴重的意外。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n.","d":"the process of cutting open the body to repair or remove something; the way something works","c":"手術；運作","s":"My grandfather had an operation on his knee last month, and now he can walk up the stairs without any pain.","t":"我爺爺上個月膝蓋動了手術，現在他上樓梯已經完全不會痛了。"},{"w":"operator","p":"n.","d":"a person who works a machine or runs a business","c":"操作員；業者","s":"The crane operator lifted the heavy steel beam carefully onto the roof while the other workers watched from below.","t":"起重機操作員小心地把沉重的鋼樑吊到屋頂上，其他工人則在下方觀看。"},{"w":"opponent","p":"n.","d":"a person or team you compete or fight against","c":"對手","s":"In the chess final, Amy faced a much older opponent who had won the city championship twice, but she still played without fear.","t":"在西洋棋決賽中，艾咪面對一位年紀大得多、曾兩次贏得市冠軍的對手，但她依然毫無畏懼地下棋。","h":1},{"w":"opposition","p":"n.","d":"strong disagreement with a plan or idea; the people who disagree","c":"反對；反對者","s":"The plan to close the old park met with strong opposition from parents, who said their children had nowhere else to play.","t":"關閉老公園的計畫遭到家長強烈反對，他們說孩子們沒有別的地方可以玩。","h":1},{"w":"oppose","p":"v.","d":"to disagree with something and try to stop it","c":"反對","s":"Most of the villagers oppose the new factory, because they worry that it will pollute the river where they catch fish.","t":"大多數村民反對新工廠，因為他們擔心它會污染他們捕魚的河流。"},{"w":"be opposed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to disagree strongly with something","c":"反對…","s":"My grandmother is opposed to the idea of eating dinner in front of the television, so we always sit together at the table.","t":"我奶奶反對在電視前吃晚餐的想法，所以我們總是一起坐在餐桌旁。","a":"is opposed to"},{"w":"opposite","p":"adj.","d":"completely different; on the other side","c":"相反的；對面的","s":"My twin brother and I have opposite personalities: he loves big parties, while I would rather stay home with a good book.","t":"我和我的雙胞胎哥哥個性完全相反：他喜歡大型派對，而我寧願待在家裡看一本好書。"},{"w":"opt","p":"v.","d":"to choose one thing instead of another","c":"選擇","s":"Because the train tickets were sold out, we had to opt for the slower bus, which took almost five hours to reach Kenting.","t":"因為火車票賣完了，我們不得不選擇比較慢的巴士，花了將近五小時才到墾丁。","h":1},{"w":"optional","p":"adj.","d":"something you can choose to do or have, but do not have to","c":"可選擇的；非強制的","s":"The school trip to the science museum is optional, so students who do not want to go can stay and study in the library.","t":"去科學博物館的校外教學是自由參加的，所以不想去的學生可以留下來在圖書館讀書。","h":1},{"w":"opt for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to choose a particular thing","c":"選擇…","s":"When the waiter asked about dessert, most of us opted for the mango ice because it was a hot afternoon in July.","t":"當服務生問要什麼甜點時，我們大多數人選擇了芒果冰，因為那是七月一個炎熱的下午。","a":"opted for"},{"w":"opt out of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide not to take part in something","c":"選擇退出…","s":"You can opt out of the company newsletter at any time by clicking the small link at the bottom of the email.","t":"你可以隨時點擊電子郵件底部的小連結選擇退出公司電子報。"},{"w":"option","p":"n.","d":"one of the things you can choose","c":"選項；選擇","s":"If you cannot afford a new laptop, buying a used one is a good option, as long as you check it carefully first.","t":"如果你買不起新筆電，買二手的是個不錯的選擇，只要你先仔細檢查過它。"},{"w":"optimism","p":"n.","d":"the belief that good things will happen in the future","c":"樂觀","s":"Even after the typhoon destroyed half of his crops, the farmer spoke with optimism about the next harvest season.","t":"即使颱風毀了他一半的農作物，這位農夫仍樂觀地談論下一個收成季節。","h":1},{"w":"optimistic","p":"adj.","d":"believing that good things will happen","c":"樂觀的","s":"The coach is optimistic about the final because every player has been practicing hard and nobody is injured this time.","t":"教練對決賽感到樂觀，因為每位球員都很努力練習，而且這次沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"optimist","p":"n.","d":"a person who always expects good things to happen","c":"樂觀的人","s":"My mother is a true optimist: when it rains on our picnic day, she simply says the flowers in the garden needed water.","t":"我媽媽是個真正的樂觀主義者：野餐那天下雨時，她只說花園裡的花需要水。"},{"w":"optimistically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you expect good things to happen","c":"樂觀地","s":"The manager optimistically promised that the new store would open before Christmas, although the building was still only half finished.","t":"經理樂觀地承諾新店會在聖誕節前開幕，儘管大樓還只蓋了一半。"},{"w":"orchard","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land where fruit trees are grown","c":"果園","s":"My uncle owns a small orchard in Taichung, and every July the whole family goes there to help pick the sweet lychees.","t":"我叔叔在台中有一座小果園，每年七月全家人都會去那裡幫忙採甜美的荔枝。","h":1},{"w":"apple orchard","p":"n.phr.","d":"a field of apple trees","c":"蘋果園","s":"In autumn, the apple orchard near the lake opens to visitors, who pay a small fee and pick as many apples as they can carry.","t":"秋天時，湖邊的蘋果園對遊客開放，付少許費用就能採走你能搬得動的所有蘋果。"},{"w":"fruit tree","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tree that produces fruit people can eat","c":"果樹","s":"Grandpa planted a fruit tree in the backyard when I was born, and now it gives us juicy guavas every single winter.","t":"我出生時爺爺在後院種了一棵果樹，現在它每年冬天都結出多汁的芭樂給我們。"},{"w":"organism","p":"n.","d":"a living thing, such as a plant, an animal, or a bacterium","c":"生物；有機體","s":"Every organism in the pond, from the tiny insects to the big fish, depends on the plants that grow along its edge.","t":"池塘裡的每個生物，從微小的昆蟲到大魚，都依賴生長在池邊的植物。","h":1},{"w":"organ","p":"n.","d":"a part of the body that has a special job, such as the heart or the liver","c":"器官","s":"The heart is the organ that pumps blood around your body, and it beats about one hundred thousand times every day.","t":"心臟是把血液輸送到全身的器官，它每天大約跳動十萬次。"},{"w":"organic","p":"adj.","d":"grown or made without chemicals; coming from living things","c":"有機的","s":"Organic vegetables cost more at the market, but my mother buys them because she trusts the farmer who grows them without chemicals.","t":"有機蔬菜在市場上比較貴，但我媽媽還是買，因為她信任那位不用化學藥劑種菜的農夫。","a":"Organic"},{"w":"microorganism","p":"n.","d":"a living thing so small that you can only see it with a microscope","c":"微生物","s":"Washing your hands with soap removes most of the harmful microorganisms that you pick up from door handles and money.","t":"用肥皂洗手可以去除你從門把和鈔票上沾到的大多數有害微生物。","a":"microorganisms"},{"w":"originality","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being new and different, not copied from others","c":"獨創性；原創性","s":"The judges praised the originality of Ken's short film, because nobody had ever told a love story from the point of view of a cat.","t":"評審稱讚阿肯短片的原創性，因為從來沒有人從貓的角度講述愛情故事。","h":1},{"w":"original","p":"adj.","d":"new and interesting, not copied; existing from the beginning","c":"原創的；原本的","s":"Instead of copying ideas from the internet, try to come up with an original design for the poster that shows your own style.","t":"與其從網路上抄想法，不如試著為海報想出一個能展現你個人風格的原創設計。"},{"w":"originally","p":"adv.","d":"at first; in the beginning","c":"原本；起初","s":"The building was originally a train station, but it was turned into a shopping center after the railway moved underground.","t":"這棟建築原本是火車站，但在鐵路地下化後被改成了購物中心。"},{"w":"origin","p":"n.","d":"the place or point where something begins","c":"起源；出身","s":"Scientists are still studying the origin of the virus to find out whether it came from bats or from another animal.","t":"科學家仍在研究這個病毒的起源，想弄清楚它是來自蝙蝠還是其他動物。"},{"w":"originate","p":"v.","d":"to start or come from a particular place or time","c":"起源於；發源","s":"Bubble tea is said to originate in Taichung in the 1980s, and today you can find it in cities all around the world.","t":"據說珍珠奶茶在一九八〇年代起源於台中，如今你可以在世界各地的城市找到它。"},{"w":"outfit","p":"n.","d":"a set of clothes worn together, especially for a special occasion","c":"全套服裝","s":"Lisa bought a new outfit for her cousin's wedding, including a pink dress, white shoes, and a small matching handbag.","t":"麗莎為表姐的婚禮買了一套新服裝，包括粉紅色洋裝、白色鞋子和一個相配的小手提包。","h":1},{"w":"outfit","p":"v.","d":"to provide someone or something with the equipment or clothes they need","c":"裝備；配備","s":"The company will outfit every new delivery rider with a helmet, a rain jacket, and a large insulated bag.","t":"公司會為每位新的外送員配備安全帽、雨衣和一個大型保溫袋。"},{"w":"outfit","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together, such as a small company or band","c":"團體；小公司","s":"He started a small design outfit with two college friends, and now their team makes websites for restaurants across Taipei.","t":"他和兩位大學朋友成立了一個小型設計工作室，現在他們的團隊為台北各地的餐廳製作網站。"},{"w":"outlet","p":"n.","d":"a store that sells goods of one company, often at lower prices","c":"暢貨中心；直營店","s":"We drove to the shoe outlet outside the city, where last year's sneakers were sold for less than half of the normal price.","t":"我們開車到市郊的鞋子暢貨中心，去年的運動鞋在那裡以不到正常價格一半的價錢出售。","h":1},{"w":"outlet","p":"n.","d":"a way of expressing strong feelings or using energy","c":"發洩的管道；出口","s":"Playing the drums is a great outlet for my brother's stress, and after an hour of practice he is always calm and happy.","t":"打鼓是我哥哥發洩壓力的絕佳管道，練習一小時後他總是又平靜又開心。"},{"w":"electrical outlet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place in a wall where you plug in electrical equipment","c":"電源插座","s":"The cafe has an electrical outlet next to every table, so students can charge their laptops while they study for hours.","t":"這家咖啡館每張桌子旁都有電源插座，所以學生可以一邊讀書幾個小時一邊幫筆電充電。"},{"w":"outlet mall","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large shopping center where brand-name goods are sold at lower prices","c":"暢貨購物中心","s":"The new outlet mall near the airport attracts thousands of shoppers every weekend because of its big discounts on famous brands.","t":"機場附近的新暢貨購物中心每個週末都吸引數千名購物者，因為知名品牌有大折扣。"},{"w":"output","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something that a person, machine, or factory produces","c":"產量；產出","s":"The factory's output rose by thirty percent after the manager bought faster machines and gave the workers better training.","t":"經理買了更快的機器並給員工更好的訓練後，工廠的產量增加了百分之三十。","h":1},{"w":"output","p":"v.","d":"to produce information or power, especially from a computer or machine","c":"輸出","s":"The solar panels on our roof can output enough electricity on a sunny day to run the air conditioner all afternoon.","t":"我們屋頂的太陽能板在晴天可以輸出足夠的電力，讓冷氣整個下午運轉。"},{"w":"output","p":"n.","d":"the information a computer produces","c":"輸出資料","s":"If the program's output shows an error message, check whether you typed the numbers in the right order first.","t":"如果程式的輸出結果顯示錯誤訊息，先檢查你輸入數字的順序是否正確。"},{"w":"input","p":"n.","d":"information or ideas that are put into something","c":"輸入；投入的意見","s":"The teacher asked for input from every student before she decided where the class would go on the spring trip.","t":"老師在決定班上春季旅行要去哪裡之前，向每位學生徵求意見。"},{"w":"outsider","p":"n.","d":"a person who does not belong to a particular group or place","c":"局外人；外人","s":"When I first moved to the small town, I felt like an outsider, because everyone else had known each other since childhood.","t":"我剛搬到那個小鎮時覺得自己像個外人，因為其他人從小就彼此認識。","h":1},{"w":"outside","p":"prep.","d":"not inside a building or place","c":"在…外面","s":"The children waited outside the school gate for almost an hour before the bus finally arrived to take them to the zoo.","t":"孩子們在校門外等了將近一個小時，接他們去動物園的巴士才終於到達。"},{"w":"insider","p":"n.","d":"a person who belongs to a group and knows things others do not","c":"內部人士；知情者","s":"According to an insider at the company, the new phone will be cheaper than everyone expects when it goes on sale next month.","t":"根據公司一位內部人士的說法，新手機下個月上市時會比大家預期的便宜。"},{"w":"the outside world","p":"n.phr.","d":"the world beyond your own small community or place","c":"外面的世界","s":"The village had no internet until last year, so the people there knew very little about the outside world.","t":"這個村子直到去年才有網路，所以那裡的人對外面的世界知道得很少。"},{"w":"overall","p":"adj.","d":"including everything; considered as a whole","c":"整體的；全面的","s":"Our team lost the last game, but the overall result of the season was excellent, with eight wins out of ten matches.","t":"我們隊輸了最後一場比賽，但本季的整體成績非常優秀，十場比賽贏了八場。","h":1},{"w":"overall","p":"adv.","d":"generally; when everything is considered","c":"整體而言；總的來說","s":"The hotel room was small and the breakfast was simple, but overall we enjoyed our stay because the staff were so friendly.","t":"飯店房間很小，早餐也很簡單，但整體而言我們很享受這次住宿，因為員工非常友善。"},{"w":"overalls","p":"n.","d":"loose trousers with a piece covering the chest, worn for work","c":"吊帶工作褲","s":"The painter put on his old blue overalls before he started work, because he knew the paint would get everywhere.","t":"油漆工開工前穿上他那件舊的藍色吊帶工作褲，因為他知道油漆會沾得到處都是。"},{"w":"overhead","p":"adv.","d":"above your head, in the sky","c":"在頭頂上；在上方","s":"We lay on the grass and watched the airplanes fly overhead, trying to guess which countries they were going to.","t":"我們躺在草地上看著飛機從頭頂上飛過，試著猜它們要飛往哪些國家。","h":1},{"w":"overhead","p":"adj.","d":"placed above your head","c":"頭頂上的；架空的","s":"Please put your small bags in the overhead locker and keep the space under the seat in front of you free.","t":"請把小型行李放進頭頂上的置物櫃，並保持前方座位下的空間淨空。"},{"w":"overhead","p":"n.","d":"the regular costs of running a business, such as rent and electricity","c":"營運成本；經常性開支","s":"The small bookshop closed because its overhead was too high; the rent alone took most of the money it made each month.","t":"那家小書店因為營運成本太高而關門了；光是房租就佔了它每月收入的大部分。"},{"w":"oversee, oversaw, overseen","p":"v.","d":"to watch and direct work to make sure it is done correctly","c":"監督；管理","s":"Mrs. Chen was hired to oversee the building of the new library and report any problems to the city government.","t":"陳女士受聘來監督新圖書館的興建，並向市政府回報任何問題。","a":"oversee","h":1},{"w":"overseer","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches and directs the work of others","c":"監督者；工頭","s":"The overseer walked around the factory floor all day, checking that each worker was following the safety rules.","t":"監工整天在工廠裡走動，檢查每位工人是否遵守安全規定。"},{"w":"oversee a project","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be in charge of a piece of work from start to finish","c":"監督一項專案","s":"It was the first time she had been asked to oversee a project by herself, so she made a careful plan for every week.","t":"這是她第一次被要求獨自監督一項專案，所以她為每一週都做了仔細的計畫。"},{"w":"overlook","p":"v.","d":"to fail to notice something; to have a view over something","c":"忽略；俯瞰","s":"It is easy to overlook small spelling mistakes when you read your own essay, so ask a friend to check it before you hand it in.","t":"讀自己的作文時很容易忽略小的拼字錯誤，所以交出去之前請朋友幫你檢查。"},{"w":"overtake, overtook, overtaken","p":"v.","d":"to pass a vehicle or person that is going more slowly","c":"超越；超車","s":"It is dangerous to overtake a truck on a mountain road, because you cannot see whether another car is coming around the bend.","t":"在山路上超越卡車很危險，因為你看不到彎道另一邊是否有車過來。","a":"overtake","h":1},{"w":"overtake","p":"v.","d":"to become bigger, better, or more important than something else","c":"超過；趕上","s":"Online shopping is expected to overtake shopping in stores within a few years, as more people buy everything from their phones.","t":"預計幾年內網路購物將超越實體商店購物，因為越來越多人用手機買所有東西。"},{"w":"take over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take control of something, such as a business or a job","c":"接管；接手","s":"When my father retires next year, my older sister will take over the family restaurant and run it with her husband.","t":"我爸爸明年退休時，我姐姐會接手家裡的餐廳，和她丈夫一起經營。"},{"w":"takeover","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking control of a company by buying it","c":"收購；接管","s":"After the takeover by the bigger company, many workers were afraid that they would lose their jobs before the end of the year.","t":"被較大的公司收購之後，許多員工擔心年底前會失去工作。"},{"w":"overturn","p":"v.","d":"to turn something over so that it is upside down","c":"翻倒；推翻（物體）","s":"A strong wind came through the open window and overturned the vase, spilling water all over my homework.","t":"一陣強風從打開的窗戶吹進來，翻倒了花瓶，水灑滿了我的作業。","a":"overturned","h":1},{"w":"overturn","p":"v.","d":"to officially change a decision so that it is no longer valid","c":"推翻（判決、決定）","s":"The higher court decided to overturn the earlier decision after new evidence showed that the man had been at home that night.","t":"在新證據顯示那名男子當晚在家後，上級法院決定推翻先前的判決。"},{"w":"turn over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move something so that the other side faces up","c":"翻過來；翻面","s":"Please turn over your test paper and do not start writing until the teacher tells you that the time has begun.","t":"請把你的試卷翻過來，在老師說計時開始之前不要動筆。"},{"w":"turnover","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money a business receives in a period of time","c":"營業額","s":"The night market stall has a surprisingly high turnover on weekends, selling more than a thousand cups of bubble tea a night.","t":"這個夜市攤位週末的營業額高得驚人，一晚賣出超過一千杯珍珠奶茶。"},{"w":"overwhelm","p":"v.","d":"to be so much or so strong that someone cannot deal with it","c":"使難以承受；壓倒","s":"The amount of homework in the first week of senior high school can overwhelm new students, so teachers advise them to plan their time well.","t":"高中第一週的作業量可能會讓新生難以承受，所以老師建議他們好好規劃時間。","h":1},{"w":"be overwhelmed by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be strongly affected by a feeling or by too much of something","c":"被…淹沒；深受…影響","s":"When she saw her whole family waiting at the airport with flowers, she was overwhelmed by joy and started to cry.","t":"當她看到全家人拿著花在機場等候時，她被喜悅淹沒，開始哭了起來。","a":"was overwhelmed by"},{"w":"overwhelming","p":"adj.","d":"very great in amount or strength; difficult to deal with","c":"壓倒性的；難以抗拒的","s":"The new policy won overwhelming support in the vote, with more than ninety percent of the members saying yes.","t":"新政策在投票中獲得壓倒性的支持，超過九成的成員投了贊成票。"},{"w":"overwhelmingly","p":"adv.","d":"by a very large amount; to a very great degree","c":"壓倒性地；絕大多數地","s":"The students voted overwhelmingly in favor of a later start to the school day, and the principal promised to consider the idea.","t":"學生們壓倒性地投票贊成延後上學時間，校長承諾會考慮這個想法。"},{"w":"parallel","p":"adj.","d":"two lines or things that are the same distance apart along their whole length","c":"平行的","s":"The two roads run parallel to each other for about five kilometers before they finally meet at the bridge.","t":"這兩條路平行延伸大約五公里，最後才在橋邊交會。","h":1},{"w":"parallel","p":"n.","d":"a similarity between two things that happen at different times or places","c":"相似之處；類似情況","s":"There is a clear parallel between the two stories: in both, a poor boy becomes rich and then loses everything.","t":"這兩個故事有明顯的相似之處：在兩者中，一個窮男孩都變得富有，然後失去一切。"},{"w":"parallel","p":"v.","d":"to happen at the same time as something and be similar to it","c":"與…相似；與…並行","s":"The growth of the city's bike paths seems to parallel the rise in the number of people who cycle to work every day.","t":"城市自行車道的成長似乎與每天騎車上班人數的增加並行。"},{"w":"draw a parallel between","p":"v.phr.","d":"to point out how two things are similar","c":"指出…之間的相似之處","s":"The teacher asked us to draw a parallel between the novel and real events in Taiwan's history, and we found more than we expected.","t":"老師要我們指出這本小說和台灣歷史真實事件之間的相似之處，結果我們發現的比預期的還多。"},{"w":"in parallel","p":"phr.","d":"at the same time, side by side","c":"同時；並行地","s":"The two teams worked in parallel on different parts of the app, so the whole project was finished a month earlier than planned.","t":"兩個團隊同時處理這個 App 的不同部分，所以整個專案比計畫提前一個月完成。"}]},{"unit":25,"theme":"participant – phase","cards":[{"w":"participant","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in an activity or event","c":"參與者","s":"Every participant in the marathon receives a medal at the finish line, no matter how long it takes him or her to complete the race.","t":"馬拉松的每位參與者在終點線都會得到一面獎牌，不論他或她花多久時間完成比賽。","h":1},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity or event","c":"參加；參與","s":"Students who participate in the school play must come to practice every afternoon for the next three weeks.","t":"參加學校話劇演出的學生在接下來三週每天下午都必須來排練。"},{"w":"participate in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take part in something","c":"參與…","s":"My grandmother still participates in the morning dance group at the park, although she is already eighty years old.","t":"我奶奶雖然已經八十歲了，但仍然參與公園裡的晨間舞蹈團。","a":"participates in"},{"w":"participation","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in something","c":"參與","s":"The teacher gives extra points for class participation, so even shy students try to answer at least one question each week.","t":"老師會為課堂參與加分，所以即使是害羞的學生每週也會試著至少回答一個問題。"},{"w":"particle","p":"n.","d":"a very small piece of something","c":"微粒；粒子","s":"After the sandstorm, every particle of dust in the air seemed to find its way into our house, and we spent the whole weekend cleaning.","t":"沙塵暴過後，空氣中的每一粒灰塵似乎都跑進了我們家，我們整個週末都在打掃。","h":1},{"w":"dust particle","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tiny piece of dust","c":"灰塵微粒","s":"When sunlight shines through the window in the morning, you can see thousands of dust particles floating slowly in the air.","t":"早晨陽光穿過窗戶照進來時，你可以看到成千上萬的灰塵微粒在空中緩緩飄浮。","a":"dust particles"},{"w":"particular","p":"adj.","d":"special; this one and not any other","c":"特定的；特別的","s":"Is there any particular reason why you want to sit by the window, or would any seat on the bus be fine for you?","t":"你想坐窗邊有什麼特別的原因嗎？還是公車上任何座位對你來說都可以？"},{"w":"particularly","p":"adv.","d":"especially; more than usual","c":"特別地；尤其","s":"The night market is particularly crowded on Saturday evenings, so we usually go on a weekday when there is more room to walk.","t":"夜市在星期六晚上特別擁擠，所以我們通常在平日去，那時走路的空間比較多。"},{"w":"partly","p":"adv.","d":"to some degree, but not completely","c":"部分地；在某種程度上","s":"The accident was partly my fault, because I was looking at my phone instead of watching the road when I crossed.","t":"這場意外有部分是我的錯，因為我過馬路時在看手機而不是看路。","h":1},{"w":"part","p":"n.","d":"one of the pieces that something is made of","c":"部分","s":"The most exciting part of the movie comes near the end, when the hero finally finds out who the real thief is.","t":"這部電影最刺激的部分在接近結尾時，主角終於發現真正的小偷是誰。"},{"w":"partial","p":"adj.","d":"not complete; only in part","c":"部分的；不完全的","s":"The doctor said my grandfather had made a partial recovery, since he can walk again but still cannot climb stairs easily.","t":"醫生說我爺爺已經部分康復了，因為他可以再走路了，但還不能輕鬆爬樓梯。"},{"w":"partially","p":"adv.","d":"not completely; partly","c":"部分地","s":"The road was partially blocked by a fallen tree after the typhoon, so cars had to drive very slowly around it.","t":"颱風過後，道路被倒下的樹部分堵住，所以車子必須非常緩慢地繞過它。"},{"w":"passionate","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing very strong feelings about something","c":"熱情的；熱愛的","s":"Our science teacher is so passionate about space that she stays after school to show us the stars through her own telescope.","t":"我們的理化老師對太空非常熱愛，她放學後留下來用她自己的望遠鏡給我們看星星。","h":1},{"w":"be passionate about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to love something very much and care about it deeply","c":"熱愛…","s":"Ever since he was a child, my brother has been passionate about cooking, and now he runs a small Italian restaurant downtown.","t":"我哥哥從小就熱愛烹飪，現在他在市中心經營一家小型義大利餐廳。","a":"has been passionate about"},{"w":"passion","p":"n.","d":"a very strong feeling of love or interest for something","c":"熱情；熱愛","s":"Music has always been her greatest passion, so nobody was surprised when she decided to study at a music college.","t":"音樂一直是她最大的熱情所在，所以當她決定進音樂學院就讀時，沒有人感到驚訝。"},{"w":"passionately","p":"adv.","d":"with very strong feelings","c":"熱情地；激動地","s":"The young lawyer spoke passionately about protecting the river, and by the end of her speech, half of the audience was standing and clapping.","t":"這位年輕律師激昂地談論保護河流，她演講結束時，半數聽眾都站起來鼓掌。"},{"w":"pastry","p":"n.","d":"a mixture of flour, fat, and water, baked and used to make pies","c":"酥皮；油酥麵團","s":"My aunt rolls out the pastry very thin before she fills it with apples, which is why her pies are always light and crispy.","t":"我阿姨在填入蘋果之前會把酥皮擀得很薄，這就是為什麼她的派總是輕盈又酥脆。","h":1},{"w":"pastry","p":"n.","d":"a small sweet cake made with pastry","c":"酥皮點心；糕點","s":"The cafe sells a different pastry every morning, and today's was a warm chocolate croissant that sold out before nine.","t":"這家咖啡館每天早上賣不同的糕點，今天是溫熱的巧克力可頌，九點前就賣完了。"},{"w":"pastry chef","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cook who makes cakes, pies, and sweet baked food","c":"糕點師傅","s":"After studying in Paris for two years, Kevin returned to Taipei and became the pastry chef at a famous five-star hotel.","t":"在巴黎學習兩年後，凱文回到台北，成為一家知名五星級飯店的糕點師傅。"},{"w":"paste","p":"n.","d":"a soft, thick, wet mixture","c":"糊；醬","s":"Mix the flour and water into a smooth paste, and then use it to stick the colored paper onto the lantern.","t":"把麵粉和水混合成滑順的糊，然後用它把彩色紙黏到燈籠上。"},{"w":"patch","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of material used to cover a hole","c":"補丁；貼片","s":"My mother sewed a patch shaped like a star over the hole in my jeans, and now all my friends want one too.","t":"我媽媽在我牛仔褲的破洞上縫了一個星形的補丁，現在我所有的朋友也都想要一個。","h":1},{"w":"patch","p":"n.","d":"a small area of something that is different from what is around it","c":"小塊區域；小片土地","s":"Grandpa grows tomatoes and beans in a small patch of land behind the house, and we eat them fresh all summer.","t":"爺爺在屋後一小塊土地上種番茄和豆子，整個夏天我們都吃新鮮採收的。"},{"w":"patch","p":"v.","d":"to repair a hole by putting a piece of material over it","c":"修補","s":"The old fisherman sat on the beach to patch his torn net, because he could not afford to buy a new one before the season began.","t":"老漁夫坐在海灘上修補他破掉的漁網，因為在漁季開始前他買不起新的。"},{"w":"patch up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become friends again after an argument; to repair quickly","c":"和好；暫時修好","s":"The two brothers finally decided to patch up their differences before their mother's birthday, so the family dinner was peaceful.","t":"兩兄弟終於決定在媽媽生日前和解彼此的分歧，所以家庭晚餐很平和。"},{"w":"eye patch","p":"n.phr.","d":"a piece of material worn over one eye to protect it","c":"眼罩","s":"After the operation, the doctor told Jason to wear an eye patch for a week so that bright light would not hurt his eye.","t":"手術後，醫生要傑森戴一週眼罩，這樣強光才不會傷到他的眼睛。"},{"w":"patent","p":"n.","d":"an official right to be the only person who can make or sell an invention","c":"專利","s":"The inventor has a patent on her folding bicycle, so no other company is allowed to copy the design for twenty years.","t":"這位發明家擁有她摺疊腳踏車的專利，所以二十年內其他公司都不能複製這個設計。","h":1},{"w":"apply for a patent","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask the government for the right to own an invention","c":"申請專利","s":"Before you show your invention to any company, you should apply for a patent, or someone else may steal your idea.","t":"在你把發明展示給任何公司之前，你應該先申請專利，否則別人可能會偷走你的想法。"},{"w":"patent","p":"v.","d":"to get a patent for an invention","c":"取得…的專利","s":"The two college students decided to patent their water-saving shower head before selling it online to customers around the world.","t":"這兩位大學生決定在把省水蓮蓬頭賣給世界各地的顧客之前，先為它申請專利。"},{"w":"patented","p":"adj.","d":"protected by a patent","c":"有專利的","s":"The company's patented cooling system keeps the laptop quiet even when you play games for hours, and no competitor has anything like it.","t":"這家公司有專利的散熱系統即使你玩遊戲好幾個小時也能讓筆電保持安靜，沒有競爭對手有類似的東西。"},{"w":"pathetic","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel sad or sorry for someone","c":"可憐的；令人同情的","s":"The lost kitten looked so pathetic sitting in the rain that the children carried it home and gave it warm milk.","t":"那隻走失的小貓坐在雨中看起來可憐極了，孩子們把牠抱回家並給牠溫牛奶。","h":1},{"w":"pathetic","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or weak; not good enough","c":"差勁的；可悲的","s":"Our team's defense was pathetic in the first half, and we let the other side score four goals in just twenty minutes.","t":"我們隊上半場的防守差勁極了，短短二十分鐘就讓對方進了四球。"},{"w":"pathetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that makes you feel sad or that is very weak","c":"可憐地；差勁地","s":"The old dog cried pathetically at the door every night after its owner moved away, until the neighbors finally adopted it.","t":"主人搬走後，那隻老狗每晚都在門口可憐地哀鳴，直到鄰居終於收養了牠。"},{"w":"sympathetic","p":"adj.","d":"kind to someone who has a problem and understanding their feelings","c":"有同情心的；體諒的","s":"The teacher was very sympathetic when I explained that my grandfather was in the hospital, and she let me hand in my essay later.","t":"當我解釋我爺爺住院時，老師非常體諒，讓我晚一點再交作文。"},{"w":"sympathy","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being sorry for someone who has a problem","c":"同情","s":"Hundreds of people sent cards and flowers to show their sympathy for the families who lost their homes in the fire.","t":"數百人寄來卡片和鮮花，向在火災中失去家園的家庭表達同情。"},{"w":"patrol","p":"n.","d":"the act of going around an area regularly to check that it is safe","c":"巡邏","s":"The security guards make a patrol of the whole building every two hours at night to check that all the doors are locked.","t":"保全人員晚上每兩小時巡邏整棟大樓一次，檢查所有的門是否都鎖好了。","h":1},{"w":"patrol","p":"v.","d":"to go around an area regularly to check that it is safe","c":"巡邏","s":"Police officers on bicycles patrol the river park on weekends, so families with small children feel safe playing there.","t":"警察週末騎著腳踏車巡邏河濱公園，所以帶著小孩的家庭在那裡玩覺得很安全。"},{"w":"on patrol","p":"phr.","d":"going around an area to check that it is safe","c":"在巡邏中","s":"While the two officers were on patrol near the night market, they noticed a lost little boy crying beside a food stall.","t":"兩位警員在夜市附近巡邏時，注意到一個迷路的小男孩在小吃攤旁哭。"},{"w":"patrol car","p":"n.phr.","d":"a police car used for driving around an area","c":"巡邏車","s":"A patrol car with flashing blue lights stopped beside us and asked whether we had seen a red motorcycle go past.","t":"一輛閃著藍燈的巡邏車在我們旁邊停下來，問我們有沒有看到一輛紅色機車經過。"},{"w":"patron","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives money or support to an artist, a museum, or a cause","c":"贊助人；資助者","s":"A rich businessman became the patron of the young painter and paid for her studio, her paints, and her first show in Taipei.","t":"一位富有的商人成為這位年輕畫家的贊助人，為她支付畫室、顏料和她在台北的第一次展覽費用。","h":1},{"w":"patron","p":"n.","d":"a person who regularly uses a particular shop, restaurant, or hotel","c":"老顧客；主顧","s":"Mr. Lee has been a patron of this noodle shop for thirty years, and the owner always gives him an extra egg for free.","t":"李先生三十年來一直是這家麵店的老主顧，老闆總是免費多給他一顆蛋。"},{"w":"patronize","p":"v.","d":"to be a regular customer of a shop or restaurant","c":"光顧","s":"My parents prefer to patronize the small family bakery on our street rather than the big supermarket, because the bread is fresher.","t":"我父母比較喜歡光顧我們街上的小型家庭麵包店，而不是大超市，因為麵包比較新鮮。"},{"w":"peasant","p":"n.","d":"a poor farmer who owns or rents a small piece of land, especially in the past","c":"農民；佃農","s":"In the old days, a peasant had to give a large part of his rice to the landlord, so his own family often went hungry in winter.","t":"在舊時代，農民必須把一大部分稻米交給地主，所以他自己的家人冬天常常挨餓。","h":1},{"w":"peasant farmer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a poor farmer who grows food mainly for his own family","c":"小農；貧農","s":"My great-grandfather was a peasant farmer in southern Taiwan who grew sweet potatoes and never traveled more than ten kilometers from home.","t":"我的曾祖父是台灣南部的一位小農，種植地瓜，一生從未離家超過十公里。"},{"w":"peasant","p":"adj.","d":"connected with poor farmers and their simple way of life","c":"農民的；鄉村的","s":"The museum has a room showing traditional peasant clothing, wooden tools, and the simple homes that farming families once lived in.","t":"博物館有一間展示傳統農民服裝、木製工具以及農家曾經居住的簡樸房屋的展廳。"},{"w":"pedal","p":"n.","d":"a flat part of a bicycle or machine that you push with your foot","c":"踏板","s":"The left pedal on my bike came loose on the way to school, so I had to push the bike for the last kilometer.","t":"我腳踏車的左邊踏板在上學途中鬆脫了，所以最後一公里我只好推著車走。","h":1},{"w":"pedal","p":"v.","d":"to push the pedals of a bicycle with your feet to make it move","c":"踩踏板；騎（腳踏車）","s":"We had to pedal as fast as we could to get home before the heavy rain started, and we still arrived completely wet.","t":"我們必須盡全力踩踏板，好在大雨開始前到家，結果到家時還是全身濕透。"},{"w":"gas pedal","p":"n.phr.","d":"the pedal in a car that you press to make it go faster","c":"油門踏板","s":"The driving teacher told me to press the gas pedal gently, because the car jumped forward every time I pushed it too hard.","t":"駕訓班教練要我輕踩油門，因為每次我踩太用力，車子就會往前衝。"},{"w":"brake pedal","p":"n.phr.","d":"the pedal in a car that you press to make it slow down or stop","c":"煞車踏板","s":"When the dog ran into the road, my father hit the brake pedal so hard that all the shopping bags flew off the back seat.","t":"當狗跑到路上時，我爸爸用力踩煞車，後座所有的購物袋都飛了出去。"},{"w":"pedestrian","p":"n.","d":"a person who is walking, especially in a town or city","c":"行人","s":"Drivers must stop when a pedestrian is waiting at the zebra crossing, but many people in this city forget the rule.","t":"當行人在斑馬線前等候時，駕駛必須停車，但這個城市裡許多人忘了這條規定。","h":1},{"w":"pedestrian","p":"adj.","d":"for people who are walking, not for cars","c":"行人的；步行的","s":"The city turned the old shopping street into a pedestrian area, so now families can walk there safely without worrying about traffic.","t":"市政府把老商店街改成行人徒步區，現在家庭可以安全地在那裡走動，不用擔心車流。"},{"w":"pedestrian crossing","p":"n.phr.","d":"a marked place on a road where people can cross safely","c":"行人穿越道","s":"Always use the pedestrian crossing even if it means walking a little further, because the traffic on this road is fast and dangerous.","t":"即使要多走一點路，也一定要走行人穿越道，因為這條路上的車速又快又危險。"},{"w":"pedestrian zone","p":"n.phr.","d":"a street or area where cars are not allowed","c":"行人徒步區","s":"On weekends, the street in front of the temple becomes a pedestrian zone, and food stalls and street musicians fill the space.","t":"週末時，廟前的街道變成行人徒步區，小吃攤和街頭音樂家擠滿了整個空間。"},{"w":"penetrate","p":"v.","d":"to go into or through something, especially something hard","c":"穿透；滲入","s":"The rain was so heavy that it began to penetrate my jacket, and by the time I got home my shirt was wet too.","t":"雨大到開始滲透我的外套，等我到家時，襯衫也濕了。","h":1},{"w":"penetrate","p":"v.","d":"to enter a market, an area, or a group and become part of it","c":"打入（市場）；滲透","s":"The small tea company hopes to penetrate the Japanese market next year by selling its bubble tea in convenience stores there.","t":"這家小型茶飲公司希望明年透過在日本便利商店販售珍珠奶茶，打入日本市場。"},{"w":"penetration","p":"n.","d":"the act of going into or through something","c":"穿透；滲透；（市場）占有","s":"Sunscreen protects your skin by slowing the penetration of harmful rays, so put it on at least twenty minutes before you go outside.","t":"防曬乳透過減緩有害光線的穿透來保護皮膚，所以出門前至少二十分鐘就要塗上。"},{"w":"penetrating","p":"adj.","d":"very sharp or strong, so that it seems to go through things; showing deep understanding","c":"刺耳的；敏銳的","s":"The detective gave the nervous young man a penetrating look, and within a minute the boy admitted that he had taken the money.","t":"偵探給了那個緊張的年輕人一個銳利的眼神，不到一分鐘男孩就承認錢是他拿的。"},{"w":"pension","p":"n.","d":"money paid regularly to a person who has stopped working because of age or illness","c":"退休金；養老金","s":"After thirty-five years as a teacher, my grandmother now lives on her monthly pension, which is enough for a quiet life.","t":"當了三十五年老師之後，我奶奶現在靠每月的退休金生活，足以過安靜的日子。","h":1},{"w":"pension fund","p":"n.phr.","d":"money that is saved and invested to pay people's pensions","c":"退休基金","s":"Every month, part of my father's salary goes into a pension fund, so that he will have enough money when he stops working at sixty-five.","t":"每個月我爸爸薪水的一部分會存入退休基金，這樣他六十五歲不工作時就會有足夠的錢。"},{"w":"pensioner","p":"n.","d":"a person who receives a pension","c":"領退休金者；退休人士","s":"The MRT offers a cheaper ticket to every pensioner over sixty-five, so many older people travel around the city during the day.","t":"捷運為每位六十五歲以上的退休人士提供較便宜的票價，所以許多年長者白天在城市裡四處走動。"},{"w":"retire on a pension","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop working and live on regular payments","c":"靠退休金退休","s":"My uncle plans to retire on a pension at sixty and spend his time fishing, which he never had a chance to do while he was working.","t":"我叔叔打算六十歲靠退休金退休，把時間花在釣魚上，那是他工作時從來沒機會做的事。"},{"w":"perceive","p":"v.","d":"to notice or understand something in a particular way","c":"察覺；認為；看待","s":"Young children often perceive time differently from adults, which is why a two-hour car ride feels like a whole day to them.","t":"幼童對時間的感知常常和大人不同，這就是為什麼兩小時的車程對他們來說像一整天。","h":1},{"w":"perception","p":"n.","d":"the way you notice or understand something; an opinion about something","c":"感知；看法","s":"Social media has changed many teenagers' perception of beauty, because they compare themselves with edited photos every single day.","t":"社群媒體改變了許多青少年對美的看法，因為他們每天都拿自己和修過的照片比較。","h":1},{"w":"be perceived as","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be seen or understood by people as a certain kind of thing","c":"被視為…","s":"In some countries, giving a clock as a present may be perceived as rude, so always ask a local friend before choosing a gift.","t":"在某些國家，送時鐘當禮物可能被視為不禮貌，所以挑禮物前一定要先問問當地朋友。"},{"w":"perceptive","p":"adj.","d":"quick to notice and understand things","c":"敏銳的；有洞察力的","s":"Our class teacher is very perceptive; she noticed that Ann was unhappy long before any of her friends realized something was wrong.","t":"我們的班導師非常敏銳；她早在安的任何朋友發現不對勁之前，就注意到安不開心。"},{"w":"performer","p":"n.","d":"a person who acts, sings, dances, or plays music for an audience","c":"表演者","s":"The best performer of the night was a twelve-year-old girl who played the drums so well that the whole audience stood up.","t":"當晚最棒的表演者是一位十二歲的女孩，她鼓打得好到全場觀眾都站了起來。","h":1},{"w":"perform","p":"v.","d":"to do something in front of an audience; to do a job or task","c":"表演；執行","s":"Our dance club will perform at the school festival next Friday, so we are practicing every day after class until six.","t":"我們的舞蹈社下週五要在校慶表演，所以我們每天放學後都練到六點。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"the act of entertaining an audience; how well someone does something","c":"表演；表現","s":"Her performance in the final exam was much better than last time, because she had studied a little every day instead of all at once.","t":"她在期末考的表現比上次好得多，因為她每天讀一點，而不是一次全部讀完。"},{"w":"street performer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who performs outdoors in public places for money","c":"街頭藝人","s":"The street performer outside the MRT station juggled five balls while riding a tall bicycle, and the crowd threw coins into his hat.","t":"捷運站外的街頭藝人一邊騎高腳踏車一邊拋接五顆球，群眾把硬幣丟進他的帽子裡。"},{"w":"persist","p":"v.","d":"to continue doing something even though it is difficult or other people are against it","c":"堅持；執意","s":"Although everyone told him that learning the violin at fifty was too late, my father decided to persist and now plays beautifully.","t":"雖然大家都告訴他五十歲學小提琴太晚了，我爸爸決定堅持下去，現在拉得非常動聽。","h":1},{"w":"persist","p":"v.","d":"to continue to exist or happen for a long time","c":"持續存在","s":"If the pain in your knee continues to persist after a week of rest, you should see a doctor instead of waiting any longer.","t":"如果休息一週後膝蓋的疼痛仍然持續，你應該去看醫生，而不是再等下去。"},{"w":"persist in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep doing something, especially something annoying or wrong","c":"堅持（做）…；執意…","s":"My little brother persists in calling the cat \"Dog\" even though we have explained a hundred times that it is not one.","t":"我弟弟執意叫那隻貓「狗狗」，即使我們已經解釋了一百次牠不是狗。","a":"persists in"},{"w":"persistent","p":"adj.","d":"continuing to do something although it is difficult; lasting for a long time","c":"堅持不懈的；持續的","s":"After three weeks of persistent coughing, my mother finally agreed to go to the clinic instead of just drinking more hot tea.","t":"持續咳嗽三週後，我媽媽終於同意去診所，而不是只喝更多熱茶。"},{"w":"persistence","p":"n.","d":"the quality of continuing to try even when it is difficult","c":"毅力；堅持","s":"Thanks to her persistence, Amy finally passed the swimming test on her fifth try, while most of her friends had given up.","t":"多虧了她的毅力，艾咪在第五次嘗試時終於通過游泳測驗，而她大多數的朋友早已放棄。"},{"w":"personnel","p":"n.","d":"the people who work for a company or organization","c":"員工；人員","s":"All medical personnel at the hospital must wear masks during the flu season to protect patients who are already weak.","t":"流感季節期間，醫院所有醫療人員都必須戴口罩，以保護已經虛弱的病人。","h":1},{"w":"personnel department","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of a company that deals with hiring and looking after workers","c":"人事部門","s":"If you want to change your working hours, you need to send a form to the personnel department at least two weeks in advance.","t":"如果你想更改工作時間，你需要至少提前兩週把表格送到人事部門。"},{"w":"personal","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to or connected with one particular person","c":"個人的；私人的","s":"Please do not read my diary; it is personal, and I would never open your messages without asking you first.","t":"請不要看我的日記；那是私人的，而我也絕不會不先問你就打開你的訊息。"},{"w":"personality","p":"n.","d":"the type of person you are, shown by the way you behave and think","c":"個性；人格","s":"Our new neighbor has a warm and friendly personality, and within a week she knew the names of everyone in the building.","t":"我們的新鄰居有溫暖友善的個性，不到一週她就知道大樓裡每個人的名字。"},{"w":"perspective","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of thinking about something; a point of view","c":"觀點；看法","s":"Living abroad for a year gave me a completely new perspective on my own country, and I came home with more questions than answers.","t":"在國外生活一年讓我對自己的國家有了全新的觀點，回家時我的問題比答案還多。","h":1},{"w":"from sb's perspective","p":"phr.","d":"seen from the point of view of a particular person","c":"從某人的角度來看","s":"From a student's perspective, a late school start sounds wonderful, but the teachers point out that classes would then end after dark in winter.","t":"從學生的角度來看，延後上學時間聽起來很棒，但老師們指出，這樣冬天的課會上到天黑之後。","a":"From a student's perspective"},{"w":"perspective","p":"n.","d":"the art of drawing objects so that they look solid and far away or near","c":"透視法","s":"In art class we learned about perspective, and suddenly my drawings of the street looked real instead of flat.","t":"美術課我們學了透視法，突然間我畫的街道看起來很真實，不再是平面的。"},{"w":"put sth in perspective","p":"v.phr.","d":"to compare something with other things so that you judge it correctly","c":"正確看待某事；客觀看待","s":"Visiting the children's hospital really put things in perspective; my bad grade on one test suddenly seemed like a very small problem.","t":"參觀兒童醫院真的讓我看清了事情的輕重；我一次考試的壞成績突然顯得是個很小的問題。","a":"put things in perspective"},{"w":"pessimism","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that bad things are more likely to happen than good things","c":"悲觀","s":"There is a lot of pessimism about the economy this year, but my aunt still opened her new flower shop and is doing well.","t":"今年大家對經濟相當悲觀，但我阿姨還是開了她的新花店，而且經營得不錯。","h":1},{"w":"pessimistic","p":"adj.","d":"expecting bad things to happen","c":"悲觀的","s":"Do not be so pessimistic about the interview; you have prepared well, and the worst that can happen is that you try again next month.","t":"不要對面試這麼悲觀；你已經準備得很好，最糟的情況也不過是下個月再試一次。"},{"w":"pessimist","p":"n.","d":"a person who always expects bad things to happen","c":"悲觀的人","s":"My uncle is such a pessimist that when we won the lottery, he immediately started worrying about the tax we would have to pay.","t":"我叔叔是個十足的悲觀主義者，我們中樂透時，他立刻開始擔心要繳的稅。"},{"w":"optimism","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that good things will happen in the future","c":"樂觀","s":"The coach's optimism spread through the whole team, and the players walked onto the field believing they could win the final.","t":"教練的樂觀感染了整支球隊，球員們走上球場時相信他們能贏得決賽。"},{"w":"petition","p":"n.","d":"a written request signed by many people asking someone in power to do something","c":"請願書；連署書","s":"The students started a petition asking the school to keep the library open until nine, and three hundred people signed it in two days.","t":"學生們發起一份請願書，要求學校讓圖書館開放到九點，兩天內就有三百人連署。","h":1},{"w":"sign a petition","p":"v.phr.","d":"to add your name to a written request to show that you support it","c":"連署請願書","s":"Would you like to sign a petition to save the old trees on our street before the city cuts them down to widen the road?","t":"你願意連署一份請願書，在市政府砍掉我們街上的老樹拓寬道路之前拯救它們嗎？"},{"w":"petition","p":"v.","d":"to make a formal request to someone in power","c":"請願；請求","s":"The villagers plan to petition the government for a new bridge, since the old one has been closed for safety reasons since March.","t":"村民們打算向政府請願建一座新橋，因為舊橋從三月起就因安全理由封閉了。"},{"w":"petty","p":"adj.","d":"small and not important","c":"瑣碎的；微不足道的","s":"Stop arguing about petty things like who gets the window seat, or we will miss the bus and the whole trip will be ruined.","t":"別再為誰坐窗邊這種瑣碎的事吵了，否則我們會錯過公車，整趟旅行就毀了。","h":1},{"w":"petty","p":"adj.","d":"caring too much about small, unimportant things, in an unkind way","c":"小心眼的；心胸狹窄的","s":"It was petty of him to refuse to lend her a pen just because she had forgotten to say thank you last week.","t":"他只因為她上週忘了說謝謝就拒絕借她一枝筆，實在很小心眼。"},{"w":"petty cash","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small amount of money kept in an office for small daily costs","c":"零用金","s":"The secretary keeps some petty cash in a box in her desk for buying stamps, tea, and other small things the office needs.","t":"秘書在她桌子的盒子裡放了一些零用金，用來買郵票、茶葉和辦公室需要的其他小東西。"},{"w":"petty crime","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small crime that is not very serious, such as stealing something cheap","c":"輕罪；小罪行","s":"The police say that petty crime such as bicycle theft has gone up in the area, so they have added more cameras near the station.","t":"警方說該地區腳踏車竊盜等輕微犯罪增加了，所以他們在車站附近加裝了更多監視器。"},{"w":"phase","p":"n.","d":"one stage in a process of development or change","c":"階段；時期","s":"The first phase of the building project will take two years, and the new school will not open until the third phase is complete.","t":"這項建築工程的第一階段要花兩年，新學校要到第三階段完成後才會開放。","h":1},{"w":"go through a phase","p":"v.phr.","d":"to pass through a period of behaving in a particular way","c":"經歷某個階段","s":"My sister went through a phase where she only wore black clothes, but after a year she went back to her bright colors.","t":"我妹妹經歷過一個階段只穿黑色衣服，但一年後她又回到了鮮豔的顏色。","a":"went through a phase"},{"w":"phase out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop using or doing something gradually over a period of time","c":"逐步淘汰","s":"The city plans to phase out its old diesel buses over the next five years and replace them with quiet electric ones.","t":"市政府計畫在未來五年逐步淘汰老舊的柴油公車，換成安靜的電動公車。"},{"w":"phase in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start using or doing something gradually over a period of time","c":"逐步引進","s":"The school will phase in the new uniform one grade at a time, so students do not have to buy everything at once.","t":"學校會一次一個年級逐步引進新制服，這樣學生就不必一次買齊所有東西。"}]},{"unit":26,"theme":"photographic – premier","cards":[{"w":"photographic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with photographs or taking photos","c":"攝影的","s":"The museum does not allow any photographic equipment inside, so visitors have to leave their cameras at the front desk.","t":"博物館內不允許任何攝影器材，所以參觀者必須把相機留在服務台。","h":1},{"w":"photographic memory","p":"n.phr.","d":"the ability to remember everything you see in great detail","c":"過目不忘的記憶力","s":"My aunt has a photographic memory, so she can remember every page of a book after reading it only once.","t":"我阿姨有過目不忘的記憶力，所以一本書只讀一次就能記住每一頁。"},{"w":"photograph","p":"n.","d":"a picture taken with a camera","c":"照片","s":"This old black-and-white photograph shows my grandparents on their wedding day, and they both look very young and happy.","t":"這張黑白老照片是我祖父母結婚那天拍的，他們兩人看起來都很年輕又快樂。"},{"w":"photographer","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes photos, especially as a job","c":"攝影師","s":"The wedding photographer asked everyone to stand closer together and smile before he took the final group picture.","t":"婚禮攝影師請大家站得更靠近一點並微笑，然後才拍下最後一張團體照。"},{"w":"photography","p":"n.","d":"the art or job of taking photos","c":"攝影","s":"She took a photography class last summer, and now she spends every weekend taking pictures of birds in the park.","t":"她去年夏天上了攝影課，現在每個週末都在公園裡拍鳥的照片。"},{"w":"pickup","p":"n.","d":"a small truck with an open back for carrying things","c":"小貨車；皮卡車","s":"My uncle drives an old pickup truck on his farm because he often needs to carry heavy bags of rice and vegetables.","t":"我叔叔在農場開一輛舊的小貨車，因為他常常需要運送沉重的米袋和蔬菜。","h":1},{"w":"pickup","p":"n.","d":"the act of collecting a person or thing from a place","c":"接送；收取","s":"The school bus pickup is at seven fifteen every morning, so you must be waiting at the corner before then.","t":"校車每天早上七點十五分接送，所以你必須在那之前在街角等著。"},{"w":"pick up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lift something; to collect a person or thing; to learn easily","c":"拿起；接（人）；學會","s":"Could you pick up your little sister from the kindergarten at four o'clock, because I have to work late today?","t":"你可以四點去幼兒園接你妹妹嗎？因為我今天必須工作到很晚。"},{"w":"pick","p":"v.","d":"to choose; to take fruit or flowers from a plant","c":"挑選；採摘","s":"We went to the farm to pick strawberries, and my little brother ate more than he put in the basket.","t":"我們去農場採草莓，我弟弟吃掉的比放進籃子裡的還多。"},{"w":"pier","p":"n.","d":"a long structure built out into the sea where boats stop","c":"碼頭","s":"We walked to the end of the pier to watch the fishing boats come back with their catch at sunset.","t":"我們走到碼頭盡頭，看漁船在日落時帶著漁獲回來。","h":1},{"w":"fishing pier","p":"n.phr.","d":"a pier where people stand to catch fish","c":"釣魚碼頭","s":"Every Sunday morning, my grandfather takes his rod to the old fishing pier and waits patiently for hours.","t":"每個星期日早上，我爺爺都帶著釣竿到那座舊的釣魚碼頭，耐心地等上好幾個小時。"},{"w":"pier","p":"n.","d":"a thick post that holds up a bridge","c":"橋墩","s":"Engineers checked each pier of the bridge after the earthquake to make sure the structure was still safe for cars.","t":"地震後工程師檢查了這座橋的每一座橋墩，以確保結構對車輛來說仍然安全。"},{"w":"pillar","p":"n.","d":"a tall strong post that holds up a building","c":"柱子","s":"A huge stone pillar stands in the center of the hall, and it has held up the roof for over three hundred years.","t":"一根巨大的石柱立在大廳中央，它支撐著屋頂已經超過三百年了。","h":1},{"w":"pillar","p":"n.","d":"a very important member or part of a group","c":"支柱；中流砥柱","s":"Mrs. Lin has taught at the school for forty years, and everyone calls her a pillar of the community.","t":"林老師在這所學校教了四十年，大家都稱她為社區的支柱。"},{"w":"a pillar of strength","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who gives others support in a hard time","c":"精神支柱","s":"After my father lost his job, my mother was a pillar of strength for the whole family and never showed her worry.","t":"我爸爸失業後，我媽媽成了全家的精神支柱，從未表現出她的擔憂。"},{"w":"pipeline","p":"n.","d":"a long line of pipes that carries oil, gas, or water","c":"管線；輸送管","s":"The new gas pipeline runs under the river for two kilometers and brings fuel to thousands of homes in the city.","t":"新的瓦斯管線在河底延伸兩公里，為城裡數千戶家庭輸送燃料。","h":1},{"w":"in the pipeline","p":"phr.","d":"being planned or prepared and coming soon","c":"在籌劃中；即將推出","s":"The company says several new phone models are in the pipeline, so you may want to wait a few months before buying one.","t":"這家公司說有幾款新手機正在籌劃中，所以你也許要等幾個月再買。"},{"w":"pipe","p":"n.","d":"a tube that carries water or gas","c":"管子；水管","s":"A water pipe under the kitchen sink broke last night, and the whole floor was wet when we woke up.","t":"昨晚廚房水槽下的一根水管破了，我們醒來時整個地板都是濕的。"},{"w":"pirate","p":"n.","d":"a person who attacks ships at sea to steal things","c":"海盜","s":"In the movie, a brave pirate with a wooden leg sails across the ocean to search for a hidden treasure.","t":"在這部電影裡，一個裝著木腿的勇敢海盜橫越大海，尋找隱藏的寶藏。","h":1},{"w":"pirate","p":"v.","d":"to copy and sell films, music, or software illegally","c":"盜版","s":"It is against the law to pirate movies and sell cheap copies on the street, and you could be fined heavily.","t":"盜版電影並在街上販賣廉價複製品是違法的，你可能會被重罰。"},{"w":"pirated","p":"adj.","d":"copied and sold illegally","c":"盜版的","s":"The police found hundreds of pirated DVDs in the small shop, and the owner was taken to the police station.","t":"警方在那家小店裡發現數百片盜版DVD，店主被帶到警察局。"},{"w":"piracy","p":"n.","d":"the crime of attacking ships; the illegal copying of films or music","c":"海盜行為；盜版","s":"Online piracy costs the music industry billions of dollars every year, so many singers now sell their songs through apps.","t":"網路盜版每年讓音樂產業損失數十億美元，所以許多歌手現在透過 App 販售歌曲。"},{"w":"pitcher","p":"n.","d":"the baseball player who throws the ball to the batter","c":"投手","s":"The pitcher threw the ball so fast that the batter did not even see it before the umpire shouted strike.","t":"投手把球投得太快了，打者還沒看到球，裁判就已經喊出好球。","h":1},{"w":"pitcher","p":"n.","d":"a large container with a handle for pouring drinks","c":"水壺；大水罐","s":"Mom put a pitcher of cold lemonade on the table, and we finished the whole thing in less than ten minutes.","t":"媽媽在桌上放了一壺冰檸檬水，我們不到十分鐘就把整壺喝完了。"},{"w":"pitch","p":"v.","d":"to throw a ball to the batter in baseball","c":"投球；投擲","s":"He will pitch in tomorrow's final game, so the coach told him to rest his arm and go to bed early tonight.","t":"他明天的決賽要投球，所以教練要他讓手臂休息，今晚早點睡。"},{"w":"pitch","p":"n.","d":"how high or low a sound is","c":"音高","s":"The singer's voice went up to a very high pitch, and the audience could not believe how long she held the note.","t":"那位歌手的聲音飆到非常高的音高，觀眾無法相信她能把那個音拉得那麼長。"},{"w":"sales pitch","p":"n.phr.","d":"a speech that tries to persuade you to buy something","c":"推銷話術","s":"The salesman gave us a long sales pitch about the new vacuum cleaner, but we still decided not to buy it.","t":"推銷員對我們講了一長串關於新吸塵器的推銷話術，但我們還是決定不買。"},{"w":"placement","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting something in a place; a job or position arranged for someone","c":"放置；安置；職務安排","s":"The placement of the sofa next to the window makes the living room look much bigger and brighter than before.","t":"把沙發放置在窗邊，讓客廳看起來比以前大得多也明亮得多。","h":1},{"w":"placement test","p":"n.phr.","d":"a test that decides which level or class you should join","c":"分級測驗","s":"All new students take a placement test on the first day so the school can put them in a class at the right level.","t":"所有新生在第一天都要參加分級測驗，這樣學校才能把他們安排到程度合適的班級。"},{"w":"place","p":"v.","d":"to put something somewhere carefully","c":"放置","s":"Please place your shoes on the shelf by the door instead of leaving them in the middle of the hallway.","t":"請把你的鞋子放在門邊的架子上，不要留在走廊中間。"},{"w":"replace","p":"v.","d":"to change something old for something new; to take the place of","c":"更換；取代","s":"We need to replace the old batteries in the smoke alarm because it has been making a beeping sound all night.","t":"我們需要更換煙霧警報器裡的舊電池，因為它整晚都在發出嗶嗶聲。"},{"w":"take place","p":"v.phr.","d":"to happen; to be held","c":"發生；舉行","s":"The school's sports day will take place on the last Friday of October if the weather is good enough.","t":"如果天氣夠好，學校的運動會將在十月的最後一個星期五舉行。"},{"w":"plea","p":"n.","d":"a serious and emotional request","c":"懇求；請求","s":"The mother made a tearful plea on television for anyone who saw her missing son to call the police.","t":"那位母親在電視上含淚懇求，請任何看到她失蹤兒子的人打電話給警方。","h":1},{"w":"plead","p":"v.","d":"to ask for something in a serious, emotional way","c":"懇求","s":"The boy began to plead with his parents to let him keep the puppy he had found in the park.","t":"男孩開始懇求父母讓他留下他在公園裡發現的小狗。","h":1},{"w":"plead guilty","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say in court that you did the crime","c":"認罪","s":"In court, the man decided to plead guilty to the theft, hoping that the judge would give him a lighter punishment.","t":"在法庭上，那名男子決定對竊盜罪認罪，希望法官能給他較輕的處罰。"},{"w":"pleading","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you want something very much","c":"懇求的","s":"She looked at her teacher with pleading eyes, hoping to get one more day to finish her science project.","t":"她用懇求的眼神看著老師，希望能多一天時間完成她的科展作品。"},{"w":"pledge","p":"n.","d":"a serious promise to do something","c":"保證；誓言","s":"Every student made a pledge to keep the school clean, and they signed their names on a big poster in the hall.","t":"每位學生都做出保持校園整潔的誓言，並在大廳的大海報上簽下自己的名字。","h":1},{"w":"pledge","p":"v.","d":"to promise seriously to do or give something","c":"保證；承諾（捐出）","s":"The company decided to pledge one million dollars to help the families who lost their homes in the flood.","t":"這家公司決定承諾捐出一百萬元，幫助在洪水中失去家園的家庭。"},{"w":"make a pledge","p":"v.phr.","d":"to promise something publicly","c":"做出承諾","s":"At the start of the campaign, each candidate had to make a pledge that he or she would never accept money from big companies.","t":"選戰一開始，每位候選人都必須做出承諾，絕不接受大公司的金錢。"},{"w":"plunge","p":"v.","d":"to fall or jump suddenly and quickly downward","c":"跳入；驟降","s":"Without even testing the water, my cousin decided to plunge into the cold lake and came out shivering a minute later.","t":"我表哥連水都沒試一下，就決定跳進冰冷的湖裡，一分鐘後發著抖爬出來。","h":1},{"w":"plunge","p":"n.","d":"a sudden fall or jump; a sudden big drop","c":"跳入；暴跌；驟降","s":"The sudden plunge in temperature surprised everyone, and many students came to school without a jacket the next morning.","t":"氣溫突然驟降讓大家都很驚訝，第二天早上許多學生沒穿外套就來上學。"},{"w":"take the plunge","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finally decide to do something big or risky","c":"下定決心（冒險）去做","s":"After thinking about it for years, my parents finally decided to take the plunge and open their own small restaurant.","t":"考慮了好幾年之後，我父母終於決定放手一搏，開了自己的小餐廳。"},{"w":"plunge into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly put something or someone into a state or situation","c":"陷入；投入","s":"When the power went out during the storm, the whole town was plunged into darkness for more than six hours.","t":"暴風雨期間停電時，整個城鎮陷入黑暗超過六個小時。","a":"plunged into"},{"w":"plural","p":"adj.","d":"showing more than one person or thing","c":"複數的","s":"In English, most plural nouns end in -s, but words like child and mouse change in a different way.","t":"在英文中，大多數複數名詞以 -s 結尾，但像 child 和 mouse 這樣的字會以不同方式變化。","h":1},{"w":"plural","p":"n.","d":"the form of a word that shows more than one","c":"複數","s":"The plural of the word tooth is teeth, which many students find confusing when they first learn English.","t":"tooth 這個字的複數是 teeth，許多學生剛學英文時覺得很困惑。"},{"w":"in the plural","p":"phr.","d":"in the form that shows more than one","c":"以複數形式","s":"When you talk about more than one cat, you must use the noun in the plural and add an s at the end.","t":"當你談到不只一隻貓時，你必須用複數形式的名詞，在字尾加上 s。"},{"w":"poetic","p":"adj.","d":"like poetry; beautiful and full of feeling","c":"詩意的；詩的","s":"The writer uses very poetic language to describe the sunset, so reading the chapter feels like listening to music.","t":"作者用非常詩意的語言描寫日落，所以讀這一章就像在聽音樂一樣。","h":1},{"w":"poem","p":"n.","d":"a piece of writing in short lines, often with rhythm or rhyme","c":"詩","s":"Our teacher asked each student to write a short poem about spring and read it aloud in front of the class.","t":"老師要每位學生寫一首關於春天的短詩，並在全班面前大聲朗讀。"},{"w":"poet","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes poems","c":"詩人","s":"The famous poet wrote most of his works while sitting under a tree beside the river near his small village.","t":"這位著名的詩人大部分的作品都是坐在他小村莊附近河邊的樹下寫成的。"},{"w":"poetry","p":"n.","d":"poems in general; the art of writing poems","c":"詩（總稱）；詩歌","s":"I did not like poetry when I was young, but now I enjoy reading a few lines every night before I sleep.","t":"我小時候不喜歡詩，但現在我喜歡每晚睡前讀幾行。"},{"w":"poetic justice","p":"n.phr.","d":"a fair result in which a bad person gets what he or she deserves","c":"應得的報應；天理","s":"The thief who stole the bike had his own car stolen the next day, which my grandmother called poetic justice.","t":"偷腳踏車的小偷第二天自己的車也被偷了，我奶奶說這就是應得的報應。"},{"w":"poke","p":"v.","d":"to push something or someone quickly with your finger or a stick","c":"戳；捅","s":"Do not poke the sleeping dog with that stick, or it may wake up angry and bite you on the hand.","t":"不要用那根棍子戳睡著的狗，否則它可能會生氣地醒來咬你的手。","h":1},{"w":"poke","p":"n.","d":"a quick push with your finger or something pointed","c":"戳；輕推","s":"My friend gave me a quick poke in the arm to wake me up when the teacher walked past our desks.","t":"老師走過我們桌子時，我朋友在我手臂上快速戳了一下把我叫醒。"},{"w":"poke fun at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make jokes about someone in an unkind way","c":"取笑","s":"The other boys liked to poke fun at his old shoes, but he smiled and said that they were his lucky pair.","t":"其他男孩喜歡取笑他的舊鞋子，但他笑著說那是他的幸運鞋。"},{"w":"poke around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look around a place in a relaxed way, often touching things","c":"翻找；四處看看","s":"While waiting for the train, we decided to poke around the little shops near the station and found some lovely postcards.","t":"等火車的時候，我們決定到車站附近的小店四處看看，找到了一些漂亮的明信片。"},{"w":"porch","p":"n.","d":"a covered area with a roof at the entrance of a house","c":"門廊","s":"On warm summer evenings, my grandparents like to sit on the front porch and watch the neighbors walk by.","t":"在溫暖的夏夜，我祖父母喜歡坐在前門廊上，看鄰居走過。","h":1},{"w":"front porch","p":"n.phr.","d":"the covered area at the front door of a house","c":"前門廊","s":"The delivery man left the package on the front porch because nobody answered the doorbell when he rang it twice.","t":"送貨員把包裹留在前門廊上，因為他按了兩次門鈴都沒有人應門。"},{"w":"porch light","p":"n.phr.","d":"the lamp outside the front door of a house","c":"門廊燈","s":"Please leave the porch light on tonight, because your sister will come home late and the street is very dark.","t":"今晚請讓門廊燈開著，因為你姐姐會很晚回家，而且街上非常暗。"},{"w":"portfolio","p":"n.","d":"a collection of your work that shows your skills","c":"作品集","s":"Art students must bring a portfolio of their best drawings and paintings to the interview at the university.","t":"美術系學生必須帶著他們最好的素描和繪畫作品集去大學面試。","h":1},{"w":"portfolio","p":"n.","d":"all the stocks and investments owned by a person","c":"投資組合","s":"My uncle checks his investment portfolio every morning to see whether his stocks have gone up or down.","t":"我叔叔每天早上都查看他的投資組合，看他的股票是漲還是跌。"},{"w":"portfolio","p":"n.","d":"a large flat case for carrying papers or drawings","c":"公事包；文件夾","s":"She carried her papers in a black leather portfolio and placed it carefully on the desk before the meeting began.","t":"她把文件放在一個黑色皮革文件夾裡，在會議開始前小心地放在桌上。"},{"w":"build a portfolio","p":"v.phr.","d":"to collect examples of your work over time","c":"建立作品集","s":"Young designers should build a portfolio early, because companies want to see real examples of their work before hiring them.","t":"年輕設計師應該早點建立作品集，因為公司在聘用之前想看到他們真實的作品範例。"},{"w":"practitioner","p":"n.","d":"a person who works in a skilled job, such as a doctor or lawyer","c":"從業者；開業醫師","s":"Dr. Wang is a well-known medical practitioner in our town, and many families have visited her clinic for over twenty years.","t":"王醫師是我們鎮上知名的開業醫師，許多家庭二十多年來都到她的診所看病。","h":1},{"w":"general practitioner","p":"n.phr.","d":"a doctor who treats all common illnesses, not a specialist","c":"家庭醫師；全科醫師","s":"If you have a cold or a mild fever, you should first see a general practitioner instead of going straight to a big hospital.","t":"如果你感冒或輕微發燒，應該先去看家庭醫師，而不是直接去大醫院。"},{"w":"practice","p":"n.","d":"doing something again and again to get better; a doctor's business","c":"練習；診所業務","s":"Daily practice is the only way to improve your piano skills, even if you can spend only twenty minutes each evening.","t":"每天練習是提升鋼琴技巧的唯一方法，即使你每晚只能花二十分鐘。"},{"w":"practice","p":"v.","d":"to do something many times so that you get better at it","c":"練習","s":"The team will practice every afternoon this week because the final game against Taichung is on Saturday.","t":"球隊這週每天下午都會練習，因為星期六要和台中隊打決賽。"},{"w":"practical","p":"adj.","d":"useful in real life; good at doing real things","c":"實用的；實際的","s":"Instead of expensive flowers, she gave her mother a practical gift, a new rice cooker that the family uses every day.","t":"她沒有送昂貵的花，而是送媽媽一個實用的禮物——一個全家每天都會用的新電鍋。"},{"w":"in practice","p":"phr.","d":"in real situations, not just in theory","c":"實際上","s":"The plan sounds perfect on paper, but in practice it will be hard to get everyone to arrive on time.","t":"這個計畫在紙上聽起來很完美，但實際上很難讓每個人都準時到達。"},{"w":"precaution","p":"n.","d":"something you do to stop something bad from happening","c":"預防措施","s":"As a precaution, the school closed early before the typhoon so that all students could get home safely.","t":"作為一項預防措施，學校在颱風來臨前提早放學，讓所有學生能安全回家。","h":1},{"w":"take precautions","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do things that protect you from possible danger","c":"採取預防措施","s":"Hikers should take precautions such as bringing extra water and telling someone which trail they plan to take.","t":"登山客應該採取預防措施，例如多帶水，並告訴別人他們打算走哪條步道。"},{"w":"precautionary","p":"adj.","d":"done to stop something bad from happening","c":"預防性的","s":"The city took precautionary measures by moving people out of the low areas two days before the heavy rain arrived.","t":"這座城市採取了預防性的措施，在大雨到來前兩天就把低窪地區的居民遷出。"},{"w":"caution","p":"n.","d":"great care that you take to avoid danger","c":"小心；謹慎","s":"Drivers should use extra caution on the mountain road because the turns are sharp and the fog is thick in the morning.","t":"駕駛在山路上應該格外小心，因為彎道很急，而且早上霧很濃。"},{"w":"cautious","p":"adj.","d":"careful to avoid danger or mistakes","c":"謹慎的","s":"My grandfather is very cautious with money, so he always compares prices in three shops before he buys anything.","t":"我爺爺用錢非常謹慎，所以他買任何東西之前總是先比較三家店的價格。"},{"w":"predator","p":"n.","d":"an animal that kills and eats other animals","c":"掠食者；捕食者","s":"The lion is a powerful predator that hunts at night and can run very fast over a short distance.","t":"獅子是強大的掠食者，它在夜間獵食，而且短距離內可以跑得非常快。","h":1},{"w":"predatory","p":"adj.","d":"living by killing and eating other animals; using others for gain","c":"掠食的；掠奪性的","s":"Sharks have predatory teeth that are perfectly shaped for catching slippery fish in the deep, dark ocean.","t":"鯊魚有掠食用的牙齒，形狀完美適合在深暗的海洋中捕捉滑溜的魚。"},{"w":"top predator","p":"n.phr.","d":"an animal at the top of the food chain that nothing else hunts","c":"頂級掠食者","s":"The great white shark is a top predator in the ocean, which means almost no other animal hunts it.","t":"大白鯊是海洋中的頂級掠食者，這表示幾乎沒有其他動物會獵捕它。"},{"w":"preference","p":"n.","d":"a greater liking for one thing than another","c":"偏好；偏愛","s":"The hotel asked about our room preference, so we told them that we wanted a quiet room with a sea view.","t":"飯店詢問我們對房間的偏好，所以我們告訴他們想要一間安靜、可以看海的房間。","h":1},{"w":"have a preference for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to like one thing more than others","c":"偏好；偏愛","s":"My grandmother has a preference for traditional Taiwanese breakfast, so she never eats bread or cereal in the morning.","t":"我奶奶偏愛傳統的台式早餐，所以她早上從不吃麵包或麥片。","a":"has a preference for"},{"w":"prefer","p":"v.","d":"to like one thing more than another","c":"比較喜歡","s":"I prefer to study in the library rather than at home because my little brothers are always too noisy.","t":"我比較喜歡在圖書館讀書而不是在家，因為我的弟弟們總是太吵了。"},{"w":"preferable","p":"adj.","d":"better or more suitable","c":"更好的；更合適的","s":"Walking to school is preferable to taking the bus when the weather is nice, because you can get some exercise.","t":"天氣好的時候，走路上學比搭公車更好，因為你可以運動一下。"},{"w":"preferably","p":"adv.","d":"if possible; as the best choice","c":"最好；寧可","s":"Please hand in your report by Friday, preferably in the morning, so that I have time to read all of them before the weekend.","t":"請在星期五前交報告，最好是早上，這樣我才有時間在週末前讀完所有的報告。"},{"w":"prejudice","p":"n.","d":"an unfair opinion about someone formed without knowing the facts","c":"偏見","s":"Racial prejudice still exists in many places, and some people are treated unfairly only because of the color of their skin.","t":"種族偏見在許多地方仍然存在，有些人只因為膚色就受到不公平的對待。","h":1},{"w":"prejudice","p":"v.","d":"to make someone have an unfair opinion; to harm something","c":"使有偏見；損害","s":"The news reports about the case could prejudice the jury before the trial even begins, so the judge warned them not to read them.","t":"關於此案的新聞報導可能在審判開始前就使陪審團產生偏見，所以法官警告他們不要去讀。"},{"w":"prejudiced","p":"adj.","d":"having an unfair opinion about a person or group","c":"有偏見的","s":"Some old people are prejudiced against teenagers and believe that all of them are lazy and spend all day on their phones.","t":"有些老人對青少年有偏見，認為他們全都很懶惰，整天都在玩手機。"},{"w":"preliminary","p":"adj.","d":"happening before the main or most important part","c":"初步的；預備的","s":"The preliminary results of the test show that most students did well, but the final scores will come out next week.","t":"測驗的初步結果顯示大多數學生表現良好，但最終成績下週才會公布。","h":1},{"w":"preliminary","p":"n.","d":"something done before the main event","c":"預備行動；開場","s":"Before the main speeches, there were a few preliminaries, including a short welcome and the singing of the national anthem.","t":"在主要演講之前有幾項開場活動，包括簡短的歡迎詞和唱國歌。","a":"preliminaries"},{"w":"preliminary round","p":"n.phr.","d":"the early stage of a competition before the final","c":"預賽","s":"Our school band performed well in the preliminary round, so we have a good chance of going to the national competition.","t":"我們學校的樂隊在預賽中表現很好，所以我們很有機會參加全國比賽。"},{"w":"premature","p":"adj.","d":"born before the normal time; happening too early","c":"早產的；過早的","s":"The baby was premature and weighed only two kilograms, so she stayed in the hospital for a month before coming home.","t":"那個寶寶是早產的，體重只有兩公斤，所以她在醫院待了一個月才回家。","h":1},{"w":"premature","p":"adj.","d":"done too soon, before you have enough information","c":"過早的；不成熟的","s":"It is premature to celebrate now because the game is not over and the other team can still score.","t":"現在慶祝還太早，因為比賽還沒結束，對方球隊還可能得分。"},{"w":"prematurely","p":"adv.","d":"too early; before the right time","c":"過早地","s":"Many young people lose their hair prematurely because of stress, poor sleep, and an unhealthy diet.","t":"許多年輕人因為壓力、睡眠不足和不健康的飲食而過早掉髮。"},{"w":"mature","p":"adj.","d":"behaving like a sensible adult; fully grown","c":"成熟的","s":"Although she is only fifteen, she is very mature for her age and always thinks carefully before she speaks.","t":"雖然她只有十五歲，但以她的年齡來說非常成熟，說話前總是仔細思考。"},{"w":"maturity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of behaving like a sensible adult; being fully grown","c":"成熟","s":"Taking care of a pet takes a lot of maturity, so my parents waited until I was twelve before they let me have a dog.","t":"照顧寵物需要很高的成熟度，所以我父母等到我十二歲才讓我養狗。"},{"w":"premier","p":"n.","d":"the leader of a government; a prime minister","c":"總理；行政院長","s":"The premier visited the flooded town yesterday and promised that the government would help people rebuild their homes.","t":"行政院長昨天視察了被淹的城鎮，並承諾政府會幫助民眾重建家園。","h":1},{"w":"premier","p":"adj.","d":"the best or most important","c":"首要的；最好的","s":"Taipei 101 was once the world's tallest building and is still the city's premier tourist attraction for visitors.","t":"台北 101 曾是世界最高的建築，至今仍是這座城市首要的觀光景點。"},{"w":"premiere","p":"n.","d":"the first public showing of a film or play","c":"首映；首演","s":"Hundreds of fans waited outside the theater for the movie's premiere, hoping to see the stars walk down the red carpet.","t":"數百名影迷在戲院外等待這部電影的首映，希望看到明星走紅地毯。"},{"w":"premiere","p":"v.","d":"to be shown or performed in public for the first time","c":"首映；首演","s":"The new musical will premiere in Taipei next month before the company takes it to Tokyo and Seoul.","t":"這部新音樂劇下個月將在台北首演，之後劇團會把它帶到東京和首爾。"}]},{"unit":27,"theme":"premise – prospect","cards":[{"w":"premise","p":"n.","d":"an idea that you accept as true and use as the basis for a plan or argument","c":"前提","s":"The whole plan is based on the premise that the weather will stay dry, so we need a backup if it rains.","t":"整個計畫建立在天氣會保持乾燥的前提上，所以如果下雨我們需要備案。","h":1},{"w":"premises","p":"n.","d":"the building and land that a business or school uses","c":"房屋及土地；營業場所","s":"Smoking is not allowed anywhere on the school premises, including the parking lot and the sports field behind the gym.","t":"學校場地內任何地方都不准吸菸，包括停車場和體育館後面的運動場。"},{"w":"on the premise that","p":"phr.","d":"based on the idea that something is true","c":"以…為前提","s":"The teacher gave us the extra day on the premise that we would hand in a much better report than before.","t":"老師多給我們一天，前提是我們要交出比之前好得多的報告。"},{"w":"premium","p":"n.","d":"money paid regularly for insurance; an extra amount above the usual price","c":"保險費；額外費用","s":"My father pays a monthly premium for his health insurance, which covers most of the cost when he goes to the hospital.","t":"我爸爸每個月為他的健康保險支付保險費，這在他去醫院時能支付大部分費用。","h":1},{"w":"premium","p":"adj.","d":"of very high quality and usually more expensive","c":"優質的；高價的","s":"The shop sells premium coffee beans from Guatemala, so one small bag costs twice as much as the regular ones.","t":"這家店賣來自瓜地馬拉的優質咖啡豆，所以一小包的價格是一般咖啡豆的兩倍。"},{"w":"at a premium","p":"phr.","d":"hard to get and therefore expensive","c":"稀缺而昂貴；供不應求","s":"Hotel rooms are at a premium during the lantern festival, so you should book at least two months before you travel.","t":"燈會期間飯店房間供不應求，所以你應該在出發前至少兩個月預訂。"},{"w":"put a premium on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to consider something very important","c":"重視","s":"Our school puts a premium on honesty, so a student who cheats on a test may be asked to leave.","t":"我們學校非常重視誠實，所以考試作弊的學生可能會被要求離開。","a":"puts a premium on"},{"w":"prescribe","p":"v.","d":"to say what medicine a sick person should take","c":"開（藥方）；規定","s":"The doctor decided to prescribe some medicine for my cough and told me to drink more warm water and rest.","t":"醫生決定為我的咳嗽開一些藥，並要我多喝溫水、多休息。","h":1},{"w":"prescription","p":"n.","d":"a paper from a doctor that says what medicine you need","c":"處方；藥方","s":"You cannot buy this medicine without a prescription, so you have to see a doctor first and bring the paper to the pharmacy.","t":"沒有處方你不能買這種藥，所以你必須先看醫生，再把單子帶到藥局。","h":1},{"w":"prescription drug","p":"n.phr.","d":"a medicine that you can get only with a doctor's note","c":"處方藥","s":"A prescription drug can be dangerous if you take it without asking a doctor, even if it helped your friend.","t":"處方藥如果沒問過醫生就服用可能很危險，即使它對你的朋友有幫助。"},{"w":"prescribed","p":"adj.","d":"decided by a rule or by a doctor","c":"規定的；處方的","s":"Students must finish the prescribed reading list before the new semester begins, or they will fall behind in class.","t":"學生必須在新學期開始前讀完規定的書單，否則上課會跟不上。"},{"w":"presidency","p":"n.","d":"the job of being president; the time someone is president","c":"總統職位；總統任期","s":"During his four-year presidency, the country built many new roads and schools, so people still remember him warmly today.","t":"在他四年的總統任期內，國家建了許多新道路和學校，所以人們至今仍懷念他。","h":1},{"w":"presidential","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a president","c":"總統的","s":"The presidential election will take place in January, and both candidates have been traveling around the island to meet voters.","t":"總統大選將在一月舉行，兩位候選人一直在環島拜訪選民。","h":1},{"w":"president","p":"n.","d":"the leader of a country or a company","c":"總統；董事長；總裁","s":"The president of the company gave a short speech to thank every worker before the New Year dinner began.","t":"公司董事長在尾牙晚宴開始前發表了簡短的演說，感謝每一位員工。"},{"w":"presidential campaign","p":"n.phr.","d":"the activities a candidate does to try to be elected president","c":"總統競選活動","s":"The presidential campaign lasted almost a year, and the candidates spent millions of dollars on television advertisements.","t":"總統競選活動持續了將近一年，候選人花了數百萬元在電視廣告上。"},{"w":"presumably","p":"adv.","d":"probably; it is reasonable to think","c":"想必；大概","s":"The lights in the office are still on, so presumably someone is still working late on the report tonight.","t":"辦公室的燈還亮著，所以想必今晚還有人在加班趕報告。","h":1},{"w":"presume","p":"v.","d":"to think that something is true without being sure","c":"推測；假定","s":"I presume you have already eaten dinner, but there is some fried rice in the kitchen if you are still hungry.","t":"我猜想你已經吃過晚餐了，但如果你還餓，廚房裡有一些炒飯。","h":1},{"w":"presumption","p":"n.","d":"something you believe is true without having proof","c":"假定；推測","s":"The presumption that all teenagers love video games is wrong, because many of them would rather play sports or read.","t":"認為所有青少年都愛電玩的假定是錯的，因為他們之中許多人寧願運動或閱讀。"},{"w":"presumed","p":"adj.","d":"believed to be true, although not proved","c":"推定的","s":"The presumed cause of the fire was an old electric heater, but the police are still checking the building.","t":"火災推定的原因是一台舊電暖器，但警方仍在檢查這棟建築。"},{"w":"prevail","p":"v.","d":"to win or be the strongest; to be common or widespread","c":"佔上風；獲勝；盛行","s":"In the end, good sense will prevail, and the two sides will agree to share the cost of repairing the wall.","t":"最後理智會佔上風，雙方會同意分攤修牆的費用。","h":1},{"w":"prevail over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to defeat or be stronger than someone","c":"戰勝；勝過","s":"The small village team managed to prevail over the city champions in the final minute of the game.","t":"這支小村莊的球隊在比賽最後一分鐘成功戰勝了城市冠軍隊。"},{"w":"prevailing","p":"adj.","d":"most common at a particular time","c":"盛行的；普遍的","s":"The prevailing view among doctors is that children should spend less time on screens and more time playing outside.","t":"醫生之間普遍的看法是，孩子應該少看螢幕，多到戶外玩。"},{"w":"prevalent","p":"adj.","d":"very common in a place or at a time","c":"普遍的；流行的","s":"Colds are especially prevalent in winter, so remember to wash your hands often and keep warm.","t":"感冒在冬天特別普遍，所以記得常洗手並保持溫暖。"},{"w":"prey","p":"n.","d":"an animal that is hunted and eaten by another animal","c":"獵物","s":"The eagle flew in a wide circle above the field, watching for any small prey that moved in the grass.","t":"老鷹在田野上空盤旋，注意草叢裡任何移動的小獵物。","h":1},{"w":"prey on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to hunt and eat another animal; to harm weak people","c":"捕食；坑害","s":"Owls prey on mice and other small animals at night, which is why farmers like having them near the fields.","t":"貓頭鷹在夜間捕食老鼠和其他小動物，這就是為什麼農夫喜歡牠們待在田地附近。"},{"w":"fall prey to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be harmed or tricked by someone or something","c":"成為…的犧牲品；受害於","s":"Many old people fall prey to phone scams because the callers sound friendly and pretend to be from the bank.","t":"許多老人成為電話詐騙的受害者，因為來電者聽起來很友善，還假裝是銀行的人。"},{"w":"bird of prey","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bird such as an eagle or hawk that hunts animals","c":"猛禽","s":"The hawk is a bird of prey with sharp eyes that can see a rabbit from hundreds of meters up in the sky.","t":"老鷹是一種猛禽，牠銳利的眼睛能從幾百公尺的高空看到一隻兔子。"},{"w":"prior","p":"adj.","d":"existing or happening before something else","c":"事先的；先前的","s":"You need prior permission from the principal if you want to use the school hall for a concert on the weekend.","t":"如果你想在週末使用學校禮堂辦音樂會，需要得到校長事先的許可。","h":1},{"w":"prior to","p":"prep.","d":"before","c":"在…之前","s":"Please arrive at the airport two hours prior to your flight, because the security line can be very long during holidays.","t":"請在班機起飛之前兩小時抵達機場，因為假日期間安檢隊伍可能非常長。"},{"w":"priority","p":"n.","d":"the thing that you think is most important and must do first","c":"優先事項","s":"Finishing my homework is my first priority tonight, so I will not watch any videos until it is done.","t":"完成功課是我今晚的第一優先事項，所以在做完之前我不會看任何影片。"},{"w":"prioritize","p":"v.","d":"to put tasks in order of importance","c":"排定優先順序","s":"When you have many things to do, learn to prioritize them and start with the most important task first.","t":"當你有很多事要做時，要學會排定優先順序，先從最重要的工作開始。"},{"w":"proclaim","p":"v.","d":"to say something publicly and officially","c":"宣告；宣布","s":"The king stood on the balcony to proclaim the end of the war, and the crowd below cheered for several minutes.","t":"國王站在陽台上宣告戰爭結束，底下的群眾歡呼了好幾分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"proclamation","p":"n.","d":"an official public statement","c":"公告；宣言","s":"The mayor read a proclamation that made the first Monday of May a holiday to honor the city's firefighters.","t":"市長宣讀了一份公告，將五月的第一個星期一定為假日，以表彰本市的消防員。"},{"w":"claim","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is true; to ask for something that is yours","c":"聲稱；認領","s":"Nobody came to claim the umbrella that was left on the bus, so the driver gave it to the lost-and-found office.","t":"沒有人來認領留在公車上的那把雨傘，所以司機把它交給了失物招領處。"},{"w":"productivity","p":"n.","d":"the rate at which work is done or things are made","c":"生產力","s":"The factory's productivity rose by twenty percent after the new machines were installed and the workers were trained to use them.","t":"新機器安裝並訓練工人使用後，工廠的生產力提高了百分之二十。","h":1},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"doing or making a lot; getting good results","c":"有成效的；多產的","s":"I had a very productive morning: I finished two essays, cleaned my room, and still had time for a short run.","t":"我度過了一個非常有成效的早晨：我寫完兩篇作文、打掃了房間，還有時間跑一小段路。"},{"w":"produce","p":"v.","d":"to make or grow something","c":"生產；製造","s":"This farm can produce enough rice to feed about five hundred families for a whole year.","t":"這座農場能生產足夠的米，養活大約五百個家庭一整年。"},{"w":"product","p":"n.","d":"something that is made to be sold","c":"產品","s":"The company's newest product is a small speaker that you can wear on your wrist like a watch.","t":"這家公司最新的產品是一個可以像手錶一樣戴在手腕上的小喇叭。"},{"w":"production","p":"n.","d":"the process of making or growing things","c":"生產；製作","s":"The production of the new phone was delayed by three months because some important parts were in short supply.","t":"新手機的生產延後了三個月，因為一些重要零件供應短缺。"},{"w":"profile","p":"n.","d":"a short description of a person's life and character","c":"簡介；人物側寫","s":"The school newspaper printed a profile of our new principal, including her hobbies and the schools she had worked at.","t":"校刊刊登了我們新校長的簡介，包括她的嗜好和她曾任教的學校。","h":1},{"w":"profile","p":"n.","d":"the shape of a face seen from the side","c":"側面；輪廓","s":"The artist drew my sister in profile, so you can see only one side of her face in the picture.","t":"畫家畫了我姐姐的側面，所以在畫裡你只能看到她半邊的臉。"},{"w":"profile","p":"v.","d":"to write or give a short description of someone","c":"描述；介紹","s":"The magazine will profile ten young scientists next month, and my cousin is one of the people they chose.","t":"這本雜誌下個月將介紹十位年輕科學家，我表哥是他們選中的其中一位。"},{"w":"keep a low profile","p":"v.phr.","d":"to avoid attracting attention","c":"保持低調","s":"After the famous singer moved to our town, she tried to keep a low profile and rarely went to busy places.","t":"那位知名歌手搬到我們鎮上之後，她盡量保持低調，很少去熱鬧的地方。"},{"w":"profound","p":"adj.","d":"very great or deep; showing great knowledge or feeling","c":"深遠的；深刻的","s":"Her teacher had a profound influence on her life, and she decided to become a teacher herself because of him.","t":"她的老師對她的人生有深遠的影響，她因為他而決定自己也成為老師。","h":1},{"w":"profoundly","p":"adv.","d":"very much; deeply","c":"深深地；極度地","s":"The whole class was profoundly moved by the story of the boy who walked ten kilometers to school every day.","t":"全班都被那個每天走十公里上學的男孩的故事深深感動了。"},{"w":"a profound effect on","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very strong and lasting influence on something","c":"對…深遠的影響","s":"The invention of the smartphone has had a profound effect on the way young people talk to each other.","t":"智慧型手機的發明對年輕人彼此交談的方式產生了深遠的影響。"},{"w":"progressive","p":"adj.","d":"supporting new ideas and social change; happening gradually","c":"進步的；漸進的","s":"The progressive school lets students choose some of their own classes and does not give any homework on weekends.","t":"這所進步的學校讓學生自己選擇部分課程，而且週末不出任何功課。","h":1},{"w":"progressive","p":"n.","d":"a person who supports new ideas and social change","c":"進步人士","s":"As a young progressive, she joined groups that fought for cleaner air and equal pay for women.","t":"身為一位年輕的進步人士，她加入了爭取更乾淨空氣和女性同工同酬的團體。"},{"w":"progress","p":"n.","d":"the process of getting better or moving forward","c":"進步；進展","s":"My English has made great progress since I started watching movies without Chinese subtitles every weekend.","t":"自從我每個週末開始看沒有中文字幕的電影後，我的英文有了很大的進步。"},{"w":"progress","p":"v.","d":"to move forward or develop over time","c":"進展；前進","s":"The building work will progress more slowly in the rainy season, so the new library may not open until next spring.","t":"建築工程在雨季會進展得比較慢，所以新圖書館可能要到明年春天才開放。"},{"w":"in progress","p":"phr.","d":"happening now and not yet finished","c":"進行中","s":"A test is in progress in Room 302, so please keep quiet when you walk past the door.","t":"302 教室正在進行考試，所以經過門口時請保持安靜。"},{"w":"progressively","p":"adv.","d":"gradually; more and more over time","c":"逐漸地","s":"The weather became progressively colder through November, and by the end of the month we all needed heavy coats.","t":"整個十一月天氣逐漸變冷，到了月底我們都需要厚外套了。"},{"w":"prohibit","p":"v.","d":"to officially say that something is not allowed","c":"禁止","s":"The new law will prohibit smoking in all parks, and anyone who breaks it will have to pay a fine of two thousand dollars.","t":"新法律將禁止在所有公園吸菸，違反者必須支付兩千元罰款。","h":1},{"w":"prohibition","p":"n.","d":"the act of officially not allowing something","c":"禁止；禁令","s":"The prohibition of plastic straws in restaurants has helped reduce the amount of trash on our beaches.","t":"餐廳禁用塑膠吸管的規定幫助減少了我們海灘上的垃圾量。"},{"w":"prohibited","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed by law or by a rule","c":"被禁止的","s":"Fireworks are prohibited in this area because the houses are made of wood and a fire could spread quickly.","t":"這個地區禁止放煙火，因為房子是木造的，火勢可能迅速蔓延。"},{"w":"projection","p":"n.","d":"a guess about the future based on information you have now","c":"預測；推估","s":"According to the government's latest projection, the population of the city will fall by ten percent over the next twenty years.","t":"根據政府最新的預測，這座城市的人口在未來二十年將減少百分之十。","h":1},{"w":"projection","p":"n.","d":"an image shown on a wall or screen by a machine","c":"投影","s":"The projection of the movie on the wall was too dark, so the teacher closed the curtains to make the picture clearer.","t":"電影在牆上的投影太暗了，所以老師拉上窗簾讓畫面更清楚。"},{"w":"project","p":"n.","d":"a piece of planned work that takes time to finish","c":"專案；計畫；作業","s":"For our science project, we grew beans in three kinds of soil and measured how tall they got each week.","t":"在我們的科學專題作業中，我們在三種土壤裡種豆子，並每週測量它們長多高。"},{"w":"project","p":"v.","d":"to say what will probably happen in the future; to show an image on a screen","c":"預計；投射","s":"Experts project that electric cars will make up half of all new cars sold in the country by 2035.","t":"專家預計到 2035 年，電動車將佔全國新車銷售的一半。"},{"w":"projector","p":"n.","d":"a machine that shows pictures or films on a wall or screen","c":"投影機","s":"The projector in our classroom stopped working this morning, so the teacher wrote all the notes on the whiteboard instead.","t":"我們教室的投影機今天早上壞了，所以老師改把所有筆記寫在白板上。"},{"w":"prolong","p":"v.","d":"to make something last longer","c":"延長","s":"Regular exercise and a healthy diet can prolong your life by several years, according to the new study.","t":"根據這項新研究，規律運動和健康飲食可以延長你的壽命好幾年。","h":1},{"w":"prolonged","p":"adj.","d":"continuing for a long time","c":"長期的；持續很久的","s":"After a prolonged period of dry weather, the farmers were finally happy to see dark clouds and heavy rain.","t":"經過一段長期的乾旱天氣後，農夫們終於很高興看到烏雲和大雨。"},{"w":"prolong one's stay","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay somewhere longer than planned","c":"延長停留時間","s":"We liked the beach town so much that we decided to prolong our stay by three more days.","t":"我們太喜歡那個海灘小鎮了，所以決定延長停留三天。","a":"prolong our stay"},{"w":"prone","p":"adj.","d":"likely to suffer from something or to do something bad","c":"易於…的；有…傾向的","s":"People who sit at a computer all day are prone to back pain, so they should stand up and stretch every hour.","t":"整天坐在電腦前的人容易背痛，所以他們應該每小時站起來伸展一下。","h":1},{"w":"be prone to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to often suffer from or do something","c":"容易…；有…傾向","s":"My little brother is prone to colds in winter, so my mother makes him wear a scarf every morning.","t":"我弟弟冬天容易感冒，所以我媽媽每天早上都要他戴圍巾。","a":"is prone to"},{"w":"accident-prone","p":"adj.","d":"often having accidents","c":"容易出意外的","s":"My cousin is so accident-prone that he has broken his arm twice and his leg once in only two years.","t":"我表弟實在太容易出意外了，短短兩年內他手臂斷了兩次，腿斷了一次。"},{"w":"propaganda","p":"n.","d":"information, often false, used to make people support an idea or leader","c":"宣傳；政治宣傳","s":"During the war, the government used posters and radio propaganda to make people believe that victory was close.","t":"戰爭期間，政府利用海報和廣播宣傳讓人民相信勝利就在眼前。","h":1},{"w":"propagate","p":"v.","d":"to spread an idea or belief to many people; to grow new plants","c":"傳播；繁殖","s":"False stories can propagate quickly on social media, so always check the source before you share something.","t":"假消息在社群媒體上可能迅速傳播，所以分享之前一定要查證來源。"},{"w":"political propaganda","p":"n.phr.","d":"information spread by a government or party to influence people","c":"政治宣傳","s":"The old film is full of political propaganda, so our history teacher asked us to notice how it tries to shape our feelings.","t":"這部老電影充滿政治宣傳，所以歷史老師要我們注意它如何試圖左右我們的感受。"},{"w":"prophet","p":"n.","d":"a person believed to receive messages from God; someone who says what will happen","c":"先知","s":"In the story, the old prophet warned the king that a great flood would come if the people did not change their ways.","t":"在故事裡，年老的先知警告國王，如果人民不改變他們的行為，大洪水就會來臨。","h":1},{"w":"prophecy","p":"n.","d":"a statement about what will happen in the future","c":"預言","s":"The prophecy said that a child born in winter would one day become king, so everyone watched the royal babies closely.","t":"預言說一個冬天出生的孩子有一天會成為國王，所以大家都密切注意王室的嬰兒。"},{"w":"prophesy","p":"v.","d":"to say what will happen in the future","c":"預言","s":"Nobody could prophesy that the small online shop would grow into one of the biggest companies in Asia.","t":"沒有人能預言那家小網路商店會成長為亞洲最大的公司之一。"},{"w":"prophetic","p":"adj.","d":"correctly saying what will happen in the future","c":"預言的；有先見之明的","s":"Her words turned out to be prophetic, because the bridge really did fall down in the next big typhoon.","t":"她的話結果真的是有先見之明的，因為那座橋真的在下一次大颱風中倒塌了。"},{"w":"proportion","p":"n.","d":"a part or share of a whole; the relationship in size between two things","c":"比例；部分","s":"A large proportion of the students in our school ride bicycles, so the parking area is always full by eight o'clock.","t":"我們學校有很大比例的學生騎腳踏車，所以停車區在八點前總是停滿了。","h":1},{"w":"in proportion to","p":"phr.","d":"in the correct relationship to the size or amount of something","c":"與…成比例","s":"The size of the pizza is in proportion to its price, so the family size costs almost twice as much as the small one.","t":"披薩的大小與價格成比例，所以家庭號的價格幾乎是小份的兩倍。"},{"w":"out of proportion","p":"phr.","d":"too big or too strong compared to the real situation","c":"不成比例；過度","s":"His anger was completely out of proportion; it was only a small mistake, but he shouted for almost ten minutes.","t":"他的憤怒完全不成比例；那只是個小錯誤，但他吼了將近十分鐘。"},{"w":"proportional","p":"adj.","d":"changing in size or amount in the same way as something else","c":"成比例的","s":"Your tax should be proportional to your income, so people who earn more money pay more to the government.","t":"你的稅應該與收入成比例，所以賺更多錢的人要付更多稅給政府。"},{"w":"proportionally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that matches the size or amount of something","c":"按比例地","s":"The prize money will be shared proportionally, so the person who sold the most tickets will get the biggest part.","t":"獎金將按比例分配，所以賣出最多票的人會得到最大的一份。"},{"w":"prosecution","p":"n.","d":"the process of trying to prove in court that someone is guilty; the lawyers who do this","c":"起訴；檢方","s":"The prosecution showed the jury a video of the man taking money from the shop, and he was found guilty an hour later.","t":"檢方向陪審團播放了那名男子從店裡拿錢的影片，一小時後他被判有罪。","h":1},{"w":"prosecute","p":"v.","d":"to officially accuse someone of a crime in court","c":"起訴","s":"The company decided to prosecute the former worker who had stolen secret plans and sold them to a rival.","t":"公司決定起訴那名偷走機密計畫並賣給競爭對手的前員工。"},{"w":"prosecutor","p":"n.","d":"a lawyer who tries to prove in court that someone is guilty","c":"檢察官","s":"The prosecutor asked the judge for a long prison sentence because the man had hurt three people in the fight.","t":"檢察官要求法官判處長期徒刑，因為那名男子在打鬥中傷了三個人。"},{"w":"prospect","p":"n.","d":"the possibility that something will happen; the idea of something in the future","c":"前景；可能性","s":"The prospect of spending a whole week at the beach made the children so excited that they could not sleep.","t":"想到要在海邊度過整整一週的前景，孩子們興奮得睡不著。","h":1},{"w":"prospects","p":"n.","d":"the chances of being successful in the future","c":"前途；成功的機會","s":"With a degree in computer science, her job prospects are excellent, and three companies have already offered her a position.","t":"有了資訊科學學位，她的工作前景非常好，已經有三家公司提供她職位。"},{"w":"prospective","p":"adj.","d":"likely to become or do something in the future","c":"未來的；可能的","s":"The school held an open day for prospective students and their parents, who walked around the campus and asked many questions.","t":"學校為未來的學生及其家長舉辦了開放日，他們在校園裡走動並提出許多問題。"},{"w":"prospect for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to search for gold, oil, or other valuable things in the ground","c":"勘探；探勘","s":"In the 1800s, thousands of people traveled to California to prospect for gold in the rivers and mountains.","t":"在 1800 年代，成千上萬的人前往加州，在河流和山區探勘黃金。"}]},{"unit":28,"theme":"province – realism","cards":[{"w":"province","p":"n.","d":"one of the large areas that some countries are divided into","c":"省","s":"My pen pal lives in a small town in the province of Quebec, where most people speak French at home.","t":"我的筆友住在魁北克省的一個小鎮，那裡大多數人在家說法語。","h":1},{"w":"provincial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a province; connected with a local area, not the capital","c":"省的；地方的","s":"The provincial government has promised to build a new hospital in the mountain area within the next three years.","t":"省政府承諾在未來三年內於山區興建一所新醫院。"},{"w":"provincial capital","p":"n.phr.","d":"the main city of a province","c":"省會","s":"Chengdu is the provincial capital of Sichuan, and it is famous for its spicy food and lovely pandas.","t":"成都是四川的省會，以辣味美食和可愛的熊貓聞名。"},{"w":"provision","p":"n.","d":"a condition or rule in a law or agreement","c":"條款；規定","s":"The contract has a provision that allows either side to end the agreement if they give one month's notice.","t":"這份合約有一項條款，允許任何一方在提前一個月通知後終止協議。","h":1},{"w":"provision","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving or supplying something that is needed","c":"提供；供應","s":"The provision of free lunches for poor students has helped many children stay in school and study better.","t":"為貧困學生提供免費午餐，幫助許多孩子留在學校並學得更好。"},{"w":"provisions","p":"n.","d":"food and other things needed for a journey","c":"糧食；補給品","s":"Before the long hike, we packed enough provisions for four days, including rice, dried fruit, and plenty of water.","t":"長途健行之前，我們打包了足夠四天的糧食補給，包括米、果乾和大量的水。"},{"w":"provide","p":"v.","d":"to give someone something that they need","c":"提供","s":"The hotel will provide free breakfast for all guests, so you do not need to buy food in the morning.","t":"飯店會為所有客人提供免費早餐，所以你早上不需要買食物。"},{"w":"make provision for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to prepare for something that will happen in the future","c":"為…預作準備","s":"Parents should make provision for their children's education by saving a little money every month from the time they are born.","t":"父母應該從孩子出生起每個月存一點錢，為孩子的教育預作準備。"},{"w":"provoke","p":"v.","d":"to make someone angry on purpose","c":"激怒；挑釁","s":"Do not provoke your little brother by taking his toys, or he will start crying and Mom will blame you.","t":"不要拿走你弟弟的玩具來激怒他，否則他會開始哭，媽媽會怪你。","h":1},{"w":"provoke","p":"v.","d":"to cause a strong reaction or feeling","c":"引起；引發","s":"The new school rule about hair color is likely to provoke a strong reaction from students and their parents.","t":"關於髮色的新校規很可能會引發學生和家長的強烈反應。"},{"w":"provocative","p":"adj.","d":"intended to make people angry or to cause discussion","c":"挑釁的；引發爭議的","s":"His provocative comments about the national team made many fans angry, and some of them wrote to the newspaper.","t":"他對國家隊挑釁的評論激怒了許多球迷，有些人還寫信給報社。"},{"w":"provocation","p":"n.","d":"an action or words that make someone angry","c":"挑釁；激怒","s":"The dog bit the boy without any provocation, so the owner has to keep it on a leash from now on.","t":"那隻狗在沒有任何挑釁的情況下咬了男孩，所以從現在起飼主必須用牽繩牽著牠。"},{"w":"pulse","p":"n.","d":"the regular beat of blood that you can feel in your body","c":"脈搏","s":"The nurse put two fingers on my wrist to check my pulse, and she said it was a little fast because I was nervous.","t":"護士把兩根手指放在我手腕上檢查脈搏，她說有點快，因為我很緊張。","h":1},{"w":"pulse","p":"v.","d":"to move or beat with a strong regular rhythm","c":"搏動；跳動","s":"The music was so loud that I could feel the beat pulse through the floor and up into my chest.","t":"音樂大聲到我能感覺到節拍穿過地板搏動，一直傳到我的胸口。"},{"w":"take sb's pulse","p":"v.phr.","d":"to count how fast someone's heart is beating","c":"量某人的脈搏","s":"The doctor will take your pulse first, and then she will listen to your heart with her stethoscope.","t":"醫生會先量你的脈搏，然後再用聽診器聽你的心跳。","a":"take your pulse"},{"w":"pulse rate","p":"n.phr.","d":"the number of heartbeats per minute","c":"脈搏速率","s":"After running up five floors, my pulse rate was over one hundred and twenty beats a minute.","t":"跑上五層樓之後，我的脈搏速率超過每分鐘一百二十下。"},{"w":"purchase","p":"v.","d":"to buy something","c":"購買","s":"You can purchase tickets for the concert online, but you must print them out and bring them to the gate.","t":"你可以在網路上購買演唱會的票，但必須把票印出來帶到入口。","h":1},{"w":"purchase","p":"n.","d":"the act of buying something; something you have bought","c":"購買；購買的物品","s":"Please keep the receipt for your purchase, because the shop will not give you a refund without it.","t":"請保留你購買商品的收據，因為沒有收據商店不會退款。"},{"w":"make a purchase","p":"v.phr.","d":"to buy something","c":"購物；買東西","s":"The website gives you free shipping when you make a purchase of more than one thousand dollars.","t":"當你購物超過一千元時，這個網站提供免運費。"},{"w":"purchaser","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys something","c":"購買者；買方","s":"The purchaser of the old house plans to turn it into a small coffee shop with a garden in the back.","t":"那棟老房子的買主打算把它改成一間後面有花園的小咖啡店。"},{"w":"pyramid","p":"n.","d":"a large stone building with a square base and sloping sides that meet at a point","c":"金字塔","s":"The largest pyramid in Egypt was built more than four thousand years ago, and it is still standing in the desert today.","t":"埃及最大的金字塔建於四千多年前，至今仍矗立在沙漠中。","h":1},{"w":"pyramid","p":"n.","d":"a shape or chart that is wide at the bottom and narrow at the top","c":"金字塔形（圖表）","s":"The food pyramid shows that we should eat a lot of vegetables and grains but only a little sugar and fat.","t":"食物金字塔顯示我們應該多吃蔬菜和穀物，但只能吃一點糖和脂肪。"},{"w":"pyramid scheme","p":"n.phr.","d":"a dishonest business in which people are paid for bringing in new members","c":"金字塔騙局；老鼠會","s":"The police warned people not to join the pyramid scheme, which promised quick money but only made the leaders rich.","t":"警方警告民眾不要加入那個金字塔騙局，它承諾快速賺錢，卻只讓上層的人致富。"},{"w":"qualify","p":"v.","d":"to have the skills or pass the test needed for a job or a competition","c":"取得資格","s":"She needs to pass one more exam to qualify as a nurse, so she is studying very hard every night.","t":"她還需要通過一場考試才能取得護理師資格，所以她每晚都非常用功。","h":1},{"w":"qualify for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have the right to enter or receive something","c":"有…的資格；取得…資格","s":"Our basketball team must win tomorrow's game to qualify for the national finals in Taipei next month.","t":"我們的籃球隊必須贏得明天的比賽，才能取得下個月台北全國決賽的資格。"},{"w":"qualified","p":"adj.","d":"having the training or skills needed for a job","c":"合格的；有資格的","s":"Only qualified teachers are allowed to lead the swimming class, because safety in the pool is extremely important.","t":"只有合格的老師才能帶游泳課，因為泳池的安全極為重要。"},{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"a skill, degree, or certificate that makes you suitable for a job","c":"資格；證書","s":"A university degree is the basic qualification for this job, but the company also wants two years of work experience.","t":"大學學位是這份工作的基本資格，但公司也希望有兩年的工作經驗。"},{"w":"disqualify","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone from taking part because they broke a rule","c":"取消資格","s":"The judges had to disqualify the runner because he started before the starting gun was fired.","t":"裁判必須取消那名跑者的資格，因為他在發令槍響之前就起跑了。"},{"w":"quest","p":"n.","d":"a long search for something important","c":"尋求；探索","s":"The knight set out on a quest to find the magic sword that could save the kingdom from the dragon.","t":"騎士踏上探索之旅，去尋找能拯救王國免受惡龍之害的魔法劍。","h":1},{"w":"in quest of","p":"phr.","d":"searching for something","c":"尋求；追求","s":"Thousands of young people move to the city every year in quest of better jobs and a more exciting life.","t":"每年有成千上萬的年輕人搬到城市，尋求更好的工作和更精彩的生活。"},{"w":"request","p":"n.","d":"the act of asking for something politely or formally","c":"要求；請求","s":"We made a request for a table by the window, and the waiter kindly moved us there after a few minutes.","t":"我們要求一張靠窗的桌子，服務生幾分鐘後很親切地把我們換到那裡。"},{"w":"request","p":"v.","d":"to ask for something politely or formally","c":"要求；請求","s":"Passengers may request a special meal when they book their flight, such as vegetarian food or a children's meal.","t":"乘客可以在訂機票時要求特別餐，例如素食或兒童餐。"},{"w":"questionnaire","p":"n.","d":"a list of questions used to collect information from people","c":"問卷","s":"Please fill in this short questionnaire about your eating habits; it will take only five minutes and your answers are private.","t":"請填寫這份關於飲食習慣的簡短問卷；只需五分鐘，而且你的答案會保密。","h":1},{"w":"fill out a questionnaire","p":"v.phr.","d":"to write your answers on a list of questions","c":"填寫問卷","s":"All the guests were asked to fill out a questionnaire about the hotel service before they checked out.","t":"所有客人在退房前都被請求填寫一份關於飯店服務的問卷。"},{"w":"question","p":"n.","d":"a sentence that asks for information","c":"問題","s":"If you have any question about the homework, you can ask me after class or send me an email tonight.","t":"如果你對功課有任何問題，可以下課後問我，或今晚寄電子郵件給我。"},{"w":"question","p":"v.","d":"to ask someone questions; to have doubts about something","c":"詢問；質疑","s":"The police will question the two men who were seen near the bank just before the robbery happened.","t":"警方將詢問搶案發生前被看到在銀行附近的那兩名男子。"},{"w":"questionable","p":"adj.","d":"not certain to be true, correct, or honest","c":"可疑的；有問題的","s":"The report uses some questionable numbers, so the teacher asked the students to check their sources again.","t":"這份報告用了一些有問題的數據，所以老師要學生再查一次資料來源。"},{"w":"quiver","p":"v.","d":"to shake slightly because you are cold, afraid, or excited","c":"顫動；發抖","s":"Her lips began to quiver as she stood on the stage, but she took a deep breath and started her speech.","t":"她站在舞台上時嘴唇開始顫抖，但她深吸一口氣，開始了她的演講。","h":1},{"w":"quiver","p":"n.","d":"a slight shaking movement","c":"顫動；顫抖","s":"There was a quiver in his voice when he told us that his old dog had died the night before.","t":"當他告訴我們他的老狗前一晚過世時，他的聲音裡帶著一絲顫抖。"},{"w":"quiver with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to shake because of a strong feeling","c":"因…而顫抖","s":"The little puppy quivers with excitement every time it hears the sound of its owner's car in the driveway.","t":"每當小狗聽到主人的車開進車道的聲音，牠就興奮得全身顫抖。","a":"quivers with"},{"w":"quota","p":"n.","d":"a fixed amount or number that is allowed or must be reached","c":"配額；限額","s":"Each salesperson has a monthly quota of fifty cars, and those who sell more receive a special bonus.","t":"每位業務員每個月有五十輛車的配額，賣得更多的人會得到特別獎金。","h":1},{"w":"meet a quota","p":"v.phr.","d":"to reach the number or amount that is required","c":"達到配額","s":"The workers had to stay late every day this week in order to meet their quota before the end of the month.","t":"工人們這週每天都得待到很晚，才能在月底前達到配額。","a":"meet their quota"},{"w":"import quota","p":"n.phr.","d":"a limit on how much of a product can be brought into a country","c":"進口配額","s":"The government set an import quota on foreign rice to protect local farmers from cheaper products.","t":"政府對外國米設定進口配額，以保護本地農民免受較便宜產品的衝擊。"},{"w":"racism","p":"n.","d":"unfair treatment of people because of their race","c":"種族主義；種族歧視","s":"The football player spoke out against racism after fans shouted hurtful words at him during the match.","t":"那名足球員在比賽中被球迷辱罵後，公開發聲反對種族歧視。","h":1},{"w":"racist","p":"adj.","d":"showing unfair treatment of people because of their race","c":"種族歧視的","s":"The company fired the manager who made racist jokes about his coworkers at the office party.","t":"公司開除了那位在辦公室派對上對同事開種族歧視玩笑的經理。"},{"w":"racist","p":"n.","d":"a person who treats others unfairly because of their race","c":"種族主義者","s":"Nobody wants to be called a racist, so think carefully before you make jokes about people from other countries.","t":"沒有人想被稱為種族主義者，所以在拿其他國家的人開玩笑之前要仔細想想。"},{"w":"race","p":"n.","d":"a group of people with the same skin color or other physical features","c":"種族","s":"People of every race and religion live together peacefully in this neighborhood, and they celebrate each other's festivals.","t":"這個社區裡各種種族和宗教的人和平共處，而且會一起慶祝彼此的節日。"},{"w":"racial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a person's race","c":"種族的","s":"The school teaches children to respect racial differences and to treat every classmate as a friend.","t":"這所學校教導孩子尊重種族差異，並把每位同學當作朋友。"},{"w":"rack","p":"n.","d":"a frame or shelf with bars for holding things","c":"架子","s":"Hang your wet coat on the rack by the door so that it can dry before you go home this evening.","t":"把你的濕外套掛在門邊的架子上，這樣它在你今晚回家前可以晾乾。","h":1},{"w":"rack one's brain","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think very hard to remember or solve something","c":"絞盡腦汁","s":"I racked my brain for an hour but still could not remember where I had left my keys.","t":"我絞盡腦汁想了一個小時，還是想不起來我把鑰匙放在哪裡。","a":"racked my brain"},{"w":"rack","p":"v.","d":"to cause great pain or suffering","c":"使痛苦；折磨","s":"The old man was racked with pain after the fall, and his family rushed him to the hospital.","t":"那位老人跌倒後飽受疼痛折磨，家人趕緊送他去醫院。","a":"racked"},{"w":"luggage rack","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shelf above the seats on a train or bus for bags","c":"行李架","s":"Put your suitcase on the luggage rack above your seat so that it does not block the aisle of the train.","t":"把你的行李箱放在座位上方的行李架上，這樣它才不會擋住火車的走道。"},{"w":"radiation","p":"n.","d":"energy sent out as waves or tiny particles, which can be harmful","c":"輻射","s":"Workers at the nuclear plant wear special suits to protect themselves from radiation, and they are checked by doctors every month.","t":"核電廠的工人穿著特殊防護衣保護自己免受輻射，而且每個月都接受醫生檢查。","h":1},{"w":"radiate","p":"v.","d":"to send out heat, light, or a feeling in all directions","c":"散發；放射","s":"The fireplace began to radiate warmth through the small room, and soon we took off our heavy coats.","t":"壁爐開始向小房間散發暖意，很快我們就脫下了厚重的外套。"},{"w":"radioactive","p":"adj.","d":"sending out radiation that can be dangerous","c":"放射性的","s":"The radioactive waste from the power plant must be stored safely underground for thousands of years.","t":"發電廠的放射性廢料必須安全地儲存在地下數千年。"},{"w":"radiator","p":"n.","d":"a metal object that gives out heat to warm a room; the part that cools a car engine","c":"暖氣片；散熱器","s":"The radiator in our hotel room was broken, so we had to sleep in our coats on the coldest night of the trip.","t":"我們飯店房間的暖氣片壞了，所以在旅途中最冷的那一晚我們只好穿著外套睡覺。"},{"w":"radical","p":"adj.","d":"very new and different; wanting great social change","c":"激進的；徹底的","s":"The new principal made some radical changes, such as starting school at nine and ending all tests on Mondays.","t":"新校長做了一些徹底的改變，例如九點才上學，以及取消所有星期一的考試。","h":1},{"w":"radical","p":"n.","d":"a person who wants great political or social change","c":"激進分子","s":"In his youth, my grandfather was a radical who marched in the streets to demand better pay for factory workers.","t":"我爺爺年輕時是個激進分子，曾走上街頭要求提高工廠工人的薪資。"},{"w":"radically","p":"adv.","d":"completely; in a very big way","c":"徹底地；根本地","s":"The town has changed radically since I was a child; the rice fields are gone, and there are tall buildings everywhere.","t":"這個小鎮自我小時候以來已經徹底改變了；稻田不見了，到處都是高樓。"},{"w":"ragged","p":"adj.","d":"old and torn; rough and uneven","c":"破爛的；衣衫襤褸的","s":"The beggar wore a ragged coat with holes in both sleeves, so a kind woman gave him her husband's old jacket.","t":"那個乞丐穿著一件兩邊袖子都有破洞的破爛外套，所以一位好心的女士把她丈夫的舊夾克給了他。","h":1},{"w":"rag","p":"n.","d":"a piece of old cloth used for cleaning","c":"破布；抹布","s":"Use this old rag to wipe the oil off the floor before someone slips and falls on it.","t":"用這塊舊抹布把地板上的油擦掉，免得有人滑倒。"},{"w":"from rags to riches","p":"phr.","d":"from being very poor to being very rich","c":"從貧窮到富有；白手起家","s":"The poor boy in the story went from rags to riches after he found a magic lamp hidden in the cave.","t":"故事裡的窮男孩在洞穴裡找到一盞神燈後，從貧窮變成富有。"},{"w":"raid","p":"n.","d":"a sudden attack; a sudden visit by the police to search a place","c":"突襲；搜查","s":"The police made a surprise raid on the warehouse at dawn and found hundreds of fake designer handbags inside.","t":"警方在黎明時對那間倉庫進行突襲搜查，在裡面發現數百個假名牌手提包。","h":1},{"w":"raid","p":"v.","d":"to attack a place suddenly; to enter a place to search for something","c":"突襲；搜查","s":"Soldiers planned to raid the enemy camp before sunrise, when most of the guards would be asleep.","t":"士兵計畫在日出前突襲敵營，那時大多數的守衛都會在睡覺。"},{"w":"air raid","p":"n.phr.","d":"an attack by planes dropping bombs","c":"空襲","s":"During the war, families hid in the basement every time the air raid warning sounded across the city.","t":"戰爭期間，每當空襲警報在全城響起，家家戶戶就躲進地下室。"},{"w":"raid the fridge","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take food from the refrigerator, especially late at night","c":"翻冰箱找東西吃","s":"My teenage brother likes to raid the fridge at midnight, so there is never any cake left for breakfast.","t":"我那青少年的弟弟喜歡在半夜翻冰箱找東西吃，所以早餐從來沒有剩下的蛋糕。"},{"w":"rail","p":"n.","d":"a bar fixed along a wall or stairs to hold on to; a metal track for trains","c":"欄杆；扶手；鐵軌","s":"Hold on to the rail when you go down these stairs, because the steps are steep and wet after the rain.","t":"下這些樓梯時要抓著扶手，因為雨後台階又陡又濕。","h":1},{"w":"by rail","p":"phr.","d":"by train","c":"搭火車","s":"Traveling by rail from Taipei to Kaohsiung takes only about ninety minutes on the high-speed train.","t":"搭火車從台北到高雄，搭高鐵只要大約九十分鐘。"},{"w":"railway","p":"n.","d":"a track for trains; the system of trains in a country","c":"鐵路","s":"The old railway was built in 1908 and still carries tourists through the mountains to the hot spring town.","t":"這條老鐵路建於 1908 年，至今仍載著遊客穿越山區到溫泉小鎮。"},{"w":"railing","p":"n.","d":"a fence made of bars that stops people from falling","c":"欄杆；圍欄","s":"The children leaned over the railing of the bridge to watch the fish swimming in the clear water below.","t":"孩子們靠在橋的欄杆上，看著下方清澈水中游動的魚。"},{"w":"rally","p":"n.","d":"a large public meeting to support an idea or a person","c":"集會","s":"Thousands of people joined the rally in front of the city hall to ask for cleaner air and safer streets.","t":"數千人參加了市政府前的集會，要求更乾淨的空氣和更安全的街道。","h":1},{"w":"rally","p":"v.","d":"to bring people together to support something; to become strong again","c":"召集；團結；恢復","s":"The coach tried to rally the players after they lost the first half, and they came back to win the game.","t":"球員輸掉上半場後，教練努力振作大家，結果他們反敗為勝。"},{"w":"rally around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to come together to help or support someone","c":"團結支持","s":"When our classmate's house burned down, the whole school rallied around her family and collected clothes and money.","t":"我們同學的房子燒毀時，全校團結支持她的家人，並募集了衣物和金錢。","a":"rallied around"},{"w":"pep rally","p":"n.phr.","d":"a school meeting to cheer for a sports team before a game","c":"誓師大會；加油大會","s":"Before the big game, the school held a pep rally in the gym, and the cheerleaders led everyone in songs.","t":"大賽之前，學校在體育館舉辦了加油大會，啦啦隊帶領大家一起唱歌。"},{"w":"ranch","p":"n.","d":"a large farm where cows, horses, or sheep are kept","c":"牧場","s":"My uncle owns a cattle ranch in the hills, where he raises more than two hundred cows for milk and beef.","t":"我叔叔在山丘上有一座養牛牧場，他在那裡養了兩百多頭牛來生產牛奶和牛肉。","h":1},{"w":"ranch","p":"v.","d":"to run a large farm with animals","c":"經營牧場","s":"His family has ranched in this valley for four generations, and he hopes his children will continue the tradition.","t":"他的家族在這個山谷經營牧場已經四代了，他希望孩子們能延續這個傳統。","a":"ranched"},{"w":"rancher","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns or works on a ranch","c":"牧場主；牧場工人","s":"The rancher rides his horse across the fields every morning to make sure that none of the cows are sick or missing.","t":"牧場主人每天早上騎馬穿過田野，確認沒有牛生病或走失。"},{"w":"random","p":"adj.","d":"chosen or happening without any plan or pattern","c":"隨機的；任意的","s":"The teacher picked five random students to answer questions, so everyone in the class had to be ready.","t":"老師隨機挑了五位學生回答問題，所以班上每個人都得準備好。","h":1},{"w":"at random","p":"phr.","d":"without any plan or pattern","c":"隨機地；任意地","s":"The winner of the prize was chosen at random from all the tickets in the box, and it turned out to be my cousin.","t":"得獎者是從箱子裡所有的票中隨機抽出的，結果竟然是我表妹。"},{"w":"randomly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that has no plan or pattern","c":"隨機地","s":"The computer randomly puts students into groups of four, so you may not be with your best friend.","t":"電腦隨機把學生分成四人一組，所以你可能不會和你最好的朋友同一組。"},{"w":"ratio","p":"n.","d":"the relationship between two amounts, shown as two numbers","c":"比率；比例","s":"The ratio of boys to girls in our class is three to two, so there are eighteen boys and twelve girls.","t":"我們班男生和女生的比例是三比二，所以有十八個男生和十二個女生。","h":1},{"w":"rate","p":"n.","d":"a number that shows how often something happens or how fast it changes","c":"比率；速率","s":"The rate of unemployment fell to three percent last year, which is the lowest number in twenty years.","t":"去年失業率降到百分之三，這是二十年來最低的數字。"},{"w":"rate","p":"v.","d":"to say how good or bad something is","c":"評價；評定","s":"Customers can rate the restaurant online with one to five stars after they finish their meal.","t":"顧客用餐結束後可以在網路上用一到五顆星評價這家餐廳。"},{"w":"rational","p":"adj.","d":"based on reason and clear thinking, not on feelings","c":"理性的；合理的","s":"Buying a second car just because your neighbor has one is not a rational decision, especially when money is tight.","t":"只因為鄰居有一輛車就買第二輛車，並不是理性的決定，尤其是在手頭很緊的時候。","h":1},{"w":"rationally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is based on reason and clear thinking","c":"理性地","s":"When you are angry, it is hard to think rationally, so wait until you calm down before you answer the message.","t":"生氣的時候很難理性地思考，所以等你冷靜下來再回覆訊息。"},{"w":"irrational","p":"adj.","d":"not based on reason; not sensible","c":"不理性的；無理的","s":"She has an irrational fear of butterflies and screams every time one flies near her in the garden.","t":"她對蝴蝶有一種不理性的恐懼，每次有蝴蝶在花園裡飛近她，她就會尖叫。"},{"w":"rationalize","p":"v.","d":"to find a reason to explain a bad action so that it seems acceptable","c":"合理化","s":"He tried to rationalize his lie by saying that he only wanted to protect his friend from getting into trouble.","t":"他試圖把自己的謊言合理化，說他只是想保護朋友不惹上麻煩。"},{"w":"rattle","p":"v.","d":"to make a series of short, quick knocking sounds","c":"發出咯咯聲；使咯咯作響","s":"The strong wind made the old windows rattle all night, so none of us could sleep well.","t":"強風讓老舊的窗戶整晚咯咯作響，所以我們沒有人睡得好。","h":1},{"w":"rattle","p":"n.","d":"a series of short, quick knocking sounds; a baby's toy that makes this sound","c":"咯咯聲；撥浪鼓","s":"The baby laughed every time her father shook the plastic rattle in front of her eyes.","t":"每次爸爸在寶寶眼前搖那個塑膠撥浪鼓，她就會笑。"},{"w":"rattle","p":"v.","d":"to make someone nervous or worried","c":"使緊張；使慌亂","s":"The tough questions from the reporters seemed to rattle the young singer, and she forgot what she wanted to say.","t":"記者們尖銳的問題似乎使那位年輕歌手慌了手腳，她忘了自己想說什麼。"},{"w":"rattle off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say something quickly and easily from memory","c":"一口氣說出；滔滔不絕地說","s":"The boy can rattle off the names of all the planets in less than ten seconds without stopping to think.","t":"那個男孩能在十秒內一口氣說出所有行星的名字，完全不用停下來想。"},{"w":"realism","p":"n.","d":"accepting things as they really are; art or writing that shows life as it really is","c":"現實主義；寫實","s":"The painting is admired for its realism; you can see every wrinkle on the old farmer's face and every stone on the road.","t":"這幅畫因其寫實而受到讚賞；你可以看到老農夫臉上的每一道皺紋和路上的每一顆石頭。","h":1},{"w":"realistic","p":"adj.","d":"sensible and possible; looking like real life","c":"實際的；逼真的","s":"Running a marathon next month is not realistic if you have never run more than three kilometers.","t":"如果你從來沒跑超過三公里，下個月跑馬拉松是不切實際的。"},{"w":"realist","p":"n.","d":"a person who accepts things as they really are","c":"現實主義者；務實的人","s":"My mother is a realist who plans for problems before they happen, while my father just hopes for the best.","t":"我媽媽是個務實的人，會在問題發生前先做好準備，而我爸爸只是抱持最好的希望。"},{"w":"reality","p":"n.","d":"the way things really are, not how you imagine them","c":"現實","s":"In the movie, the hero can fly, but in reality nobody can jump off a building and live.","t":"在電影裡英雄會飛，但在現實中沒有人能從大樓跳下來還活著。"},{"w":"realize","p":"v.","d":"to understand or notice something; to make a plan or dream happen","c":"意識到；實現","s":"I did not realize how late it was until I looked at the clock and saw that it was already midnight.","t":"直到我看了時鐘發現已經半夜了，我才意識到時間有多晚。"}]},{"unit":29,"theme":"realm – resident","cards":[{"w":"realm","p":"n.","d":"an area of activity, interest, or knowledge; a kingdom","c":"領域；範圍；王國","s":"Artificial intelligence used to belong to the realm of science fiction, but today it helps doctors, teachers, and even farmers every day.","t":"人工智慧過去屬於科幻小說的領域，但今天它每天幫助醫生、老師，甚至農夫。","h":1},{"w":"in the realm of","p":"phr.","d":"within a particular area of activity or thought","c":"在…的範圍內；屬於…的領域","s":"Flying cars are still in the realm of dreams, although several companies say they will sell one within ten years.","t":"飛行汽車仍然屬於夢想的範圍，儘管有幾家公司說十年內就會開始販售。"},{"w":"within the realm of possibility","p":"phr.","d":"something that could really happen","c":"有可能的；在可能範圍內","s":"Winning the national championship is within the realm of possibility for our small school team, so the players train hard every single day.","t":"對我們學校的小球隊來說，贏得全國冠軍是有可能的，所以球員們每天都努力練習。"},{"w":"rear","p":"adj.","d":"at the back of something","c":"後面的；後部的","s":"Please use the rear door of the bus when you get off, because the front one is only for passengers getting on.","t":"下車時請使用公車的後門，因為前門只給上車的乘客使用。","h":1},{"w":"rear","p":"n.","d":"the back part of something","c":"後部；後面","s":"The students who arrived late had to sit at the rear of the hall, where it was hard to see the stage.","t":"遲到的學生只能坐在大廳的後面，那裡很難看到舞台。"},{"w":"rear","p":"v.","d":"to care for children or young animals until they are grown","c":"養育；飼養","s":"My grandparents reared seven children on a small farm, and all of them grew up to be healthy and hard-working adults.","t":"我的祖父母在一座小農場上養育了七個孩子，他們全都長成健康又勤奮的大人。","a":"reared"},{"w":"bring up the rear","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the last in a line or group","c":"殿後；排在最後","s":"During the mountain hike, the teacher walked in front, and the school nurse brought up the rear to make sure nobody was left behind.","t":"登山健行時，老師走在前面，校護殿後，以確保沒有人被落下。","a":"brought up the rear"},{"w":"rearview mirror","p":"n.phr.","d":"the mirror inside a car that shows the road behind","c":"後視鏡","s":"Before you change lanes on the highway, always check the rearview mirror and look over your shoulder for motorcycles.","t":"在高速公路上變換車道之前，一定要先看後視鏡並回頭確認有沒有機車。"},{"w":"reassure","p":"v.","d":"to say or do something to make someone feel less worried","c":"使安心；安撫","s":"The doctor tried to reassure the nervous patient by explaining that the operation was simple and would take only thirty minutes.","t":"醫生解釋手術很簡單、只需三十分鐘，試著安撫緊張的病人。","h":1},{"w":"reassuring","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel less worried","c":"令人安心的","s":"It was reassuring to hear my mother's calm voice on the phone after the earthquake, and I finally stopped shaking.","t":"地震後在電話裡聽到媽媽平靜的聲音，真是令人安心，我終於不再發抖了。"},{"w":"reassuringly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that makes someone feel less worried","c":"安撫地；令人安心地","s":"The nurse smiled reassuringly and told the boy that the needle would feel like a tiny pinch for just one second.","t":"護士安撫地微笑，告訴男孩針只會像被輕捏一下，只有一秒鐘。"},{"w":"reassurance","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that make someone feel less worried","c":"安慰；保證","s":"The new students needed some reassurance on the first day, so the teacher told them that everyone makes mistakes at the beginning.","t":"新生在第一天需要一些安慰，所以老師告訴他們每個人剛開始都會犯錯。"},{"w":"assure","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone that something is certainly true","c":"向…保證","s":"The shop owner assured us that the phone would be repaired by Friday, but it was still not ready a week later.","t":"店主向我們保證手機星期五前會修好，但一週後仍然沒好。","a":"assured"},{"w":"rebellion","p":"n.","d":"an attempt by many people to change the government by force; refusing to obey","c":"叛亂；反抗","s":"The rebellion against the king began when farmers refused to pay the new tax, and soon thousands of people joined them.","t":"反抗國王的叛亂始於農民拒絕繳納新稅，很快就有數千人加入他們。","h":1},{"w":"rebel","p":"n.","d":"a person who fights against the government or refuses to obey rules","c":"反叛者；叛軍","s":"The rebels hid in the mountains for two years, and the government soldiers could never find their secret camp.","t":"叛軍在山裡躲了兩年，政府軍始終找不到他們的秘密營地。","a":"rebels"},{"w":"rebel","p":"v.","d":"to fight against authority or refuse to obey","c":"反叛；反抗","s":"Teenagers often rebel against strict rules at home, but most of them understand their parents better when they grow up.","t":"青少年常常反抗家裡嚴格的規定，但他們大多長大後會更理解父母。"},{"w":"rebellious","p":"adj.","d":"fighting against authority; not willing to obey","c":"叛逆的","s":"My rebellious younger brother dyed his hair green the day after the school told everyone to keep their hair natural.","t":"我叛逆的弟弟在學校要大家保持自然髮色的隔天，就把頭髮染成綠色。"},{"w":"recession","p":"n.","d":"a period when a country's economy is doing badly","c":"經濟衰退","s":"During the recession, many factories closed, and my uncle lost the job he had kept for more than twenty years.","t":"經濟衰退期間，許多工廠關閉，我叔叔也失去了他做了二十多年的工作。","h":1},{"w":"recede","p":"v.","d":"to move back or become more distant; to get smaller","c":"後退；退去；減退","s":"After the typhoon passed, the flood water slowly began to recede, and people returned to clean their muddy homes.","t":"颱風過後，洪水慢慢開始退去，人們回來清理泥濘的家。"},{"w":"economic recession","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when business is bad and many people lose their jobs","c":"經濟衰退","s":"Experts warn that an economic recession may be coming, so families are saving more money and spending less on travel.","t":"專家警告經濟衰退可能即將到來，所以家庭都在多存錢、少花錢旅行。"},{"w":"recipient","p":"n.","d":"a person who receives something","c":"接受者；收件人；得獎者","s":"The recipient of this year's science prize is a young teacher who built a cheap water filter for mountain villages.","t":"今年科學獎的得獎者是一位年輕老師，他為山區村落打造了便宜的濾水器。","h":1},{"w":"receive","p":"v.","d":"to get something that is given or sent to you","c":"收到；接受","s":"Did you receive the package I sent last Monday, or should I call the post office and ask about it?","t":"你收到我上星期一寄的包裹了嗎？還是我應該打電話問郵局？"},{"w":"receipt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper showing that you have paid for something","c":"收據","s":"Keep the receipt in a safe place, because the store will not let you return the shoes without it.","t":"把收據放在安全的地方，因為沒有它商店不會讓你退鞋。"},{"w":"reception","p":"n.","d":"a formal party to welcome someone; the desk where visitors are greeted","c":"招待會；接待處","s":"Please wait at the reception desk on the first floor, and a nurse will call your name when the doctor is ready.","t":"請在一樓的接待櫃台等候，醫生準備好時護士會叫你的名字。"},{"w":"recite","p":"v.","d":"to say a poem or text aloud from memory","c":"背誦；朗誦","s":"Every student had to recite a short English poem in front of the class, and some of them were extremely nervous.","t":"每位學生都必須在全班面前背誦一首英文短詩，有些人非常緊張。","h":1},{"w":"recital","p":"n.","d":"a performance of music or poetry by one person or a small group","c":"獨奏會；獨唱會；朗誦會","s":"My sister's piano recital is next Saturday evening, and our whole family will be sitting in the front row to cheer for her.","t":"我妹妹的鋼琴獨奏會在下星期六晚上，我們全家會坐在第一排為她加油。"},{"w":"recitation","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying something aloud from memory","c":"背誦；朗誦","s":"The recitation contest will be held in the school hall, and each speaker has three minutes to perform a poem.","t":"朗誦比賽將在學校禮堂舉行，每位參賽者有三分鐘表演一首詩。"},{"w":"recommend","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone or something is good and worth choosing","c":"推薦；建議","s":"If you like spicy food, I strongly recommend the beef noodles at the small shop across from the train station.","t":"如果你喜歡辣的食物，我強烈推薦火車站對面那家小店的牛肉麵。","h":1},{"w":"recommendation","p":"n.","d":"a suggestion that something is good; a letter saying someone is good","c":"推薦；建議","s":"I bought this novel on the recommendation of my English teacher, and I finished all three hundred pages in two days.","t":"我因為英文老師的推薦買了這本小說，兩天就把三百頁全部讀完。","h":1},{"w":"letter of recommendation","p":"n.phr.","d":"a letter written to say that a person is good for a job or school","c":"推薦信","s":"To apply for the scholarship, you need two letters of recommendation from teachers who know your work well.","t":"申請這項獎學金，你需要兩封熟悉你表現的老師寫的推薦信。","a":"letters of recommendation"},{"w":"recommended","p":"adj.","d":"suggested as good or correct","c":"建議的；推薦的","s":"The recommended amount of sleep for teenagers is eight to ten hours, but most high school students get far less than that.","t":"青少年建議的睡眠時間是八到十小時，但大多數高中生睡得遠少於此。"},{"w":"highly recommend","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say strongly that something is very good","c":"強力推薦","s":"I highly recommend this travel app because it shows you the cheapest trains and tells you when the platform changes.","t":"我強力推薦這個旅遊 App，因為它會顯示最便宜的火車，還會告訴你月台何時更改。"},{"w":"recruit","p":"v.","d":"to find new people to join a company, army, or team","c":"招募；徵募","s":"The basketball club is trying to recruit tall first-year students, so the coach visits every new class during the first week.","t":"籃球社正在努力招募高個子的一年級新生，所以教練在第一週拜訪每個新班級。","h":1},{"w":"recruit","p":"n.","d":"a person who has recently joined a company, army, or group","c":"新成員；新兵","s":"The new recruits were given uniforms on their first morning, and then they ran five kilometers before breakfast.","t":"新兵在第一天早上領到制服，然後在早餐前跑了五公里。","a":"recruits"},{"w":"recruitment","p":"n.","d":"the process of finding new people to join","c":"招募；徵才","s":"The company's recruitment of engineers has slowed down this year because fewer students are studying computer science.","t":"這家公司今年工程師的招募速度變慢了，因為讀資訊科學的學生變少了。"},{"w":"recruiter","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to find new workers or members","c":"招募人員","s":"A recruiter from a famous tech company came to our university to talk with students who will graduate next June.","t":"一位知名科技公司的招募人員來到我們大學，和明年六月畢業的學生談話。"},{"w":"refuge","p":"n.","d":"a place that gives protection from danger or bad weather","c":"避難所；庇護","s":"When the storm hit, the hikers found refuge in a small wooden cabin and waited there until the wind died down.","t":"暴風雨來襲時，登山客在一間小木屋裡找到避難處，在那裡等到風停。","h":1},{"w":"take refuge in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go to a place to be safe","c":"躲避於；在…避難","s":"Hundreds of families took refuge in the school gym after the flood destroyed their homes along the river.","t":"洪水沖毀河邊的家園後，數百個家庭躲進學校體育館避難。","a":"took refuge in"},{"w":"refugee","p":"n.","d":"a person forced to leave their country because of war or danger","c":"難民","s":"The refugee children learned the new language quickly, and within a year they were helping their parents at the market.","t":"難民孩子很快學會了新語言，一年之內就在市場幫父母的忙。"},{"w":"wildlife refuge","p":"n.phr.","d":"an area where wild animals are protected","c":"野生動物保護區","s":"Thousands of birds spend the winter at the wildlife refuge near the coast, and visitors can watch them from wooden towers.","t":"數千隻鳥在海岸附近的野生動物保護區過冬，遊客可以從木塔上觀賞它們。"},{"w":"regardless","p":"adv.","d":"without being affected by anything else; anyway","c":"不管如何；無論怎樣；照樣","s":"The weather report said it might rain, but we decided to go to the beach regardless and had a wonderful day.","t":"氣象報告說可能會下雨，但我們決定照樣去海邊，度過了美好的一天。","h":1},{"w":"regardless of","p":"phr.","d":"without being affected by; no matter what","c":"不論；不管","s":"The library is open to everyone regardless of age, so you will often see grandparents reading next to small children.","t":"圖書館對所有人開放，不論年齡，所以你常會看到爺爺奶奶坐在小孩旁邊閱讀。"},{"w":"regard","p":"v.","d":"to think of someone or something in a particular way","c":"視為；認為","s":"Many people regard the old teacher as the heart of the school because she has taught there for forty years.","t":"許多人把這位老教師視為學校的核心，因為她在那裡教了四十年。"},{"w":"regarding","p":"prep.","d":"about; concerning","c":"關於","s":"The school sent a letter to parents regarding the new lunch menu, and most families were happy with the healthier choices.","t":"學校寄了一封關於新午餐菜單的信給家長，大多數家庭對更健康的選擇感到滿意。"},{"w":"disregard","p":"v.","d":"to ignore something or treat it as unimportant","c":"忽視；不理會","s":"The driver chose to disregard the warning sign and drove onto the flooded road, where his car soon stopped working.","t":"那位駕駛選擇忽視警告標誌，開上被淹的道路，他的車很快就停擺了。"},{"w":"regime","p":"n.","d":"a government, especially a strict one that was not elected","c":"政權；政體","s":"The old regime controlled all the newspapers, so people could not read any news that criticized the leaders.","t":"舊政權控制所有報紙，所以人們讀不到任何批評領導人的新聞。","h":1},{"w":"training regime","p":"n.phr.","d":"a planned program of exercise","c":"訓練計畫","s":"The swimmer follows a strict training regime that includes two hours in the pool every morning before school.","t":"這位游泳選手遵循嚴格的訓練計畫，包括每天上學前早上在泳池游兩小時。"},{"w":"regulate","p":"v.","d":"to control something by rules","c":"管制；調節","s":"The government plans to regulate the sale of energy drinks to children because they contain too much sugar and caffeine.","t":"政府計畫管制對兒童販售能量飲料，因為它們含有太多糖和咖啡因。"},{"w":"regulation","p":"n.","d":"an official rule","c":"規定；法規","s":"Under the new regulation, all restaurants must show the calories of each dish on the menu so customers can choose wisely.","t":"根據新規定，所有餐廳必須在菜單上標示每道菜的熱量，讓顧客能明智選擇。"},{"w":"rehearsal","p":"n.","d":"a practice performance before the real show","c":"排演；排練","s":"Our final rehearsal for the school play is tomorrow afternoon, so please bring your costume and know all your lines.","t":"我們學校戲劇的最後一次排演在明天下午，請帶著戲服並記熟所有台詞。","h":1},{"w":"rehearse","p":"v.","d":"to practice a play, music, or speech before performing it","c":"排演；排練","s":"The band will rehearse in the music room every evening this week because the concert is only ten days away.","t":"樂團這週每天晚上都會在音樂教室排練，因為音樂會只剩十天了。"},{"w":"dress rehearsal","p":"n.phr.","d":"the last practice of a play, with costumes, before the real show","c":"彩排；正式預演","s":"During the dress rehearsal, the lights suddenly went out, but the actors kept performing as if nothing had happened.","t":"彩排時燈光突然熄滅，但演員們繼續表演，好像什麼事都沒發生。"},{"w":"reinforce","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger","c":"加強；強化；加固","s":"Workers used steel bars to reinforce the old bridge so that it could carry heavy trucks safely for another thirty years.","t":"工人用鋼條加固這座舊橋，讓它能再安全地承載重型卡車三十年。","h":1},{"w":"reinforcement","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something stronger; extra soldiers or police","c":"強化；增援","s":"Positive reinforcement, such as praise and small rewards, helps young children learn good habits faster than punishment does.","t":"正向強化，例如稱讚和小獎勵，比處罰更能幫助幼童快速學會好習慣。"},{"w":"force","p":"n.","d":"physical power or strength","c":"力量；武力","s":"The force of the wind was so great that it pushed over several trees and broke the windows of the old church.","t":"風的力量大到推倒了幾棵樹，還打破了老教堂的窗戶。"},{"w":"forcefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a strong and determined way","c":"強而有力地","s":"The lawyer argued forcefully that her client was innocent, and after two hours the jury agreed with her completely.","t":"律師強而有力地主張她的客戶是無辜的，兩小時後陪審團完全同意她的看法。"},{"w":"enforce","p":"v.","d":"to make people obey a law or rule","c":"執行；強制實施","s":"The police will strictly enforce the new speed limit near schools, and drivers who break it will pay a heavy fine.","t":"警方將在學校附近嚴格執行新的速限，違規的駕駛將支付高額罰款。"},{"w":"reminder","p":"n.","d":"something that makes you remember","c":"提醒；提示","s":"My phone sends me a reminder every evening at nine to take my medicine, and I have not forgotten it since.","t":"我的手機每天晚上九點都會發提醒叫我吃藥，從那之後我就沒忘過了。","h":1},{"w":"remind","p":"v.","d":"to make someone remember something","c":"提醒","s":"Could you remind me to call my grandmother tonight? Her birthday is tomorrow, and I do not want to miss it.","t":"你可以提醒我今晚打電話給奶奶嗎？她明天生日，我不想錯過。"},{"w":"remind sb of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone think of a similar person or thing","c":"使某人想起","s":"This small fishing village reminds me of the town where I grew up, with its narrow streets and friendly old shopkeepers.","t":"這個小漁村讓我想起我長大的小鎮，有狹窄的街道和友善的老店主。","a":"reminds me of"},{"w":"a gentle reminder","p":"n.phr.","d":"a polite message that makes someone remember","c":"溫和的提醒","s":"This is just a gentle reminder that your library books are due on Friday, so please return them before the weekend.","t":"這只是溫和的提醒，您的圖書館書籍星期五到期，請在週末前歸還。"},{"w":"removal","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking something away","c":"移除；去除；拆除","s":"The removal of the old factory took almost a year, and now a beautiful park stands in its place beside the river.","t":"拆除舊工廠花了將近一年，現在河邊原址上有一座美麗的公園。","h":1},{"w":"remove","p":"v.","d":"to take something away or off","c":"移走；脫掉；去除","s":"Please remove your shoes before you enter the temple, and put them neatly on the wooden shelf by the door.","t":"進入寺廟前請脫下鞋子，並把它們整齊地放在門邊的木架上。"},{"w":"removable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be taken off or away","c":"可拆卸的；可移除的","s":"The jacket has a removable hood, so you can take it off on sunny days and put it back when it rains.","t":"這件夾克有可拆卸的帽子，所以晴天時可以拆下，下雨時再裝回去。"},{"w":"remover","p":"n.","d":"a liquid or product that takes something away","c":"去除劑","s":"She used nail polish remover to clean the pink color off her fingers before the job interview on Monday morning.","t":"她在星期一早上面試前，用指甲油去光水把手指上的粉紅色清掉。"},{"w":"render","p":"v.","d":"to cause someone or something to be in a particular state","c":"使成為；使變得","s":"The sudden loud noise was enough to render the whole class silent, and everyone looked toward the door.","t":"突然的巨響足以使全班變得安靜，大家都看向門口。","h":1},{"w":"render","p":"v.","d":"to give help or a service to someone","c":"提供（幫助、服務）","s":"The firefighters rendered first aid to the injured driver until the ambulance arrived about fifteen minutes later.","t":"消防員對受傷的駕駛提供急救，直到大約十五分鐘後救護車抵達。","a":"rendered"},{"w":"render sth useless","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make something no longer able to work or be used","c":"使…無用；使…報廢","s":"A single drop of water inside the phone was enough to render it useless, so now I keep it in a waterproof case.","t":"手機裡的一滴水就足以讓它報廢，所以現在我把它放在防水殼裡。","a":"render it useless"},{"w":"rendering","p":"n.","d":"a drawing or picture that shows what a building will look like","c":"效果圖；（建築）示意圖","s":"The architect showed us a computer rendering of the new library, with large windows and a garden on the roof.","t":"建築師給我們看了新圖書館的電腦效果圖，有大窗戶和屋頂花園。"},{"w":"rental","p":"n.","d":"the act of renting; something you rent; the money paid for renting","c":"租用；出租；租金","s":"Bike rental is cheap in this city, and you can pick up a bicycle at one station and leave it at another.","t":"這座城市的腳踏車租借很便宜，你可以在一站取車，在另一站還車。","h":1},{"w":"rental","p":"adj.","d":"available to rent","c":"租用的；出租的","s":"We stayed in a rental apartment near the beach for a week, which cost much less than a hotel room.","t":"我們在海邊附近的一間出租公寓住了一週，比旅館房間便宜很多。"},{"w":"rent","p":"v.","d":"to pay money to use something for a short time","c":"租；租用","s":"Many students rent rooms near the university because the dormitory does not have enough space for everyone.","t":"許多學生在大學附近租房間，因為宿舍沒有足夠空間給所有人。"},{"w":"rent","p":"n.","d":"the money you pay regularly to use a house or room","c":"租金","s":"The rent for this small apartment is twelve thousand dollars a month, and it does not include water or electricity.","t":"這間小公寓的租金每月一萬兩千元，而且不含水電。"},{"w":"car rental","p":"n.phr.","d":"a business that rents cars to people","c":"租車（服務）","s":"There is a car rental office right outside the airport, so we can drive to the hotel instead of waiting for the bus.","t":"機場外就有一間租車公司，所以我們可以開車去旅館而不用等公車。"},{"w":"repay","p":"v.","d":"to pay back money that you borrowed","c":"償還","s":"I promise to repay the money you lent me as soon as I receive my salary at the end of this month.","t":"我保證在這個月底收到薪水後，就馬上償還你借我的錢。","h":1},{"w":"repay","p":"v.","d":"to do something good for someone in return for their help","c":"回報；報答","s":"She helped me so much when I was sick that I do not know how I can ever repay her kindness.","t":"我生病時她幫了我很多，我不知道該如何報答她的好意。"},{"w":"repayment","p":"n.","d":"the act of paying back money; the money paid back","c":"償還；還款","s":"The monthly repayment on the car loan is eight thousand dollars, so my brother works extra hours on weekends.","t":"汽車貸款每月的還款是八千元，所以我哥哥週末加班工作。"},{"w":"pay back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to return money that you borrowed","c":"還錢；償還","s":"If you lend me five hundred dollars for the concert ticket, I will pay you back next Friday when I get paid.","t":"如果你借我五百元買演唱會門票，我下星期五領薪水時就還你錢。","a":"pay you back"},{"w":"republican","p":"n.","d":"a person who believes a country should be ruled by elected leaders, not a king","c":"共和主義者；共和黨人","s":"In the 1700s, many republicans in France believed that the country should be governed by elected leaders rather than a king.","t":"在十八世紀，法國許多共和主義者認為國家應由選出的領導人而非國王來治理。","a":"republicans","h":1},{"w":"republican","p":"adj.","d":"related to a republic or to republicans","c":"共和的；共和黨的","s":"The republican government replaced the old royal family and gave ordinary citizens the right to vote for the first time.","t":"共和政府取代了舊的王室，第一次給予普通公民投票權。"},{"w":"republic","p":"n.","d":"a country ruled by elected leaders and a president, not a king","c":"共和國","s":"Taiwan is a republic whose president is chosen by the people in an election that takes place every four years.","t":"台灣是一個共和國，總統由人民在每四年舉行一次的選舉中選出。"},{"w":"public","p":"adj.","d":"for everyone; open to all people","c":"公眾的；公共的","s":"The new public swimming pool is free for children under twelve, so it is always crowded on hot summer afternoons.","t":"新的公共游泳池對十二歲以下的兒童免費，所以炎熱的夏日午後總是很擠。"},{"w":"publicly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that everyone can see or know about","c":"公開地","s":"The mayor publicly thanked the volunteers who cleaned the beach, and their photo appeared in the newspaper the next morning.","t":"市長公開感謝清理海灘的志工，他們的照片隔天早上出現在報紙上。"},{"w":"resemblance","p":"n.","d":"the fact of looking like someone or something","c":"相似；相像","s":"There is a strong resemblance between the twins, and even their teachers sometimes call them by the wrong names.","t":"這對雙胞胎之間有很強的相似之處，連老師有時也會叫錯他們的名字。","h":1},{"w":"resemble","p":"v.","d":"to look like or be similar to someone or something","c":"像；類似","s":"My little cousin resembles her grandmother so much that old family photos look like pictures of her in costume.","t":"我的小表妹長得非常像她奶奶，以至於老家庭照片看起來就像她穿著古裝的照片。","a":"resembles"},{"w":"bear a resemblance to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look similar to someone or something","c":"與…相似；看起來像","s":"The new shopping mall bears a resemblance to a huge ship, which is why local people call it 'the boat' instead of its real name.","t":"新購物中心看起來像一艘巨大的船，這就是為什麼當地人叫它「大船」而不叫它的真名。","a":"bears a resemblance to"},{"w":"reservoir","p":"n.","d":"a large lake, often man-made, where water is stored","c":"水庫","s":"Because there has been no rain for three months, the reservoir is only thirty percent full, and the city may limit water use.","t":"因為三個月沒下雨，水庫只剩三成的水，市府可能會限制用水。","h":1},{"w":"reserve","p":"v.","d":"to arrange for a seat, room, or table to be kept for you","c":"預訂；保留","s":"You should reserve a table at that restaurant at least a week ahead because it is always full on weekends.","t":"你應該至少提前一週預訂那家餐廳的桌位，因為它週末總是滿座。"},{"w":"reserve","p":"n.","d":"a supply of something kept for later use","c":"儲備；儲藏量","s":"The country keeps a large reserve of rice in case a typhoon or drought damages the crops in the fields.","t":"這個國家保有大量的稻米儲備，以防颱風或乾旱損害田裡的作物。"},{"w":"reservation","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to have a seat, room, or table kept for you","c":"預訂","s":"I made a reservation for two at the hotel restaurant, but when we arrived they said they had no record of it.","t":"我在飯店餐廳預訂了兩個人的位子，但我們到達時他們說沒有紀錄。"},{"w":"reserved","p":"adj.","d":"kept for a particular person; shy and not showing feelings","c":"保留的；預留的；內斂的","s":"These front seats are reserved for the parents of the graduating students, so please sit somewhere further back.","t":"這些前排座位是保留給畢業生家長的，所以請坐到後面一點。"},{"w":"residence","p":"n.","d":"the place where someone lives, especially a large house","c":"住所；住宅","s":"The old stone building on the hill was once the residence of a rich merchant, but today it is a public museum.","t":"山丘上那棟古老的石造建築曾是一位富商的住宅，但今天是一座公立博物館。","h":1},{"w":"resident","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a particular place","c":"居民；住戶","s":"Every resident of the building received a letter about the elevator repair, which will take place next Tuesday morning.","t":"這棟大樓的每位住戶都收到一封關於電梯維修的信，維修將在下星期二早上進行。","h":1},{"w":"resident","p":"adj.","d":"living in a place","c":"居住的；常駐的","s":"The hotel has a resident doctor who stays on the top floor, so guests can get help quickly if they feel sick at night.","t":"這家飯店有一位常駐醫生住在頂樓，所以客人夜裡不舒服時能很快獲得協助。"},{"w":"reside","p":"v.","d":"to live in a particular place","c":"居住","s":"My grandparents reside in a small village in the mountains, and they have no plans to move to the city.","t":"我的祖父母居住在山區的一個小村莊，他們沒有搬到城市的計畫。"},{"w":"residential","p":"adj.","d":"related to homes rather than offices or factories","c":"住宅的","s":"Trucks are not allowed to drive through this quiet residential area after ten at night because the noise wakes people up.","t":"卡車在晚上十點後不准駛過這個安靜的住宅區，因為噪音會把人吵醒。"},{"w":"permanent resident","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person allowed to live in a country for as long as they want","c":"永久居民","s":"After living in Canada for five years, my uncle finally became a permanent resident and no longer needs to renew his visa.","t":"在加拿大住了五年後，我叔叔終於成為永久居民，不再需要更新簽證。"}]},{"unit":30,"theme":"residential – salon","cards":[{"w":"residential","p":"adj.","d":"related to homes; where people live","c":"住宅的","s":"Our school is in a quiet residential neighborhood, so there are no factories or noisy bars anywhere near the campus.","t":"我們學校位於一個安靜的住宅區，所以校園附近沒有工廠或吵鬧的酒吧。","h":1},{"w":"residential area","p":"n.phr.","d":"a part of a town where people live","c":"住宅區","s":"The city plans to build a new MRT line through the residential area so that people can get downtown without driving.","t":"市府計畫興建一條穿過住宅區的新捷運線，讓人們不必開車就能到市中心。"},{"w":"residence","p":"n.","d":"the place where someone lives, especially a large house","c":"住所；官邸","s":"The president's official residence is open to visitors on national holidays, and thousands of people line up to see the gardens.","t":"總統的官方官邸在國定假日開放參觀，數千人排隊想看花園。"},{"w":"resident","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a particular place","c":"居民；住戶","s":"Only residents of the building may park in the garage, so visitors have to leave their cars on the street outside.","t":"只有這棟大樓的住戶可以把車停在車庫，所以訪客必須把車停在外面的街上。","a":"residents"},{"w":"reside","p":"v.","d":"to live in a particular place","c":"居住","s":"Many foreign engineers reside in Hsinchu because the science park there offers thousands of well-paid technology jobs.","t":"許多外國工程師居住在新竹，因為那裡的科學園區提供數千個高薪的科技工作。"},{"w":"resort","p":"n.","d":"a place where people go for a holiday","c":"度假勝地；度假村","s":"Every summer my family spends a week at a beach resort in Kenting, where we swim, eat seafood, and watch the sunset.","t":"每年夏天我們全家都會在墾丁的一個海灘度假村待一週，在那裡游泳、吃海鮮、看日落。","h":1},{"w":"resort to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use something bad because nothing else works","c":"訴諸；採取（不好的手段）","s":"When the two boys could not agree on the rules, they resorted to shouting, and the teacher had to step in.","t":"當兩個男孩無法就規則達成共識時，他們訴諸大吼大叫，老師只好介入。","a":"resorted to"},{"w":"as a last resort","p":"phr.","d":"only when everything else has failed","c":"作為最後的手段","s":"The doctor said surgery should be used only as a last resort, after medicine and rest have failed to help the patient.","t":"醫生說手術只應該作為最後的手段，在藥物和休息都無法幫助病人之後才使用。"},{"w":"ski resort","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place in the mountains where people go to ski","c":"滑雪度假村","s":"My cousin works at a ski resort in Japan every winter, where he teaches beginners how to stop and turn safely.","t":"我表哥每年冬天都在日本的一個滑雪度假村工作，教初學者如何安全地停下來和轉彎。"},{"w":"respondent","p":"n.","d":"a person who answers questions in a survey","c":"受訪者；回答者","s":"More than half of the respondents in the survey said they sleep less than six hours a night during exam week.","t":"調查中超過一半的受訪者表示，考試週他們每晚睡不到六小時。","a":"respondents","h":1},{"w":"respond","p":"v.","d":"to answer; to react","c":"回應；回答","s":"I sent the company an email about my broken headphones last week, but they still have not responded.","t":"我上週寄了一封關於耳機壞掉的電子郵件給那家公司，但他們還沒有回覆。","a":"responded"},{"w":"response","p":"n.","d":"an answer or reaction","c":"回應；答覆","s":"The teacher asked a difficult question, and the only response from the class was a long and uncomfortable silence.","t":"老師問了一個困難的問題，全班唯一的回應是一陣漫長又不自在的沉默。"},{"w":"responsive","p":"adj.","d":"reacting quickly and positively","c":"反應快的；積極回應的","s":"The new customer service team is very responsive, and they usually answer every message within an hour.","t":"新的客服團隊反應非常迅速，他們通常在一小時內回覆每一則訊息。"},{"w":"in response to","p":"phr.","d":"as an answer or reaction to something","c":"為了回應…；作為對…的回應","s":"In response to the heavy rain, the school decided to cancel all outdoor activities and move the sports day to next month.","t":"為了回應大雨，學校決定取消所有戶外活動，把運動會延到下個月。","a":"In response to"},{"w":"resume","p":"v.","d":"to start again after a pause","c":"恢復；重新開始","s":"After the fire alarm turned out to be a mistake, the students returned to the hall and the exam resumed ten minutes later.","t":"火警警報證實是誤報之後，學生們回到大廳，考試在十分鐘後重新開始。","a":"resumed","h":1},{"w":"resume","p":"n.","d":"a short written record of your education and jobs","c":"履歷","s":"Before the interview, she updated her resume to include the summer job she had at the bookstore last year.","t":"面試前，她更新了履歷，加入去年暑假在書店打工的經歷。"},{"w":"resumption","p":"n.","d":"the act of starting again","c":"重新開始；恢復","s":"Farmers welcomed the resumption of train service to the village, since trucks had been unable to reach the market for a month.","t":"農民們歡迎通往村莊的火車服務恢復，因為卡車一個月來都無法抵達市場。"},{"w":"retail","p":"n.","d":"the selling of goods to the public in shops","c":"零售","s":"My aunt has worked in retail for twenty years, and she now manages three clothing stores in the city center.","t":"我阿姨在零售業工作了二十年，現在管理市中心的三家服飾店。","h":1},{"w":"retail","p":"adj.","d":"connected with selling goods to the public","c":"零售的","s":"The retail price of this phone is twenty thousand dollars, but the online store is selling it for two thousand less.","t":"這支手機的零售價是兩萬元，但網路商店賣的價格少兩千元。"},{"w":"retail","p":"v.","d":"to sell goods to the public","c":"零售","s":"The company makes its shoes in Taichung and retails them through its own stores in five Asian countries.","t":"這家公司在台中製造鞋子，並透過自己在五個亞洲國家的門市零售。","a":"retails"},{"w":"retailer","p":"n.","d":"a person or shop that sells goods to the public","c":"零售商","s":"The small retailer on the corner cannot sell rice as cheaply as the big supermarket, so it offers friendly service instead.","t":"轉角的小零售商無法像大超市那樣便宜地賣米，所以它改以親切的服務取勝。"},{"w":"revenue","p":"n.","d":"money that a company or government receives","c":"收入；營收；歲入","s":"The night market's revenue dropped sharply last year because the heavy rain kept tourists away for most of the summer.","t":"夜市去年的營收大幅下降，因為大雨讓遊客整個夏天幾乎都沒來。","h":1},{"w":"tax revenue","p":"n.phr.","d":"money a government gets from taxes","c":"稅收","s":"The government uses tax revenue to build roads and schools, so paying taxes on time is a duty for every citizen.","t":"政府用稅收興建道路和學校，所以準時繳稅是每位公民的義務。"},{"w":"generate revenue","p":"v.phr.","d":"to produce income","c":"創造收入","s":"The school hopes the new coffee shop will generate revenue to pay for more books and computers in the library.","t":"學校希望新的咖啡店能創造收入，用來為圖書館添購更多書籍和電腦。"},{"w":"reverse","p":"v.","d":"to change to the opposite; to go backwards","c":"逆轉；倒車；顛倒","s":"The driver tried to reverse the car into the narrow parking space, but he hit the wall on his first try.","t":"駕駛試著把車倒進狹窄的停車位，但第一次就撞到了牆。","h":1},{"w":"reverse","p":"n.","d":"the opposite","c":"相反；反面","s":"I expected the test to be easy, but the reverse was true, and most students did not finish it in time.","t":"我以為考試會很簡單，但相反才是事實，大多數學生沒能及時寫完。"},{"w":"reverse","p":"adj.","d":"opposite to the usual direction or order","c":"相反的；反向的","s":"Write the numbers in reverse order, starting with the largest and ending with the smallest, before you hand in the worksheet.","t":"交學習單之前，請把數字按相反的順序寫，從最大的開始，到最小的結束。"},{"w":"reversible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed back; able to be worn inside out","c":"可逆的；雙面可穿的","s":"This jacket is reversible, so you can wear the blue side on school days and the red side on weekends.","t":"這件夾克是雙面可穿的，所以上學日可以穿藍色那面，週末穿紅色那面。"},{"w":"reversal","p":"n.","d":"a change to the opposite","c":"逆轉；翻轉","s":"In a surprising reversal, the team that had lost every game this season beat the champions by ten points.","t":"在一場令人驚訝的逆轉中，這季每場都輸的球隊以十分之差打敗了冠軍隊。"},{"w":"rhetoric","p":"n.","d":"speech or writing meant to persuade, often without real meaning","c":"修辭；花言巧語","s":"Voters are tired of empty rhetoric; they want the candidates to explain exactly how they will lower the price of housing.","t":"選民厭倦了空洞的修辭；他們希望候選人確切說明將如何降低房價。","h":1},{"w":"rhetorical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with persuasive speech; asked only for effect","c":"修辭的；反問的","s":"When the coach shouted 'Do you want to win?', it was a rhetorical question, and nobody was expected to answer.","t":"當教練大喊「你們想贏嗎？」時，那是一個反問句，沒有人需要回答。"},{"w":"rhetorical question","p":"n.phr.","d":"a question asked for effect, not for an answer","c":"反問句；修辭性問句","s":"'Who doesn't love a holiday?' is a rhetorical question; the speaker already knows that everybody agrees with her.","t":"「誰不愛假期呢？」是一個反問句；說話者早就知道每個人都同意她。"},{"w":"rib","p":"n.","d":"one of the curved bones around your chest","c":"肋骨","s":"He fell off his bike and broke a rib, so the doctor told him not to play basketball for six weeks.","t":"他從腳踏車上摔下來，斷了一根肋骨，所以醫生要他六週內不要打籃球。","h":1},{"w":"ribs","p":"n.","d":"meat from the rib bones, often cooked on a grill","c":"肋排","s":"The restaurant's barbecue ribs are so popular that people line up outside the door an hour before it opens.","t":"這家餐廳的烤肋排非常受歡迎，人們在開門前一小時就在門外排隊。"},{"w":"rib cage","p":"n.phr.","d":"the ribs that protect your heart and lungs","c":"胸腔；肋骨架","s":"The rib cage protects the heart and lungs, which is why a hard hit to the chest can be so dangerous.","t":"胸腔保護心臟和肺，這就是為什麼胸口受到重擊會如此危險。"},{"w":"ridge","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow top of a mountain or hill","c":"山脊；山嶺","s":"After four hours of climbing, we finally reached the ridge and could see the ocean on both sides of the island.","t":"爬了四小時後，我們終於到達山脊，可以看到島嶼兩側的海洋。","h":1},{"w":"ridge","p":"n.","d":"a raised line on a surface","c":"隆起；凸起的線","s":"You can feel a small ridge on the back of the coin, which helps blind people tell it from other coins.","t":"你可以摸到硬幣背面有一道小小的凸起，這幫助盲人分辨它和其他硬幣。"},{"w":"mountain ridge","p":"n.phr.","d":"the long top edge of a mountain","c":"山脊","s":"The hikers walked along the narrow mountain ridge for two hours, with steep drops on both sides of the path.","t":"登山客沿著狹窄的山脊走了兩小時，小路兩側都是陡峭的落差。"},{"w":"ridiculous","p":"adj.","d":"very silly or unreasonable","c":"荒謬的；可笑的","s":"It is ridiculous to pay three hundred dollars for a cup of coffee just because a famous singer once drank at that café.","t":"只因為某位名歌手曾在那家咖啡店喝過咖啡，就花三百元買一杯咖啡是很荒謬的。","h":1},{"w":"ridiculously","p":"adv.","d":"in a very silly or unreasonable way; extremely","c":"荒謬地；離譜地","s":"The hotel near the stadium was ridiculously expensive during the concert weekend, so we stayed with my aunt instead.","t":"演唱會那個週末，體育場附近的旅館貴得離譜，所以我們改住阿姨家。"},{"w":"ridicule","p":"v.","d":"to laugh at someone in an unkind way","c":"嘲笑；奚落","s":"Nobody should ridicule a classmate for making mistakes in English, because everyone sounds strange when learning a new language.","t":"沒有人應該因為同學英文犯錯就嘲笑他，因為學新語言時每個人聽起來都很奇怪。"},{"w":"ridicule","p":"n.","d":"unkind laughter at someone","c":"嘲笑；奚落","s":"The young inventor faced ridicule at first, but ten years later his strange machine was in every kitchen in the country.","t":"這位年輕發明家起初遭到嘲笑，但十年後他奇怪的機器進入了全國每個廚房。"},{"w":"rifle","p":"n.","d":"a long gun that you hold against your shoulder","c":"步槍","s":"The hunter carried an old rifle that had belonged to his grandfather, but he used it only to scare wild pigs away.","t":"獵人帶著一把曾屬於他祖父的舊步槍，但他只用它來嚇走野豬。","h":1},{"w":"rifle through","p":"v.phr.","d":"to search quickly through something","c":"翻找；快速搜尋","s":"The thief rifled through the drawers looking for money, and he left the whole bedroom in a terrible mess.","t":"小偷翻遍抽屜找錢，把整個臥室弄得一團糟。","a":"rifled through"},{"w":"rifle range","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where people practice shooting","c":"靶場","s":"Soldiers spend many hours at the rifle range every month so that they can hit a target from two hundred meters away.","t":"士兵每個月在靶場花很多小時練習，以便能擊中兩百公尺外的目標。"},{"w":"rigid","p":"adj.","d":"strict and not easy to change","c":"死板的；嚴格的","s":"The old school had rigid rules about hair and uniforms, and students were punished for even a small mistake.","t":"這所老學校對頭髮和制服有死板的規定，學生即使犯一點小錯也會受罰。","h":1},{"w":"rigid","p":"adj.","d":"stiff and not easy to bend","c":"僵硬的；堅硬的","s":"The plastic becomes rigid when it cools, so you have to shape it quickly while it is still warm and soft.","t":"塑膠冷卻後會變得堅硬，所以你必須在它還溫熱柔軟時快速塑形。"},{"w":"rigidly","p":"adv.","d":"in a strict way that does not change","c":"死板地；嚴格地","s":"The manager followed the company rules so rigidly that he refused to let a sick worker leave five minutes early.","t":"經理死板地遵守公司規定，甚至拒絕讓生病的員工提早五分鐘下班。"},{"w":"rigidity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being stiff or strict","c":"僵硬；死板","s":"The rigidity of the school timetable means that students cannot choose any classes until their final year.","t":"學校課表的死板意味著學生直到最後一年才能選任何課。"},{"w":"rim","p":"n.","d":"the edge of something round, like a cup or wheel","c":"邊緣；輪圈；籃框","s":"The basketball hit the rim of the basket, rolled around twice, and finally dropped through the net at the last second.","t":"籃球打到籃框邊緣，繞了兩圈，最後在最後一秒掉進網裡。","h":1},{"w":"rim","p":"v.","d":"to form an edge around something","c":"環繞…的邊緣","s":"Tall palm trees rim the lake, so it is a lovely place to walk in the evening when the sun goes down.","t":"高大的棕櫚樹環繞著湖邊，所以傍晚太陽下山時這裡是散步的好地方。"},{"w":"the rim of","p":"n.phr.","d":"the edge of something round","c":"…的邊緣","s":"Dark chocolate was sprinkled around the rim of the cup, which made the hot drink look like a dessert.","t":"杯子的邊緣周圍撒了黑巧克力，讓這杯熱飲看起來像甜點。"},{"w":"riot","p":"n.","d":"a violent protest by a crowd of people","c":"暴動；騷亂","s":"The football match ended in a riot, and police had to use water cannons to clear angry fans from the streets.","t":"足球賽以一場暴動收場，警方必須用水砲驅散街上憤怒的球迷。","h":1},{"w":"riot","p":"v.","d":"to behave violently in a crowd","c":"暴動；鬧事","s":"Hungry people began to riot in the capital when the price of bread doubled for the third time that year.","t":"當麵包價格在那一年第三次翻倍時，飢餓的人們開始在首都暴動。"},{"w":"rioter","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a riot","c":"暴動者","s":"Several rioters were arrested after they broke shop windows and set fire to two cars outside the station.","t":"幾名暴動者在打破商店櫥窗並在車站外放火燒了兩輛車後被捕。","a":"rioters"},{"w":"run riot","p":"v.phr.","d":"to behave wildly without control","c":"失控；撒野","s":"When the teacher left the room for ten minutes, the children ran riot, throwing paper and jumping on the desks.","t":"老師離開教室十分鐘時，孩子們徹底失控，丟紙張、在桌上跳。","a":"ran riot"},{"w":"rip","p":"v.","d":"to tear something quickly and violently","c":"撕裂；撕開","s":"Be careful not to rip the pages when you turn them, because this old book is more than a hundred years old.","t":"翻頁時小心不要撕破書頁，因為這本舊書已有一百多年歷史。","h":1},{"w":"rip","p":"n.","d":"a long tear in cloth or paper","c":"裂口；破洞","s":"There is a long rip in the tent, so we got wet during the night when it started to rain.","t":"帳篷上有一道長長的裂口，所以夜裡開始下雨時我們都淋濕了。"},{"w":"rip off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cheat someone by charging too much","c":"敲竹槓；詐騙","s":"The taxi driver tried to rip off the tourists by driving around the city twice before taking them to their hotel.","t":"計程車司機試圖敲遊客竹槓，載他們繞城兩圈才送到旅館。"},{"w":"rip-off","p":"n.","d":"something that costs far too much","c":"敲竹槓的東西","s":"Paying five hundred dollars for a small bottle of water at the concert is a total rip-off, so bring your own.","t":"在演唱會花五百元買一小瓶水完全是敲竹槓，所以自己帶水吧。"},{"w":"rip up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tear something into pieces","c":"撕碎","s":"She was so angry about the low grade that she wanted to rip up the test paper and throw the pieces into the bin.","t":"她對低分氣得把考卷撕碎，然後把碎片丟進垃圾桶。"},{"w":"risky","p":"adj.","d":"involving the possibility of something bad happening","c":"有風險的；危險的","s":"Swimming in the river after heavy rain is risky, because the water moves much faster than it looks from the bank.","t":"大雨後在河裡游泳是有風險的，因為水流比從岸邊看起來快得多。","h":1},{"w":"risk","p":"n.","d":"the possibility that something bad will happen","c":"風險","s":"Wearing a helmet greatly reduces the risk of a serious head injury when you fall off your scooter.","t":"戴安全帽能大大降低從機車摔下時嚴重頭部受傷的風險。"},{"w":"risk","p":"v.","d":"to put something in danger","c":"冒…的危險","s":"The firefighter risked his life to save a little girl from the burning apartment on the sixth floor.","t":"消防員冒著生命危險從六樓著火的公寓裡救出一個小女孩。","a":"risked"},{"w":"at risk","p":"phr.","d":"in danger","c":"處於危險中；有…的風險","s":"Children who skip breakfast are at risk of feeling tired and losing concentration during their morning classes.","t":"不吃早餐的孩子有在早上課堂上感到疲倦、失去專注力的風險。"},{"w":"take a risk","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something even though it may go wrong","c":"冒險","s":"Sometimes you have to take a risk and try something new, or you will never find out what you are really good at.","t":"有時你必須冒個險嘗試新事物，否則你永遠不會知道自己真正擅長什麼。"},{"w":"ritual","p":"n.","d":"a set of actions always done the same way, often for religious reasons","c":"儀式；慣例","s":"Lighting incense and bowing three times is an important ritual that my grandmother performs at the temple every morning.","t":"點香並鞠躬三次是我奶奶每天早上在寺廟進行的重要儀式。","h":1},{"w":"ritual","p":"adj.","d":"done as part of a ceremony or fixed habit","c":"儀式的；例行的","s":"The ritual dance of the tribe tells the story of their ancestors, and every step has a special meaning.","t":"這個部落的儀式舞蹈講述他們祖先的故事，每一步都有特殊的意義。"},{"w":"rite","p":"n.","d":"a traditional ceremony","c":"儀式；典禮","s":"In many cultures, a wedding is the most important rite of a person's life, and the whole village comes to celebrate.","t":"在許多文化中，婚禮是一個人一生中最重要的儀式，全村的人都會來慶祝。"},{"w":"morning ritual","p":"n.phr.","d":"something you do the same way every morning","c":"早晨例行活動","s":"A cup of coffee and ten minutes of quiet reading is my morning ritual, and I feel lost on days when I skip it.","t":"一杯咖啡加十分鐘安靜閱讀是我的早晨例行活動，跳過它的日子我會覺得心神不寧。"},{"w":"rival","p":"n.","d":"a person or team you compete with","c":"競爭對手；對手","s":"Our school's biggest rival in basketball is the high school across the river, and the games between us are always exciting.","t":"我們學校籃球最大的對手是河對岸的那所高中，我們之間的比賽總是很精彩。","h":1},{"w":"rival","p":"adj.","d":"competing with each other","c":"競爭的；對立的","s":"The two rival companies both released a new phone on the same day, hoping to win more customers before the holidays.","t":"兩家競爭的公司在同一天推出新手機，希望在假期前贏得更多顧客。"},{"w":"rival","p":"v.","d":"to be as good as someone or something","c":"與…匹敵；比得上","s":"No restaurant in town can rival my grandmother's beef noodle soup, which she has been making for fifty years.","t":"鎮上沒有一家餐廳比得上我奶奶的牛肉麵，那是她做了五十年的料理。"},{"w":"rivalry","p":"n.","d":"competition between people or groups","c":"競爭；對抗","s":"The friendly rivalry between the two brothers pushed both of them to study harder and get into good universities.","t":"兩兄弟之間友善的競爭促使他們更用功讀書，考上好大學。"},{"w":"rod","p":"n.","d":"a long thin straight stick of metal or wood","c":"桿；棒","s":"The curtain rod fell down in the middle of the night and woke everyone in the house with a loud crash.","t":"窗簾桿在半夜掉了下來，巨大的聲響吵醒了屋裡的每個人。","h":1},{"w":"fishing rod","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long stick with a line used for catching fish","c":"釣竿","s":"My grandfather gave me his old fishing rod and promised to teach me how to catch fish in the river next summer.","t":"我爺爺把他的舊釣竿給我，並答應明年夏天教我在河裡釣魚。"},{"w":"lightning rod","p":"n.phr.","d":"a metal rod on a roof that protects a building from lightning","c":"避雷針","s":"Tall buildings have a lightning rod on the roof, which carries electricity from a storm safely down into the ground.","t":"高樓的屋頂上有避雷針，它把暴風雨的電安全地引入地下。"},{"w":"sacred","p":"adj.","d":"connected with religion; very important and deserving respect","c":"神聖的","s":"The mountain is sacred to the local tribe, so visitors are asked not to shout, litter, or climb the highest rock.","t":"這座山對當地部落來說是神聖的，所以遊客被要求不要喧嘩、亂丟垃圾或攀爬最高的岩石。","h":1},{"w":"sacred site","p":"n.phr.","d":"a holy place","c":"聖地","s":"Visitors must take off their shoes before entering the sacred site, and photographs are not allowed inside the main hall.","t":"遊客進入聖地前必須脫鞋，而且主殿內不允許拍照。"},{"w":"sacrifice","p":"n.","d":"something valuable you give up for a good reason","c":"犧牲","s":"My parents made many sacrifices so that I could study abroad, and I promise to make them proud.","t":"我父母為了讓我能出國讀書做了許多犧牲，我保證會讓他們引以為傲。","a":"sacrifices"},{"w":"sacrifice","p":"v.","d":"to give up something valuable for a good reason","c":"犧牲","s":"She sacrificed her weekends for a whole year to train for the marathon, and she finally finished it in under four hours.","t":"她整整一年犧牲週末來為馬拉松訓練，最後以不到四小時的時間完賽。","a":"sacrificed"},{"w":"saddle","p":"n.","d":"a seat for a rider on a horse or bicycle","c":"馬鞍；（腳踏車）座墊","s":"The saddle on my bicycle is too low, so my knees hurt after riding to school every day this week.","t":"我腳踏車的座墊太低，所以這週每天騎車上學後膝蓋都痛。","h":1},{"w":"saddle","p":"v.","d":"to put a saddle on a horse","c":"給（馬）裝鞍","s":"The farmer taught his daughter how to saddle the horse properly so that neither she nor the animal would get hurt.","t":"農夫教女兒如何正確地給馬裝鞍，這樣她和馬都不會受傷。"},{"w":"be saddled with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be given something unpleasant to deal with","c":"背負（負擔）","s":"After the business failed, my uncle was saddled with debts that took him almost ten years to pay off.","t":"生意失敗後，我叔叔背負著花了將近十年才還清的債務。","a":"was saddled with"},{"w":"in the saddle","p":"phr.","d":"riding a horse; in control","c":"在馬背上；掌權","s":"After three hours in the saddle, the young riders were tired and sore, but they were smiling from ear to ear.","t":"在馬背上三小時後，年輕的騎手們又累又痠，但他們笑得合不攏嘴。"},{"w":"saint","p":"n.","d":"a person honored by the church for being very holy","c":"聖人；聖徒","s":"The church is named after a saint who lived five hundred years ago and gave everything he had to the poor.","t":"這座教堂以五百年前一位聖人命名，他把所有財產都給了窮人。","h":1},{"w":"saint","p":"n.","d":"a very kind and patient person","c":"非常善良的人","s":"My neighbor is a real saint; she cooks meals for three elderly people on our street every single day.","t":"我的鄰居真是個大善人；她每天都為我們街上三位老人煮飯。"},{"w":"saintly","p":"adj.","d":"very good, kind, and patient","c":"聖潔的；聖人般的","s":"The nurse had a saintly patience with the difficult patient, never raising her voice no matter how rude he was.","t":"這位護士對那個難搞的病人有著聖人般的耐心，不管他多無禮都從不大聲說話。"},{"w":"patron saint","p":"n.phr.","d":"a saint believed to protect a place or group of people","c":"守護聖人","s":"Many fishermen in the village pray to their patron saint before they sail out to sea in the early morning.","t":"村裡許多漁民在清晨出海前會向他們的守護聖人祈禱。"},{"w":"salmon","p":"n.","d":"a large fish with pink flesh","c":"鮭魚","s":"Grilled salmon with lemon is my favorite dish at the Japanese restaurant, and it is also full of healthy oils.","t":"檸檬烤鮭魚是我在那家日本餐廳最愛的菜，而且它富含健康油脂。","h":1},{"w":"salmon","p":"adj.","d":"orange-pink in color","c":"橙粉色的","s":"She wore a salmon dress to the wedding, and the soft pink color looked beautiful next to the white flowers.","t":"她穿了一件橙粉色的洋裝去參加婚禮，柔和的粉色和白花相映成趣。"},{"w":"smoked salmon","p":"n.phr.","d":"salmon that has been preserved with smoke","c":"煙燻鮭魚","s":"For breakfast at the hotel, we had bread with smoked salmon and cream cheese, which I had never tried before.","t":"旅館早餐我們吃了配煙燻鮭魚和奶油乳酪的麵包，那是我以前從沒吃過的。"},{"w":"salon","p":"n.","d":"a shop where you get your hair or nails done","c":"美髮沙龍；美容院","s":"My mother goes to the same hair salon every month because the stylist there knows exactly how she likes her hair cut.","t":"我媽媽每個月都去同一家美髮沙龍，因為那裡的設計師很清楚她喜歡怎樣的髮型。","h":1},{"w":"beauty salon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop that does hair, nails, and skin care","c":"美容院","s":"Before the graduation party, the girls spent two hours at the beauty salon getting their hair and nails done.","t":"畢業派對前，女孩們在美容院花了兩小時做頭髮和指甲。"},{"w":"nail salon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop where people have their nails done","c":"美甲店","s":"A new nail salon opened next to the bakery, and it offers a discount to students who show their school ID.","t":"一家新的美甲店在麵包店旁邊開幕，出示學生證的學生可以享有折扣。"}]},{"unit":31,"theme":"sandal – setting","cards":[{"w":"sandal","p":"n.","d":"a light open shoe with straps, worn in warm weather","c":"涼鞋","s":"In summer most students wear sandals to the beach, but the school still requires proper shoes on campus.","t":"夏天大多數學生穿涼鞋去海灘，但學校在校園內仍要求穿正式的鞋子。","a":"sandals","h":1},{"w":"a pair of sandals","p":"n.phr.","d":"two sandals, one for each foot","c":"一雙涼鞋","s":"She bought a pair of sandals at the night market for two hundred dollars, and they broke after only three days.","t":"她在夜市花兩百元買了一雙涼鞋，才三天就壞了。"},{"w":"leather sandals","p":"n.phr.","d":"sandals made of animal skin","c":"皮涼鞋","s":"My grandfather has worn the same brown leather sandals every summer for ten years, and he says they are still comfortable.","t":"我爺爺十年來每個夏天都穿同一雙棕色皮涼鞋，他說它們仍然很舒服。"},{"w":"scan","p":"v.","d":"to read something with a machine; to copy a picture into a computer","c":"掃描","s":"Please scan the QR code on the poster with your phone to see the full schedule of the school festival.","t":"請用手機掃描海報上的 QR code，查看校慶的完整時程表。","h":1},{"w":"scan","p":"v.","d":"to look through something quickly to find information","c":"快速瀏覽","s":"I only had five minutes before the bus came, so I scanned the newspaper headlines instead of reading the articles.","t":"公車來之前我只有五分鐘，所以我快速瀏覽報紙標題，而不是閱讀文章。","a":"scanned"},{"w":"scan","p":"n.","d":"a medical test that takes pictures of the inside of your body","c":"掃描；掃描檢查","s":"The doctor ordered a brain scan after the accident to make sure that the boy had no serious injury inside his head.","t":"事故後醫生安排了腦部掃描，以確認男孩頭部內沒有嚴重的傷。"},{"w":"scanner","p":"n.","d":"a machine that copies pictures or text into a computer","c":"掃描器","s":"The library has a new scanner that can copy a whole page in two seconds and send it straight to your email.","t":"圖書館有一台新掃描器，兩秒鐘就能複製一整頁並直接寄到你的電子信箱。"},{"w":"scandal","p":"n.","d":"an action or event that shocks people because it is wrong","c":"醜聞","s":"The scandal about the mayor's secret bank account was on the front page of every newspaper for a week.","t":"關於市長秘密銀行帳戶的醜聞佔據了每家報紙頭版一整週。","h":1},{"w":"scandalous","p":"adj.","d":"shocking and wrong","c":"可恥的；令人震驚的","s":"It is scandalous that the company paid its workers so little while the boss bought himself a third sports car.","t":"公司付給員工這麼少的薪水，而老闆卻為自己買了第三輛跑車，這真是可恥。"},{"w":"cause a scandal","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something that shocks people","c":"引起醜聞","s":"The singer's rude comment about her fans caused a scandal, and thousands of people stopped buying her music.","t":"這位歌手對粉絲的粗魯評論引起了醜聞，數千人不再購買她的音樂。","a":"caused a scandal"},{"w":"scar","p":"n.","d":"a mark left on the skin after a cut has healed","c":"疤痕","s":"He has a small scar above his left eye from the time he fell off his bicycle when he was seven.","t":"他左眼上方有一道小疤痕，是七歲時從腳踏車上摔下來留下的。","h":1},{"w":"scar","p":"v.","d":"to leave a permanent mark on the skin or in the mind","c":"留下疤痕；留下創傷","s":"The deep cut on her hand healed slowly, and the doctor warned that it would probably scar for life.","t":"她手上的深傷口癒合得很慢，醫生警告那可能會留下一輩子的疤痕。"},{"w":"scarred","p":"adj.","d":"having scars","c":"有疤痕的；受創的","s":"The old fisherman's hands were scarred from forty years of pulling heavy ropes and handling sharp hooks.","t":"老漁夫的手因四十年拉重繩、處理尖鉤而滿是疤痕。"},{"w":"leave a scar","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause lasting damage to the body or the feelings","c":"留下疤痕；留下創傷","s":"Losing the final game by one point left a scar on the young team, and they talked about it for months.","t":"以一分之差輸掉決賽在這支年輕球隊心中留下了創傷，他們談論了好幾個月。","a":"left a scar"},{"w":"scenario","p":"n.","d":"a possible situation or series of events","c":"情境；設想的情況","s":"In the worst scenario, the typhoon will hit the island directly on Saturday, so the festival may have to be canceled.","t":"在最糟的情況下，颱風將在週六直接襲擊本島，所以慶典可能必須取消。","h":1},{"w":"worst-case scenario","p":"n.phr.","d":"the worst thing that could possibly happen","c":"最壞的情況","s":"Let's plan for the worst-case scenario: if the bus breaks down, we will call taxis so that nobody misses the exam.","t":"我們為最壞的情況做好計畫：如果公車拋錨，我們就叫計程車，這樣沒有人會錯過考試。"},{"w":"scene","p":"n.","d":"the place where something happens; a part of a play or film","c":"場景；現場","s":"The police arrived at the scene of the accident within five minutes and quickly closed the road to other cars.","t":"警方在五分鐘內抵達事故現場，並迅速封閉道路，不讓其他車輛通行。"},{"w":"scenery","p":"n.","d":"the natural things you can see in the countryside","c":"風景","s":"The train ride through the mountains offers beautiful scenery, with green valleys, waterfalls, and small farms along the way.","t":"穿越山區的火車之旅沿途有美麗的風景，有綠色的山谷、瀑布和小農場。"},{"w":"scent","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant smell","c":"香味；氣味","s":"The scent of fresh bread from the bakery downstairs wakes me up every morning before my alarm clock does.","t":"樓下麵包店新鮮麵包的香味每天早上在鬧鐘響之前就把我叫醒。","h":1},{"w":"scent","p":"n.","d":"the smell that an animal or person leaves behind","c":"氣味；嗅跡","s":"The police dog picked up the scent of the missing boy and led the officers straight to the old barn.","t":"警犬嗅到失蹤男孩的氣味，帶領警察直接找到了舊穀倉。"},{"w":"scent","p":"v.","d":"to smell or notice something","c":"嗅出；察覺","s":"The hungry bear scented the food in our tent and came into the campsite in the middle of the night.","t":"飢餓的熊嗅到我們帳篷裡的食物，半夜闖進了營地。","a":"scented"},{"w":"scented","p":"adj.","d":"having a pleasant smell added","c":"有香味的","s":"My aunt gave me a scented candle that smells like lavender, and I light it when I study at night.","t":"我阿姨送我一支薰衣草味的香氛蠟燭，我晚上讀書時會點它。"},{"w":"scheme","p":"n.","d":"an official plan or system; a secret plan","c":"計畫；方案；陰謀","s":"The city has started a new scheme that lets students ride the MRT for half price on weekends and holidays.","t":"市府推出一項新方案，讓學生在週末和假日搭捷運半價。","h":1},{"w":"scheme","p":"v.","d":"to make secret plans","c":"密謀；策劃","s":"The two brothers schemed for weeks to surprise their mother with a trip to Japan on her fiftieth birthday.","t":"兩兄弟密謀了好幾週，要在母親五十歲生日時用日本之旅給她驚喜。","a":"schemed"},{"w":"color scheme","p":"n.phr.","d":"the set of colors used in a room or design","c":"配色","s":"The designer chose a simple color scheme of white and light blue for the bedroom to make it feel calm and cool.","t":"設計師為臥室選擇了白色和淡藍色的簡單配色，讓它感覺平靜涼爽。"},{"w":"scope","p":"n.","d":"the range of things that something deals with","c":"範圍","s":"The question of how to reduce pollution is beyond the scope of today's lesson, so we will discuss it next week.","t":"如何減少污染的問題超出今天課程的範圍，所以我們下週再討論。","h":1},{"w":"scope","p":"n.","d":"the chance or room to do something","c":"空間；餘地","s":"There is plenty of scope for improvement in your writing, so try to use more linking words in your next essay.","t":"你的寫作還有很大的進步空間，所以下一篇作文試著多用一些連接詞。"},{"w":"beyond the scope of","p":"phr.","d":"outside the range of what something covers","c":"超出…的範圍","s":"Fixing the school's old computers is beyond the scope of the student club, so the principal has hired a professional company.","t":"修理學校的舊電腦超出學生社團的能力範圍，所以校長聘請了一家專業公司。"},{"w":"telescope","p":"n.","d":"an instrument for looking at things that are far away","c":"望遠鏡","s":"Through the telescope on the roof of the science building, we could clearly see the rings of Saturn last night.","t":"透過科學大樓屋頂上的望遠鏡，我們昨晚清楚地看到了土星環。"},{"w":"microscope","p":"n.","d":"an instrument that makes very small things look bigger","c":"顯微鏡","s":"Under the microscope, a single drop of pond water turned out to be full of tiny living creatures moving around.","t":"在顯微鏡下，一滴池塘水竟然充滿了四處移動的微小生物。"},{"w":"scramble","p":"v.","d":"to move or climb quickly, often with difficulty; to rush to get something","c":"爭搶；匆忙移動；攀爬","s":"When the fire alarm rang, the students scrambled for the exits, and some of them left their bags behind.","t":"火警警報響起時，學生們爭先恐後地衝向出口，有些人把書包都留下了。","a":"scrambled","h":1},{"w":"scramble","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which people rush to get something","c":"爭奪；搶購","s":"There was a scramble for tickets when the concert was announced, and the website crashed within ten minutes.","t":"演唱會一公布，門票就出現一陣搶購，網站在十分鐘內就當機了。"},{"w":"scrambled eggs","p":"n.phr.","d":"eggs mixed and cooked in a pan","c":"炒蛋","s":"My father makes scrambled eggs with cheese and tomatoes every Sunday morning, and it is the best breakfast of the week.","t":"我爸爸每個星期天早上都會做加起司和番茄的炒蛋，那是一週中最棒的早餐。"},{"w":"scramble up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to climb quickly using hands and feet","c":"爬上","s":"The children scrambled up the rocks at the beach to get a better view of the boats coming into the harbor.","t":"孩子們爬上海灘的岩石，想更清楚地看進港的船。","a":"scrambled up"},{"w":"scrap","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of something, especially paper","c":"碎片；小片","s":"She wrote her phone number on a scrap of paper, but I lost it before I could save it in my phone.","t":"她把電話號碼寫在一小片紙上，但我還沒存進手機就把它弄丟了。","h":1},{"w":"scrap","p":"v.","d":"to get rid of something or stop a plan","c":"廢棄；取消","s":"The government decided to scrap the plan for a new airport after thousands of people protested against the noise.","t":"在數千人抗議噪音之後，政府決定取消興建新機場的計畫。"},{"w":"scraps","p":"n.","d":"small pieces of food left after a meal","c":"剩菜；碎屑","s":"After dinner, my grandmother feeds the scraps to the chickens, so almost no food is ever wasted in her house.","t":"晚餐後，我奶奶把剩菜拿去餵雞，所以她家幾乎從不浪費食物。"},{"w":"scrap metal","p":"n.phr.","d":"old metal that can be used again","c":"廢金屬","s":"The old man collects scrap metal from the streets and sells it to a factory, earning a few hundred dollars a day.","t":"這位老人從街上收集廢金屬賣給工廠，一天賺幾百元。"},{"w":"scrapbook","p":"n.","d":"a book in which you keep pictures, tickets, and other memories","c":"剪貼簿","s":"My sister keeps a scrapbook of movie tickets, photos, and postcards from every trip she has taken since high school.","t":"我姐姐有一本剪貼簿，收集她從高中起每次旅行的電影票、照片和明信片。"},{"w":"script","p":"n.","d":"the written words of a play, film, or speech","c":"劇本；腳本","s":"The actors received the script two months before the play, so they had plenty of time to learn their lines.","t":"演員在演出前兩個月拿到劇本，所以他們有充分的時間背台詞。","h":1},{"w":"script","p":"v.","d":"to write the words for a play or film","c":"為…寫劇本","s":"The short film was scripted by a high school student, and it won first prize at the city's youth film festival.","t":"這部短片由一名高中生編寫劇本，在市青年影展獲得第一名。","a":"scripted"},{"w":"scriptwriter","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes the words for films or TV shows","c":"編劇","s":"The scriptwriter changed the ending of the movie three times because the director did not think it was sad enough.","t":"編劇把電影結局改了三次，因為導演認為它不夠悲傷。"},{"w":"manuscript","p":"n.","d":"a book or article written by hand or typed before it is printed","c":"手稿；原稿","s":"The writer sent her manuscript to ten publishers, and only one of them agreed to print the book.","t":"這位作家把手稿寄給十家出版社，只有一家同意出版這本書。"},{"w":"describe","p":"v.","d":"to say what someone or something is like","c":"描述","s":"Can you describe the man who took your bag? The police need to know his height, his clothes, and his hair color.","t":"你能描述拿走你包包的那個男人嗎？警方需要知道他的身高、衣著和髮色。"},{"w":"sector","p":"n.","d":"a part of a country's business or economy","c":"部門；領域；產業","s":"More and more young people want to work in the technology sector because the pay is high and the offices are modern.","t":"越來越多年輕人想在科技產業工作，因為薪水高、辦公室又現代化。","h":1},{"w":"public sector","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of the economy run by the government","c":"公部門","s":"My mother works in the public sector as a city planner, so her job is stable, but she will never become rich.","t":"我媽媽在公部門擔任都市規劃師，所以她的工作穩定，但永遠不會變得富有。"},{"w":"private sector","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of the economy run by companies, not the government","c":"私部門；民間企業","s":"After ten years as a teacher, he moved to the private sector and now trains new workers at a large bank.","t":"當了十年老師後，他轉到民間企業，現在在一家大銀行培訓新員工。"},{"w":"section","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts that something is divided into","c":"部分；區域；版面","s":"The sports section of the newspaper is always the first part my brother reads at breakfast every morning.","t":"報紙的體育版總是我哥哥每天早餐時最先讀的部分。"},{"w":"segment","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts that something is divided into","c":"部分；片段；區隔","s":"The TV news program has a short segment about weather at the end, which my grandfather never misses.","t":"這個電視新聞節目最後有一小段天氣報導，我爺爺從不錯過。","h":1},{"w":"segment","p":"v.","d":"to divide something into parts","c":"分割；區隔","s":"The company segments its customers by age so that it can send different advertisements to teenagers and to parents.","t":"這家公司按年齡區隔顧客，以便向青少年和家長發送不同的廣告。","a":"segments"},{"w":"orange segment","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of the natural pieces inside an orange","c":"橘瓣","s":"She peeled the fruit and gave each child an orange segment, and the juice ran down their chins as they ate.","t":"她剝開水果，給每個孩子一瓣橘子，他們吃的時候果汁流到了下巴。"},{"w":"seminar","p":"n.","d":"a meeting or class where a group discusses a subject","c":"研討會；專題討論課","s":"The university is holding a seminar on climate change next Friday, and high school students are welcome to attend for free.","t":"這所大學下週五舉行一場氣候變遷研討會，歡迎高中生免費參加。","h":1},{"w":"attend a seminar","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go to a meeting where a subject is discussed","c":"參加研討會","s":"Teachers from all over the island will attend a seminar on new ways to teach reading at the education center this weekend.","t":"來自全島的老師將在本週末於教育中心參加一場關於閱讀教學新方法的研討會。"},{"w":"seminar room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room used for small group classes or discussions","c":"研討室","s":"The seminar room on the third floor has a round table and a large screen, so it is perfect for group discussions.","t":"三樓的研討室有一張圓桌和一個大螢幕，非常適合小組討論。"},{"w":"senator","p":"n.","d":"a member of a senate, the upper house of a government","c":"參議員","s":"The senator visited our school to talk about how laws are made and answered questions from students for an hour.","t":"這位參議員來我們學校談論法律如何制定，並回答學生的提問一個小時。","h":1},{"w":"senate","p":"n.","d":"the upper house of a government that makes laws","c":"參議院","s":"In the United States, every state sends two members to the senate, no matter how large or small its population is.","t":"在美國，每個州都派兩名成員進入參議院，無論該州人口多寡。"},{"w":"senior","p":"adj.","d":"older or higher in position","c":"資深的；年長的；高年級的","s":"My father is a senior engineer at the company, so he leads a team of twelve younger workers on big projects.","t":"我爸爸是公司的資深工程師，所以他帶領一個十二人的年輕團隊做大型專案。"},{"w":"senior citizen","p":"n.phr.","d":"an old person, usually over sixty-five","c":"年長者；銀髮族","s":"The museum offers free entry to every senior citizen over sixty-five, and there are special guided tours on Tuesday mornings.","t":"博物館對六十五歲以上的每位年長者免費開放，週二早上還有特別導覽。"},{"w":"sensation","p":"n.","d":"a physical feeling","c":"感覺","s":"After sitting on the floor for an hour, I felt a strange tingling sensation in my legs when I tried to stand up.","t":"在地板上坐了一小時後，我試著站起來時感到雙腿有一種奇怪的刺麻感覺。","h":1},{"w":"sensation","p":"n.","d":"great excitement; a person or thing that causes it","c":"轟動；引起轟動的人事物","s":"The young singer became an overnight sensation after her video was watched fifty million times in just one week.","t":"這位年輕歌手的影片一週內被觀看五千萬次後，她一夜之間成為轟動人物。"},{"w":"sensational","p":"adj.","d":"causing great excitement; shocking","c":"轟動的；聳動的","s":"The newspaper printed a sensational story about a ghost in the school, but it turned out to be a student's joke.","t":"報紙刊登了一則關於學校鬧鬼的聳動報導，但結果是一個學生的惡作劇。"},{"w":"sense","p":"n.","d":"one of the natural powers of sight, hearing, smell, taste, and touch","c":"感官；感覺","s":"Dogs have a much stronger sense of smell than people, which is why they are used to find lost hikers.","t":"狗的嗅覺比人強得多，這就是為什麼牠們被用來尋找迷路的登山客。"},{"w":"cause a sensation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a lot of people excited or shocked","c":"引起轟動","s":"The new phone caused a sensation when it was first shown, and people lined up overnight to buy it.","t":"新手機首次亮相時引起轟動，人們徹夜排隊購買。","a":"caused a sensation"},{"w":"sensitivity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to notice small changes; the quality of being easily affected","c":"靈敏度；敏感","s":"The new camera's sensitivity to light is so high that it can take clear photos even in a dark room.","t":"新相機對光線的靈敏度非常高，即使在黑暗的房間也能拍出清晰的照片。","h":1},{"w":"sensitivity","p":"n.","d":"understanding of other people's feelings","c":"體貼；敏感度","s":"The nurse treated the frightened child with great sensitivity, speaking softly and explaining each step before she did it.","t":"護士以極大的體貼對待那個害怕的孩子，輕聲說話並在每個步驟前先解釋。"},{"w":"sensitive","p":"adj.","d":"easily hurt or affected; able to notice small changes","c":"敏感的；易受傷的","s":"My skin is very sensitive to the sun, so I always wear a hat and put on sunscreen before going outside.","t":"我的皮膚對陽光非常敏感，所以我出門前總是戴帽子並擦防曬乳。"},{"w":"insensitive","p":"adj.","d":"not caring about other people's feelings","c":"不體貼的；麻木的","s":"It was insensitive of him to joke about her weight, especially when he knew she had been trying so hard to get healthy.","t":"他拿她的體重開玩笑真是不體貼，尤其是他知道她一直很努力想變健康。"},{"w":"sensitive information","p":"n.phr.","d":"private information that must be kept secret","c":"敏感資訊","s":"Never share sensitive information such as your password or ID number with anyone who contacts you through a message online.","t":"絕不要把密碼或身分證字號等敏感資訊分享給任何透過網路訊息聯絡你的人。"},{"w":"sensor","p":"n.","d":"a device that notices heat, light, movement, or sound","c":"感應器","s":"The lights in the hallway have a motion sensor, so they turn on by themselves when someone walks past at night.","t":"走廊的燈有動作感應器，所以晚上有人經過時燈會自動亮起。","h":1},{"w":"temperature sensor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a device that measures how hot or cold something is","c":"溫度感應器","s":"A temperature sensor inside the baby's room sends a message to the parents' phones if the air gets too hot or too cold.","t":"嬰兒房裡的溫度感應器會在空氣太熱或太冷時傳訊息到父母的手機。"},{"w":"sensory","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the senses of sight, hearing, touch, smell, and taste","c":"感官的","s":"The new museum offers a sensory experience where visitors can touch, smell, and hear the rainforest, not just look at pictures.","t":"新博物館提供一種感官體驗，遊客可以觸摸、聞嗅、聆聽雨林，而不只是看圖片。"},{"w":"sentiment","p":"n.","d":"a feeling or opinion, especially one shared by many people","c":"情緒；看法；感想","s":"Public sentiment turned against the new tax after people learned that the money would be spent on a golf course.","t":"民眾得知這筆錢將用來蓋高爾夫球場後，公眾情緒轉而反對這項新稅。","h":1},{"w":"sentimental","p":"adj.","d":"connected with feelings and memories rather than money","c":"感傷的；有紀念意義的","s":"This old watch is not worth much money, but it has great sentimental value because it belonged to my grandfather.","t":"這支舊手錶不值多少錢，但它有很大的紀念價值，因為它曾屬於我爺爺。","h":1},{"w":"sentimental","p":"adj.","d":"easily moved by feelings of love, sadness, or memory","c":"多愁善感的","s":"My mother gets very sentimental whenever she looks at my baby photos, and she always ends up crying a little.","t":"我媽媽每次看我的嬰兒照片都會變得很多愁善感，最後總是會哭一下。"},{"w":"sentimentality","p":"n.","d":"too much emotion, especially sadness or love","c":"感傷；多愁善感","s":"The movie was full of sentimentality, with sad music and long goodbyes, but many people in the theater still cried.","t":"這部電影充滿了感傷情調，有悲傷的音樂和漫長的道別，但戲院裡仍有許多人哭了。"},{"w":"sequence","p":"n.","d":"the order in which things happen or are arranged","c":"順序；一連串","s":"Put the pictures in the correct sequence to show how a caterpillar slowly changes into a beautiful butterfly.","t":"把圖片按正確的順序排列，以顯示毛毛蟲如何慢慢變成美麗的蝴蝶。","h":1},{"w":"sequence","p":"v.","d":"to arrange things in order; to find the order of DNA","c":"按順序排列；定序","s":"Scientists can now sequence the DNA of a plant in a few days, which once took them several years of hard work.","t":"科學家現在幾天內就能定序一株植物的 DNA，這在過去需要好幾年的辛苦工作。"},{"w":"in sequence","p":"phr.","d":"one after another in the correct order","c":"依序地","s":"The steps must be done in sequence, because if you add the eggs before the butter, the cake will not rise.","t":"步驟必須依序進行，因為如果你在奶油之前加蛋，蛋糕就不會膨脹。"},{"w":"sequel","p":"n.","d":"a book or film that continues the story of an earlier one","c":"續集","s":"The sequel to the movie comes out next month, and fans are hoping it will be as exciting as the first one.","t":"這部電影的續集下個月上映，粉絲們希望它能像第一集一樣精彩。"},{"w":"consequence","p":"n.","d":"a result of an action, often a bad one","c":"後果","s":"Skipping class may seem fun now, but the consequence will be a low grade and a long talk with your parents.","t":"翹課現在看起來可能很好玩，但後果將是低分和一場與父母的長談。"},{"w":"series","p":"n.","d":"a number of similar things that happen one after another","c":"系列；一連串","s":"There has been a series of small earthquakes this week, and scientists are watching the area very carefully.","t":"這週發生了一連串小地震，科學家正密切觀察這個地區。","h":1},{"w":"series","p":"n.","d":"a set of TV programs with the same characters","c":"影集","s":"My favorite TV series has ten episodes in each season, and I always watch the final one with my friends.","t":"我最喜歡的電視影集每季有十集，最後一集我總是和朋友一起看。"},{"w":"a series of","p":"n.phr.","d":"several things of the same kind, one after another","c":"一系列的；一連串的","s":"The school is holding a series of talks on healthy eating, and a famous chef will give the first one on Monday.","t":"學校正在舉辦一系列健康飲食講座，一位名廚將在週一主講第一場。"},{"w":"serial","p":"adj.","d":"doing the same bad thing again and again; in parts","c":"連續的；連載的","s":"The police finally caught the serial thief who had broken into twelve houses in the same neighborhood this year.","t":"警方終於抓到今年在同一社區闖入十二戶人家的連續竊賊。"},{"w":"server","p":"n.","d":"a computer that stores information and sends it to other computers","c":"伺服器","s":"The school website went down this morning because the server could not handle so many students checking their grades at once.","t":"學校網站今天早上當機，因為伺服器無法處理這麼多學生同時查成績。","h":1},{"w":"server","p":"n.","d":"a person who brings food to your table in a restaurant","c":"服務生","s":"Our server at the restaurant was so friendly and quick that my father left her a much bigger tip than usual.","t":"餐廳裡的服務生親切又迅速，所以我爸爸給了她比平常多很多的小費。"},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give people food or drink; to work for","c":"服務；供應；服役","s":"This small restaurant serves the best dumplings in town, and the owner has been making them by hand for thirty years.","t":"這家小餐廳供應鎮上最好吃的水餃，老闆親手做了三十年。","a":"serves"},{"w":"service","p":"n.","d":"the help given to customers in a shop, hotel, or restaurant","c":"服務","s":"The hotel's room service was slow, and we waited almost an hour for two sandwiches and a pot of tea.","t":"飯店的客房服務很慢，我們等了將近一小時才拿到兩個三明治和一壺茶。"},{"w":"servant","p":"n.","d":"a person who works in someone else's house doing cooking and cleaning","c":"僕人","s":"In the old days, rich families had several servants to cook, clean, and take care of the children.","t":"以前有錢人家有好幾個僕人負責煮飯、打掃和照顧孩子。","a":"servants"},{"w":"session","p":"n.","d":"a period of time used for a particular activity","c":"一段時間（的活動）；一堂","s":"The coach added an extra training session on Saturday morning because the team has an important game next week.","t":"教練在週六早上加了一堂訓練課，因為球隊下週有一場重要比賽。","h":1},{"w":"session","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting of a court or government","c":"會議；開庭","s":"The city council will hold a special session tonight to discuss whether the old market should be torn down.","t":"市議會今晚將召開一場特別會議，討論舊市場是否應該拆除。"},{"w":"in session","p":"phr.","d":"meeting or working at the moment","c":"開會中；上課中","s":"Please do not enter the room while the meeting is in session; wait outside until the door opens.","t":"會議進行中請勿進入房間；請在外面等到門打開。"},{"w":"training session","p":"n.phr.","d":"a period of time spent learning or practicing something","c":"訓練課程","s":"Every new worker must complete a two-hour training session on fire safety before they are allowed to start their job.","t":"每位新員工在獲准開始工作前，必須完成兩小時的消防安全訓練課程。"},{"w":"setting","p":"n.","d":"the place and time where a story happens; the surroundings","c":"背景；環境","s":"The setting of the novel is a small fishing village in the 1950s, long before cars and televisions arrived there.","t":"這本小說的背景是一九五〇年代的一個小漁村，那時汽車和電視都還沒出現。","h":1},{"w":"setting","p":"n.","d":"a position on a machine that controls how it works","c":"設定","s":"If the screen is too bright at night, you can change the setting on your phone so that it turns darker automatically.","t":"如果晚上螢幕太亮，你可以更改手機上的設定，讓它自動變暗。"},{"w":"set, set, set","p":"v.","d":"to put something somewhere; to decide a time or price","c":"設定；放置；訂定","s":"Please set the alarm for six o'clock, because we have to leave the house before seven to catch the early train.","t":"請把鬧鐘設定在六點，因為我們必須在七點前出門趕早班火車。","a":"set"},{"w":"set up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to build or start something; to put something in position","c":"設立；搭起；安裝","s":"It took us two hours to set up the tent because the wind kept blowing it over before we could fix the ropes.","t":"我們花了兩小時才搭好帳篷，因為在固定繩子之前風一直把它吹倒。"},{"w":"set off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start a journey","c":"出發","s":"We plan to set off at five in the morning so that we can reach the top of the mountain before the sun gets too hot.","t":"我們計畫早上五點出發，以便在太陽太烈之前到達山頂。"},{"w":"setback","p":"n.","d":"a problem that delays or stops progress","c":"挫折","s":"Breaking her leg was a serious setback for the young runner, but she returned to the track six months later.","t":"腿骨折對這位年輕跑者是一個嚴重的挫折，但她六個月後重回跑道。"}]},{"unit":32,"theme":"shareholder – soak","cards":[{"w":"shareholder","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns part of a company","c":"股東","s":"At the yearly meeting, every shareholder can vote on who should run the company for the next twelve months.","t":"在年度會議上，每位股東都可以投票決定接下來十二個月由誰來經營公司。","h":1},{"w":"share","p":"n.","d":"one of the equal parts that a company is divided into","c":"股份","s":"My uncle bought two hundred shares in a chocolate company, and he receives a small payment from it every year.","t":"我叔叔買了一家巧克力公司的兩百股，每年都會從中拿到一筆小小的款項。","a":"shares"},{"w":"share","p":"v.","d":"to have or use something together with others","c":"分享；分擔","s":"In our family we always share the housework, so nobody has to wash all the dishes alone after dinner.","t":"在我們家，我們總是分擔家事，所以晚餐後沒有人需要獨自洗所有的碗盤。"},{"w":"holder","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns or has something","c":"持有人","s":"Only the ticket holder may enter the concert hall, so please do not lend your ticket to anyone else.","t":"只有票券持有人可以進入音樂廳，所以請不要把你的票借給別人。"},{"w":"shatter","p":"v.","d":"to break suddenly into many small pieces","c":"粉碎；砸碎","s":"The baseball flew through the window and made the glass shatter into a thousand tiny pieces on the floor.","t":"棒球飛過窗戶，讓玻璃粉碎成地上成千的小碎片。","h":1},{"w":"shattered","p":"adj.","d":"very upset; broken into pieces","c":"心碎的；破碎的","s":"She felt completely shattered when she heard that her best friend was moving to another country next month.","t":"當她聽到最好的朋友下個月要搬到另一個國家時，她覺得心都碎了。"},{"w":"shatter sb's dreams","p":"v.phr.","d":"to destroy someone's hopes completely","c":"粉碎某人的夢想","s":"The serious knee injury shattered her dreams of becoming a professional dancer, but she later found joy in teaching.","t":"嚴重的膝傷粉碎了她成為職業舞者的夢想，但她後來在教學中找到了快樂。","a":"shattered her dreams"},{"w":"shed, shed, shed","p":"v.","d":"to lose something naturally, such as leaves, hair, or tears","c":"脫落；流（淚）","s":"In autumn, many trees shed their leaves, so the streets in our neighborhood are covered with red and gold.","t":"秋天時，許多樹木會落葉，所以我們社區的街道上覆蓋著紅色與金色。","a":"shed","h":1},{"w":"shed","p":"n.","d":"a small simple building for storing things","c":"小屋；棚子","s":"My grandfather keeps his old tools and bicycle in a small wooden shed at the back of the garden.","t":"我爺爺把他的舊工具和腳踏車放在花園後面的一間小木棚裡。"},{"w":"shed tears","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cry","c":"流淚","s":"Even the strongest players shed tears when they lost the final game by only one point in the last minute.","t":"當他們在最後一分鐘以一分之差輸掉決賽時，連最堅強的球員也流下了眼淚。"},{"w":"shed light on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help people understand something","c":"闡明；解釋清楚","s":"The new photos from the camera on the street may shed light on what really happened on the night of the accident.","t":"街上攝影機拍到的新照片可能有助於釐清事故當晚究竟發生了什麼事。"},{"w":"sheer","p":"adj.","d":"complete; nothing but","c":"純粹的；完全的","s":"It was sheer luck that we found a parking space right in front of the restaurant on such a busy Saturday night.","t":"在這麼忙碌的星期六晚上，我們能在餐廳正前方找到停車位純粹是運氣。","h":1},{"w":"sheer","p":"adj.","d":"very steep, almost straight up or down","c":"陡峭的","s":"The climbers stood at the bottom of the sheer cliff and wondered how they could ever reach the top.","t":"攀岩者站在陡峭的懸崖底下，不知道該怎麼才能爬到頂端。"},{"w":"the sheer number of","p":"n.phr.","d":"the very large amount of something","c":"龐大的數量","s":"Teachers are worried about the sheer number of students who use their phones during class instead of listening.","t":"老師們很擔心上課時滑手機而不聽課的學生數量之多。"},{"w":"sheriff","p":"n.","d":"the chief police officer of a county in the US","c":"警長","s":"In the old western movie, the brave sheriff rides into town alone to stop the gang of bank robbers.","t":"在這部老西部片裡，勇敢的警長獨自騎馬進城，去阻止那群銀行搶匪。","h":1},{"w":"sheriff's office","p":"n.phr.","d":"the place where a sheriff and his officers work","c":"警長辦公室","s":"If you find a lost wallet in this small town, you can take it to the sheriff's office on Main Street.","t":"如果你在這個小鎮撿到遺失的皮夾，可以把它送到大街上的警長辦公室。"},{"w":"deputy sheriff","p":"n.phr.","d":"a police officer who helps the sheriff","c":"副警長","s":"A deputy sheriff is a police officer who helps the sheriff and takes charge when the sheriff is away.","t":"副警長是協助警長的警察，當警長不在時由他負責。"},{"w":"shield","p":"n.","d":"a large flat object that soldiers held to protect themselves","c":"盾","s":"The ancient soldier held a heavy metal shield in his left hand to protect himself from arrows and swords.","t":"古代士兵左手拿著沉重的金屬盾，保護自己不被弓箭和刀劍傷害。","h":1},{"w":"shield","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone or something from harm","c":"保護；遮蔽","s":"Parents naturally want to shield their children from bad news, but kids often understand more than adults think.","t":"父母自然想保護孩子不接觸壞消息，但孩子懂的往往比大人以為的多。"},{"w":"a shield against","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that protects you from harm","c":"抵擋…的保護","s":"Sunscreen acts as a shield against the harmful rays of the sun, so put some on before you go to the beach.","t":"防曬乳是抵擋太陽有害光線的保護，所以去海邊前要擦一些。"},{"w":"windshield","p":"n.","d":"the glass window at the front of a car","c":"擋風玻璃","s":"The driver turned on the wipers because heavy rain was running down the windshield and he could hardly see the road.","t":"司機開了雨刷，因為大雨不斷流過擋風玻璃，他幾乎看不到路。"},{"w":"shiver","p":"v.","d":"to shake because you are cold or afraid","c":"顫抖；發抖","s":"We waited for the bus in the cold wind for thirty minutes, and everyone began to shiver without a warm coat.","t":"我們在冷風中等了三十分鐘的公車，沒有穿暖外套的每個人都開始發抖。","h":1},{"w":"shiver","p":"n.","d":"a shaking movement of the body caused by cold or fear","c":"顫抖；寒顫","s":"A sudden shiver ran down my back when I heard a strange noise coming from the dark empty classroom.","t":"當我聽到黑暗空教室裡傳來奇怪的聲音時，一股突然的寒顫竄過我的背。"},{"w":"shiver with cold","p":"v.phr.","d":"to shake because you are very cold","c":"冷得發抖","s":"The little dog was shivering with cold in the rain, so we brought it inside and dried it with a towel.","t":"那隻小狗在雨中冷得發抖，所以我們把它帶進屋裡，用毛巾把它擦乾。","a":"shivering with cold"},{"w":"shortage","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which there is not enough of something","c":"短缺；不足","s":"Because of the long dry summer, there is a serious water shortage in the south, and farmers cannot water their fields.","t":"由於漫長乾燥的夏天，南部出現嚴重的水資源短缺，農民無法灌溉田地。","h":1},{"w":"be short of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not have enough of something","c":"缺少；不足","s":"We are short of chairs for the party, so could you borrow a few from the neighbors before the guests arrive?","t":"我們派對的椅子不夠，所以你能在客人到之前跟鄰居借幾張嗎？","a":"are short of"},{"w":"shorten","p":"v.","d":"to make something shorter","c":"縮短","s":"The teacher decided to shorten the test from sixty minutes to forty because the fire alarm had taken so much time.","t":"老師決定把考試從六十分鐘縮短到四十分鐘，因為火警警報佔用了太多時間。"},{"w":"shortly","p":"adv.","d":"soon; in a short time","c":"不久；很快","s":"The train will arrive shortly, so please stand behind the yellow line and get ready to board.","t":"火車很快就會進站，所以請站在黃線後面，準備上車。"},{"w":"shortcut","p":"n.","d":"a quicker way to get somewhere or do something","c":"捷徑","s":"If you take the shortcut through the park, you can get to school ten minutes faster than by the main road.","t":"如果你走穿過公園的捷徑，到學校會比走大馬路快十分鐘。"},{"w":"shove","p":"v.","d":"to push someone or something roughly","c":"推；猛推","s":"People started to shove each other to get on the crowded train, and a small boy almost fell onto the tracks.","t":"人們開始互相推擠要擠上擁擠的火車，一個小男孩差點跌到軌道上。","h":1},{"w":"shove","p":"n.","d":"a rough push","c":"猛推","s":"The angry man gave the door a hard shove, and it swung open and hit the wall with a loud bang.","t":"那個生氣的男人用力推了門一下，門猛地打開，砰的一聲撞到牆上。"},{"w":"push and shove","p":"v.phr.","d":"to push roughly in a crowd","c":"推擠","s":"Please do not push and shove in the line; everyone will get a ticket if we wait patiently for our turn.","t":"請不要在隊伍裡推擠；如果我們耐心等待輪到自己，每個人都會拿到票。"},{"w":"shrug","p":"v.","d":"to raise your shoulders to show you do not know or do not care","c":"聳肩","s":"When I asked my brother where my headphones were, he just shrugged and went back to his video game.","t":"當我問哥哥我的耳機在哪裡時，他只是聳聳肩，又回去玩他的電動了。","a":"shrugged","h":1},{"w":"shrug","p":"n.","d":"a movement of raising your shoulders","c":"聳肩","s":"She answered my question with a quick shrug of her shoulders, which told me she did not really care.","t":"她用快速地聳一下肩來回答我的問題，這告訴我她其實不在乎。"},{"w":"shrug off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to treat something as unimportant","c":"不理會；對…不以為意","s":"A good athlete learns to shrug off bad comments from the crowd and focus only on the game in front of him.","t":"好的運動員學會不理會觀眾的負面評論，只專注於眼前的比賽。"},{"w":"shuttle","p":"n.","d":"a bus, train, or plane that travels regularly between two places","c":"接駁車；穿梭班機","s":"A free shuttle runs between the airport and the hotel every twenty minutes, so you do not need to take a taxi.","t":"免費接駁車每二十分鐘在機場和飯店之間往返一趟，所以你不需要搭計程車。","h":1},{"w":"shuttle","p":"v.","d":"to travel back and forth between two places regularly","c":"穿梭往返","s":"Buses shuttle fans between the parking lot and the stadium all day long on game days.","t":"比賽日當天，公車整天在停車場和體育場之間往返接送球迷。"},{"w":"shuttle bus","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bus that goes back and forth between two places","c":"接駁公車","s":"Take the shuttle bus from the MRT station to the night market; it leaves every ten minutes and the ride is free.","t":"從捷運站搭接駁公車到夜市；每十分鐘一班，而且免費。"},{"w":"space shuttle","p":"n.phr.","d":"a spacecraft that can fly into space and return","c":"太空梭","s":"The space shuttle carried seven astronauts into space, and millions of people watched the launch on television.","t":"太空梭載著七名宇航員進入太空，數百萬人透過電視觀看了發射。"},{"w":"shuttlecock","p":"n.","d":"the small light object hit in badminton","c":"羽毛球","s":"In badminton, players hit a light shuttlecock over the net with their rackets, and it should not touch the ground.","t":"打羽毛球時，球員用球拍把輕盈的羽毛球打過網，而且它不能落地。"},{"w":"sibling","p":"n.","d":"a brother or sister","c":"兄弟姊妹","s":"As the oldest sibling in the family, Mary often has to take care of her two younger brothers after school.","t":"身為家中年紀最大的兄弟姊妹，瑪麗放學後常常得照顧兩個弟弟。","h":1},{"w":"sibling rivalry","p":"n.phr.","d":"competition between brothers and sisters","c":"兄弟姊妹間的競爭","s":"Sibling rivalry is common in many homes, so parents should try not to compare one child with another.","t":"兄弟姊妹間的競爭在許多家庭很常見，所以父母應盡量不要拿孩子互相比較。","a":"Sibling rivalry"},{"w":"only child","p":"n.phr.","d":"a child who has no brothers or sisters","c":"獨生子女","s":"Being an only child, he never had to share his toys, but he sometimes felt lonely on weekends.","t":"身為獨生子，他從不需要和別人分享玩具，但週末時他有時會覺得孤單。"},{"w":"siege","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which an army surrounds a place to make it give up","c":"圍城；包圍","s":"During the long siege, the people inside the city walls ran out of food and had to eat whatever they could find.","t":"在漫長的圍城期間，城牆內的人們食物吃完了，只能吃任何找得到的東西。","h":1},{"w":"lay siege to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to surround a place with an army to make it give up","c":"圍攻","s":"The enemy army decided to lay siege to the castle instead of attacking it, and waited for the people inside to give up.","t":"敵軍決定圍攻城堡而不是直接進攻，等待裡面的人投降。"},{"w":"under siege","p":"phr.","d":"surrounded by an army; attacked by many complaints","c":"被包圍；備受攻擊","s":"The school principal felt under siege after hundreds of angry parents wrote emails about the new lunch menu.","t":"在數百位憤怒的家長寫電子郵件抱怨新午餐菜單後，校長覺得自己備受攻擊。"},{"w":"skeleton","p":"n.","d":"all the bones of a person or animal","c":"骨骼；骨架","s":"In the science museum, children can touch a real dinosaur skeleton and compare its bones with their own.","t":"在科學博物館裡，孩子們可以觸摸真正的恐龍骨架，並把它的骨頭和自己的做比較。","h":1},{"w":"skeleton","p":"n.","d":"the basic frame or structure of something","c":"骨架；框架","s":"The skeleton of the new building is already finished, and the workers will add the walls and windows next month.","t":"新大樓的骨架已經完成，工人下個月會加上牆壁和窗戶。"},{"w":"skeleton key","p":"n.phr.","d":"a key that can open many different locks","c":"萬能鑰匙","s":"The hotel manager used a skeleton key to open the room after the guest locked herself out and lost her card.","t":"客人把自己鎖在門外又弄丟房卡後，飯店經理用萬能鑰匙打開了房間。"},{"w":"skeletal","p":"adj.","d":"very thin, so that the bones can be seen","c":"骨瘦如柴的","s":"After weeks without enough food, the lost hikers looked skeletal, and the rescue team gave them hot soup at once.","t":"好幾個星期沒有足夠食物後，迷路的登山客看起來骨瘦如柴，救難隊立刻給他們熱湯。"},{"w":"skull","p":"n.","d":"the bones of the head","c":"頭骨；頭顱","s":"Always wear a helmet when you ride a motorcycle, because it protects your skull and brain in an accident.","t":"騎機車時一定要戴安全帽，因為在事故中它能保護你的頭骨和大腦。","h":1},{"w":"skull and crossbones","p":"n.phr.","d":"a picture of a skull with two crossed bones, a sign of danger or pirates","c":"骷髅標誌（危險／海盜標誌）","s":"The bottle in the lab had a skull and crossbones on the label, which means the liquid inside is poisonous.","t":"實驗室裡的那個瓶子標籤上有骷髅標誌，表示裡面的液體有毒。"},{"w":"fracture one's skull","p":"v.phr.","d":"to break the bones of the head","c":"頭骨骨折","s":"The cyclist fractured his skull when he hit the ground without a helmet, and he stayed in the hospital for a month.","t":"那位自行車騎士沒戴安全帽摔到地上時頭骨骨折，在醫院住了一個月。","a":"fractured his skull"},{"w":"slam","p":"v.","d":"to shut something with great force and a loud noise","c":"砰地關上；猛摔","s":"Please do not slam the door when you leave the room; your grandmother is sleeping and the noise will wake her.","t":"離開房間時請不要用力甩門；你奶奶在睡覺，噪音會吵醒她。","h":1},{"w":"slam","p":"n.","d":"the loud noise of something closing with force","c":"砰的一聲","s":"We heard the slam of a car door outside, and a moment later someone rang the doorbell twice.","t":"我們聽到外面車門砰的一聲，過了一會兒有人按了兩次門鈴。"},{"w":"slam on the brakes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop a vehicle very suddenly","c":"緊急煞車","s":"The driver had to slam on the brakes when a cat suddenly ran across the road in front of his car.","t":"當一隻貓突然跑過他車前的馬路時，司機不得不緊急煞車。"},{"w":"grand slam","p":"n.phr.","d":"winning all the major competitions in a sport; a top tennis event","c":"大滿貫","s":"The young tennis player won her first grand slam title in Paris, and the whole country celebrated with her.","t":"這位年輕網球選手在巴黎贏得她的第一個大滿貫冠軍，全國都和她一起慶祝。"},{"w":"slap","p":"v.","d":"to hit someone or something with the flat part of your hand","c":"拍；打（巴掌）","s":"If a mosquito lands on your arm, you can slap it quickly before it has a chance to bite you.","t":"如果蚊子停在你手臂上，你可以在它有機會咬你之前趕快拍死它。","h":1},{"w":"slap","p":"n.","d":"a hit with the flat part of the hand","c":"巴掌","s":"The actor's face turned red after the slap in the movie scene, because the actress had hit him for real.","t":"電影那一幕的巴掌之後，男演員的臉紅了，因為女演員真的打了他。"},{"w":"a slap in the face","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that insults or disappoints you badly","c":"侮辱；當頭一棒","s":"Losing the job to a much younger worker felt like a slap in the face to the man who had worked there for twenty years.","t":"工作輸給一個年輕許多的員工，對這位在那裡工作了二十年的男人來說像是一記當頭棒喝。"},{"w":"slavery","p":"n.","d":"the system of owning people and forcing them to work","c":"奴隸制度","s":"Slavery was finally made illegal in the United States in 1865, after a long and terrible war between the North and the South.","t":"在南北之間一場漫長而可怕的戰爭之後，奴隸制度終於在一八六五年於美國被定為非法。","a":"Slavery","h":1},{"w":"slave","p":"n.","d":"a person who is owned by another person and must work for them","c":"奴隸","s":"In ancient Rome, a slave had no rights and had to work for his owner without any pay for his whole life.","t":"在古羅馬，奴隸沒有任何權利，必須一輩子無償為主人工作。"},{"w":"slave away","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work very hard for a long time","c":"拼命工作","s":"My mother slaved away in the kitchen all afternoon to prepare a big dinner for twelve guests.","t":"我媽媽整個下午在廚房拼命忙，為十二位客人準備豐盛的晚餐。","a":"slaved away"},{"w":"become a slave to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be controlled by something you cannot stop using","c":"成為…的奴隸；受制於","s":"It is easy to become a slave to your phone and check it every few minutes, even during meals with your family.","t":"人很容易成為手機的奴隸，每隔幾分鐘就看一下，甚至在和家人吃飯時也是。"},{"w":"slot","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow hole that you put something into","c":"投幣口；狹槽","s":"Put a ten-dollar coin into the slot and press the green button, and the machine will give you a cold drink.","t":"把十元硬幣投進投幣口，按下綠色按鈕，機器就會給你一杯冷飲。","h":1},{"w":"slot","p":"n.","d":"a time when something is planned to happen","c":"時段","s":"The dentist has a free slot at three o'clock on Thursday, so I booked it before anyone else could take it.","t":"牙醫星期四三點有一個空的時段，所以我在別人預約之前先訂了。"},{"w":"slot","p":"v.","d":"to put something into a narrow space","c":"放入；插入","s":"You just slot the memory card into the side of the camera, and it will start saving your photos right away.","t":"你只要把記憶卡插入相機側邊，它就會立刻開始儲存你的照片。"},{"w":"slot machine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a gambling machine that you put coins into","c":"吃角子老虎機","s":"My uncle lost all his holiday money on a slot machine in Las Vegas and had to borrow some from my aunt.","t":"我叔叔在拉斯維加斯的吃角子老虎機上輸光了所有度假的錢，只好向我阿姨借錢。"},{"w":"time slot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a particular time when a program or activity happens","c":"時段","s":"The popular cartoon moved to a later time slot on Sunday evenings, so many young children can no longer watch it.","t":"這部受歡迎的卡通改到星期天晚上較晚的時段播出，所以許多小孩子再也不能看了。"},{"w":"smash","p":"v.","d":"to break something into pieces with great force","c":"打碎；砸碎","s":"The thief used a stone to smash the car window and stole the laptop that was lying on the back seat.","t":"小偷用石頭砸碎車窗，偷走了放在後座的筆記型電腦。","h":1},{"w":"smash","p":"n.","d":"a hard downward hit of the ball in tennis or badminton","c":"扣殺","s":"In the final point, she jumped and hit a powerful smash that her opponent had no chance to return.","t":"在最後一分，她跳起來打出一記強力扣殺，對手根本沒有機會回擊。"},{"w":"smash hit","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very successful movie, song, or show","c":"轟動一時的作品","s":"The new animated movie became a smash hit and earned more money in one weekend than any other film this year.","t":"這部新動畫電影成為轟動之作，一個週末賺的錢比今年任何其他電影都多。"},{"w":"smash into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to crash into something with great force","c":"猛烈撞上","s":"The truck lost control on the icy road and smashed into a wall, but luckily the driver was not badly hurt.","t":"卡車在結冰的路上失控，猛烈撞上一道牆，但幸運的是司機沒有受重傷。","a":"smashed into"},{"w":"smog","p":"n.","d":"dirty air made of smoke and fog that hangs over a city","c":"煙霧；霧霾","s":"On days with heavy smog, the city tells people to stay indoors and wear masks if they must go outside.","t":"在霧霾嚴重的日子，市政府要大家待在室內，如果一定要外出就要戴口罩。","h":1},{"w":"smoggy","p":"adj.","d":"full of smog","c":"煙霧瀰漫的；霧霾的","s":"It was so smoggy this morning that we could not see the tall buildings on the other side of the river.","t":"今天早上霧霾太嚴重，我們看不到河對岸的高樓。"},{"w":"smoke","p":"n.","d":"the gray or black gas from something burning","c":"煙","s":"Thick black smoke rose from the burning factory, and people living nearby were told to close their windows.","t":"濃濃的黑煙從燃燒的工廠升起，附近的居民被要求關上窗戶。"},{"w":"fog","p":"n.","d":"thick cloud near the ground that makes it hard to see","c":"霧","s":"The airport closed for three hours this morning because the fog was too thick for the planes to land safely.","t":"今天早上機場關閉了三個小時，因為霧太濃，飛機無法安全降落。"},{"w":"snatch","p":"v.","d":"to take something quickly and roughly","c":"搶奪；奪取","s":"A man on a motorcycle tried to snatch the woman's handbag as she walked along the dark street last night.","t":"昨晚一名騎機車的男子在那位女士走在黑暗的街上時，試圖搶走她的手提包。","h":1},{"w":"snatch","p":"n.","d":"a short part of something you hear or see","c":"片段","s":"I only heard a snatch of their conversation, but it sounded like they were planning a surprise party for Tom.","t":"我只聽到他們談話的一個片段，但聽起來他們好像在為湯姆籌劃驚喜派對。"},{"w":"snatch up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to buy or take something quickly before others can","c":"搶購；迅速抓起","s":"Fans snatched up all the concert tickets within ten minutes, and many people were left disappointed.","t":"粉絲們在十分鐘內搶購了所有演唱會門票，許多人因此失望而歸。","a":"snatched up"},{"w":"bag snatcher","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thief who grabs bags from people in the street","c":"搶包賊","s":"Police caught the bag snatcher after a shop camera recorded his face and the number of his motorcycle.","t":"商店的攝影機錄下他的臉和機車車號之後，警方逮到了那名搶包賊。"},{"w":"sneak","p":"v.","d":"to go somewhere quietly so that nobody sees you","c":"偷偷地走；潛行","s":"The teenagers tried to sneak into the movie theater without paying, but the manager caught them at the back door.","t":"那些青少年試圖不付錢偷偷溜進電影院，但經理在後門抓到了他們。","h":1},{"w":"sneak out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave a place quietly without being noticed","c":"偷偷溜出去","s":"My little sister tried to sneak out of the house to meet her friends, but Dad was sitting right by the front door.","t":"我妹妹想偷偷溜出家門去見朋友，但爸爸就坐在前門旁邊。"},{"w":"sneaky","p":"adj.","d":"doing things secretly and unfairly","c":"狡猾的；偷偷摸摸的","s":"That was a sneaky trick, hiding the last cookie behind the milk so that nobody else in the family could find it.","t":"把最後一片餅乾藏在牛奶後面讓家裡其他人找不到，真是個狡猾的把戲。"},{"w":"sneakers","p":"n.","d":"soft sports shoes","c":"運動鞋","s":"You should wear sneakers instead of sandals for the hike, because the path is rocky and your feet need protection.","t":"去健行你應該穿運動鞋而不是涼鞋，因為路上石頭很多，你的腳需要保護。"},{"w":"sneak peek","p":"n.phr.","d":"a quick look at something before it is shown to everyone","c":"先睹為快；搶先看","s":"The company gave reporters a sneak peek at its new phone a week before anyone else could see it.","t":"公司讓記者在其他人看到前一週就搶先看了它的新手機。"},{"w":"sniff","p":"v.","d":"to breathe in through your nose to smell something","c":"聞；嗅","s":"The dog began to sniff the ground near the door, and a minute later it found the hidden bag of dog food.","t":"狗開始嗅門邊的地面，一分鐘後它找到了藏起來的那袋狗食。","h":1},{"w":"sniff","p":"n.","d":"the act of smelling something quickly","c":"聞一下","s":"She took a quick sniff of the milk and decided it had gone bad, so she poured it down the sink.","t":"她快速聞了一下牛奶，判定它已經壞了，所以把它倒進水槽。"},{"w":"sniff out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to find something by smelling; to discover something hidden","c":"嗅出；查出","s":"Police dogs are trained to sniff out drugs hidden in suitcases at the airport, and they rarely make mistakes.","t":"警犬受過訓練，能在機場嗅出藏在行李箱裡的毒品，而且很少出錯。"},{"w":"sniffle","p":"v.","d":"to breathe in noisily through your nose, usually because of a cold","c":"抽鼻涕；吸鼻子","s":"He had a bad cold and kept sniffling through the whole movie, which annoyed the people sitting next to him.","t":"他得了重感冒，整部電影一直在吸鼻子，惹得坐在旁邊的人很煩。","a":"sniffling"},{"w":"soak","p":"v.","d":"to leave something in liquid for a long time","c":"浸泡","s":"Before you cook the beans, soak them in water overnight so that they become soft and cook much faster.","t":"煮豆子之前，先把它們浸泡在水裡一整夜，這樣它們會變軟，煮得快很多。","h":1},{"w":"soak","p":"n.","d":"a long time spent lying in a bath","c":"泡澡；浸泡","s":"After the long hike, a hot soak in the bath was exactly what my tired legs needed.","t":"長途健行之後，在浴缸裡熱熱地泡個澡正是我疲累的雙腿所需要的。"},{"w":"soaking wet","p":"adj.phr.","d":"completely wet","c":"濕透的","s":"We forgot our umbrellas and got soaking wet on the way home, so we had to change all our clothes.","t":"我們忘了帶傘，回家路上全身濕透，所以得把所有衣服都換掉。"},{"w":"soak up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take in liquid, heat, or an experience fully","c":"吸收；盡情享受","s":"On the first day of vacation, we lay on the beach and soaked up the sunshine for hours.","t":"假期的第一天，我們躺在海灘上盡情享受了好幾個小時的陽光。","a":"soaked up"}]},{"unit":33,"theme":"soar – spine","cards":[{"w":"soar","p":"v.","d":"to rise very quickly to a high level","c":"飆升；猛漲","s":"Because of the war in the Middle East, oil prices began to soar, and a tank of gas now costs twice as much as last year.","t":"由於中東的戰爭，油價開始飆升，現在加滿一箱油的價格是去年的兩倍。","h":1},{"w":"soar","p":"v.","d":"to fly high in the sky","c":"翱翔；高飛","s":"We watched the eagle soar high above the valley without moving its wings, carried only by the warm wind.","t":"我們看著老鷹不動翅膀，只靠暖風的托舉，在山谷上空高高翱翔。"},{"w":"soaring","p":"adj.","d":"rising very fast; very high","c":"飛漲的；高聳的","s":"Soaring house prices mean that many young couples in Taipei cannot afford to buy even a small apartment.","t":"飛漲的房價意味著台北許多年輕夫妻連一間小公寓都買不起。","a":"Soaring"},{"w":"sob","p":"v.","d":"to cry noisily, taking short quick breaths","c":"啜泣；嗚咽","s":"The little girl began to sob when she realized that she had lost her favorite teddy bear at the park.","t":"小女孩發現自己把最愛的泰迪熊弄丟在公園時，開始啜泣起來。","h":1},{"w":"sob","p":"n.","d":"the sound of crying with short quick breaths","c":"啜泣聲","s":"Through the thin wall, I could hear a quiet sob from the next room, so I knocked to ask if she was all right.","t":"隔著薄薄的牆，我聽到隔壁房間傳來輕輕的啜泣聲，所以我敲門問她是否還好。"},{"w":"sob story","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sad story told to make people feel sorry for you","c":"博取同情的故事","s":"The man told the police a long sob story about his sick mother, but they soon found out that none of it was true.","t":"那名男子向警方講了一個關於他生病母親的冗長博取同情的故事，但警方很快就發現全是假的。"},{"w":"sober","p":"adj.","d":"not drunk","c":"清醒的；未喝醉的","s":"If you plan to drink at the party tonight, make sure one friend stays sober so that he can drive everyone home safely.","t":"如果你今晚打算在派對上喝酒，一定要有一位朋友保持清醒，好讓他能安全載大家回家。","h":1},{"w":"sober","p":"adj.","d":"serious and calm","c":"嚴肅的；冷靜的","s":"After the accident, the whole class was in a sober mood, and nobody felt like joking or playing games.","t":"事故之後，全班都處於嚴肅的氣氛中，沒有人想開玩笑或玩遊戲。"},{"w":"sober up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become no longer drunk","c":"清醒過來；醒酒","s":"He drank three cups of strong black coffee to sober up before his parents came home from their trip.","t":"他在父母旅行回家之前喝了三杯濃黑咖啡來醒酒。"},{"w":"soften","p":"v.","d":"to become or make something soft","c":"軟化；變軟","s":"Leave the butter on the table for twenty minutes to soften before you mix it with the sugar and eggs.","t":"把奶油放在桌上二十分鐘讓它變軟，然後再把它和糖、蛋混合。","h":1},{"w":"soften","p":"v.","d":"to make something less strong or less unpleasant","c":"緩和；使溫和","s":"The teacher tried to soften the bad news by telling the students they could take the test again next week.","t":"老師告訴學生下週可以再考一次，試圖緩和這個壞消息。"},{"w":"soft","p":"adj.","d":"not hard; pleasant to touch","c":"柔軟的","s":"The kitten's fur is so soft and warm that everyone who visits wants to hold it for a few minutes.","t":"小貓的毛那麼柔軟又溫暖，每個來訪的人都想抱牠幾分鐘。"},{"w":"softly","p":"adv.","d":"in a quiet or gentle way","c":"輕柔地；輕聲地","s":"The mother sang softly to her baby until his eyes closed and he fell asleep in her arms.","t":"媽媽輕柔地對寶寶唱歌，直到他閉上眼睛，在她懷裡睡著。"},{"w":"sole","p":"adj.","d":"only; single","c":"唯一的","s":"She was the sole student in our class who got full marks on the math test, so the teacher gave her a prize.","t":"她是我們班上唯一一位數學考滿分的學生，所以老師給了她一個獎品。","h":1},{"w":"sole","p":"n.","d":"the bottom part of your foot or of a shoe","c":"腳底；鞋底","s":"After walking around the city all day, the sole of my shoe came off, and I had to buy a new pair.","t":"在城裡走了一整天後，我的鞋底掉了，我只好買一雙新鞋。"},{"w":"solely","p":"adv.","d":"only; not involving anyone or anything else","c":"僅僅；單獨地","s":"The success of the team was not solely the coach's work; every player trained hard for months before the games.","t":"球隊的成功不僅僅是教練的功勞；每位球員在比賽前都苦練了好幾個月。"},{"w":"solo","p":"n.","d":"a piece of music played or sung by one person","c":"獨奏；獨唱","s":"In the middle of the concert, the guitar player stood up and played a five-minute solo that made the crowd cheer.","t":"演唱會中途，吉他手站起來演奏了一段五分鐘的獨奏，讓觀眾歡呼起來。","h":1},{"w":"solo","p":"adj.","d":"done by one person alone","c":"單獨的；個人的","s":"After years in a famous band, the singer finally released her first solo album, and it sold a million copies.","t":"在知名樂團待了多年後，這位歌手終於發行她的第一張個人專輯，賣出了一百萬張。"},{"w":"solo","p":"adv.","d":"alone; without anyone else","c":"單獨地","s":"My brother is not allowed to fly solo yet; he still needs ten more hours of practice with his flight teacher.","t":"我哥哥還不能單獨飛行；他還需要和飛行教練再練習十個小時。"},{"w":"soloist","p":"n.","d":"a person who performs a solo","c":"獨奏者；獨唱者","s":"The young soloist played the violin so beautifully that the audience stood up and clapped for five minutes.","t":"那位年輕的獨奏者小提琴拉得太美了，觀眾起立鼓掌了五分鐘。"},{"w":"sophisticated","p":"adj.","d":"advanced and complicated","c":"精密的；複雜的","s":"The new hospital uses sophisticated machines that can find a tiny problem in the heart long before the patient feels sick.","t":"新醫院使用精密的儀器，能在病人感到不適之前很久就發現心臟的微小問題。","h":1},{"w":"sophisticated","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of experience of the world and good taste","c":"世故的；有品味的","s":"After living in Paris for five years, my cousin has become very sophisticated and knows a lot about wine, art, and fashion.","t":"在巴黎住了五年後，我表姐變得非常有品味，對酒、藝術和時尚都很懂。"},{"w":"sophistication","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being advanced or having good taste","c":"精密；世故；品味","s":"The sophistication of modern phones amazes my grandfather, who still remembers when a phone could only make calls.","t":"現代手機的精密讓我爺爺很驚訝，他還記得手機只能打電話的年代。"},{"w":"unsophisticated","p":"adj.","d":"simple; not having much experience of the world","c":"不精密的；單純的","s":"The village people seemed unsophisticated to the city visitors, but they knew far more about the mountains and weather than anyone else.","t":"村民在城市訪客眼中似乎很單純，但他們對山林和天氣的了解遠超過任何人。"},{"w":"sophomore","p":"n.","d":"a student in the second year of high school or university","c":"二年級學生","s":"As a sophomore at the university, my sister has finished her first year and now has to choose her major.","t":"身為大學二年級學生，我姐姐已經讀完第一年，現在必須選擇主修。","h":1},{"w":"freshman","p":"n.","d":"a student in the first year of high school or university","c":"一年級新生","s":"Every freshman must attend the welcome meeting on the first day of school to learn about the library and the clubs.","t":"每位一年級新生都必須參加開學第一天的歡迎會，認識圖書館和社團。"},{"w":"junior","p":"n.","d":"a student in the third year of high school or university","c":"三年級學生","s":"As a junior in high school, Amy is one year away from graduation and has started to look at universities.","t":"身為高中三年級學生，艾咪距離畢業還有一年，已經開始看大學了。"},{"w":"senior","p":"n.","d":"a student in the last year of high school or university","c":"畢業班學生；高年級生","s":"Every senior must hand in a final project before graduation, so the library is full of fourth-year students this month.","t":"每位畢業班學生都必須在畢業前交出畢業專題，所以這個月圖書館擠滿了四年級學生。"},{"w":"souvenir","p":"n.","d":"something you keep to remember a place or event","c":"紀念品","s":"I bought a small wooden boat as a souvenir of our trip to Japan, and it still sits on my desk today.","t":"我買了一艘小木船作為我們日本之旅的紀念品，它至今仍放在我的書桌上。","h":1},{"w":"souvenir shop","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop that sells things for tourists to remember a place","c":"紀念品店","s":"Right next to the museum exit there is a souvenir shop where you can buy postcards, cups, and T-shirts of the paintings.","t":"博物館出口旁邊就有一家紀念品店，你可以在那裡買到印有畫作的明信片、杯子和T恤。"},{"w":"keepsake","p":"n.","d":"a small thing you keep to remember a person","c":"紀念物","s":"My grandmother gave me her old watch as a keepsake, so I would always remember her when I looked at the time.","t":"奶奶把她的舊手錶送給我當紀念物，這樣我每次看時間都會想起她。"},{"w":"sovereignty","p":"n.","d":"the power of a country to rule itself","c":"主權","s":"The small island nation fought for many years to protect its sovereignty and the right to make its own laws.","t":"這個小島國奮戰多年，以保護它的主權和制定自己法律的權利。","h":1},{"w":"sovereign","p":"adj.","d":"independent and ruling itself","c":"擁有主權的；獨立的","s":"After the war ended, the former colony finally became a sovereign state with its own flag, army, and government.","t":"戰爭結束後，這個前殖民地終於成為一個擁有自己國旗、軍隊和政府的主權國家。"},{"w":"sovereign","p":"n.","d":"a king or queen","c":"君主","s":"In the old kingdom, the sovereign had the final word on every law, and nobody dared to question his decisions.","t":"在古老的王國裡，君主對每一條法律都有最後決定權，沒有人敢質疑他的決定。"},{"w":"sow, sowed, sown","p":"v.","d":"to plant seeds in the ground","c":"播種","s":"Farmers in this area usually sow rice seeds in early spring, when the weather becomes warm and wet.","t":"這一帶的農民通常在初春天氣變得溫暖潮濕時播稻種。","a":"sow","h":1},{"w":"sow the seeds of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start something that will grow into a bigger problem or result","c":"埋下…的種子","s":"Unfair treatment of workers can sow the seeds of anger that later grows into a big strike at the factory.","t":"對工人的不公平待遇可能埋下憤怒的種子，日後演變成工廠的大罷工。"},{"w":"reap what you sow","p":"phr.","d":"to get good or bad results because of what you did","c":"種什麼因，得什麼果","s":"My father always says that you reap what you sow, so if you study hard now, you will enjoy the results later.","t":"我爸爸總是說種什麼因得什麼果，所以如果你現在努力讀書，以後就會享受到成果。"},{"w":"seed","p":"n.","d":"the small hard part of a plant from which a new plant grows","c":"種子","s":"Plant each seed about two centimeters deep, water it every morning, and you should see green leaves in a week.","t":"把每顆種子種在大約兩公分深的地方，每天早上澆水，一週內你應該就能看到綠葉。"},{"w":"spacious","p":"adj.","d":"large, with a lot of space inside","c":"寬敞的","s":"The new apartment is bright and spacious, with a living room big enough for the whole family to eat together.","t":"新公寓明亮又寬敞，客廳大到足以讓全家人一起吃飯。","h":1},{"w":"space","p":"n.","d":"an empty area that can be used for something","c":"空間","s":"There is not enough space in my bedroom for a second bed, so my cousin will have to sleep on the sofa.","t":"我的臥室沒有足夠的空間放第二張床，所以我表弟得睡沙發。"},{"w":"outer space","p":"n.phr.","d":"the area beyond the Earth where the stars and planets are","c":"外太空","s":"Scientists are still looking for signs of life in outer space, but so far they have found nothing on any other planet.","t":"科學家仍在外太空尋找生命的跡象，但到目前為止在其他行星上什麼都沒找到。"},{"w":"sparkle","p":"v.","d":"to shine with small bright flashes of light","c":"閃耀；閃閃發光","s":"The sea began to sparkle in the morning sun, and the children ran down to the beach to swim.","t":"大海在晨光中開始閃閃發光，孩子們跑到海灘去游泳。","h":1},{"w":"sparkle","p":"n.","d":"a bright shining quality in someone's eyes or in an object","c":"光彩；閃光","s":"There was a sparkle in her eyes when she talked about her plan to study art in Italy next year.","t":"當她談到明年要去義大利學藝術的計畫時，眼裡閃著光彩。"},{"w":"sparkling","p":"adj.","d":"shining brightly; (of a drink) with bubbles","c":"閃閃發光的；氣泡的","s":"The waiter asked whether we wanted still or sparkling water, and my sister chose the one with bubbles.","t":"服務生問我們要無氣泡水還是氣泡水，我姐姐選了有泡泡的那種。"},{"w":"spark","p":"n.","d":"a very small piece of burning material or flash of light","c":"火花","s":"A tiny spark from the campfire landed on the dry grass, and within minutes the whole field was burning.","t":"營火的一小點火花落在乾草上，幾分鐘內整片草地就燒了起來。"},{"w":"specialist","p":"n.","d":"a person who knows a lot about one subject","c":"專家；專科醫生","s":"My family doctor sent me to a heart specialist in Taipei because she wanted an expert to check the test results.","t":"我的家庭醫師把我轉介給台北的心臟專科醫生，因為她希望由專家來檢查檢驗結果。","h":1},{"w":"specialize","p":"v.","d":"to spend most of your time on one subject or activity","c":"專精；專門從事","s":"This restaurant specializes in seafood, so you should try the fish and shrimp rather than the beef.","t":"這家餐廳專做海鮮，所以你應該嘗嘗魚和蝦，而不是牛肉。","a":"specializes","h":1},{"w":"specialty","p":"n.","d":"a food or product that a place is famous for; something you are very good at","c":"特產；專長","s":"Mango ice is the specialty of this old shop, and people line up for it every summer afternoon.","t":"芒果冰是這家老店的招牌特產，每個夏天的下午都有人排隊買。","h":1},{"w":"special","p":"adj.","d":"different from usual; important","c":"特別的","s":"My mom made a special dinner with all my favorite dishes to celebrate my passing the exam.","t":"我媽媽做了一頓有我所有最愛菜色的特別晚餐，來慶祝我通過考試。"},{"w":"especially","p":"adv.","d":"more than usual; in particular","c":"特別是；尤其","s":"I love fruit, especially mangoes, so summer is my favorite season of the whole year.","t":"我愛水果，尤其是芒果，所以夏天是我一整年最愛的季節。"},{"w":"specialized","p":"adj.","d":"designed or trained for one particular purpose","c":"專門的；專業的","s":"Repairing old watches requires specialized tools that you cannot buy in a normal hardware store.","t":"修理老手錶需要專門的工具，這些在普通五金行買不到。"},{"w":"specify","p":"v.","d":"to say exactly what is needed or wanted","c":"明確指出；具體說明","s":"The recipe does not specify how much salt to add, so I just put in a small spoonful and tasted the soup.","t":"食譜沒有明確說明要加多少鹽，所以我只放了一小匙，然後嘗了嘗湯。","h":1},{"w":"specific","p":"adj.","d":"exact and clear; particular","c":"明確的；特定的","s":"Please give me a specific time for the meeting, because \"sometime in the afternoon\" is not clear enough for my schedule.","t":"請給我一個明確的會議時間，因為「下午某個時候」對我的行程來說不夠清楚。"},{"w":"specifically","p":"adv.","d":"in a clear and exact way; for one particular purpose","c":"明確地；特別地","s":"The teacher specifically told us to bring a calculator, so I do not understand why half the class forgot it.","t":"老師明確地要我們帶計算機，所以我不懂為什麼半個班都忘了。"},{"w":"specification","p":"n.","d":"a detailed description of how something should be made or what it contains","c":"規格","s":"Before you buy a laptop, read the specifications carefully to make sure it has enough memory for your video editing.","t":"買筆電之前，仔細閱讀規格，確認它有足夠的記憶體供你剪輯影片。","a":"specifications"},{"w":"specimen","p":"n.","d":"an animal, plant, or object kept as an example for study","c":"標本","s":"The science teacher showed us a butterfly specimen in a glass box and explained how its wings are made.","t":"自然老師給我們看一個放在玻璃盒裡的蝴蝶標本，並解釋牠的翅膀是怎麼構成的。","h":1},{"w":"specimen","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of blood, urine, etc. taken for testing","c":"樣本；檢體","s":"The nurse asked me for a blood specimen so that the doctor could check whether I had any infection.","t":"護士要我提供血液檢體，好讓醫生檢查我是否有任何感染。"},{"w":"sample","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of something that shows what the rest is like","c":"樣本；樣品","s":"The shop gave every customer a free sample of the new ice cream, and most people bought a whole box after tasting it.","t":"店家給每位顧客一份新冰淇淋的免費試吃樣品，大多數人嘗過之後都買了一整盒。"},{"w":"spectacular","p":"adj.","d":"very impressive and exciting to look at","c":"壯觀的；精彩的","s":"The view from the top of the mountain was spectacular, with a sea of white clouds below us and the sun rising above them.","t":"山頂的景色非常壯觀，我們腳下是一片白雲海，太陽正從雲海上升起。","h":1},{"w":"spectacle","p":"n.","d":"a very impressive sight or show","c":"壯觀的場面；奇觀","s":"The New Year fireworks over the river were a wonderful spectacle that thousands of people came to watch.","t":"河面上的新年煙火是一場精彩的奇觀，成千上萬的人前來觀賞。"},{"w":"spectacles","p":"n.","d":"glasses that you wear to see better","c":"眼鏡","s":"My grandfather cannot read the newspaper without his spectacles, so he keeps them in his shirt pocket all day.","t":"我爺爺沒有眼鏡就沒辦法看報紙，所以他整天都把眼鏡放在襯衫口袋裡。"},{"w":"spectacularly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very impressive or very noticeable way","c":"壯觀地；驚人地","s":"The plan failed spectacularly: the company lost all its money in six months and had to close every store.","t":"這個計畫驚人地失敗了：公司在六個月內賠光所有的錢，必須關閉每一家店。"},{"w":"spectator","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches a game or event","c":"觀眾","s":"Every spectator at the stadium stood up and cheered when the home team scored in the final minute of the game.","t":"當主隊在比賽最後一分鐘得分時，體育場裡的每位觀眾都起立歡呼。","h":1},{"w":"spectator sport","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sport that many people enjoy watching","c":"觀賞性運動","s":"Baseball is the most popular spectator sport in Taiwan, and tens of thousands of fans fill the stadiums every weekend.","t":"棒球是台灣最受歡迎的觀賞性運動，每個週末都有數萬名球迷擠滿球場。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch or listen to a performance","c":"觀眾；聽眾","s":"The audience laughed so loudly at the comedian's jokes that he had to stop and wait before he could continue.","t":"觀眾被喜劇演員的笑話逗得大笑，笑聲大到他得停下來等一等才能繼續。"},{"w":"onlooker","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches something happening without taking part","c":"旁觀者","s":"A crowd of onlookers gathered around the street artist as he drew a lifelike picture of the old temple with chalk.","t":"街頭藝術家用粉筆畫出栩栩如生的古廟時，一群旁觀者圍在他身邊。","a":"onlookers"},{"w":"spectrum","p":"n.","d":"the band of colors that light is divided into","c":"光譜","s":"When sunlight passes through a glass prism, it breaks into a spectrum of colors from red to violet.","t":"當陽光穿過玻璃稜鏡時，會分成從紅到紫的一道光譜。","h":1},{"w":"spectrum","p":"n.","d":"a complete range of different things or people","c":"範圍；領域","s":"The new library offers a wide spectrum of activities, from story time for babies to computer classes for the elderly.","t":"新圖書館提供範圍很廣的活動，從給嬰兒的故事時間到給長者的電腦課都有。"},{"w":"a broad spectrum of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very wide range of","c":"廣泛的；各式各樣的","s":"The survey collected opinions from a broad spectrum of people, including students, workers, farmers, and retired teachers.","t":"這項調查收集了各式各樣的人的意見，包括學生、工人、農民和退休教師。"},{"w":"speculate","p":"v.","d":"to guess about something without knowing all the facts","c":"推測；猜測","s":"Nobody knows why the famous singer suddenly stopped performing, so fans continue to speculate about the real reason online.","t":"沒有人知道那位知名歌手為什麼突然停止演出，所以粉絲們持續在網路上猜測真正的原因。","h":1},{"w":"speculate","p":"v.","d":"to buy and sell things in the hope of making money, with the risk of losing it","c":"投機","s":"My uncle lost most of his savings when he tried to speculate in gold, so now he keeps his money in the bank.","t":"我叔叔試圖投機黃金時賠掉了大部分積蓄，所以現在他把錢放在銀行。"},{"w":"speculation","p":"n.","d":"guessing without knowing the facts; risky buying and selling","c":"推測；投機","s":"There has been a lot of speculation about who will be the next coach, but the team has not announced anything yet.","t":"關於誰會是下一任教練有很多猜測，但球隊還沒有宣布任何消息。"},{"w":"speculative","p":"adj.","d":"based on guessing, not on facts","c":"推測的；投機的","s":"The newspaper story was purely speculative; the reporter had no real proof that the two companies were planning to join.","t":"那篇報紙報導純屬推測；記者沒有真正的證據證明那兩家公司打算合併。"},{"w":"sphere","p":"n.","d":"a round solid shape like a ball","c":"球體","s":"The Earth is not a perfect sphere; it is slightly flatter at the top and bottom than around the middle.","t":"地球不是一個完美的球體；它的頂部和底部比中間稍微扁一些。","h":1},{"w":"sphere","p":"n.","d":"an area of activity, interest, or knowledge","c":"領域","s":"The famous scientist is well known not only in the sphere of physics but also in politics and education.","t":"這位著名科學家不僅在物理學領域聞名，在政治和教育方面也很有名。"},{"w":"spherical","p":"adj.","d":"shaped like a ball","c":"球形的","s":"Most planets are roughly spherical because gravity pulls their material equally toward the center from every direction.","t":"大多數行星大致是球形的，因為重力從各個方向把它們的物質均勻地拉向中心。"},{"w":"hemisphere","p":"n.","d":"one half of the Earth","c":"半球","s":"When it is winter in the Northern Hemisphere, people in Australia are enjoying their summer holidays at the beach.","t":"當北半球是冬天時，澳洲的人們正在海灘上享受他們的暑假。","a":"Hemisphere"},{"w":"spicy","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong hot taste","c":"辛辣的","s":"The curry at that restaurant is so spicy that my eyes watered and I had to drink three glasses of milk.","t":"那家餐廳的咖哩辣到我眼淚直流，得喝三杯牛奶。","h":1},{"w":"spice","p":"n.","d":"a powder or seed from a plant used to give food a strong taste","c":"香料","s":"Cinnamon is a sweet-smelling spice that is often added to apple pie and hot drinks in winter.","t":"肉桂是一種氣味香甜的香料，冬天常被加進蘋果派和熱飲裡。"},{"w":"spice up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make something more interesting or exciting","c":"增添趣味；使更有意思","s":"The teacher tried to spice up the boring grammar lesson with a few games and funny videos.","t":"老師試著用幾個遊戲和有趣的影片來增添無聊文法課的趣味。"},{"w":"spine","p":"n.","d":"the line of bones down the middle of your back","c":"脊椎；脊柱","s":"Sitting in front of a computer for ten hours a day is bad for your spine, so stand up and stretch every hour.","t":"每天坐在電腦前十小時對你的脊椎不好，所以每小時都要站起來伸展一下。","h":1},{"w":"spine","p":"n.","d":"the narrow back edge of a book where the pages are joined","c":"書脊","s":"The title of the book is printed on its spine, so you can read it easily when the book is standing on the shelf.","t":"書名印在書脊上，所以當書立在書架上時你可以輕鬆讀到它。"},{"w":"spinal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the spine","c":"脊椎的","s":"The motorcycle rider suffered a serious spinal injury in the crash and may never be able to walk again.","t":"那位機車騎士在車禍中脊椎嚴重受傷，可能再也無法走路。"},{"w":"spineless","p":"adj.","d":"weak and afraid to do what is right","c":"沒骨氣的；懦弱的","s":"He was too spineless to tell his boss that the plan would fail, so he just kept quiet and let it happen.","t":"他太懦弱，不敢告訴老闆這個計畫會失敗，所以只是保持沉默，任由它發生。"}]},{"unit":34,"theme":"sponge – straightforward","cards":[{"w":"sponge","p":"n.","d":"a soft object with many holes used for washing or cleaning","c":"海綿","s":"Use a wet sponge to wipe the table after dinner, and then dry it with a clean cloth.","t":"晚餐後用濕海綿擦桌子，然後再用乾淨的布擦乾。","h":1},{"w":"sponge","p":"v.","d":"to clean something with a wet sponge or cloth","c":"用海綿擦洗","s":"She sponged the dirty marks off the wall with warm soapy water before the guests arrived.","t":"客人到之前，她用溫肥皂水用海綿擦掉牆上的髒痕。","a":"sponged"},{"w":"sponge cake","p":"n.phr.","d":"a light soft cake made with eggs, sugar, and flour","c":"海綿蛋糕","s":"My grandmother's sponge cake is so light and soft that it almost disappears in your mouth.","t":"我奶奶的海綿蛋糕又輕又軟，幾乎一入口就化了。"},{"w":"sponge off sb","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get money or food from someone without giving anything back","c":"靠某人過活；揩油","s":"He is thirty years old but still sponges off his parents instead of looking for a job.","t":"他已經三十歲了，卻還靠父母過活，而不去找工作。","a":"sponges off"},{"w":"sponsor","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that gives money to support an event or person","c":"贊助者；贊助商","s":"A local bank is the main sponsor of the marathon, so its name is printed on every runner's T-shirt.","t":"一家當地銀行是這場馬拉松的主要贊助商，所以它的名字印在每位跑者的T恤上。","h":1},{"w":"sponsorship","p":"n.","d":"money given by a company to support an event or activity","c":"贊助；資助","s":"Without sponsorship from several big companies, the school could never afford to hold such a large music festival.","t":"如果沒有幾家大公司的贊助，學校根本無法負擔舉辦這麼大型的音樂節。","h":1},{"w":"sponsor","p":"v.","d":"to give money to support an event, person, or team","c":"贊助","s":"A sports company agreed to sponsor our basketball team and gave us new uniforms and shoes for the season.","t":"一家運動用品公司同意贊助我們的籃球隊，並給了我們這一季的新球衣和球鞋。"},{"w":"sponsored walk","p":"n.phr.","d":"a walk in which people collect money for a good cause","c":"募款健走","s":"The students organized a sponsored walk and raised fifty thousand dollars for the animal shelter.","t":"學生們舉辦了一場募款健走，為動物收容所募得五萬元。"},{"w":"spouse","p":"n.","d":"a husband or wife","c":"配偶","s":"Please write the name of your spouse on the form if you are married, and leave the space empty if you are single.","t":"如果你已婚，請在表格上填寫你配偶的姓名；如果單身，就把空格留白。","h":1},{"w":"husband","p":"n.","d":"the man that a woman is married to","c":"丈夫","s":"Her husband cooks dinner every evening while she helps the children with their homework at the kitchen table.","t":"她丈夫每天晚上做晚餐，而她則在餐桌旁幫孩子們寫功課。"},{"w":"wife","p":"n.","d":"the woman that a man is married to","c":"妻子","s":"My uncle always buys flowers for his wife on their wedding anniversary, even after thirty years of marriage.","t":"我叔叔在結婚紀念日總是會買花給他妻子，即使已經結婚三十年了。"},{"w":"partner","p":"n.","d":"the person you are married to or live with","c":"伴侶","s":"The invitation says you may bring your partner, so I will ask my girlfriend if she wants to come to the dinner.","t":"邀請函上說可以帶伴侶，所以我會問我女朋友想不想來參加晚宴。"},{"w":"squad","p":"n.","d":"a group of players from which a team is chosen","c":"（運動）小隊；全體隊員","s":"The coach picked a squad of twenty players for the national team, but only eleven can play in each game.","t":"教練為國家隊挑選了一支二十人的隊伍，但每場比賽只能有十一人上場。","h":1},{"w":"squad","p":"n.","d":"a small group of soldiers or police officers with a special job","c":"小隊；分隊","s":"A special police squad was sent to the airport after someone reported a strange bag left near the gate.","t":"有人通報登機門附近有個可疑的袋子後，一支特別警察小隊被派往機場。"},{"w":"squad car","p":"n.phr.","d":"a police car","c":"警車","s":"Two squad cars with flashing lights raced down the street, and all the cars pulled over to let them pass.","t":"兩輛閃著警燈的警車沿街疾駛而過，所有的車都靠邊讓它們通過。","a":"squad cars"},{"w":"squash","p":"v.","d":"to press something so that it becomes flat or damaged","c":"壓扁；壓壞","s":"Do not put the eggs at the bottom of the shopping bag, or the heavy cans will squash them on the way home.","t":"不要把蛋放在購物袋底部，否則回家路上重重的罐頭會把它們壓壞。","h":1},{"w":"squash","p":"n.","d":"a game played by two people hitting a small ball against walls","c":"壁球","s":"Squash is a fast indoor game in which two players hit a small rubber ball against the walls of a closed room.","t":"壁球是一種快速的室內運動，兩名球員在密閉房間裡把小橡膠球打向牆壁。","a":"Squash"},{"w":"squash","p":"n.","d":"a large vegetable with hard skin, such as a pumpkin","c":"南瓜類蔬菜","s":"Pumpkin is a kind of squash, and in autumn farmers sell many sizes and colors of it at the market.","t":"南瓜是一種南瓜類蔬菜，秋天時農民會在市場賣各種大小和顏色的南瓜。"},{"w":"squash into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to push into a small space","c":"擠進","s":"Six of us squashed into the back of the small car, and nobody could move until we reached the beach.","t":"我們六個人擠進小車的後座，到海灘之前沒有人能動一下。","a":"squashed into"},{"w":"squat","p":"v.","d":"to bend your knees and sit low with your bottom near the ground","c":"蹲下","s":"You should squat down and lift the box with your legs, not your back, or you may hurt yourself.","t":"你應該蹲下來用腿的力量抬箱子，而不是用背，否則可能會受傷。","h":1},{"w":"squat","p":"n.","d":"an exercise in which you bend your knees and stand up again","c":"深蹲","s":"The trainer told me to do twenty squats every morning to make my legs stronger for the race.","t":"教練要我每天早上做二十個深蹲，讓我的腿為比賽變得更強壯。","a":"squats"},{"w":"squat","p":"adj.","d":"short and wide","c":"矮胖的；矮而寬的","s":"A squat little house with a red roof stood at the end of the road, half hidden by tall trees.","t":"一棟紅屋頂的矮胖小房子立在路的盡頭，一半被高大的樹木遮住。"},{"w":"stability","p":"n.","d":"the state of being steady and not changing","c":"穩定；安定","s":"After years of war, the people of the country wanted peace and stability more than anything else.","t":"經過多年的戰爭，這個國家的人民最想要的就是和平與安定。","h":1},{"w":"stable","p":"adj.","d":"firm and steady; not likely to change or fall","c":"穩定的；穩固的","s":"Make sure the ladder is stable before you climb up to clean the windows on the second floor.","t":"爬上去清洗二樓窗戶之前，要確定梯子是穩固的。"},{"w":"unstable","p":"adj.","d":"not steady; likely to change or fall","c":"不穩定的","s":"The old bridge is unstable and shakes when a truck drives over it, so the city plans to close it next month.","t":"這座舊橋不穩固，卡車開過時會搖晃，所以市政府計畫下個月封閉它。"},{"w":"stabilize","p":"v.","d":"to make something steady or stop it from changing","c":"使穩定","s":"The doctors worked all night to stabilize the patient's condition after the serious car accident.","t":"嚴重車禍後，醫生們整夜努力穩定病人的狀況。"},{"w":"instability","p":"n.","d":"the state of being likely to change suddenly","c":"不穩定","s":"Political instability in the region has made many foreign companies afraid to build new factories there.","t":"該地區的政治不穩定讓許多外國公司不敢在那裡建新工廠。"},{"w":"stack","p":"n.","d":"a neat pile of things placed one on top of another","c":"一堆；一疊","s":"There is a stack of old newspapers by the door, so please take them to the recycling truck on Thursday.","t":"門邊有一疊舊報紙，請在星期四把它們拿去回收車。","h":1},{"w":"stack","p":"v.","d":"to put things in a neat pile","c":"堆疊；堆放","s":"After dinner, the children stacked the dirty plates neatly in the sink so that Dad could wash them later.","t":"晚餐後，孩子們把髒盤子整齊地疊在水槽裡，好讓爸爸稍後清洗。","a":"stacked"},{"w":"stack up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to increase in amount, especially of work or problems","c":"堆積；累積","s":"Work began to stack up while I was sick, and now I have three reports to write before Friday.","t":"我生病時工作開始堆積，現在星期五之前我有三份報告要寫。"},{"w":"stain","p":"n.","d":"a dirty mark that is hard to remove","c":"污漬；污點","s":"There is a coffee stain on your white shirt, so you had better change before the interview starts.","t":"你的白襯衫上有一塊咖啡污漬，面試開始前你最好換一件。","h":1},{"w":"stain","p":"v.","d":"to leave a mark that is hard to remove","c":"弄髒；染污","s":"Be careful with the red wine, because it will stain the tablecloth if you spill even a few drops.","t":"小心紅酒，因為哪怕只灑幾滴，它也會弄髒桌布。"},{"w":"stained","p":"adj.","d":"covered with marks that are hard to remove","c":"有污漬的","s":"The painter's stained jeans were covered with blue and yellow marks from years of work.","t":"那位油漆工沾滿污漬的牛仔褲上布滿了多年工作留下的藍色和黃色痕跡。"},{"w":"stainless steel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a type of steel that does not rust","c":"不鏽鋼","s":"The kitchen knives are made of stainless steel, so they will not rust even if you leave them wet in the sink.","t":"這些菜刀是不鏽鋼做的，所以即使你把它們濕濕地放在水槽裡也不會生鏽。"},{"w":"stake","p":"n.","d":"a strong wooden or metal stick pushed into the ground","c":"木樁；樁","s":"The farmer drove a wooden stake into the ground and tied the young tree to it so the wind would not break it.","t":"農夫把一根木樁打進土裡，把小樹綁在上面，這樣風就不會把樹吹斷。","h":1},{"w":"at stake","p":"phr.","d":"in danger of being lost; at risk","c":"危急關頭；有風險","s":"The doctors must decide quickly, because the patient's life is at stake and every minute counts.","t":"醫生必須快速做決定，因為病人的生命危在旦夕，每一分鐘都很重要。"},{"w":"stake","p":"n.","d":"a share in a business; a strong interest in something","c":"股份；利害關係","s":"My father owns a 20 percent stake in the restaurant, so he goes there every month to check the accounts.","t":"我爸爸擁有那家餐廳百分之二十的股份，所以他每個月都去那裡查帳。"},{"w":"stake","p":"v.","d":"to risk money or something important on a result","c":"以…為賭注；押上","s":"I would not stake my whole savings on a company that was started only six months ago.","t":"我不會把全部積蓄押在一家六個月前才成立的公司上。"},{"w":"stakeholder","p":"n.","d":"a person or group that is affected by a business or plan","c":"利害關係人","s":"Before the new park is built, the city will listen to every stakeholder, including nearby residents and shop owners.","t":"在新公園興建之前，市政府會聽取每一位利害關係人的意見，包括附近居民和店家。"},{"w":"stall","p":"n.","d":"a small open shop or table where things are sold","c":"攤位；攤子","s":"The night market has a famous stall that sells fried chicken, and the line is always at least twenty people long.","t":"夜市裡有一個賣炸雞的知名攤位，排隊的人總是至少有二十個。","h":1},{"w":"stall","p":"v.","d":"(of an engine) to stop suddenly","c":"（引擎）熄火","s":"The old car stalled at the red light, and my father had to try three times before the engine started again.","t":"那輛老車在紅燈前熄火了，我爸爸試了三次引擎才再次發動。","a":"stalled"},{"w":"stall","p":"v.","d":"to delay doing something on purpose","c":"拖延","s":"The manager tried to stall for time by asking more questions, because he had not read the report yet.","t":"經理試圖透過多問問題來拖延時間，因為他還沒讀過那份報告。"},{"w":"stance","p":"n.","d":"an opinion that you state clearly","c":"立場；態度","s":"The mayor has taken a firm stance against building more factories near the river, and many voters support her.","t":"市長對反對在河邊興建更多工廠採取堅定的立場，許多選民支持她。","h":1},{"w":"stance","p":"n.","d":"the way you stand, especially in a sport","c":"站姿","s":"The baseball coach corrected my stance at the plate so that I could swing the bat with more power.","t":"棒球教練糾正了我在打擊區的站姿，讓我揮棒更有力。"},{"w":"take a stance","p":"v.phr.","d":"to state your opinion clearly on an issue","c":"表明立場","s":"Our teacher asked everyone to take a stance on the school uniform rule and explain our reasons in a short speech.","t":"老師要每個人對校服規定表明立場，並用簡短的演講說明理由。"},{"w":"startle","p":"v.","d":"to surprise or frighten someone suddenly","c":"使驚嚇；使吃驚","s":"Please do not startle the horse by shouting or running near it, because it may kick you if it gets scared.","t":"請不要在馬旁邊大叫或奔跑而驚嚇到牠，因為牠受驚時可能會踢你。","h":1},{"w":"startled","p":"adj.","d":"suddenly surprised or frightened","c":"受驚的；吃驚的","s":"The startled cat jumped off the table and ran under the bed when the fireworks began outside.","t":"外面煙火開始時，受驚的貓從桌上跳下來，跑到床底下。"},{"w":"startling","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising or shocking","c":"令人吃驚的","s":"The report contains some startling facts about how much plastic ends up in the ocean every single day.","t":"這份報告包含一些令人吃驚的事實，說明每天有多少塑膠最後流進海洋。"},{"w":"statistical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with numbers and facts collected for study","c":"統計的","s":"The scientists used statistical methods to prove that the new medicine really works better than the old one.","t":"科學家用統計方法證明新藥真的比舊藥更有效。","h":1},{"w":"statistics","p":"n.","d":"numbers and facts collected to show information about something","c":"統計數字；統計學","s":"The statistics show that more young people are riding bicycles to work than ten years ago.","t":"統計數字顯示，騎腳踏車上班的年輕人比十年前更多。"},{"w":"statistically","p":"adv.","d":"according to statistics","c":"從統計上來看","s":"Statistically, flying is much safer than driving, even though many people are more afraid of planes than cars.","t":"從統計上來看，搭飛機比開車安全得多，即使許多人更怕飛機而不是汽車。","a":"Statistically"},{"w":"statistician","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies and works with statistics","c":"統計學家","s":"The company hired a statistician to study the sales numbers and find out which products were most popular with teenagers.","t":"公司聘請了一位統計學家研究銷售數字，找出哪些產品最受青少年歡迎。"},{"w":"steer","p":"v.","d":"to control the direction of a vehicle","c":"駕駛；操控方向","s":"It is hard to steer a bicycle with one hand, so put your phone away and hold the handlebars properly.","t":"單手很難操控腳踏車，所以把手機收起來，好好握住把手。","h":1},{"w":"steer","p":"v.","d":"to guide a conversation or situation in a particular direction","c":"引導","s":"The teacher tried to steer the discussion back to the main topic after the students started talking about the weekend.","t":"學生們開始聊週末之後，老師試著把討論引導回主題。"},{"w":"steer clear of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to avoid someone or something","c":"避開；遠離","s":"My doctor told me to steer clear of sweet drinks and fast food if I want to lose weight before summer.","t":"醫生告訴我，如果想在夏天前減重，就要避開含糖飲料和速食。"},{"w":"steering wheel","p":"n.phr.","d":"the wheel a driver turns to control a car","c":"方向盤","s":"Keep both hands on the steering wheel while you drive, and never try to read a text message at the same time.","t":"開車時雙手要放在方向盤上，絕對不要同時看簡訊。"},{"w":"stereotype","p":"n.","d":"a fixed idea about what a group of people is like, which is often wrong","c":"刻板印象","s":"The idea that all teenagers are lazy is just a stereotype; many of my classmates work hard both at school and at part-time jobs.","t":"「所有青少年都很懶」只是一種刻板印象；我許多同學在學校和打工時都很努力。","h":1},{"w":"stereotype","p":"v.","d":"to have a fixed idea about a group of people","c":"對…有刻板印象","s":"It is unfair to stereotype people by their age, because a seventy-year-old can learn new technology as well as anyone.","t":"用年齡來給人貼標籤是不公平的，因為七十歲的人也能和任何人一樣學會新科技。"},{"w":"stereotypical","p":"adj.","d":"based on a fixed idea about a group of people","c":"刻板的；老套的","s":"The movie shows a stereotypical mother who only cooks and cleans, which made many women in the audience angry.","t":"這部電影呈現了一個只會煮飯打掃的刻板母親形象，讓許多女性觀眾很生氣。"},{"w":"stew","p":"n.","d":"a dish of meat and vegetables cooked slowly in liquid","c":"燉菜；燉肉","s":"On cold winter nights, my grandmother makes a big pot of beef stew with carrots and potatoes for the whole family.","t":"在寒冷的冬夜，我奶奶會為全家做一大鍋有紅蘿蔔和馬鈴薯的燉牛肉。","h":1},{"w":"stew","p":"v.","d":"to cook food slowly in liquid","c":"燉；燜煮","s":"You need to stew the meat slowly for two hours so that it becomes soft enough for Grandpa to eat.","t":"你需要把肉慢慢燉兩個小時，讓它軟到爺爺可以吃。"},{"w":"stewed","p":"adj.","d":"cooked slowly in liquid","c":"燉煮的","s":"The dessert was stewed apples with a little honey, and it was the perfect ending to the heavy meal.","t":"甜點是加了一點蜂蜜的燉蘋果，是這頓大餐的完美結尾。"},{"w":"stimulate","p":"v.","d":"to make something develop or become more active","c":"刺激；激發","s":"Reading to young children helps to stimulate their imagination and makes them want to learn new words.","t":"讀書給幼兒聽有助於激發他們的想像力，讓他們想學習新單字。","h":1},{"w":"stimulus","p":"n.","d":"something that makes a person or thing more active","c":"刺激物；激勵","s":"The lower taxes were meant to act as a stimulus to the economy by making people spend more money in shops.","t":"降低稅收的用意是作為經濟的刺激，讓人們在商店裡花更多錢。","h":1},{"w":"stimulation","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something more active or interesting","c":"刺激","s":"Babies need plenty of stimulation such as colors, sounds, and gentle touch, to help their brains develop.","t":"嬰兒需要大量的刺激，像是顏色、聲音和輕柔的觸摸，來幫助大腦發育。"},{"w":"stimulating","p":"adj.","d":"interesting and making you think","c":"刺激的；富有啟發性的","s":"The science teacher gives such stimulating lessons that even the students who hate science look forward to her class.","t":"這位自然老師的課非常富有啟發性，連討厭自然科的學生都期待上她的課。"},{"w":"stink, stank, stunk","p":"v.","d":"to smell very bad","c":"發臭","s":"The fish we forgot in the car began to stink so badly that we had to leave all the windows open for a week.","t":"我們忘在車裡的魚開始發臭，臭到我們得把所有車窗開著一個星期。","a":"stink","h":1},{"w":"stink","p":"n.","d":"a very bad smell","c":"臭味","s":"What a stink! Did someone leave the garbage bag in the kitchen over the whole long weekend?","t":"好臭啊！是不是有人整個連假都把垃圾袋留在廚房裡？"},{"w":"stinky","p":"adj.","d":"smelling very bad","c":"臭的；發臭的","s":"My brother's stinky socks were left under the sofa for days, and the smell filled the whole living room.","t":"我哥哥臭臭的襪子在沙發下放了好幾天，臭味充滿了整個客廳。"},{"w":"stink of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to smell strongly of something unpleasant","c":"散發…的臭味","s":"If you do not shower after football practice, you will stink of sweat, and nobody will want to sit next to you.","t":"如果你足球練習後不洗澡，你會散發汗臭味，沒有人會想坐在你旁邊。"},{"w":"stock","p":"n.","d":"the goods that a shop has available to sell","c":"存貨；庫存","s":"The shop has plenty of umbrellas in stock, so you can buy one even on the rainiest day of the year.","t":"這家店有很多雨傘庫存，所以即使在一年中雨最大的日子你也能買到。","h":1},{"w":"stock","p":"n.","d":"a share in a company that people buy and sell","c":"股票","s":"My aunt bought stock in a small technology company ten years ago, and now it is worth twenty times more.","t":"我阿姨十年前買了一家小科技公司的股票，現在價值漲了二十倍。"},{"w":"stock market","p":"n.phr.","d":"the business of buying and selling shares in companies","c":"股市","s":"When the stock market fell sharply last week, many people lost a lot of money in just a few days.","t":"上週股市大跌時，許多人在短短幾天內損失了很多錢。"},{"w":"out of stock","p":"phr.","d":"not available in the shop at the moment","c":"缺貨","s":"The popular game is out of stock at every store in town, so I ordered it online and will wait a week.","t":"這款熱門遊戲在城裡每家店都缺貨，所以我在網路上訂了，要等一個星期。"},{"w":"stock","p":"v.","d":"to keep goods available for sale","c":"進貨；備有","s":"The supermarket does not stock that brand of tea anymore, so we have to order it from Japan.","t":"超市不再進那個牌子的茶了，所以我們得從日本訂購。"},{"w":"stock up on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to buy a lot of something to use later","c":"囤積；大量購買","s":"Before the typhoon arrived, everyone rushed to stock up on water, instant noodles, and batteries.","t":"颱風來之前，大家都趕著囤積水、泡麵和電池。"},{"w":"storage","p":"n.","d":"the act of keeping things in a place until they are needed","c":"儲存；儲藏","s":"We put our winter clothes in storage under the bed during the summer to make more room in the closet.","t":"夏天時我們把冬衣收納在床底下，好讓衣櫃有更多空間。","h":1},{"w":"store","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in a place for later use","c":"儲存；存放","s":"You can store thousands of photos on this small memory card and look at them on any computer.","t":"你可以在這張小小的記憶卡上儲存數千張照片，並在任何電腦上觀看。"},{"w":"storage room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room where things are kept until they are needed","c":"儲藏室","s":"The old desks are kept in the storage room on the first floor until the school decides what to do with them.","t":"舊書桌暫時放在一樓的儲藏室裡，直到學校決定如何處理它們。"},{"w":"straighten","p":"v.","d":"to make something straight or neat","c":"弄直；整理","s":"The teacher asked us to straighten the rows of desks before the visitors came to look at our classroom.","t":"參觀者來看我們教室之前，老師要我們把一排排的課桌排整齊。","h":1},{"w":"straightforward","p":"adj.","d":"easy to understand or do; not complicated","c":"簡單的；直截了當的","s":"The instructions for the new phone were straightforward, so even my grandmother could set it up without any help.","t":"新手機的說明很簡單明瞭，所以連我奶奶都能不用幫忙就設定好。","h":1},{"w":"straighten up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stand up straight; to make a place tidy","c":"挺直身體；整理","s":"Straighten up and stop looking at your shoes when you give your speech, or the audience will think you are not confident.","t":"演講時挺直身體，別一直盯著鞋子看，否則觀眾會覺得你沒有自信。","a":"Straighten up"},{"w":"straight","p":"adj.","d":"not bent or curved","c":"直的","s":"Draw a straight line from the top of the page to the bottom, and then fold the paper along it.","t":"從頁面頂端到底部畫一條直線，然後沿著它把紙摺起來。"},{"w":"straight","p":"adv.","d":"directly, without stopping or turning","c":"直接地；筆直地","s":"After school, go straight home and do not stop at the game shop, because Grandma is coming for dinner.","t":"放學後直接回家，不要在遊戲店停留，因為奶奶要來吃晚餐。"},{"w":"straightforward","p":"adj.","d":"honest and saying exactly what you think","c":"坦率的；直率的","s":"My boss is very straightforward; if she does not like your work, she will tell you right away instead of hiding it.","t":"我的老闆非常直率；如果她不喜歡你的作品，她會馬上告訴你，而不是藏在心裡。"}]},{"unit":35,"theme":"strain – surplus","cards":[{"w":"strain","p":"n.","d":"pressure or worry that is hard to deal with","c":"壓力；緊張；負擔","s":"Working twelve hours a day for a whole month put a lot of strain on her, so her doctor told her to take a break.","t":"連續一個月每天工作十二小時給她帶來很大的壓力，所以醫生要她休息一下。","h":1},{"w":"strain","p":"v.","d":"to hurt a muscle by stretching it too much","c":"拉傷；扭傷","s":"Be careful not to strain your back when you lift that heavy box, and always bend your knees first.","t":"抬那個重箱子時小心不要拉傷背部，而且一定要先彎曲膝蓋。"},{"w":"strain","p":"n.","d":"an injury caused by stretching a muscle too much","c":"拉傷","s":"The basketball player has a muscle strain in his left leg, so he will miss the next two games this month.","t":"那位籃球員左腿肌肉拉傷，所以這個月接下來的兩場比賽他都無法上場。"},{"w":"under strain","p":"phr.","d":"having too much pressure or work","c":"承受壓力；負荷過重","s":"The city's hospitals have been under strain since the flu season started, and many nurses are working extra shifts.","t":"自從流感季開始，這座城市的醫院一直承受壓力，許多護理師都在加班。"},{"w":"strained","p":"adj.","d":"not friendly or relaxed because of problems","c":"緊張的；不自然的","s":"The relationship between the two brothers has been strained ever since they argued about their father's house last year.","t":"自從去年兩兄弟為了父親的房子吵架以來，他們的關係一直很緊張。"},{"w":"strand","p":"n.","d":"a single thin piece of hair, thread, or wire","c":"一縕；一股（頭髮、線）","s":"She found a long strand of blonde hair on his jacket, and she wondered where it had come from.","t":"她在他的夾克上發現一縕金色長髮，心想那是從哪裡來的。","h":1},{"w":"strand","p":"v.","d":"to leave someone in a place with no way to leave","c":"使滯留；使受困","s":"The heavy snow may strand thousands of travelers at the airport tonight, so the airline is handing out blankets and food.","t":"大雪今晚可能使數千名旅客滯留在機場，所以航空公司正在發放毛毯和食物。"},{"w":"be stranded","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be stuck somewhere and unable to leave","c":"受困；滯留","s":"When our car broke down in the mountains, we were stranded for six hours before a truck finally stopped to help.","t":"我們的車在山區故障時，我們受困了六個小時，才終於有一輛卡車停下來幫忙。","a":"were stranded"},{"w":"strap","p":"n.","d":"a long thin piece of leather or cloth used to hold or carry something","c":"帶子；皮帶；肩帶","s":"The strap on my school bag broke this morning, so I had to carry all my heavy books in my arms.","t":"我書包的背帶今天早上斷了，所以我只好把所有厚重的書抱在手上。","h":1},{"w":"strap","p":"v.","d":"to fasten something with a strap","c":"用帶子綁住；捆","s":"The movers will strap the piano to the truck carefully so that it does not move during the long drive.","t":"搬家工人會小心地把鋼琴用帶子綁在卡車上，這樣長途行駛時它才不會移動。"},{"w":"strap in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fasten yourself with a seat belt","c":"繫好安全帶","s":"The flight attendant asked everyone to strap in because the plane was about to fly through a storm.","t":"空服員要求每個人繫好安全帶，因為飛機即將穿過暴風雨。"},{"w":"shoulder strap","p":"n.phr.","d":"a strap that goes over your shoulder","c":"肩帶","s":"This camera bag has a wide shoulder strap, so it feels comfortable even when you walk around the city all day.","t":"這個相機包有寬的肩帶，所以即使你在城市裡走一整天也覺得舒服。"},{"w":"strategic","p":"adj.","d":"done as part of a careful plan to reach a goal","c":"策略性的；戰略的","s":"Opening a store right next to the MRT station was a strategic decision, and sales doubled within the first year.","t":"在捷運站旁邊開店是一個策略性的決定，第一年營業額就翻倍了。","h":1},{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a careful plan for reaching a goal","c":"策略；戰略","s":"Our team needs a better strategy for the second half, or we will lose the game by more than twenty points.","t":"我們的球隊下半場需要更好的策略，否則我們會輸超過二十分。"},{"w":"strategically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that follows a careful plan","c":"策略性地","s":"The supermarket places candy strategically near the checkout, where tired parents and bored children are most likely to buy it.","t":"超市策略性地把糖果放在結帳櫃台附近，那裡疲憊的父母和無聊的孩子最可能買。"},{"w":"strategist","p":"n.","d":"a person who is good at planning how to reach goals","c":"策略家；戰略家","s":"The company hired a marketing strategist to help them sell their new phone to young people in Asia.","t":"這家公司聘請了一位行銷策略家，幫助他們把新手機賣給亞洲的年輕人。"},{"w":"striking","p":"adj.","d":"very unusual or attractive, so people notice it","c":"引人注目的；顯著的","s":"There is a striking difference between the two photos, because the glacier has lost half its size in only thirty years.","t":"這兩張照片有顯著的差異，因為冰河在短短三十年內縮小了一半。","h":1},{"w":"strike, struck, struck","p":"v.","d":"to hit someone or something hard; to stop working in protest","c":"打擊；撞擊；罷工","s":"Lightning may strike tall trees during a storm, so you should never stand under one when you hear thunder.","t":"暴風雨時閃電可能擊中高大的樹木，所以聽到雷聲時絕對不要站在樹下。","a":"strike"},{"w":"strike","p":"n.","d":"a period when workers refuse to work to get better pay or conditions","c":"罷工","s":"The bus drivers' strike lasted three days, and thousands of students had to walk or ride bikes to school.","t":"公車司機的罷工持續了三天，數千名學生不得不走路或騎腳踏車上學。"},{"w":"on strike","p":"phr.","d":"refusing to work in order to protest","c":"罷工中","s":"The factory workers have been on strike for two weeks because the company refused to raise their pay.","t":"工廠工人已經罷工兩週了，因為公司拒絕提高他們的薪資。"},{"w":"strikingly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is very noticeable","c":"顯著地；驚人地","s":"The twins look strikingly similar, and even their teachers sometimes call them by the wrong names.","t":"這對雙胞胎看起來驚人地相似，連他們的老師有時都會叫錯名字。"},{"w":"structural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the way something is built or organized","c":"結構上的；結構性的","s":"The engineers found serious structural problems in the old bridge, so it will be closed to traffic until next spring.","t":"工程師在這座舊橋發現嚴重的結構問題，所以它將封閉禁止通行到明年春天。","h":1},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"the way parts are put together; a building","c":"結構；建築物","s":"The structure of this essay is clear because each paragraph begins with a main idea and ends with an example.","t":"這篇文章的結構很清楚，因為每個段落都以主旨開頭，並以例子結尾。"},{"w":"structure","p":"v.","d":"to arrange or organize something in a planned way","c":"組織；安排","s":"Before you give a speech, you should structure your ideas carefully so that the audience can follow them easily.","t":"在演講之前，你應該仔細組織你的想法，這樣聽眾才能輕鬆跟上。"},{"w":"infrastructure","p":"n.","d":"the basic systems a country needs, such as roads and power","c":"基礎建設","s":"The government is spending billions on infrastructure, including new highways, railways, and a faster internet network for rural areas.","t":"政府正花費數十億在基礎建設上，包括新的高速公路、鐵路和鄉村地區更快的網路。"},{"w":"stumble","p":"v.","d":"to almost fall while walking or running","c":"絆倒；蹣跚","s":"The old man started to stumble on the wet stairs, but luckily a young woman caught his arm just in time.","t":"老先生在濕滑的樓梯上開始絆倒，幸好一位年輕女子及時抓住了他的手臂。","h":1},{"w":"stumble","p":"n.","d":"the act of almost falling; a small mistake","c":"絆倒；失足；小失誤","s":"The skater made only one small stumble during her performance, yet it was enough to cost her the gold medal.","t":"這位滑冰選手在表演中只有一次小失誤，卻足以讓她失去金牌。"},{"w":"stumble across","p":"v.phr.","d":"to find something by chance","c":"偶然發現","s":"While cleaning the attic last weekend, I stumbled across a box of letters that my grandfather wrote during the war.","t":"上週末打掃閣樓時，我偶然發現一箱爺爺在戰爭期間寫的信。","a":"stumbled across"},{"w":"stumbling block","p":"n.phr.","d":"a problem that stops you from making progress","c":"障礙；絆腳石","s":"The high cost of land is the biggest stumbling block for young couples who want to buy their first home in Taipei.","t":"高昂的土地成本是想在台北買第一間房子的年輕夫妻最大的絆腳石。"},{"w":"sturdy","p":"adj.","d":"strong and not easily broken or damaged","c":"堅固的；結實的","s":"You will need a pair of sturdy boots for the hike, because the rocky trail is steep and often wet.","t":"這次健行你需要一雙堅固的靴子，因為多石的小徑很陡，而且常常潮濕。","h":1},{"w":"sturdy","p":"adj.","d":"strong and healthy in body","c":"健壯的；強壯的","s":"The farmer's sturdy son can carry two heavy bags of rice at the same time without stopping to rest.","t":"農夫健壯的兒子可以同時扛兩大袋米，不用停下來休息。"},{"w":"sturdily","p":"adv.","d":"in a strong, solid way","c":"堅固地；結實地","s":"This wooden table was sturdily built by my grandfather fifty years ago, and we still eat dinner at it every night.","t":"這張木桌是我爺爺五十年前堅固地打造的，我們現在每晚還在它上面吃晚餐。"},{"w":"submit","p":"v.","d":"to give a document or plan to someone so they can decide on it","c":"提交；呈交","s":"All students must submit their science reports by Friday afternoon, or they will lose ten points for being late.","t":"所有學生必須在星期五下午前提交科學報告，否則會因遲交被扣十分。","h":1},{"w":"submit to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to accept someone's power or control","c":"屈服於；服從","s":"The small country refused to submit to the demands of its powerful neighbor, even though a war seemed likely.","t":"這個小國拒絕屈服於強大鄰國的要求，即使戰爭看起來很可能發生。"},{"w":"submission","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving a document to someone; accepting someone's power","c":"提交；屈服","s":"The deadline for the submission of your college application is March first, so do not wait until the last minute.","t":"大學申請提交的截止日期是三月一日，所以不要等到最後一刻。"},{"w":"submissive","p":"adj.","d":"always willing to obey others without arguing","c":"順從的；服從的","s":"The puppy became quiet and submissive as soon as the trainer spoke to it in a calm, firm voice.","t":"訓練師用平靜而堅定的聲音對小狗說話，小狗立刻變得安靜又順從。"},{"w":"subsequent","p":"adj.","d":"happening after something else","c":"隨後的；後來的","s":"The first meeting went badly, but in subsequent meetings the two companies slowly learned to trust each other.","t":"第一次會議進行得不順利，但在隨後的會議中，兩家公司慢慢學會信任彼此。","h":1},{"w":"subsequently","p":"adv.","d":"after something else happened; later","c":"隨後；後來","s":"She failed the driving test twice, but she subsequently passed it with a perfect score after taking more lessons.","t":"她駕照考試失敗了兩次，但在多上幾堂課後，她隨後以滿分通過了。"},{"w":"subsequent to","p":"phr.","d":"after; following","c":"在…之後","s":"Subsequent to the earthquake, the government checked every school building in the city to make sure it was safe.","t":"在地震之後，政府檢查了市內每一棟校舍，以確保它們是安全的。","a":"Subsequent to"},{"w":"subsidy","p":"n.","d":"money given by the government to help keep prices low or support an activity","c":"補助金；補貼","s":"Farmers in this area receive a subsidy from the government, which helps them survive when rice prices fall.","t":"這個地區的農民獲得政府的補助金，這幫助他們在米價下跌時撐下去。","h":1},{"w":"subsidize","p":"v.","d":"to pay part of the cost of something to make it cheaper","c":"補助；資助","s":"The city plans to subsidize electric scooters next year, so riders will pay about half the normal price.","t":"市政府計畫明年補助電動機車，所以騎士只需付大約一半的正常價格。"},{"w":"government subsidy","p":"n.phr.","d":"money the government gives to support something","c":"政府補助","s":"Thanks to a government subsidy, the family was able to install solar panels on their roof for a very low price.","t":"多虧了政府補助，這家人得以用很低的價格在屋頂安裝太陽能板。"},{"w":"substantial","p":"adj.","d":"large in amount or importance","c":"大量的；重大的","s":"The company made a substantial profit last year, so every worker received an extra month of pay as a bonus.","t":"這家公司去年獲得可觀的利潤，所以每位員工都多領一個月薪水作為獎金。","h":1},{"w":"substantial","p":"adj.","d":"solid and strong; large and filling","c":"堅固的；豐盛的","s":"After hiking for six hours, we were ready for a substantial meal of rice, meat, and three kinds of vegetables.","t":"健行六小時後，我們準備好享用一頓有米飯、肉和三種蔬菜的豐盛大餐。"},{"w":"substantially","p":"adv.","d":"by a large amount; greatly","c":"大幅地；實質上","s":"Ticket prices have risen substantially since last year, and many families can no longer afford to go to concerts.","t":"票價自去年以來大幅上漲，許多家庭再也負擔不起去聽演唱會。"},{"w":"substance","p":"n.","d":"a type of material; the most important part of something","c":"物質；實質；重點","s":"The police found a strange white substance in the bag, and they sent it to a laboratory to find out what it was.","t":"警方在袋子裡發現一種奇怪的白色物質，他們把它送到實驗室查明是什麼。"},{"w":"substitute","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that takes the place of another","c":"代替者；代替品","s":"Our math teacher is sick this week, so a substitute will teach the class until she comes back.","t":"我們的數學老師這週生病了，所以會有一位代課老師教這個班，直到她回來。","h":1},{"w":"substitute","p":"v.","d":"to use something or someone instead of another","c":"代替；取代","s":"If you do not have butter at home, you can substitute olive oil for it when you bake this cake.","t":"如果家裡沒有奶油，你烤這個蛋糕時可以用橄欖油代替。"},{"w":"substitute teacher","p":"n.phr.","d":"a teacher who takes the place of the regular teacher","c":"代課老師","s":"The substitute teacher did not know our names, so she asked each of us to introduce ourselves before the lesson began.","t":"代課老師不知道我們的名字，所以她在上課前請我們每個人自我介紹。"},{"w":"substitution","p":"n.","d":"the act of using one thing or person instead of another","c":"代替；替換（球員）","s":"The coach made a late substitution, and the new player scored the winning goal two minutes before the end of the game.","t":"教練在比賽尾聲做了一次換人，新上場的球員在終場前兩分鐘踢進致勝球。"},{"w":"subtle","p":"adj.","d":"not easy to notice or understand; small but important","c":"微妙的；不明顯的","s":"There is a subtle difference between the two colors, and most people cannot see it unless they look very closely.","t":"這兩種顏色之間有微妙的差異，大多數人除非仔細看才看得出來。","h":1},{"w":"subtly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is not easy to notice","c":"微妙地；不易察覺地","s":"The teacher subtly changed the subject when the students began to ask about her private life.","t":"當學生開始問起她的私生活時，老師巧妙地轉移了話題。"},{"w":"subtlety","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being small and hard to notice; a small detail","c":"微妙；細微之處","s":"Young learners often miss the subtlety of a joke in English, so they laugh a few seconds after everyone else.","t":"年輕的學習者常常聽不出英文笑話的微妙之處，所以他們比別人晚幾秒才笑。"},{"w":"suburban","p":"adj.","d":"connected with an area where people live outside the center of a city","c":"郊區的","s":"Many young families move to suburban areas because houses there are bigger and cheaper than in the city center.","t":"許多年輕家庭搬到郊區，因為那裡的房子比市中心更大也更便宜。","h":1},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"an area where people live outside the center of a city","c":"郊區","s":"My uncle lives in a quiet suburb of Taichung, and it takes him forty minutes to drive to his office downtown.","t":"我叔叔住在台中一個安靜的郊區，開車到市中心的辦公室要四十分鐘。"},{"w":"in the suburbs","p":"phr.","d":"in the areas outside the center of a city","c":"在郊區","s":"We grew up in the suburbs, where every house had a garden and children could ride their bikes safely on the streets.","t":"我們在郊區長大，那裡每棟房子都有花園，孩子可以安全地在街上騎腳踏車。"},{"w":"urban","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a town or city","c":"城市的；都市的","s":"Air pollution is a serious urban problem, so the city is planting thousands of trees along its busiest roads.","t":"空氣污染是一個嚴重的都市問題，所以市政府正沿著最繁忙的道路種植數千棵樹。"},{"w":"successor","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes a job or position after someone else","c":"接班人；繼任者","s":"The old king chose his youngest daughter as his successor, which surprised the whole country because her brothers were older.","t":"老國王選擇他最小的女兒作為繼任者，這讓全國都很驚訝，因為她的哥哥們年紀更大。","h":1},{"w":"succeed","p":"v.","d":"to take a position or job after someone else","c":"接任；繼承","s":"When the manager retires in June, his assistant will succeed him and take charge of the whole department.","t":"經理六月退休時，他的助理將接任他的職位，負責整個部門。"},{"w":"succession","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking over a position; a series of things one after another","c":"繼承；接續；一連串","s":"The team won five games in succession, and the fans began to believe they could really win the championship.","t":"這支球隊連續贏了五場比賽，球迷開始相信他們真的能贏得冠軍。"},{"w":"successive","p":"adj.","d":"happening one after another without a break","c":"連續的；接連的","s":"It rained for seven successive days, so the farmers worried that their vegetables would rot in the wet fields.","t":"連續下了七天雨，所以農民擔心他們的蔬菜會在濕透的田裡腐爛。"},{"w":"in succession","p":"phr.","d":"one after another","c":"連續地；接連地","s":"The young pianist played three difficult pieces in succession without a single mistake, and the audience stood up to cheer.","t":"這位年輕鋼琴家連續演奏三首困難的曲子而沒有一個錯誤，觀眾起立歡呼。"},{"w":"suite","p":"n.","d":"a set of connected rooms in a hotel","c":"套房","s":"For their anniversary, my parents stayed in a suite with a living room and a view of the whole harbor.","t":"為了慶祝結婚紀念日，我父母住在一間有客廳、能看到整個港口的套房。","h":1},{"w":"suite","p":"n.","d":"a set of related things, such as software or furniture","c":"一套；套裝（軟體、傢俱）","s":"The school bought a new office suite for every computer, so students can now write reports and make slides easily.","t":"學校為每台電腦購買了新的辦公套裝軟體，所以學生現在可以輕鬆寫報告和做簡報。"},{"w":"hotel suite","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large hotel room with more than one room","c":"飯店套房","s":"The movie star booked the most expensive hotel suite in the city, which costs more than my father earns in a month.","t":"這位電影明星預訂了市內最貴的飯店套房，價格比我爸爸一個月賺的還多。"},{"w":"superb","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; excellent","c":"極好的；一流的","s":"The food at the new Italian restaurant was superb, and we have already decided to go back there next weekend.","t":"那家新義大利餐廳的食物極好，我們已經決定下週末再去。","h":1},{"w":"superbly","p":"adv.","d":"extremely well","c":"極好地；出色地","s":"The young actress performed superbly in her first movie, and many people believe she will win an award this year.","t":"這位年輕女演員在她的第一部電影中表現出色，許多人相信她今年會獲獎。"},{"w":"superior","p":"adj.","d":"better than others in quality or ability","c":"較好的；優越的","s":"This brand of running shoes is more expensive, but its quality is superior and the shoes last twice as long.","t":"這個牌子的跑鞋比較貴，但品質較優，而且鞋子可以穿兩倍久。"},{"w":"superiority","p":"n.","d":"the state of being better than others","c":"優越；優勢","s":"The team showed its superiority in the first ten minutes, scoring three goals before the other side even touched the ball.","t":"這支球隊在前十分鐘就展現了優勢，在對方還沒碰到球之前就進了三球。"},{"w":"superstition","p":"n.","d":"a belief that some things bring good or bad luck, not based on reason","c":"迷信","s":"According to an old superstition, breaking a mirror brings seven years of bad luck, but of course nobody can prove it.","t":"根據一個古老的迷信，打破鏡子會帶來七年的壞運氣，但當然沒有人能證明這一點。","h":1},{"w":"superstitious","p":"adj.","d":"believing that some things bring good or bad luck","c":"迷信的","s":"My grandmother is very superstitious, so she never lets us open an umbrella inside the house.","t":"我奶奶非常迷信，所以她絕不讓我們在屋子裡撐開傘。"},{"w":"superstitiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows a belief in luck","c":"迷信地","s":"Before every game, the pitcher superstitiously touches his cap three times because he believes it helps him throw better.","t":"每場比賽前，這位投手都會迷信地摸三次帽子，因為他相信這能幫他投得更好。"},{"w":"supervise","p":"v.","d":"to watch over people or work to make sure everything is done correctly","c":"監督；管理","s":"Two teachers will supervise the students during the field trip to make sure that nobody gets lost in the museum.","t":"校外教學期間，兩位老師會監督學生，確保沒有人在博物館裡走失。","h":1},{"w":"supervision","p":"n.","d":"the act of watching over people or work","c":"監督；管理","s":"Young children should never swim without adult supervision, even if the pool is shallow and they can swim well.","t":"幼童絕對不應在沒有成人監督的情況下游泳，即使泳池很淺而且他們會游泳。","h":1},{"w":"supervisor","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to watch over other workers","c":"主管；監督者；指導教授","s":"If you have any problems with your schedule, please talk to your supervisor before the end of the week.","t":"如果你的班表有任何問題，請在週末前和你的主管談一談。","h":1},{"w":"under the supervision of","p":"phr.","d":"being watched and guided by someone","c":"在…的監督下","s":"The students did the chemistry experiment under the supervision of their teacher, who reminded them to wear safety glasses.","t":"學生們在老師的監督下做化學實驗，老師提醒他們要戴護目鏡。"},{"w":"supervisory","p":"adj.","d":"connected with watching over and managing others","c":"監督的；管理的","s":"After five years at the company, she was given a supervisory role and now leads a team of twelve people.","t":"在公司工作五年後，她獲得一個管理職位，現在帶領一個十二人的團隊。"},{"w":"supposedly","p":"adv.","d":"as people say or believe, though it may not be true","c":"據說；據推測","s":"The old house on the hill is supposedly haunted, but my brother and I spent a night there and saw nothing.","t":"山丘上的老房子據說有鬼，但我和哥哥在那裡過了一夜，什麼也沒看到。","h":1},{"w":"suppose","p":"v.","d":"to think that something is probably true","c":"認為；猜想；假定","s":"I suppose the train will be late again because of the heavy rain, so let's leave home ten minutes earlier.","t":"我猜想火車會因為大雨再次誤點，所以我們提早十分鐘出門吧。"},{"w":"be supposed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be expected or required to do something","c":"應該；理應","s":"You are supposed to hand in your homework before class, not after the teacher has already started the lesson.","t":"你應該在上課前交作業，而不是在老師已經開始上課之後。","a":"are supposed to"},{"w":"supposition","p":"n.","d":"an idea that you believe is true although you have no proof","c":"推測；假設","s":"The police report is based on supposition rather than facts, so the judge refused to accept it as evidence.","t":"這份警方報告是基於推測而不是事實，所以法官拒絕接受它作為證據。"},{"w":"supreme","p":"adj.","d":"highest in rank or importance; greatest","c":"最高的；至高的","s":"In the past, the emperor had supreme power over the whole country, and nobody dared to question his decisions.","t":"過去，皇帝擁有全國最高的權力，沒有人敢質疑他的決定。","h":1},{"w":"Supreme Court","p":"n.phr.","d":"the highest court in a country","c":"最高法院","s":"The case went all the way to the Supreme Court, and its final decision changed the law for the whole country.","t":"這個案件一路上訴到最高法院，它的最終判決改變了全國的法律。"},{"w":"supremely","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; to the highest degree","c":"極其；至高地","s":"She looked supremely confident as she walked onto the stage, even though it was her first time speaking in public.","t":"她走上舞台時看起來極其自信，儘管那是她第一次公開演講。"},{"w":"supremacy","p":"n.","d":"the position of having more power than anyone else","c":"至高無上；霸權","s":"For many years, the two countries fought for supremacy in the region, and smaller nations were caught in the middle.","t":"多年來，這兩個國家為了該地區的霸權而爭鬥，較小的國家則被夾在中間。"},{"w":"surplus","p":"n.","d":"an amount that is more than what is needed","c":"剩餘；過剩；盈餘","s":"The farmers had a surplus of cabbages this winter, so they sold them at half price to avoid wasting food.","t":"農民今年冬天高麗菜過剩，所以他們以半價出售以免浪費食物。","h":1},{"w":"surplus","p":"adj.","d":"more than what is needed","c":"多餘的；剩餘的","s":"The company donated its surplus computers to a school in the mountains instead of throwing them away.","t":"這家公司把多餘的電腦捐給山區的一所學校，而不是把它們丟掉。"},{"w":"trade surplus","p":"n.phr.","d":"a situation in which a country sells more than it buys from other countries","c":"貿易順差","s":"The country had a large trade surplus last year because it sold far more electronics abroad than it imported.","t":"這個國家去年有巨額的貿易順差，因為它賣到國外的電子產品遠多於進口。"}]},{"unit":36,"theme":"surveillance – thigh","cards":[{"w":"surveillance","p":"n.","d":"the act of watching a person or place carefully, often secretly","c":"監視；監控","s":"The police kept the suspect under close surveillance for two weeks before they finally arrested him at his home.","t":"警方對嫌犯進行了兩週的嚴密監視，最後才在他家中將他逮捕。","h":1},{"w":"under surveillance","p":"phr.","d":"being watched carefully, often by the police","c":"在監視之下","s":"The old warehouse has been under surveillance since last month because the police believe stolen cars are hidden inside.","t":"那座舊倉庫自上個月起就受到監視，因為警方認為裡面藏有失竊的汽車。"},{"w":"surveillance camera","p":"n.phr.","d":"a camera that records what happens in a place","c":"監視攝影機","s":"A surveillance camera at the bank recorded the robber's face, so the police were able to find him within a day.","t":"銀行的監視攝影機錄下了搶匪的臉，所以警方在一天內就找到了他。"},{"w":"survey","p":"n.","d":"a set of questions asked to many people to find out what they think","c":"調查；問卷調查","s":"According to a recent survey, more than half of the students in our school sleep less than six hours a night.","t":"根據最近的一項調查，我們學校超過一半的學生每晚睡不到六小時。"},{"w":"survey","p":"v.","d":"to ask many people questions to find out what they think; to look at a whole area","c":"調查；勘測；環視","s":"The company will survey two thousand customers next month to learn what they think about the new bubble tea flavors.","t":"這家公司下個月將調查兩千名顧客，了解他們對新珍珠奶茶口味的看法。"},{"w":"suspend","p":"v.","d":"to stop something for a short time; to stop someone from attending school or work","c":"暫停；中止；停學；停職","s":"The school decided to suspend the student for three days after he was caught cheating on the final exam.","t":"學校決定讓那名學生停學三天，因為他在期末考作弊被抓到。","h":1},{"w":"suspend","p":"v.","d":"to hang something from somewhere","c":"懸掛；吊","s":"The workers will suspend the large lantern from the ceiling of the temple before the festival begins next week.","t":"工人們將在下週慶典開始前，把大燈籠懸掛在寺廟的天花板上。"},{"w":"suspension","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping something for a time; the punishment of being kept out of school or work","c":"暫停；停學；停職；懸吊","s":"The basketball player received a two-game suspension for pushing the referee, and his team lost both games without him.","t":"那位籃球員因為推裁判而被禁賽兩場，他的球隊在沒有他的情況下輸了兩場。"},{"w":"suspense","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of excitement or worry while waiting to find out what will happen","c":"懸疑；緊張感","s":"The movie kept us in suspense until the last five minutes, when we finally learned who the real killer was.","t":"這部電影讓我們一直處於懸疑中，直到最後五分鐘我們才知道真正的兇手是誰。"},{"w":"suspension bridge","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bridge that hangs from strong cables","c":"吊橋","s":"The old suspension bridge swings a little when you walk across it, so some tourists are afraid to look down at the river.","t":"這座古老的吊橋在你走過時會輕微搖晃，所以有些遊客不敢往下看河流。"},{"w":"sustain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something going over a long time; to support","c":"維持；支撐；供養","s":"The small island cannot sustain so many tourists every summer, because there is not enough fresh water for everyone.","t":"這座小島無法每年夏天支撐這麼多遊客，因為沒有足夠的淡水供所有人使用。","h":1},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to continue for a long time without harming the environment","c":"可持續的；永續的","s":"Solar and wind power are sustainable sources of energy, so many countries are building fewer coal power plants now.","t":"太陽能和風力是永續的能源來源，所以許多國家現在減少興建燃煤電廠。","h":1},{"w":"sustain","p":"v.","d":"to suffer an injury or damage","c":"遭受（傷害、損失）","s":"Two of the passengers managed to sustain only minor injuries in the crash, although the car was completely destroyed.","t":"雖然車子完全毀了，但兩名乘客在車禍中只受了輕傷。"},{"w":"sustainability","p":"n.","d":"the ability to continue without harming the environment","c":"永續性；可持續性","s":"Our school started a sustainability project this year, and every class now grows vegetables and recycles all of its paper.","t":"我們學校今年開始了一個永續計畫，現在每個班級都種蔬菜並回收所有紙張。"},{"w":"sustained","p":"adj.","d":"continuing for a long time without stopping","c":"持續的；不間斷的","s":"After years of sustained effort, the scientist finally found a cheaper way to clean dirty river water.","t":"經過多年持續的努力，這位科學家終於找到了更便宜的方法來淨化髒污的河水。"},{"w":"swap","p":"v.","d":"to give something to someone and get something else in return","c":"交換；調換","s":"My sister and I often swap clothes on weekends, so it feels like we both have twice as many outfits.","t":"我和姊姊週末常常交換衣服穿，所以感覺我們倆的衣服都多了一倍。","h":1},{"w":"swap","p":"n.","d":"the act of exchanging one thing for another","c":"交換","s":"The two students did a quick swap of their lunch boxes because each of them liked the other's food better.","t":"這兩個學生快速交換了便當，因為他們都比較喜歡對方的食物。"},{"w":"swap places","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change seats or positions with someone","c":"交換位置","s":"Could we swap places so that I can sit next to the window and take some photos of the mountains?","t":"我們可以交換位置嗎？這樣我就能坐在窗邊拍一些山的照片。"},{"w":"symbolic","p":"adj.","d":"representing something important, such as an idea or feeling","c":"象徵性的；象徵的","s":"Planting a tree on the first day of school was a symbolic act that showed the students' hope for a greener future.","t":"在開學第一天種一棵樹是一個象徵性的舉動，顯示學生們對更綠色未來的希望。","h":1},{"w":"symbol","p":"n.","d":"a sign, shape, or object that stands for something else","c":"象徵；符號","s":"In many cultures, the dove is a symbol of peace, which is why you often see it on posters against war.","t":"在許多文化中，鴿子是和平的象徵，這就是為什麼你常在反戰海報上看到牠。"},{"w":"symbolize","p":"v.","d":"to be a sign of something; to represent","c":"象徵；代表","s":"In Chinese culture, red lanterns symbolize good luck, so people hang them outside their doors during the New Year.","t":"在華人文化中，紅燈籠象徵好運，所以人們在新年期間把它們掛在門外。"},{"w":"symbolism","p":"n.","d":"the use of symbols to show ideas or feelings","c":"象徵主義；象徵手法","s":"Our teacher explained the symbolism in the poem, and we learned that the winter snow actually stands for death.","t":"老師解釋了這首詩中的象徵手法，我們才知道冬天的雪其實代表死亡。"},{"w":"symptom","p":"n.","d":"a sign in your body that shows you are ill","c":"症狀","s":"A high fever and a sore throat are common symptoms of the flu, so you should stay home and rest if you have them.","t":"發高燒和喉嚨痛是流感常見的症狀，如果你有這些症狀，就應該待在家休息。","a":"symptoms","h":1},{"w":"symptom","p":"n.","d":"a sign that a serious problem exists","c":"徵兆；跡象","s":"Heavy traffic every morning is a symptom of a bigger problem: the city has grown faster than its roads and trains.","t":"每天早上的塞車是一個更大問題的徵兆：這座城市的成長速度超過了它的道路和鐵路。"},{"w":"show symptoms of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have signs of an illness","c":"出現…的症狀","s":"Several children in the kindergarten began to show symptoms of the same illness, so the teachers called their parents right away.","t":"幼兒園裡有幾個孩子開始出現同一種疾病的症狀，所以老師立刻打電話給他們的父母。"},{"w":"syndrome","p":"n.","d":"a medical condition with a group of signs that happen together","c":"症候群；綜合症","s":"Doctors still do not fully understand this rare syndrome, which makes children feel tired and weak all the time.","t":"醫生仍然不完全了解這種罕見的症候群，它讓孩子們總是感到疲倦和虛弱。","h":1},{"w":"syndrome","p":"n.","d":"a set of feelings or behaviors that are typical of a situation","c":"（某種情況特有的）一組現象；心態","s":"Many parents feel sad and lonely when their children leave home for college, and doctors call this feeling empty nest syndrome.","t":"許多父母在孩子離家上大學時感到難過和孤單，醫生稱這種感覺為空巢症候群。"},{"w":"Down syndrome","p":"n.phr.","d":"a condition a person is born with that affects learning and the body","c":"唐氏症","s":"The young man with Down syndrome works at the coffee shop near our school, and he always greets every customer with a smile.","t":"那位患有唐氏症的年輕人在我們學校附近的咖啡店工作，他總是微笑著迎接每位顧客。"},{"w":"tackle","p":"v.","d":"to deal with a difficult problem","c":"處理；應付；著手解決","s":"The new mayor promised to tackle the city's traffic problems by building more bike lanes and adding extra buses.","t":"新市長承諾要透過增建自行車道和增加公車來解決城市的交通問題。","h":1},{"w":"tackle","p":"v.","d":"in sports, to try to take the ball from another player or stop them by catching them","c":"擒抱；攔截；搶球","s":"In rugby, you are allowed to tackle the player who has the ball, but you must not hit him above the shoulders.","t":"在橄欖球中，你可以擒抱持球的球員，但不能攻擊他肩膀以上的部位。"},{"w":"tackle","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping another player in sports","c":"擒抱；攔截","s":"The defender made a perfect tackle just before the striker could shoot, and the whole stadium cheered loudly.","t":"就在前鋒要射門前，後衛做了一次完美的攔截，整個體育場都大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"fishing tackle","p":"n.phr.","d":"the equipment used for fishing","c":"釣具","s":"Grandpa keeps all his fishing tackle in a green box in the garage, and he cleans every hook before each trip.","t":"爺爺把他所有的釣具放在車庫的一個綠色箱子裡，每次出發前都會清理每個魚鉤。"},{"w":"tactic","p":"n.","d":"a method you use to get what you want","c":"策略；手段；戰術","s":"Crying loudly in the toy store is a tactic that my little brother often uses to make Mom buy him something.","t":"在玩具店大聲哭是我弟弟常用的手段，用來讓媽媽買東西給他。","h":1},{"w":"tactics","p":"n.","d":"the methods used to win a game, a battle, or an argument","c":"戰術；策略","s":"The coach changed his tactics at halftime, asking the players to pass the ball faster and shoot from farther away.","t":"教練在中場休息時改變了戰術，要求球員傳球更快並從更遠的地方射門。"},{"w":"tactical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the methods used to reach a goal","c":"戰術的；策略的","s":"Moving the shop's opening time to seven in the morning was a tactical move to catch students on their way to school.","t":"把店的開門時間改到早上七點是一個策略性的行動，為了吸引上學途中的學生。"},{"w":"tangle","p":"n.","d":"a mass of threads, hair, or wires twisted together; a confused state","c":"糾結；纏結；混亂","s":"After the storm, the fisherman spent the whole morning pulling his nets out of a tangle of ropes and seaweed.","t":"暴風雨過後，漁夫花了一整個早上把漁網從繩子和海草的糾結中拉出來。","h":1},{"w":"tangle","p":"v.","d":"to become twisted together in a messy way","c":"使纏結；糾纏","s":"If you leave your earphones loose in your pocket, the wires will tangle and you will waste minutes untying them.","t":"如果你把耳機隨便放在口袋裡，線會纏在一起，你就得浪費好幾分鐘解開它們。"},{"w":"tangled","p":"adj.","d":"twisted together in a messy way","c":"纏結的；糾結的","s":"Her long hair was so tangled after the beach trip that it took her mother half an hour to brush it.","t":"去海邊玩之後她的長髮糾結得很嚴重，媽媽花了半小時才梳開。"},{"w":"get tangled up in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become caught in something; to become involved in a difficult situation","c":"被…纏住；捲入","s":"The young sea turtle got tangled up in an old fishing net, and the volunteers worked for an hour to set it free.","t":"小海龜被一張舊漁網纏住，志工們花了一個小時才把牠救出來。","a":"got tangled up in"},{"w":"tempt","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do or have something, especially something they should not","c":"誘惑；引誘","s":"The smell of fresh bread from the bakery may tempt you to buy more than you planned, so bring only a little money.","t":"麵包店飄出的新鮮麵包香味可能會誘惑你買得比預計的多，所以只帶一點錢就好。","h":1},{"w":"temptation","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to do or have something, especially something bad","c":"誘惑","s":"During the exam, he felt a strong temptation to look at his neighbor's paper, but he kept his eyes on his own desk.","t":"考試期間，他感到一股強烈的誘惑想看鄰座的考卷，但他的眼睛一直盯著自己的桌子。","h":1},{"w":"be tempted to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to want to do something even though it may be wrong","c":"很想…；受誘惑去做…","s":"I was tempted to skip my morning run when it rained, but I put on my jacket and went out anyway.","t":"下雨時我很想跳過晨跑，但我還是穿上外套出門了。","a":"was tempted to"},{"w":"tempting","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and making you want to have or do something","c":"誘人的；吸引人的","s":"The offer of a free trip to Japan sounded very tempting, but we had to read the small print carefully first.","t":"免費日本之旅的優惠聽起來非常誘人，但我們必須先仔細閱讀小字說明。"},{"w":"resist temptation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop yourself from doing something you want to do","c":"抵抗誘惑","s":"It is hard to resist temptation when there is a box of chocolates on the table, especially late at night.","t":"桌上放著一盒巧克力時很難抵抗誘惑，尤其是在深夜。"},{"w":"terminal","p":"n.","d":"a large building at an airport, bus station, or port","c":"航廈；航站；終點站","s":"Our flight to Tokyo leaves from Terminal two, so we need to take the airport train from the first building.","t":"我們飛往東京的班機從第二航廈出發，所以我們需要從第一航廈搭機場捷運過去。","a":"Terminal","h":1},{"w":"terminal","p":"adj.","d":"describing an illness that cannot be cured and will cause death","c":"末期的；無法治癒的","s":"Although the old man had a terminal illness, he spent his last months traveling and laughing with his grandchildren.","t":"雖然老先生患有末期疾病，但他把最後幾個月用來旅行，並和孫子們一起歡笑。"},{"w":"terminal","p":"n.","d":"a computer screen and keyboard connected to a larger computer system","c":"終端機","s":"Each worker in the warehouse uses a small terminal to check how many boxes are left on every shelf.","t":"倉庫裡的每位工人都使用一台小型終端機來查看每個貨架上還剩多少箱子。"},{"w":"terminate","p":"v.","d":"to end something; to bring something to an end","c":"終止；結束","s":"The company decided to terminate the contract with the cleaning service because the offices were still dirty every morning.","t":"這家公司決定終止與清潔公司的合約，因為辦公室每天早上仍然很髒。"},{"w":"termination","p":"n.","d":"the act of ending something","c":"終止；結束","s":"The sudden termination of the bus service left many elderly people in the village with no way to get to the hospital.","t":"公車服務突然終止，讓村裡許多老人沒有辦法去醫院。"},{"w":"terrify","p":"v.","d":"to make someone extremely frightened","c":"使驚嚇；使恐懼","s":"Loud fireworks terrify my dog every New Year's Eve, so we close all the windows and play soft music.","t":"每年除夕夜，響亮的煙火都會嚇壞我的狗，所以我們會關上所有窗戶並播放輕柔的音樂。","h":1},{"w":"terrified","p":"adj.","d":"extremely frightened","c":"非常害怕的；驚恐的","s":"She was terrified of the dark as a child, so her parents always left a small lamp on in the hallway.","t":"她小時候非常害怕黑暗，所以父母總是在走廊留一盞小燈。"},{"w":"terrifying","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel extremely frightened","c":"可怕的；令人恐懼的","s":"The earthquake last night was the most terrifying experience of my life, and I could not sleep until the sun came up.","t":"昨晚的地震是我一生中最可怕的經歷，我直到太陽升起才睡著。"},{"w":"terror","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great fear","c":"恐懼；驚駭","s":"The children screamed in terror when the lights suddenly went out during the ghost story at camp.","t":"露營時講鬼故事的時候燈突然熄滅，孩子們驚恐地尖叫。"},{"w":"testify","p":"v.","d":"to say in a court of law what you know is true","c":"作證","s":"The shop owner agreed to testify in court about what she saw on the night of the robbery.","t":"店主同意在法庭上就她在搶案當晚看到的事情作證。","h":1},{"w":"testimony","p":"n.","d":"a formal statement about what is true, given in a court","c":"證詞；證言","s":"The judge listened carefully to the testimony of the young witness, who described the accident in great detail.","t":"法官仔細聆聽那位年輕證人的證詞，他非常詳細地描述了那起事故。"},{"w":"testify against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give evidence in court that shows someone did something wrong","c":"作證指控…","s":"Nobody in the village was brave enough to testify against the powerful businessman, so the case was finally dropped.","t":"村裡沒有人敢出庭指證那位有權勢的商人，所以案件最終被撤銷。"},{"w":"texture","p":"n.","d":"the way something feels when you touch it, or the way food feels in your mouth","c":"質地；口感；紋理","s":"I love the soft texture of this cake, which is light and creamy without being too sweet.","t":"我喜歡這個蛋糕柔軟的口感，它輕盈滑順又不會太甜。","h":1},{"w":"textile","p":"n.","d":"any type of cloth made by weaving","c":"紡織品；布料","s":"Taiwan's textile industry was very strong in the 1970s, and many factories in Taichung made clothes for the whole world.","t":"台灣的紡織業在一九七○年代非常強盛，台中許多工廠為全世界製作衣服。"},{"w":"textured","p":"adj.","d":"having a surface that is not smooth","c":"有紋理的；質感粗糙的","s":"The textured wallpaper in the hotel room looks like real stone, but it feels soft when you touch it.","t":"飯店房間裡有紋理的壁紙看起來像真的石頭，但摸起來很柔軟。"},{"w":"theft","p":"n.","d":"the crime of stealing something","c":"偷竊；盜竊","s":"Bicycle theft is common near the train station, so always lock your bike to something solid and never leave it overnight.","t":"火車站附近常發生腳踏車偷竊，所以一定要把腳踏車鎖在堅固的東西上，而且絕不要放一整晚。","h":1},{"w":"thief","p":"n.","d":"a person who steals things","c":"小偷；竊賊","s":"The thief climbed in through an open window while the family was watching television in the living room.","t":"一家人在客廳看電視時，小偷從一扇開著的窗戶爬了進來。"},{"w":"identity theft","p":"n.phr.","d":"the crime of using someone else's personal information to steal money","c":"身分盜用","s":"To protect yourself from identity theft, never share your ID number or bank password with people you do not know.","t":"為了保護自己免於身分盜用，絕不要把你的身分證字號或銀行密碼告訴不認識的人。"},{"w":"theology","p":"n.","d":"the study of religion and God","c":"神學","s":"My cousin is studying theology at a university in Rome because he hopes to become a priest one day.","t":"我表哥在羅馬的一所大學研讀神學，因為他希望有一天能成為神父。","h":1},{"w":"theological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the study of religion","c":"神學的","s":"The two professors had a long theological discussion about why a good God would allow so much suffering in the world.","t":"兩位教授針對為何良善的神會允許世上有這麼多苦難，進行了長時間的神學討論。"},{"w":"theologian","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies religion and God","c":"神學家","s":"The famous theologian wrote more than twenty books about faith, and some of them are still read in churches today.","t":"這位著名的神學家寫了二十多本關於信仰的書，其中一些至今仍在教會中被閱讀。"},{"w":"theoretical","p":"adj.","d":"based on ideas rather than practice or experience","c":"理論的；理論上的","s":"The course is too theoretical for me, because we read about engines all day but never actually fix one.","t":"這門課對我來說太理論了，因為我們整天讀引擎的資料，卻從來沒有真正修過一台。","h":1},{"w":"theory","p":"n.","d":"an idea that tries to explain why something happens","c":"理論；學說","s":"Some scientists have a new theory that explains why the dinosaurs disappeared so quickly millions of years ago.","t":"一些科學家有一個新的理論，解釋為什麼恐龍在數百萬年前這麼快就消失了。"},{"w":"theoretically","p":"adv.","d":"according to ideas, although it may not work in real life","c":"理論上","s":"Theoretically, the train should arrive at nine, but it is usually ten minutes late because the line is so busy.","t":"理論上火車應該九點到，但因為這條線太繁忙，它通常會晚十分鐘。","a":"Theoretically"},{"w":"in theory","p":"phr.","d":"according to ideas, but perhaps not in practice","c":"理論上","s":"In theory, anyone can learn to cook, but in practice many people simply do not have the time or patience.","t":"理論上任何人都能學會做菜，但實際上許多人就是沒有時間或耐心。","a":"In theory"},{"w":"therapist","p":"n.","d":"a person trained to help people with physical or emotional problems","c":"治療師","s":"After the accident, a therapist visited my grandfather twice a week to help him learn to walk again.","t":"意外之後，一位治療師每週探視我爺爺兩次，幫助他重新學習走路。","h":1},{"w":"therapy","p":"n.","d":"the treatment of a physical or emotional problem over a period of time","c":"治療；療法","s":"Music therapy has helped many children with special needs to relax and express their feelings in a safe way.","t":"音樂治療幫助許多有特殊需求的孩子放鬆，並以安全的方式表達他們的感受。","h":1},{"w":"physical therapy","p":"n.phr.","d":"treatment that uses exercise and movement to help the body recover","c":"物理治療","s":"The football player needed six months of physical therapy before his knee was strong enough for him to play again.","t":"這位足球員需要六個月的物理治療，膝蓋才強壯到足以再次上場。"},{"w":"therapeutic","p":"adj.","d":"helping to treat an illness or make you feel better","c":"有療效的；治療的","s":"Many people find gardening therapeutic, because working with plants helps them forget their worries for a while.","t":"許多人覺得園藝有療癒效果，因為照顧植物能讓他們暫時忘記煩惱。"},{"w":"thereby","p":"adv.","d":"in that way; as a result of that","c":"藉此；因此","s":"The factory now reuses its waste water, thereby saving millions of liters of fresh water every single year.","t":"這家工廠現在重複使用廢水，藉此每年節省數百萬公升的淡水。","h":1},{"w":"therefore","p":"adv.","d":"for that reason; so","c":"因此；所以","s":"The roads were covered with ice this morning, and therefore all the schools in the area were closed for the day.","t":"今天早上道路被冰覆蓋，因此該地區所有學校當天都停課。"},{"w":"thereafter","p":"adv.","d":"after that time","c":"此後；之後","s":"The company opened its first store in Taipei in 1990, and shortly thereafter it had branches in every major city.","t":"這家公司一九九○年在台北開了第一家店，此後不久就在每個主要城市都有分店。"},{"w":"thesis","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of writing done for a university degree","c":"論文（學位論文）","s":"My brother spent two years writing his master's thesis on how social media changes the way teenagers make friends.","t":"我哥哥花了兩年撰寫他的碩士論文，主題是社群媒體如何改變青少年交朋友的方式。","h":1},{"w":"thesis","p":"n.","d":"the main idea or argument of an essay or speech","c":"論點；主旨","s":"The thesis of her speech was simple: every student should learn to cook before leaving high school.","t":"她演講的論點很簡單：每個學生在高中畢業前都應該學會做菜。"},{"w":"thesis statement","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sentence that tells the main idea of an essay","c":"主旨句；論點陳述","s":"A good thesis statement should appear at the end of your first paragraph so that readers know what you are going to argue.","t":"好的主旨句應該出現在第一段的結尾，這樣讀者才知道你要論證什麼。"},{"w":"hypothesis","p":"n.","d":"an idea that is suggested as an explanation but has not been proved yet","c":"假設；假說","s":"The students tested their hypothesis that plants grow faster with music by playing songs to half of the bean plants.","t":"學生們透過對一半的豆苗播放歌曲，來驗證他們「植物聽音樂長得更快」的假設。"},{"w":"thigh","p":"n.","d":"the top part of your leg, between your knee and your hip","c":"大腿","s":"The runner felt a sharp pain in her right thigh halfway through the race, but she still managed to finish.","t":"這位跑者在比賽中途感到右大腿一陣劇痛，但她還是設法跑完了。","h":1},{"w":"chicken thigh","p":"n.phr.","d":"the meat from the upper part of a chicken's leg","c":"雞腿肉（大腿部分）","s":"This recipe uses chicken thigh instead of breast meat, because it stays soft and juicy after an hour in the oven.","t":"這個食譜用雞腿肉而不是雞胸肉，因為在烤箱裡烤一小時後它仍然柔軟多汁。"},{"w":"thigh bone","p":"n.phr.","d":"the long bone in the upper part of your leg","c":"大腿骨；股骨","s":"The thigh bone is the longest and strongest bone in the human body, and it can support many times your weight.","t":"大腿骨是人體中最長、最強壯的骨頭，它可以支撐你體重的好幾倍。"}]},{"unit":37,"theme":"threshold – tribute","cards":[{"w":"threshold","p":"n.","d":"the level or point at which something starts to happen","c":"門檻；臨界點；起點","s":"The government raised the income threshold for free school lunches, so about two thousand more children can now get them.","t":"政府提高了免費營養午餐的收入門檻，所以現在大約多了兩千名孩子可以領取。","h":1},{"w":"threshold","p":"n.","d":"the floor at the entrance of a door","c":"門檻；門口","s":"In many old Taiwanese houses, the wooden threshold at the front door is high, so visitors must step over it carefully.","t":"在許多台灣老房子裡，大門的木製門檻很高，所以訪客必須小心地跨過去。"},{"w":"on the threshold of","p":"phr.","d":"at the beginning of an important new time or event","c":"即將開始…；在…的開端","s":"Scientists say we are on the threshold of a new age of medicine, in which many diseases will be cured by changing our genes.","t":"科學家說我們正處於醫學新時代的開端，許多疾病將透過改變基因而被治癒。"},{"w":"pain threshold","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of pain a person can bear","c":"痛覺閾值；忍痛能力","s":"My brother has a very high pain threshold, so he did not even cry when the dentist pulled out two of his teeth.","t":"我弟弟的忍痛能力非常高，所以牙醫拔掉他兩顆牙時他連哭都沒哭。"},{"w":"thrill","p":"n.","d":"a sudden strong feeling of excitement","c":"興奮；刺激；激動","s":"Riding the roller coaster for the first time gave me a thrill that I will never forget as long as I live.","t":"第一次搭雲霄飛車給了我一種只要活著就永遠不會忘記的刺激感。","h":1},{"w":"thriller","p":"n.","d":"a book, film, or play with an exciting story, often about crime","c":"驚悚片；驚悚小說","s":"We watched a thriller about a detective chasing a killer through Tokyo, and nobody dared to go to the bathroom.","t":"我們看了一部關於偵探在東京追捕殺手的驚悚片，沒有人敢去上廁所。","h":1},{"w":"thrill","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel very excited and happy","c":"使興奮；使激動","s":"The news that the famous singer would visit our school managed to thrill every student, even the teachers.","t":"那位知名歌手將造訪我們學校的消息令每個學生都興奮不已，連老師也是。"},{"w":"thrilled","p":"adj.","d":"very excited and pleased","c":"非常興奮的；欣喜的","s":"My grandmother was thrilled to receive a video call from all of her grandchildren on her ninetieth birthday.","t":"我奶奶九十歲生日時收到所有孫子的視訊電話，她非常開心。"},{"w":"thrilling","p":"adj.","d":"very exciting","c":"驚險刺激的；令人興奮的","s":"The final game of the season was thrilling from start to finish, and our team won by a single point in the last second.","t":"本季最後一場比賽從頭到尾都驚險刺激，我們的球隊在最後一秒以一分之差獲勝。"},{"w":"thrive","p":"v.","d":"to grow, develop, or become successful","c":"茁壯成長；蓬勃發展；興旺","s":"Small coffee shops thrive in this neighborhood because thousands of university students live within walking distance.","t":"小咖啡店在這個社區蓬勃發展，因為有數千名大學生住在步行可達的範圍內。","h":1},{"w":"thrive on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to enjoy or do well in a situation that others may find difficult","c":"在…中成長茁壯；樂於面對","s":"Some people hate working under pressure, but my sister seems to thrive on tight deadlines and difficult clients.","t":"有些人討厭在壓力下工作，但我姊姊似乎樂於面對緊迫的期限和難搞的客戶。"},{"w":"thriving","p":"adj.","d":"growing and successful","c":"繁榮的；興旺的","s":"Twenty years ago this street was almost empty, but today it is a thriving market full of food stalls and music.","t":"二十年前這條街幾乎空無一人，但今天它是一個充滿小吃攤和音樂的繁榮市集。"},{"w":"throne","p":"n.","d":"the special chair of a king or queen; the position of being king or queen","c":"王座；王位","s":"The young prince sat nervously on the golden throne while hundreds of guests watched him become king.","t":"年輕的王子緊張地坐在金色王座上，數百名賓客看著他成為國王。","h":1},{"w":"come to the throne","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become king or queen","c":"登基；即位","s":"Queen Elizabeth II came to the throne in 1952 when she was only twenty-five, and she ruled for seventy years.","t":"伊莉莎白二世女王於一九五二年登基時只有二十五歲，她統治了七十年。","a":"came to the throne"},{"w":"heir to the throne","p":"n.phr.","d":"the person who will become the next king or queen","c":"王位繼承人","s":"As the heir to the throne, the princess had to study history, law, and five languages before she turned eighteen.","t":"身為王位繼承人，公主在十八歲之前必須學習歷史、法律和五種語言。"},{"w":"thrust, thrust, thrust","p":"v.","d":"to push something suddenly and strongly","c":"猛推；猛塞；用力插入","s":"The angry customer thrust the broken phone into the clerk's hands and demanded to get his money back immediately.","t":"憤怒的顧客把壞掉的手機猛塞進店員手中，要求立刻退錢。","a":"thrust","h":1},{"w":"thrust","p":"n.","d":"the force that pushes a plane or rocket forward","c":"推力","s":"The rocket's engines must produce enough thrust to lift more than five hundred tons off the ground in a few seconds.","t":"火箭的引擎必須產生足夠的推力，才能在幾秒鐘內把超過五百噸的重量推離地面。"},{"w":"thrust","p":"n.","d":"the main point or purpose of something","c":"主旨；要點；重點","s":"The main thrust of her speech was that students should spend less time on their phones and more time outdoors.","t":"她演講的主要重點是學生應該少花時間在手機上，多花時間在戶外。"},{"w":"tick","p":"n.","d":"a mark (✓) that shows something is correct or done","c":"勾號；打勾記號","s":"The teacher put a red tick next to every correct answer, and I was happy to count twenty of them on my paper.","t":"老師在每個正確答案旁邊打了一個紅色勾，我很高興數到考卷上有二十個。","h":1},{"w":"tick","p":"v.","d":"to make a mark (✓) next to something on a list","c":"打勾","s":"Please tick the box at the bottom of the form if you want to receive our newsletter by email every month.","t":"如果你想每個月透過電子郵件收到我們的電子報，請在表格底部的方框打勾。"},{"w":"tick","p":"n.","d":"the short regular sound that a clock makes","c":"滴答聲","s":"The room was so quiet during the exam that I could hear every tick of the clock on the wall.","t":"考試期間教室非常安靜，我能聽到牆上時鐘的每一聲滴答。"},{"w":"tick off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to mark items on a list as done","c":"在清單上勾掉；逐項核對","s":"Before we leave for the camping trip, let's tick off everything on the packing list so that nothing is forgotten.","t":"出發去露營之前，我們把行李清單上的每一項都勾掉，這樣才不會忘記東西。"},{"w":"tile","p":"n.","d":"a flat, thin piece of baked clay or stone used to cover floors, walls, or roofs","c":"磁磚；瓦片","s":"Be careful in the bathroom, because the white floor tile becomes very slippery when it gets wet.","t":"在浴室裡要小心，因為白色的地板磁磚弄濕後會變得非常滑。","h":1},{"w":"tile","p":"v.","d":"to cover a surface with tiles","c":"鋪磁磚","s":"My father decided to tile the kitchen floor himself last summer, and it took him three whole weekends.","t":"我爸爸去年夏天決定自己鋪廚房地板的磁磚，花了他整整三個週末。"},{"w":"tiled","p":"adj.","d":"covered with tiles","c":"鋪了磁磚的","s":"The tiled roofs of the old temple shine bright orange in the morning sun, and tourists love to photograph them.","t":"古廟鋪瓦的屋頂在早晨的陽光下閃耀著明亮的橘色，遊客喜歡拍攝它們。"},{"w":"roof tile","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tile used to cover a roof","c":"屋瓦","s":"Strong winds blew several roof tiles off the house last night, so Dad will climb up and replace them this weekend.","t":"昨晚強風吹掉了房子的幾片屋瓦，所以爸爸這個週末會爬上去更換。","a":"roof tiles"},{"w":"tin","p":"n.","d":"a soft silver-colored metal","c":"錫","s":"Long ago, people mixed copper with tin to make bronze, which was strong enough for tools and weapons.","t":"很久以前，人們把銅和錫混合製成青銅，它堅固到足以製作工具和武器。","h":1},{"w":"tin","p":"n.","d":"a metal container for food or drink; a can","c":"罐頭；金屬罐","s":"We opened a tin of tomatoes and added it to the soup because we did not have any fresh ones at home.","t":"我們開了一罐番茄加進湯裡，因為家裡沒有新鮮的番茄。"},{"w":"tin foil","p":"n.phr.","d":"very thin metal sheet used to wrap food","c":"錫箔紙；鋁箔紙","s":"Wrap the fish in tin foil with some lemon and butter before you put it in the oven for twenty minutes.","t":"把魚和一些檸檬及奶油用錫箔紙包起來，再放進烤箱烤二十分鐘。"},{"w":"toll","p":"n.","d":"money you pay to use a road, bridge, or tunnel","c":"通行費；過路費","s":"Drivers must pay a toll of forty dollars to cross the new bridge, but the old road is still free.","t":"駕駛人必須支付四十元的通行費才能過新橋，但舊路仍然免費。","h":1},{"w":"toll","p":"n.","d":"the number of people killed or hurt in an accident or disaster","c":"（事故、災難的）傷亡人數","s":"The toll from the earthquake rose to over three hundred as rescue workers searched the fallen buildings for survivors.","t":"隨著救難人員在倒塌的建築中搜尋生還者，地震的傷亡人數上升到三百多人。"},{"w":"toll","p":"v.","d":"to ring a bell slowly, especially for a death","c":"（緩慢地）鳴鐘","s":"The church bells began to toll at noon to remember the soldiers who died in the war one hundred years ago.","t":"教堂的鐘在中午開始鳴響，以紀念一百年前在戰爭中陣亡的士兵。"},{"w":"take a toll on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause harm or damage over time","c":"對…造成損害","s":"Years of working at night took a toll on his health, and the doctor told him to find a daytime job as soon as possible.","t":"多年的夜班工作對他的健康造成了損害，醫生要他儘快找一份日班工作。","a":"took a toll on"},{"w":"death toll","p":"n.phr.","d":"the number of people killed in an accident, war, or disaster","c":"死亡人數","s":"The death toll from the flood is expected to rise, because many villages in the mountains still cannot be reached.","t":"洪水的死亡人數預計會上升，因為山區許多村莊仍然無法到達。"},{"w":"torch","p":"n.","d":"a stick with a flame at the end that gives light; a small electric light you carry","c":"火炬；火把；手電筒","s":"The villagers carried a burning torch through the dark streets during the festival, and children followed with lanterns.","t":"慶典期間，村民們舉著燃燒的火炬走過黑暗的街道，孩子們提著燈籠跟在後面。","h":1},{"w":"torch","p":"v.","d":"to set fire to something on purpose","c":"放火燒；縱火","s":"The police believe that someone tried to torch the empty shop last night, because they found matches and gasoline nearby.","t":"警方認為昨晚有人試圖縱火燒那間空店鋪，因為他們在附近發現了火柴和汽油。"},{"w":"Olympic torch","p":"n.phr.","d":"the flame carried from Greece to the city where the Olympic Games are held","c":"奧運聖火","s":"Thousands of people lined the streets to watch a famous runner carry the Olympic torch through the center of the city.","t":"數千人站在街道兩旁，觀看一位著名跑者舉著奧運聖火穿過市中心。"},{"w":"torment","p":"n.","d":"great physical or mental pain","c":"折磨；痛苦","s":"Waiting a whole month for the exam results was pure torment for her, and she checked the website ten times a day.","t":"等待整整一個月的考試成績對她來說是純粹的折磨，她每天查看網站十次。","h":1},{"w":"torment","p":"v.","d":"to make someone suffer greatly","c":"折磨；使痛苦","s":"The older boys used to torment him at school by hiding his bag and laughing when he could not find it.","t":"那些大男孩以前在學校常常折磨他，把他的書包藏起來，在他找不到時嘲笑他。"},{"w":"be tormented by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suffer greatly because of something","c":"受…折磨；飽受…之苦","s":"For years after the accident, the driver was tormented by the thought that he could have stopped the car in time.","t":"事故發生後多年，那位駕駛一直飽受「他本來可以及時停車」這個念頭的折磨。","a":"was tormented by"},{"w":"tournament","p":"n.","d":"a competition with many players or teams, in which the winner goes on to the next round","c":"錦標賽；聯賽","s":"Our school's basketball team will play in the national tournament next month, and the first game is against last year's champions.","t":"我們學校的籃球隊下個月將參加全國錦標賽，第一場比賽的對手是去年的冠軍。","h":1},{"w":"tennis tournament","p":"n.phr.","d":"a competition for tennis players","c":"網球錦標賽","s":"She won her first tennis tournament at the age of fourteen, beating players who were five or six years older.","t":"她十四歲時贏得了第一座網球錦標賽冠軍，擊敗了比她大五六歲的選手。"},{"w":"tour","p":"n.","d":"a journey to visit several places; a series of performances or games in different places","c":"旅行；巡迴（演出、比賽）","s":"The band is going on a world tour next year, and the first concert will be held in Taipei in March.","t":"這個樂團明年將進行世界巡迴演出，第一場演唱會將於三月在台北舉行。"},{"w":"toxic","p":"adj.","d":"poisonous; harmful to living things","c":"有毒的","s":"The smoke from burning plastic is highly toxic, so you should never burn garbage in your backyard.","t":"燃燒塑膠產生的煙是高度有毒的，所以你絕不應該在後院燒垃圾。","h":1},{"w":"toxic waste","p":"n.phr.","d":"poisonous material left over from factories","c":"有毒廢棄物","s":"The factory was fined ten million dollars for dumping toxic waste into the river that supplies the town with drinking water.","t":"這家工廠因為把有毒廢棄物倒入供應小鎮飲用水的河流而被罰款一千萬元。"},{"w":"toxin","p":"n.","d":"a poisonous substance, especially one made by living things","c":"毒素","s":"Some fish contain a powerful toxin that can kill a person, so only trained chefs are allowed to prepare them.","t":"有些魚含有能致人於死的強烈毒素，所以只有受過訓練的廚師才可以料理牠們。"},{"w":"non-toxic","p":"adj.","d":"not poisonous; safe","c":"無毒的","s":"These crayons are non-toxic, so parents do not have to worry if their small children put them in their mouths.","t":"這些蠟筆是無毒的，所以如果小孩把它們放進嘴裡，父母不必擔心。"},{"w":"trait","p":"n.","d":"a particular quality in someone's character or in a living thing","c":"特徵；特質；特點","s":"Honesty is the trait that I admire most in my best friend, because she always tells me the truth even when it hurts.","t":"誠實是我最欣賞我最好的朋友的特質，因為即使真相令人難受，她也總是對我說實話。","h":1},{"w":"personality trait","p":"n.phr.","d":"a quality that is part of someone's character","c":"人格特質；性格特徵","s":"Patience is an important personality trait for a teacher, because students do not always understand things the first time.","t":"耐心是老師重要的人格特質，因為學生並不總是第一次就能理解事情。"},{"w":"genetic trait","p":"n.phr.","d":"a quality passed from parents to children through genes","c":"遺傳特徵","s":"Eye color is a genetic trait, which is why two brown-eyed parents usually have children with brown eyes too.","t":"眼睛的顏色是一種遺傳特徵，這就是為什麼兩個棕眼睛的父母通常也會生出棕眼睛的孩子。"},{"w":"traitor","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not loyal to their country, group, or friends","c":"叛徒；叛國者","s":"The general was called a traitor after he secretly sold his country's military plans to the enemy during the war.","t":"那位將軍在戰爭期間秘密把國家的軍事計畫賣給敵人後，被稱為叛徒。","h":1},{"w":"betray","p":"v.","d":"to hurt someone who trusts you by not being loyal to them","c":"背叛；出賣","s":"I would never betray my best friend by telling her secrets to other people, no matter how angry I was at her.","t":"無論我多生她的氣，我絕不會把最好的朋友的秘密告訴別人來背叛她。"},{"w":"betrayal","p":"n.","d":"the act of hurting someone who trusts you","c":"背叛；出賣","s":"Reading her private diary was a betrayal of trust, and it took months before she could forgive her brother.","t":"偷看她的私人日記是一種對信任的背叛，她花了好幾個月才原諒她的哥哥。"},{"w":"treason","p":"n.","d":"the crime of trying to harm your own country or its leader","c":"叛國罪","s":"In the past, anyone found guilty of treason was put to death, and even the king's closest friends were not safe.","t":"過去，任何被判叛國罪的人都會被處死，連國王最親近的朋友也不安全。"},{"w":"transaction","p":"n.","d":"the act of buying or selling something; a business deal","c":"交易；買賣","s":"You can see every transaction on your bank app within seconds, so check it carefully if your card is lost or stolen.","t":"你可以在幾秒內在銀行 App 上看到每一筆交易，所以如果卡片遺失或被偷，請仔細檢查。","h":1},{"w":"transact","p":"v.","d":"to do business, such as buying or selling","c":"交易；辦理（業務）","s":"Many small companies now transact most of their business online, so they no longer need an office in the city center.","t":"許多小公司現在大部分業務都在網路上交易，所以不再需要市中心的辦公室。"},{"w":"business transaction","p":"n.phr.","d":"an act of buying or selling between companies or people","c":"商業交易","s":"Every business transaction over one million dollars must be reported to the government, which helps to stop criminals from hiding money.","t":"每筆超過一百萬元的商業交易都必須向政府申報，這有助於防止罪犯藏匿資金。"},{"w":"transformation","p":"n.","d":"a complete change in the form or appearance of something","c":"轉變；變革；改造","s":"The transformation of the old factory into a modern art museum took five years and cost the city over a billion dollars.","t":"把舊工廠改造成現代藝術博物館花了五年，耗費市政府超過十億元。","h":1},{"w":"transform","p":"v.","d":"to change something completely, usually in a good way","c":"使徹底改變；改造","s":"A fresh coat of paint and some new furniture can transform a dark room into a bright and comfortable place to study.","t":"一層新油漆和一些新傢俱可以把一間昏暗的房間改造成明亮舒適的讀書空間。"},{"w":"transform into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change completely into something different","c":"轉變成；變成","s":"Over the summer, the shy boy seemed to transform into a confident young man who could speak in front of hundreds of people.","t":"經過一個夏天，這個害羞的男孩似乎變成了一個能在數百人面前演講的自信年輕人。"},{"w":"transit","p":"n.","d":"the movement of people or goods from one place to another","c":"運輸；運送；過境","s":"Passengers who are only in transit through the airport do not need a visa, as long as they stay inside the building.","t":"只是在機場過境的旅客不需要簽證，只要他們待在航廈內。","h":1},{"w":"in transit","p":"phr.","d":"being moved from one place to another","c":"運送途中；在途中","s":"Your package is currently in transit and should arrive at your door within two working days, according to the website.","t":"根據網站的資訊，你的包裹目前在運送途中，應該會在兩個工作天內送到你家門口。"},{"w":"mass transit","p":"n.phr.","d":"public transportation such as buses and trains that carry many people","c":"大眾運輸","s":"The city is spending billions on mass transit so that fewer people will drive to work and the air will be cleaner.","t":"市政府正花費數十億在大眾運輸上，這樣就會有更少的人開車上班，空氣也會更乾淨。"},{"w":"transition","p":"n.","d":"the process of changing from one state or condition to another","c":"過渡；轉變；轉換","s":"The transition from elementary school to junior high was hard for me, because suddenly I had seven different teachers.","t":"從國小到國中的過渡期對我來說很難，因為突然間我有七個不同的老師。","h":1},{"w":"transition to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change gradually to a new state or way of doing things","c":"轉變為；過渡到","s":"Many companies decided to transition to a four-day work week last year, and most of their workers say they are happier now.","t":"許多公司去年決定轉變為每週工作四天，他們大多數的員工說現在更快樂了。"},{"w":"transitional","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a change from one state to another","c":"過渡性的；過渡期的","s":"The new government will serve for a transitional period of six months before the country holds its first free election.","t":"新政府將在國家舉行第一次自由選舉之前，先執政六個月的過渡期。"},{"w":"transmission","p":"n.","d":"the act of passing something from one person or place to another, such as a disease or a message","c":"傳播；傳染；傳送","s":"Washing your hands often is the easiest way to stop the transmission of the virus from one person to another.","t":"經常洗手是阻止病毒在人與人之間傳播最簡單的方法。","h":1},{"w":"transmit","p":"v.","d":"to send a signal or message; to pass a disease to someone","c":"傳送；傳播；傳染","s":"The satellite can transmit a television signal to every home on the island within a fraction of a second.","t":"這顆衛星可以在不到一秒的時間內把電視訊號傳送到島上的每個家庭。"},{"w":"transmitter","p":"n.","d":"a piece of equipment that sends out radio or television signals","c":"發射器；發射機","s":"The radio station built a taller transmitter on the hill, so people in the valley can finally hear its programs clearly.","t":"電台在山丘上建了一座更高的發射器，所以山谷裡的人終於能清楚聽到它的節目。"},{"w":"transmission","p":"n.","d":"the part of a car that carries power from the engine to the wheels","c":"變速箱；傳動裝置","s":"The mechanic said the transmission in my old car needs to be replaced, and the repair will cost more than the car is worth.","t":"技師說我那輛舊車的變速箱需要更換，而修理費會比車子本身的價值還高。"},{"w":"transparent","p":"adj.","d":"clear enough to see through","c":"透明的","s":"The restaurant uses transparent boxes for its cakes, so customers can see exactly what they are buying before they pay.","t":"這家餐廳的蛋糕使用透明的盒子，所以顧客在付錢前就能清楚看到自己買的東西。","h":1},{"w":"transparent","p":"adj.","d":"open and honest, with nothing hidden","c":"公開透明的；坦率的","s":"Voters want the government to be more transparent about how it spends their tax money every year.","t":"選民希望政府對每年如何使用他們的稅金更加公開透明。"},{"w":"transparency","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being open and honest; the quality of being easy to see through","c":"透明度；公開透明","s":"The charity publishes a full report every year to ensure transparency, so donors know exactly where their money goes.","t":"這個慈善機構每年發布完整報告以確保透明度，讓捐款人清楚知道他們的錢去了哪裡。"},{"w":"trauma","p":"n.","d":"a very bad experience that causes lasting emotional pain; a serious injury","c":"精神創傷；創傷","s":"Losing their home in the fire was a terrible trauma for the children, and they still have bad dreams about it.","t":"在火災中失去家園對孩子們來說是可怕的創傷，他們現在仍會做關於它的惡夢。","h":1},{"w":"traumatic","p":"adj.","d":"causing great emotional pain that lasts a long time","c":"造成創傷的；令人痛苦的","s":"The car accident was so traumatic for my aunt that she did not drive again for almost three years.","t":"那場車禍對我阿姨來說創傷太大，以至於她將近三年沒有再開車。"},{"w":"traumatize","p":"v.","d":"to shock and upset someone so badly that it affects them for a long time","c":"使受到精神創傷","s":"Seeing the earthquake destroy their school seemed to traumatize some of the younger students, so counselors were sent to help them.","t":"看到地震摧毀學校似乎使一些年幼的學生受到創傷，所以學校派了輔導人員去幫助他們。"},{"w":"treaty","p":"n.","d":"a formal written agreement between two or more countries","c":"條約；協定","s":"The two countries signed a treaty in 1895 that gave the island to Japan for the next fifty years.","t":"兩國在一八九五年簽署了一項條約，把這座島交給日本統治接下來的五十年。","h":1},{"w":"peace treaty","p":"n.phr.","d":"an agreement that ends a war between countries","c":"和平條約","s":"After four years of fighting, the leaders finally met in Paris to sign a peace treaty and end the terrible war.","t":"經過四年的戰鬥，領導人終於在巴黎會面，簽署和平條約以結束那場可怕的戰爭。"},{"w":"sign a treaty","p":"v.phr.","d":"to formally agree to a written agreement between countries","c":"簽署條約","s":"More than one hundred countries signed a treaty promising to cut their carbon emissions in half by the year 2050.","t":"一百多個國家簽署了一項條約，承諾在二○五○年前將碳排放減半。","a":"signed a treaty"},{"w":"tribute","p":"n.","d":"something you say or do to show respect or admiration for someone","c":"致敬；讚頌；悼念","s":"The concert was a tribute to the famous singer who died last year, and many of her old friends performed her songs.","t":"這場演唱會是對去年過世的知名歌手的致敬，她的許多老朋友演唱了她的歌。","h":1},{"w":"pay tribute to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show respect or admiration for someone publicly","c":"向…致敬；讚揚","s":"At the ceremony, the mayor paid tribute to the firefighters who saved more than fifty people from the burning hotel.","t":"在典禮上，市長向從燃燒的飯店中救出五十多人的消防員致敬。","a":"paid tribute to"},{"w":"tribute","p":"n.","d":"money or goods that one country or ruler had to pay to a more powerful one in the past","c":"貢品；貢金","s":"In ancient times, smaller kingdoms sent gold, silk, and horses as tribute to the emperor every single year.","t":"古代，較小的王國每年都要把黃金、絲綢和馬匹作為貢品送給皇帝。"}]},{"unit":38,"theme":"trigger – utilize","cards":[{"w":"trigger","p":"v.","d":"to make something start to happen","c":"引發；觸發","s":"Loud noises and bright lights can trigger a terrible headache for my mother, so she always avoids crowded night markets.","t":"吵雜的聲音和刺眼的燈光會引發我媽媽劇烈的頭痛，所以她總是避開擁擠的夜市。","h":1},{"w":"trigger","p":"n.","d":"the part of a gun that you pull to fire it","c":"扳機","s":"The police officer kept his finger away from the trigger of his gun until he was sure the man was dangerous.","t":"那位警察一直讓手指遠離槍的扳機，直到他確定那個男人是危險的。"},{"w":"trigger","p":"n.","d":"something that causes another thing to happen","c":"誘因；導火線","s":"Doctors believe that stress was the main trigger for his skin problem, so they told him to rest more and exercise often.","t":"醫生認為壓力是他皮膚問題的主要誘因，所以要他多休息、常運動。"},{"w":"pull the trigger","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fire a gun; to finally make a difficult decision","c":"扣扳機；（終於）做出決定","s":"The hunter waited for the deer to come closer, but in the end he could not pull the trigger because it looked so beautiful.","t":"獵人等著鹿靠近，但最後他無法扣下扳機，因為那隻鹿看起來太美了。"},{"w":"trim","p":"v.","d":"to cut a small amount off something to make it neat","c":"修剪","s":"My father uses a pair of big scissors to trim the bushes in front of our house every two or three weeks in summer.","t":"夏天時，我爸爸每兩三週就用一把大剪刀修剪我們家門前的灌木。","h":1},{"w":"trim","p":"n.","d":"a short haircut that makes your hair neat","c":"修剪（頭髮）","s":"I don't want a new hairstyle; I just need a quick trim because my hair is starting to cover my eyes.","t":"我不想換新髮型，我只需要快速修剪一下，因為我的頭髮開始遮住眼睛了。"},{"w":"trim","p":"adj.","d":"thin, healthy, and in good shape","c":"苗條的；健美的","s":"My grandfather is still trim and strong at seventy because he swims every morning and never eats fried food.","t":"我爺爺七十歲了仍然身材精瘦又強壯，因為他每天早上游泳，而且從不吃油炸食物。"},{"w":"trim","p":"v.","d":"to reduce the amount of money, time, or workers","c":"削減；縮減","s":"The company had to trim its budget by ten percent this year, so there will be no big year-end party for the workers.","t":"公司今年必須把預算削減百分之十，所以今年不會為員工舉辦盛大的尾牙。"},{"w":"triple","p":"v.","d":"to become three times as large or many","c":"增至三倍","s":"The number of tourists visiting the small town has tripled since the famous movie was filmed there three years ago.","t":"自從那部知名電影三年前在那裡拍攝以來，造訪這個小鎮的觀光客人數已經增加到三倍。","a":"tripled","h":1},{"w":"triple","p":"adj.","d":"three times as much or as many; having three parts","c":"三倍的；三重的","s":"The new stadium is triple the size of the old one, so it can hold over sixty thousand fans for a big game.","t":"新體育場是舊體育場的三倍大，所以大型比賽時可以容納超過六萬名球迷。"},{"w":"triple","p":"n.","d":"in baseball, a hit that lets the batter reach third base","c":"三壘安打","s":"The batter hit a triple in the last inning, running all the way to third base while the crowd cheered loudly.","t":"打者在最後一局擊出一支三壘安打，一路跑上三壘，觀眾大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"triplets","p":"n.","d":"three children born to the same mother at the same time","c":"三胞胎","s":"My aunt gave birth to triplets last month, so now she has three baby girls who look exactly the same.","t":"我阿姨上個月生了三胞胎，所以現在她有三個長得一模一樣的女嬰。"},{"w":"threefold","p":"adv.","d":"by three times as much","c":"三倍地","s":"Sales of electric scooters in Taipei have increased threefold in the past five years, and gas scooters are becoming less popular.","t":"台北電動機車的銷量在過去五年增加了三倍，燃油機車越來越不受歡迎。"},{"w":"trivial","p":"adj.","d":"not important or serious","c":"瑣碎的；微不足道的","s":"Please don't call me during the meeting about trivial problems like a missing pen; only call if something serious happens.","t":"開會時請不要為了像少一枝筆這種瑣碎的問題打電話給我，只有發生嚴重的事才打。","h":1},{"w":"trivia","p":"n.","d":"small facts that are not important; facts used in quiz games","c":"瑣事；冷知識","s":"My brother loves trivia and can tell you how many bones are in a cat's body or how tall Taipei 101 is.","t":"我哥哥熱愛冷知識，他可以告訴你貓的身體有幾根骨頭，或台北101有多高。"},{"w":"trivialize","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem less important than it really is","c":"輕視；使顯得微不足道","s":"We should never trivialize the problem of bullying, because even small jokes can hurt a student's feelings for years.","t":"我們絕不應該輕忽霸凌問題，因為即使是小小的玩笑也可能傷害學生的感受好幾年。"},{"w":"trophy","p":"n.","d":"a cup or other object given as a prize for winning","c":"獎盃","s":"Our team lifted the shining trophy above their heads after winning the national championship for the first time in twenty years.","t":"我們的隊伍二十年來首次贏得全國冠軍後，把閃亮的獎盃高舉過頭。","h":1},{"w":"trophy","p":"n.","d":"something you keep to show that you were successful, especially in hunting or war","c":"戰利品；紀念品","s":"The hunter kept the deer's horns on his wall as a trophy, but his daughter thought it was cruel and asked him to remove them.","t":"獵人把鹿角掛在牆上當作戰利品，但他女兒覺得很殘忍，要他拿下來。"},{"w":"trophy case","p":"n.phr.","d":"a glass cupboard where prizes are shown","c":"獎盃櫃；獎盃展示櫃","s":"The school's trophy case in the main hall is full of cups and medals won by students over the past fifty years.","t":"學校大廳的獎盃櫃裡擺滿了學生過去五十年來贏得的獎盃和獎牌。"},{"w":"tuition","p":"n.","d":"the money you pay to a school or university for teaching","c":"學費","s":"Private university tuition has risen sharply in recent years, so many students have to work part-time to pay for their studies.","t":"私立大學的學費近年來大幅上漲，所以許多學生必須打工來支付學業費用。","h":1},{"w":"tuition","p":"n.","d":"teaching, especially to one person or a small group","c":"教學；講授；家教","s":"She receives private tuition in math twice a week, and her test scores have improved a lot since last semester.","t":"她每週接受兩次數學個別教學，從上學期以來她的考試成績進步了很多。"},{"w":"tuition fees","p":"n.phr.","d":"the money paid for a course or for studying at a school","c":"學費","s":"The tuition fees for this summer English course are twelve thousand dollars, which include all the books and a field trip.","t":"這個暑期英文課程的學費是一萬兩千元，包含所有書籍和一次校外教學。"},{"w":"tumor","p":"n.","d":"a mass of cells growing in the body that should not be there","c":"腫瘤","s":"The doctor found a small tumor in her lung during a health check, but luckily it was removed before it could spread.","t":"醫生在健康檢查時發現她肺部有一個小腫瘤，幸好在擴散之前就切除了。","h":1},{"w":"brain tumor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tumor that grows in the brain","c":"腦瘤","s":"After the operation to remove his brain tumor, my uncle had to learn how to walk and speak clearly again.","t":"在切除腦瘤的手術之後，我叔叔必須重新學習走路和清楚地說話。"},{"w":"benign tumor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tumor that is not cancer and will not spread","c":"良性腫瘤","s":"The test results showed that the lump was a benign tumor, which means it is not cancer and will not spread to other parts.","t":"檢查結果顯示那個腫塊是良性腫瘤，這表示它不是癌症，也不會擴散到其他部位。"},{"w":"tuna","p":"n.","d":"a large sea fish, or its meat used as food","c":"鮪魚","s":"For lunch I usually make a tuna sandwich with some lettuce and tomatoes, because it is quick, cheap, and healthy.","t":"午餐時我通常做一個加些生菜和番茄的鮪魚三明治，因為它快速、便宜又健康。","h":1},{"w":"canned tuna","p":"n.phr.","d":"tuna meat sold in a metal can","c":"鮪魚罐頭","s":"Students living in dorms often buy canned tuna because it does not need a refrigerator and can be eaten with rice.","t":"住在宿舍的學生常常買鮪魚罐頭，因為它不需要冰箱，而且可以配飯吃。"},{"w":"bluefin tuna","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very large kind of tuna with blue on its back","c":"黑鮪魚","s":"Every spring, fishermen in Donggang hope to catch a giant bluefin tuna, which can sell for more than one million dollars.","t":"每年春天，東港的漁民都希望捕到一條巨大的黑鮪魚，牠可以賣到超過一百萬元。"},{"w":"ultimate","p":"adj.","d":"final; happening at the end of a long process","c":"最終的；終極的","s":"Winning an Olympic gold medal is the ultimate goal of every athlete on our national team, and they train six hours a day.","t":"贏得奧運金牌是我們國家隊每位選手的最終目標，他們每天訓練六個小時。","h":1},{"w":"ultimate","p":"adj.","d":"the best, biggest, or most extreme of its kind","c":"極致的；最好的","s":"This new phone is advertised as the ultimate camera for travelers, but I think my old one still takes better pictures.","t":"這支新手機被宣傳為旅行者的最佳相機，但我覺得我的舊手機還是拍得比較好。"},{"w":"ultimately","p":"adv.","d":"in the end; finally","c":"最後；最終","s":"We argued about where to go on vacation for weeks, but ultimately we decided to stay home and save our money.","t":"我們為了去哪裡度假爭論了好幾個星期，但最後我們決定待在家裡存錢。"},{"w":"uncover","p":"v.","d":"to discover something that was secret or hidden","c":"揭露；發現","s":"The reporter worked for months to uncover the truth about the company, which had been dumping waste into the river at night.","t":"那位記者花了好幾個月揭露那家公司的真相，原來它一直在夜裡把廢棄物倒進河裡。","h":1},{"w":"uncover","p":"v.","d":"to remove the cover from something","c":"揭開…的蓋子","s":"You should uncover the pot and stir the soup every ten minutes, or the vegetables at the bottom will burn.","t":"你應該每十分鐘掀開鍋蓋攪拌一下湯，否則底部的蔬菜會燒焦。"},{"w":"cover up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to hide a mistake or crime so people do not find out","c":"掩蓋；隱瞞","s":"The manager tried to cover up the mistake, but one of the workers told the newspaper what had really happened.","t":"經理試圖掩蓋這個錯誤，但其中一名員工把真正發生的事告訴了報社。"},{"w":"undergo, underwent, undergone","p":"v.","d":"to experience something, especially something difficult or necessary","c":"經歷；接受（手術、檢查等）","s":"My grandmother will undergo surgery on her knee next week, and the doctor says she will need a month to recover.","t":"我奶奶下週要接受膝蓋手術，醫生說她需要一個月才能康復。","a":"undergo","h":1},{"w":"undergo changes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change a lot","c":"經歷變化","s":"Our small town has undergone changes since the high-speed railway station opened, with new hotels, shops, and restaurants everywhere.","t":"自從高鐵站開通以來，我們的小鎮經歷了許多變化，到處都是新的飯店、商店和餐廳。","a":"undergone changes"},{"w":"go through","p":"v.phr.","d":"to experience a difficult situation or process","c":"經歷；經過","s":"Every new pilot must go through months of hard training before he or she is allowed to fly a passenger plane.","t":"每位新飛行員都必須經歷數個月的嚴格訓練，才被允許駕駛客機。"},{"w":"undergraduate","p":"n.","d":"a university student who is studying for a first degree","c":"大學生；大學部學生","s":"As an undergraduate, my cousin studied chemistry, but after graduating she decided to become a high school teacher instead.","t":"身為大學部學生時，我表姊讀的是化學，但畢業後她決定改當高中老師。","h":1},{"w":"undergraduate","p":"adj.","d":"connected with students studying for a first degree","c":"大學部的","s":"The university offers more than fifty undergraduate programs, and students can change their major after the first year.","t":"這所大學提供五十多個大學部學程，學生在第一年之後可以轉系。"},{"w":"graduate","p":"n.","d":"a person who has finished a degree at a university or school","c":"畢業生","s":"Every year, the company hires about twenty new university graduates and trains them for six months before giving them real work.","t":"這家公司每年雇用大約二十名大學應屆畢業生，先培訓六個月再交付正式工作。","a":"graduates"},{"w":"graduate school","p":"n.phr.","d":"a part of a university where students study for a master's degree or PhD","c":"研究所","s":"After finishing college, she plans to go to graduate school in the United States to get a master's degree in education.","t":"大學畢業後，她打算去美國讀研究所，取得教育碩士學位。"},{"w":"underline","p":"v.","d":"to draw a line under a word or sentence","c":"在…下面畫線","s":"While you read the article, please underline any words you don't know, and we will look them up together later.","t":"你閱讀這篇文章時，請在任何不認識的字下面畫線，我們等一下一起查。","h":1},{"w":"underline","p":"v.","d":"to show clearly that something is important","c":"強調；突顯","s":"The terrible accident seemed to underline the need for stricter rules about drinking and driving in our country.","t":"這起可怕的意外似乎突顯了我國需要更嚴格的酒駕規定。"},{"w":"underline","p":"n.","d":"a line drawn under a word","c":"底線","s":"In this exercise, the words with an underline are the ones you need to change into the past tense.","t":"在這個練習中，有底線的字就是你需要改成過去式的字。"},{"w":"undermine","p":"v.","d":"to make someone or something weaker, often slowly","c":"逐漸削弱；暗中破壞","s":"Constant criticism from his coach began to undermine the young player's confidence, and he started making simple mistakes.","t":"教練不斷的批評開始削弱這位年輕球員的信心，他開始犯一些簡單的錯誤。","h":1},{"w":"undermine trust","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people trust each other less","c":"破壞信任","s":"Telling even small lies can undermine trust between friends, because people stop believing what you say.","t":"即使只是說小謊也可能破壞朋友之間的信任，因為別人會不再相信你說的話。"},{"w":"undermine","p":"v.","d":"to damage the ground under something so that it may fall","c":"侵蝕…的基礎；挖…的牆腳","s":"Years of heavy rain began to undermine the old wall by the river, and one day it suddenly fell into the water.","t":"多年的豪雨開始侵蝕河邊那道老牆的地基，有一天它突然倒進了水裡。"},{"w":"undertake, undertook, undertaken","p":"v.","d":"to agree to do or start a piece of work, especially a big one","c":"承擔；從事；著手","s":"The city will undertake a huge project to build a new subway line, which is expected to take eight years to finish.","t":"市政府將著手進行一項興建新捷運線的大型工程，預計需要八年才能完成。","a":"undertake","h":1},{"w":"undertaking","p":"n.","d":"a large or difficult piece of work","c":"任務；事業；工作","s":"Planning a wedding for three hundred guests is a huge undertaking, so many couples hire a professional to help them.","t":"為三百位賓客籌備婚禮是一項艱鉅的任務，所以許多新人會請專業人士幫忙。"},{"w":"undertake to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to promise to do something","c":"答應做；保證做","s":"The landlord undertook to fix the broken heater before winter, but it is December now and we are still cold.","t":"房東答應在冬天前修好壞掉的暖氣，但現在已經十二月了，我們還是很冷。","a":"undertook to"},{"w":"undo, undid, undone","p":"v.","d":"to open something that is tied or fastened","c":"解開","s":"My little brother cannot undo his shoelaces by himself yet, so he always asks me to help him after school.","t":"我弟弟還不會自己解開鞋帶，所以放學後他總是要我幫他。","a":"undo","h":1},{"w":"undo","p":"v.","d":"to cancel the effect of something you have done","c":"撤銷；取消；復原","s":"If you delete the wrong file by mistake, just press Control and Z to undo your last action on the computer.","t":"如果你不小心刪錯了檔案，只要按 Control 加 Z 就可以復原你在電腦上的上一個動作。"},{"w":"undone","p":"adj.","d":"not finished; not tied or fastened","c":"未完成的；鬆開的","s":"I left my homework undone last night because I fell asleep, so I had to finish it on the bus this morning.","t":"我昨晚睡著了，作業還沒做完，所以今天早上必須在公車上把它寫完。"},{"w":"undoubtedly","p":"adv.","d":"certainly; without any doubt","c":"無疑地；肯定地","s":"She is undoubtedly the best singer in our school, and everyone expects her to win the competition next week.","t":"她無疑是我們學校最好的歌手，大家都預料她下週會贏得比賽。","h":1},{"w":"doubt","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of not being sure about something","c":"懷疑；疑慮","s":"There is no doubt that exercise is good for your health, but many people still find it hard to start.","t":"運動對健康有益是毫無疑問的，但許多人仍然覺得很難開始。"},{"w":"doubtful","p":"adj.","d":"not sure; not likely to happen","c":"懷疑的；不太可能的","s":"The weather report says it will rain all weekend, so it is doubtful that the baseball game will be played on Saturday.","t":"氣象報告說整個週末都會下雨，所以星期六的棒球賽不太可能舉行。"},{"w":"doubtfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you are not sure","c":"懷疑地；不確定地","s":"She looked doubtfully at the old ladder before she climbed up, because two of its steps were already broken.","t":"她爬上去之前懷疑地看著那把舊梯子，因為它有兩階已經壞了。"},{"w":"unemployment","p":"n.","d":"the state of not having a job; the number of people without jobs","c":"失業；失業率","s":"The government is worried because unemployment among young people has risen to over twelve percent this year.","t":"政府很擔心，因為今年年輕人的失業率已經上升到百分之十二以上。","h":1},{"w":"unemployed","p":"adj.","d":"without a job","c":"失業的","s":"My uncle has been unemployed for six months since his factory closed, so he is taking computer classes to find new work.","t":"我叔叔自從工廠關閉後已經失業六個月了，所以他正在上電腦課以找新工作。"},{"w":"employment","p":"n.","d":"work that you are paid for; the act of giving someone a job","c":"就業；工作；僱用","s":"The new factory will provide employment for about five hundred local people, which is great news for this small town.","t":"新工廠將為大約五百名當地人提供工作機會，對這個小鎮來說是個好消息。"},{"w":"unemployment benefits","p":"n.phr.","d":"money the government gives to people who have lost their jobs","c":"失業救濟金","s":"After losing his job, he applied for unemployment benefits, which gave him some money each month while he looked for work.","t":"失去工作後，他申請了失業救濟金，讓他在找工作期間每個月有一些收入。"},{"w":"unfold","p":"v.","d":"to open something that was folded","c":"打開；展開（摺疊的東西）","s":"She sat down on the bench and began to unfold the map, trying to find the way to the old temple.","t":"她在長椅上坐下，開始攤開地圖，試著找出去那座古廟的路。","h":1},{"w":"unfold","p":"v.","d":"(of events or a story) to develop and become known","c":"（事件、故事）展開；逐漸呈現","s":"We watched the dramatic rescue unfold on live TV as firefighters climbed the tall building to save the trapped workers.","t":"我們在電視直播上看著那場驚險的救援逐漸展開，消防員爬上高樓營救受困的工人。"},{"w":"fold","p":"v.","d":"to bend something so that one part lies on top of another","c":"摺疊","s":"After drying the clothes, please fold them neatly and put them back in the closet instead of leaving them on the bed.","t":"衣服乾了之後，請把它們摺整齊放回衣櫥，而不是丟在床上。"},{"w":"unlock","p":"v.","d":"to open a lock with a key, code, or password","c":"開鎖；解鎖","s":"I forgot my password and could not unlock my phone, so I had to ask my brother to call the store for me.","t":"我忘記密碼，無法解鎖手機，所以只好請我哥哥幫我打電話給店家。","h":1},{"w":"unlock","p":"v.","d":"to discover or set free something that was hidden","c":"揭開（秘密）；釋放（潛力）","s":"Scientists hope the new study will unlock the secrets of how birds find their way home across thousands of kilometers.","t":"科學家希望這項新研究能揭開鳥類如何飛越數千公里找到回家路線的秘密。"},{"w":"unlocked","p":"adj.","d":"not locked","c":"未上鎖的","s":"Someone stole my bicycle last night because I left it unlocked outside the convenience store for only five minutes.","t":"昨晚有人偷了我的腳踏車，因為我把它沒上鎖地停在便利商店外面，只停了五分鐘。"},{"w":"unprecedented","p":"adj.","d":"never having happened or existed before","c":"前所未有的；空前的","s":"The heavy rain caused unprecedented flooding in the city, and some streets were under water for the first time in history.","t":"豪雨在市區造成前所未有的淹水，有些街道史上第一次被水淹沒。","h":1},{"w":"precedent","p":"n.","d":"an earlier event or decision that is used as an example later","c":"先例；前例","s":"There is no precedent for a case like this, so the judges will need to think very carefully before they decide.","t":"像這樣的案子沒有先例，所以法官們在判決之前必須非常仔細地思考。"},{"w":"set a precedent","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something that will be used as an example for the future","c":"開先例","s":"If we let one student hand in homework late without a reason, it will set a precedent and everyone will want the same.","t":"如果我們讓一個學生沒有理由就遲交作業，這會開先例，大家都會想要同樣的待遇。"},{"w":"update","p":"v.","d":"to make something more modern; to add the newest information","c":"更新","s":"Remember to update the apps on your phone regularly, because new versions often fix security problems.","t":"記得定期更新手機上的應用程式，因為新版本常會修正安全性問題。","h":1},{"w":"update","p":"n.","d":"the newest information about something","c":"最新消息；更新","s":"The teacher gave us an update on the class trip: the bus will leave at seven, not eight, on Friday morning.","t":"老師告訴我們校外教學的最新消息：遊覽車星期五早上七點出發，不是八點。"},{"w":"up to date","p":"adj.phr.","d":"modern; having the newest information","c":"最新的；跟上時代的","s":"Our geography textbook is not up to date, because it still says that the population of Taiwan is about twenty million.","t":"我們的地理課本不是最新的，因為它還寫著台灣人口大約兩千萬。"},{"w":"upgrade","p":"v.","d":"to improve something or change it to a better kind","c":"升級；提升","s":"The airline decided to upgrade us to business class for free, because the economy seats on the flight were all full.","t":"航空公司決定免費把我們升等到商務艙，因為那班飛機的經濟艙座位都滿了。","h":1},{"w":"upgrade","p":"n.","d":"a change to a better or newer version","c":"升級；改良","s":"My laptop is very slow, so I'm planning to buy a memory upgrade instead of a whole new computer.","t":"我的筆電很慢，所以我打算買記憶體升級，而不是買一台全新的電腦。"},{"w":"downgrade","p":"v.","d":"to make something lower in importance, value, or rank","c":"降級；調降","s":"The company had to downgrade its sales forecast after fewer people bought the new phone than it had expected.","t":"在購買新手機的人比預期少之後，公司只好調降銷售預測。"},{"w":"utility","p":"n.","d":"a service such as water, gas, or electricity that people use every day","c":"公用事業；水電瓦斯","s":"The rent for the apartment is fifteen thousand dollars a month, but it does not include utilities such as water and electricity.","t":"這間公寓的租金一個月一萬五千元，但不包含水電等公用事業費用。","a":"utilities","h":1},{"w":"utility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being useful","c":"效用；實用性","s":"Many people question the utility of learning cursive writing today, since almost everything is typed on computers now.","t":"現在很多人質疑學習草寫的實用性，因為幾乎所有東西都是用電腦打字的。"},{"w":"utility bill","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bill you pay for water, gas, or electricity","c":"水電費帳單","s":"Our utility bill was much higher in August because we used the air conditioner all day during the heat wave.","t":"我們八月的水電費帳單高很多，因為熱浪期間我們整天開冷氣。"},{"w":"utilize","p":"v.","d":"to use something in an effective way","c":"利用；運用","s":"The farmers utilize rainwater to water their crops, which saves money and protects the river during dry seasons.","t":"農夫們利用雨水灌溉作物，這樣既省錢，又能在乾季保護河川。","h":1},{"w":"utilization","p":"n.","d":"the act of using something effectively","c":"利用；使用","s":"Better utilization of empty classrooms after school could give students more quiet places to study for their exams.","t":"放學後更妥善地利用空教室，可以讓學生有更多安靜的地方準備考試。"},{"w":"make use of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use something that is available","c":"利用；使用","s":"Students should make use of the school library more often, because it has thousands of books and free computers.","t":"學生應該更常利用學校圖書館，因為那裡有數千本書和免費的電腦。"}]},{"unit":39,"theme":"vacuum – volcano","cards":[{"w":"vacuum","p":"n.","d":"a space with no air or other gas in it","c":"真空","s":"Sound cannot travel through a vacuum, so astronauts working outside the space station must use radios to talk to each other.","t":"聲音無法在真空中傳播，所以在太空站外工作的太空人必須用無線電互相交談。","h":1},{"w":"vacuum","p":"v.","d":"to clean something with a vacuum cleaner","c":"用吸塵器清掃","s":"Could you please vacuum the living room carpet before our guests arrive? There are cookie crumbs everywhere.","t":"可以請你在客人到之前用吸塵器吸一下客廳地毯嗎？到處都是餅乾屑。"},{"w":"vacuum cleaner","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine that cleans floors by sucking up dirt","c":"吸塵器","s":"Our old vacuum cleaner is so noisy that the dog runs and hides under the bed every time my mother turns it on.","t":"我們家的舊吸塵器很吵，所以每次媽媽一打開，狗就跑去躲在床底下。"},{"w":"in a vacuum","p":"phr.","d":"separately, without being affected by other things","c":"孤立地；與外界隔絕地","s":"Students do not learn in a vacuum; their families, friends, and environment all affect how well they study.","t":"學生並不是在真空中學習的；他們的家人、朋友和環境都會影響他們的學習成效。"},{"w":"vague","p":"adj.","d":"not clear or detailed","c":"模糊的；含糊的","s":"The directions he gave us were so vague that we got lost twice and arrived at the party an hour late.","t":"他給我們的路線指示非常含糊，結果我們迷路兩次，晚了一個小時才到派對。","h":1},{"w":"vaguely","p":"adv.","d":"not clearly; slightly","c":"模糊地；隱約地","s":"I vaguely remember visiting this beach when I was four, but I can't remember who took me there.","t":"我隱約記得四歲時來過這個海灘，但我不記得是誰帶我來的。"},{"w":"vagueness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of not being clear","c":"含糊；不明確","s":"The vagueness of the new school rule confused many students, so the principal explained it again at the morning meeting.","t":"新校規的含糊不清讓許多學生感到困惑，所以校長在朝會上又解釋了一次。"},{"w":"valid","p":"adj.","d":"legally or officially acceptable; still able to be used","c":"有效的","s":"Your passport must be valid for at least six months after you arrive, or the airline will not let you get on the plane.","t":"你的護照在抵達後必須至少還有六個月有效期，否則航空公司不會讓你登機。","h":1},{"w":"valid","p":"adj.","d":"based on good reasons; reasonable","c":"合理的；站得住腳的","s":"You made a valid point about the price, so let's look for a cheaper hotel near the train station instead.","t":"你對價格提出了一個合理的看法，所以我們改找火車站附近比較便宜的旅館吧。"},{"w":"invalid","p":"adj.","d":"not legally or officially acceptable","c":"無效的","s":"The ticket was invalid because it was for last Saturday's show, so the staff did not let us into the theater.","t":"那張票是無效的，因為那是上週六演出的票，所以工作人員不讓我們進劇院。"},{"w":"validity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being legally acceptable or reasonable","c":"有效性；正確性","s":"The scientists questioned the validity of the study, because only twelve people took part in the experiment.","t":"科學家們質疑這項研究的可信度，因為只有十二個人參加了實驗。"},{"w":"variable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change often","c":"多變的；易變的","s":"The weather in the mountains is very variable, so bring a raincoat even if the sky looks clear in the morning.","t":"山上的天氣非常多變，所以即使早上看起來晴朗，也要帶雨衣。","h":1},{"w":"variation","p":"n.","d":"a change or difference in amount or level","c":"變化；差異","s":"There is a big variation in temperature between day and night in the desert, so travelers need both T-shirts and jackets.","t":"沙漠裡白天和晚上的溫度差異很大，所以旅客需要同時帶T恤和外套。","h":1},{"w":"variable","p":"n.","d":"a thing that can change, especially in an experiment","c":"變數；變因","s":"In our science experiment, the amount of sunlight was the only variable we changed; everything else stayed the same.","t":"在我們的科學實驗中，日照量是我們唯一改變的變因，其他一切都保持不變。"},{"w":"vary","p":"v.","d":"to be different in different situations; to change","c":"變化；不同","s":"Prices of hotel rooms vary a lot from season to season, so it is much cheaper to travel in winter.","t":"旅館房價隨季節變動很大，所以冬天旅行便宜得多。"},{"w":"various","p":"adj.","d":"of many different kinds","c":"各種的；各式各樣的","s":"The night market sells various kinds of snacks, from stinky tofu to bubble tea and grilled squid.","t":"夜市賣各式各樣的小吃，從臭豆腐到珍珠奶茶和烤魷魚都有。"},{"w":"variety","p":"n.","d":"a number of different types of things","c":"多樣化；種種","s":"A healthy diet should include a variety of fruits and vegetables, not just the ones you like best.","t":"健康的飲食應該包含各種蔬菜水果，而不只是你最喜歡的那幾種。"},{"w":"vein","p":"n.","d":"a tube in the body that carries blood to the heart","c":"靜脈；血管","s":"The nurse found a vein in my arm and took some blood for the test, which only took about thirty seconds.","t":"護理師在我手臂上找到一條靜脈，抽了一些血做檢查，只花了大約三十秒。","h":1},{"w":"vein","p":"n.","d":"a thin line on a leaf or an insect's wing","c":"葉脈；翅脈","s":"If you hold a leaf up to the sunlight, you can see each tiny vein that carries water to every part of it.","t":"如果你把一片葉子舉向陽光，就能看到每一條把水分送到葉子各處的細小葉脈。"},{"w":"vein","p":"n.","d":"a particular style or mood of speaking or writing","c":"風格；語氣","s":"The speaker started in a serious vein, but soon she was telling funny stories that made everyone laugh.","t":"講者一開始用嚴肅的語氣，但很快她就開始講讓大家哈哈大笑的有趣故事。"},{"w":"vendor","p":"n.","d":"a person who sells things, especially from a stall or cart","c":"小販；攤販；賣方","s":"The old vendor at the corner sells the best sweet potatoes in town, and there is always a long line in winter.","t":"街角那位老小販賣的是鎮上最好吃的地瓜，冬天總是大排長龍。","h":1},{"w":"street vendor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who sells food or goods on the street","c":"街頭小販","s":"Every evening, a street vendor sets up a small stand outside our school and sells fried chicken to hungry students.","t":"每天傍晚，一位街頭小販會在我們學校外面擺個小攤，賣炸雞給飢腸轆轆的學生。"},{"w":"vending machine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine that sells drinks or snacks when you put in money","c":"自動販賣機","s":"I put fifty dollars into the vending machine at the train station, but no drink came out and my money was gone.","t":"我在火車站投了五十元到自動販賣機裡，但飲料沒有掉出來，錢也不見了。"},{"w":"venture","p":"n.","d":"a new business or activity that involves risk","c":"冒險事業；新創事業","s":"Opening a coffee shop with her best friend was an exciting venture, but it also cost all of her savings.","t":"和最好的朋友一起開咖啡店是一項令人興奮的創業冒險，但也花光了她所有的積蓄。","h":1},{"w":"venture","p":"v.","d":"to go somewhere that may be dangerous or unknown","c":"冒險前往；大膽走進","s":"The children were told not to venture too far into the forest, because it gets dark very quickly in winter.","t":"孩子們被告知不要冒險走進森林太深，因為冬天天黑得很快。"},{"w":"joint venture","p":"n.phr.","d":"a business started by two or more companies together","c":"合資企業","s":"The two companies started a joint venture to build electric cars, sharing both the costs and the profits.","t":"這兩家公司成立了一家合資企業來製造電動車，共同分擔成本與分享利潤。"},{"w":"adventure","p":"n.","d":"an exciting and unusual experience","c":"冒險；奇遇","s":"Our trip across Australia in an old van was a real adventure, and we still laugh about the night we slept on the beach.","t":"我們開著一輛舊廂型車橫越澳洲的旅程是一場真正的冒險，我們到現在還會笑談睡在海灘上的那一晚。"},{"w":"venue","p":"n.","d":"the place where an event such as a concert or meeting happens","c":"場地；會場","s":"The venue for this year's school concert has changed from the gym to the city's cultural center because of the repairs.","t":"由於整修工程，今年學校音樂會的場地從體育館改到了市立文化中心。","h":1},{"w":"concert venue","p":"n.phr.","d":"a building or place where concerts are held","c":"演唱會場地","s":"The new concert venue in Kaohsiung can hold fifteen thousand people, and famous singers from all over Asia perform there.","t":"高雄新的演唱會場地可以容納一萬五千人，亞洲各地的知名歌手都在那裡表演。"},{"w":"wedding venue","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where a wedding or wedding party is held","c":"婚宴場地","s":"Finding a wedding venue in October was difficult, because many couples want to get married when the weather is cool.","t":"要在十月找到婚宴場地很困難，因為很多新人都想在天氣涼爽時結婚。"},{"w":"verbal","p":"adj.","d":"spoken, not written","c":"口頭的","s":"The landlord only gave us a verbal promise to fix the roof, so we asked him to write it down and sign it.","t":"房東只給了我們修屋頂的口頭承諾，所以我們請他寫下來並簽名。","h":1},{"w":"verbal","p":"adj.","d":"using words; connected with words","c":"言語的；文字的","s":"Shouting at people and calling them names is a kind of verbal bullying, and it can hurt as much as hitting.","t":"對人大吼和罵人是一種言語霸凌，它造成的傷害可能和打人一樣大。"},{"w":"verbally","p":"adv.","d":"in spoken words","c":"口頭上","s":"He agreed verbally to lend me his car for the weekend, but later he said he had never made such a promise.","t":"他口頭上答應週末借我車，但後來他說他從來沒有做過這樣的承諾。"},{"w":"nonverbal","p":"adj.","d":"not using words","c":"非言語的","s":"Smiling, nodding, and making eye contact are forms of nonverbal communication that show people you are listening.","t":"微笑、點頭和眼神接觸都是非言語的溝通方式，能讓別人知道你在聽。"},{"w":"verdict","p":"n.","d":"the official decision made in a court about whether someone is guilty","c":"判決；裁決","s":"After three days of discussion, the jury finally reached a verdict and found the man not guilty of the crime.","t":"經過三天的討論，陪審團終於做出裁決，判定那名男子無罪。","h":1},{"w":"verdict","p":"n.","d":"an opinion or judgment after trying or testing something","c":"意見；判斷；評價","s":"We tried the new beef noodle shop last night, and our verdict is that the soup is great but the noodles are too soft.","t":"我們昨晚去吃了那家新的牛肉麵店，我們的評價是湯很棒但麵太軟。"},{"w":"reach a verdict","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a final decision, especially in a court","c":"做出判決","s":"The judges could not reach a verdict on the first day, so they will meet again tomorrow morning to discuss the case.","t":"法官們第一天未能做出判決，所以他們明天早上會再開會討論這個案子。"},{"w":"version","p":"n.","d":"a form of something that is a little different from other forms","c":"版本","s":"The newest version of the game has better graphics, but my old computer is too slow to run it.","t":"這款遊戲的最新版本畫面更好，但我的舊電腦太慢跑不動。","h":1},{"w":"version","p":"n.","d":"one person's description of an event","c":"說法；描述","s":"Each of the two drivers told the police a different version of the accident, so the officer checked the street cameras.","t":"兩位駕駛各自向警方提出了不同的車禍說法，所以警員調閱了路口監視器。"},{"w":"English version","p":"n.phr.","d":"the form of a book or film that is in English","c":"英文版","s":"I read the English version of the novel first, and then I read the Chinese translation to compare the two.","t":"我先讀了這本小說的英文版，然後再讀中文譯本來比較兩者。"},{"w":"versus","p":"prep.","d":"against, in a sports game or competition","c":"對（比賽中）","s":"Tonight's baseball game is Taiwan versus Japan, and the tickets were sold out within ten minutes of going on sale.","t":"今晚的棒球賽是台灣對日本，門票開賣十分鐘內就賣光了。","h":1},{"w":"versus","p":"prep.","d":"compared with","c":"與…相比；相對於","s":"In English class today, we discussed the advantages of living in the city versus living in the countryside.","t":"今天英文課我們討論了住在城市相對於住在鄉下的優點。"},{"w":"against","p":"prep.","d":"competing with or fighting with","c":"對抗；與…對打","s":"Our school team will play against last year's champions next Saturday, so the coach has added two extra practices this week.","t":"我們校隊下週六要對上去年的冠軍，所以教練這週加了兩次練習。"},{"w":"unlike","p":"prep.","d":"different from","c":"不像；與…不同","s":"My cousin, unlike her shy older brother, loves talking to strangers and making new friends wherever she goes.","t":"我表妹不像她那害羞的哥哥，她無論到哪裡都喜歡和陌生人聊天、交新朋友。"},{"w":"vertical","p":"adj.","d":"pointing straight up from the ground","c":"垂直的；直立的","s":"The climbers stared at the vertical wall of rock in front of them and wondered how anyone could reach the top.","t":"登山者們盯著眼前垂直的岩壁，心想怎麼可能有人爬得到頂端。","h":1},{"w":"vertical","p":"n.","d":"a vertical line or position","c":"垂直線；垂直位置","s":"The old tower is leaning about four degrees from the vertical, and engineers are working hard to stop it from falling.","t":"那座古塔偏離垂直線大約四度，工程師們正努力防止它倒塌。"},{"w":"vertically","p":"adv.","d":"in an up-and-down direction","c":"垂直地；直立地","s":"Hold your phone vertically when you record videos for social media, because most people watch them that way.","t":"為社群媒體錄影片時要把手機直拿，因為大多數人都是那樣觀看的。"},{"w":"horizontal","p":"adj.","d":"flat and level with the ground","c":"水平的；橫的","s":"Draw a horizontal line across the middle of the page, and then write your name above it and the date below it.","t":"在頁面中間畫一條水平線，然後在線上面寫你的名字，下面寫日期。"},{"w":"veteran","p":"n.","d":"a person who has been a soldier, especially in a war","c":"退伍軍人；老兵","s":"My grandfather is a war veteran who still tells us stories about the years he spent as a soldier on Kinmen.","t":"我爺爺是一位戰爭老兵，他到現在還會跟我們講他在金門當兵那幾年的故事。","h":1},{"w":"veteran","p":"n.","d":"a person with a lot of experience in a job or activity","c":"老手；資深人員","s":"Mr. Lin is a veteran of the newspaper business who has worked as a reporter for more than thirty years.","t":"林先生是新聞界的老將，他當記者已經超過三十年了。"},{"w":"veteran","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of experience","c":"經驗豐富的；資深的","s":"The veteran pilot calmly landed the plane in the storm, and all the passengers clapped when the wheels touched the ground.","t":"那位經驗豐富的機長在暴風雨中冷靜地降落飛機，輪子一著地，所有乘客都鼓掌。"},{"w":"via","p":"prep.","d":"going through a place on the way to another place","c":"經由；取道","s":"We flew from Taipei to London via Dubai, where we stopped for three hours and walked around the huge airport.","t":"我們從台北經杜拜飛往倫敦，在那裡停留三個小時，逛了逛那座巨大的機場。","h":1},{"w":"via","p":"prep.","d":"by means of; using","c":"透過；藉由","s":"The teacher sent us the homework via email, so please check your inbox before you go to bed tonight.","t":"老師透過電子郵件寄作業給我們，所以今晚睡前請檢查你的收件匣。"},{"w":"via","p":"prep.","d":"with the help of a person","c":"透過（某人）","s":"I heard about the job via a friend who works at the company, and she helped me prepare for the interview.","t":"我是透過一位在那家公司上班的朋友得知這份工作的，她還幫我準備面試。"},{"w":"viable","p":"adj.","d":"able to work successfully; possible","c":"可行的","s":"Taking the train instead of driving is a viable way to save money, especially now that gas prices are so high.","t":"搭火車而不開車是一個省錢的可行方法，尤其是現在油價這麼高。","h":1},{"w":"viability","p":"n.","d":"the ability to work successfully","c":"可行性","s":"Before opening the restaurant, they studied the viability of the plan by asking hundreds of local people what they wanted.","t":"開餐廳之前，他們詢問了數百位當地居民的需求，來研究這個計畫的可行性。"},{"w":"viable option","p":"n.phr.","d":"a choice that can really work","c":"可行的選擇","s":"If the bridge is closed, the ferry is the only viable option for people who need to cross the river to get to work.","t":"如果橋封閉了，渡輪就是需要過河上班的人唯一可行的選擇。"},{"w":"vicious","p":"adj.","d":"violent and dangerous; wanting to hurt others","c":"兇猛的；兇殘的","s":"A vicious dog attacked the mailman yesterday, so the owner must now keep it on a leash at all times.","t":"昨天一隻兇猛的狗攻擊了郵差，所以現在主人必須隨時用狗鍊拴著牠。","h":1},{"w":"vicious","p":"adj.","d":"cruel and unkind in what you say","c":"惡毒的；惡意的","s":"Someone spread a vicious rumor about her online, and she was too upset to go to school for two days.","t":"有人在網路上散播關於她的惡毒謠言，她難過到兩天沒辦法去上學。"},{"w":"vicious circle","p":"n.phr.","d":"a situation in which one problem causes another, which makes the first one worse","c":"惡性循環","s":"Staying up late makes me tired in class, so I nap after school and then stay up late again; it's a vicious circle.","t":"熬夜讓我上課很累，所以我放學後睡午覺，然後又熬夜；這是一個惡性循環。"},{"w":"viciously","p":"adv.","d":"in a violent or cruel way","c":"兇狠地；惡毒地","s":"The two cats fought viciously in the alley last night, and one of them came home with a bleeding ear.","t":"那兩隻貓昨晚在巷子裡兇狠地打架，其中一隻回家時耳朵流著血。"},{"w":"viewer","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches television, a film, or a video","c":"觀眾；觀看者","s":"The final episode of the drama attracted over two million viewers, which is a record for a Taiwanese TV show.","t":"這部劇的最後一集吸引了超過兩百萬名觀眾，創下台灣電視節目的紀錄。","a":"viewers","h":1},{"w":"viewpoint","p":"n.","d":"a way of thinking about a subject","c":"觀點；看法","s":"Try to see the problem from your parents' viewpoint; they are worried because they love you, not because they want to control you.","t":"試著從你父母的觀點看這個問題；他們擔心是因為愛你，而不是想控制你。","h":1},{"w":"viewpoint","p":"n.","d":"a place from which you can see a beautiful view","c":"觀景點；瞭望點","s":"We stopped at a viewpoint halfway up the mountain to take photos of the sea of clouds below us.","t":"我們在半山腰的一個觀景點停下來，拍下方雲海的照片。"},{"w":"point of view","p":"n.phr.","d":"the position from which a story is told; an opinion","c":"觀點；角度","s":"The story is told from the point of view of a little dog, so readers see everything through his eyes.","t":"這個故事是從一隻小狗的觀點來敘述的，所以讀者透過牠的眼睛看到一切。"},{"w":"view","p":"n.","d":"what you can see from a place","c":"景色；視野","s":"Our hotel room had a beautiful view of the ocean, so we sat on the balcony and watched the sunset every evening.","t":"我們的飯店房間有美麗的海景，所以我們每天傍晚都坐在陽台上看夕陽。"},{"w":"vinegar","p":"n.","d":"a sour liquid used to flavor food","c":"醋","s":"Add a little vinegar and soy sauce to the dumplings, because the sour taste makes them even more delicious.","t":"在水餃裡加一點醋和醬油，因為酸味會讓它們更好吃。","h":1},{"w":"rice vinegar","p":"n.phr.","d":"vinegar made from rice","c":"米醋","s":"Japanese cooks usually mix rice vinegar with a little sugar and salt to give the rice for sushi its special taste.","t":"日本廚師通常會把米醋和少許糖、鹽混合，讓壽司飯有獨特的味道。"},{"w":"white vinegar","p":"n.phr.","d":"a clear vinegar, often used for cleaning or pickling","c":"白醋","s":"Many people clean their windows with water and white vinegar, because it is cheap and does not contain strong chemicals.","t":"許多人用水和白醋清洗窗戶，因為它便宜又不含強烈的化學物質。"},{"w":"virtual","p":"adj.","d":"made to look real by a computer; online","c":"虛擬的；線上的","s":"We took a virtual tour of the museum online, so we could see famous paintings without leaving our classroom.","t":"我們在線上參加了博物館的虛擬導覽，所以不用離開教室就能看到名畫。","h":1},{"w":"virtual","p":"adj.","d":"almost completely the thing described","c":"實際上的；事實上的；幾乎完全的","s":"The traffic jam brought the city to a virtual stop, and many people walked home instead of waiting for buses.","t":"塞車讓整座城市幾乎完全停擺，許多人走路回家而不等公車。"},{"w":"virtually","p":"adv.","d":"almost completely","c":"幾乎；差不多","s":"The new phone is virtually the same as the old one, so I don't understand why it costs five thousand dollars more.","t":"新手機和舊手機幾乎一模一樣，所以我不懂為什麼要貴五千元。"},{"w":"virtual reality","p":"n.phr.","d":"images and sounds made by a computer that seem real to the user","c":"虛擬實境","s":"Medical students now use virtual reality to practice difficult operations before they work on real patients.","t":"醫學系學生現在使用虛擬實境練習困難的手術，然後才在真正的病人身上操作。"},{"w":"visa","p":"n.","d":"an official mark in your passport that allows you to enter a country","c":"簽證","s":"Taiwanese tourists do not need a visa to visit Japan for less than ninety days, so many families travel there in summer.","t":"台灣遊客赴日本停留少於九十天不需要簽證，所以很多家庭夏天去那裡旅行。","h":1},{"w":"apply for a visa","p":"v.phr.","d":"to formally ask for permission to enter a country","c":"申請簽證","s":"My sister had to apply for a visa three months before she started studying at a university in the United States.","t":"我姊姊在到美國的大學就讀前三個月就必須申請簽證。"},{"w":"student visa","p":"n.phr.","d":"a visa that allows you to study in another country","c":"學生簽證","s":"With a student visa, you can study in the country, but you are usually only allowed to work twenty hours a week.","t":"持有學生簽證可以在該國讀書，但通常每週只允許工作二十小時。"},{"w":"vocal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the voice","c":"聲音的；嗓音的","s":"Singers must protect their vocal cords by drinking warm water and not shouting at noisy sporting events.","t":"歌手必須透過喝溫水和不在吵鬧的運動賽事中大喊來保護他們的聲帶。","h":1},{"w":"vocal","p":"adj.","d":"expressing opinions strongly and often","c":"直言不諱的；大聲疾呼的","s":"Parents have been very vocal about the dangerous crossing near the school, and they want the city to add a traffic light.","t":"家長們對學校附近危險的路口一直大聲疾呼，他們希望市政府加裝紅綠燈。"},{"w":"vocals","p":"n.","d":"the part of a piece of music that is sung","c":"（歌曲中的）演唱部分；人聲","s":"The band's new song has great guitar parts, but the vocals are too quiet, so it's hard to hear the words.","t":"這個樂團的新歌吉他部分很棒，但人聲太小聲，所以很難聽清楚歌詞。"},{"w":"vocalist","p":"n.","d":"a singer, especially in a band","c":"歌手；主唱","s":"She was the lead vocalist in a rock band in college, and now she teaches music at a junior high school.","t":"她大學時是一個搖滾樂團的主唱，現在在一所國中教音樂。"},{"w":"volcano","p":"n.","d":"a mountain with a hole at the top from which hot rock and gas sometimes come out","c":"火山","s":"The volcano in Iceland erupted last night, and thick smoke closed several airports in northern Europe.","t":"冰島的火山昨晚爆發，濃煙導致北歐好幾座機場關閉。","h":1},{"w":"volcanic","p":"adj.","d":"produced by or connected with a volcano","c":"火山的；火山引起的","s":"Yangmingshan was formed by volcanic activity long ago, which is why there are hot springs all over the area.","t":"陽明山是很久以前由火山活動形成的，這就是為什麼那一帶到處都有溫泉。"},{"w":"active volcano","p":"n.phr.","d":"a volcano that may erupt","c":"活火山","s":"Mount Fuji is still an active volcano, although it has not erupted for more than three hundred years.","t":"富士山仍然是一座活火山，雖然它已經超過三百年沒有噴發了。"},{"w":"erupt","p":"v.","d":"(of a volcano) to send out smoke, fire, and hot rock suddenly","c":"（火山）爆發；噴發","s":"Scientists warned that the mountain could erupt at any time, so everyone living nearby was told to leave their homes.","t":"科學家警告那座山隨時可能爆發，所以住在附近的每個人都被告知要離開家園。"}]},{"unit":40,"theme":"vomit – yield","cards":[{"w":"vomit","p":"v.","d":"to bring food from your stomach back out through your mouth","c":"嘔吐","s":"The little boy began to vomit after eating too much cake at the party, so his mother quickly took him to the bathroom.","t":"小男孩在派對上吃了太多蛋糕後開始嘔吐，所以他媽媽趕緊帶他去廁所。","h":1},{"w":"vomit","p":"n.","d":"food that has come back up from the stomach","c":"嘔吐物","s":"The bus driver had to stop and clean the vomit off the floor after a passenger got carsick on the mountain road.","t":"一名乘客在山路上暈車後，公車司機只好停車把地上的嘔吐物清乾淨。"},{"w":"throw up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to vomit (informal)","c":"吐；嘔吐","s":"The road to Alishan has so many curves that my sister always feels like she is going to throw up.","t":"去阿里山的路彎道太多，我妹妹總是覺得自己快要吐了。"},{"w":"voucher","p":"n.","d":"a printed paper that can be used instead of money to buy something","c":"代金券；禮券；票券","s":"I got a five-hundred-dollar voucher for my birthday, so I can buy any book I like at that bookstore.","t":"我生日時收到一張五百元的禮券，所以我可以在那家書店買任何我喜歡的書。","h":1},{"w":"gift voucher","p":"n.phr.","d":"a voucher given as a present","c":"禮券","s":"If you don't know what to buy for your teacher, a gift voucher for a nice restaurant is always a good choice.","t":"如果你不知道要送老師什麼，一張高級餐廳的禮券總是不錯的選擇。"},{"w":"coupon","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of paper that lets you pay less for something","c":"優惠券；折價券","s":"With this coupon, you can get a second cup of coffee for only ten dollars before eleven in the morning.","t":"憑這張優惠券，早上十一點以前第二杯咖啡只要十元。"},{"w":"vow","p":"v.","d":"to promise very seriously","c":"發誓；立誓","s":"After failing the math test, Tom decided to vow that he would study for at least two hours every night until the final exam.","t":"數學考試不及格後，湯姆決定發誓在期末考前每晚至少讀書兩小時。","h":1},{"w":"vow","p":"n.","d":"a serious promise","c":"誓言；誓約","s":"At the wedding, the bride and groom each made a vow in front of two hundred guests, promising to love each other forever.","t":"在婚禮上，新娘和新郎在兩百位賓客面前各自許下誓言，承諾永遠相愛。"},{"w":"break one's vow","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not do what you seriously promised","c":"違背誓言","s":"He promised never to smoke again, but he broke his vow only three weeks later at a friend's party.","t":"他承諾再也不抽菸，但僅僅三週後就在朋友的派對上違背了他的誓言。","a":"broke his vow"},{"w":"vulnerable","p":"adj.","d":"easily hurt physically or emotionally","c":"易受傷害的；脆弱的","s":"Old people and small children are more vulnerable to the flu, so they should get a flu shot every autumn.","t":"老人和小孩比較容易受到流感侵襲，所以他們每年秋天都應該打流感疫苗。","h":1},{"w":"vulnerability","p":"n.","d":"a weakness that makes something easy to attack or hurt","c":"弱點；脆弱性","s":"The hackers found a vulnerability in the bank's computer system and stole the personal information of thousands of customers.","t":"駭客在銀行的電腦系統中找到一個漏洞，偷走了數千名客戶的個人資料。"},{"w":"invulnerable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to hurt or damage","c":"刀槍不入的；無懈可擊的","s":"In the movie, the hero seems invulnerable, because bullets and fire never hurt him at all.","t":"在電影裡，主角似乎刀槍不入，因為子彈和火焰完全傷不了他。"},{"w":"warehouse","p":"n.","d":"a large building where goods are stored","c":"倉庫","s":"All the online orders are packed in a huge warehouse outside the city and then sent to customers by truck.","t":"所有網路訂單都在城外一座巨大的倉庫打包，然後用卡車送到顧客手上。","h":1},{"w":"warehouse","p":"v.","d":"to keep goods in a warehouse","c":"把…存放在倉庫","s":"The company warehouses its extra furniture in Taoyuan until the new store opens next spring.","t":"這家公司把多餘的家具存放在桃園的倉庫，直到明年春天新店開幕。","a":"warehouses"},{"w":"warehouse sale","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sale of goods at very low prices, often held in a warehouse","c":"倉庫拍賣；清倉特賣","s":"The shoe company is holding a warehouse sale this weekend, and everything is sold at half price or even less.","t":"這家鞋業公司這個週末舉辦倉庫特賣，所有商品都半價甚至更便宜。"},{"w":"warrior","p":"n.","d":"a brave soldier or fighter, especially in the past","c":"戰士；勇士","s":"In the old story, a brave warrior fought against a huge dragon to save the people of his village.","t":"在古老的故事裡，一位勇敢的戰士和一條巨龍搏鬥，拯救了他村子裡的人。","h":1},{"w":"war","p":"n.","d":"fighting between countries or groups using weapons","c":"戰爭","s":"My great-grandfather lived through the war and often told us how hard life was when there was not enough food.","t":"我曾祖父經歷過那場戰爭，常常告訴我們食物不夠吃時生活有多艱苦。"},{"w":"weekend warrior","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who does sports or hobbies very hard only on weekends","c":"週末運動族；週末戰士","s":"My dad is a weekend warrior; he sits at a desk all week but plays basketball for five hours every Saturday.","t":"我爸爸是個週末戰士；他整個星期都坐在辦公桌前，但每週六打五個小時的籃球。"},{"w":"wary","p":"adj.","d":"careful because you think something may be dangerous","c":"小心的；警惕的","s":"Be wary of strangers who call and say you have won a prize, because many of them are trying to steal your money.","t":"要提防那些打電話來說你中獎的陌生人，因為他們很多都想偷你的錢。","h":1},{"w":"warily","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful way, because of possible danger","c":"小心翼翼地；警惕地","s":"The cat looked warily at the new dog for a whole day before it finally came close enough to smell it.","t":"那隻貓警戒地盯著新來的狗看了一整天，最後才靠近到能聞牠的距離。"},{"w":"beware","p":"v.","d":"to be careful of something dangerous","c":"小心；提防","s":"Signs at the beach tell swimmers to beware of strong waves, especially when a typhoon is coming.","t":"海灘上的告示牌提醒泳客小心大浪，尤其是颱風快來的時候。"},{"w":"weird","p":"adj.","d":"very strange and unusual","c":"奇怪的；詭異的","s":"I heard a weird noise coming from the kitchen at midnight, but when I turned on the light, nothing was there.","t":"半夜我聽到廚房傳來奇怪的聲音，但我開燈時什麼也沒有。","h":1},{"w":"weirdly","p":"adv.","d":"in a strange way; strangely","c":"奇怪地；出奇地","s":"The streets were weirdly quiet on New Year's morning, because almost everyone was still asleep after the fireworks.","t":"元旦早上街道出奇地安靜，因為幾乎每個人看完煙火後都還在睡。"},{"w":"weirdo","p":"n.","d":"a person who behaves strangely (informal, not polite)","c":"怪人；怪胎","s":"Some classmates called him a weirdo because he wore a cape to school, but he didn't care at all.","t":"有些同學叫他怪胎，因為他穿披風來上學，但他一點也不在乎。"},{"w":"whatsoever","p":"adj.","d":"at all (used after a noun in negative sentences for emphasis)","c":"任何的；一點也（不）","s":"I have no interest whatsoever in horror movies, so please don't ask me to watch one with you.","t":"我對恐怖片一點興趣也沒有，所以請不要叫我陪你看。","h":1},{"w":"whatever","p":"pron.","d":"anything or everything","c":"任何事物；凡是…的東西","s":"You can order whatever you like from the menu tonight, because it's your birthday and I'm paying.","t":"今晚你可以從菜單上點任何你喜歡的東西，因為今天是你生日，我請客。"},{"w":"whatever","p":"adj.","d":"any; no matter what","c":"無論什麼樣的；任何的","s":"Please call me immediately if you have any problems, whatever time it is, even in the middle of the night.","t":"如果你有任何問題請馬上打給我，不管幾點，就算是半夜也可以。"},{"w":"none whatsoever","p":"phr.","d":"none at all","c":"完全沒有","s":"Did he show any regret for breaking the window? No, none whatsoever; he just laughed and walked away.","t":"他打破窗戶有表現出任何悔意嗎？不，完全沒有；他只是笑一笑就走了。"},{"w":"wheelchair","p":"n.","d":"a chair with wheels for people who cannot walk","c":"輪椅","s":"After he broke his leg, my grandfather had to use a wheelchair for two months, so we pushed him around the park every day.","t":"爺爺摔斷腿後必須坐兩個月的輪椅，所以我們每天推他在公園裡散步。","h":1},{"w":"wheelchair-accessible","p":"adj.","d":"easy for people in wheelchairs to enter and use","c":"無障礙的；輪椅可通行的","s":"All new MRT stations must be wheelchair-accessible, with elevators and wide doors for people who cannot walk.","t":"所有新的捷運站都必須是無障礙的，要有電梯和寬大的門給無法行走的人使用。"},{"w":"wheel","p":"n.","d":"a round object that turns to help a vehicle move","c":"輪子；車輪","s":"One wheel of my suitcase broke at the airport, so I had to carry the heavy bag up the stairs.","t":"我的行李箱有一個輪子在機場壞掉了，所以我只好把沉重的箱子扛上樓梯。"},{"w":"whereabouts","p":"n.","d":"the place where someone or something is","c":"下落；行蹤","s":"The police are still trying to find out the whereabouts of the missing hiker, who was last seen near the top of the mountain.","t":"警方仍在設法查出失蹤登山客的下落，他最後一次被看到是在山頂附近。","h":1},{"w":"whereabouts","p":"adv.","d":"in or near what place (used in questions)","c":"在哪裡；大概在什麼地方","s":"Excuse me, whereabouts in Taipei do you live? I'm also from the north, so I might know your neighborhood.","t":"不好意思，你住在台北哪一帶？我也是北部人，所以可能知道你住的社區。"},{"w":"wherever","p":"conj.","d":"in any place; to any place","c":"無論何處；不管到哪裡","s":"My little dog follows me wherever I go, even into the bathroom, because she does not like to be alone.","t":"我的小狗不管我到哪裡都跟著我，連進廁所也是，因為牠不喜歡獨處。"},{"w":"whereas","p":"conj.","d":"used to compare two different facts or situations","c":"然而；而","s":"My older sister loves spicy food, whereas I can't eat even a little chili without drinking a lot of water.","t":"我姊姊很愛吃辣，而我連一點點辣椒都吃不了，一吃就得喝很多水。","h":1},{"w":"while","p":"conj.","d":"used to show a difference between two things","c":"而；然而","s":"Some students prefer to study in the library, while others like to study at home with music on.","t":"有些學生喜歡在圖書館讀書，而其他人喜歡在家一邊聽音樂一邊讀。"},{"w":"whenever","p":"conj.","d":"every time that; at any time that","c":"每當；無論何時","s":"My grandmother makes my favorite beef soup whenever I visit her, even if it is a hot summer day.","t":"每當我去看奶奶時，她都會煮我最愛的牛肉湯，就算是大熱天也一樣。"},{"w":"whether","p":"conj.","d":"used to talk about a choice between two things","c":"是否；究竟是…還是…","s":"I can't decide whether to join the basketball team or the school band, because practice for both is on Friday.","t":"我無法決定要參加籃球隊還是學校樂隊，因為兩者都在星期五練習。"},{"w":"whine","p":"v.","d":"to complain in an annoying way","c":"抱怨；發牢騷","s":"Stop whining about the homework and just start doing it; you will finish faster if you stop complaining.","t":"別再抱怨作業了，趕快開始寫；不再發牢騷的話你會更快寫完。","a":"whining","h":1},{"w":"whine","p":"v.","d":"(of a dog) to make a long high sad sound","c":"（狗）嗚咽；哀鳴","s":"Our puppy began to whine at the door because she wanted to go outside for a walk.","t":"我們的小狗開始在門口嗚嗚叫，因為牠想出去散步。"},{"w":"whine","p":"n.","d":"a long high unpleasant sound","c":"嗡嗡聲；哀鳴聲","s":"I could hear the high whine of a mosquito near my ear all night, so I didn't sleep well at all.","t":"我整晚都聽到耳邊蚊子尖細的嗡嗡聲，所以我完全沒睡好。"},{"w":"widespread","p":"adj.","d":"happening in many places or among many people","c":"廣泛的；普遍的","s":"The use of smartphones is now widespread among elementary school students, and many parents are worried about it.","t":"智慧型手機的使用現在在小學生之間很普遍，許多家長對此感到擔憂。","h":1},{"w":"widely","p":"adv.","d":"by a lot of people or in a lot of places","c":"廣泛地；普遍地","s":"English is widely used in international business, so many companies want workers who can speak it well.","t":"英語在國際商務中被廣泛使用，所以許多公司想要英文說得好的員工。"},{"w":"spread, spread, spread","p":"v.","d":"to move or cover a larger area; to make something known by more people","c":"擴散；蔓延；散布","s":"The fire spread quickly through the dry forest because of the strong winds, and hundreds of firefighters were sent there.","t":"由於強風，火勢在乾燥的森林中迅速蔓延，數百名消防員被派往現場。","a":"spread"},{"w":"wig","p":"n.","d":"a covering of false hair worn on the head","c":"假髮","s":"The actor wore a long white wig and a fake beard to play the old king in the school play.","t":"那位演員戴著長長的白色假髮和假鬍子，在學校話劇中飾演老國王。","h":1},{"w":"wear a wig","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put on false hair","c":"戴假髮","s":"For the Halloween party, my brother decided to wear a wig with bright green hair and dress up as a monster.","t":"萬聖節派對時，我哥哥決定戴一頂亮綠色的假髮，打扮成怪物。"},{"w":"wig","p":"n.","d":"false white hair worn by judges in some countries","c":"（法官戴的）假髮","s":"In British courts, judges traditionally wear a white wig, which makes them look very serious and old-fashioned.","t":"在英國的法庭上，法官傳統上會戴白色假髮，這讓他們看起來非常嚴肅又老派。"},{"w":"wilderness","p":"n.","d":"a large natural area where no people live","c":"荒野；荒地","s":"The hikers spent five days in the wilderness without seeing another person, a road, or even a single building.","t":"登山客在荒野中度過五天，沒看到任何人、道路，甚至連一棟建築也沒有。","h":1},{"w":"wildlife","p":"n.","d":"animals and plants that live in nature","c":"野生動物；野生生物","s":"The national park protects the local wildlife, including black bears, monkeys, and many kinds of rare birds.","t":"國家公園保護當地的野生動物，包括黑熊、獼猴和許多種稀有鳥類。","h":1},{"w":"wild","p":"adj.","d":"living or growing in nature, not kept by people","c":"野生的","s":"These wild monkeys often steal food from tourists, so keep your bags closed when you walk on the mountain path.","t":"這些野生獼猴常常搶遊客的食物，所以走山路時要把包包關好。"},{"w":"in the wild","p":"phr.","d":"in natural conditions, not in a zoo","c":"在野外","s":"Fewer than two thousand of these pandas still live in the wild, so the government works hard to protect them.","t":"這種貓熊只剩不到兩千隻還生活在野外，所以政府努力保護牠們。"},{"w":"wildfire","p":"n.","d":"a large fire that spreads quickly through forests or grassland","c":"野火；森林大火","s":"The wildfire burned for two weeks and destroyed more than a thousand homes in California last summer.","t":"去年夏天那場野火燒了兩個星期，摧毀了加州一千多棟房屋。"},{"w":"windshield","p":"n.","d":"the large glass window at the front of a car","c":"擋風玻璃","s":"A small stone hit the car's windshield on the highway and made a long crack right in front of the driver.","t":"一顆小石頭在高速公路上打到車子的擋風玻璃，就在駕駛正前方留下一道長長的裂痕。","h":1},{"w":"windshield wiper","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long thin arm that moves across a windshield to clean off rain","c":"雨刷","s":"It was raining so hard that even with the windshield wipers going at full speed, my father could hardly see the road.","t":"雨下得非常大，就算雨刷開到最快，我爸爸也幾乎看不到路。","a":"windshield wipers"},{"w":"wind","p":"n.","d":"moving air","c":"風","s":"A strong wind blew my umbrella inside out as I was walking to the bus stop this morning.","t":"今天早上我走去公車站時，一陣強風把我的雨傘吹翻了。"},{"w":"wither","p":"v.","d":"(of a plant) to become dry and start to die","c":"枯萎；凋謝","s":"The flowers on my desk began to wither after only three days, because I forgot to change the water.","t":"我桌上的花才三天就開始枯萎了，因為我忘了換水。","h":1},{"w":"wither","p":"v.","d":"to become weaker and slowly disappear","c":"衰退；減弱；消失","s":"Her hope of winning the game began to wither when the other team scored three goals in five minutes.","t":"當對手在五分鐘內連進三球時，她贏球的希望開始破滅。"},{"w":"withered","p":"adj.","d":"dry and dead or dying","c":"枯萎的；乾枯的","s":"Grandpa picked up a withered leaf from the ground and told us that autumn had arrived in the mountains.","t":"爺爺從地上撿起一片枯葉，告訴我們山上已經入秋了。"},{"w":"witty","p":"adj.","d":"clever and funny in what you say","c":"機智的；風趣的","s":"Our English teacher is so witty that even students who hate grammar laugh during her lessons.","t":"我們的英文老師非常風趣，連討厭文法的學生在她的課上都會笑。","h":1},{"w":"wit","p":"n.","d":"the ability to say clever and funny things","c":"機智；風趣","s":"The comedian is famous for his quick wit, and he always has a funny answer to every question from the audience.","t":"那位喜劇演員以反應快、機智出名，他對觀眾的每個問題總有好笑的回答。"},{"w":"wittily","p":"adv.","d":"in a clever and funny way","c":"機智地；詼諧地","s":"She answered the reporter's difficult question wittily, and the whole room burst into laughter at the press conference.","t":"她機智地回答了記者的難題，整個會場哄堂大笑。"},{"w":"workshop","p":"n.","d":"a meeting where people learn about a subject by discussing and practicing","c":"研習會；工作坊","s":"Our teachers attended a two-day workshop on how to use AI tools in the classroom during the winter vacation.","t":"我們的老師在寒假參加了一場為期兩天、關於如何在課堂上使用AI工具的研習工作坊。","h":1},{"w":"workshop","p":"n.","d":"a room or building where things are made or repaired","c":"工作室；工廠","s":"My uncle builds wooden chairs and tables in a small workshop behind his house, and he sells them online.","t":"我舅舅在他家後面的一間小工作室裡做木椅和木桌，然後在網路上販售。"},{"w":"writing workshop","p":"n.phr.","d":"a class where people write and comment on each other's work","c":"寫作工作坊","s":"I joined a writing workshop at the library, where we shared our stories and gave each other helpful comments.","t":"我參加了圖書館的寫作工作坊，我們在那裡分享故事並互相給予有用的意見。"},{"w":"worship","p":"v.","d":"to show love and respect to a god, often by praying","c":"敬拜；崇拜（神明）","s":"Many people in Taiwan worship Mazu, the goddess of the sea, and visit her temples during the big festival in spring.","t":"台灣許多人敬拜海上女神媽祖，並在春天的大型慶典期間參拜她的廟宇。","h":1},{"w":"worship","p":"n.","d":"the act of praying to or showing respect for a god","c":"禮拜；敬拜","s":"The old temple is still a place of worship, so visitors should speak quietly and not take photos inside.","t":"這座古廟仍是一個敬拜的場所，所以遊客應該輕聲說話，不要在裡面拍照。"},{"w":"worship","p":"v.","d":"to love and admire someone very much","c":"崇拜；熱愛","s":"My little brother worships his basketball coach and tries to copy everything he does on the court.","t":"我弟弟非常崇拜他的籃球教練，試著模仿他在球場上的一舉一動。","a":"worships"},{"w":"worthwhile","p":"adj.","d":"useful or important enough to spend time, money, or effort on","c":"值得做的；有價值的","s":"Volunteering at the animal shelter is hard work, but it is worthwhile because you can help so many dogs find homes.","t":"在動物收容所當志工很辛苦，但很值得，因為你可以幫助許多狗狗找到家。","h":1},{"w":"worthy","p":"adj.","d":"deserving respect, praise, or attention","c":"值得的；配得上的","s":"Her brave actions during the fire are worthy of our respect, and the mayor will give her a special award.","t":"她在火災中的勇敢行為值得我們尊敬，市長將頒給她一個特別獎。","h":1},{"w":"worth","p":"adj.","d":"good or useful enough to do; having a certain value","c":"值得；價值…","s":"The museum is a little far from the station, but it is definitely worth a visit if you love art.","t":"那間博物館離車站有點遠，但如果你熱愛藝術，絕對值得一遊。"},{"w":"worthless","p":"adj.","d":"having no value or use","c":"無價值的；沒用的","s":"The old coins that we found in the box turned out to be worthless, so we gave them to my little brother to play with.","t":"我們在盒子裡找到的舊硬幣結果是一文不值的，所以我們把它們給弟弟玩。"},{"w":"yacht","p":"n.","d":"a large boat with sails or an engine, used for pleasure","c":"遊艇；帆船","s":"The rich businessman spent his summer sailing around the Greek islands on his private yacht with his family.","t":"那位富商和家人搭他的私人遊艇在希臘群島航行，度過了整個夏天。","h":1},{"w":"yacht club","p":"n.phr.","d":"a club for people who sail yachts","c":"遊艇俱樂部","s":"My uncle joined a yacht club in Kaohsiung, and now he goes sailing every weekend when the weather is good.","t":"我叔叔加入了高雄的一個遊艇俱樂部，現在天氣好的週末他都會去航行。"},{"w":"sailing","p":"n.","d":"the sport or activity of traveling in a boat with sails","c":"帆船運動；航行","s":"Kenting is a great place for sailing, because the wind is strong and the sea is clear and warm.","t":"墾丁是從事帆船運動的好地方，因為那裡風大，海水清澈又溫暖。"},{"w":"yield","p":"v.","d":"to produce crops, profits, or results","c":"生產；產出；產生","s":"This small farm can yield more than two tons of rice a year, because the soil is rich and there is plenty of rain.","t":"這座小農場一年可以生產兩噸多的稻米，因為土壤肥沃、雨量充足。","h":1},{"w":"yield","p":"v.","d":"to let other cars or people go first","c":"讓路；讓行","s":"Drivers must yield to people walking across the street, or they will have to pay a big fine.","t":"駕駛人必須禮讓過馬路的行人，否則要繳一大筆罰款。"},{"w":"yield to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finally agree to do what someone wants after being forced","c":"屈服於；向…讓步","s":"The company finally yielded to pressure from its workers and agreed to give them two more days of holiday.","t":"公司最後屈服於員工的壓力，同意再多給他們兩天假。","a":"yielded to"},{"w":"yield","p":"n.","d":"the amount of crops or profit produced","c":"產量；收益","s":"Because of the long dry season, this year's mango yield is much lower than last year's, so prices have gone up.","t":"由於漫長的乾季，今年芒果的產量比去年低很多，所以價格上漲了。"}]}];
